[{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"‘Moreish’ by Super Hans (Hardback)","instanceDates":"22 September-22 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"711403ATCQTQSKHJDHCLVKCRMRHDKGNTT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-22T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-22T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-22T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-22T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Britain's foremost TV writer and showrunner takes us through his life in television, and behind the scenes on some of our favourite shows.\r\n\r\nThe Queerest of Folk distils Russell T Davies's career in television, taking us from his early days working on children’s shows and soaps through to the giddy heights of relaunching Doctor Who and bringing queer relationships onto the mainstream screen.\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"‘The Queerest of Folk: A Life in Television' by Russell T Davies","instanceDates":"8 October-8 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"736803APNRJKJGBHHBQNQLTTRKSBDQLBB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-08T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-08T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-08T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-08T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Nearing the end of her life, Edna decides to remount the Broadway show from the 1950’s that nearly made her a star.\r\nHere lies an informal live reading/singing of the first act of a new, original musical, ‘The Revival’, written by Nicola and Rosie Dempsey (Flo & Joan) and Connor Thompson (Second City), and performed by an ensemble cast.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"“The Revival (Workshop)”  by Nicola Dempsey, Rosie Dempsey and Connor Thompson","instanceDates":"26 April-26 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"542003APLNBMQPCPKRPCCRRRKVQDVNQDT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-26T15:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-26T14:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-26T15:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-26T14:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"New Writing","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Work In Progress","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"Nightlife gatecrash, raucous cabaret and musical extrava-ganza; 0800 CUPID is a genre-defying queer countercultural opus from THISISPOPBABY that fizzes between performance and reality. Through her drag persona, crumbling club-kid ‘Cupid’, Emer Dineen grapples with love in a lonely capitalist paradigm. Hungover, moulting and disorientated, our re-dundant deity battles modern life, unravelling Emer’s true story of navigating loss, crises, chaotic relationships and feeling the sweet sting of meaningful connection where she least expects it.\r\n0800 CUPID is an SOS response to the swelling social anxiety of a post-pandemic pre-apocalyptic world. A camp catalyst for reconnection; it's a musical march into and back from the existential brink.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":80,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"0800 CUPID","instanceDates":"16 October-26 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"567803AMLRVSSJVNCLPCBMCDDLHLMVSDJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-16T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-16T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-26T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-26T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"After a two time sell-out Edinburgh Fringe and raising over £8000 for Medical Aid for Palestinians- Aisha Amanduri (Runner-up Bath Comedy Fest. New Act Award) and Hasan Al-Habib (winner B’ham Comedy Fest. Breaking Talent Award 2023) return! \r\nExpect gameshows, sharp-wit and EDL (extremely deafening laughter). \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"2 Muslim 2 Furious 3: Sharia? I hardly know her!","instanceDates":"9 February-9 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"683003AHPGRSJHCBBDJTVMVMGGPVKLCBH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-09T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-09T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-09T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-09T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Three improvisers. Endless possibilities.\r\nThree of the UK's best improvisers will create a unique and hilarious theatrical comedy experience, improvised entirely in the moment. In this miraculous feat of spontaneous storytelling, the three performers will play every character - inspired by three audience suggestions, a live musician and three pieces of set - to create a one-of-a-kind show. \r\n\r\nFeaturing very special guest Ambika Mod, star of the global sensation One Day (Netflix) and This is Going to Hurt (BBC). \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"3: An Improvised Comedy Show","instanceDates":"29 March-19 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"601203ABMNBPMPNKTMLSNDCNMNMJLCSJL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-29T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-29T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-19T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-19T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"“Mum, forgot to tell you - I’m a lesbian. Sorry it’s late - fifteen years late, but grab a rainbow flag and don some Docs... I’m 30 and I’m coming out.”\r\nOn her 30th birthday, Kit left her twenties, her boyfriend and the closet. While her friends marry, have babies and get mortgages, she is starting from scratch in a whirlwind of drugs, clubs and heartbreak. \r\n\r\nJoin Kit in this hilarious, sexy and painful portrayal of what it means to start life all over again. Is it too late to be a lesbian? Does she need a cat and an undercut? Will coming out complete her?\r\n\r\nUsing touching interviews, innovative projection and powerful storytelling, Sinclair takes us on a memorable journey about drawing your own blueprint, discovering identity and losing yourself along the way.\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"30 and Out by Kit Sinclair","instanceDates":"5 February-6 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"520403AGBJBKJSVTBRQSQDLKLLBNLSBLM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-05T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-05T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-06T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-06T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"Dre and Jo are busy-important-slugs-on-the rise, going straight to the top. Lett-uce be frank: these queer deviants will be dancing, lip syncing and writhing around in lots... and lots of SLIME.\r\n\"50 ways to Kill a Slug\" celebrates queerness, ugliness, and uselessness, exploring the slug as a political symbol of resistance. Rejecting the relentless grind, these sluggies embrace radical slowness, defiantly rejecting the binary \"BE PRODUCTIVE OR DIE!\".\r\nWatch them strive to transcend their terrestrial existence in a sexy, ugly divergence from the unsustainable norm. Join us in slug land, where it's safe— or is it? Squish!\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"50 Ways To Kill A Slug","instanceDates":"17 June-17 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"615003AHTKBRLQKVLJGQVRQLRBCCRRMMR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-17T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-17T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-17T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-17T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"“What's the worst thing that's ever made you feel like a woman?” \r\n\r\n52 Monologues for Young Transsexuals is a raucous and unapologetic speed-drive through transfeminine experience. Performers Laurie Ward and Charli Cowgill sat down with other trans women to get sleepover-honest about bodies, sex and love. Armed with baby oil and lots of pink glitter, they're taking you from Barbra Streisand to BDSM, in a fever dream of hilarious and gut-wrenching confession. And no - there aren't actually 52 Monologues...\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"52 Monologues for Young Transexuals","instanceDates":"4 March-16 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"515603ARPRPLRMPSQPHJTTQTCDPGDRCSC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-04T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-04T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-16T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-16T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"Three-time consecutive Fringe First Award winners Xhloe and Natasha return to London with their critically acclaimed piece.\r\nBoyhood is all about spit-shakes, rope swings, and playing soldiers, but only the good guys of course. Whether it’s stories around the campfire, pranks on their superior, or a prayer to their favorite president, these two scouts just want their moms to see the big strong men they’ve become. \r\nA Letter To Lyndon B Johnson or God: Whoever Reads This First is an absurdist two-hander that blurs the lines of 1960s American Boy Scouts and drafted US Soldiers in Vietnam using clowning, physical theatre, and storytelling. \r\nFrom three time consecutive Fringe First Award winners and creators of And Then The Rodeo Burned Down and What If They Ate The Baby?, Xhloe and Natasha return to London with their critically acclaimed piece. \r\nXhloe Rice (Creator/ Performer) \r\nNatasha Roland (Creator/ Performer) \r\nAngelo Sagnelli (Lighting Designer/ Technical Director)\r\n13+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"A Letter To Lyndon B Johnson or God: Whoever Reads This First","instanceDates":"18 March-29 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"597203AJSMLTJGSQJTTTJCNBBVSRJJTDD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-18T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-18T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-29T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-29T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Performance Art","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Comedy"},{"description":"Cult comedy icon. Performer of many a sold-out-critically-acclaimed-standing-ovation-filled run with us at Soho Theatre and the Edinburgh Fringe. Now headed to our biggest stage yet for ONE, that’s right, ONE Magical Evening at Soho Theatre Walthamstow.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"A Magical Evening With Patti Harrison","instanceDates":"26 July-26 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"626403ANLMKNJQLGBRJQTMKDDBPPQMSST","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-26T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-26T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-26T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-26T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"This isn’t just comedy-it’s a rebellion. Watch The Director live-direct his company of clowns in a melodramatic period piece, as YOU shower them with bottomless banana peels*!\r\nModern audiences are obligated to offer ovations and applause regardless of a performance’s quality. By tossing out the rulebook (and a few peels*), ANOD reclaims the honesty of live theatre that was celebrated centuries ago.\r\nToss a peel*, join a chant, or boo just because you feel like it!\r\nThis is improvised clown madness with a dream to be grand and a mission to entertain. Weuse >70 peels* per show.\r\n*peels provided\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"A Night of Drama","instanceDates":"19 June-19 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"615203ADSHVNBBDHVNRKPSSNQLGCNTMML","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-19T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-19T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-19T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-19T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Waltham Forest Music Service Presents: A Place of Wonder - Featuring Songs of the Forest\r\nAn Enchanted Journey through the Heritage, Legends & Magic of Waltham Forest.\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"A Place of Wonder","instanceDates":"30 June-30 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"728603ACNBBGSMCRVNQCSKTDVMPSTHQVR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-30T14:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-30T13:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-30T18:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-30T17:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Families","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Access"},{"description":"In Alfie’s fantasy world, it’s hard to tell who he is – rockstar, guru, actor, shark. Which version of him is showing up today?\r\nRenowned autistic artists Cian Binchy (‘The Level’ ITV) and Anna Constable (‘Imposter 22’, Royal Court) bend the lines of fantasy, reality and masking, as they try to figure out how to be in the world. In a darkly comic universe, with shark chases, a rap about Devon, and some lovely cardboard cut-outs, they ask:\r\n\r\nWhen the person you show to the world is just a mask, what’s underneath? \r\n\r\nCo-produced by award winning company Access All Areas and The Lowry, and created by Cian Binchy in collaboration with Nick Llewellyn (‘Madhouse’, ‘The Interrogation’) and writers Shaun Dunne (‘How to Tell a Secret’ Netflix) and Leah Moore (‘Good Omens’ Amazon Prime).\r\n\r\nA small enclosed room with a shark. What could go wrong? \r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":65,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"A Small Enclosed Room with Alfie Murphy","instanceDates":"13 May-17 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"607403AHMRJDTKJPDLTDTQGJDNVBHVHPB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-13T18:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-13T17:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-17T18:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-17T17:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Access","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"\"Cause how am I gonna have the summer to end all summers with no one to share it with?”\r\nAmani and Brianna are getting ready for a blind date, but getting there is the real test. Between teefing sisters, gentrified patties, flying bird poo, missing barbers, and a trim that could end a man, romance might not be the only thing on the line… \r\n \r\nSet to a Caribbean South London soundtrack, A to B is about the beauty and absurdity of trying to be seen and to connect in a world that won’t stop interrupting. It’s about showing up: for love, family, yourself, even when you’re late, lost, or covered in mud. A coming-of-age romcom where nothing goes to plan, but everything still matters.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":80,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"A to B By Tia Renee Mullings","instanceDates":"12 June-3 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"692003ADJJKBCBTKRHPLJDRHQGKSJBMBP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-12T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-12T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-03T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-03T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Meet Honourabelle Mention, a sharp-tongued scullery maid who accidentally discovers the magic hidden in music and decides to swap the broom stick for the mic stand. She is now on a mission to spread the songs of the Band (no, not the one you know). An adventure through witty parodies that is chaotic, charming and guaranteed to leave you humming. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"A Tribute to the Band","instanceDates":"4 February-4 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"683203AQKGCTVRVCKHBMPCCMJTDTTCTLB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-04T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-04T22:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-04T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-04T22:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Sheeps are 'arguably the best sketch group of their generation' (The Guardian), and now they’re inarguably the best Christmas-themed band of their generation too. They will be performing songs from their unexpectedly-chart-placing album* A VERY SHEEPS CHRISTMAS (which will be available to buy in the foyer), some surprise tracks and new songs.\r\nWith lots of special guests TBA. And yes, it’s Christmas, so it’s Christmas songs! Don’t come and then be confused that it’s songs!\r\n\r\nThe Sheeps Christmas Band are: Jonno (Head writer of Saturday Night Live UK), Al Roberts (Stath Lets Flats, Starstruck), Johnny White Really-Really (Don’t Hug Me I’m Scared, Make That Movie), Luke Bainbridge, Charlie Flynn & Sophie Burrows. Plus guest vocalist Liam Williams (Ladhood, Pls Like).\r\n*58th in the Official Album Downloads Charts.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":140,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"A Very Sheeps Christmas - Live in Concert!","instanceDates":"8 December-8 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"744203ANSVGSCCRSQKLVDRJGPCQPDQHBK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-08T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-08T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-08T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-08T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Sketch","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Sheeps are “arguably the best sketch group of their generation” (Guardian), and now they’re inarguably the best Christmas-themed band of their generation too. \r\nFor one night only, Sheeps and their full live band will be performing songs from their unexpectedly-chart-placing album* A VERY SHEEPS CHRISTMAS (available to buy in the foyer), and some surprise tracks.  \r\n\r\nWith approximately 4 surprise guests! And yes, it’s Christmas, so it’s Christmas songs! Don’t come and then be confused that it’s songs! \r\n \r\n\r\nPrevious special guests have included Jamie Demetriou, Rose Matafeo, Lolly Adefope, Charlotte Ritchie, David O’Doherty, Emma Sidi, Paul Williams, Jazz Emu, Ania Magliano & more. \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nSheeps continue to be Al Roberts (Stath Lets Flats, Starstruck), Liam Williams (Ladhood, Pls Like) & Jonno (Seinfeld). \r\n\r\nSheeps’ live band are: Johnny White Really-Really, Luke Bainbridge, Charlie Flynn, Sophie Burrows & John Tothill. \r\n\r\n*58th in the Official Album Downloads Charts. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":135,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"A Very Sheeps Christmas - Live in Concert! (Dec 2025)","instanceDates":"17 December-17 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"655603AKHCPVCKCNDDJHNQQGRGRBTHTCH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-17T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-17T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-17T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-17T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"With a playful interactive twist this isn’t just a show, it’s an invitation to get involved, dose up on dopamine and soak up the serotonin. Part cabaret, part house party, Do All The Things is a celebration of commonality, an ode to the absurd, and, at its heart, a joyous middle finger to despair and disconnection. With big prizes. “\r\n\r\nI think they’re amazing” Phoebe Waller-Bridge","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"A&E Comedy: Do All The Things","instanceDates":"6 June-6 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"716803AHDVLRLSKSGBDGSJTSRMCSSMJMT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-06T16:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-06T15:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-06T16:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-06T15:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"'You're allowed to put whatever you like in your blurb. It doesn't even have to describe the show' Aaron\r\nBorn and raised in Sydney, Aaron's quickly climbed the ranks of the international comedy scene.\r\nAaron made his mark on Australian comedy with his debut solo show in 2017 and has since toured to sold-out crowds and rave reviews, earning him the sought-after awards for Best Newcomer and Director's Choice and nomination for Best Show at Melbourne International Comedy Festival.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Aaron Chen: Funny Garden","instanceDates":"5 September-7 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"561203ADQTPBVDLBQJLTNQGSQVNJNMVND","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-05T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-05T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-07T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-07T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Using his trademark blend of audience interaction and razor-sharp improvisation, Rob creates a full discography for a fictional artist created by you, the audience.  \r\n\r\nWith a sample-pad necklace to trigger the high-production beats and hooks he freestyles over, Rob creates the kind of exhilarating live experience that has won him a string of awards, and the highest of international critical acclaim. \r\n\r\nAbandoman supported multi-platinum artist Ed Sheeran on his sell out UK tour, enthralled audiences on Channel 4’s 8 out of 10 Cats Does Countdown, BBC1’s The One Show and BBC2′s The Stephen K Amos Show, guested on various radio shows from Nick Grimshaw (BBC Radio 1) to Christian O Connell (Absolute Radio) and held a song writing residency with Chris Hawkin (BBC 6 Music).  \r\n\r\nAbandoman has headlined comedy stages at every major UK music festival from Glastonbury to Latitude and stormed international stages in Australia, Europe, The USA, Canada and Hong Kong.\r\n\r\n‘Clever, quick-witted and audacious’ ★★★★ The Scotsman \r\n‘Raucous, expansive and relentlessly hilarious‘ ★★★★ The Times \r\n‘A freestyle talent that is unparalleled anywhere… comedic timing and witty rhyming that’s so impressive it could’ve been scripted’  ★★★★The Independent \r\n‘Flight of the Conchords meets 8 Mile”’★★★★ Chortle\r\n‘Broderick has us in the palm of his hand from the minute he starts until the very last mic drop’ ★★★★★ Broadway Baby\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Abandoman aka Rob Broderick: Discography","instanceDates":"12 April-14 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"459203ATQJNSSBPLPMKRVHJQNSTQTHLQR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-12T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-12T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-14T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-14T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"After a smash hit worldwide tour, international comedy sensation and Forbes 30 Under 30 honoree Abby Govindan makes her Soho Theatre debut with her new comedy hour Pushing 30, a gritty and unflinching dissection of generational trauma and finding love in the age of big tech. \r\nReferences to domestic violence, racism, death, child marriage. 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Abby Govindan: Pushing 30","instanceDates":"20 November-21 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"760003ARGJTDBVQNBTTKSRHGTTSPHJPMD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-20T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-20T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-21T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-21T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Edinburgh Comedy Awards Best Newcomer Nominee and ISH Awards Best Newcomer Winner, Abby Wambaugh, brings her critically acclaimed debut show to Soho Theatre.\r\nAfter waking up in the hospital following a late miscarriage, Abby-still high on anesthesia—made an unexpected decision: to become a comedian. Now, in her uniquely goofy and heartfelt hour, Abby shares her 17 best ideas for for her first show. From \"Old Man Learns Parkour\" to an absurdly long impression of the number nine, Abby’s debut is packed with playful, surprising, and hilarious moments. \r\n\r\nA Funny Women finalist and co-host of the \"Help Hole\" podcast with Sofie Hagen, Abby’s comedy is bold, original, and filled with unexpected twists. Don’t miss Abby's rise to stardom in this unforgettable, deeply personal, and wildly funny performance. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Abby Wambaugh: The First 3 Minutes of 17 Shows","instanceDates":"9 January-18 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"579203ALSRSDVGRHVLDBNLGJJTLPKQRLM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-09T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-09T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-18T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-18T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Abhishek takes you on a hilarious journey through the everyday quirks and absurdities of life. \r\nWith his unique observational humor, he takes on everything from relationships and technology to Indian culture and more, offering a fresh perspective on the world we live in. \r\n \r\nPerformed in Hindi \r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Abhishek Upmanyu: Toxic","instanceDates":"25 July-25 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"728203AKQHVQSVTVPSQMLMQVRDMKPMQBT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-25T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-25T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-25T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-25T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"“Where all your mistakes are forgiven. Even encouraged. <3”\r\nFollowing their hit UK debut at the Edinburgh Fringe and Soho Theatre in 2023, India’s most-watched crowd-work duo are back with a brand new improv show, previewing ahead of a return to the Fringe this year. Welcome to the Positivity Centre, where everyone is encouraged to confess their worst mistakes. Literally the worst evil things or opinions you have. Anonymously, of course. Abishek and Nirmal are Guruji and his assistant, here to justify your submissions and find the positive aspects, no matter how messed up they are. Everyone is happy here. No roasting, only positivity. (This is satire.) 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Abishek & Nirmal: The Great Indian Positivity House","instanceDates":"21 July-26 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"622603AGRLVVSSTVDMMMCJHGJQKHRTNVL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-21T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-21T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-26T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-26T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Abishek Kumar and Nirmal Pillai are back on the road with their hugely fun and interactive show that's guaranteed to leave you cackling.\r\nThese two very high-energy performers make their way to the stage after taking the world of Instagram reels by storm. Since then, they’ve starred in reality shows, feature films, web series and gained some very humble recognitions like Instagram’s official list of 25 Under 25 Influencers 2021 and #5 on Forbes 100 Digital Stars 2022.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Abishek & Nirmal: The Reel to Real – Crowd Work Tour","instanceDates":"31 October-4 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"493403AGMRGKCSPTDNCQKPKDMPKKDLHLJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-31T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-31T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-04T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-04T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Sell-out Edinburgh Fringe debuters and BAFTA-nominated freaks Ada & Bron invite you to third wheel an unmissable hour of weirdo soulmates and \"sheer oddball charisma\" Scotsman. With \"gorgeous chemistry, total commitment and delightfully inventive playfulness\", The Origin of Love is a spectacle for lovers of the strange, stupid and sexy. A cursed couple's character comedy show from the Broadcast Award winning creators of Channel 4's Peaked. \r\nAs heard on BBC Radio 4's Time of The Week.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ada and Bron: The Origin of Love","instanceDates":"13 October-17 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"652204AJHQCTPJJDHBMJKBVRGJTSRPQPN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-13T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-13T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-17T22:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-17T22:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The Times - Top 3 Rising Stars of the Fringe\r\nBritish Comedy Guide Top Picks of The Fringe\r\n★★★★ - Pick of the Fringe \r\nIvo Graham - “despicably multi talented”\r\n\r\n\r\n‘Ay up ducks, it’s me (fella doing the show). It’s a stand-up odyssey about reinvention with a few tricks up its sleeve*, so get on Stoke-on-Trent’s premium cultural export. Critics are already calling the show 'please stop emailing' and 'unsubscribe'...well they were until they started saying some nice things about me, so that joke doesn’t work as well now – a crown of thorns. See ya there for a big comedy blow out.’\r\n\r\n*spent whole budget on an autotune pedal.\r\n\r\n16+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Adam Flood: Remoulded","instanceDates":"11 March-13 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"517804ASVSMMKSSCSTKTQTPNDGTJRLSKV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-11T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-11T21:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-13T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-13T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The nation's twelfth-favourite doctor brings his brand new show on to Soho Theatre Walthamstow, fresh from a record-breaking run at the Edinburgh Fringe and a sell-out season in the West End.\r\nThis is Going to Hurt was a literary sensation, selling three million copies and becoming a multi-BAFTA-winning BBC series. \r\n\r\nUndoctored follows on from This is Going to Hurt, leaving audiences laughing and crying with Adam's unique tales of life on and off the wards. It also contains the ‘degloving’ story because people ask for refunds if they don't hear it.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Adam Kay: UNDOCTORED","instanceDates":"21 November-22 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"602203ACHKCJMSTDCMRDBQCJKPPDSCDDK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-21T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-21T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-22T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-22T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Baubles. Banter. Bromance. Ballads.\r\nIt's the Christmas show you've all been waiting for (in September).  \r\nThe show that takes two titans of the light entertainment industry; two icons of the theatre world; two award-winning behemoths of the modern age…\r\n…and brings them together to play Michael Ball and Alfie Boe.\r\nFor the first time ever, Edinburgh Comedy Award winners Adam Riches and John Kearns team up to become one of music's most bangable duos, for a once in a lifetime yuletide extravaganza guaranteed to have you doublechecking exactly what list Santa put you on for this to happen. \r\nExpect songs. Anticipate goosebumps. Pray for harmonies.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Adam Riches and John Kearns are 'Ball & Boe'","instanceDates":"27 September-27 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"622003ALPTSLQNQVBVMNTDMBDNDMQRTRJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-27T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-27T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-27T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-27T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"Baubles. Banter. Bromance. Ballads.\r\nIt's the Christmas show you've all been waiting for.  \r\nThe show that takes two titans of the light entertainment industry; two icons of the theatre world; two award-winning behemoths of the modern age…\r\n…and brings them together to play Michael Ball and Alfie Boe.\r\n \r\nFor the first time ever, Edinburgh Comedy Award winners Adam Riches and John Kearns team up to become one of music's most bangable duos, for a once in a lifetime yuletide extravaganza guaranteed to have you doublechecking exactly what list Santa put you on for this to happen. \r\nExpect songs. Anticipate goosebumps. Pray for harmonies.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Adam Riches and John Kearns are 'Ball & Boe’ - For Fourteen Nights Only","instanceDates":"10 December-19 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"577403ANCCCGQRHPBNCVBHVLLMCCJGQHT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-10T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-10T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-19T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-19T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Like an undescended testicle en route to its final destination, Christmas is a-coming!\r\nAnd nothing yells Yule louder than Sean Bean in full on medieval mode, challenging you all to a sackful of seasonal games, hellbent on getting you all giddy. \r\nSo come join Edinburgh Comedy Award Winner Adam Riches, (Cats Does Countdown), as he hits the road once more with his (k)night of chaotic buffoonery, to give you bastards a Christmas present you’ll never forget.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Adam Riches AS Sean Bean in ‘THE 12 BEANS OF CHRISTMAS’","instanceDates":"15 December-16 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"660403ABTCDKLKDBDNGNJMBSRDNMMLCKS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-15T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-15T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-16T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-16T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Adam Riches’ 2025 show which was named a Must-See Christmas Show by The Independent, The Times, Time Out and The Guardian, and featured in Chortle’s 10 Most Memorable Comedy Gigs of 2025, is followed by an entirely new production for 2026. Last Christmas, he gave you his heart. But the very next year, you gave it away. What the hell were you thinking? So now The Bean is back. Back with more chaos. Back with more bufoonery. Back to save Christmas, once and for all. Starring Edinburgh Comedy Award Winner Adam Riches AS ‘Sean Bean’ and All of You AS ‘A Bunch of Bastards’.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Adam Riches IS Sean Bean IN “How the Bean Saved Christmas” ","instanceDates":"8 December-10 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"749803ALVJVPPMJPDCNNTHVDBCDMHJSLG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-08T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-08T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-10T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-10T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"“Last night, ten tortoises were massacred in a tombola related prank gone wrong. So tonight, all members of the Beakington Council… aka YOU… will be hauled before an independent adjudicator… aka ME… to find out what happened.”\r\n\r\nAn interactive comedy whodunnit from the mind of Adam Riches, an absolute (Edinburgh Comedy Award-winning) twonk. \r\n\r\nAs seen on BBC4’s acclaimed Detectorists and Channel 4’s 8 out of 10 Cats Does Countdown as ‘Sean Bean’. \r\n\r\nAlso featuring Edinburgh Comedy Award Best Newcomer Nominee and ‘maverick physical comedian’ (Guardian), Ben Target. \r\n\r\nAdam Riches’ 2019 Edinburgh Fringe sell-out smash hit, finally makes its London transfer… \r\n\r\nReviews for Beaky: \r\n\r\n‘A delightful tortoise murder mystery… it’s massively enjoyable, sheer fun’  \r\n★★★★ TIMES\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Adam Riches: The Beakington Town Hall Murders","instanceDates":"12 June-17 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"458803AKMGCPHGLDKJTKGBVHDVLHVRGSM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-12T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-12T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-17T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-17T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Additional Dietary Requirements For Mad Hatters Tea Party","instanceDates":"25 July-25 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"739804ATGVCQPNRKSVBQMRLBTGGJDGDKJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-25T12:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-25T11:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-25T13:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-25T12:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Add-ons Soho Theatre Walthamstow","instanceDates":"16 January-4 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"603203ABQMBKPBJVMPSNGMSLGGHLCSSQL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-16T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-16T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-04T13:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-04T13:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Is fatherhood REAL or is it a lie made up by BIG childhood to sell MORE therapy? Join Adi Parmar (gay), as he recalls his unforgettable childhood in North India (India) and his unexpected fatherhood in North Holland (Netherlands) and makes sense of it all using the best medicine there is: Laughter (hahaha). Sexually explicit themes, References to cultural and/or political issues. 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Adi Parmar: Sunny Boy","instanceDates":"7 January-9 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"762003AJSTBJPQLQRCDKNNNJDQVHVKGNT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-01-07T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-01-07T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-01-09T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-01-09T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"A stand-up comedian went to 1st Base with Mount Everest. In her new hour Mittal takes a small trek and makes a big deal out of it.\r\nAditi is a comedian, actress and writer based in Mumbai. One of the first women to do stand-up in India, she has been rated amongst India's top 10 comedians by The Times of India. \r\n\r\nShe has 2 stand-up comedy specials on Netflix, 1 on Amazon Prime (made with Soho Theatre) and her own BBC Radio 4 series. Her work has been featured on multiple documentaries across the world. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Aditi Mittal: Bad Altitude","instanceDates":"9 September-14 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"551003ASJTRBRTTRKVGTQQMTBQKHKHMJG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-09T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-09T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-14T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-14T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"After marinating in her own juices for three years of the pandemic, Aditi Mittal is back at Soho Theatre because her mother can’t stand to have her at home any longer.  Featuring jokes about the burning world, our decaying bodies and the fall of mankind. Catch her live, before she Unalives.\r\n\r\nAditi has 2 Netflix stand-up comedy specials, 1 on Amazon Prime, BBC Radio 4 and her work has been featured on multiple documentaries across the world. She plays many characters, sometimes on stage, mostly in her head. Her stand-up comedy videos have millions of views because she has a massive family and a persistent dad. You can hear her hosting the Women In Labour podcast and scaring listeners as a guest on The Bugle.\r\n\r\n‘Forthright performer with a sharp critical mind.’ Guardian\r\n\r\n‘She specialises in the ludicrousness of the everyday.’ Skinny\r\n\r\n‘No topic, no matter how controversial or lighthearted, is safe from her sharp and quick-witted humour.’ Ed Fest Mag\r\n\r\n16+ recommendation ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Aditi Mittal: Unalive","instanceDates":"12 June-17 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"466603ABKGGTHQSTCJPLBJRJBTSDBLCQK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-12T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-12T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-17T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-17T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"India/South Asian heritage"},{"description":"An atom travels to Earth on a quest for greatness, finding himself inside some of the most important people who have ever lived.\r\nJoin Adrian Bliss on a wild ride through history and give your seven octillion atoms an experience they will never forget.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Adrian Bliss: Inside Everyone","instanceDates":"18 September-30 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"487003ANSLKKTVDCKSNVCSQNJKJTBHGPL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-18T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-18T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-30T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-30T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Sketch","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"RRP £10","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Afterthoughts: or Some Pistachios Won't Open by Richard Ayoade - Hardback Edition","instanceDates":"27 June-27 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"705803AQQKLLMCTRGMNRSKBKQNCPLLNKJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-27T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-27T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-27T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-27T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Inspired by hospices, mystics and trips to the cemetery, Age is a Feeling wrestles with our endless chances to change course while we’re alive. A covert rallying cry against cynicism and regret. A call to seize our time.\r\nWritten and performed by Haley McGee, this never-the-same-twice show is a gripping story about how our relationship with mortality shapes the way we live. Charting the seminal moments, rites of passage and turning points in an adult life - your life - from the day you turn 25 through to your death, Age is a Feeling celebrates the glorious and melancholy unknowability of human life.\r\n\r\nFollowing its critically acclaimed premiere at Edinburgh and Soho and transfer to Toronto’s Soulpepper, the Olivier-nominated and Fringe First winning Age Is A Feeling returns to London’s newest venue, Soho Theatre Walthamstow for a strictly limited run.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Age is A Feeling","instanceDates":"5 March-7 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"629003ADBJHCRLLMVGTJDLTJKJLKCLDRJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-05T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-05T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-07T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-07T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Part of National Theatre Connections","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Age is Revolting, created by Abi Zakarian, performed by Plashet School","instanceDates":"30 April-30 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"538803ACJNVLMNVQRBTHTCQPVRSDKGDJB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-30T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-30T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-30T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-30T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Edinburgh Comedy Award Winner Ahir Shah returns to Soho with ENDS: a show about family, immigration, marriage, history, politics, and beans.\r\nHis last Fringe show, 2019’s Dots, is now a special on HBO Max. As seen on Mock the Week, The Mash Report, QI, Live at the Apollo, Frankie Boyle’s New World Order, Have I Got News For You, and 8 Out of 10 Cats Does Countdown.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ahir Shah: Ends","instanceDates":"24 September-28 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"562803AGLBPGPBQJDMRHPKQTHVKHPSNJK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-24T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-24T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-28T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-28T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Political","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Ahir Shah brings the Edinburgh Comedy Award-winning ENDS to Soho Theatre Walthamstow: a show about family, immigration, marriage, history, politics, and beans.\r\nHis last Fringe show, 2019’s Dots, is now a special on HBO Max. As seen on Mock the Week, The Mash Report, QI, Live at the Apollo, Frankie Boyle’s New World Order, Have I Got News For You, and 8 Out of 10 Cats Does Countdown.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":100,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ahir Shah: ENDS","instanceDates":"16 May-16 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"580003APLKLVKJVKLVRMDPJPSSCVRKQNB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-16T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-16T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-16T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-16T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"India/South Asian heritage"},{"description":"Double Edinburgh Comedy Award nominee Ahir Shah returns to Soho with ENDS: a show about family, immigration, marriage, history, politics, and beans.\r\nHis last Fringe show, 2019's DOTS, is now a special on HBO Max. As seen on Mock the Week, The Mash Report, QI, Live at the Apollo, Frankie Boyle's New World Order, Have I Got News For You, and 8 Out of 10 Cats Does Countdown. ***** (Telegraph). **** (Guardian). **** (Times).\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ahir Shah: Ends.","instanceDates":"16 October-27 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"494003AMJRHGVKKQGJCTKRKNPGRTJVGKN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-16T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-16T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-27T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-27T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Political","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"HBO and Netflix star Ahir Shah (Live at the Apollo, Mock The Week, Have I Got News For You, QI) is back with his new stand-up show Golden.\r\nHis last show, Ends, won the prestigious Edinburgh Comedy Award for Best Show, sold out shows across the world, and was recorded as a comedy special for Netflix.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":100,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ahir Shah: Golden","instanceDates":"8 May-8 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"701803AVQHKNJMDBNNNDPPKPSDJQKRLQN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-05-08T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-05-08T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-05-08T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-05-08T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"HBO and Netflix star Ahir Shah (Live at the Apollo, Mock The Week, Have I Got News For You, QI) is back with his new stand-up show Golden. \r\nHis last show, Ends, won the prestigious Edinburgh Comedy Award for Best Show, sold out shows across the world and was recorded as a comedy special for Netflix. \r\nAhir has also been seen and heard on shows including Ahir Shah: Dots (HBO), Jurassic World 3, Foundation (Apple TV), Richard Osman’s House of Games (BBC2), The Last Leg (C4), The Mash Report (BBC2), Frankie Boyle's New World Order (BBC2) and The Now Show (BBCR4). \r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ahir Shah: Golden","instanceDates":"5 October-17 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"702203ASPQQBSLKDTBLSRNMDSJVRVRMDQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-05T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-05T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-17T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-17T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"BAFTA and British Comedy Award-winning Irish stand-up Aisling Bea is finally hitting the road.\r\nWith tales of travel, home, immigration, history, sex, babies, music, lovers and enemies.\r\n\r\nShe will even answer your big life questions. It's not about the destination babes, it's about the journey, but also the destinations are very important, so check out if she is coming to one near YOU.\r\n\r\nAs seen on Taskmaster, QI, 8 Out of 10 Cats, Last One Laughing, Live at the Apollo, Travel Man and creator, writer and star of the award-winning Channel 4 and Hulu series This Way Up.\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"AISLING BEA: OLDER THAN JESUS","instanceDates":"27 February-28 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"637203ANTLHRPLPHRCBVNBCLQRLMNSRRS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-27T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-27T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-28T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-28T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Aisling Bea drops in to Soho Theatre Dean Street to preview (workshop 🤓🫠😬) her new show ahead of her UK & Ireland tour.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Aisling Bea: Work in Progress","instanceDates":"23 February-23 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"694803ALPTKKCSVLVDKMGQSJMBLLTCHDQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-23T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-23T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-23T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-23T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A comic thriller\r\ninspired by H.G. Wells’ The Invisible Man\r\nStrange things are happening in Wellston - a haunted pub quiz, students with demonic powers, a missing woman. NO ONE is a modern re-mix of ‘The Invisible Man’ by H.G. Wells as a touching and comic, high-octane thriller. \r\nThe show balances laughter and tragedy, keeping the audience on the edge of their seats as the thriller unfolds. We blend emotional scenes with fast paced fights and slick movement sequences.\r\nThe story follows Thomas Marvel as he accidentally befriends an invisible man, bringing him fame and fortune, love and violence.\r\nFramed as an investigation by the local police force of the fictional town of Wellston, they question if Griffin truly exists and if he is the violent monster everyone would have us believe.\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Akimbo Theatre: No One","instanceDates":"17 June-17 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"477203ANQQDNHGBGHMRQCJRMKSQTSCHRV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-17T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-17T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-17T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-17T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The nation's favourite Pub Landlord records his brand-new stand-up special across two shows at Soho Theatre Walthamstow!\r\nThere’s no denying the world’s a mess daddio, but there is a glimmer of hope as the Guv brings his like-nobody-else Common Sense hot-takes for the masses, offering a much-needed truth tonic (pint for the fella/glass of white wine for the lady) for these whacked out and troubled times. With a fresh and frothing pint to hand, a barrel of laughs to pour from, and a flower in his heart, Guv is all you need.\r\nAnd for the brave, bold, and plain straight crazy cats amongst you who want to be in on the action in the ‘Splash Zone’, book them quick and wear the damn ponchos!\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Al Murray: Al You Need Is Guv (Live Special Recording)","instanceDates":"26 April-26 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"700803AGRHQNKGRQBMCQCNPTQNTCJCHPT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-26T17:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-26T16:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-26T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-26T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The chance to catch Britain’s favourite publican as he tries out material for his new tour Guv Island.\r\n\r\nThis is a rare opportunity to catch one of Britain’s finest comedians in an intimate setting as he polishes his legendary bar-room banter.\r\n‘A supremely polished performer’ ★★★★★ Mail on Sunday\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Al Murray: Work in Progress","instanceDates":"21 November-22 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"508403ATNPQQDBJNLPTMTHSLMMQJDPSMV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-21T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-21T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-22T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-22T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join Alan Carr as he tries out new material with some of his comedy friends.\r\n14+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Alan Carr & Friends","instanceDates":"7 March-7 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"687803AJCLGGPCQHMMJDMSSVQNDDMRPRL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-07T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-07T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-07T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-07T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"He thinks he’s Marty McFly but he’s older than Doc Brown. He spends more time in the pharmacy than the gym. Subject to relentless eye rolls from his kids. What is he? A late middle-aged stand up on tour for the first time in a decade. Funnier than ever, he says.\r\nAlan Davies is a critically acclaimed stand-up comedian, actor, writer, and TV personality. He is a staple of British television, known for his performance as the eponymous hero of David Renwick’s hugely popular, long-running TV series Jonathan Creek, and as a permanent panellist on QI. His talk show, Alan Davies: As Yet Untitled, recently reached its seventh season. He is also one of the UK’s best-loved comedians. His stand-up show Urban Trauma ran in London’s West End and Life is Pain and Little Victories sold out in venues across the UK. His second memoir, Just Ignore Him, was published in 2020 and the third instalment, White Male Stand-Up, was published last year. 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":130,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Alan Davies: Think Ahead","instanceDates":"3 October-3 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"743403ASPBGRLMPCKGQKSDSMNVRDKTHTM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-03T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-03T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-03T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-03T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Alana Jackson, winner of So You Think You're Funny? 2024 brings her debut show Last Orders to Soho theatre, after a sell out run at the Edinburgh fringe. \r\nTales of being from Glasgow, moving to London, going to drama school and working/drinking in pubs, Alana tells all, bringing to life the characters she's met along the way. \r\nFest magazine described the show as ‘rich in charisma and wit’ with one4review adding ‘the show was a hoot from start to finish, the sell out audience were kept laughing all the way through.’\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Alana Jackson: Last Orders","instanceDates":"13 February-13 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"683004ANTCRNHCKBPSMLKGBQQVLDDQGRS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-13T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-13T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-13T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-13T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Alex Bertulis-Fernandes (British Comedy Guide Pro Award Winner, Channel 4 Sean Lock Award Finalist, BBC New Comedy Awards Nominee) presents an hour about the worst year of her life (so far). \r\nLonglisted for the ISH Edinburgh Comedy Awards Best Newcomer and shortlisted for the ISH Edinburgh Comedy Awards Best Joke of the Fringe. \r\nWarning: This show contains content you may find distressing. If you don’t, you have a cold, cold heart. Previous subjects discussed include (in order of popularity): dating, dogs, death, body image, sexual harassment and suicide. It's gonna be a riot. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Alex Bertulis-Fernandes: May Find Distressing (Work In Progress)","instanceDates":"11 February-11 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"683204AJJBVKCJVDTKBTBPTNGNHVNRQGD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-11T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-11T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-11T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-11T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"One of the most critically hailed comedians of his generation, Alex Edelman is best known for solo shows that blur the line between his stand-up comedy roots and narrative-driven storytelling.His last offering, JUST FOR US, played more than 500 performances all over the world - including acclaimed runs off- and on-Broadway. It premiered as an HBO original comedy special in April of 2024, earning him a place on the Time 100 list, a Tony Award, and an Emmy Award for Best Writing for a Variety Special. Edelman appeared in Jerry Seinfeld’s directorial debut for Netflix, UNFROSTED. Beyond stand-up, he writes regularly for TV and can currently seen starring in Peacock’s The Paper, a Greg Daniels-helmed spiritual successor to The Office. He also writes on the show as a Consulting Producer.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Alex Edelman: What Are You Going To Do","instanceDates":"30 June-3 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"712203AKKPKHHPMGTBNGPVRTCGDQLVTTH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-30T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-30T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-03T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-03T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"In 2024, trans girl Alex (me) started HRT. Now she (me) feels the most alive she's (me's) ever felt; and she wants to make you feel alive too, or die trying.\r\nA ludicrous, musical, chaotic, joyful show about the colours of the world becoming slowly brighter and giving people furniture via the tube. Also being trans.\r\nDirected by Dom Stephens.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Alex Franklin: Gurl Code","instanceDates":"14 April-15 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"595203AGPSBRJQCPSQGVSNKNVBMJPHSDQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-14T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-14T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-15T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-15T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"What if we kissed? Right now? Xx xXx Xx xxX XX xx (*kissing*) Wow. That was wonderful. Until we meet again. 'Proper star in the making' (Chortle), Alex (me), has a show just for you (you) about kissing (x) and romance (<3) and dating (:O) and kissing (x). Also the fetishisation and demonisation of trans bodies BLAH BLAH BLAH but mostly kissing xx. Maybe even about us? Kissing each other? Haha no way, just kissi- kidding. Just kidding!...xx Brighton Fringe Best Comedy Show Nominee 2024. As seen/heard on Channel 4, HBO Max, BBC Radio 4. 16+ (Sexually explicit themes, references to homophobia and transphobia - see webpage for current content advice).","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Alex Franklin: Kiss Me x","instanceDates":"26 October-28 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"750603AHQLBHJVMKQMMPTSTBQTKJCCNLS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-26T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-26T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-28T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-28T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"After a 5-star, sell-out run at the Edinburgh Fringe, the \"almost sexily cerebral\" (★★★★ Daily Telegraph) stand-up Alex Kealy is taking his new stand-up show about fear on a national tour.\r\nOne of the country's most exciting up-and-coming stand-ups, Alex has been the tour support for Jack Dee, Shaparak Khorsandi, Tom Rosenthal and Kieran Hodgson.\r\n\r\nAlong with Ivo Graham, he hosts hit podcast Gig Pigs, which regularly topped the music podcasts charts during its first 2 seasons, as well as being featured in The Guardian's readers' Top 10 Podcasts of 2023.\r\n\r\nHis sharp joke-writing and political takes have been featured on multiple guest appearances on BBC Radio 4's The Now Show as well as Catherine Bohart's TL;DR and Rhys James's What Are You Talking About (both Radio 4). He's also been a regular writer for Mock The Week and The News Quiz.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Alex Kealy: The Fear","instanceDates":"25 June-26 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"609803AGJPNKLGPGCCLKJBVTQTDLBSJRP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-25T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-25T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-26T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-26T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join comedy equivalent of sunshine Alex Prescot for a delightful debut hour that's tailor-made for each audience. Expect a warm and fuzzy blend of joyful musical comedy and quick-witted improvisation. Don't expect his notably absent double-act partner. \r\nBest-Reviewed Edinburgh Fringe Shows 2025 (British Comedy Guide) \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Alex Prescot: Cosy","instanceDates":"12 February-12 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"683403APVKDLMMNGGKTQGKMBTKBBVMGPH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-12T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-12T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-12T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-12T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Do you have a critical inner voice? Join Alexander as he interrogates his own, tries to kill it, then comes for yours. A show about hating yourself and, amongst other things, choosing not to.\r\nAlexander hosts the high-concept podcast Born Yesterday with Andy Barr, is the creator of the cult comedy game show Hell To Play and regularly works with the acclaimed Alternative Comedy Memorial Society and Weirdos collectives. He was a key player in Mark Watson’s Comedy Marathon, was nominated at the Leicester Comedy Awards as part of Consignia and co-orchestrated a huge charity event at the Pleasance Grand in Edinburgh called Dan Vs Food, in which a cast of 25+ comedians (including Ed Gamble, Iain Stirling, Nick Helm, Sophie Duker and Ivo Graham) watched a man called Dan eat his lunch. He has recently appeared on Radio 4, Insane in the Men Brain, Shame is Delicious and The Comedian's Comedian podcast. Alexander has filmed several stand-up specials and has been a guest lecturer at the Royal College of Art and Fourth Monkey Theatre Company.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Alexander Bennett: I Can’t Stand the Man, Myself","instanceDates":"29 April-30 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"524203ADCKGGHLGQNPRMLQJRMCNHVJVLH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-29T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-29T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-30T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-30T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"a love letter to all the DIVAS and the GAYS who stan them! welcome to an original queer musical comedy about alexis's childhood as a stan. after moving to rural germany from new york city at age 8, discovering pop divas online was his only salvation... now he's ready to sing about it! join alexis for this edinburgh fringe preview as he attempts to get his p.h.diva in stanology, with a concentration in motherological studies and a minor in slayviation. does this queer bo burnham have what it takes to be... a lil gay diva?!\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Alexis Sakellaris: A Stan is Born (Edinburgh Preview)","instanceDates":"20 July-20 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"562003AGSQQTCMBQSSSQHRCLQQNLPMQCQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-20T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-20T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-20T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-20T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"LGBTQ+","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"Here. A little something from Alfie Packham. Enjoy this gift of a show that unwraps love, death and less thematic stuff like shoplifting, football and milk. 'As thought provoking as it is hilarious' (ThreeWeeks).16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Alfie Packham: My Gift to You","instanceDates":"19 February-19 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"589803ADNGMLBLBSDDSLBRLLSPLJHGKKM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-19T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-19T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-19T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-19T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"Nominated for the Comedians' Choice Beast Show 2022. Ali Brice is embracing life after almost losing it. Three years on, he's admitted defeat and is back on his feet and trying again. Through therapy, friends and... sausages, he's living in the moment and celebrating the little things life has to offer. A sincere, heartfelt, and happy show. Expect silly stories, big questions, and jokes aplenty from a ridiculous man with a stupid moustache. \r\n'Ali Brice is funny' (The List). \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ali Brice: I Tried To Be Funny, But You Weren't Looking","instanceDates":"3 July-4 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"461603AQBMDQGSVKRGCSQGLCTJNGTVNMJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-03T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-03T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-04T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-04T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Fresh from her word of mouth hit at Edinburgh Fringe a busy corporate woman comes to Soho Theatre.\r\nFresh from her word of mouth hit at Edinburgh Fringe a busy corporate woman comes to Soho Theatre.\r\nMeet Susan. She showered before she came. She hopes you did too...  she works in an office but nobody really knows what she does there… but she does something. Tippy tippy tap tap tap tapppyahhgauyhjrghsmunrifnf&$+%#$$\\#\r\nImportant business stuff, woman working really hard at her job. \r\nSusan has high expectations. Of this job? Of this show? Of your life? Of everything ever. Well it's everything you'll ever dream of and more too. It's kind of clown. Kind of not. Stupid. Important. Unhinged. Chaotic. Outrageous. Messy. Gritty. Real-life drama. Never been done before. \r\nCreated by Alice Cockayne\r\nAssociate director and dramaturg Tanika Lay-Meachen \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Alice Cockayne: I Showered Before I Came","instanceDates":"10 November-29 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"502403ARVMDKDTHPTQGGHKQKBRGKMSVPS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-10T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-10T22:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-29T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-29T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Ratty wig girl. Business b*tch. Working momma. Tippy tap tap queen Alice Cockayne is back with an hour of intellectual prophecy.\r\nStrap in for a whirlwind of pure late-night nonsense that will leave you thinking about this night for the rest of your life. \r\n\r\nAlice is a writer and performer for BBC Radio 4's Time of the Week. British Comedy Guide's Top 20 shows 2023. Nominated for Best Newcomer at the ISH Edinburgh Comedy Awards.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Alice Cockayne: Licensed. Professional. Trained. Qualified.","instanceDates":"24 September-27 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"653403AMPLPDDQSMKTKCVKBTJCDGVSRDS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-24T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-24T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-27T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-27T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A Comedy Show About Writing A Book About Romance\r\nAlice Fraser has fallen in love… with romance novels. She’s written a delirious love letter to the genre and now she has to live with the consequences. \r\nIf you love romance novels, or if you have no idea how anyone could love romance novels, this is the show for you. \r\nA show that will make you laugh, cry, and rethink happily ever after. \r\n(With a guest appearance from the reclusive, mysterious, interdimensionally successful and arguably fictional self published romance maven and online bestseller, D’Ancey LaGuarde)\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Alice Fraser: A Passion For Passion","instanceDates":"6 August-9 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"620803ATCMDJGRVVBKLKGJKKHVSBPTNNN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-06T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-06T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-09T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-09T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Tumble down the rabbit hole into the fantastical world of Wonderland, where up is down, and nonsense reigns supreme!\r\nJoin Alice on her unforgettable adventure as she shrinks and grows, meeting peculiar characters at every turn. Who will she encounter next? Will the mischievous Cheshire Cat guide her through the madness? Can the hurried White Rabbit help her uncover the secrets she’s searching for? And could the Queen of Hearts cause her to truly lose her head?\r\n This internationally celebrated production brings Lewis Carroll’s delightful chaos to life with extraordinary puppets, exquisite costumes and an original score that will captivate audiences of all ages. With creative stagecraft that will leave you spellbound, this visually breathtaking experience is a “must-see” for families seeking an enchanting escape.\r\n5+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Alice in Wonderland ","instanceDates":"5 August-16 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"710603AKGQBTLGSCBNVGPRCKJKHQGNQKB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-05T14:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-05T13:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-16T15:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-16T14:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Families","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"After years away from stand-up (due to the global pandemic and a lack of interest in being out late), the co-writer and co-director of BBC and HBO's Starstruck returns with a brand-new show!\r\nHighly Credible will cover: Alice's life in the last three years; her car getting stolen; fertility; a bit of gay stuff (yet to be written but feels pretty likely). 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Alice Snedden: Highly Credible","instanceDates":"22 April-26 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"600603AVTTLCQRJLTGRCLCCDVLPJHVRPG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-22T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-22T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-26T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-26T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Following a run at Edinburgh Fringe, Alison Larkin returns to Soho with her ‘improbably funny’ and life-affirming  show about love, loss and hope.\r\nFollowing its world premiere at Edinburgh Fringe, Alison Larkin previews her ‘improbably funny’, life-affirming show about love, loss and hope.\r\n ‘Alison Larkin is hugely entertaining… marvellously light-footed’ Times\r\nThe English-American writer/comedian returns to the UK with the world premiere of her funny, life-affirming show about love, loss and hope. Alison found true love for the first time in her 50s with an Indian climate scientist who had also immigrated to the US. Then he died. Then something wildly unexpected happened. When Archbishop Desmond Tutu found out about it, he insisted she write this show “because it will bring hope.”\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Alison Larkin: Grief… a Comedy","instanceDates":"27 August-31 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"560203ARHTBTPTNNPBCNHVPHCMQJVHMRH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-27T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-27T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-31T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-31T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Ahead of a run at Edinburgh Fringe, Alison Larkin previews her ‘improbably funny’ and life-affirming  show about love, loss and hope.\r\nThe English-American writer/comedian returns to the UK with the world premiere of this 'improbably funny, life-affirming, bright bauble of a piece' about love, loss and hope (Berkshire Eagle). Alison found true love for the first time in her 50s with an Indian climate scientist who had also immigrated to the US. Then he died. Then something wildly unexpected happened. When Archbishop Desmond Tutu found out about it, he insisted she write this show. So if you don't like it, you can blame him. Music by Gary Schreiner. 'Alison Larkin is hugely entertaining... marvellously light-footed' (Times).\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Alison Larkin: Grief… a Comedy (Edinburgh Preview)","instanceDates":"27 July-27 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"550803ATMBLSTKVGSQKKDDHGTSMPKGPSS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-27T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-27T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-27T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-27T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Alison Larkin returns to Soho Theatre with this ‘improbably funny’ and life-affirming  show about love, loss and hope. \r\nThe British writer/comedian found true love for the first time in her 50’s with an Indian climate scientist who had also immigrated to the US. Then he died. Then something wildly unexpected happened.  When Archbishop Desmond Tutu found out about it, he insisted she write this show. So if you don’t like it, you can blame him. \r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Alison Larkin: Grief… a Comedy.","instanceDates":"6 November-8 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"492003AQQRQQBHRGKDQTTHJGKBJJHVBNM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-06T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-06T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-08T14:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-08T14:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"The award-winning sellout smash hit show of this summer’s Edinburgh Fringe comes to London for the first time!\r\nA man told Alison to sit down and now she's doing a whole stand up show about it. \r\n\r\nWinner of the Comedian’s Choice Award for Best Show 2025.\r\nWinner of the Comedy Poster Awards 2025.\r\n\r\nAlison has made appearances on House of Games, Celebrity Goggle Box and Pointless Celebrities, and on the popular podcasts Off Menu, The Gargle and Trusty Hogs. \r\n\r\nShe is the co-host of her new podcast Magazine Party, and has also co-hosted Wheel of Misfortune and Guilty Feminist. \r\n\r\nYou may have also seen Alison as the support act for Fern Brady, Rob Delaney and Maria Bamford on tour.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Alison Spittle: BIG","instanceDates":"2 December-6 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"659003ARDMBSQLNJPNKJGLBNNHVLJTKBK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-02T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-02T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-06T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-06T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Comedian du jour Alison Spittle is simmering with jokes and probably rage, she doesn't know what the burning sensation is. This silly goose has appeared on Off Menu, You're Dead To Me, Guilty Feminist, The Gargle. She's the co-host of BBC Sounds' hugely popular Wheel of Misfortune podcast with Kerry Katona. Voted one of British Comedy Guide's best reviewed artists of the Fringe, Alison - formerly tour support for Maria Bamford and Fern Brady - heads out on her own.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Alison Spittle: Soup","instanceDates":"20 March-23 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"511403ASQJVMNBSGCLVBGMQRSSTDQNHVC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-20T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-20T21:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-23T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-23T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Fresh off the back of a complete sell out run at The Edinburgh Fringe and voted one of the best reviewed shows in the comedy section, Alison is diving into her debut at The Soho Theatre. Alison loves to do star jumps in the water. She also likes to watch people fight in chip shops. Her two worlds collide as a fight breaks out in aqua-aerobics and she's never felt so alive. When the foam settles, Alison realises she's an outwardly nice person who lives for confrontation. Host of BBC Sounds Wheel of Misfortune, The Guilty Feminist podcast and writer for Have I Got News For You. 'A kind of genius' **** (Irish Times). Praise for WET Pow! Showbiz ★★★★★ One4Review ★★★★.5 The Skinny ★★★★ Broadway Baby ★★★★ Entertainment Now ★★★★ The List ★★★★\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Alison Spittle: Wet","instanceDates":"10 May-10 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"432803AMGTRMTLJSTRJNVKSPPJRPBQHBS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-10T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-10T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-10T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-10T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"It's personal, not political. An all-singing, all-dancing comedy cabaret ... about abortion.\r\nIn a bracing, booming and brash autobiographical tale of pro-choice, Award-winning performer, writer and activist Lilly Burton asks: have you ever just closed your eyes and hoped that it’ll all just go away? \r\nThis show is for the people who felt lonely, guilty, relieved - or nothing at all. For the people who think about it often and the people who don’t. For the boy who never knew, for the girl who never said and for anyone who didn’t know how to ask about Abortion. Bringing you a cry-to-arms that will have you slamming down your pints in support of reproductive rights. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"All Aboard! At Termination Station by Lilly Burton","instanceDates":"15 February-15 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"522004AVHVCJHQVQQSNHRMBRKTLDRRNMB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-15T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-15T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-15T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-15T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Kiri Pritchard-McLean (QI, 8 Out Of 10 Cats) and Rachel Fairburn (House of Games, Live At The Apollo) are here to take it to the next level with a Halloween outing of their smash-hit true crime comedy podcast All Killa No Filla!\r\nIt’s the most macabre time of the year… and Kiri Pritchard-McLean (QI, 8 Out Of 10 Cats) and Rachel Fairburn (House of Games, Live At The Apollo) are here to take it to the next level with a Halloween outing of their smash-hit true crime comedy podcast All Killa No Filla!\r\n\r\nJoin the two acclaimed stand-ups for the event of the year - a very special live edition of All Killa No Filla at the brand new (and soon to be iconic) Soho Theatre Walthamstow.\r\n\r\nAll the Legends know that that means: an evening of true-crime chinwagging, ill-advised fancy dress, and a couple of hours of chat that in other circumstances would be considered slander and/or oversharing. \r\n\r\nNever been to an All Killa No Filla live show before? There’s no revision required. Get your best fancy dress out of the attic (not compulsory) and prepare to see two hilarious and outspoken stand-ups at the top of their game.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"All Killa No Filla: Live - At Halloween!","instanceDates":"30 October-30 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"630003AJKVLCJDBKNLPDQLGCGJMRQDMTN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-30T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-30T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-30T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-30T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":80,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"All The Happy Things","instanceDates":"8 April-26 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"599603AHBRPRMKQHRJJRBCTBDQDGHBTNS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-08T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-08T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-26T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-26T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"ALOK returns with their most intimate show yet: a comedy about love, heartbreak, and the end times with razor-sharp wit.\r\nInternationally condemned stand-up comedian ALOK returns with their most intimate show yet: a comedy about love, heartbreak, and the end times. Their therapist said stop dating projects, so they built one and are charging admission. A journey of self-discovery… and poor decision-making. With razor-sharp wit, ALOK dissects desire, denial, and the stories we tell ourselves to keep going. Suffering is universal. It might as well be funny. ALOK (they/them) is an internationally acclaimed poet, comedian, public speaker, and actor. ALOK’s literary works “Beyond the Gender Binary,” “Femme in Public,” and “Your Wound, My Garden,” have garnered global recognition. Their dynamic presence has captivated audiences in over 40 countries, with sold-out shows at the Edinburgh Fringe Festival and the Netflix is a Joke Festival. ALOK’s first comedy special BIOLOGY! was executive produced by Christopher Guest. They are the subject of the docu-short “ALOK” executive produced by Jodie Foster and directed by Alex Hedison, which made its debut at the Sundance Film Festival in 2024. On screen, they can also be seen in Complicated Order, The Trans List, and Absolute Dominion. On television, they can be seen on HBO’s Sex Lives of College Girls, Sort Of and Random Acts of Flyness, Hulu’s Planet Sex with Cara Delevingne, and Netflix’s Gender Agenda Comedy Special and Getting Curious with Jonathan Van Ness.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"ALOK: Eat Pray Leave","instanceDates":"6 December-6 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"741203AJLNNNJRPSBCVJSJNCCSGTPRGBD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-06T18:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-06T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-06T18:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-06T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Sake Katana The fastest sword in Japan Lost in Western lands A warm and mischievous comedy about honour, identity and very Western problems. He must learn strange new customs, find love and friendships, and to prove he’s still the fastest sword in the country. ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Alvin Liu: Sake Katana","instanceDates":"4 February-4 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"686203AJBKBCCPVDSRLCSGHSSRBTJRBNQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-04T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-04T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-04T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-04T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"ISH Comedy Award Best Newcomer and rapping sensation Amelia Hamilton presents her debut hour of comedy. Set to an original soundtrack of live rap, Hamilton brings her character blend of wit, charm, and musical talent in this high-energy stand-up hour with 'a proper gag in every line' (Chortle). She hilariously delves into relatable rap battles with her own intrusive thoughts, campaigns for women in STEM, and questions how not to be forgotten. \r\n\r\nA featured artist on BBC iPlayer and BBC Radio, Runner Up Komedia New Comedy Awards 2024, BBC New Comedy Awards Nominee 2024, Amelia Hamilton breaks the mould.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Amelia Hamilton: Forget Me Not","instanceDates":"2 January-3 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"672603ARTRLSVVNJKHNQGSBHKBKJPKDNR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-02T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-02T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-03T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-03T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Finish this sentence: \r\n\r\nAmy Annette _______________\r\n\r\na) was called an old soul, as a child (because you can't say 'what happened to this child')\r\nb) was described as a 'Fun Aunt', recently (despite no nieces or nephews to speak of)\r\nc) is \"gregarious, enthusiastic, communicative, gossipy and slightly naughty, ensuring she’s convivial company over an hour that whips by.\" (Chortle ★★★★)\r\nd) was in the 'Best Reviewed Shows' 2025 with her show about social labels 'Busy Body' \r\ne) is a fan of pointless lists as a format for communicating self-promotion cutely...\r\n6) is \"a delight to behold\" (Guardian ★★★★)\r\nVII) all of the above\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Amy Annette: Busy Body Jun26","instanceDates":"16 June-17 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"721403ADLVVVJMJDNCPNLMVDJLJSNTGBK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-16T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-16T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-17T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-17T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Finish this sentence: \r\n\r\nAmy Annette _______________\r\n\r\na) was called an old soul, as a child (because you can't say 'what happened to this child')\r\nb) was described as a 'Fun Aunt', recently (despite no nieces or nephews to speak of)\r\nc) is \"gregarious, enthusiastic, communicative, gossipy and slightly naughty, ensuring she’s convivial company over an hour that whips by.\" (Chortle ★★★★)\r\nd) was in the 'Best Reviewed Shows' 2025 with her show about social labels 'Busy Body' \r\ne) is a fan of pointless lists as a format for communicating self-promotion cutely...\r\n6) is \"a delight to behold\" (Guardian ★★★★)\r\nVII) all of the above\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Amy Annette: Busy Body.","instanceDates":"28 January-31 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"666003ASMVQTGTCVRSQGPMCSSTVBGMNCQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-28T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-28T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-31T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-31T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Fresh from a SOLD-OUT RUN at the Edinburgh Fringe, with EXTRA DATES added, Amy Annette brings her debut show to the Soho Theatre.\r\nThe noughties are back, which is good and bad. But mostly bad. Body image - bad, but original Sugababes line up - good! \r\nAmy is ready to arm you with tales, and tricks, to survive the worst of the 00s, in 2025. THICK SKIN is big fun, from a big gal. \r\nTHICK SKIN is about being a weird teenager, Trinny and Susannah, Girls Magazines, Collective nouns (“that trusty comedic watering hole from which all stand-ups must occasionally sip on their long journeys across the plains” ?! CHORTLE) And more!  \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Amy Annette: Thick Skin","instanceDates":"23 January-25 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"582203ABGKGGRNSLCJCQLPLGKVMRRRGTJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-23T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-23T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-25T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-25T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Amy Gledhill – quadruple Edinburgh Comedy Award nominee, National Comedy Award nominee and 1/3 of cult double act The Delightful Sausage – brings her award-winning solo show back to Soho Theatre for an extended run.  \r\nAmy is a multi award-winning comedian, actor and writer, and is the only act ever to be nominated for the prestigious Edinburgh Comedy Award twice in the same year. Following her hugely successful debut show, The Girl Before The Girl You Marry, Amy Gledhill’s back with a brand new show about self-confidence, romance and bin bags.\r\nAs seen on Live at the Apollo, Would I Lie to You?, The Jonathan Ross Show, Never Mind the Buzzcocks, 8 Out of 10 Cats Does Countdown and many more. She is also co-host of hit podcasts Northern News (featured in The Guardian’s Best Podcasts of 2023) and Single Ladies In Your Area, and as an actor has starred in Sex Education, Alma's Not Normal, Hull Raisers and many more. 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Amy Gledhill: Make Me Look Fit on the Poster","instanceDates":"27 January-8 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"577203AJQTLNDJNQSKLQTMVGHJNLQHCGP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-27T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-27T21:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-08T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-08T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Amy Gledhill – quadruple Edinburgh Comedy Award nominee, National Comedy Award nominee and 1/3 of cult double act The Delightful Sausage – returns to Soho Theatre with a brand new show about self-confidence, romance and bin bags.\r\nAmy is a multi award-winning comedian, actor and writer, and is the only act ever to be nominated for the prestigious Edinburgh Comedy Award twice in the same year. Following her hugely successful debut show, The Girl Before The Girl You Marry, Amy Gledhill returns with another stand-up offering. \r\nAs seen on Would I Lie to You?, The Jonathan Ross Show, Never Mind the Buzzcocks, 8 Out of 10 Cats Does Countdown and many more. She is also co-host of hit podcast Northern News (featured in The Guardian’s Best Podcasts of 2023), and as an actor has starred in Sex Education, Alma's Not Normal, Hull Raisers and many more.\r\nEdinburgh Comedy Awards 2024 | Best Show Nominee\r\nISH Edinburgh Comedy Awards 2024 | Best Show Nominee\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Amy Gledhill: Make Me Look Fit on the Poster.","instanceDates":"3 September-7 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"568403ANRHQKKMCBHKRVPBPLCTKQGCKNT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-03T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-03T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-07T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-07T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Amy Gledhill has appeared on the biggest comedy shows on TV, won the most prestigious award in live comedy AND starred in a Netflix blockbuster…\r\nThen why can't she nail just one first date, social interaction or trip to the spa? (She is now banned) Join the Taskmaster alumnus, Last One Laughing’s cruellest red card, and co-host of smash-hit podcasts Single Ladies In Your Area and Northern News on her brand new stand-up tour, as Amy Gledhill says Thanks For Having Me to audiences up and down the country. Amy won the Edinburgh Comedy Award in 2024, is triple Edinburgh Comedy Award nominee, National Comedy Award nominee and 1/3 of cult double act The Delightful Sausage. She’s also appeared on Live at the Apollo (BBC), Would I Lie To You? (BBC), The Jonathan Ross Show (ITV), Never Mind The Buzzcocks (Sky), Run Away (Netflix), Alma’s Not Normal (BBC) and 8 Out of 10 Cats Does Countdown (C4).\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Amy Gledhill: Thanks For Having Me","instanceDates":"27 February-27 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"709803AKKRDJVCVGJVTJCVCHVVDLBPMHB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-27T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-27T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-27T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-27T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Dave's Edinburgh Comedy Awards Best Newcomer Nominee 2022 Intranet sensation Amy Gledhill (1/3 of cult double act The Delightful Sausage) brings her Dave's Edinburgh Comedy Award nominated show about resilience and dancing - two of the best things - to Soho Theatre. \r\nAs seen on: Hypothetical (Dave), The Stand Up Sketch Show (ITV2), Alma’s Not Normal (BBC2), Late Night Mash (Dave), The Emily Atack Show (ITV2), Richard Ayoade’s Question Team (Dave) and Harry Hill’s Clubnite (Channel 4).\r\n‘Joyous hour… remember Gledhill’s name, because it’s about to be everywhere’ ★★★★★ Independent \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Amy Gledhill: The Girl Before the Girl You Marry","instanceDates":"19 April-22 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"415204ASLNQTLKJJLTPGCJNBBHSHVNSCH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-19T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-19T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-22T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-22T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"When Amy Mason got hacked, she lost her number, bank account and social media access. And then the hackers started sending her gifts...\r\nA surprising, somewhat filthy dive into connection, intimacy, and the perils of using your dead cat's name as your password for literally everything. \r\nBehold! is a silly yet razor-witted examination of digital dependency, friendship and community, delivered with Amy Mason’s signature blend of off-kilter storytelling and deadpan warmth. \r\nAs heard on Radio 1, Radio 5 and Radio 4. Guardian's Top 10 Funniest Jokes of Edinburgh Fringe 2024. \r\nDirected by Jessica Fostekew.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":55,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Amy Mason: Behold!","instanceDates":"27 April-29 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"692803APJRRRVVNQRTLNSPNCKCLBKHRBS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-27T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-27T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-29T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-29T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"After an unsettling encounter with a wildlife enthusiast, the Funny Women Award finalist and one of the Guardian's 10 Funniest Jokes of the Edinburgh Fringe 2024 - Amy Mason - explores what it means to be a human animal (nightmare tbh).\r\nA \"cheekily boundary-pushing\" (Scotsman) debut hour from the brilliant comedian and writer. Expect coming out in your 30s, rinsing homophobes, and forming a coven with your kids. Over 11 million views on TikTok, as heard on BBC Radio 1, Radio 5, Radio 4.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Amy Mason: Free Mason","instanceDates":"10 May-10 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"612203ARGMJGKJVHJKJCQBTRMVCMMNHMD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-10T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-10T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-10T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-10T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Amy doesn’t get angry and she’s starting to feel left out, so she’s on a quest to feel fury; from what she can discern from the world around her, it appears to be all the rage… literally. Amy is navigating the joy of her first queer relationship whilst dusting herself off from a string of several alcoholic partners. You’d think she’d have plenty to be cross about, and yet, whilst everyone seems to be more furious than ever, she just can’t seem to tap into her own anger - so she’s challenged herself to learn. This lack of wrath may also have something to do with a processing lag that is becoming increasingly disruptive - and comical - in her life. Her emotions seemed to be delivered by carrier pigeon, if they arrive at all. This is a show about being Best Supporting Actor in one’s own life, queer joy, and how a potion from 2002 cursed the world.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Amy Matthews: Definitions of Toast","instanceDates":"10 December-12 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"759003ANGSCHTGTHHDPGTGTLMKNTBMVBB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-10T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-10T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-12T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-12T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Amy spins a sparkling web of comedy magic between the two states she finds herself caught between – stability and restlessness. She swings between the unbridled joy in the freedom that everything can change and the crawling anxiety that nothing is certain. This is a show about the thrill of falling and the thud of landing. And after a thud comes a laugh. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Amy Matthews: I Feel Like I’m Made of Spiders","instanceDates":"18 March-19 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"525403AKTMTDDSSKJMTDGJMGHHTVKDJDT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-18T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-18T21:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-19T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-19T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Written and performed by François Pandolfo\r\n\r\nA one-man-cat-drag-late-night comedy. \r\nThe last chapter in the autobiography of infamous feline movie star Milly-Liu. The cat's out of the bag and Milly-Liu is ready to spill the beans on all your favourite celebrity pussies.  She's worked with the best of them, and been to bed with the rest of them!  Come join her (if you dare), but be warned, she'll throw you round like a half dead mouse.  And FFS don't mention David Attenborough! \r\n \r\nDirected by Dan Jones.  \r\n\r\n‘Has the makings of a cabaret legend.’ **** The Stage\r\n \r\nWINNER: The David Johnson Emerging Talent Award 2022\r\n‘Written and skilfully performed with a genuine sense of danger by François Pandolfo, the sort of quintessential Fringe experience that David would have loved - bonkers and filthy yet oddly moving.’ John Mackay\r\n\r\nContent warning\r\n\r\nThis show contains audience participation, strong language, scenes of a sexual nature, nudity, drug use and vomiting, references to paedophilia, sexual assault, violence, animal harm / bestiality, death, ableist language and misogynistic language\r\n\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"An Audience with Milly-Liu","instanceDates":"1 April-1 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"433803ADMVLJDGRDNKTLSCSJLCLDDLDVJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-01T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-01T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-01T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-01T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Join Felix White – The Maccabees, Sunday Times bestselling author, co-host of the much-loved cricket podcast Tailenders and film composer – for a one-off evening that fuses football, memoir, and music to celebrate his new book Whatever Will Be, Will Be: A Matter of Life and Football. \r\nWhatever Will Be, Will Be finds Felix on the cusp of 40, on tour, and reflecting on his past. Felix will share how a spontaneous decision to watch Penrith Town face Pickering Town in the FA Cup’s very first round set him on an extraordinary mission: to follow the whole journey of the world's most historic cup competition, all the way to Wembley. \r\n\r\n  \r\n\r\nAlong the way, he introduces us to the characters who give English football its heart, revealing how the game offers focus, community, and (often misguided) hope. In his hands, the FA Cup becomes more than a competition: it’s a lens on belonging, obsession, aging, childhood, work addiction, and the messy art of finding meaning in modern life. \r\n\r\n  \r\n\r\nIn this special evening, Felix will weave together memoir  and matchday magic. Expect live music too, as Felix goes beyond Whatever Will Be, Will Be to discuss and perform the endless correlations between music and sport in his work. \r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"An Evening with Felix White","instanceDates":"28 October-28 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"657003AMSRKLPCBRTMLVSHJTBDKHCVNNN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-28T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-28T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-28T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-28T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"You know the name. You know the carnage. Now he's coming to tell you about it in person.\r\nSuper Hans is back—and with his debut novel Moreish in hand, there's no Jez around to talk him out of it\r\nExpect tales of bad trips, deep thoughts, and absolute bangers. From meeting 'The One' in a Berlin nightclub, to attempting to run a moped rental business in Macedonia and getting banned in multiple countries—all while somehow remaining the world's greatest superstar DJ.\r\nEqual parts riotous comedy, unreliable travelogue, and strangely heartfelt memoir. No filter, no agenda—just 100% pure, distilled Hans. \r\nBut behind every great disaster is an even greater man. In the second half, Super Hans's alter ego—the rather more respectable comedian, writer and actor Matt King—joins the stage for an in-conversation special, delving into comedy, his remarkable career, and the making of the iconic BAFTA award-winning Peep Show.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":false,"name":"An Evening with Matt King AKA Super Hans","instanceDates":"22 September-22 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"711203AQRHNBJPPHLKJSKPRRHKTBVQRGT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-22T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-22T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-22T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-22T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"There’ll be drums, stories and more. He wants you to kick back, relax and let him take you on a journey. It'd be a shame if someone were to ruin it...\r\nThere’ll be drums, stories and more. He wants you to kick back, relax and let him take you on a journey. It'd be a shame if someone were to ruin it...\r\n\r\n“We do not really mean that what we’re about to say is true. A story, a story; let it come, let it go.”\r\n\r\nKwami invites you for a chilled night of storytelling. Combining the Ghanaian folk tales called Anansi stories and stories from his own life, it should be a lot of fun. Join us for Kwami Odoom's debut play with live drumming and good vibes.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Anansi And Other Such Stories by Kwami Odoom","instanceDates":"21 February-22 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"590003ASKMHQTMRSPRTBPPTLBPLHDHSGQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-21T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-21T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-22T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-22T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"There’ll be drums, loop pedals, stories and more. He wants you to kick back, relax and let him take you on a journey. It'd be a shame if someone were to ruin it... \r\n“We do not really mean that what we’re about to say is true. A story, a story; let it come, let it go.”\r\nKwami invites you for a chilled night of storytelling. Combining the Ghanaian folk tales called Anansi stories and stories from his own life, it should be a lot of fun. \r\nThis is a script in hand rehearsed reading of Kwami Odoom's debut play, written on Soho Writers Lab.\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Anansi and Other Such Stories by Kwami Odoom.","instanceDates":"17 February-17 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"521604APNVDTQTRQMMVRGTDTHSPDNGMDR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-17T15:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-17T15:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-17T15:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-17T15:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"New Writing","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A sticky, spooky horror comedy about gender-reveal parties, demons from hell, and a Gay Witch Sex Cult (a sex cult for gay witches). \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Andrew Doherty: Gay Witch Sex Cult","instanceDates":"6 February-8 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"585203ANNNDVJTNDSGSKTRGRMHLHQJBVQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-06T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-06T22:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-08T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-08T22:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A sticky, spooky horror comedy about gender reveal parties, demons from hell, and above all, a Gay Witch Sex Cult (a sex cult for gay witches).\r\n\r\nAs Kaelan Trough and his husband celebrate the gender reveal of their as yet unborn child, they invite their nearest and dearest for an unforgettable party.\r\n\r\nHowever, the party takes a sinister turn as Prosecco is drunk, demons are summoned (oops!) and prophecies are fulfilled.\r\n\r\nKaelan soon realises that he is merely a pawn in the machinations of a powerful, terrifying and sexy organisation, and he will be lucky to escape with his life.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Andrew Doherty: Gay Witch Sex Cult.","instanceDates":"18 April-20 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"524803ASKHBLPQDSSDSJPVDQDDHQHNTCB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-18T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-18T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-20T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-20T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Sketch","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A sticky, spooky horror comedy about gender-reveal parties, demons from hell, and a Gay Witch Sex Cult (a sex cult for gay witches).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Andrew Doherty: Gay Witch Sex Cult.","instanceDates":"30 October-2 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"566403ABRVKNQRCLGMDVBCDPPNGVGGGVS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-30T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-30T22:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-02T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-02T22:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"From the twisted homosexual mind that brought you 'Gay Witch Sex Cult' (\"the finest horror pastiche I can recall on the Fringe since Garth Marenghi\" ★★★★ The Guardian), Andrew Doherty returns to Soho with Edinburgh Fringe hit ‘Sad Gay AIDS Play’. \r\nAndrew relaunches himself with a groundbreaking piece of tragic theatre – the depressed love child of ‘A Little Life’ and ‘Angels in America’, cooked up in an effort to be taken more seriously by The Pulitzer committee and earn his one way ticket to success. ‘Sad Gay AIDS Play’ sees brave and fame hungry Andrew throw the book at AIDS and ask the Arts Council to pick it up. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Andrew Doherty: Sad Gay Aids Play","instanceDates":"16 March-21 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"666803AJQDLKLBHVRLMJMJJQJKQRVVLBR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-16T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-16T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-21T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-21T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Andrew Frost just wants to do a fun card magic show but people keep trying to figure out how he’s doing the tricks. This must stop. He is going to do whatever it takes to suspend your disbelief. \r\n\r\nFollowing a sell-out run at the 2026 Edinburgh Fringe, acclaimed contemporary magician Andrew Frost brings his new five-star show to London‘s Soho Theatre. \r\n\r\nExpect laughs, emotional manipulation and lying from a 34-year-old man with bionic eyes and a 45-year-old son. 14+ (Audience participation and strong language, check webpage for current info).","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Andrew Frost: Just Let Me Have This","instanceDates":"13 November-13 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"758203ADRGCMJLGMBRNMDGMDVNDCNGBRL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-13T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-13T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-13T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-13T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Andy Zaltzman – host of The News Quiz and The Bugle podcast, statistician on Test Match Special, Taskmaster series 18 champion – returns with his stand-up review of the global year, for the first time this decade. \r\n\r\nFollowing his sell-out The Zaltgeist tour show, Andy will assess the state of our world-renowned planet at the conclusion of another furiously odd year, in his unique comedic style.   \r\n\r\nEven the biggest 2026 fans would concede that it has been far from flawless as a year, even in the context of this incurable buffoon of a decade.  Humanity has stared into the ravening maw of Artificial Intelligence, wondering whether or not it has already eaten us.  Across the world, existential crises have become the must-have accessories for nations, art forms, sports and species.   \r\n\r\nAndy will attempt to harness the powers of modern and ancient technologies to find shards of genuine hope amongst the cavalcade of cantankerousness, before 2026 is certifiably consigned to the history books, where it emphatically belongs.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Andy Zaltzman: 2026 – The Certifiable History","instanceDates":"14 December-9 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"754203AMDDKVDSKJVCRDVMQNBNMBLMBJM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-14T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-14T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-01-09T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-01-09T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Following a sell-out 2024/2025 national run, Andy Zaltzman – host of The Bugle podcast and BBC Radio 4’s The News Quiz, statistician on Test Match Special, and champion of Taskmaster series 18 – extends his hit tour into 2026. \r\nFully updated due to the UK and the world both steadfastly refusing to sort themselves out, Andy assesses the state of renowned planet Earth, its under-pressure current in-house millennium, and its most famous and controversial species – the human race. \r\n\r\nWith politicians the world over striving to outdo each other in splattering their people with a cocktail of incompetence, inexplicability and insatiable dishonesty, Andy, the universe’s leading and only 2-in-1 political-comedian-and-professional-cricket-statistician, harnesses the combined 21st-century witchcraft of A.I. and his live audience.  Between them, they will concoct vaguely plausible answers to perennially troublesome questions such as What?, Who?, When?, Where?, and above all Why? \r\n\r\nWARNING: May feature talking penguin. \r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":125,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Andy Zaltzman: The Zaltgeist 2026 – A Second Thwack ","instanceDates":"17 April-17 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"657403AQRTBNMVKRLTSLBDVMKDPBRJSVP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-17T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-17T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-17T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-17T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Political","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"You know when you're trying to wee on a night out, and you're interrupted by a random girl who insists on telling you all her secrets even though you've never met? Imagine that, but she has a microphone.\r\nAfter two critically acclaimed sell-out runs at the Edinburgh Festival Fringe and a sold-out Soho Theatre run, Edinburgh Comedy Award Best Show 2023 nominee Ania Magliano is back on tour.\r\n‘Consistently amusing and deceptively daring' (**** Times' Top 4 Best Comedy Shows 2023). ***** (Telegraph), **** (Guardian, Evening Standard, Time Out).\r\nWriter for Amelia Dimoldenberg.\r\nAnia’s choices on Off Menu are widely regarded as the worst of all time.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ania Magliano: Forgive Me, Father","instanceDates":"14 October-26 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"561003AHKNKRRHHJMKMMDQGPSCRRPGSKK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-14T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-14T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-26T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-26T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"To the hairdresser at [redacted] Salon: You can take my money. You can take my dignity. You can take too much off the ends. But you cannot take my right to talk about it on stage.\r\n\r\nThis is a show about the worst haircut of Ania Magliano's life.\r\n\r\nAnia's critically acclaimed 2022 debut run sold out at Edinburgh, Soho Theatre and Leicester Square Theatre.\r\n\r\nShe's supported Marc Maron, Cat Cohen and Ed Gamble on tour, and writes for Amelia Dimoldenberg's Chicken Shop Date.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ania Magliano: I Can’t Believe You’ve Done This","instanceDates":"16 October-21 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"484003ASHKDPVPDDQMRLMGKKTBHDKRRCN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-16T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-16T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-21T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-21T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Comedy"},{"description":"Fresh from starring in the latest series of Taskmaster, Ania Magliano (Live At The Apollo, Edinburgh Comedy Awards Best Show Nominee) brings a brand-new show full of jokes, confessions, and occasionally unhinged observations to venues nationwide. From the quirks of her own body to the legend that is Eve (yes, from Adam and), to her newly discovered boundaries, Peach Fuzz is Ania at her most relatable – and most funny.\r\n\r\nAnia has opened for Ed Gamble, Marc Maron and Catherine Cohen, and writes for Amelia Dimoldenberg’s Chicken Shop Date. Her choices on the Off Menu podcast are widely regarded as the worst of all time.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ania Magliano: Peach Fuzz","instanceDates":"22 June-4 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"657803ALRRDPCLGLPLDDLNPJHRCMVVKKV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-22T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-22T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-04T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-04T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Anirban Dasgupta returns to Soho Theatre with his signature smart, relatable and insightful comedy.\r\nDebuted at the Melbourne International Comedy Festival earlier this year, Cry Daddy explores two childhoods - with a twist. Anirban's childhood dream was to become a sports person. But instead of Lord’s, he ended up at Soho Theatre. Clearly it didn't work out. \r\n\r\nNow, as a dad navigating the chaotic second half of life, he’s rethinking the rules and wondering if everything from comedy to raising a kid is actually just a game? Who’s winning, who’s losing, what’s really the endgame? Come find out in this new stand-up comedy thriller that will go down to the wire!\r\n\r\n'Bulletproof material' **** Guardian\r\n'A suave, smooth, international veteran' **** Beat Magazine\r\n'Original and uplifting comedy from India' ***** Theatre Vibe\r\n\r\nKolkata-born, Mumbai-based Anirban is a stand-up comedian, screenwriter and new father with a distinct comedic style. A former corporate salesman, Anirban has performed extensively in India and across the world including the prestigious Just For Laughs in Montreal and the Melbourne International Comedy Festival. His first stand-up special Take It Easy was released on Amazon Prime Video to wide acclaim, as was Afsos, the dark comedy series he created.\r\nPerformed in English.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Anirban Dasgupta: Cry Daddy","instanceDates":"30 September-4 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"636003ACDRCDGHPCRCRMLMMDGCMKTBTKV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-30T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-30T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-04T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-04T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Personal stories, sardonic cynicism and big laughs from the smart and relatable Indian comedy star.\r\nKolkata-born, Mumbai-based Anirban Dasgupta explores three generations of his family back to British India, the birth of his daughter, and the immediate question: what world did he bring his child into? A world full of war, misinformation, disease and division? Is there hope after all? Expect personal stories, sardonic cynicism and big laughs from the smart, relatable star of his special Take It Easy and the creator of dark comedy Afsos (both Amazon Prime). \r\n\r\nAnirban is a stand-up comedian and screenwriter with a distinct comedic style. He left his career as a corporate salesman, and has since headlined across India and around the world. He is the first comedian from India to appear on Just For Laughs Montréal New Faces International (2022) and at the Melbourne International Comedy Festival opening night gala (2023). He also appeared in the Melbourne International Comedy Festival Roadshow, which toured across Australia. As well as touring his latest stand-up Polite Provocation, he is writing a Bollywood film and developing an upcoming series for a major streaming service.\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Anirban Dasgupta: Polite Provocation","instanceDates":"28 October-2 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"570403APSQMSPRHNHRSGHGJNJMPQRTNJQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-28T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-28T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-02T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-02T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Personal stories, sardonic cynicism and big laughs as this smart, relatable star makes his UK debut at Soho Theatre.\r\nIn Polite Provocation, Anirban talks about life in India, three generations of his family going back to British India, the recent birth of his daughter and the immediate question - what world did he bring his child into? A world full of war, misinformation, disease and division? Is there hope after all? \r\n\r\nKolkata-born, Mumbai-based Anirban is a stand-up comedian, screenwriter and new father with a distinct comedic style. A former corporate salesman, Anirban has performed extensively in India and across the world including the prestigious Just For Laughs in Montreal and the Melbourne International Comedy Festival. His first stand-up special Take It Easy was released on Amazon Prime Video to wide acclaim, as was Afsos, the dark comedy series he created. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Anirban Dasgupta: Polite Provocation.","instanceDates":"3 January-9 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"508803AVRHQMRPLDCBHSQNHCGTSPNJHKB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-03T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-03T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-09T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-09T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Anisha is the star of the Bravo show, Family Karma, and host of the Dear Media podcast, Currently Cringing. Family Karma showcases Anisha managing her first-generation Indian identity along with her family dynamics and culture. Anisha is a successful entrepreneur and has been featured in Vogue US, Vogue India, The New Yorker, ET, Page Six, Elle, People, and Harper’s Bazaar. Anisha is best known for her viral comedic one-liners. To her, no topic is off-limits.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Anisha Ramakrishna: Material Girl","instanceDates":"5 December-6 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"510603AMRGHJTKMNLKRDGKPTCPQGLRLRC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-05T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-05T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-06T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-06T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Zeppelin Entertainment proudly presents Anubhav Singh Bassi live in London ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Anubhav Singh Bassi: Kisi Ko Batana Mat ","instanceDates":"23 November-23 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"663803ABKRHSBKMJQDNKBVTSMJSVBGQGS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-23T14:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-23T14:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-23T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-23T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Anuvab Pal returns on official business.\r\nPost-Brexit, the British government want to sell the idea of Britishness to India. It has been done before, with dubious results. Now, they've set up a Department of Britishness and hired him. He will explain in detail why Indians should embrace Britishness, having done it himself. There is trouble ahead. 'Very clever, very funny' (Guardian). 'India's most intelligent comedian' (New York Times). 'One of India's top comedians' ***** (EdFestMag.com). As seen on Amazon Prime, QI and Big Asian Stand-Up (BBC Two).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Anuvab Pal: The Department Of Britishness","instanceDates":"4 June-8 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"529803AGGRPBHGBHLMHBRVCKVTRDMRHCC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-04T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-04T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-08T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-08T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Iceland’s biggest stand-up comedian (and first-ever Netflix star) returns to the UK following sold out runs at Edinburgh Fringe, Melbourne and Soho Theatre.\r\nThe grandson of a previous president, Ari is the beating heart and unofficial ambassador for a fascinatingly humorous frozen rock called Iceland. A family man with a unique perspective being locally famous in his own country; having run-ins with Icelandic tabloids, a new relationship and being a father while all the time being a traveling comedian. This former flight attendant’s fast comedy is utterly charming; the coldness of his homeland is in stark contrast to the warmness of his delivery.\r\n\r\nBorn and raised in Reykjavík, Ari has appeared on Pardon My Icelandic (Netflix), Mock the Week (BBC Two) and performed with the Icelandic Symphony Orchestra.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ari Eldjárn: Return of the Icelandic","instanceDates":"9 April-13 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"524603AVMJPBQLKTDQNVHTQVLBJVVMBGH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-09T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-09T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-13T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-13T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A hilarious double act drama about age, friendship, grief, regret, love and showbiz.\r\nTwo men meet on a park bench. They reflect on religion, politics and life, reminiscing about the days when Instagram was just an efficient drug dealer and Tik Tok was what clocks did.\r\n\r\nAs they revisit their past we discover it’s the first time they’ve met in 30 years and there’s more to their relationship than we first realise as skeletons tumble from the cupboard. \r\n‘Tear-inducingly tender and disarmingly silly.’ **** Times\r\n\r\n‘The more I think about it the more I realise just how bloody clever and moving it is. The fact that it’s also bloody funny just makes it better. Don’t miss it.’ **** Entertainment Now\r\n\r\nDirected by Kevin Day\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Arthur Smith & Phil Nice: OOF","instanceDates":"3 April-5 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"596603ADMTDJHCLNMHQCDPPNVKJJBMQKQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-03T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-03T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-05T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-05T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Passion. Betrayal. Bollywood... After an unexpected phone call takes her back to Delhi, Radhika Elizabeth Kapoor suddenly finds herself in a world where nothing is as it seems. Surrounded by an interfering family, chased by gangsters with shady motives and with Gulab Jamon bullets flying, Radhika is forced to confront the two sides of her own identity in this epic road trip across India…  16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ashes by Convoy","instanceDates":"17 August-18 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"733203ALMTNTNMSGNJSNLNTLBDTMVCLDB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-17T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-17T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-18T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-18T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"It's been over a year since Aurie toured his sold-out, award winning show GREEN, but the question is, has he kept his promise? Has he endeavoured to remain GREEN in the time that has passed? For those who missed out on what this means, or wants to check in on the progress… come and see an exclusive run of 'GREENER?’ for two nights only at Soho Theatre, this Summer. \r\nAs seen on ‘Deep Fake Neighbour Wars’ (ITVX), ‘Comedy Central Live’, ‘Jonathan Ross’ Comedy Club’ (ITV), & ‘Mo Gilligan’s Black British & Funny' (C4).\r\n\r\nBritish Comedy Guide Recommended 2022\r\n***** - I Talk Telly\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Aurie Styla: Greener?","instanceDates":"2 June-3 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"460803APKHVKNDJMLRGNCSGJKKNKTDQPS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-02T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-02T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-03T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-03T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Ever since she was a baby and her mother took her own life, Avital has felt summoned to the other side, aka the vast nothingness.\r\nBut she'd hate to be labelled a copycat, plus, who wants to turn into their mother? Avital Ash's critically acclaimed Fringe debut explores growing up a Hasidic Jew, depression, queer identity, and generational Holocaust trauma, all while being hilarious. The results are an irreverent show where Avital expertly bounces from black humour to jokes so silly you almost miss the gospel in them. \r\n\r\nAvital is a writer on an upcoming comedy series for Netflix, with over 100 million views and over 300k followers for her standup on TikTok and Instagram. She had a recurring role on BARRY, and did voice over on the smash hit video game OXENFREE and its new sequel. \r\n\r\nAvital Ash Workshops Her Suicide Note received 11 four-star reviews, including from The Telegraph, The Scotsman, and Chortle. She brings it to LA, NY, and back to the UK in early 2024. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Avital Ash: Workshops Her Suicide Note","instanceDates":"13 May-14 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"525603AMNJTSCDVKTHDQKJQBSTMJTNRRD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-13T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-13T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-14T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-14T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Fresh from a sold-out, award-winning Edinburgh Fringe debut, Ayo Adenekan brings his breakout show Black Mediocrity to Soho Theatre.\r\nJoint winner of Best Newcomer at the ISH Edinburgh Comedy Awards 2025 and the Bestie Award for Emerging Talent, Ayo has quickly become one of the most exciting new voices in UK comedy. His debut sold out its entire Edinburgh Fringe run, with three extra shows added, and earned nominations at the Comedians’ Comedian Awards for and across the press.\r\nWith laid-back charm and razor-sharp storytelling, Ayo takes us from primary school nativity plays to lads’ holidays, from respectability politics to Red Bull sponsorship. Exploring race, sexuality, and belonging with warmth and wit, he crafts a show that’s as heartfelt as it is hilarious.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ayo Adenekan: Black Mediocrity","instanceDates":"27 October-28 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"658403ARRDTTPTSJTTTKVVPTSGCJNLPLG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-27T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-27T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-28T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-28T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"BBC New Comedy Award finalist and writer for SNLUK returns following his sold-out debut, with a romantic sophomore hour Homeland Insecurity. One Edinburgh Fringe, before Ayo had ever picked up a mic, a summer fling changed his life. Homeland Insecurity is about love, coming out, family, B&Q and pulled pork. Laid back and effortlessly charming, Ayo blends big laughs with beautifully observed storytelling about work, friendship, family and love.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ayo Adenekan: Homeland Insecurity","instanceDates":"25 November-28 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"753203ATKMNTTRVJBGNHNVQDSSTCRQKHJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-25T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-25T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-28T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-28T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The critically acclaimed debut show about suffering (and smiling) from Nigerian stand-up Ayoade Bamgboye, nominated for Best Newcomer at the 2025 Edinburgh Comedy Awards.\r\nFollowing her sold-out run at this year’s Edinburgh Fringe, Swings and Roundabouts transfers to Soho Theatre. \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nBurdened by the gift of sight, a primeval awareness that something is not quite right, and almost three accents, she'll ask life's big questions and provide absolutely no answers. \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nBorn in London, raised in Lagos, sacked in Budapest, the poor woman has been there and done that – and to what end? \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nSwings and Roundabouts is about going nowhere fast, being too British to stop apologising, and too Nigerian to stop shouting. \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nWinner of NextUp’s Biggest Award In Comedy 2025. \r\n\r\nNominated for Best Newcomer at the 2025 ISH Awards. \r\n\r\nAs seen in her own Channel 4 Playground.  \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ayoade Bamgboye: Swings and Roundabouts","instanceDates":"6 October-24 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"654403AMJRRPNMSKHBTQKKCPKGTGMTHSQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-06T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-06T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-24T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-24T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Babes in Arms","instanceDates":"6 December-4 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"652003APNVQRMRHPNVCDTVBKSKPTNMNCP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-06T11:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-06T11:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-04T13:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-04T13:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Up to 18 months","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Babes in arms (Rosie & Hugh","instanceDates":"22 August-25 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"563203ARQPCKKQPSGBRGNVCJMLSMQPRNC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-22T11:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-22T10:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-25T14:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-25T13:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Babes in Arms (The Gruffalo)","instanceDates":"12 December-13 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"724003ABSJNRDCNBSSNNVGMJRMPTRPJPD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-12T10:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-12T10:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-13T13:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-13T13:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Get ready for an outrageous evening of bombastic bad taste in the killer new show from cult drag superstar Baby Lame!\r\nWannabe scream queen Baby has always dreamt of playing a chainsaw-wielding, kickass Final Girl in her very own slasher movie and tonight’s the night she’s going to make it happen. The location is set and the cameras are ready to roll. There’s just one problem, Baby hasn’t found anyone to kill her… yet!\r\n\r\nCo-created and directed by Deanna Fleysher (Red Bastard, Butt Kapinski) and co-starring the entire audience. Final Baby Girl! is a genre-bending thrill ride featuring kinky roleplays, trash-tastic original songs, deliriously camp film clips and riotous balls-out performance. From erotic vampire fantasies to slasher camp massacres, one thing's for sure... you'll be screaming for more!\r\nBaby Lame has performed across London's alternative drag scene for the last 10 years with her brand of punk-horror, gender-bending, cabaret clowning and continues to be a fixture of the scene, creating chaos and queer AF work. She is the MC and co-producer of iconic circus-cabaret club night MIMIs and the creator of the underground queer revue Shit Show. Baby is a senior consultant producer on RuPaul's Drag Race UK and co-hosted the official Drag Race UK podcast with Scarlett Moffatt for BBC Sounds/Radio 1.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Baby Lame: Final Baby Girl!","instanceDates":"13 October-14 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"495003ASDNCDLMJRGNKBVGKNCPDDHKMQP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-13T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-13T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-14T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-14T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Comedy"},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Bar Test","instanceDates":"30 January-30 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"603803AGHHCLLGMQQKQKGKPRRHMMDQBHT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-30T15:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-30T15:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-30T15:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-30T15:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Willow is ignoring that Jordan wants to play with a Barbie doll while Jason thinks it’s just a phase, Cherelle thinks it’s homophobia and Vivi is wondering why nobody has just asked Jordan? This family party is about to get real messy…\r\nBarbie Come To Tea explores family dynamics, class race, sexuality and masculinity. Everything a family party needs! \r\nPlease note: This is a script in hand rehearsed reading. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Barbie comes to tea by Shanika Warren-Markland","instanceDates":"10 February-10 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"520603AGPGBQDLNLCGGKJGGKLMBMBDPDL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-10T15:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-10T15:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-10T15:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-10T15:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"This Edinburgh Fringe First winning daring, poignant and wit-ty one-woman show rips the lid off the myths of female madness.\r\nFresh from an award-winning run at Edinburgh Fringe, psy-cho-siren Leah Shelton’s acclaimed work BATSHIT, directed by Olivier award-winning Ursula Martinez, is a powerful reckoning with the myths and misconceptions of female madness.\r\n\r\nA theatrical gut-punch inspired by her grandmother’s incar-ceration for seeking independence in 1960s Australia, this one-woman tour de force tears apart the labels used to con-trol and undermine women through razor-sharp wit, raw storytelling, and unflinching performance. \t\t\t\t\r\nWinner - Scotsman Fringe First & Mental Health Foundation Fringe Awards at Edinburgh Fringe 2024. \r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":50,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"BATSHIT","instanceDates":"24 September-27 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"638004AMBJNLDLLDDQRVBTGLKQQDSDTMV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-24T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-24T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-27T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-27T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Performance Art","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"In the dark, deathly world of the Middle Ages, one (annoying) woman strives to find the light. Join Batilda Bigbum, a female mystic in a world of male dullards, as she escapes from a life of monotony to a life of devotion. This is CHRISTBRIDE: a “dementedly funny and fast-paced” (The Scotsman) new character comedy from Bebe Cave.\r\n“A masterclass of anarchic comedy” (The List), Bebe Cave’s award-winning debut (The List Festival Awards’ Best Comedy Show) is both irreverent and irresistible. It’s a “Clueless-meets-Monty-Python medieval romp” (The Skinny) that’s “as fiery as the flames that burned witches of yore.” (Broadway World)\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Bebe Cave: CHRISTBRIDE","instanceDates":"21 May-23 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"708803AQNMCKPRBQDBNHSBPNTLRSSPKCC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-21T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-21T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-23T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-23T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"In the dark, deathly world of the Middle Ages, one (annoying) woman strives to find the light. Join Batilda Bigbum, a female mystic in a world of male dullards, as she escapes from a life of monotony to a life of devotion. This is CHRISTBRIDE: a “dementedly funny and fast-paced” (The Scotsman) new character comedy from Bebe Cave.\r\n“A masterclass of anarchic comedy” (The List), Bebe Cave’s award-winning debut (The List Festival Awards’ Best Comedy Show) is both irreverent and irresistible. It’s a “Clueless-meets-Monty-Python medieval romp” (The Skinny) that’s “as fiery as the flames that burned witches of yore.” (Broadway World)\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Bebe Cave: CHRISTBRIDE Oct25","instanceDates":"1 December-6 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"660803AJGLQQHSQJRJGBQJTKKGRQJQHNJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-01T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-01T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-06T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-06T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Award-winning character comedian and actress Bebe Cave explores historical female main character syndrome. This time it's the Victorian era, where men wear top hats and waistcoats and ladies don't have the vote yet. Good times!  Through the lens of the pre-Raphaelite brotherhood, some very silly men who were very good at painting, and their most famous muses, Bebe skewers pretentious male artistry and the women they love to drown in \"a uniquely gleeful, centuries spanning romp\" (★★★★★ Chortle). Why are women such beautiful artistic objects, especially when they're dead, and why are the men who paint them so difficult and very much alive?\r\nSee this award-nominated, \"Smart, slapstick and silly\" (★★★★ The Guardian) comedy that is \"a riotously funny demonstration of Cave's irresistible talent\" (★★★★ The Scotsman). (16+ references to death/drug use - check webpage for current advice).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Bebe Cave: Swoon","instanceDates":"25 January-30 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"754603APNLDMCKBRCHMCSCHGPGMJVSHGL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-01-25T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-01-25T21:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-01-30T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-01-30T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Attending The Receipts Podcast Live solo? Join us for a pre-show social before the main event.\r\nSoho Theatre presents, ‘Before the Receipts: Mix, Sip & Gist’ Creative Engagement have curated our very own pre-show mixer for the babes attending The Receipts Podcast Live. Join us for this 2-hour social lead by Déviniat and we’re talking icebreakers, hot social topics, games and activities all whilst sipping on our signature rum punch for the day, Keep the Balance. Come ready to play, connect and meet like-minded individuals ahead of Tolly & Audrey’s main course right here at Walthamstow, live and direct. To make things even better, stick around after the Receipts Podcast Live for a post-show function at our speakeasy bar. Vibes brought to you by a rising female DJ and plenty of room to shake a leg. Hurry, limited places available x This event will include photography.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Before the Receipts: Mix, Sip & Gist","instanceDates":"9 May-9 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"712803AVGBMLRGBBQGQNMMRJRRSHKVSKR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-09T16:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-09T15:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-09T16:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-09T15:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Political","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Access","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Family"},{"description":"Sell-out Edinburgh Fringe star Bella Hull has made another show with her restless mind and restlesser heart. \r\nThere are hundreds of jokes in it - thousands if you count wrong. She will tell them all with great showmanship and warmth, unless of course the crowd is nasty. The Times, Telegraph and Guardian Funniest Jokes Of the Fringe champ returns with a \"beautifully wrought, irreverent\" (★★★★ Guardian) hour of surreal diversions, back-to-back laughs and a healthy dose of sorcery.16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Bella Hull: Doctors Hate Her","instanceDates":"2 January-3 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"676803AKHHNMNNCLVRGLKKMCGKGBSQNRG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-02T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-02T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-03T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-03T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Sell-out Edinburgh Fringe star Bella Hull has made another show with her restless mind and restlesser heart. \r\nThere are hundreds of jokes in it - thousands if you count wrong. She will tell them all with great showmanship and warmth, unless of course the crowd is nasty. The Times, Telegraph and Guardian Funniest Jokes Of the Fringe champ returns with a \"beautifully wrought, irreverent\" (★★★★ Guardian) hour of surreal diversions, back-to-back laughs and a healthy dose of sorcery.\r\nBritish Comedy Guide Recommended\r\nGuardian 10 funniest jokes of the fringe 2025 \r\nTimes best jokes of the fringe 2025\r\nLoaded Magazine picks of the fringe \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Bella Hull: Doctors Hate Her.","instanceDates":"23 October-25 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"658803AKDHMMCCDSPMKPLPDKTLTVLTKJT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-23T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-23T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-25T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-25T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Have I Got News for You star and SNL UK ingenue Bella Hull returns after yet another sold out, critically acclaimed Edinburgh Fringe hit.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Bella Hull: Mad Cow Disease","instanceDates":"16 November-21 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"747003ADGQJTNCNKQNJCPQTJTKTDDHBGR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-16T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-16T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-21T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-21T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Ben Pope - \"a total delight\" (Fest) - is bored of small talk. So here it is! A show about The Big Stuff: God, death, love, the galaxy and, most of all, chocolate.\r\nWhat happens after you die? What’s God up to? Is love forever? Why do people like stargazing when it’s so desperately boring?\r\nBen’s got some huge questions and the answers are, well, sublime.\r\n\r\nAs seen on Comedy Central, Dave and BBC Radio 4 Extra.\r\n\r\n\"Consistently funny and deceptively thoughtful\" (The Scotsman)\r\n\"Classy, stylish and accomplished\" (Chortle)\r\n\"Always spot-on\" (The Skinny)\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ben Pope: Holy Cow","instanceDates":"31 July-1 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"465603AHNKTDPLLRVPNNTKRJRCCTPCQNR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-31T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-31T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-01T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-01T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Ben Pope – 'a total delight' ⭐⭐⭐⭐ (Fest) – brings his Fringe-hit stand-up show to Soho. And this time, it's surgical. Last year, Ben got circumcised. On purpose, and as recommended by medical professionals. This show is a 55min inventory of his ensuing masculine panic. Expect jokes and stories on: the male ego, pillow talk, charity shops, the sublime mystery of having a father, and also exactly one pig. See you there. Chop chop. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ben Pope: The Cut","instanceDates":"3 November-5 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"658003ATSTVHDHHCCGGRQDQJSBVDVQLDT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-03T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-03T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-05T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-05T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Ben Target is a critically-acclaimed performance artist and multi-award-winning comedian (yawn), but in 2020 he gave this up to become the live-in carer for an irascible octogenarian prankster. A life-affirming story about death, conveyed through the popular mediums of storytelling, servitude to the audience and live carpentry, a combination not seen on the world stage since Nazareth (circa 30AD).\r\n'Imagine there was no Ben Target. The world would unquestionably be a darker, less interesting place' (Chortle.co.uk).\r\n'A beautiful, gentle, touching thing...spellbinding' (Scotsman). 'A true original and a legend in the making' (Guardian). \r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":65,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ben Target: LORENZO","instanceDates":"27 September-14 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"485203AMQLDSQHCNDKKCRRKDDKSSMVQND","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-27T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-27T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-14T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-14T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Storytelling","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Performance Art","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Ben Target is a critically-acclaimed performance artist and multi-award-winning comedian (yawn), but in 2020 he gave this up to become the live-in carer for an irascible octogenarian prankster. A life-affirming story about death, conveyed through the popular mediums of storytelling, servitude to the audience and live carpentry, a combination not seen on the world stage since Nazareth (circa 30AD).\r\n'Imagine there was no Ben Target. The world would unquestionably be a darker, less interesting place' (Chortle.co.uk).\r\n'A beautiful, gentle, touching thing...spellbinding' (Scotsman). 'A true original and a legend in the making' (Guardian). \r\nCredits:\r\n•\tWriter / Performer – Ben Target \r\n•\tDirector / Dramaturg – Adam Brace\r\n•\tAssociate Director – Lee Griffiths\r\n•\tSet Design – Tom Hartshorne and Ben Target\r\n\r\n14+ guideline","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":65,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ben Target: LORENZO (Preview)","instanceDates":"17 July-29 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"474203ANKTDNQVGMBJDPNSBDJGLLHVRDC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-17T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-17T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-29T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-29T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Storytelling","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Work In Progress","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Psychiatrist, comedian and best-selling author Dr Benji unlocks the doors to the psych ward with Maddening. Following a sold-out run at the Edinburgh Festival, expect stand-up, book readings and an audience Q&A (your best chance to speak to an NHS psychiatrist without the 12-month wait). 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Benji Waterhouse: Maddening","instanceDates":"6 February-25 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"686403AJKQHVQJRNMQSHJBPVBQLDVCSVN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-06T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-06T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-25T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-25T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"BEST IN CLASS IS A CROWD FUNDED PROFIT SHARING SHOW THAT CHAMPIONS THE RICH TALENT OF WORKING CLASS COMEDIANS.\r\n\r\nSponsored by waste grounds, knock off trainers, spam, weed, the unions, crap schools, bunking off, failed MOT’s, failed GCSE’s, bus stops, payday loans, fierce mums, tired dads and empowerment.\r\n\r\nHosted by award winning comedian Sian Davies (“Compelling and distinctive” The Scotsman) and featuring the very best comics, who just so happen to be from working class backgrounds.\r\n\r\nBest in Class was founded in 2018 by Sian Davies, who was fed up with class, money and social status being used as a barrier to performing.  The project works with a squad of working class comedians and enables them to perform at the Edinburgh Fringe. The comics work tirelessly in the run up to the festival to crowdfund the costs involved. Crucially, none of the acts pay to participate and they all receive payment for the work they do.\r\n\r\nBest In Class has been a runaway success at the Edinburgh Fringe. Audiences flock to see the show, queueing early for a seat and selling it out daily. There is a real buzz around this group of comics bringing something different to the table at the world’s biggest arts festival, which is often dominated by middle class voices.\r\nBest In Class alumni have gone on to achieve fantastic successes within their comedy careers. Graduates of the project have had nominations for Best Comedy Show at the Edinburgh Fringe Awards, created shows for BBC Radio 4, signed for agents, gained TV work, created sell out shows and had critically acclaimed work.\r\n\r\nIn 2022 Best In Class were awarded the Panel Prize at the Edinburgh Comedy Awards. \r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Best in Class","instanceDates":"18 April-18 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"415004AJTDBMGCJJBQBQCPDMCRKHKGDCK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-18T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-18T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-18T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-18T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"In 2019 Beth faced turning 40 head on and moved to a small village just outside the town she grew up in.  She imagined she'd be able to get away from it all, but in today's hyper connected age that was more difficult than she imagined...  A queer story of rural living, conspiracies, an unfortunate medical condition and PC building. \r\n\r\nAs seen in Cucumber, Banana, Tofu (C4), Doctor Who (BBC). \r\nJoe.co.uk comedy award 2020. \r\n\r\n\"You’re onto a winner with Bethany.\" **** Funny Women. \r\n**** Fest Mag. \r\n\"Comedy's Henry Cavill\" - Joe Lycett\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Bethany Black: Always Bet on Beth","instanceDates":"24 May-24 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"456803AMCLPRSJMNLGVCSPLHHSBKDBNLQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-24T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-24T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-24T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-24T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Dolphin Orgies, Intersex snails, Gay giraffes, Transgender fish…\r\nLondon drag King Bi-Curious George presents Queer Planet: a raucous drag celebration of queerness and the animal kingdom. \r\n\r\nBi-Curious George is a rising star of the London drag scene and the 2022 winner of the prestigious Not Another Drag Competition at the Royal Vauxhall Tavern. His work centres around queer ecology; queerness in the natural world.\r\n\r\n“Probably one of the most ingenious ideas for a production I have ever seen [..] A performance of sheer perfection” \r\nGet The Chance Wales \r\n\r\nQueer Planet is a raucous romp through the animal kingdom which aims to shatter the heteronormative binaries through which we view the natural world. It is both a parody of and a homage to Britains beloved nature documentaries - combining drag, stand up comedy, parody songs and all manner of ridiculous behaviour.\r\n\r\n\"Shines and shimmers in queer Euphoria”\r\nBinge Fringe Magazine\r\nQueer Planet was developed through work in progress performances in independent queer venues. The entire piece is an ongoing conversation and collaboration with, as well as a small window into, the wonderful queer community which Bi-curious George has come from.\r\n\r\n “Pretty much everything you could want in a drag show” \r\nTheatre and Other Things\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Bi Curious George: Queer Planet","instanceDates":"16 February-16 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"522403AMTCVMMNGVBJGTTSGTHKBHPQQLC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-16T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-16T22:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-16T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-16T22:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"To be a Gold Digger or not to be?\r\nThat is the question women worldwide ask while working a minimum-wage job in today's economy. Join Czech-born, LA-based stand-up Bianca Cristovao as she delves into topics like money, sex, greed, passports, and her short-lived relationship with a billionaire. \r\nAs seen on The Late Show with Stephen Colbert. Opening act for Bill Burr.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Bianca Cristovao: Gold Digger","instanceDates":"3 January-4 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"586203AKLJNBLJLRJKNVDKDNQQKLGNMCJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-03T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-03T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-04T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-04T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Two teenagers perform fake Bigfoot sightings in their Appalachian town until a neighbour’s dog turns up torn to pieces. Aside from sparking a panic that spirals out of their control, it forces them to question what might actually be terrorising their underresourced and already superstitious community. From “the Fringe’s most dynamic theatrical duo” (Telegraph) comes a brand new Brechtian puppet show ripped in two about conspiracy, misdirection, and seeing something with your own eyes. Praise for Xhloe & Natasha’s previous work: ‘A tightly woven masterpiece’ ★★★★★ Skinny ‘Explosive’ ★★★★★ Playbill ‘An absurdist masterpiece… unmissable’ ★★★★★ Everything Theatre ‘Deliciously off-kilter’ ★★★★ Stage ‘Brilliantly choreographed, whip-smart and yet heart-breaking’ ★★★★ Scotsman\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":65,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Bigfoot Ripped My Dog In Half I Saw It","instanceDates":"7 September-26 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"718203ARSKLQSGQBLCDQNDNDDDKDQHMLT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-07T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-07T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-26T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-26T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Performance Art","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Bilal Zafar returns with a brand-new show about how he spent a year working in a care home for very wealthy people.\r\n\r\nEdinburgh Fringe Best newcomer nominee and New Act of the Year (NATYS) award winner Bilal Zafar returns with a brand-new show about how he spent a year working in a care home for very wealthy people.\r\n\r\nFresh out of university with a media degree, Bilal was dropped into the real world where he was given far too much responsibility for a 21-year-old that had just spent 3 years watching films. \r\n\r\nAs seen/heard on his very successful Twitch channel, BBC1, BBC2, Channel 4, and BBC Radio 4.\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Bilal Zafar: Care","instanceDates":"5 April-8 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"428804AVMGTCCKPGSNBHCHQSRMJLBJRPR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-05T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-05T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-08T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-08T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Bilal Zafar, nominated for Best Newcomer at the Edinburgh Fringe and winner of New Act of the Year 2016, is back with a brand-new show about how his usually stress-free house share took a turn and his housemate tried to get him arrested five times.\r\n\r\nHe has appeared on BBC One, BBC Two, BBC Radio 4 and built up his own online audience on Twitch as he plays an unhinged football manager in an ongoing improvised series.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Bilal Zafar: Imposter","instanceDates":"1 May-4 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"520003ADTSNGNBKPLVKVBCCTLHBMNPRBC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-01T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-01T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-04T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-04T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"The writer and executive producer of Apple’s smash hit comedy Shrinking makes his UK debut with his hilarious and powerful true story about the American Veteran experience.\r\nNo one wins and breaks hearts like writer/ comedian Bill Posley (Shrinking, Kobra Kai). Some people accidentally miss their bus, some accidentally misplace their keys, but Bill? In The Day I Accidentally Went to War, Bill will take you on a journey through childhood traumas to basic training and deployment, to coming home. Packed with laughs, gasps and all the feels, this show bares brutal truths, honours the Veteran experience, and celebrates the human spirit.\r\n\r\nFrom the award-winning team behind ‘The Day I Became Black’ (2019 Off Broadway Alliance Best Solo Performance) comes a poignant, emotional and hilarious comedy about the good, the bad and the ugly of Bill’s own Veteran experience.\r\n\r\nOfficial Selection: International Fringe Encores - Soho Playhouse, NYC\r\nOfficial Selection: Best of the Broadwater, Hollywood\r\nWinner: Splash Award for Excellence in Cultural Arts - Namba Performing Arts, Ventura\r\nNominee: Best Solo Show - Hollywood Fringe Festival 2024\r\n‘Bill Posley’s life experience is told with true-life images, movement, and his beautiful affable presence that will leave you feeling remarkable in many ways. This is a hell yes, must-see, for all! It is an inspiring performance of the resilience of us.’ Front Row Center\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Bill Posley: The Day I Accidentally Went to War","instanceDates":"2 September-13 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"640003ALNSLKVSTPJRBMJTSCQKLQBJJJC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-02T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-02T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-13T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-13T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Biswa Kalyan Rath is back — and he’s funnier, sharper and more gloriouslyunfiltered than ever\r\nAfter the international success of his last show, Inventions, Biswa returns toSoho Theatre Walthamstow with a brand-new hour of razor-sharp stand-up. Expect trademark rants, brilliantly offbeat observations and the kind ofwit that turns everyday absurdities into big laughs.One of India’s most celebrated comedians, Biswa is known to audiencesaround the world for the hugely popular YouTube series Pretentious MovieReviews with Kanan Gill, for mentoring emerging comics on Comicstaanseasons 1 and 2, and for his hit stand-up specials Biswa Mast Aadmi, Sushiand Mood Kharaab, filmed live at Soho Theatre.Don’t miss this fresh new set of never-before-seen material — catch himnow, before AI takes your place","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Biswa Kalyan Rath: An Evening of Laughter Before AI Takes Our Job","instanceDates":"15 January-16 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"732803AKKDVNLKTQHNCGQBSCRMVGKSQLR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-01-15T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-01-15T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-01-16T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-01-16T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Biswa is back in London with his latest inspired crowd work show. \r\nFollowing his Edinburgh Festival Fringe debut this year, he makes a welcome return to Soho Theatre  – packed with his trademark angry rant-styled delivery and unique worldview. \r\n\r\nOne of India’s most established comedians, Biswa can be seen on his hugely popular YouTube series Pretentious Movie Reviews alongside Kanan Gill, mentoring budding comics in Comicstaan seasons 1 and 2 and in his own hit stand-up specials Biswa Mast Aadmi, Sushi and his latest, this year’s acclaimed Mood Kharaab, filmed live at Soho Theatre.\r\n\r\nBiswa was one of six South Asian artists we brought to the Edinburgh Fringe Festival this year through Soho Theatre India. Over the past decade we’ve introduced over 30 Indian acts to the UK, on stages ranging from Soho Theatre to the Eventim Apollo and Royal Albert Hall.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Biswa Kalyan Rath: God Knows What This Show Is","instanceDates":"18 December-6 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"502003ADQMCRJVNRRGBRCBNHRBKBGPDRK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-18T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-18T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-06T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-06T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Biswa Kalyan Rath is back in London, and this time, he's diving deep into the labyrinth of the English language, love and marriage (yes they are separate and you will know why!) and a little bit of cross-border curiosity.\r\nFrom the hip lingo of South Bombay's elite to the peculiar quirks of English words, Biswa's sharp wit and observational humor will have you laughing until your sides ache, with the same intensity of how Mumbaikars heads ache while hunting for flats. And as if that weren't enough, he'll also tackle the delicate dance of negotiating with your spouse on daily chores and the bureaucratic maze that a govt office is.\r\n\r\nThe show is brand new. The jokes are fresh out of the oven. Over 5000 people have seen it, it’s your turn now London.\r\n\r\nPerformed in Hinglish\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Biswa Kalyan Rath: Hinglish & Engdi.","instanceDates":"1 November-23 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"570203ASLQTQHJQRGCNVVBQDLJTNKBHVR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-01T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-01T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-23T16:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-23T16:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Biswa Kalyan Rath is back in London (this time at our iconic Soho Theatre Walthamstow venue) with a brand-new show…\r\n\r\nFrom the hip lingo of South Bombay’s elite to the peculiar quirks of English words, Biswa’s sharp wit and observational humor will have you laughing until your sides ache, with the same intensity of how Mumbaikars heads ache while hunting for flats.\r\n\r\nAfter multiple sell-out runs at Soho Theatre Dean Street, join Biswa for his biggest ever London shows.\r\n\r\nPerformed in Hindi\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":80,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Biswa Kalyan Rath: Live","instanceDates":"30 August-6 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"582003AQTTKDBRLTBBKPJBVMJNKSQMTRQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-30T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-30T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-06T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-06T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Due to exceptional demand, Biswa Kalyan Rath will perform his show as a work in progress in English at Soho Theatre, following his sell-out weekend at Soho Theatre Walthamstow.\r\nFrom the hip lingo of South Bombay’s elite to the peculiar quirks of English words, Biswa’s sharp wit and observational humour will have you laughing until your sides ache, with the same intensity of how Mumbaikars heads ache while hunting for flats.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Biswa Kalyan Rath: Live (Work In Progress English Version)","instanceDates":"6 September-6 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"655403AKNLGMMMJPTMGQMRDRLVNLVPSGT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-06T16:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-06T15:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-06T16:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-06T15:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Blizzard is the brand-new solo show written and performed by Emily Woof, which premiered at Edinburgh Festival Fringe and transfers to Soho Theatre in summer 2024. \r\n \r\nA woman’s brain-scientist husband falls ill just as he is due to give the keynote lecture at a Swiss conference. She reluctantly agrees to give the lecture on his behalf. But when she arrives in Switzerland, her life starts to unravel. Clothes don't want to be clothes anymore. A dress becomes reluctant to be seen in public. Emily Woof's comic, philosophical adventure asks what is the self, what is thinking, what is the body? And in a godless universe, how do we connect with this thing called the soul? \r\n \r\nEmily Woof’s landmark solo shows Sex III and Revolver won back to back Edinburgh Fringe Firsts and were performed at Royal Court Theatre over twenty years ago. Now she is back with an intimate epic, a surreal and hilarious shaggy-dog story, about philosophy and neuroscience, dance and animals, love and the soul, which asks the question: how should we really live in body and mind?\r\n \r\nBlizzard is directed by Hamish McColl, founder of The Right Size whose hit show The Play What I Wrote was a smash in the West End and on Broadway and whose movies as screenwriter include Paddington, Jonny English and Mr Bean’s Holiday.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Blizzard","instanceDates":"7 May-25 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"516003ABQHKBRGNKVPSCTGGTBGQHJQRBH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-07T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-07T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-25T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-25T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Comedy"},{"description":"I have a uniform. A suitcase that becomes a horse. Fake snow. This will have to be enough. One Polish clown attempts the most epic adventure story ever told. He carries an orange. A gift from the love of his life. He carries everything except what he actually needs. Heroic, absurd, melodramatic, and stupidly beautiful. Wordless physical comedy from the creator of Furiozo. WIP.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Blizzard WIP","instanceDates":"1 June-1 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"712603AGGSTCTBLJLBMLPBPVCNJLHCHCH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-01T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-01T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-01T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-01T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"After a sell-out run at the Traverse Theatre during the 2022 Edinburgh Festival Fringe, the award-winning Bloody Elle comes to Soho. Eve’s eyes are green like guacamole, she has posh-hair and a freckle on her chin and when she puts her hand on Elle’s arm… This heart-warming and belly-achingly funny story is stuffed full of those stomach-flipping-time-stopping moments, a touch, a glance, a kiss, that everyone will recognise. Set to an original live score that builds loops and layers of sound to make you feel like there is a ten-piece band on stage, audiences are transported to a sweaty, packed out gig in the back of a pub or a 10,000 seat arena. Original production made in association with Rebel Productions.14+ recommendation","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":85,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Bloody Elle","instanceDates":"11 July-29 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"466003AKMKRKCSBDBDMTQKVKCPBBLDNKN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-11T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-11T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-29T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-29T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"Bob the Drag Queen is coming to London for one performance only to answer all your most burning questions.\r\nTaking a break from opening for Madonna on her Celebration tour, join Bob for a night of comedy, Q&A, and the advice you’ve always needed.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Bob The Drag Queen: Advice Special – Live Recording","instanceDates":"4 December-4 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"508603ACQBJHCSMTTKSNMGSRBCRKRQVDT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-04T21:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-04T21:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-04T21:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-04T21:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Drag","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Created to celebrate the opening of Soho Theatre Walthamstow, Bryony Kimmings’ first solo show for nearly half a decade is about how we have been busy forgetting what it feels like to nuzzle into the bosom of mother nature... and what amazing things will happen if we all remember. \r\nBryony Kimmings was wrangled enough. Single mum, disabled kid, slammed with work, barely keeping it together mentally and physically. She didn’t have time to think about the planet, thanks. But then she fell in love with an eco-warrior... who really wanted to talk about the future of civilisation… a lot. Just what Kimmings needed, some extra guilt and existential dread to pile on life's compost heap.\r\n\r\nBog Witch is Kimmings’ first show for nearly half a decade and it's a solo. It’s the story of her being dragged kicking and screaming into the countryside; decamping her entire life onto a regenerative acre and finding herself plugged directly back into the yucky ecosystem. From slick city bitch to big boggy witch.\r\n\r\nBog Witch is about what happens when you turn and face things instead of hiding from them. Something that at 44, Bryony only just learnt was good to do.  Expect panic, joy and crying (and that’s just from her!) \r\n\r\nThis show is about that weird longing that magically stops when you hold a stone a kid gives you... or you stare into a fire. A show about filling that hole (not in that way, you pervert) but the one in your soul that aches no matter how well you are doing at work, what you buy, how heavy you lift or how many shags you get. \r\n\r\nThe hole that feels… not to be woo-woo, but…ANCIENT.\r\n\r\nBog Witch is about anxiety and apathy, mushrooms and loneliness, vegetables and free stuff, birdsong and paganism, black cats and water supplies, wild flowers and even wilder women. A show about reducing the burden, unpacking the guilt and the joy of stepping up. About loving yourself as the simple, stinking animal you… cos right now everything is TOO MUCH. In Bryony's true ramshackle and glamorous fashion... Songs, screens, stories and lots of recycled costumes.\r\nBog Witch is about uncertain times, the workings of the human brain, doing shit we don’t want to do and finding new ways to be happy.\r\nA show about how we have forgotten what it feels like to nuzzle into the bosom of mother nature... and what amazing and radical things might happen if we all remember.\r\nSpecially commissioned for the launch season of Soho Theatre Walthamstow, Bog Witch is our latest collaboration with Bryony. In the 15 years we have worked together she has created some of the most memorable shows to have played on our stages - from Sex Idiot and Seven Day Drunk to Credible Likeable Superstar Role Model and Fake it ‘til You Make It – and we can’t wait to see what comes next.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":105,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Bog Witch by Bryony Kimmings","instanceDates":"9 October-25 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"601403AMMVTSRLHGPHQTBTMSBVTJTKRNC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-09T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-09T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-25T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-25T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Performance Art","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"TOTAL-SELL OUT: EDINBURGH FESTIVAL FRINGE 2023. It’s Mr. Bean if he was a sexy Asian lady. “it's Benny Hill meets surprisingly friendly sex dungeon; delightful perverted nonsense.” Fest. Part of London Clown Festival 2024.\r\nThis show promises songs and dances in the Music Hall style, delivered by Marny Godden and Tom Turner. This is the tale of a London Fancy Rat.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Bonnie He: A Terrible Show for Terrible People","instanceDates":"11 July-11 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"543603AQTLNRDQRTRJNDBRHRJGHGQCRVN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-11T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-11T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-11T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-11T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Thousands of copies sold and fresh off his Indian tour, Jassa Ahluwalia returns to Soho Theatre to celebrate the launch of BOTH NOT HALF in paperback. Hosted by Eshaan Akbar, with audience Q&A, plus a book signing and street food by Curry On Naanstop!\r\nTicketholders to this event will receive 50% off on all food offers by Curry On Naanstop at Soho Theatre Bar. Valid for one night only.  \r\n12+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Both Not Half: The Paperback Launch","instanceDates":"21 May-21 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"618603AJLBLKBTHHLTHDNKNQSJPJKDNSG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-21T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-21T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-21T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-21T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"One woman clings to a box from her past as the world tilts and sweeps shelter from her feet. Fleeting friendships, custard creams, UK Garage, posh wine and the power of pounded yam keep her afloat. Chance encounters and the quiet magic of everyday survival lead to a hair salon where life - and the box - crack open. “Boxes are usually really disappointing. But no, not this one.”16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Boxes","instanceDates":"3 February-4 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"683603ACKMJHHMGTNKPNNJTJDBHVRDCNJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-03T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-03T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-04T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-04T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"“I wonder what I have to do for people to recognise me as a threat. Do I have to smash a glass over the head of every single man I come into contact with, just so I leave a mark?”\r\nIrina takes erotic photos of average looking men. Always behind the lens, she watches, she moulds, and she stalks. These boys are putty in her hands, just the way she likes it.\r\nWhen the opportunity to show her photographs in a fashionable London gallery – “darling, you just don’t get chances like this in the North” - coincides with a new boy to obsess over, cracks begin to appear. How far can she push her new prey for the perfect shot, or has she already gone too far?\r\nBased on the critically acclaimed debut novel by Eliza Clark (Finalist in Women’s Prize for Fiction) and adapted by Gillian Greer, Boy Parts is a pitch-black psychological thriller that subverts the erotic gaze and asks what happens when our need for connection gets twisted.\r\nDirected by Sara Joyce (Dust by Milly Thomas; Fringe First winning The Last Return) and produced by Broadway World “Best New Production” award-winning Metal Rabbit Productions (Radiant Vermin & Cuckoo, Soho Theatre) and Soho Theatre.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":80,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Boy Parts","instanceDates":"20 October-25 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"481803APNKGSPLJRGLDLNRNPTQTVDSKRM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-20T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-20T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-25T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-25T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A father waits for his son. Kids hang around skipping school. Fights break out after nights of drinking. Featuring six actors in multiple roles, the play is a bold, kaleidoscopic tale of violence and vulnerability, set entirely in the confines of a men's public toilet. \r\n\r\nWritten by Sam Grabiner, the 2022 winner of Soho Theatre’s acclaimed Verity Bargate Award, Boys on the Verge of Tears is a 'brutal, tender' exploration of what it is to be a man. The new play will be directed by James Macdonald, best known for his work with Caryl Churchill and Sarah Kane.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":100,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Boys on the Verge of Tears","instanceDates":"11 April-18 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"513003ABNMSHNCBHVJRDRSRNGBCCTQCHH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-11T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-11T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-18T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-18T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Strap in & strap on for a spicy drag king cabaret romp & come on a journey with Bas Vegas's - barrow boy - Brent Would! Because he would anything…literally anything…especially you!\r\nBrent takes you from being wooed by him to being at one with him, with a peppering of arboreal factoids, in case you thought this show was legitimately about wood. An insight into the lurid & desire filled mind of a drag king with a perpetual hard on for love…who longs to get it right, but so often gets it wrong to hilarious effect! This Essex lad's love of music has led him to write some original sexy pieces and he will even improvise some for you, using your suggestions and interactions. And if you’re dead lucky you can win a date with the man himself. Score! Willing participants only - consent is sexy...just like you!\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Brent Would’s Got Wood by Francesca Reid / Brent Would","instanceDates":"9 February-9 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"520803ATKKKHHBVGDMHKDPSHJPRVKPMMT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-09T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-09T22:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-09T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-09T22:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Comedy"},{"description":"WRITTEN BY Rae Mainwaring \r\nDIRECTED BY Tessa Walker \r\nI was 23 when it came crashing into my life; without warning, when everything was going so well, just when I was really, really happy…\r\nA three-woman, one-woman show about Multiple Sclerosis, MS for short, not to be confused with M&S or S&M.\r\nWith 90s pop, a costume box and a whole heap of glitter, Bright Places is a darkly funny and deeply honest autobiographical story about growing up in the shadow of chronic illness.\r\nPartner & Funder Acknowledgement: \r\nPresented by Carbon Theatre, in association with Birmingham Rep, and supported using public funding by the National Lottery through Arts Council England. The play was originally commissioned by Birmingham Rep in 2020, with generous support from the Barry Jackson Trust.\r\nWe are proud to be working with charity partner, Shift.ms: the digital community for people with MS. \r\nAccess: This production has embedded audio description and creative captioning. \r\n12+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Bright Places","instanceDates":"2 December-7 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"564003ASBLMBSLGQTBRQGNTQHJQLLJTHV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-02T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-02T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-07T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-07T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Access","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"Emmy nominated sketch duo BriTANicK (Brian McElhaney and Nick Kocher) have written for Saturday Night Live, It’s Always Sunny in Philadelphia, and other shows that nobody saw. They were named Variety’s “Top 10 Comics To Watch”, have amassed over 100 million views online, and performed sold out runs at the Edinburgh Fringe, the Soho Theatre, Montreal’s JFL Festival, and all over the US. Come see their brand new show that is 1/3 sketch comedy, 1/3 childhood trauma, and 3/4 them being bad at math.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"BriTANicK: Dummy","instanceDates":"27 August-31 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"557803ANNLMPLRKBBRTNKSMMLGGMQVHND","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-27T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-27T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-31T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-31T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Sketch","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"BriTANicK is the sketch comedy duo of Brian McElhaney and Nick Kocher. Together, they have written for Saturday Night Live and It’s Always Sunny in Philadelphia. After sold out runs at the Edinburgh Fringe and the Montreal Just For Laughs Festival they are thrilled to be returning to Soho Theatre. Join them as they workshop their newest hour.\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"BriTANicK: Work in Progress","instanceDates":"6 March-9 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"518203AMHPCHNJBTPDQDPBGKPRQLQQTMK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-06T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-06T21:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-09T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-09T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Sketch","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Three kids - an emotional tweenager, a four-year old stalker and the middle one. Just when things couldn’t get any harder, she bought a puppy. A million plates in the air, even more smashed on the ground around her feet. Bron wears the battle scars of an ex high-school teacher and is still reeling from the initial shock of motherhood 12 years ago. Tackling juggle-parenting, teaching, career change and flailing mental health, if you’ve ever thought ‘if one thing goes wrong, we’re all dead meat’ this is the show for you. VicScreen Greenlight Award Winner and total sold-out run, Melbourne International Comedy Festival 2026. 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Bron Lewis: Chaos","instanceDates":"20 August-29 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"717203AQLHTRGSGMTCTBRDRQPQHJBSBVR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-20T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-20T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-29T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-29T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Best friends Mohsen and Kash are gearing up for the biggest night of their lives – Jess Denver's pool party. There's just one problem... they can't swim. \r\nFuelled by halal Haribo and chicken wings, the pair throw themselves in at the deep end, tackling cramped cubicles and cold showers as they learn how to be at one with the water. \r\nFierce, funny, and brimming with heart, Karim Khan examines the pressures faced by young Muslim men in this exhilarating new play about fitting in and striking out. \r\nWinner of a Fringe First and the 2022 BBC Popcorn Writing award, Brown Boys Swim embarks on a national tour following sell-out runs at the Edinburgh Fringe and Soho Theatre.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Brown Boys Swim","instanceDates":"3 October-7 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"483403ALVLRBQCMCJRHSDHGBQRNRMPSKP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-03T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-03T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-07T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-07T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"BACK DUE TO POPULAR DEMAND!\r\n\r\nFierce, funny and wonderfully frank, Poppy and Rubina have sex and they aren’t ashamed to talk about it. \r\n\r\nIn this hilarious and ground-breaking show, they explore messy realities, heartbreak, fantasies, sexpectations and navigating life and relationships as British Asian women – and this time on their home turf!\r\n\r\nBringing their trademark honesty, quick wit and infectious personalities to the stage, Poppy and Rubina reflect on what is means to be Brown British women and explore the seminal moments from their lives from first orgasms and loves to racism and family politics.  \r\n\r\nTheir award-winning and groundbreaking BBC Sounds podcast Brown Girls Do It Too (‘Podcast of the Year’ 2020 and ‘Best Sex and Relationship Podcast’ 2023 at the British Podcast Awards, “Best Podcast’ Asian Media 2021), now in its 6th series, has amassed fans who love their honesty and openness (love a period sex sesh…anyone else?) and faced enormous backlash online for breaking the silence on sex in Asian communities.\r\n\r\nWith songs, sketches and some very graphic content, this is a celebration of brown British women, genital warts and all.\r\n\r\nPlease note: This show contains language that could be deemed offensive, such as swearing and adult references.  \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Brown Girls Do It Too: Mama Told Me Not to Come","instanceDates":"9 September-13 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"601003AQMLMBQPTVSCBMKCJBJMKPNDMDP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-09T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-09T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-13T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-13T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"India/South Asian heritage"},{"description":"Fierce, funny and wonderfully frank, Poppy and Rubina have sex and they aren’t ashamed to talk about it.  \r\nJoin them as they preview their hilarious and ground-breaking show ahead of their Edinburgh Fringe debut and Soho Theatre Walthamstow run, as they explore messy realities, heartbreak, fantasies, sexpectations and navigating life and relationships as British Asian women.\r\nBringing their trademark honesty, quick wit and infectious personalities to the stage, Poppy and Rubina reflect on what is means to be Brown British women and explore the seminal moments from their lives from first orgasms and loves to racism and family politics.\r\nTheir award-winning and groundbreaking BBC Sounds podcast Brown Girls Do It Too (‘Podcast of the Year’ 2020 and ‘Best Sex and Relationship Podcast’ 2023 at the British Podcast Awards, “Best Podcast’ Asian Media 2021), now in its 6th series, has amassed fans who love their honesty and openness (love a period sex sesh…anyone else?) and faced enormous backlash online for breaking the silence on sex in Asian communities.\r\nWith songs, sketches and some very graphic content, this is a celebration of brown British women, genital warts and all.\r\n\r\n ‘Gasps of joy…  a show with a solid emotional and political core’ ★★★★ Guardian\r\n\r\n‘As life enhancing as it is entertaining”\r\n★★★★ Evening Standard\r\n\r\n‘Refreshing and riotously funny’\r\n★★★★ Stage\r\n\r\n‘The mix of chit-chat, liberation sexology and the comedy of cultural identity, is a potent one’ \r\n★★★★ Guardian\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":80,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Brown Girls Do It Too: Mama Told Me Not to Come Previews","instanceDates":"10 June-14 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"611203ATVNMVLGQTPDKGLMNJVKVMMPQSQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-10T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-10T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-14T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-14T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Fierce, funny, and wonderfully frank, Poppy and Rubina have sex and they aren’t ashamed to talk about it.  Their critically acclaimed podcast Brown Girls Do It Too (‘Best Podcast of the Year’ British Podcast Awards 2020, Asian Media 2021), explores messy realities, fantasies, sexpectations and navigating life and relationships as British Asian women. \r\n\r\nTwo seasons in, they have amassed fans who love their honesty and openness (love a period sex sesh…anyone else?) and faced enormous backlash online for breaking the silence on sex in Asian communities.\r\n\r\nBringing their characteristic candour, quick wit and infectious personalities to the stage, Poppy and Rubina reflect on the seminal moments from their lives from first orgasms and loves, to racism and family politics. Expect songs, sketches, and some very graphic content!\r\n\r\nThis is a celebration of brown British women, genital warts and all.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Brown Girls Do It Too: Mama Told Me Not To Come.","instanceDates":"23 May-10 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"433203AVHTBSRRJHDDDSQSSPTSJVSLLMD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-23T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-23T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-10T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-10T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Fierce, funny and wonderfully frank, Poppy and Rubina have sex and they aren’t ashamed to talk about it.  \r\n Join them for these limited run WORK IN PROGRESS evenings as they try out some new sketches and ideas and ask for your input, ahead of their run at Soho Walthamstow in September. \r\n \r\nJust like in their full length show, they’ll explore messy realities, heartbreak, fantasies, sexpectations and navigating life and relationships as British Asian women.\r\n \r\nBringing their trademark honesty, quick wit and infectious personalities to the stage, Poppy and Rubina reflect on what is means to be Brown British women and explore the seminal moments from their lives from first orgasms and loves to racism and family politics.  \r\n \r\nTheir award-winning and groundbreaking BBC Sounds podcast Brown Girls Do It Too (‘Podcast of the Year’ 2020 and ‘Best Sex and Relationship Podcast’ 2023 at the British Podcast Awards, “Best Podcast’ Asian Media 2021), now in its 6th series, has amassed fans who love their honesty and openness (love a period sex sesh…anyone else?) and faced enormous backlash online for breaking the silence on sex in Asian communities.\r\n \r\nWith songs, sketches and some very graphic content, this is a celebration of brown British women, genital warts and all.\r\n\r\n ‘Gasps of joy…  a show with a solid emotional and political core’ ★★★★ Guardian\r\n\r\n‘As life enhancing as it is entertaining”\r\n★★★★ Evening Standard\r\n\r\n‘Refreshing and riotously funny’\r\n★★★★ Stage\r\n\r\n‘The mix of chit-chat, liberation sexology and the comedy of cultural identity, is a potent one’ \r\n★★★★ Guardian\r\n\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":45,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Brown Girls Do It Too: Work in Progress","instanceDates":"25 March-20 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"611003AJRPJDSRGJMLRNPQPMTJCJHDBVB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-25T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-25T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-20T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-20T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Brynley's sexual awakening happened when that alien touched Mel B's boob in Spice World: The Movie. Now she's back at Soho Theatre to explore that.\r\nAfter the breakup of her long-term relationship, Brynley gave herself a year to have a wild time and generate some steamy content for her upcoming comedy show…instead she made a show about being Frigid.\r\nPrepare for a raucous hour of absurdist sketch comedy and storytelling from New Zealand’s least sexually active comedian.\r\nAs seen on Taskmaster NZ, Snort Comedy.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Brynley Stent: Frigid","instanceDates":"29 July-3 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"559803ACRPCHBCVJQSKBCDNVQDDPVPRDT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-29T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-29T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-03T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-03T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Sketch","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The self-described Pansexual People’s Princess of New Zealand, Brynley Stent, brings her latest absurdist solo sketch show to Soho Theatre.\r\nAfter a breakup, a haunted holiday house weekend, and a lifetime of irrational fears, Brynley must face the two most powerful forces in her subconscious: abandonment issues, and a sexually aggressive witch.\r\nInspired by the ’90s VHS interactive board game Nightmare, SLUT WITCH is part theatrical horror show, part group therapy session. You’ll laugh*. You’ll scream**. You’ll confess your deepest fear into a papier-mâché well***.\r\n*Not guaranteed.\r\n**Not guaranteed.\r\n***Not guaranteed.\r\nAs seen on Taskmaster New Zealand, Snort Comedy.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Brynley Stent: Slut Witch","instanceDates":"8 August-9 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"639803AHCRJTKMJRBQPLRTHNNCDVGRPSC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-08T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-08T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-09T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-09T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"One of New Zealand's least sexually active comedians Brynley Stent (Taskmaster NZ, Snort Comedy) brings her absurdist solo sketch show to Soho!\r\nLet's raise a toast to lying to your therapist, dancing to call-waiting music, playing the bagpipes at midnight and dealing with emotional shit through the tried-and-true medium of \"making jokes\". Because people like jokes, but they don't like others crying in front of them. \r\nPrepare for a raucous hour of characters, mime* and sketch comedy. \r\n*Brynley broke her wrist recently so please adjust your expectations accordingly for the mime.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Brynley Stent: Soft Carnage","instanceDates":"3 August-5 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"490403ADMHGHDKCTKSCRQTBTJSBHBTGHD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-03T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-03T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-05T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-05T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Nick Cassenbaum invites you into the warmth of the Canning Town Schvitz. \r\n\r\nAmongst the steam, live klezmer and ritual Nick will take you on a journey to find the place he belongs.\r\nBubbemeises is Yiddish, it translates as a grandmother's story, a tall story, an old wives' tale.\r\n \r\nWriter and street performer Nick Cassenbaum invites you into the warmth of the Canning Town Schvitz, East London’s last authentic bath house. Amongst the steam, live klezmer and ritual Nick will take you on a journey to find the place he belongs.\r\n \r\nSchlaping through summer camps, barber shops and Spurs football games. Will he find what he was looking for?\r\n\r\nBubble Schmeisis is full of intimate and personal true stories about identity, home and getting schmeised (washed) by old men.\r\n\r\nNick has been performing this show for ten years and done it over 150 times. The show has not changed…but Nick has and so has the world. (but not the photo- that is 10 years old…not a catfish)\r\nTo celebrate 10 years and to officially retire the show Nick is bringing it back to the Soho theare. \r\n\r\nYour last chance to see it. \r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Bubble Schmeisis","instanceDates":"6 May-10 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"607203ATHRBCQGSPVLSJGTVTVDLPCGBHC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-06T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-06T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-10T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-10T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Winner of the Bruntwood Prize for Playwriting 2022, this is a love letter to Birmingham exploring Black masculinity through Beyonce lyrics, techno raves and the deeply intimate relationship between a man and his barber. \r\nTrim? Fresh. \r\nSkin? Glowing. \r\nVibes? Immaculate. \r\n \r\nNathaniel is a serious romantic who sees love as a fine art. He’s looking for the Mona Lisa to his da Vinci, and tonight is the night: his date with Destiny…’s Child. \r\n \r\nWinner of the Bruntwood Prize for Playwriting 2022, Nathan Queeley-Dennis’ debut play is a love letter to Birmingham, exploring Black masculinity through Beyonce lyrics, techno raves and the deeply intimate relationship between a man and his barber. Directed by Dermot Daly. \r\n14+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Bullring Techno Makeout Jamz by Nathan Queeley-Dennis","instanceDates":"4 November-16 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"551403ALVQBKNDMDBTJHSLPSCTBLTNRQG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-04T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-04T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-16T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-16T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"When Cabaret & Drag Lab put on a show – they really put on a show!\r\n\r\nParticipants have been working with cabaret & drag extraordinaire Me the Queen over 10 weeks, creating exciting new sets for this one-off show. Expect glitter, lip-syncs, queer joy and dancing in your seat. \r\n\r\nIf you’re thinking about applying to the course yourself, come and see what it’s all about.\r\n\r\n18+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Cabaret & Drag Lab Sharing","instanceDates":"17 July-17 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"484403AHLPHTDCTPVKDVVGKBCSVMGKKRJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-17T18:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-17T17:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-17T18:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-17T17:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Description:\r\n(Age restrictions - blurb performance warnings, e.g., haze/nudity/strobe)\tWhen Cabaret & Drag Lab put on a show – they really put on a show!\r\n\r\nParticipants have been working with cabaret & drag extraordinaire Len Blanco over 10 weeks, creating exciting new sets for this one-off show. Expect glitter, lip-syncs, queer joy and dancing in your seat. \r\n\r\nIf you’re thinking about applying to the course yourself, come and see what it’s all about.\r\n\r\n18+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Cabaret & Drag Lab Showcase Dec23","instanceDates":"4 December-4 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"509603AKSTSMMTTRVRTLCRDRHBLVGGJVM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-04T18:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-04T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-04T18:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-04T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"When Cabaret & Drag Lab put on a show – they really put on a show!\r\n\r\nParticipants have been working with cabaret & drag extraordinaire Len Blanco over 10 weeks, creating exciting new sets for this one-off show. Expect glitter, lip-syncs, queer joy and dancing in your seat. \r\n\r\nIf you’re thinking about applying to the course yourself, come and see what it’s all about.\r\n\r\n18+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Cabaret & Drag Lab Showcase Mar24","instanceDates":"18 March-18 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"530403ATVRTLCNMDCBHLSPMRLTPJPMBDK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-18T18:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-18T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-18T18:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-18T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"If you’ve ever been curious about the world of cabaret, drag queens, drag kings and drag things, then this is for you.\r\nCome discover the world of lipsyncing, wild costumes and glitter. \r\nOur Cabaret & Drag taster sessions are run by epic drag king, musician, comedian and performance-maker Len Blanco (All the King’s Men in the West End, All Together Now on BBC One) and drag diva Rhys’ Pieces who has performed all over the UK at Glastonbury, National Theatre, Latitude Festival and Soho House.\r\nOpen to everyone 18+ who’s ever wanted to dip their toe in the water and try some drag and cabaret-style performance. You can have any level of experience (including none at all), from all backgrounds and lived experiences.\r\nSpecialist sessions\r\nSat 10 May and Sat 28 June: Cabaret & Drag taster session for participants from global majority backgrounds.\r\nSat 24 May: Cabaret & Drag taster session for d/Deaf, disabled and neurodivergent participants.\r\nWhile of course we welcome and encourage participants from global majority and d/Deaf, disabled and neurodivergent backgrounds in all of the taster sessions we offer, we also acknowledge that sometimes cabaret & drag spaces can feel exclusive or difficult to access. So with that in mind, the above specialist tasters are for anyone who wants to explore cabaret in a safe space, with other participants who you may share a sense of community with, as well as tailored access support. \r\nYou can do just one or any combination of the above sessions – just book yourself in for whatever you fancy. Please note, these are stand alone sessions, and not a running weekly course. So if you book for multiple sessions some content may be repeated.\r\nSat 10 May 14:00 - 16:30 cabaret & drag taster session for people from global majority backgrounds, led by Rhys’ Pieces \r\nSat 17 May 14:00 - 16:30 cabaret & drag taster session, led by Len Blanco (open to all)\r\nSat 24 May 14:00 - 16:30 cabaret & drag taster session for d/Deaf, disabled and neurodivergent artists, led by Len Blanco and XO\r\nSat 31 May 14:00 - 16:30 cabaret & drag taster session, led by Len Blanco (open to all)\r\nSat 07 June 12:45-15:15 cabaret & drag taster session, led by Len Blanco (open to all)\r\nSat 21 June 14:00 - 16:30 cabaret & drag taster session, led by Len Blanco (open to all)\r\nSat 28 June 14:00 - 16:30 cabaret & drag taster session for people from global majority backgrounds, led by Rhys’ Pieces \r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":150,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Cabaret & Drag Taster Labs","instanceDates":"17 May-28 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"622403AVLHCPRSRMHDBKKHQHHRRHKHBTV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-17T14:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-17T13:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-28T14:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-28T13:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Drag","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Studio","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"When Cabaret & Drag Lab put on a show – they really put on a show!\r\n\r\n\r\nParticipants have been working with course leader Len Blanco and guest artists Donna Poderosa, Me the Drag Queen, Evelyn Carnet and Miss Terri Boxx over 10 weeks, creating exciting new sets for this one-off show. Expect kings, queens, things, lip sync, burlesque, comedy and MORE!\r\n\r\nIf you’re thinking about applying to the course yourself, come and see what it’s all about.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":135,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Cabaret and Drag Lab Showcase","instanceDates":"30 March-30 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"701203AGMDJCQPKLGBJTVPPTJQBMTQNBH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-30T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-30T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-30T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-30T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"When Cabaret & Drag Lab put on a show – they really put on a show! Participants have been working with cabaret & drag royalty Me the Queen and Len Blanco over 10 weeks, creating exciting new sets for this one-off show. Expect glitter, lip-syncs, queer joy and dancing in your seat. If you’re thinking about applying to the course yourself, come and see what it’s all about. 18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":135,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Cabaret and Drag Lab Showcase Dec24","instanceDates":"2 December-2 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"582403ALKVBCCDNMKRDJDHRCLPPKPCVPN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-02T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-02T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-02T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-02T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"When Cabaret & Drag Lab put on a show – they really put on a show!\r\n\r\n\r\nParticipants have been working with course leader Len Blanco and guest artists Wet Mess, Donna Poderosa, Richard Energy, and Me the Drag Queen over 10 weeks, creating exciting new sets for this one-off show. Expect kings, queens, things, lip sync, burlesque, comedy and MORE!\r\n\r\nIf you’re thinking about applying to the course yourself, come and see what it’s all about.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":135,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Cabaret and Drag Lab Showcase Dec25","instanceDates":"1 December-1 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"673003AMVGNJKBBNKJMHKKLCNMVNHBPHR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-01T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-01T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-01T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-01T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"When Cabaret & Drag Lab put on a show – they really put on a show!\r\nParticipants have been working with cabaret & drag royalty Me the Queen and Len Blanco over 10 weeks, creating exciting new sets for this one-off show. Expect glitter, lip-syncs, queer joy and dancing in your seat. \r\n\r\nIf you’re thinking about applying to the course yourself, come and see what it’s all about.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":135,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Cabaret and Drag Lab Showcase Jul24","instanceDates":"15 July-15 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"559003AGHPRRTKMKVRBDDPTNGTQNGLKVD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-15T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-15T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-15T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-15T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"When Cabaret & Drag Lab put on a show – they really put on a show!\r\n\r\n\r\nParticipants have been working with course leader Len Blanco and guest artists Cyro, Miss Terri Box, Evelyn Carnate and Me the Drag Queen over 10 weeks, creating exciting new sets for this one-off show. Expect kings, queens, things, lip sync, burlesque, comedy and MORE!\r\n\r\nIf you’re thinking about applying to the course yourself, come and see what it’s all about.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":135,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Cabaret and Drag Lab Showcase Mar25","instanceDates":"24 March-24 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"613803ALSQGGMPJSCBJSPQHQCHMQKTPPK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-24T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-24T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-24T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-24T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Drag","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Workshops led by TBC ages 18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":150,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Cabaret and Drag Lab Winter23","instanceDates":"7 October-7 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"497003ADMNPGMKGPGQNTCKKCMPPSHMLBJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-07T15:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-07T14:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-07T15:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-07T14:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Our Cabaret & Drag Lab: Plus Showcase features some of London’s most exciting acts, kings, queens and things doing brand new work that is guaranteed to blow you out of your seat...  \r\n\r\nCome see some of the freshest boldest artists of the cabaret and drag scene for one night only. \r\n\r\n15 epic gigging cabaret and drag artists shake up their acts with course leader Me the Drag Queen and guest artists Ella the Great/Richard Melanin III, Bourgeoise, Demi Noire and Cyro over 10 weeks. Pushing the boundaries of their creative practice to present to you new and reimagined acts. Expect kings, queens, things, lip sync, burlesque, comedy, choreography and MORE! \r\n\r\nIf you’re thinking about applying to the Labs courses yourself, come through and see what it’s all about. \r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Cabaret and Drag Lab: PLUS Showcase","instanceDates":"20 July-20 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"735803AKKPHGRHKBMKCHTGDMQBVGGRBLC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-20T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-20T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-20T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-20T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Comedy","attribute_Venue":""},{"description":"Description/copy – bold text intro for website (20-25 words)\tCome see some of the hottest new stars of cabaret and drag be glorious for one night only, before they’re simply too famous.\r\n\r\n\r\nDescription/copy – main copy\t15 epic up-and-coming cabaret and drag artists have been working with course leader Me the Drag Queen and guest artists Demi Noire, Lolo Brow, Elf Lyons and Len Blanco over 10 weeks, pushing the boundaries of their creative practice for this one-off show. Expect kings, queens, things, lip sync, burlesque, comedy and MORE!\r\n\r\nIf you’re thinking about applying to the Labs courses yourself, come and see what it’s all about.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":135,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Cabaret and Drag Lab: Plus Showcase Jun25","instanceDates":"30 June-30 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"633203APJPJTMCGGMHJBQMNDNDDCVMNBL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-30T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-30T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-30T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-30T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Drag","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"An impossible variety show created by John-Luke Roberts. Amazing acts attempt to perform while confronted by obstacles and increasingly difficult circumstances, randomly chosen by spinning wheels. Find out if a singer can still sing with a bubble machine pointed point-blank in their face, how a hula hooper gets on while haunted by a Victorian ghost, or if a comedian's jokes work when the microphone is held in the mouth of the oldest audience member. The late-night sensation of Edinburgh Fringe 2022. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Cabaret Impedimenta","instanceDates":"15 June-15 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"480003ASTBQHQLVHLVKTLMNRTJCGKNRHB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-15T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-15T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-15T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-15T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Comedy"},{"description":"Witness multi-award winning cinematic drag chaos in stunning CinemaScopeVision! \r\nMinimum wage cinema employee turned multi award-winning tragic fool Cabbage the Clown's debut hour marries a buffet of genres in polygamous holy matrimony in the name of drag in their “Gen-Z, loudly queer and thoroughly hilarious” (Binge Fringe) debut hour.\r\nWith over 8 million views online for their genre-busting brand of multimedia drag-clowning, Cabbage presents their critically-acclaimed debut show: One part breathless parody of cinematic history, one part thoughtful dissection of minimum wage careers, one part rolling around on the floor covered in popcorn. So talk through the trailers, get the loudest snacks available, then sit back, relax and enjoy this Bechdel Test-passing, BBFC-unapproved, global premiere.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Cabbage the Clown: Cinemadrome","instanceDates":"14 May-16 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"708603ARHNHGDGHMHBLRKPBLCJSVDPLNT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-14T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-14T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-16T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-16T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":""},{"description":"Witness multi-award winning cinematic drag chaos in stunning CinemaScopeVision!\r\nMinimum wage cinema employee turned multi award-winning tragic fool, Cabbage the Clown's debut hour marries a buffet of genres in polygamous holy matrimony in the name of drag in their \"Gen-Z, loudly queer and thoroughly hilarious\" (Binge Fringe) debut hour.\r\nWith over 8 million views online for their genre-busting brand of multimedia drag-clowning, Cabbage presents their critically-acclaimed debut show: One part breathless parody of cinematic history, one part thoughtful dissection of minimum wage careers, one part rolling around on the floor covered in popcorn. So talk through the trailers, get the loudest snacks available, then sit back, relax and enjoy this Bechdel Test-passing, BBFC-unapproved, global premiere. \r\n16+ ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Cabbage the Clown: Cinemadrome Oct25","instanceDates":"9 October-11 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"659803AHTCCGNPSGNMLJJHTLVHQVNTHGK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-09T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-09T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-11T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-11T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":""},{"description":"Fresh from its sold-out Off-Broadway debut, Caitlin Cook brings you her hit bathroom graffiti musical This is a show for comedy nerds, musical theatre kids, art history buffs, and anyone who's ever seen something written in a bathroom and thought, \"I wonder who wrote that?”\r\nConfessional, immersive, uproariously funny, and a New York Times Critic's Pick, this one-of-a-kind show—literally set in a dive bar bathroom—transforms graffiti scrawled all over the bathroom stalls into the lyrics of Caitlin Cook’s original songs and the trail markers along the hilarious and heartfelt journey she takes us upon.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Caitlin Cook: The Writing on the Stall","instanceDates":"4 June-7 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"605803AKNHKCTJKMNDRBTDKLJSQDVGLLJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-04T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-04T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-07T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-07T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"‘Caleb is one of the most effortlessly funny people I’ve ever met, relax in the immediate knowledge you’re watching someone who was born to do comedy’ – Mae Martin\r\n\r\nCaleb Hearon is a comedian at whom nobody has ever been mad. He currently resides in Los Angeles, where he is a writer for Netflix’s spinoff of their hit show Big Mouth - Human Resources. He recently shot the TBS pilot Space, where he will be a series regular, and will appear in I Used to Be Funny, the feature directorial debut of Ally Pankiw (Feel Good, The Great, Shrill). In 2020, Variety named Caleb one of their Top Comics to Watch and Just For Laughs named him one of their New Faces: Creators. \r\n\r\nCaleb started his career in Chicago where he performed every week at iO Chicago, Second City, The Hideout, and on Twitter (@calebsaysthings), if video monologues count. He can be seen on Showtime’s Work in Progress, FX’s Fargo and opposite Phoebe Bridgers in the MUNA music video for Silk Chiffon. \r\n\r\nHe's originally from Missouri where he was raised by four strong women—his mother, Kellie, and the Dixie Chicks.\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Caleb Hearon","instanceDates":"23 August-26 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"480403AMRMBRVGHSCNSBKNVKKTNJBMCJP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-23T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-23T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-26T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-26T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_Venue":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"There are eight planets in the solar system. Cameron Sinclair Harris will become all of them before your very eyes.\r\nAre we alone in the universe? How do we balance the wonder of discovery with a universal sense of grief? If we could speak to the planets, what would they say back? Cameron Sinclair Harris, earthling, non-binary deviant & Fully Qualified Astronaut will hurl themselves into the galactic void in order to discover the answers. And also for your entertainment. Join them as they become every planet! Every planet! YES! \r\n\r\nPLANETS!!! is a low-budget space odyssey, an existential breakdown disguised as a character comedy show, a howl into the uncompromising yonder of space. Strap in for an hour of rampant silliness & cosmic yearning that will leave you forever stargazing. \r\n\r\nBrighton Fringe 2024 Award Nominee: Gemini Design for Print \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Cameron Sinclair Harris: Planets","instanceDates":"21 February-21 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"590203AMSBTKKQTJJSMPCPCKTRLKCMSLH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-21T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-21T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-21T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-21T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"A love letter in song, Camille’s celebrates dear friend Shane MacGowan, Sinéad O’Connor, David Bowie, Radiohead, Brel, Nick Cave and more.\r\nChameleon-like on stage, each song has a different character with its story to tell. Camille with long-time collaborator Feargal Murray has created an intimate, heartfelt show with a little bit of joyful, mad chaos as her life unravels, capturing the honest response to those much loved and lost.\r\n\r\nDark, sexy, fierce, amusing and mesmerizing, Camille transforms each song she performs into an intense, emotional, and theatrical experience. Expect joy and pure passion.\r\n\r\nVoted “One of the top 25 performances ever on Later with Jools BBC” Daily Telegraph “ and Queen of the Edinburgh Festival\" (BBC), Camille toured with the Pogues, guested at Yoko Ono’s & Richard Thompson’s RFH Meltdown and original star of Olivier Award-winning La Clique. Previously an award-winning architect and painter, Camille was born in London to a French mother and Irish/English father, she grew up in a village in Cork, Ireland listening to her parents & sisters eclectic music collection that shaped her into the unique interpreter she is today.\r\n\r\nThe multi-award-winning singer has stunned audiences around the world with her five-star sell-out performances, including the Sydney Opera House, Royal Festival Hall, The Roundhouse, won the coveted Herald Angel award for her RSC solo performance ‘The Rape of Lucrece’ and recently an Architectural RIAI 2025 award. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Camille O'Sullivan: Loveletter","instanceDates":"24 November-9 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"650003ABCNJLCVJGHQCHDNTTVKLDMLJRH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-24T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-24T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-09T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-09T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Music","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A character comedy night about a depraved Jewish couple’s unique take on kosher matchmaking.\r\nHoward and Michelle Fissure are piloting their warped and wonderful seminar on love and relationships. Including promotional videos and original songs, their live show-cum-workshop encompasses Jewish takes on items you’d find on dating shows. Expect: kosher sex tips, live shidduchs (matchmaking), couples therapy and free chicken soup on tap!\r\n16+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Candy Gigi & Tom Joseph: Chicken Soup Dates","instanceDates":"29 April-29 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"544003AHLTPDTLDBGGBGCCKTTRPJKRPSK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-29T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-29T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-29T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-29T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"A character comedy night about a depraved Jewish couple’s unique take on kosher matchmaking.\r\nUltra-Orthodox, sex positive love gurus, Howard and Michelle Fissure, are back at the Soho Theatre with their warped and wonderful seminar on love, relationships and kosher sex.\r\n\r\nDesigned for everyone of any faith (or none) their live show-cum-workshop includes Jewish conversion therapy, live matchmaking, couples therapy and chicken soup on tap!\r\n16+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Candy Gigi & Tom Joseph: Chicken Soup Dates","instanceDates":"29 July-27 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"636004AMQLCMJGPVRNQSCKBBQQQHQRHMD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-29T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-29T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-27T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-27T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Friday Night Sinner! is a one-woman horror-comedy musical about a Jewish, sexually repressed, newly married maniac.\r\nShe has delusions of grandeur and wants to become the biggest star in the universe – or at least in Borehamwood – and spills her guts out to her guests over a highly unconventional Friday night dinner.\r\n‘Dark, provocative and wild, would do Mel Brookes proud.’\r\nChortle\r\nThere will be twists and turns, gruesome deaths and comedy at its darkest and most horrifying. Think Gypsy meets Stepford Wives, or Sunset Boulevard meets The Exorcist.\r\n‘Glorious… a one-psychopath tour de force’ **** Scotsman\r\nMusic by Jordan Clarke\r\nDirected by Valentina Ceschi\r\n\r\n18+ recommended ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Candy Gigi: Friday Night Sinner!","instanceDates":"3 May-20 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"438603AHLGHJLHPPRMRNRCKQPPGBRJMHK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-03T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-03T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-20T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-20T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Cara and Kelly are best friends, soul mates even. It’s 2013. They’re 14 and in the prime of their lives! Kelly is smashing it on the netball team. Cara is certain that love is blossoming with her crush. Most importantly, they’re gonna be besties forever. But everything starts to go wrong when a new face arrives. Things that once seemed certain are no longer quite so clear. Cara and Kelly, who’ve never had to doubt each other before, start to question how far they’re willing to go for their friendship.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Cara and Kelly Are Best Friends Forever For Life","instanceDates":"13 February-14 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"683604AJBJBBVTKTSRCHHHCGNNVJGMRRG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-13T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-13T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-14T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-14T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Carl used to spend the Fringe in a haze of booze, narcotics and award nominations but now finds himself a married middle-aged father with recurring stomach ulcers, a bald patch and recently even considered purchasing some anti-leakage boxer shorts. Oh god. A show about the indignity of ageing while being happier for it. \r\n\r\nPreviously nominated for both the Best Newcomer and Best Show in the Edinburgh Comedy Awards, he’s appeared on ‘Mock The Week’ and ‘Russell Howard’s Good News’. He has also performed at every major comedy festival including Melbourne, Just For Laughs and more as well as recently supporting Kevin Bridges on his international tour. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Carl Donnelly: Boosegumps","instanceDates":"3 January-4 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"586403AJDNKHGMHKCSGBTJGTHLSNPLJJB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-03T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-03T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-04T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-04T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Course Info:\r\nCarnesky's Finishing School Soho\r\nIntroduction to solo short-form performance and cabaret including classes in conceiving, devising, making, producing and presenting.\r\n10 week evening class for performers and beginners\r\nThursday evenings\r\nSeptember 15th - November 17th\r\n6pm - 9pm\r\n6 - 12 Manette Street, London W1D 4AT\r\n£250\r\n\r\nCarnesky's Finishing School\r\nFrom September 1st - December 31st 2016 artist Marisa Carnesky takes on the role of headmistress at the Carnesky's Finishing School Soho. This 'School for Illegitimate Entertainers of all Persuasions' is St Trinians for the queer esoteric cabaret generation. Over the coming months you will have 3 opportunities to sign up for Carnesky's ever popular performance creating, devising, and presenting intensives, drop-in classes in hula hooping, lip synching and magic and weekend courses run by an eclectic bunch of artist and cabaret professionals.\r\nThis is your chance to unleash the hidden performance artist inside yourself under the unique tutelage of performance provocateur Dr Marisa Carnesky and join her demented array of graduates.\r\nCarnesky's Finishing School Soho is putting the heART back into Soho, with a unique performance, exhibition & bar space created and programmed in partnership with the legendary Bethnal Green Working Men's Club and artist-in-residence John Lee Bird.\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":180,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Carnesky's Finishing School Evening Classes","instanceDates":"29 September-29 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":"421","id":"68001AVGQGHPGPGDNBSVTRMTDGHNQRSLV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2016-09-29T18:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2016-09-29T17:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2016-09-29T18:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2016-09-29T17:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_Venue":"Carnesky Finishing School Soho","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Carnesky's Finishing School Soho\r\nconceiving, making and presenting performance\r\n5-day intensive for beginners\r\nOctober 14th, 15th, 16th, 22nd and 23rd\r\n11am - 5pm\r\n6 - 12 Manette Street, London W1D 4AT\r\n£250\r\n\r\n\r\nCarnesky's Finishing School\r\nFrom September 1st - December 31st 2016 artist Marisa Carnesky takes on the role of headmistress at the Carnesky's Finishing School Soho. This 'School for Illegitimate Entertainers of all Persuasions' is St Trinians for the queer esoteric cabaret generation. Over the coming months you will have 3 opportunities to sign up for Carnesky's ever popular performance creating, devising, and public presenting intensives, drop-in classes in hula hooping, lip synching and magic and weekend courses run by an eclectic bunch of artist and cabaret professionals.\r\nThis is your chance to unleash the hidden performance artist inside yourself under the unique tutelage of performance provocateur Dr Marisa Carnesky. Come and join her esteemed array of demented graduates.\r\nCarnesky's Finishing School Soho is putting the heART back into Soho, with a unique performance, exhibition & bar space created and programmed in partnership with the legendary Bethnal Green Working Men's Club and artist-in-residence John Lee Bird.\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":360,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Carnesky's Finishing School for Beginners","instanceDates":"14 October-14 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":"420","id":"67802ADJQJRBTTBGCCBHVGCSMVTTPPHQL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2016-10-14T11:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2016-10-14T10:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2016-10-14T11:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2016-10-14T10:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_Venue":"Carnesky's Finishing School Soho","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Carnesky's Finishing School Soho\r\nPerformance conceiving, making and presenting \r\n5-day intensive for performers\r\nSeptember 16th, 17th, 18th, 24th and 25th\r\n11am - 5pm\r\n6 - 12 Manette Street, London W1D 4AT\r\n£250\r\n\r\nLink to information on Carnesky’s Finishing school\r\nhttp://carnesky.com/productions/work/carneskys-finishing-school/","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":360,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Carnesky's Finishing School for Solo Performers","instanceDates":"16 September-16 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":"419","id":"67601AVHPCSTMMBKTGKLCGLQQCGMMBVSK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2016-09-16T11:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2016-09-16T10:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2016-09-16T11:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2016-09-16T10:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_Venue":"Carnesky's Finishing School Soho","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Ivo Graham steps away from the frivolity of his stand-up and invites you onto his own carousel: a searingly direct, exquisitely soundtracked story of a life. \r\nIvo Graham, who has watched this Mad Men clip approximately 100 times, steps away from the frivolity of his stand-up and invites you onto his own carousel: around and around, backwards and forwards, to the places he aches to go again. \r\n\r\nA searingly direct, exquisitely soundtracked story of a life: good luck at your next meeting.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Carousel: A Theatre Show by Ivo Graham","instanceDates":"28 May-7 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"609003AKTKGDDGCQNGLCKPHSNSGJRVNMC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-28T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-28T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-07T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-07T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The Man. The Myth. The Idiot. \r\nTobias Finlay-Fraser is the greatest actor of his generation. Only problem is, he's played by little-known actor/comedian Casey Filips. \r\nVirtuoso is an award-winning one-man comedy hour following actor Tobias, a pretentious yet charming idiot doing anything he can in the audition of a lifetime.\r\nWinner: Take a Chance Adelaide Award 2024 Adelaide Fringe\r\nWinner: Judges' Pick 2024 Melbourne Fringe\r\nNominated: Best Comedy Melbourne Fringe 2024\r\nMervyn Stutter's Pick of the Edinburgh Fringe 2024\r\n•\t'Utterly brilliant' 5 Stars -The Age\r\n•\t'A ridiculously well-crafted night of fun' 5 stars -Funny Tonne \r\n•\t'A flawless hour of impressive character comedy' 5 stars -AYoungishPerspective\r\n•\t'Monstrously funny' 4 Stars - The List\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Casey Filips: Virtuoso","instanceDates":"4 September-6 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"649003AHPNNRKMRTGQKKJPHQJLJVDSVHG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-04T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-04T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-06T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-06T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Sketch","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"\"What a character\" – Ancient Australian proverb. Idiom, used to describe either the best or worst person you know. Example: \"Wow, that Casey Filips… what a character\" Following his critically acclaimed debut show Virtuoso, multi award-winning Australian comic Casey Filips brings us a brand-new character hour that’s 'as genius as it is absolutely hilarious' ***** (EdFringe Review). 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Casey Filips: What a Character","instanceDates":"26 November-28 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"757603AJVBCCNCTRHHVVJTRBKSDDMTSJH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-26T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-26T22:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-28T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-28T22:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Multi Award-winning Cassie Workman time travels through nineties Washington, to unravel life, death, and rock and roll, in this heartbreaking homage to an icon.\r\nIn 1994 the world lost one of its most beloved musicians; grunge icon, Kurt Cobain. Part eulogy, part fantasy, part biography, Aberdeen, is an in-the-round conversation with Kurt, about life and death, taking place across Washington, including his hometown, of Aberdeen. Traverse time and space as multi award-winning comedian and storyteller Cassie Workman races in a desperate bid to save the life of her hero, by attempting to manipulate time itself. \r\n\r\nAberdeen is an epic, about loss, music, and memory; an extraordinarily heartfelt love poem, to the voice of a generation.\r\n\r\nWINNER: Scotsman Fringe First 2022\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Cassie Workman: Aberdeen","instanceDates":"5 December-16 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"504003AJTMRJGSPSPRTVTTPRSJMBGJJNQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-05T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-05T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-16T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-16T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"After a sell-out run of shows in February, Edinburgh Comedy Award winner Cat Cohen returns to Soho to preview her next show ‘Broad Strokes’, with new jokes and songs never heard before in the UK.\r\nFollowing acclaimed tours for ‘The Twist... ? She’s Gorgeous’ and ‘Come For Me’, specials on Netflix and VEEPS, and her 2024 album OVERDRESSED, Cat is back in London to try out her brand new show.\r\n\r\nAs seen on Cats Does Countdown, Only Murders In The Building, Girls5eva, What We Do In The Shadows and the Off Menu podcast.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Cat Cohen: Work In Progress","instanceDates":"15 July-17 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"630203AQNNPGQTCNJCCVCSVKHBQPTMDTR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-15T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-15T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-17T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-17T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Edinburgh Comedy Award winner Cat Cohen returns to Soho Theatre to workshop her next show, with new jokes and songs never heard before in the UK.\r\nFollowing acclaimed tours for ‘The Twist... ? She’s Gorgeous’ and ‘Come For Me’, specials on Netflix and VEEPS, and her 2024 album OVERDRESSED, Catherine is back in London to try out brand new material.\r\n\r\nAs seen on Cats Does Countdown, Only Murders In The Building, Girls5eva, What We Do In The Shadows and the Off Menu podcast.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Cat Cohen: Work In Progress.","instanceDates":"18 February-1 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"596803AKHRSSMVJKKJRNKKJSSNNHBBNBJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-18T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-18T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-01T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-01T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Come and create your very own Cat in the Hat hat to take home, inspired by the magical world of Dr. Seuss. With fun, creativity and plenty of imagination, this interactive workshop is the perfect way to anticipate the upcoming stage show. All materials are provided – just bring your imagination! Only children need tickets; adults can participate or watch the session, but children should remain accompanied at all times. ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":30,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Cat in the Hat Workshop","instanceDates":"25 July-25 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"740003ALHSPLDJHJMMRJNHSKCMMQMMNJB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-25T11:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-25T10:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-25T14:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-25T13:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Families","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Family","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"The 2024 Edinburgh Comedy Award nominee is back and ready to talk about her feelings (again)...\r\nJoin one of the UK and Ireland’s most-exciting comics for a hilariously twisted second coming-of-age saga as she reckons with death-obsessed parents, queer reproduction and how adulthood, frankly, isn’t living up to her expectations.\r\n\r\nHost of hit podcast Trusty Hogs. As seen and heard on Live at the Apollo, The Mash Report, Immaculate (Amazon Prime special), Mock the Week and The News Quiz.\r\n\r\nEdinburgh Comedy Awards 2024 Best Show Nominee\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Catherine Bohart: Again, With Feelings","instanceDates":"4 December-10 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"568603AGRHTKRCJMVSBDCKHLHNSHRTNKN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-04T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-04T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-10T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-10T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Join one of the UK and Ireland’s most-exciting comics for a special filming of her Edinburgh Comedy Award nominated hit show Again, With Feelings. \r\nA hilariously twisted second coming-of-age saga as she reckons with death-obsessed parents, queer reproduction and how adulthood, frankly, isn’t living up to her expectations.\r\n\r\nHost of hit podcast Trusty Hogs. As seen and heard on Live at the Apollo, The Mash Report, Immaculate (Amazon Prime special), Mock the Week and The News Quiz.\r\n\r\nEdinburgh Comedy Awards 2024 Best Show Nominee\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Catherine Bohart: Again, With Feelings (Live Recording)","instanceDates":"16 September-16 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"654003AJMRMLQJTMKKQCHHKKCRHDKJCMC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-16T18:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-16T17:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-16T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-16T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Catherine Bohart’s back and older than ever. And adulthood frankly isn’t living up to her expectations.\r\nJoin this “effortless” (Chortle) “star in the making” (Skinny) for a hilariously twisted second coming of age saga as she reckons with death obsessed parents, living in a house share with OCD and queer reproduction in her thirties.\r\n\r\nAs seen and heard on Live at the Apollo, The Mash Report, Immaculate (Amazon Prime Special) and Mock the Week.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Catherine Bohart: Again, With Feelings at Cambridge Junction","instanceDates":"2 June-2 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"537203ACRBLTTRVKLPPBCJKHVHCCTKKVP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-02T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-02T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-02T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-02T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Cambridge Junction","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Catherine Bohart’s back and older than ever. And adulthood frankly isn’t living up to her expectations.\r\nJoin this “effortless” (Chortle) “star in the making” (Skinny) for a hilariously twisted second coming of age saga as she reckons with death obsessed parents, living in a house share with OCD and queer reproduction in her thirties.\r\n\r\nAs seen and heard on Live at the Apollo, The Mash Report, Immaculate (Amazon Prime Special) and Mock the Week.\r\n\r\n“She keeps the laughs coming” Times\r\n\r\n“A show that’s worth holding onto” Guardian\r\n\r\n“Pretty much the perfect comedy package” Beyond The Joke\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Catherine Bohart: Again, With Feelings.","instanceDates":"4 March-23 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"506804AHLTDRNMNHJHQHRNKKVVRVDPHJK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-04T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-04T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-23T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-23T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Edinburgh Comedy Award nominee Catherine Bohart is back with a brand new show in 2026, and you should be there!\r\nPerfect Makes Perfect will be Catherine's best show yet, and she can't wait to see you. \r\nAs seen and heard on Live at the Apollo, QI, The Last Leg, A League of Their Own, Mock the Week, The Mash Report, The News Quiz, Last One Laughing Ireland, and her Amazon Prime special Immaculate. Host of hit podcast Trusty Hogs. Edinburgh Comedy Award nominee 2024.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Catherine Bohart: Borrowing Trouble","instanceDates":"21 September-3 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"670003ALQSRHVLLMPSDDVQGPHQGGVMSJQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-21T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-21T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-03T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-03T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Catherine Bohart is back with a brand new show about her birthright - all encompassing, generational worry. But it’s a laugh! As seen and heard on Live at the Apollo, QI, The Last Leg, A League of Their Own, Mock the Week, The Mash Report, The News Quiz, Last One Laughing Ireland, and her Amazon Prime special Immaculate. Host of hit podcast Trusty Hogs. Edinburgh Comedy Award nominee 2024. 16+ (See webpage for current information).","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":100,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Catherine Bohart: Borrowing Trouble ","instanceDates":"19 February-19 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"755203AVRSKBQTRMQNCVPRTNVMTSVRTRT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-19T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-19T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-19T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-19T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"An hour of new material from Catherine Bohart. As seen and heard on Live At The Apollo, Mock The Week, Roast Battle, 8 Out of 10 Cats, The Stand Up Sketch Show and The Guilty Feminist Podcast. \r\n \r\n‘Destined for stardom’ (Evening Standard)\r\n‘The laughs keep coming and, finally, so does a tear or two. Marvellous’ ★★★★ (Times)\r\n‘Beautifully-delivered hour’ ★★★★ (Skinny)\r\n‘Packed full of laughs’ ★★★★ (Herald)\r\n‘A winning mixture of self-deprecation and confidence’ ★★★★ (Beyond The Joke) \r\n‘A fully developed comic voice’ ★★★★ (Fest)\r\n‘Truly special’ ★★★★ (Edinburgh Festivals Magazine) \r\n\r\n16+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Catherine Bohart: Work in Progress","instanceDates":"23 August-23 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"467403ADNPJLSVBBJNHBVMTGBMLRSRTPG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-23T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-23T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-23T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-23T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"It’s been nine years since Celia Pacquola last graced a UK stage. Nine years! She went back to Australia because she missed the spiders and since then, she’s been busy. Celia has filmed multiple comedy specials, was nominated for best show at the Melbourne International Comedy Festival three times, starred in hit Aussie series (Utopia, Rosehaven), hosted the legendary Thank God You’re Here, won a bunch of awards, swore on live TV, made a quiche for the first time and also a baby. Now, she’s back, and it’s time for a catch-up (where only she talks).\r\n \r\nNot familiar with Australian TV? No worries. You might remember Celia from Live at the Apollo, Russell Howard’s Good News, The Rob Brydon Show, or Never Mind the Buzzcocks. Or maybe you caught her during one of her acclaimed Edinburgh Fringe runs or at live shows up, down and across the UK between 2010 and 2016.\r\n \r\nI’m As Surprised As You Are is Celia’s seventh and best hour yet. It’s a silly, gossipy, wine-fuelled hour of personal stories from a performer at the top of her game. Four shows only. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Celia Pacquola: I’m As Surprised As You Are","instanceDates":"29 April-3 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"614203ACCJKVVTMTNJQGNHRSPCNHNLRJQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-29T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-29T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-03T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-03T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"‘One of the most gifted joke writers of our age’ ★★★★ (Chortle), the Live At The Apollo star returns with a brand new show.\r\nThe only light, the white screen of a challenging email Celya was drafting. The only sound, the tap-tap-tap of the keyboard. This was, without a doubt, “rock bottom”. Also contains hot takes on judges, toothpaste and the sexiest thing anyone can do on a date.  \r\n \r\nFollowing multiple sell-out tours and barnstorming appearances at JFL Montreal and Melbourne ICF, Celya is back to tackle the big three: beauty, money and the void, in her most personal show yet.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Celya AB: Of All People","instanceDates":"21 January-4 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"574203AGVDRGDPTSVVGDDBBHJCMKCDJNQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-21T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-21T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-04T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-04T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"As a child, all she wanted was to be an adult. Now she's at the table, she wants out.\r\nFollowing her acclaimed, debut hour Swimming selling out multiple runs at London’s Soho Theatre and the Edinburgh Fringe, Celya returns with her stunning follow up, Second Rodeo for her first UK tour. Expect tales of romance, a hologram and a near-death experience in Thorpe Park. Named Chortle’s Best Newcomer 2022, Celya has been seen on the BBC, Comedy Central and Funny Festival Live, and supported Fern Brady, Maria Bamford and St Vincent on tour.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Celya AB: Second Rodeo","instanceDates":"23 January-27 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"507803APMSDBQQMQMRHGKBGGLSDTSGJTC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-23T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-23T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-27T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-27T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Fresh from a sell-out run at the Edinburgh Fringe this summer, this is the stunning debut hour full of “sharp and observant gags” (Joe Lycett) from one of comedy's most exciting breakthrough voices. A show about moving from Paris to Birmingham, finding yourself and learning to swim at 25. Chortle Best Newcomer winner 2022. Star of BBC’s New Comedy Award and Funny Festival Live. Tour support for Maria Bamford, The Guilty Feminist and St Vincent. Celya's magnetic stage presence and brilliantly crafted material has been seen on Comedy Central and the BBC. \r\n\r\n\r\n“Great jokes, both classy and funny. A thoroughly engaging presence… a fine talent”\r\nChortle\r\n\r\n“A knowing, multifaceted show…with an instinctive silliness.” \r\n★★★★ The Scotsman\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Celya AB: Swimming","instanceDates":"1 April-1 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"423603APSNCNDMHGBCCLBSNRSQDTHDDKK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-01T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-01T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-01T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-01T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Come and see participants of Soho Theatre’s Character Comedy Lab transform themselves for you in the name of comedy for just one night (well, afternoon) only. \r\nParticipants have been working with course leader Jonathan Oldfield for 10 weeks to create brand new comedy characters that they’re now ready to share with the world! Get ready for belly laughs and surprises. \r\n\r\nIf you’re thinking about applying to the course yourself, come and see what it’s all about.\r\n16+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Character Comedy Lab Showcase Dec24","instanceDates":"7 December-7 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"582603AJKSQQVNHJTQRKJKGNJJBLBJQCH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-07T12:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-07T12:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-07T12:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-07T12:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Whether you fancy developing a comedy character or enjoy improv games and ridiculous personas, our Character Comedy tasters might just be for you.\r\nCreate a new character, unlock your creativity and find what makes you uniquely funny by trying out our Character Comedy taster. From Diane Morgan to Victoria Wood, Alan Partridge to Lolly Adefope, there’s a rich history of UK character comedians - now it’s your turn to find freedom, joy and hilarity in yourself, by pretending to be somebody else. \r\n\r\nLed by award-winning performer, writer and director Jonathan Oldfield (who was a BBC New Comedy Award Finalist 2024, co-creator of BBC Radio 4 sketch show Time of the Week and recently appeared in Nick Mohammed's A Christmas Carol-ish in the West End) and iconic actress, writer, comedian and improviser Kathryn Bond (of critically acclaimed comedy That Pair, now performing her solo show Loo Roll around the country. Doctor Brown's Channel 4 Blaps, Call the Midwife, Radio 4 Sketchorama and Expenses Only).\r\n\r\nOpen to everyone 18+ who’s ever wanted to try stand-up. You can have any level of experience (including none at all), from all backgrounds and lived experiences\r\n10 May 10:30-13:00 character comedy taster session, led by Jonathan Oldfield\r\n17 May 10:30-13:00 character comedy taster session, led by Jonathan Oldfield\r\n24 May character comedy taster session, leader TBC\r\n31 May 10:30 - 13:00 character comedy taster session, led by Kathryn Bond\r\n07 June 15:30 - 18:00  character comedy taster session, led by Kathryn Bond\r\n21 June 10:30 - 13:00 character comedy taster session, led by Kathryn Bond\r\n28 June 10:30-13:00 character comedy taster session, led by Jonathan Oldfield\r\nYou can do just one or any combination of the above sessions – just book yourself in for whatever you fancy. Please note, these are stand alone sessions, and not a running weekly course. So if you book for multiple sessions some content may be repeated.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":150,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Character Comedy Taster Lab","instanceDates":"10 May-28 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"622604ATVRVPHJBDVTQPRRTKDTCJVKKSB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-10T10:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-10T09:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-28T10:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-28T09:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Studio","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Come and see brand new character comedy from the freshest acts in the game.\r\n\r\nParticipants of Soho’s Character Comedy Lab have spent the last 10 weeks playing and exploring character with course leader Jonathan Oldfield and guest artists Sarah McGuiness and Lorna Rose Treen. Expect mayhem.\r\n\r\nIf you’re thinking about applying for the course yourself, come along and see what it’s all about.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Character Lab Showcase Mar25","instanceDates":"29 March-29 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"614003AHPSKTGGTCHPKMDVKVDPLTHSBMT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-29T12:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-29T12:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-29T12:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-29T12:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"This is a show about a break up - but think ‘Bridget Jones on acid’ not ‘Eat, Pray, Love’. \r\n\r\nFrom the winner of Best Comedy at Adelaide Fringe 2026 and Shortlisted Best Newcomer Ish Edinburgh Comedy Awards 2025, this ‘brilliant mix of character work and clowning’ (Chortle) comes to Soho for two nights only. \r\n\r\nCome witness the chaotic car crash of Amber’s breakup, as she valiantly attempts to find love again—with help from a horny nun, a lonely star, and a bona fide man-eater. \r\n\r\n'Likely the funniest thing you'll see all day' ****1/2 A Young(ish) Perspective \r\n\r\n'Exquisitely pitched performance' **** The Scotsman \r\n\r\n'One-part Rik Mayall to one-part Adam Riches' **** Chortle \r\n\r\nDirected by Caitlin Campbell\r\n\r\n4 stars - Chortle \r\n4 stars - The Scotsman \r\n4.5 stars - A young(ish)perspective \r\n4 stars - Ed Fringe Review\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Charlie Mulliner: Love Hunt","instanceDates":"12 June-13 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"717003ANMTHKCVMJVGDKKSPDLHTCGVPGT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-12T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-12T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-13T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-13T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Funny Women Stage Award and Sketch Off 2023 finalist Charlie Vero-Martin brings her surreal character comedy fresh from the Edinburgh Fringe. Packed with laughter, puppets and dark twists, this is a one-woman sketch show like no other. \r\n\"Hilarious character sketches stuffed to the gills with mad ideas from a truly gifted performer” **** (The Wee Review)\r\n\"This show is absurd and silly, but it is also carefully crafted\" **** (One4Review)\r\n\"so unhinged\" **** (Edinburgh Reviews)\r\nRecommended by the British Comedy Guide and Telegraph’s Best Comedy Shows and Jokes of the Fringe\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Charlie Vero-Martin: Picnic","instanceDates":"14 February-14 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"522603ACLPVNCNSDHKBHVHHKNGMGHDBGK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-14T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-14T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-14T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-14T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Sketch","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"What if your anger just simmers underneath? If it never quite reaches boiling point, but it's present, burning your insides. Combining spoken word, football chants, live art and theatre, Chat Sh*t, Get Hit dives into women's anger: how it fuels, how it festers and how it is swallowed. \r\nA funny and uncompromising show about recovery, solidarity and the suppression of women's rage. \r\nWritten & performed by Martha Pailing \r\nDirected by Ursula Martinez \r\nDramaturgy by Annie Siddons \r\nTechnical Design by Lily Dawford \r\nCostume Design by Moa Johansson \r\nEdinburgh Fringe produced by Jenny Gilvear \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Chat Sh*t, Get Hit","instanceDates":"5 February-6 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"683803AKLQNCRNJRSGNDJCGVSKQKTJDPD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-05T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-05T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-06T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-06T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Chelsea Birkby returns to Soho Theatre Downstairs with her double-award nominated sophomore stand-up hour (Best Show: Comedian's Choice Awards, Edinburgh Comedy Festival ISH Awards). Playfully combining pop culture and philosophy, this smart and silly show unpacks being in the moment, desire and also ass. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Chelsea Birkby: This is Life, Cheeky Cheeky","instanceDates":"19 May-19 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"618003ADVMLLHCQKTPRRDGKKPKDVNHDHJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-19T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-19T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-19T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-19T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"What does a kebab wrapper, a flat white and an ASBO all have in common? Meet Cherry, Dagenham’s answer to Frank Gallagher. She’s shameless and wants you to know why. After a life changing medical diagnosis, Cherry has a few final words and two middle fingers she wants to share with the public.\r\n“I’m selfish, and greedy, and a bit of a cow. But I own those stripes. Like a badge of damn honour. There is nothing no one round here can tell me about myself because it’s the foundations of my own internal dialogue. Not in like a depressing way, but a self-acknowledgement - I wake up in the morning and it’s who I am. My permanent makeup. A selfish, greedy cow.”\r\nFollowing on from a sold out run at the Vault’s Festival 2023, Cherry! Returns to the stage. Written by Maygan Forbes and directed by Hamish Clayton, this isn’t a tale of hometown glory – Cherry wants the world to know she’s everything you hate, dirty, raw and so much more\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Cherry by Maygan Forbes","instanceDates":"7 February-7 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"521003ARNNKCPQDVGVMDDBTLLBPHVSDLK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-07T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-07T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-07T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-07T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"'Funny, charming, and hilariously honest, Chin is fast becoming one of the most exciting new acts to see' (The Comedy Store). ‘She has a charming air of being cheerfully baffled by it all,.. evokes some cartoonishly amusing mental images’(Chortle)\r\nBorn and raised in China, Chin Wang left her homeland for the UK at the tender age of 18. At the still-tender age of 28, She had enough of both countries and decided she should lead a new country. A Wang-derful nation has therefore been born. \r\nFresh from Edinburgh Fringe. this show is all about the oddities of British culture, the illogical language of English, and also a few hazard warnings for any first generation immigrants from East Asia to the UK. (This show should not be used as a survival guide, but it should be, though.) \r\n\r\nAs seen on BBC 3, as heard on BBC Radio. Tour support for Olga Koch. Nominated for BBC New Comedy Award 2022. Finalist of Scottish Comedian of the Year 2021. 2NorthDown New Act Competition 2021. Winner of King Gong at The Comedy Store. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Chin Wang: Wang's Republic","instanceDates":"6 February-6 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"521203APVTLHNNNPQLPSJJPPKKGHVTMGL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-06T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-06T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-06T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-06T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Following three sell-out shows, Chloe Petts (Live at the Apollo, Have I Got News for You) returns with a brand-new tour, and she's delving where she's never delved before: this is a show about sex. The problem is that she blushes every time she says that word. \r\nExpect routines about Page 3, lad culture and most importantly, big, fat naturals.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Chloe Petts: Big Naturals","instanceDates":"2 January-17 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"646603ADLTLSNBHMLMCDBSHQBNSQHHHCD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-02T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-02T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-17T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-17T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Chloe Petts, breakout star of Taskmaster S22 (Ch4) and \"one of the most compelling young comics\" (The Guardian), returns with a new stand-up hour of trademark critically-acclaimed cerebral laddishness. After four successful smash-hit tours, show number five examines Petts’ newfound identity as a Passenger Princess, a tricksy snake called Medusa, and the trials and tribulations of being the only sober one at a Pitbull concert. It's Petts' most honest show yet.\r\nOn television and radio, Petts has also appeared on Have I Got News For You (BBC1), Live at the Apollo (BBC2), Bake Off: An Extra Slice (Channel 4) and has been a regular host on Sky Sports News. In terms of podcasts, Petts has appeared on Off Menu with (Ed Gamble and James Acaster), Shagged. Married. Annoyed. (Chris & Rosie Ramsey), Films to Buried With (Brett Goldstein) and co-hosted The Guilty Feminist alongside Deborah Frances-White.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Chloe Petts: Call Me By My Surname","instanceDates":"25 January-6 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"754803AJTSSNCJPPDTMGMKCLQGNRSHLHH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-01-25T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-01-25T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-06T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-06T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"After two consecutive critically acclaimed shows, rising star Chloe Petts is back on the road with a brand-new hour… and this time she’s getting personal.\r\nBetween her newly found trolls, oldly found school bullies, and an excellent relationship with her food tech teacher, Chloe brings her trademark laddishness to tell you who she really is, all while her Head Girl badge glistens upon her chest. \r\nStar of Hannah Gadsby's Gender Agenda (Netflix), host of Toilet Humour (BBC Radio 4), has had her own regular segment on Sky Sports News, and has also been seen and heard on Have I got News for You (BBC), MOTDx (BBC), The Frank Skinner Show (Absolute Radio), Jonathan Ross’s Comedy Club (ITV), The Stand-Up Sketch Show (ITV2), and Richard Osman's House of Games (BBC).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Chloe Petts: How You See Me, How You Don't","instanceDates":"9 June-14 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"596203ACPBKLRDVKQPRBHQCGPRBMQLQMG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-09T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-09T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-14T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-14T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"After two consecutive critically acclaimed shows, rising star Chloe Petts is back on the road with a brand-new hour… and this time she’s getting personal.\r\nBetween her newly found trolls, oldly found school bullies, and an excellent relationship with her food tech teacher, Chloe brings her trademark laddishness to tell you who she really is, all while her Head Girl badge glistens upon her chest. \r\nStar of Hannah Gadsby's Gender Agenda (Netflix), host of Toilet Humour (BBC Radio 4), has had her own regular segment on Sky Sports News, and has also been seen and heard on Have I got News for You (BBC), MOTDx (BBC), The Frank Skinner Show (Absolute Radio), Jonathan Ross’s Comedy Club (ITV), The Stand-Up Sketch Show (ITV2), and Richard Osman's House of Games (BBC).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Chloe Petts: How You See Me, How You Don't Jan25","instanceDates":"13 January-25 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"549203AHQHTPDTDCNJSCJJSGVPVSTGTNR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-13T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-13T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-25T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-25T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Fresh from her smash hit Edinburgh Fringe run and Soho Theatre sell-out debut, Chloe Petts returns with her follow-up hour. Everyone complimented her on how polite she was with big issues in the last show so now she's cashing in those points and plans on being really rude. Expect routines on Greta Thunberg, the footie and calling you all a bunch of virgins.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Chloe Petts: If You Can’t Say Anything Nice","instanceDates":"30 October-4 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"491003ASVVLTDCPNQGSDHVCBCJGGSRMRJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-30T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-30T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-04T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-04T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"In this gutsy, honest and electric solo show from a New York City-based rising star, Chloe Radcliffe admits to the guilty secret that most people keep forever. (FYI: Coming to the show doesn’t make you a cheater… actually, avoiding it seems way more suspicious). Chloe starred in Command Z from Steven Soderbergh, was named one of New York Magazine’s Comedians You Should And Will Know, has been seen on Comedy Central and After Midnight, and was a writer for The Tonight Show with Jimmy Fallon.16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Chloe Radcliffe: CHEAT","instanceDates":"15 May-17 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"609203ANKVSPGHPQTSPBLBHGCBRTLVSMG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-15T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-15T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-17T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-17T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A reluctant adventurer and an unlikely fellowship converge in this epic tale of an overdue reunion gone awry.\r\nJoin Edinburgh Comedy Award nominee Chris Cantrill as he wrestles with the consequences of exile, middle-aged friendships, and the best way to admit you wear a cape sometimes. As seen on Alma's Not Normal (BBC 2) and Don't Hug Me I'm Scared (Channel 4). Thrice-nominated for the Edinburgh Comedy Award (Best Show). Co-creator of BBC Radio 4 series Icklewick FM. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Chris Cantrill: Easily Swayed","instanceDates":"19 September-7 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"568203AKGCRMKPNPGNNDCKGQQJQLDLSNP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-19T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-19T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-07T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-07T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Edinburgh Comedy Award winner, Chris Cantrill (SNL UK, Icklewick FM) returns with a new show about community, vengeance and custard. The critically-acclaimed Rewilding tells the story of a rural borderlands community, an act of vandalism and the outsider who’s determined to make it all about him.\r\n \r\nHaving embraced village life, Chris is happy to see out his days whittling, signing for packages and glaring at passing hikers. But when a beloved local tree is cut down in the dead of night, he’s drawn into a mystery that reveals a far darker side to his idyllic surroundings …\r\n \r\nRewilding is a show for people who are passionate about community and keeping a very close eye on their neighbours. \r\n \r\nDirected by Edinburgh Comedy Award nominated Tom Parry.  16+ (Check webpage for content advice).","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Chris Cantrill: Rewilding","instanceDates":"23 November-5 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"748403AMRHVSHHVHRKJSPCMDTBMCTPKRP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-23T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-23T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-05T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-05T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"I’ve heard the expression ‘Stop being so dramatic” my whole life, but only now, at the culturally relevant age of 34, am I ready to address it and face these drama queen allegations head-on. Please join me, Chris Parker, for an hour of high-intensity, feverishly paced and dizzyingly expressive comedy. Sure, I’ve cried in every speech I’ve ever had to deliver publicly, and yes, there may have been a situation this year where I slept on my neck weirdly and bought myself an unnecessary neck brace. Still, I’m desperate to prove that I’m really chill and down to earth. So, what better way to get you to understand that than with a one-man variety hour spectacle chill stand-up comedy hour at London’s Soho Theatre?\r\nNew Zealand superstar Chris Parker returns to the UK after six years away and almost too many achievements to list here: he’s competed on Taskmaster New Zealand, Thank God You’re Here, and Guy Mongtomery’s Guy Mont-Spelling Bee; toured sold-out theatre across New Zealand and Australia; hosted the New Zealand Comedy Festival Galas; and created and written his own critically acclaimed sitcom Double Parked.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Chris Parker: Stop Being So Dramatic!","instanceDates":"18 August-23 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"634803ALDSBHMSMJHBDPSJJLTPNPGCMLG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-18T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-18T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-23T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-23T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"New Zealand superstar Chris Parker returns to Soho Theatre with a brand-new show, after a sold out week of performances last year.\r\n“Hello! I've been vying for your attention for a long time now. I'd comfortably say, it's been 30 years. Thirty years of trying to make people look at me. In that time there have been many attempts to try and masquerade it as something \"important\" or \"educational\" but the longer I've sat with it, the more I've come to accept that it could maybe just be vanity. So I won't sugar coat it in the blurb. There're no secrets about to be dished, no valuable lesson to take away. I'm just a 35-year-old gay man, who was told there was something special about him as a kid and has been grappling with that ever since, standing in front of an audience asking them to take a good hard look at ME!” Chris Parker has competed on Taskmaster New Zealand, Thank God You’re Here, and Guy Montgomery’s Guy Mont-Spelling Bee; toured sold-out theatres across New Zealand and Australia; hosted the New Zealand Comedy Festival Galas; and created and written his own critically acclaimed sitcom Double Parked.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Chris Parker: Take A Good Hard Look at Me","instanceDates":"17 August-22 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"709403ANKQPLCPPBKDVBBSSHVRGQBBKGG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-17T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-17T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-22T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-22T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Chris Ramsey: Here Man (Live Special Recording)","instanceDates":"22 April-22 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"702603ADRCVNRBJHRTMGQDDSDDRLCLDLV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-22T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-22T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-22T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-22T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Former Saturday Night Live star, Emmy Award winner, and star of his HBO stand-up special returns to London’s Soho Theatre with a brand new hour.\r\nChris Redd’s first one-hour comedy special “Why Am I Like This?” premiered in November of last year and is currently streaming on HBO MAX. He co-created and is set to voice a lead role in a yet-to-be titled project from Broadway Video and Audible, and stars opposite Eddie Murphy in CANDY CANE LANE. Redd is the co-creator, writer, and star of Peacock’s scripted comedy series, “Bust Down”. He was a repertory player on NBC’s “Saturday Night Live” for 5 seasons. \r\nRedd received the Emmy Award in 2018 for Outstanding Original Music and Lyrics for the “SNL” song “Come Back, Barack.” In 2019 Redd released his debut stand-up album, “But Here We Are.” He appeared in the 2016 film “Popstar: Never Stop Never Stopping” and opposite Kathy Bates in the Netflix original comedy series “Disjointed” and was featured in the series “Wet Hot American Summer,” NBC’s “Will & Grace,” Netflix’s “Love”, Comedy Central’s “Detroiters” and “Comedy Central Stand-Up Presents.” He portrayed the character of ‘Gary Williams’ on the NBC comedy “Kenan” for two seasons. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":false,"name":"Chris Redd: Workin’ On Me","instanceDates":"14 May-24 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"530203AJVDBQPDCCKCBLDHNLKCGKLQVGK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-14T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-14T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-24T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-24T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"CHRISTEENE is a raw spirit of ferocious music, unabashed sexuality, and fiery intimate stank.\r\nReports from live shows describe raw and intimate exchanges, distressed choreography, macabre scenes involving butt plugs tied to bouquets of balloons being released from the singer’s ass, wardrobes styled from the forgotten scraps of society, and heated sermons on the state of the world as we know it.\r\n\r\nThe artist has collaborated with as well as performed with numerous acclaimed musicians, including Faith No More, Peaches, Fever Ray, John Grant, Kembra Pfahler, Suicide, Roddy Bottum, Tribe 8, Narcissister, Marc Almond, Bronski Beat, and Justin Vivian Bond. Longtime collaborators include award winning filmmaker PJ Raval, along with iconic fashion designer Rick Owens and artist Michèle Lamy. CHRISTEENE has been photographed by Juergen Teller, Katerina Jebb, Matt Lambert and Wolfgang Tillmans, and featured in magazines such as anOther, Noisey, Dazed, Art Forum, Spin, Vice, Numero, The New Yorker, Interview, Man About Town. \r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"CHRISTEENE","instanceDates":"7 June-7 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"599003ATRGBHJLMCSBRSCJTNTMLHRCNRP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-07T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-07T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-07T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-07T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"LGBTQ+","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join CHRISTEENE at the afterparty to celebrate her Soho Theatre Walthamstow show.\r\n\r\nFeaturing guest DJs until 2am.\r\n\r\nAdvance booking essential. \r\n18+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":240,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"CHRISTEENE: AFTER PARTY","instanceDates":"7 June-7 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"602803ABMNRGLTRRRVGHLPMJLBQCSQPDT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-07T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-07T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-07T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-07T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"LGBTQ+","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Christian Dart brings his acclaimed smash hit, sell-out EdFringe 2025 show GUMSHOE! to Soho Theatre!\r\n\r\nA grizzled New York Detective embarks on his final, most deadly and most ridiculous case yet. Join Gumshoe as he attempts to solve the unsolvable case. Who did the whodunnit?! \r\n\r\nEmbark on an exciting, comedy noir adventure written and performed by award-winning comedian Christian Dart. Can you help solve the case? \r\n\r\nBest Show: Leicester Comedy Fest 2025 - Nominee\r\nFinalist: Sketch-Off! 2025\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Christian Dart: Gumshoe!","instanceDates":"7 November-8 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"660603ASMJLGPDJPMSMKNTBSMQPGGMCRH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-07T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-07T22:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-08T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-08T22:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Sketch","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join the London Gay Men’s Chorus as we pull our fabulous festive cracker to kickstart the festive season for 2026!\r\nFeaturing artists from Pink to Kelly Clarkson; The Sugababes to Wham and the iconic, homegrown E17 alongside hits from Sister Act, Mary Poppins and Sunset Boulevard, this will be a rollercoaster of Christmas hits and camp surprises packed with audience fun! Over 100 singers from the chorus with a live band will fill this fantastic theatre with music, magic and mayhem. With bespoke arrangements, stunning harmonies and slick choreography, the chorus will deliver an unforgettable Christmas show with its signature style.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Christmas Cracker - London Gay Men's Chorus","instanceDates":"7 December-7 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"748203AVJBSRLSRJJMLMDTRBGCRLTCLNK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-07T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-07T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-07T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-07T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Shropshire’s worst writer has decided to pull on his socks and sandals, comb his curtains, and leave Shropshire for the fifth time in his life to bring his latest show to Soho Theatre.\r\n\r\nRob Carter's brilliant alter-ego returns, as seen on 8 Out Of 10 Cats Does Countdown teaching Suzie Dent about the English language.\r\n\r\n★★★★★ Mervyn Stutter's Pick of the Fringe\r\n“This is how character comedy should be done” - ★★★★ Chortle\r\n\"Truly unique... when you're not laughing, you're left hooked on this man's every word\" ★★★★ Deadline News\r\n“Deliciously Fun” - The Guardian\r\nBritish Comedy Guide Recommended Fringe Show 2022\r\n\r\nWARNING: Some of the material in this show is extremely nice.\r\n\r\n16+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Christopher Bliss: Captain Words Eye","instanceDates":"16 May-18 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"468203ADGQGVTNDBJMTLBPQJCDTRRLBBD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-16T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-16T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-18T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-18T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A new hour of stand-up by the wee guy with the glasses from Glasgow.\r\nFeaturing routines and jokes on such topics as Edinburgh Zoo, going for a walk, and the collapse of the British state. As seen on Frankie Boyle’s New World Order, Comedy Central Live and BBC New Comedy Awards, and heard on the Enjoy An Album and Some Laugh podcasts. Tour support for Frankie Boyle and Susie McCabe.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Christopher Macarthur-Boyd: Scary Times","instanceDates":"23 May-25 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"516403ASKDQKQNMPGKDJGBJNMCNNDJVMG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-23T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-23T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-25T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-25T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"There's anarchy in the monarchy as renowned swordsman and dumb hussy Don Rodolfo has risen from humble peasant to the highest seat in the land. But now, with his enemies at the gates, King Rodolfo is forced to look back on his inglorious reign as one of the most bloody, violent and sexy periods in history. An epically funny action-adventure and follow-up to the smash-hit Don Rodolfo. \r\n\r\nWinner - Edinburgh Comedy Award 2018 - Best Newcomer\r\n\r\n'The funniest show you will see this year' **** (Telegraph\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ciaran Dowd: King Rodolfo","instanceDates":"17 April-22 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"439403ALKKRHKVSQBJHTNNJNTBKHHDVKN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-17T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-17T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-22T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-22T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Ever wanted to run away with the Circus? Now is your chance. These exciting and accessible sessions delivered in partnership with Walthamstow Youth Circus, offer a range of ground-based circus skills including juggling, devil sticks, hula hoop, acrobatic balance, walking globe, rolla bolla and clowning.Through games, creativity and the magic of circus you will develop new skills in balance, coordination, strength and flexibility and be ready for life under the big top!\r\n\r\nFamily Circus – for ages 6 to 11 (plus parent/carer) \r\nA session for children and their grown - ups to work together.\r\n \r\nYoung Person Workshop (11 - 18) \r\nA session for older children to work together. \r\n\r\nThis workshop is fully accessible and suitable for complete beginners. You will be required to fill in a consent form to take part. Unfortunately, this workshop isn’t suitable for pregnant individuals.  \r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Circus Skills Workshop ","instanceDates":"25 July-25 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"739803AJSJQJQJDRVGMTHRHTKKVSMRRGT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-25T10:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-25T09:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-25T14:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-25T13:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Families","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Step right up to witness the power of Disability, a power the world tries to take from us. Cirque du Handicap is a show celebrating the power within Disability. It features exaggerated circus acts, theatre and spoken word poetry to represent the life of Disability activist, writer and actor Simi Roach. The performance takes us through Simi’s life story to demonstrate how the world tries to diminish the natural power within Disabled people. Audience interaction included.  \r\n  \r\nSimi Roach is a Jamaican-British actor, writer, and Disability justice activist. Their work explores Disability culture, history, and innovative Disabled representation through both written fiction and live performance. Simi has also performed as a spoken word poet, public speaker and educator, and is both an experienced stage and screen actor.  \r\n\r\nStep right up and spread the word! The circus is about to come to town.  \r\n\r\nStarring: Simi Roach and Rudzani Moleya  \r\nSet and prop designers: Luca Apostolos and Varvara Ivanova  \r\nComposer: DJ OTDelta \r\nPromotional art: Theo Angel \r\n\r\n“It was such a rich and powerful piece. A true expression of identity and, at its core, a celebration and ode to life itself. I laughed, I teared up, and I really enjoyed getting to know more of who Simi was through the work. I found the choice of a circus setting especially interesting. There is such a striking contrast between the vulnerability and raw honesty of their voice on race, disability, and life events, set within something almost comical and entertaining.”  \r\n  \r\n“I wish I could eloquently illustrate how great Simi’s performance was. It was bold, bare, brave, black, commanding, courageous, funny, heartwarming, heartbreaking, eye-opening, intensely engaging, educational, and most importantly, connecting! They’ve got real star power. It was an honor to be in the audience. I’m looking forward to seeing what else they have under their Ringmaster's hat.”  16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Cirque du Handicap","instanceDates":"21 August-22 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"733403AGNDGTDHSMVVCTGDKQBNHDDBCTR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-21T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-21T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-22T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-22T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Access","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Boorish Trumpson is your rehearsal conductor. Just for rehearsal. No other ambitions. None. Nope… \r\n\r\nAn interactive, music and clowning-filled satire of power from critically acclaimed Lecoq-trained clown Claire Parry.\r\nBoorish Trumpson is your rehearsal conductor. \r\nYOU are the orchestra. \r\n#MakeMusicGreatAgain. \r\n\r\nWith clowning games, audience interaction and unexpected orchestral manipulations, Boorish Trumpson will stop at nothing to gain ultimate control over the orchestra\r\n. A unique sound-design, virtuosic physicality and script constructed from quotes and tweets of Trump and Johnson creates a raucous humour whilst the bigger questions bubble below: in our world of troubled politics, how complicit are we in enabling such figures to rise to the top? An interactive, music and clowning-filled satire of power and those who wield it from critically acclaimed \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Claire Parry: Boorish Trumpson","instanceDates":"20 February-20 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"590403AQNMGNQCJRBTCBQHRVGMCDKQTKH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-20T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-20T22:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-20T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-20T22:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"In this intimately absurd hour, Woolner attempts to perform a retrospective of her ‘greatest’ works, only to embark on a battle with her own maniacal self-loathing and loads of fruit. Part of London Clown Festival 2024.\r\nClaire Woolner, Los Angeles based absurdist comedian, blows hard on the brutalist edges of performance art and swims into surrealist clown in this intimate evening in which she attempts to perform a retrospective of her 'greatest' most 'moving' and 'important' work. \r\nAbsurdist comedic bits, playful performance pieces and authentic breakdowns, make this an experience of tragicomedy at its finest. Teetering between what is intended and what is improvised, A Retrospection brings the audience on an exciting (and at times nerve wracking","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Claire Woolner: A Retrospection","instanceDates":"13 July-13 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"544803ASBPDPQKHRRGTNDDLKMGDKGLGCM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-13T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-13T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-13T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-13T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"In this intimately absurd hour, Woolner attempts to perform a retrospective of her ‘greatest’ works, only to embark on a battle with her own maniacal self-loathing and loads of fruit.\r\nClaire Woolner, Los Angeles based absurdist comedian, blows hard on the brutalist edges of performance art and swims into surrealist clown in this intimate evening in which she attempts to perform a retrospective of her 'greatest' most 'moving' and 'important' work. \r\nAbsurdist comedic bits, playful performance pieces and authentic breakdowns, make this an experience of tragicomedy at its finest. Teetering between what is intended and what is improvised, A Retrospection brings the audience on an exciting (and at times nerve wracking) ride of ego battle, failure and creativity and how to survive, discover and connect amidst them all.  \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Claire Woolner: A Retrospection","instanceDates":"17 July-20 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"554003AKNRMRNCLPSHMJBGNSRHCMNMPKN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-17T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-17T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-20T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-20T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join Sunday Times Bestselling author, journalist and TV presenter, Candice Brathwaite, and her co-host, comedy star of TikTok, presenter and actor, Coco Sarel, for the first ever live recording of their critically-acclaimed podcast - Closet Confessions!\r\nFor one night only you'll be invited into the closet as Candice & Sarel share their most intimate and hilarious stories. From laugh-out-loud accounts of dating disasters to tales of bad behaviour and hot takes on celebrity culture, this will be an unforgettable - and confessional - evening. \r\nBuy your ticket here but don’t forget - what’s said in the closet, stays in the closet…\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Closet Confessions: Live!","instanceDates":"27 June-27 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"479803AKPSQHLHBLMJMBQLPGCVKDNSJSG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-27T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-27T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-27T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-27T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Distinguished guests–hold on tight as we try to let go.\r\nWelcome to the Closure Cabaret, a vaudevillian variety show hosted by Razmatastique–your hopefully devoted, French-accented emcee who cannot let her exes rest in peace. Instead, she summons them back for one final encore in pursuit of that ever-elusive promise: closure. \r\nFrom bad-boy playground pirates to wannabe hip-hop stars and emotionally unavailable illusionists, each former flame returns with a glittering cabaret act–jazz-handed into public inspection.  \r\nExpect quick changes, original music and riotous audience participation as Razmatastique leads us through an odyssey of romantic misadventure. \r\nCreated and performed by Maria Ansdell, this solo clown and character comedy show exposes romance as performance–and heartbreak as something we compulsively replay. \r\nSomewhere between a theatrical fever dream and an emotional exorcism, Closure Cabaret prompts the question\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Closure Cabaret","instanceDates":"5 June-30 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"713003ACNMKLLHDMDSBLGKGBGQTBTDKVQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-05T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-05T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-30T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-30T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The Fringe-First-winning triple-Offie-nominated immersive club/theatre experience comes to Soho. Join Lemon Jelly’s Fred Deakin and his cast on an interactive joyride through his wild 80s/90s clubland adventures. Travel back in time to help Fred and his five-strong cast recreate his classic club nights and bring the fashion tribes of the late 20th century back to life. Or just watch! “A raucous house party that doubles as a meditation on counter-cultural extinction” (The Guardian), over two and a half hours this innovative show switches between theatre and club mode to tell Fred’s story. Dancing is very welcome and indeed encouraged, but all participation is entirely optional and the show can be fully enjoyed without leaving your seat.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":150,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Club Life","instanceDates":"7 July-12 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"623603AKJPHGQJMPGJLVBBCKDHQKDKNHB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-07T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-07T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-12T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-12T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Cody Dahler: The State of This!\r\nWhy are our rivers full of more shit than the average tabloid newspaper? Why are seemingly intelligent people voting for Reform UK? And why do our PMs change more often than your bedsheets?\r\nAward-winning comedian, satirist, political writer, and straight-talking oracle to over 2 million followers across his platforms, Cody is one of the funniest and most accessible voices making sense of the absolute state of modern Britain.\r\nIn this brand-new live show, Cody will be joined on stage by fascinating special guest hosts discussing his book and answering your questions head-on, whether they be deep, dumb or deranged.\r\nExpect fast-paced, fact-filled plunges into the history and origins of our current political malaise, as Cody takes on today's deteriorating climate of identity-driven, social-media hot-take, culture war-fuelled brainrot politics.\r\nHilarious, insightful and entertaining, this is an evening guaranteed to leave you feeling sharper, less baffled, and absolutely not looking like a thicky thicky dumb dumb in front of your mates.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Cody Dahler: The State of This!","instanceDates":"4 November-16 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"724203ASTBKBQKKBGPKBQPDRDTTMLDSDN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-04T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-04T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-16T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-16T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Political","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Cody Dahler's Book 'The State of This!'","instanceDates":"4 November-16 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"738603ALRNDHGDVBTTHJVLPTNQRJBCRJD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-04T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-04T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-16T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-16T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\t<img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/sohotheatre/files/0945c21d-4443-4359-9b1e-5ec82607f865.jpeg\" /><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Nam dapibus eros at risus auctor sagittis.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><ul><li> Sed ut perspiciatis unde omnis iste </li><li> Neque porro quisquam est, qui dolorem </li><li> Sed ut perspiciatis unde omnis iste natu