 you’re thinking about applying to the course yourself, come and see what it’s all about.\r\n\r\n18+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Comedy Plus Lab Showcase Mar24","instanceDates":"23 March-23 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"531603APHDBQGNLNLNPKHGVRVMPGCCJHV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-23T15:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-23T15:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-23T15:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-23T15:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":160,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Comedy Sans Frontiere","instanceDates":"31 January-31 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"675603ACBQLKVGKMCCKPLKKPSRNKKGMSJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-31T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-31T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-31T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-31T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Come and see participants of Soho Theatre’s Stand-Up Lab make their stand-up comedy debut. Quick, before they’re all famous!\r\n\r\n\r\nThe group have spent the last 10 weeks discovering the artform for the first time and developing new skills with course leader Sikisa Bostwick-Barnes and guest artists  Kemah Bobb and Morgan Reese.\r\n\r\nIf you’re thinking about applying for the course yourself, come and see what it’s all about.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Comedy: Stand-Up Lab Showcase","instanceDates":"7 April-7 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"702003APTBGDLPTDRMBKBBGDCRBKTHNDM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-07T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-07T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-07T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-07T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Come and see participants of Soho Theatre’s Stand-Up Lab make their stand-up comedy debut. Quick, before they’re all famous!\r\n\r\n\r\nThe group have spent the last 10 weeks discovering the artform for the first time and developing new skills with course leader Sikisa Bostwick-Barnes and guest artist Josh Glanc.\r\n\r\nIf you’re thinking about applying for the course yourself, come and see what it’s all about.\r\n18+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Comedy: Stand-Up Lab Showcase Dec25","instanceDates":"8 December-8 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"673603AKSHHTPSBGRHJLJGHCQPCGPMCTK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-08T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-08T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-08T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-08T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"A creative, social and physical well being meet-up for people over 50.\r\nSoho Theatre and Leyton-based Communi-tea and bringing these relaxed and informal sessions to the the new Soho Theatre Walthamstow this summer. \r\n\r\nEach session includes a satisfying combination of chair-based Yoga-inspired exercise plus a Soho Theatre intro to theatre and comedy workshop. \r\n\r\nAll abilities are welcome. The session is unpressurised and you can participate in as much as you want.\r\n\r\nThe intro to theatre will be led by Jessica Green, the Communi-Tea workshop leader.\r\n\r\nThe comedy workshop will help you find your comedic voice and hone your writing and performing skills. Led by theatre-maker and performer Ben Salmon you’ll be able to do as little or as much as you;re able and willing to do.\r\n50+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":150,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Communi-tea: Meet up for over 50s","instanceDates":"13 May-12 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"620003ANSBHVGSTSDRMQJKRRCCLQKDSMG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-13T14:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-13T13:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-12T14:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-12T13:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Studio 1","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Access","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Quick Duck Theatre Presents Confetti Written & Performed by Will Jackson\r\nStar Reviews:\r\n“A Rising Comic Star” Attitude Magazine\r\n“A Gleeful, Glittery One-Man Rom-Com” The Scotsman\r\n★★★★★ - “A Cracking Show\" British Theatre\r\n★★★★★ - “Unmissable!\" Everything Theatre\r\n★★★★★ - “Comedic Genius!\" Feminist Fringe Reviews\r\n★★★★★ - “Fabulous!\" Somewhere: For Us\r\n★★★★ - “Magical” Voice Magazine\r\n★★★★ - “Hilarious” EdFringeReview\r\n ★★★★ - “Terrifically fun!” Mix Up Theatre\r\n \r\nWill Jackson, star of Yours Sincerely (“A Rising Comic Star” Attitude Magazine), returns to Soho Theatre with his new Edinburgh Fringe smash hit. Confetti is a hilarious, queer romcom  led with Jackson’s infectious charm. \r\n“The perfect 00s rom-com, Richard Curtis can eat his heart out.” ★★★★★ Everything Theatre\r\nFelix is uptight and unlucky in love. He’s the mate of honour at his best friend’s wedding - one they’ve been planning since childhood - and he’s going to make sure it’s absolutely perfect. That is, as long as there are no distractions along the way…\r\n“A Gleeful, Glittery One-Man Rom-Com” The Scotsman\r\n“One wedding you wouldn’t want to miss” ★★★★★ North West End\r\nConfetti is produced by Quick Duck Theatre with funding and support from New Vic Theatre, Arts Council England & Attenborough Arts Centre.\r\nCredits:\r\nWriter & Performer Will Jackson\r\nDirector Hannah Birkin\r\nDesigner Maria Terry\r\nMovement Director Eleanor Rattenbury\r\nComposer & Sound Designer Tom Rackham\r\nDramaturg Joanna Bowman\r\nProduction Manager Chaz Webb\r\nCo-producer Ben Anderson\r\nAssistant Producers Hannah Valente & Jo Wickham\r\nCarpenter Matthew Gardner\r\nPromotional Photography Emma Jones\r\nShow Photography Rachel Baker\r\n\r\n13+ recommendation ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Confetti","instanceDates":"13 July-15 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"464603APHQMNPCSGGHQHJLVMMDJMHHVPQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-13T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-13T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-15T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-15T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Storytelling","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"Conner O'Malley presents new research on Comedy products and showcases newly developed Comedy technologies, including sustainable comedy technology that will innovate the global digital comedy makerspace with new videos, stand up, and much much more.\r\n\r\nAs seen in Joe Pera Talks with You, I Think You Should Leave with Tim Robinson, Shrill and Broad City.\r\n\r\n18+ guildline","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Conner O’Malley: Research and Development Comedy","instanceDates":"10 July-15 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"475403AMQBNKMTVJBKMDRJBDDLNGTGRSN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-10T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-10T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-15T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-15T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Conner O'Malley presents new research on Comedy products and showcases newly developed Comedy technologies, including sustainable comedy technology that will innovate the global digital comedy makerspace with new videos, stand up, and much much more.\r\n\r\nAs seen in Joe Pera Talks with You, I Think You Should Leave with Tim Robinson, Shrill and Broad City.\r\n\r\n16+ recommendation","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Conner O’Malley:(OLD) Research and Development Comedy","instanceDates":"24 April-29 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"438803ARLSKHCKQHTDJMLVKMMGNBNTRVS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-24T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-24T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-29T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-29T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A punchline-packed show featuring submarines, relationships and the inevitable family drama from Scotland’s fastest rising comedy star.Hot on the heels of a totally sold out 2023 Edinburgh Fringe, which saw him add over 2000 extra seats, Scotland’s fastest rising comedy star comes to Soho Theatre.\r\n\r\nVertigo\r\nA sensation of whirling and loss of balance.\r\nOED\r\n\r\nVERTIGO is a punchline-packed show featuring submarines, relationships and the inevitable family drama. Hilarious, relatable, a bit rude in places of course and all-the-while served up with superb material, brilliant delivery and proper belly laughs. \r\n\r\nIn 2023 Connor sold-out multiple solo shows across Australia over a two-month tour, opened for the international stand-up tour Daniel Sloss and closed the Sydney Comedy Festival gala at the Sydney Opera House. In June Connor filmed his debut comedy special, “Vertigo” at the Glasgow Stand for future release. And in 2022 he toured Downunder an unprecedented three times in one year additionally taping a set in Sydney for the illustrious Just For Laughs Comedy Festival.\r\n\r\nConnor toured Australia an unprecedented three times in a single year in 2022, recording a set in Sydney for the prestigious Just For Laughs Comedy Festival. In 2023 he returned to sell-out multiple solo shows across Australia, opened Daniel Sloss’s international stand-up tour and closed the Sydney Comedy Festival gala at the Sydney Opera House.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Connor Burns: Vertigo","instanceDates":"16 November-18 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"503803ADKQVDJKJNQKNCGCLMPNRRHBKSJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-16T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-16T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-18T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-18T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A clown odyssey: Fisherman Jon invites you to embark on an epic voyage of self discovery, to find out what is truly on the end of his rod. Part of London Clown Festival 2024.\r\nJon, a lonely fisherman sailing the seas, catches something unexpected… unbeknownst to Jon, this catch will change his life forever.\r\n“What’s on the end of my rod?” is an evocative and beautiful clown-odyssey told by a loveable idiot discovering the true power of love.\r\nWritten by: Coral Bevan, Ricky Hunt and David Alwyn.\r\nDirected by: Ricky Hunt and David Alwyn.\r\nCharacter created by: Coral Bevan\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Coral Bevan: Fisherman Jon: What’s on the end of my rod?","instanceDates":"13 July-13 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"544603ARGKMDNVSCRGDLJCPGHCDDQRVJR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-13T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-13T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-13T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-13T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A real-life ghost story from an award-winning comedian. Kirsty bought a house. Sure, it was derelict. And in a dodgy area. And OK someone just died in it. But she didn't mind because she didn't believe in ghosts. She does now. \r\n\r\n'The Woman in Black meets Catherine Tate' ★★★★★ (The Fourth Wall). \r\n★★★★★ (Fringefeed).\r\n★★★★★ (The Scoop). \r\n★★★★★ (Fringe Benefits). \r\n★★★★★ (Scenestr). \r\n\r\nWinner: Best Theatre, Adelaide Fringe 2026. \r\nWinner: Best Comedy, Fringe World 2024.\r\n\r\n18+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"CORPSE","instanceDates":"2 February-13 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"743603ASBDQBQLPTJLGDSQVMLQJBGVRRJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-02T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-02T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-13T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-13T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"New Writing","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Comedy"},{"description":"From the creators of LESBIAN SPACE CRIME and PANSEXUAL PREGNANT PIRACY comes this bone-chillingly hilarious riot and gay goth’s wet dream\r\nButch loner Count Dykula loves her life, even though she’s technically dead. Her gothic castle slaps and she gets to prey upon humans who stray behind the big Asda. \r\nBut trouble looms when cultural powerhouse Scare Universi-ty starts preaching “the right way to be a monster”, and the ultra-femme busty bloodsuckers being presented as the per-fect vampire girlies are a far cry from the Count. \r\nWith her masculine pride hanging on by a cheap carabiner, she sets out to tear down Scare U’s human-normative re-gime. After all, she loves a garlic naan and can only turn into a bat after a few beers. \r\nWith more fake blood, fake boobs, and bats (real) than ever before, COUNT DYKULA is Airlock Theatre’s third big queer musical extravaganza. From the creators of LESBIAN SPACE CRIME and PANSEXUAL PREGNANT PIRACY comes this bone-chillingly hilarious riot and gay goth’s wet dream. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Count Dykula","instanceDates":"11 February-1 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"584003ALQPLDPTCJHBPCKHTRMBMKRBQVJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-11T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-11T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-01T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-01T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"After two sell-out runs earlier this year, Courtney Pauroso is back at Soho Theatre for 10 shows due to popular demand!\r\nLA clown Courtney Pauroso returns as sex robot Vanessa 5000, who - over the course of her product demonstration - grows increasingly conflicted about technology, modernity and her own existence. Artificially intelligent. Genuinely stupid. ChatGPT ain't got nothing on Vanessa 5000's sweet synthetic ass. Directed by Corey Podell. \r\nCourtney Pauroso is an award-winning actor, writer and comedian based in LA. She co-wrote and appeared in Two Pink Doors, a series of 5-minute shorts for FX, directed by Dr Brown, and has several television projects in development with long time collaborator Natalie Palamides, including a series produced by Mark Duplass. She was a series regular on Like & Subscribe, and has also appeared in Jackass Forever, Reno 911, Key & Peele, 2 Broke Girls, Florida Girls, The Opening Act, and Dogleg. She is a former member of the Groundlings Sunday Company and Washington D.C.’s internationally renowned physical theatre company Synetic Theater.\r\nSold Out Run: Edinburgh Fringe (2019)\r\nSold Out Run: New York Comedy Festival (2019)\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Courtney Pauroso: Vanessa 5000","instanceDates":"13 December-22 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"507403ATJLBGNGHDLRPDVPHPJHCPPHQGB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-13T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-13T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-22T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-22T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"After a soldout run of her debut show Gutterplum in 2019, LA clown Courtney Pauroso returns as sex robot Vanessa 5000, who - over the course of her product demonstration - grows increasingly conflicted about technology, modernity and her own existence. Artificially intelligent. Genuinely stupid. ChatGPT ain't got nothing on Vanessa 5000's sweet synthetic ass. Directed by Corey Podell. \r\nCourtney Pauroso is an award-winning actor, writer and comedian based in LA. She co-wrote and appeared in Two Pink Doors, a series of 5-minute shorts for FX, directed by Dr Brown, and has several television projects in development with long time collaborator Natalie Palamides, including a series produced by Mark Duplass. She was a series regular on Like & Subscribe, and has also appeared in Jackass Forever, Reno 911, Key & Peele, 2 Broke Girls, Florida Girls, The Opening Act, and Dogleg. She is a former member of the Groundlings Sunday Company and Washington D.C.’s internationally renowned physical theatre company Synetic Theater.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Courtney Pauroso: Vanessa 5000.","instanceDates":"30 August-16 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"492603AGVTHVHDPVDVCQDMNVDJRDRHGDQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-30T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-30T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-16T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-16T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"2025 Edinburgh Comedy Award Nominees and creators of cult-smash “SLUGS”, the Creepy Boys return to the UK with their self-titled show. \r\nThis time they are throwing their 13th birthday party and you’re invited.\r\nIt will have everything. Games. Gifts. Possibly Satan. Probably Cake. Combining 2000s sexy songs, satanic rituals, and Willam Dafoe, these horny little boys do whatever it takes to make their birthday dreams come true.\r\nThis is one birthday party you’d be cursed to miss.\r\nFrom real-life-lovers-turned-identical-twins, Sam Kruger (Winner - Just for Laughs Comedy Award 2019) and S.E. Grummett (Winner - Best Theatre, Adelaide Fringe 2021) comes a bizarre comedy with just a splash of the occult.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Creepy Boys","instanceDates":"29 September-30 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"656203AVDVVQBDQSKDDLBPGPKSMMPCLVM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-29T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-29T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-30T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-30T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"It’s about nothing, nothing, nothing, nothing, nothing, nothing, nothing, nothing, nothing, nothing, nothing. \r\nWe promise. \r\nFor tonight, we are free. \r\n\r\nNominated - Edinburgh Comedy Award - Best Comedy Show\r\nJoin us for a technocolour acid trip where you’ll meet puppet Joni Mitchell, a two-person horse and every body part we have. \r\n\r\nA techno-punk concert, a play, a clown show, a basement puppet nightmare all rolled into one, SLUGS is about trying to have a good time while the world burns. \r\n18+ full nudity","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Creepy Boys: Slugs","instanceDates":"17 February-21 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"672403AJRVHKSKSBVMLTRNBSHDCCTVMHM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-17T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-17T21:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-21T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-21T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Sketch","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Crizards, the ‘classic double act’ (The Guardian), are back with a wonky war epic directed by Edinburgh Comedy Award winner, Jordan Brookes.\r\nThe musical duo's gentle bangers provide the soundtrack to their bulletproof patter as they stumble into a world of false memories and tall tales from the battlefield. They say you are your own worst enemy... well, not during wartime.\r\nAs seen on BBC One, BBC Three, Dave\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Crizards: This Means War","instanceDates":"5 June-8 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"528203AGBVCVNBKCNTQCNCRTVKQKJLLLT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-05T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-05T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-08T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-08T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Tom Crowley’s cult sketch, character and etc. comedy podcast arrives at the Soho Theatre with a new live episode! Experience the titular rollicking space expedition alongside all-new appearances from your favourite characters, special guest stars and live music and sound from award-winning composer Odinn Orn Hilmarsson. Link Tangent, Space Cartographer, will face his greatest challenge yet, map-based or otherwise - but will Galactic Central Command survive? You’ll have to come and see it to find out!\r\n\r\nTom Crowley is best known for performing in British Podcast Award winner Wooden Overcoats and in television’s The Royals, as well as for writing the adaptation of the world stage premiere of the Rocky Horror sequel, Shock Treatment. He has also been seen recently in Netflix’s Back in Action, heard regularly in The Beef and Dairy Network Podcast, as a lead performer in critically-acclaimed comedy detective romp Victoriocity, and in BBC Radio 4’s Thanks A Lot, Milton Jones!, Ankle Tag and The Brig Society.\r\n\r\nOdinn Orn Hilmarsson is an Icelandic composer and sound designer working primarily in theatre, podcasts and short film. He currently co-produces and does all the audio for horror-comedy anthology podcast Ramon Fear’s Terror Tapes. He has recently composed and sound designed Girl in the Machine (Young Vic), Murder for Dummies (online series), and the award-winning short film Two Stars Short (Sweet Doh). Winner: Best Original Song at the 24/25 Copenhagen Headliner Film Festival. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Crowley Time: Link's Gambit","instanceDates":"6 May-6 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"706803ALLPDKDNSLGVDKNDJPHRGBLGRJV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-06T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-06T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-06T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-06T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"JanFirst returns with Crush – a double sell out hit by emerging new writer Hadsan Mohamud. A clinic waiting room. Two Somali teens. One awkward meet-cute. Najma has been in treatment for years. Zakariya's just starting out. She sketches. He writes poems. Neither of them is ready to talk. Until they meet each other. As their sessions continue, so do the chats. And the jokes. And the secrets. Crush is a tender, funny and honest story about identity, connection and the messy path to healing. 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Crush","instanceDates":"7 February-7 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"684003ARDHSHVKMKHLLGDCDNPKSQDTPHR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-07T15:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-07T15:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-07T18:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-07T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"One week. Two shows. Back II back. \r\nSketch comedy stalwarts Crybabies bring their sell-out smash-hit sci-fi spectacular back to Soho Theatre for one last time. \r\nJoin James (still tall), Ed (less handsome) and Michael (??) in their sophomore narrative sketch adventure about finding home, forbidden love, monsters, mystery and massive regret. \r\nThe trio have appeared in Afterlife, Bridgerton, Outsiders and Lockwood & Co and now they return to Soho with TWO critically acclaimed shows. Catch Bagbeard and their Edinburgh Comedy Award nominated debut Danger Brigade back to back for one week only. Honestly, this is it now. \r\nNominee: Chortle Awards Best Show 2022\r\n          ★★★★★ 'Good lord did it make me howl with laughter' Telegraph \r\n          ★★★★★ ‘Simply top tier’ Chortle\r\n          ★★★★★ ‘An absolute must watch’ Voice\r\n          ★★★★★ ‘Will have you crying with laughter’ Everything Theatre \r\n          ★★★★ ‘Stellar stuff’ Guardian\r\n          ★★★★ ‘Funnier, more dramatic, more spectacular’ Times\r\n          ★★★★ ‘An unequivocal triumph’ Scotsman\r\n          ★★★★ ‘Sidesplitting’ Time Out\r\n\r\nFor one week only, Crybabies are performing both of their smash hit shows Danger Brigade and Bagbeard at Soho Theatre. This is the ticket page for Bagbeard - to buy tickets for Danger Brigade, click here: INSERT LINK FOR DANGER BRIGADE ONCE BUILT.\r\nCome and see both shows and get 20% off your tickets!*\r\n\r\n*Discount will be applied at checkout stage. Not available in conjunction with any other offers or memberships.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Crybabies: Bagbeard","instanceDates":"8 August-12 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"479403ASTNNMSQKBTQSNBCKQGMCCHTNTJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-08T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-08T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-12T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-12T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Storytelling","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Comedy"},{"description":"One week. Two shows. Back II back. \r\nSketch comedy stalwarts Crybabies resurrect their Edinburgh Comedy Award nominated debut for one last time. \r\nGermany. 1945. War? Yes. Join James (tall), Ed (handsome) and Michael (?) for a narrative sketch hour of action, suspense, singing, dancing, character development, rats, crisps, and concerns of the heart. Buckle up for an offbeat adventure through the seductive waters of World War II, truly the Godfather Part II of world wars.\r\nThe trio have appeared in Afterlife, Bridgerton, Outsiders and Lockwood & Co and their cult hit follow up Bagbeard achieved widespread critical acclaim. Catch both shows back to back for one week only. Honestly, this is it now. \r\nNominee: Dave's Edinburgh Comedy Awards Best Newcomer 2019\r\n★★★★ \"Highly impressive\" The Guardian\r\n★★★★ \"High concept farce of the first order\" The Telegraph  \r\n★★★★ \"Out-there originality\" Chortle \r\n★★★★ The Skinny\r\n★★★★ Beyond The Joke\r\n★★★★ Three Weeks\r\n★★★★ Broadway World\r\n★★★★★ Mumble Comedy\r\n\r\nFor one week only, Crybabies are performing both of their smash hit shows Danger Brigade and Bagbeard at Soho Theatre. This is the ticket page for Danger Brigade - to buy tickets for Bagbeard, click here: INSERT LINK FOR BAGBEARD ONCE BUILT.\r\nCome and see both shows and get 20% off your tickets!*\r\n\r\n*Discount will be applied at checkout stage. Not available in conjunction with any other offers or memberships.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Crybabies: Danger Brigade","instanceDates":"7 August-12 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"479203AJPRLJKBBJCJQJKVQDJCJSQSBBH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-07T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-07T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-12T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-12T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Storytelling","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Comedy"},{"description":"Heeeeeeere's Crybabies. When a former priest checks into a remote hotel, he soon discovers that all is not as it screams (seems). \r\n\r\nJoin the Edinburgh Comedy Award-nominated sketch group and 'masters of the craft' (Guardian) for a terrifying tale about fear, faith, fathers (dads), fathers (priests), fantoms (phantoms) and finally moving on. \r\n\r\nDirected by Jon Brittain and from the Olivier Award-winning producers of Fleabag, Baby Reindeer and Kathy and Stella Solve a Murder! \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Crybabies: The Scaring","instanceDates":"3 September-23 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"729803AGVSPQCRPTJPTJKGJHSPMLJSTPS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-03T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-03T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-23T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-23T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Sketch","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"After the huge success of ‘Big Night Out’’s Edinburgh 2025 run as well as the Autumn 2025 UK Tour it was only right to return to London’s iconic Soho Theatre for one final run!\r\nCalling all VIPS. Daisy brings together her iconic characters Steve Porters, The Divine Karen Moonstone and Häns Off for one BIG NIGHT OUT! Get on ze GL bishes. Hannah Gadsby tour support. \r\nOver 30 million views across TikTok & IG. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Daisy Doris May: Big Night Out","instanceDates":"24 March-28 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"690003ATPCKGSMCVMTNMKBHRRKDHQCBDB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-24T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-24T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-28T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-28T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Jamaican-born comedian Dale Elliott Jr. brings his highly anticipated \"Son Of An Immigrant\" World Tour to Soho Theatre Walthamstow.\r\nJamaican-born comedian Dale Elliott Jr. brings his highly anticipated \"Son Of An Immigrant\" World Tour to stages across the globe! \r\n\r\nDrawing from his experience as a child left behind while both parents ventured to \"foreign,\" Elliott masterfully weaves cultural expectations, identity shifts, and the perpetual quest for validation into sharp, relatable humour. \r\n\r\nWith fresh insights after his sold-out \"Bad Pickney\" and \"No Hard Feelings\" tours, he delivers an authentically Jamaican lens on everything from racial dynamics to the surprising cultural overlaps that unite us. \r\n\r\nFrom navigating the complex waters of assimilation to celebrating Jamaica's outsized impact on global culture, Elliott's comedy reminds us that immigrant stories bridge more than oceans.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":100,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dale Elliott Jr: Son Of An Immigrant","instanceDates":"26 June-26 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"597803ASRPMHVTRDNKCQLTKPQTVRSKPQJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-26T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-26T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-26T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-26T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Award-winning comedian Dan Lees brings to life bizarre record covers he’s found in charity shops.\r\nMeet the music legends you never knew you knew, as award-winning comedian Dan Lees brings to life bizarre record covers he’s found in charity shops. A riotous night of musical mayhem and clowning.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dan Lees: The Vinyl Countdown","instanceDates":"23 November-25 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"503603ADCHGTNTNLMTVLVKCMVCJNVBHTL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-23T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-23T22:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-25T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-25T22:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Award-winning comedian and musician Dan Lees recreates bizarre and obscure vinyl album covers he finds in charity shops. He brings these forgotten stars to life and sings their hits with hilarious results.\r\n\r\nNOMINEE London Off West End Award Best Cabaret, 2024\r\nWINNER Edinburgh Malcolm Hardee Award Comic Originality 2022\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dan Lees: The Vinyl Countdown Vol II","instanceDates":"19 June-19 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"615403ADDQVNDTKJSDJQVQQPNTJJSQSQL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-19T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-19T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-19T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-19T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"I can’t focus. I don’t know if it’s microplastics, long covid or because I pay $500 a week to live in a mould experiment. \r\nThis year:\r\n•\tI went to a rally dressed as Boba Fett and was bashed by both police and protestors. \r\n\r\n•\tI formed a parasocial relationship with a Doordash chatbot\r\n\r\n•\tI lost all my crypto trying to buy a mermaid skeleton\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dan Rath: Tropical Depression","instanceDates":"28 August-30 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"649803ABPHRBHNNQCGQLKCLSNSVJNCBNR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-28T22:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-28T21:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-30T22:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-30T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Following a third consecutive sell-out, award-nominated run at the Edinburgh Fringe, Dan Tiernan is back at Soho Theatre and he’s giving you everything he’s got. No bluffing.\r\nAll In is a blistering hour of stand-up from one of the most exciting voices in comedy. Expect explosive energy, razor-sharp punchlines, and tightly-packed gags about a man on the brink. \r\n\r\nAs seen on Live at the Apollo (BBC), QI (BBC), 8 Out Of 10 Cats does Countdown (Channel 4), Unforgivable (Dave) and Comedy Central Live.\r\n\r\nNOMINEE: Best Comedy Show – Edinburgh Comedy Awards\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dan Tiernan: All In","instanceDates":"17 February-21 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"671603ASJGPCLRHMNLQJJDSDQDDQTSGJP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-17T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-17T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-21T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-21T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"The reigning BBC New Comedy Awards winner and British Comedian of the Year presents his Edinburgh Comedy Award Best Newcomer-nominated debut hour. He's 27, gay and riddled with dyspraxia. Dan's had a big year, quitting his job as a dinner lady, going full-time in comedy and finally leaving home, yet somehow he still feels he's completely going under. Tour support for Micky Flanagan and Jamali Maddix. As seen on BBC, Channel 4, Comedy Central, Dave and ITV2.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dan Tiernan: Going Under","instanceDates":"10 January-13 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"499603ARMQTBHMGLBSPLJKGTLDNHKDJHL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-10T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-10T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-13T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-13T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"2023 Edinburgh Comedy Award Best Newcomer nominee and 'Mancunian wild-man' (Guardian) returns with show two.\r\nFollowing two sell-out runs at the Edinburgh Fringe, Dan Tiernan is back at Soho Theatre with his trademark high-energy chaos. \r\n\r\nCome for tightly-packed gags about gout and gay-awakenings, stay for a show-stopping magical finale. \r\n \r\nAs seen on QI (BBC), 8 out of 10 Cats does Countdown (Channel 4), Unforgivable (Dave) and Comedy Central Live.\r\n \r\nTour support for Micky Flanagan, Jamali Maddix, Fern Brady and Fin Taylor.\r\n\r\nNominee - Chortle Club Comedian 2024\r\nNominee - Edinburgh Comedy Awards Best Newcomer 2023\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dan Tiernan: Stomp","instanceDates":"10 February-12 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"585803AVKPMNPQNJMKQKNLSPKCNNBCBNN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-10T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-10T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-12T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-12T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"2023 Edinburgh Comedy Award Best Newcomer nominee and 'Mancunian wild-man' (Guardian) returns with show two.\r\nFollowing two sell-out runs at the Edinburgh Fringe, Dan Tiernan is back at Soho Theatre with his trademark high-energy chaos. \r\n\r\nCome for tightly-packed gags about gout and gay-awakenings, stay for a show-stopping magical finale. \r\n \r\nAs seen on QI (BBC), 8 out of 10 Cats does Countdown (Channel 4), Unforgivable (Dave) and Comedy Central Live.\r\n \r\nTour support for Micky Flanagan, Jamali Maddix, Fern Brady and Fin Taylor.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dan Tiernan: Stomp.","instanceDates":"4 September-6 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"568003ARHGJRHPNVHPGLPKLPDSKHPQMRC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-04T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-04T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-06T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-06T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Have you experienced the intensity of being famous without any of the perks? Been doppelgäng-banged to the point you no longer exist?\r\n\r\nLube up for this deep dive into fame and misfortune, accidental celebrity identity theft and being simultaneously on the cusp of tragic and iconic at all times.\r\n\r\nA hilarious debut hour from one of the country's most prominent comedy / cabaret performers, the award-winning Dan Wye AKA Séayoncé. Exploring the power and joy in your identity and the absurd reality of it being taken away by someone with four Brit awards.\r\nDirected by Lee Griffiths\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dan Wye Am I Sam Smith?","instanceDates":"16 April-19 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"595403ARMSGKKTDHGHRGTLNTKPBBCLPGQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-16T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-16T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-19T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-19T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Daniel was determined to handle his Big Breakup with the grace of Julia Roberts. He didn’t.\r\nJoin him as he navigates dating in your 30s, Le Creuset addiction and 12-step skincare routines, all while trying very hard to emanate love and light.\r\n\r\nDescribed by Rolling Stone as ‘utterly hilarious and effortlessly charismatic’, award-winning stand-up Daniel is best known for his viral comedy videos, which are enjoyed by millions of women and gays online. \r\n\r\nHis critically-acclaimed debut show Villain toured internationally, including a sell-out run at New York’s SoHo Playhouse and London's legendary Clapham Grand. He co-hosts the podcast Welcome To Hell with fellow comic Dane Buckley, which debuted in Apple and Spotify's Top 10 comedy charts, and he is the author of the hit book Bedtime Stories for Privileged Children. \r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":130,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Daniel Foxx: How Lovely","instanceDates":"13 November-13 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"669003AMMNNJQCVTKCKQDPNTMHGKDLNNS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-13T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-13T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-13T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-13T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Daniel was determined to handle his Big Breakup with the grace of Julia Roberts. He didn’t.\r\nJoin him as he navigates dating in your 30s, Le Creuset addiction and 12-step skincare routines, all while trying very hard to emanate love and light.\r\n\r\nDescribed by Rolling Stone as ‘utterly hilarious and effortlessly charismatic’, award-winning stand-up Daniel is best known for his viral comedy videos, which are enjoyed by millions of women and gays online. \r\n\r\nHis critically-acclaimed debut show Villain toured internationally, including a sell-out run at New York’s SoHo Playhouse and London's legendary Clapham Grand. He co-hosts the podcast Welcome To Hell with fellow comic Dane Buckley, which debuted in Apple and Spotify's Top 10 comedy charts, and he is the author of the hit book Bedtime Stories for Privileged Children. \r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Daniel Foxx: How Lovely","instanceDates":"17 February-20 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"680603ADPDDRCKMJLMJKSQSHQMQJMTMPT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-17T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-17T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-20T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-20T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Fresh from a complete sell-out extended run at the Edinburgh Fringe, award-winning gossip and TikTok starlet Daniel Foxx delivers a sensational show about childhood, Tilda Swinton and bullying (but in a chic way). \r\n\r\nWith his trademark wit and grandmother's pearls, he's taking us back to the 2000s, when the Special K diet was all the rage and the only queer representation was Jafar. \r\n\r\nAs seen on BBC One, BBC Three, Comedy Central UK and on Instagram and TikTok. Tour support for Josh Widdicombe, Rosie Jones, Sofie Hagen and Judi Love.\r\n\r\nNominated for the NextUp BIGGEST Award in Comedy at Edinburgh Fringe 2023, officially recommended by British Comedy Guide and featured in Dave’s Top Ten Jokes of the Fringe 2023. \r\n\r\n‘Utterly hilarious and effortlessly charismatic’ ★★★★★ Rolling Stone\r\n‘Foxx is a supremely gifted comic whose skill for recall, rapport with the audience and witty, intelligent, filthy material makes him a true Fringe stand-out’ ★★★★★ North West End UK\r\n‘Relentlessly hilarious’ ★★★★★ Broadway World\r\n‘Foxx is a compelling and incredibly talented composer and lyricist’★★★★★ BroadwayBaby\r\n‘A show that made us laugh so hard we’re pretty sure we broke a sound barrier’ ★★★★★ Starburst Magazine\r\n‘An impressively accomplished act for one so relatively new, in secure knowledge of himself and his talents’ ★★★★ The Scotsman\r\n‘This is a proper funny show with hidden depths’ ★★★★ The List\r\n'Fabulous' - Nigella Lawson\r\n\r\n14+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Daniel Foxx: Villain","instanceDates":"30 November-2 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"496003AJCGLLQVQSVCDSLVTSRPJKPLJNQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-30T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-30T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-02T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-02T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Fresh from a completely sold out run at the Edinburgh Festival.\r\nThis is the sequel to my 2014 show ‘Dear Epson…’ My favourite ever show. It’s a hybrid of stand up and theatre, but really that just means I get to sit down for bits of it.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Danny Bhoy: Dear World…","instanceDates":"3 February-8 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"577404AQGMCMVMPTGBGRKKKRRPJDKCDHM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-03T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-03T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-08T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-08T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Dara O Briain is back with a brand-new live show!\r\nAfter the huge international success of his last tour, 'So, Where Were We?'  which sold out 173 venues across 20 countries and was named UK Comedy Tour of the Year 2023 (Chortle), Dara's new show 'Re:Creation' sees one of Ireland's finest live comedians back doing his favourite thing: standing in a theatre, telling stories and creating madness with the audience.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dara O Briain: Re:Creation","instanceDates":"21 May-21 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"594403ABBJSTSKNSRHPRDGLNKHMNJDDBQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-21T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-21T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-21T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-21T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Hot on the heels of Dara’s last tour ‘So, Where Were We?’ named as the UK Comedy Tour of the Year 2023 (Chortle), Dara will be running out 2025/26’s global tour ‘Re:Creation’ in this intimate setting in aid of Shelter.\r\nOff The Kerb Productions will donate 100% of net profits from this show to Shelter, the National Campaign for Homeless People Limited, a registered charity in England & Wales (263710) and Scotland (SC002327).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dara Ó Briain: Tour Warm Up in aid of Shelter","instanceDates":"2 January-2 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"578603AKBQGMBKRCQDQDTQPTTTVVSKDBP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-02T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-02T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-02T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-02T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Winner of the prestigious Amused Moose Edinburgh Comedy Award 2023.\r\n\r\nDave Bibby, '\"madcap musical-character-sketch comedy pioneer\" (BroadwayWorld), set out to create a theatrical masterpiece: A one-man Jurassic Park. But then he had a baby and well… he’s been a bit tired tbqhwy. But creation is an act of sheer will. \r\n\r\nBibby aims to improve on a Hollywood Blockbuster by reshaping the classic movie and adding songs, characters and *ahem* multi award-winning stand-up. Voted the ‘Most Fun Show Edinburgh Fringe 2023’. \r\n\r\nA comedy show 65 million years in the making.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dave Bibby: Baby Dinosaur","instanceDates":"19 June-20 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"532203ASGKQTGGDVNSNSVRSGBNGGTNSVP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-19T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-19T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-20T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-20T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"New York City-based cult comedian Dave Hill combines stand-up, storytelling, music, and occasional, ill-advised feats of strength into a face-melting hour that explores life, death, love, and various snack foods in an often-confusing, futuristic world. \r\nHe also comes clean on being banned for life from Twitter and the one day he worked as a driver for Bjork. He does all this while ripping sweet guitar solos whenever appropriate, which is always! ‘Brilliant’ (nymag.com) As seen on Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt, Inside Amy Schumer, Would I Lie to You? US\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dave Hill: Caveman in a Spaceship","instanceDates":"15 May-18 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"519003AQVNMDPQGVRLDBDBNPPVJLHLLMK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-15T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-15T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-18T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-18T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"\r\nFollowing a sell-out run at Soho Theatre in 2025 and a critically acclaimed, sold out Edinburgh Fringe, the cult hit show returns. Together with his audience, veteran improviser Elms ‘builds a comedy mind palace before your very eyes. And you’ll want to move in for good!’ - Phil Wang\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"David Elms Describes a Room","instanceDates":"24 September-3 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"743803AJRCRPHBNVLRSJDGHSHRCCHPVDT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-24T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-24T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-03T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-03T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"After a total sell-out run at the Edinburgh Fringe and a whirlwind year of critical acclaim, David Elms invites you to a milestone celebration of his cult-hit phenomenon.  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nPart improv, part storytelling, and entirely unique, this is the 100th time David will step onto a stage to describe a room that isn't there with you, the audience. \r\n\r\n  \r\n\r\nCome and be part of this very special show with a limited edition “Describer” cap included in the price of your ticket! \r\n\r\n  \r\n\r\nIt is rare for an improvised show to break into the mainstream awards circuit, but David Elms Describes a Room has done just that. A firm Chortle favorite, the show earned a glowing 4-star review and a spot on Steve Bennett’s \"Most Memorable Shows of 2025\" list. It also secured a prestigious Chortle Award nomination, a rare feat for the medium. 14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"David Elms Describes a Room - The 100th Show Special!","instanceDates":"20 May-20 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"703603ANCCHCCGVNRBDCGQSJJTJBQPJJN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-20T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-20T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-20T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-20T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Following a sell-out run at Soho Theatre in 2025 and a critically acclaimed, sold out Edinburgh Fringe, the cult hit show returns.\r\nTogether with his audience, veteran improviser Elms ‘builds a comedy mind palace before your very eyes. And you’ll want to move in for good!’ - Phil Wang\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"David Elms Describes a Room (May 2026)","instanceDates":"18 May-30 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"682203ARHPLQHKMMVRTSGJMTVRMHMJTDL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-18T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-18T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-30T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-30T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Veteran improviser David Elms brings his sell-out cult hit to Soho Theatre this Spring. \r\nCome and take part in this hilarious and unexpected one-of-a-kind theatrical experience by helping David describe the objects in the room, the stories behind those objects, and the people behind those stories. Then come back the next night and do it all over again.\r\n\r\nCreated by David Elms\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"David Elms Describes a Room.","instanceDates":"31 March-4 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"605203ARRNNGQVNVNJQRKQGQNRSGRSBDS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-31T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-31T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-04T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-04T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"\"In a dark, dark house on a dark, dark street, a house of horrors wakes from sleep.\" Mime and physical comedy performer David Hoskin presents a hysterical, terrifying, and surreal tale about one hair-raising night in a haunted house. On a tour of a spooky old mansion, silly vignettes and strange time loops reveal murder, memory loss, and dancing zombies. It’s like spending the night with the League of Gentlemen and Jacques Tati in a Hammer horror film. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"David Hoskin: A Haunted House","instanceDates":"6 February-6 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"686603AJTDKMQBKJKRKBDVBJQGLTJGJBP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-06T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-06T22:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-06T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-06T22:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A new opus from the hairy Enya, the Ryanair Bublé, the nine-volt battery powered Beethoven.\r\nStar of 8 Out of 10 Cats Does Countdown (Channel 4), Live at the Apollo (BBC) and host of the What Did You Do Yesterday? podcast.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"David O'Doherty: Highway to the David Zone","instanceDates":"6 November-7 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"629803ABHKNBGNNGBMJCJPDPKMMNDDQTN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-06T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-06T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-07T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-07T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Deacon the Vampire, star of the cult hit movie What We Do In The Shadows leaps from the silver screen to bring you Deacon the Vampire: UNLIVE!\r\n\r\nIf you’ve seen What We Do In The Shadows, the chances are you can’t get Deacon's infamous erotic dance out of your head. Well, good news, vampire fans! Deacon the bad boy is coming to Soho Theatre to perform his own questionable vision of the dramatic arts. Join him for his last shot at redemption, as he relives his sordid past in a desperate effort to understand the gaping, dusty hole inside himself. Where did it all go wrong? Why do people think he’s a narcissist? Can he bring his long-lost ex-girlfriend back from the dead?\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":55,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Deacon the Vampire: UNLIVE!","instanceDates":"27 June-28 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"628004AHJQMNQTDLRVGJNMNHPMTNBNPVB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-27T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-27T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-28T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-28T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Nominated for Best Studio Production (WhatsOnStage 2024), Dear Young Monster is Pete MacHale’s debut solo show, pulling apart fear, otherness, and what it means to embrace being the monster that the world keeps telling you that you are.\r\nStruggling at the beginning of his medical transition, a young trans man has dropped out of university and returned to his quiet hometown.\r\nHis friends are away, the locals are becoming increasingly hostile, his body is transforming before his very eyes into someone he doesn’t quite recognise yet and it’s all becoming too much... Until he catches a midnight screening of Frankenstein. \r\nAt last, when he looks into the monsters big, dead, sad eyes, staring down at him from the screen, he feels seen.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":65,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dear Young Monster","instanceDates":"5 August-16 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"633003ATKSTSMPJSKCGNSMKTTGJGRMMRQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-05T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-05T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-16T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-16T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"She’s here! She’s queer! Her parents are sort of used to it!\r\nFresh, exciting, and overall, just happy to be here, Dee is the greatest transgender comedian her small village has ever produced. \r\nThis debut stand-up show is about reconciling with the past, coming out, and going through two puberties (frankly, two too many). As seen on the BBC New Comedy Awards Final, ITV’s The Stand Up Sketch Show and Comedy Central Live. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dee Allum: Deadname","instanceDates":"10 October-12 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"570003ARCQRBDJRGQMMKKRJKCRPTJPTDC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-10T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-10T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-12T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-12T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"There’s a point beyond burnout where all you can do is laugh, and Deirdre O’Kane has well and\r\ntruly reached it. Don’t miss the star of Sky’s The Deirdre O’Kane Show and Moone Boy, and the voice of Gogglebox Ireland, as she returns to London’s Soho Theatre.\r\n'O’Kane dazzles the audience from start to finish.' (List).\r\n'O’Kane quickly sets up a rhythm of her own and when she exits, applause follows her all the way down the street.' (Scotsman).\r\n14+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Deirdre O’Kane: Demented","instanceDates":"19 July-22 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"468803AQBTHPMRDQDPRDPMGCMVVHRKPDS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-19T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-19T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-22T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-22T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Following sold-out shows at The Edinburgh Fringe Festival, Amando Houser invites you to their unhinged clown hour of self-discovery. Inspired by the \"witch hunt\" on trans rights in the United States, DeliaDelia happens to be as nasty on the eyes as she is on the basketball court.\r\nOn a quest to become a \"real girl\" and also join a human basketball team, will she finally get her shot at greatness or will she be cursed forever? \r\nDirected by Kedian Keohan. \r\nProduced by Beth Sitek. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"DeliaDelia! The Flat Chested Witch!","instanceDates":"11 December-13 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"668603ABPQMNPVJMLDTSRPMTCNQMDNCVM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-11T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-11T22:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-13T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-13T22:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Edinburgh Comedy Awards 2024 | Best Newcomer Nominee\r\nDemi Adejuyigbe is a writer, comedian, filmmaker, and – inexplicably – a musician best known for his former podcasts, Punch Up The Jam and Gilmore Guys, as well as his popular September 21st video series, and his roles as a writer/producer on shows like NBC's The Good Place, Peacock's The Amber Ruffin Show, Netflix's NEON, and Apple TV's Strange Planet. He has never had anything to do with Spider-Man or Star Wars but he's hoping that someone loosely skimming this bio will now think that he did. \r\nDemi Adejuyigbe Is Going To Do One (1) Backflip is a very special comedy show featuring original comedic songs, presentations, bits, and one (1) single backflip performed by an aging, sedentary man who had to stand up and crack his knees in the middle of writing this.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Demi Adejuyigbe is Going To Do One (1) Backflip","instanceDates":"27 January-15 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"576203ALHVTPJBSQMHHGNCBMMSGSTRSSJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-27T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-27T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-15T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-15T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Demi Adejuyigbe is a writer, comedian, filmmaker, and – inexplicably – a musician best known for his former podcasts, Punch Up The Jam and Gilmore Guys, as well as his popular September 21st video series, and his roles as a writer/producer on shows like NBC's The Good Place, Peacock's The Amber Ruffin Show, Netflix's NEON, and Apple TV's Strange Planet. He has never had anything to do with Spider-Man or Star Wars but he's hoping that someone loosely skimming this bio will now think that he did. \r\nDemi Adejuyigbe Is Going To Do One (1) Backflip is a very special comedy show featuring original comedic songs, presentations, bits, and one (1) single backflip performed by an aging, sedentary man who had to stand up and crack his knees in the middle of writing this.\r\n\r\nDirected by BriTANicK\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Demi Adejuyigbe is Going To Do One (1) Backflip.","instanceDates":"27 August-31 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"541803ALCRSPDTVLLJMDTBVCKTJLJBRBN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-27T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-27T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-31T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-31T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Demi Adejuyigbe is a writer, comedian, filmmaker, and– inexplicably– musician best known for his former podcasts, Punch Up The Jam and Gilmore Guys, as well as his popular September 21st video series, and his roles as a writer/producer on shows like NBC's The Good Place, Peacock's The Amber Ruffin Show, Netflix's NEON, and Apple TV's Strange Planet. He has never had anything to do with Spider-Man or Star Wars but he's hoping that someone loosely skimming this bio will now think that he did. \r\nDemi Adejuyigbe Is Going To Do One (1) Backflip is a very special comedy show featuring original comedic songs, presentations, bits, and one (1) single backflip performed by an aging, sedentary man who had to stand up and crack his knees in the middle of writing this.\r\n16","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Demi Adejuyigbe is Going To Do One (1) Backflip: Work in Progress","instanceDates":"14 March-16 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"519403ACMSQDVQPGDVCBKHMDLTHSLGLPL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-14T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-14T21:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-16T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-16T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"After a sold-out 2026 Edinburgh Fringe run Demi Adejuyigbe Sells Out comes to Soho Theatre Walthamstow, performed with a full band.\r\nDemi Adejuyigbe Sells Out is brand-new hour of original jokes, songs, and bits in which Demi Adejuyigbe abandons all sense and desperately attempts to become famous. \r\n\r\nEdinburgh Comedy Award Best Newcomer nominee Demi Adejuyigbe is best known for his former podcasts Punch Up The Jam and Gilmore Guys, as well as his popular September 21st video series, and as a writer/producer on NBC’s The Good Place, Netflix’s NEON, Apple TV’s Strange Planet, and more. 16+ ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Demi Adejuyigbe Sells Out","instanceDates":"4 March-5 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"745803ALNVTLGTBCPQPSCNNTJRHMCBDKC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-03-04T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-03-04T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-03-05T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-03-05T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"The Edinburgh Comedy Award Best Newcomer nominee is back in the UK working up his new show. \r\nDemi Adejuyigbe Sells Out is a brand-new hour of original jokes, songs, and bits in which Demi Adejuyigbe abandons all sense and desperately attempts to become famous. Come and see him try out some of these desperate attempts ahead of this year’s Fringe. \r\n\r\nDemi is best known for his former podcasts Punch Up The Jam and Gilmore Guys, as well as his popular September 21st video series, and as a writer/producer on NBC’s The Good Place, Netflix’s NEON, Apple TV’s Strange Planet, and more. \r\n\r\nBest Newcomer Nominee, Edinburgh Comedy Awards 2024 \r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Demi Adejuyigbe Sells Out (Edinburgh Preview)","instanceDates":"15 June-20 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"723203AKHCDLJKCCTQKBLKDKJTSHSGPQJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-15T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-15T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-20T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-20T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Work In Progress","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Fresh off a sold-out, five-star Edinburgh run and over 120 international performances, this debut hour of stand-up and characters from the ‘out-and-out hilarious’ (The Stage) Derek Mitchell is a high-octane exploration of cultural clashes between Dutchness, Englishness and Americanness. \r\n Mitchell’s online sketches have generated over half a billion views worldwide. But with his trademark physicality and vivid characterisations he brings cultural quirks to life live onstage in this laugh-out-loud celebration of what it means to belong – or not.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Derek Mitchell: Double Dutch","instanceDates":"10 March-14 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"592803AGQQDGGQQBQCGVPJVPMTMPGBBMP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-10T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-10T22:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-14T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-14T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The brand-new live show from Derek Mitchell, comedian and viral creator behind @letsdoubledutch.\r\nAfter hundreds of sold-out performances of his hit debut Double Dutch – seen by tens of thousands around the world – Derek returns with a follow-up that goes deeper and is packed with even more laughs. With nearly a million followers and over half a billion views online, Derek has built a global fanbase through his whip-smart characters and satirical takes on Dutch, British and North American cultures. But Double Dutch: Two is something different. This time, it’s personal.\r\nIt’s a show about life between cultures, marrying into Dutchness, and finding meaning in the mess of modern life. It’s about loneliness and connection. And yes, it’s also very funny.\r\nFeaturing characters, stories and stand-up, Double Dutch: Two is a joyful night that brings people together in a way no social feed ever could.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Derek Mitchell: Double Dutch Two","instanceDates":"18 May-23 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"694003ATQPVRBSRKCNLGBMGCBKHQTPQGK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-18T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-18T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-23T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-23T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Dark, theatrical comedy meets nostalgia in Goblin, written and performed by Derek Mitchell. Set in 2007, it tells the story of Eliot, an emo kid with an imaginary goblin who just wants to be loved. Peppered with period details  ¯\\_(ツ)_/¯, Eliot’s life takes a series of turns when he meets a much older reality TV star and begins transforming into something truly horrifying: the co-owner of a spin studio.\r\nNamed one of i News’ best shows of the 2024 Fringe, Goblin showcases Mitchell’s signature tight joke writing, intricately woven narratives, and nuanced characterisations, as he brings to life Eliot and the characters that populate his world.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Derek Mitchell: Goblin","instanceDates":"13 March-14 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"593003AMGRRPKKSNJHJHHHLBJTGCGGMCS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-13T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-13T22:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-14T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-14T22:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Soho Theatre's favourite “funny ghoul” herself, Dina Martina will descend upon the dungeon of Dean Street with a hilarious new show this October.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dina Martina: Halloweena!","instanceDates":"21 October-31 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"734803AGDBSJVLJHSGCNKQTBGHQTMQRGH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-21T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-21T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-31T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-31T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"The unwittingly hilarious Dina Martina is barreling back to the UK with DINA MARTINA: SUB-STANDARDS, the hysterically funny show that people are calling her best show EVER!\r\nDINA MARTINA: SUB-STANDARDS is filled to the rim with the best intentions, yet tempered with inadvertently sad songs, ill-fitting costumes, and pointless stories. Over the years, Dina Martina has been hailed as \"divinely funny\" (Time Out London), \"the most original drag performer in America today\" (The Village Voice), \"as graceful as a Coke machine moving about on a hand truck\" (Seattle P-I) and has garnered a star-studded list of admirers including Eric Idle, Jennifer Coolidge, Graham Norton, Bridget Everett, Christopher Meloni and Chloë Sevigny. \r\n\r\nDina Martina has performed in more than one country and is a classically trained gymnast. \r\n \r\n“Dina goes way beyond drag into some new kind of twisted art.”  John Waters \r\n\r\n\"Performance art never looked so good.\" Whoopi Goldberg\r\n\r\n\"Staggeringly funny!\" Michael Musto \r\n\r\n\"Comic Genius!\" The Atlantic \r\n\r\n\"Hilarious!\" Time Out New York \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dina Martina: Sub-Standards","instanceDates":"13 February-24 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"513203AQSQBMRMCTJCNQCJLLJRLMKQSQN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-13T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-13T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-24T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-24T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Dina Martina is pleasured to return to return to Soho Theatre with The Comparable Dina Martina, her all-new show, which is chock-full of hysterically funny songs, stories, and video.\r\nDina Martina is an American cabaret and theatre entertainer whose hilarious performances are characterized by a \"different\" type of singing, mixed with peculiar storytelling and costumes that other entertainers might not choose to wear. \r\n\r\nSince her 1989 debut at Seattle's Center on Contemporary Art, she has gone on to thrill capacity audiences at Seattle's ACT Theatre, London's Soho Theatre, San Francisco's Great American Music Hall, and The Metropolitan Museum of Art in New York. \r\n\r\nHer shows, such as Sedentary Lady, Chariots of Failure, and Forgotten But Not Gone, as well as the annual Dina Martina Christmas Show, have garnered a dedicated following. Not unlike the late, great Peter Allen, Dina Martina is bi-coastal and splits her time between Seattle and Provincetown.\r\n\r\nOver the years, Dina Martina has been hailed as “divinely funny” (Time Out), “the most original drag performer in America today” (Village Voice), “as graceful as a Coke machine moving about on a hand truck” (Seattle PI) and has garnered a star-studded list of admirers including Eric Idle, Jennifer Coolidge, Graham Norton, Bridget Everett, Christopher Meloni and Chloë Sevigny.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dina Martina: The Comparable Dina Martina","instanceDates":"28 October-8 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"648603ALVBMSTVRJDPRGVCVVCLLQVNJKL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-28T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-28T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-08T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-08T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"Following a sold-out show last December, the queen of the season Diane Chorley is back at Soho Theatre Walthamstow for another massive Christmas bash.\r\n\r\nJoin her as she dusts off her signature pout, drags Milky and Ron off Universal Credit, and does her damndest to spread a little festive mustard on this terrifying sausage we call Earth. For one night only, backed by her riotous band The Buffet and her arsenal of (festive) belters, she’ll say goodbye to 2026 with a swift, high-heeled boot up the jacksie. So round up the work Christmas party, puff up that flammable turkey hat from Temu, and prepare yourself for one of the finest, most joyous celebrations of the season. Catch this cult icon before she disappears up the estuary for another year.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ding Dong Merrily Diane","instanceDates":"11 December-11 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"738803ABRHPVRHBRQHKPDQNLBNMBMPMMN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-11T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-11T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-11T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-11T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"It’s that time of year again, when Diane Chorley dusts off her signature pout, drags Milky and Ron off Universal Credit, and does her damndest to spread a little festive mustard on this terrifying sausage we call Earth.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ding Dong Merrily Diane 25","instanceDates":"19 December-19 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"663403AVCCRMNNVTMPHRKJPJRQGGHBNPL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-19T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-19T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-19T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-19T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"THE UPSETTERS present\r\nDismissed by Daniel Rusteau \r\nIdealistic Ashley is in her second year of teaching at one of the lowest ranked secondary schools in London. When she reports her favourite student brought a hunting knife onto school premises, she’s stunned by the sudden reaction of a bureaucratic head-teacher. Ashley is determined to save him from expulsion but quickly finds herself fighting a problematic system, apprehensive colleges, and intimidating and unforgiving parents.\r\n\r\nTony Craze Award shortlisted playwright Daniel Rusteau’s debut play Dismissed is a grounded and propulsive, witty but hard-hitting drama that shines a light on class and racism in the state education system and raises questions about masculinity, punishment and parenting of young Black men.\r\nThere will be post-show events taking place after each Saturday matinee performance. Further details to be announced soon. \r\n\r\n16+ recommendation","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dismissed","instanceDates":"16 May-3 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"463803ABKCMDVPCBRCJLSTKJNLDHNTVQJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-16T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-16T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-03T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-03T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Consider this your official invite to the most unhinged Christmas party in town. Part cabaret, part house party, Do All The Christmas Things wraps up, chaos, and pure joy in one big sparkly bow—and gives a glittery middle finger to festive burnout and winter gloom. Crack open the dopamine, sip the serotonin, and get stuck in. With nightly special guests and big prizes. (no peeking before Christmas). 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Do All The Christmas Things","instanceDates":"18 December-19 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"758803ALPQKRMMSKGRSNVCNDSTJBTSRTL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-18T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-18T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-19T15:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-19T15:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"To celebrate his return to the stage, Doctor Brown presents 3 special late-night performances of his classic award-winning show, Befrdfgth. \r\nThis totally silent show full of  ‘superbly constructed, slow-burning routines, and a killer finale’ (Time Out) took the comedy world by storm in 2012. \r\n\r\nWINNER: Edinburgh Comedy Awards Best Show 2012\r\nWINNER: Melbourne International Comedy Festival Best Show 2012. \r\nWINNER: Total Theatre Award for Innovation 2012\r\n18+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Doctor Brown: Befrdfgth","instanceDates":"9 May-11 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"536803AHDGPNLLCBJDJSBRBDMPLQDHTJG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-09T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-09T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-11T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-11T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"After starting with absolutely nothing on stage at the Soho Theatre a little over a year ago, Doctor Brown is back with his fully-formed brand new show.\r\nIt's been 12 long years since his last one - which won the Edinburgh Comedy Award, the Melbourne International Comedy Festival for Best Show and Total Theatre Award for Innovation in 2012. \r\n\r\nThis is silent comedy at its most silly, surreal and absurd from an internationally renowned clown.\r\n18+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Doctor Brown: Beturns","instanceDates":"22 April-14 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"536603ALLNBHNVNBSNKQBCPPNCPNHDRHG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-22T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-22T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-14T21:40:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-14T20:40:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"What happens when an unstoppable force (one man's vanity) meets an immovable object (Catholicism)?\r\nFind out in the Edinburgh Comedy Award nominated debut hour of standup from one of the UK's most exciting young comedians, fresh from his sold out run at Edinburgh Fringe Festival. Dom McGovern is the co-writer of Chicken Shop Date, a BBC New Comedy Award Nominee, and has been on tour supporting Aisling Bea, Olga Koch, Sophie Duker, and Urooj Ashfaq.\r\n\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dom McGovern: Prize Hog","instanceDates":"12 October-6 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"747404APRQDDBDMMLCTBGNMDTSHKGLBMB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-12T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-12T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-06T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-06T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Stuns in New Photo is the work-in-progress show from award-entering comedian Dominic McGovern (Chicken Shop Date co-writer, BBC New Comedy Awards, Melbourne International Comedy Festival). \r\nJoin Dom as he refuses to engage with any form of self-acceptance and instead yaps at you for 55 minutes about rock climbing, Miss Piggy, and the TV show Glee. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dom McGovern: Stuns in New Photo (WIP)","instanceDates":"3 February-3 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"684203AKVVHTLBJHLQTMQHKPVKMRNJMDV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-03T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-03T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-03T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-03T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The 9-time award-winning ★★★★★ clown showdown arrives in London. Don Toberman — played by Gaulier-trained comedian Chase Brantley — takes on the entire audience in a world-class pantomime ping-pong championship. It’s an absurd, sensitive, and totally unhinged satire of American sports culture. Grab a paddle & hold on tight! Featuring award-winning special guests. “The laughter never stops” ★★★★★ The Wee Review “Simply one of the funniest shows I've ever seen” ★★★★★ The Real Chrisparkle “Master of physical comedy…a sweaty, seductive and very silly joyride” ★★★★ Broadway Baby \"Who knew that an hour of invisible ping pong could be this enthralling\" ★★★★★ Denver Fringe Awards: Outstanding Comedy - San Diego Fringe Best of Fest - San Diego Fringe Artist Pick - San Diego Fringe Homegrown Audience Choice - Atlanta Fringe Tour Ready - Fringe Italia Tour Ready - Lagos Fringe Fringe AF – Denver Fringe Critics' Choice – KC Fringe\r\n\r\nAudience Choice - Richmond Fringe\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Don Toberman: Ping-Pong Champ","instanceDates":"17 September-19 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"734403ALVLPTRRPMKSSTTHPKTJSHTKKQM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-17T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-17T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-19T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-19T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The near future. Chris never wanted to end up here. She’s a proud woman and hates asking for help but when her condition deteriorated she had no choice but to claim benefits.  Ralph believes in the new system. He knows it can work for Chris. He’s here today, in her home, to assess her. To prove to her that there has been no mistake – she is fit and capable of working. Can Chris persuade him to change his mind? And, if not, how far is she willing to go to save herself?\r\nThis riveting new dark comedy from Rob Drummond “brings a laser-like focus to the current plight of disabled people in Britain” (★★★★ Joyce McMillan, The Scotsman)\r\nJoin Scotland’s preeminent disability led theatre company for a “laugh-out-loud comedy, psychological thriller, and deep conversation on the disabled experience of the state” (★★★★★  The Quinntessential Review)\r\nAll performances are captioned and have creatively embedded BSL interpretation, with audio description integrated into the script.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Don’t. Make.Tea","instanceDates":"26 March-6 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"515203ANRVKNHMGQBGVCRGSLPHHJHHJDH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-26T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-26T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-06T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-06T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Access","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Access","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":""},{"description":"Many people know Douglas Lim for his comedic commentaryabout all things Malaysia\r\nThey know his thoughts about politics, social norms,traditions, food, etc… They know this because he’s beentalking about it for the last 18 years!But what about his personal story? His half naked debut intheatre? His misadventures in the world of TV and film? Histestosterone level?VITAL STATS is Douglas Lim’s brand-new show for 2026. Andafter 18 years of stand-up comedy, he’s ready to talk abouthimself.It will be funny. It will be surprising. It will be personal\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Douglas Lim: Vital Stats","instanceDates":"2 October-5 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"733003AJJJJBRJCNCRKKRDKTJNQSMPLMM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-02T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-02T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-05T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-05T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Hilarious, macabre, surreal, and touching, this epic song-cycle from Richard Thomas and Dr Adam Perchard is cabaret at its funniest and most full of heart. \r\nDr Adam Perchard (cabaret star, comedian, poet, and occasional fortune-teller to the international elite) is an old vamp with one hell of a backstory – and Richard Thomas (Oliver Award-winning composer of Jerry Springer the Opera) is here to get the scoop!  Featuring dazzling original music, vocal fireworks, and rampant repartee, sit back and let this iconic duo take you on a whirlwind tour of the doctor’s brain.  \r\nBy turns joyful, dark, and extremely silly, the interview covers everything from hyper-realistic cakes to how to negotiate a nervous breakdown in Darlington, from giant bugs to finding love at an orgy – and it reveals what’s really going through your university lecturer’s brain when they’re teaching you Romantic poetry. With an Olivier Award-winning composer asking the questions and an international singing star giving the answers, this is an interview like you’ve never seen – or heard.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dr Adam Perchard and Richard Thomas: Interview With The Vamp","instanceDates":"10 July-13 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"543003AKTRKBQPGHPJBVPRJCHJVNMSHRK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-10T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-10T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-13T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-13T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"LGBTQ+","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"One year after starting with absolutely nothing on stage at the Soho Theatre, Dr. Brown finally has a fully-formed show.\r\nIt's been 11 long years since his last one - which won the Edinburgh Comedy Award Most Outstanding Show and the Melbourne International Comedy Festival in 2012. This is silent comedy at it’s most silly, surreal, and absurd from an internationally renowned clown.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"DR BROWN BETURNS","instanceDates":"11 July-12 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"486403AQQLGLVBGPTJRCHLQJMRQMTGBRB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-11T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-11T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-12T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-12T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference1":""},{"description":"You’ve seen him on Countryfile, Blue Peter and that episode of Springwatch that the BBC have tried to scrub (SCRUB!) from the internet. Now (meaning immediately), join Dr John Dolittle, PhD (yours truly and the very same), as he thrills with an animal adventure from yesteryear - before the fame, before the fortune, before they took away his OBE. \r\n\r\nAn award-winning character comedy caper brimming with gags, original music, animation and (patent-pending) Animal-tronics.\r\n\r\nWritten and performed by Aidan Pittman\r\nDirected and written by Hudson Hughes \r\nOriginal music by Robbie George \r\n\r\nA Dinner Daddies Production\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dr Dolittle Kills A Man (And Reads Extracts From His New Book)","instanceDates":"30 January-1 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"585004ADDLDGGMQGLVNKBTNVTCDVDSCJV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-30T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-30T22:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-01T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-01T22:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Drag Pub Quiz with Juxta Pose","instanceDates":"5 February-5 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"691003ABTLHCSPDNVDKTGHQKPHSDCGBTM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-05T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-05T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-05T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-05T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Comedy"},{"description":"Multi Award Winning (Offie, British Comedy Guide, Musical Comedy Award, Malcolm Hardee Award) “Master clown” (Threeweeks) DruCripps shares his debut phenomenally successful improvised loopstation-based shenanigans.\r\nJuicy bits earned five 5-star reviews and sold out the Edinburgh Fringe completely-including extra dates.\r\nEach show is bespoke to the audience that is in that evening as this improvising rising star uses “questionable musical abilities” (Disrupt)and “funny bones and  fast wit” (Beyondthejoke) to leave audiences “rolling in the aisles with laughter.” (Threeweeks)\r\nArmed with nothing more than his trusty-crotch-fixed-loopstation, join Cripps as he whips up an improvised hour that transforms audience suggestions into improvised songs, spontaneous sketches, and “utterly winning” (Chortle) chaos.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dru Cripps: Juicy Bits","instanceDates":"4 June-4 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"713203ALMQBGCQPQNSTTMDGHBVHSTDGMC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-04T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-04T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-04T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-04T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"“A civilization flourishes when men plant trees under which they themselves never sit. What you need to understand is, Ghana is home.”\r\nAs the afternoon sun hits London’s BBC Broadcasting House, photographer James Barnor encounters broadcaster Mike Eghan for the first time. Thrown together far from home, two rising Ghanaian creatives navigate their perception of identity, success, assimilation and home.\r\nInspired by real events, this joyful and poignant play fuses storytelling, music and dance; capturing a unique snapshot of the swinging sixties.\r\n\r\nDRUM premiered with a critically acclaimed sold-out run at Omnibus Theatre in 2022.\r\n\r\nWinner of the 2024 Untapped Award.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Drum by Jacob Roberts-Mensah","instanceDates":"12 February-13 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"587203ACLGRGQNSSLMGVSDDJPBTRVDDND","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-12T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-12T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-13T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-13T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Daily Show correspondent Dulcé Sloan performs her first ever shows at Soho Theatre as part of a strictly limited run.\r\nComedian and actress Dulcé has appeared on The Daily Show with Trevor Noah since 2017, earning an Emmy Award and a GLAAD Award nomination for her work on the show. \r\nShe is also the co-host of podcast Hold Up with Daily Show writer and fellow comedian Josh Johnson, and has appeared as a guest judge on the iconic long-running series RuPaul’s Drag Race.\r\n\r\nDulcé’s memoir Hello, Friends! – Stories of Dating, Destiny, and Day Jobs was released in 2024, and her new Netflix set premiered as part of their new standup series Verified Stand Up (In less than 15 minutes, her set packs a wallop – The New York Times).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dulcé Sloan","instanceDates":"17 March-22 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"593803ABPNQHQVHPGDHVDVQLHRSNMHVTD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-17T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-17T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-22T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-22T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Adam Riches rides back into town for three spins of his late-night cult Edinburgh Fringe hit!\r\n\r\nJoin Lord Sean of House Bean as he invites you deep inside his dungeon lair to throw down the gauntlet and challenge you to a series of quests, questions and 'quaudience quinteractions'. Think Pat Sharp’s Funhouse meets Krull in the show TV commissioners will soon be calling ‘a hard pass’. \r\nTrigger warning – may contain triggers (of the crossbow variety).  \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dungeons 'n Bastards - An Adam Riches Gameshow","instanceDates":"20 December-22 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"511404AMCSHQHJQHBLGMGKMMHLLSDHTQD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-20T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-20T22:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-22T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-22T22:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Dylan Mulvaney to preview her solo musical FAGHAG at Soho Theatre, before heading to Edinburgh Fringe.\r\nAn ex-twink tries on a new label for size as she navigates dating, delusion and God through storytelling, stand-up and a musical number or two. Directed by Tim Jackson, FAGHAG has work in progress previews at Soho Theatre prior to a run at Edinburgh Fringe. \r\nDylan is an actress, comedian and content-creator known for her viral series Days of Girlhood which has a billion views online and was named Forbes' 30-under-30, Out 100 and Attitude's Woman of the Year.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dylan Mulvaney: FAGHAG","instanceDates":"22 July-27 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"563603AHQQNMJVNBJLHQCRVJJMCSSLHPR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-22T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-22T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-27T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-27T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Queer performance artist Jibz Cameron, best known for her multimedia alter ego Dynasty Handbag, invites you to an evening of performance and readings celebrating the debut of her memoir. Entitled Hell in a Handbag, the book traces Cameron’s unique perspective, shaped by a childhood spent with hippie clowns in Northern California, to making morbid zines as a teen in the East Bay punk scene, to in-your-face experiences of misogyny in New York City’s avant-garde theater scene. \r\nBy turns both frank and funny, Cameron addresses the impact of addiction and mental illness in her life, as well as her mother’s suicide, in a candid account of her journey. This personal narrative culminates in the birth of Dynasty Handbag, and her gutting commentary on contemporary life. In a first, both Jibz Cameron and Dynasty Handbag will appear each evening to tell the story of these intimately intertwined halves of one iconic individual\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dynasty Handbag: Hell in a Handbag","instanceDates":"29 July-1 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"724803APKQMCLPPBPRGJMTHRPTQMKPSCH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-29T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-29T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-01T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-01T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Fresh from its five-star, sell-out Edinburgh Fringe run: a hilarious, politically sharp story of a working-class Scouser navigating Cambridge University, hiding her cleaning job, and exposing privilege with wit and charm.\r\nEat the Rich (but maybe not me mates x)\r\nFresh from a sell-out, five-star debut at the Edinburgh Fringe, Jade Franks’s award-winning solo show is back. \r\nWinner of The Scotsman’s Fringe First Award, The Holden Street Theatres Award and The Filipa Bragança Award, this is the play everyone’s talking about.\r\nInspired by Franks’s own time as a working-class student at Cambridge, the show follows Jade, a Scouse fresher juggling secret cleaning shifts with the culture shock of Oxbridge privilege. With razor-sharp wit and a dozen unforgettable characters, Eat the Rich exposes the absurdities of class, money and belonging in Britain today.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Eat the Rich (but maybe not me mates x)","instanceDates":"13 January-3 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"668403ASLJPQLTLKRPJHKBKTTRRCDBGJQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-13T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-13T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-03T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-03T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Political","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join Ed as he takes a long hard look at himself and tries to decide if he has any traits that are worth passing on to his children. Lauded as one of the finest observational comedians in the Industry, it is no surprise that he is now a TV name. BBC appearances recently have included Mock The Week, QI and on Virtual Reality 360 filming stand up show for Pico. This is the last chance to see this hugely successful touring show before Ed moves onto his brand-new show (Ed Byrne: Tragedy Plus Time) also previewing for Edinburgh at Soho Theatre in June. Please note this show is being filmed for DVD release and there is a strong chance you will end up in the final edit! By purchasing a ticket you are giving permission to be filmed. ***** “Masterful, go see!” Sunday Times ***** “Definitely stand-up at its best” VOICE MAG UK ***** “My face still hurts from laughing so much. Bravo Ed” Student Newspaper \r\n\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":105,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ed Byrne: If I’m Honest (LIVE RECORDING)","instanceDates":"25 May-25 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"469403ARSDJCHKCBMGGNBBCQHVQTVHKRK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-25T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-25T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-25T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-25T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Attributed to Mark Twain, humour is defined as Tragedy Plus Time. Come and join Ed as he tests that formula by mining the most tragic event in his life for laughs.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ed Byrne: Tragedy Plus Time","instanceDates":"19 February-13 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"496403ADQQKGMQMLBMRDCHBNQHLSNKLHB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-19T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-19T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-13T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-13T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Attributed to Mark Twain, humour is defined as Tragedy Plus Time. Join Ed as he tests that formula by mining the most tragic event in his life for laughs. \r\n\r\n✭✭✭✭✭ Edinburgh Festivals Magazine\r\n✭✭✭✭✭ Broadway Baby\r\n\r\n16+ reccomendation","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ed Byrne: Tragedy Plus Time – Work in Progress","instanceDates":"26 June-18 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"461803AGRLBCHHTCPKTPKLPMGTCBKHNQM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-26T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-26T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-18T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-18T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_Venue":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Hi there, I’m Ed Night. I’m a stand-up comedian.\r\nI’ve just come back from the Edinburgh Fringe and soon enough it’ll be time for me to sling a microphone over my shoulder and start hopping on boxcars bound for every corner of this dusty old isle (and beyond, God willing!) to tour my new stand-up comedy show, The Plunge. Won’t you join me in the warm?\r\n\r\nAs seen and heard on Comedy Central, ITV2, and BBC Radio 4. Best reviewed shows of Edinburgh Fringe 2024.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ed Night: The Plunge","instanceDates":"21 October-22 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"571404AVBJPJVJVNGNTTHGJSKVLRQGNMB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-21T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-21T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-22T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-22T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Multi award nominated Ed Night returns to Soho Theatre, and has cooked up another scorching stand-up hour. Won't you come in and have a taste?\r\nBest Show Nominee - Edinburgh Comedy Awards 2025\r\n\r\nAs seen and heard on Comedy Central, Stand Up Sketch Show (ITV2) and BBC Radio 4. \r\n16+ ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ed Night: Your Old Mucker","instanceDates":"2 March-7 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"680403APBHRCMVPVSNRQLCVDMRHVJQRRK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-02T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-02T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-07T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-07T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Eddy Hare (BBC New Comedy Awards Nominee) serves up his debut hour.\r\nHold your bowl steady and watch this promising uncle of three as he spoons it out with care. One half of double act Crizards (★★★★ The Guardian). Directed by Ben Target.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Eddy Hare: This One’s On Me","instanceDates":"13 May-14 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"596003AGNSHKCBNSTLBNDLMSRNRKSKQSJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-13T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-13T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-14T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-14T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A new show fresh from the Fringe, from two fresh young gals who, honestly, are absolutely fine.\r\nEGG are Anna Leong Brophy (Shadow and Bone, This Is Going to Hurt) and Emily Lloyd-Saini (Code 404, Catastrophe), but they don’t like to bang on about it.\r\nAs seen on Harry Hill’s Club Nite (Channel 4). Nominee, Comedy Breakthrough, VAULT Festival ’23.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Egg: Absolutely Fine","instanceDates":"24 April-27 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"532803AMHMBMGGJLVCJMCPJPQVKLVNBVS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-24T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-24T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-27T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-27T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Sketch","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Ele McKenzie's back (at her parents' house), baby!\r\nSexually constipated. Literally constipated. Addicted to Rennies. Life has truly never been better! No, really!!  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nIn her highly anticipated debut hour, the Pleasance Comedy Reserve alum is going to tell you all about it – maybe a little too much?  \r\n\r\nAs seen in Funboys and Everyone Else Burns. Royal Television Society Breakthrough Award winner.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ele McKenzie: Bringing It All Back Home","instanceDates":"15 March-17 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"762203ATRGTHQBVNGMJNDBTLQBNDVBCDT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-03-15T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-03-15T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-03-17T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-03-17T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Have you ever seen a ghost? Eleanor hasn’t… yet…\r\nEleanor Morton brings her award winning Fringe show Haunted House to Soho Theatre. Join online viral comedian Morton in her hit show exploring all things ghostly, growing up in ‘the world’s spookiest city’, real life ghost stories and what it truly means to be haunted. Are you alright to be afright?\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Eleanor Morton: Haunted House","instanceDates":"24 March-26 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"595003ARLHPCDSPBJRHNRSTDHVMQNVRTL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-24T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-24T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-26T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-26T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Elf Lyons is The Woman on the Edge","instanceDates":"27 January-30 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"747203ANQSHMJRHMPCJDHVNTNHBNJJJKC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-01-27T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-01-27T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-01-30T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-01-30T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Elf Lyons is bringing her Sky Arts 2025 Award Winning show Horses, the first ever comedy show performed entirely by a horse,  to Soho Theatre this January, after a hugely successful run at the Edinburgh Festival Fringe and UK tour. Bring your most enthusiastic childhood horse-loving energy to this new hour, all about play and the power of pretending. Treacle’s masterful performance has been directed by Elf Lyons, assisted creatively by Trygve Wakenshaw and Dylan Moran.\r\nISH Comedy Award 2024 – Winner\r\nComedians Choice Award 2024 – Winner\r\nMervyn Stutter’s Spirit of the Fringe Awards 2024 – Winner\r\nAdelaide Fringe Best Comedy & Pick of the Fringe 2024 – Winner\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Elf Lyons: Horses","instanceDates":"7 January-10 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"665403AKHTSBHVGNNDGBGBHDRHCRPRCDV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-07T21:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-07T21:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-10T21:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-10T21:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The first ever comedy show performed entirely by a horse. Made by award-winning Elf Lyons, performed by Treacle.\r\nWINNER - Comedians’ Choice Award Best Show  2024\r\nWINNER - (ISH) Edinburgh Comedy Award for Best Show, 2024\r\nWINNER - Spirit of the Fringe, 2024\r\nBritish Comedy Guide Recommended\r\n15+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Elf Lyons: Horses.","instanceDates":"14 July-16 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"642803ARKPQKNPKCNNQBQNHTPKQTPKPPT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-14T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-14T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-16T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-16T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Elf Lyons sell out cult horror hit ‘Raven' returns to Soho Theatre, the only show you need to see this Halloween.\r\n'Monsters are real. Ghosts are real too. They live inside us and sometimes, they win\" - Stephen King\r\nPart Mad Clown comedy spectacle, part Hammer Horror - in Raven,  Elf becomes your own personal Pennywise as she merges horror, clowning and old school storytelling to make you laugh and shiver in equal measure. \r\n \r\nGet a glass of Red Rum, bring your pal Tony and laugh with Elf forever and ever. It will be a Misery if you can’t come. \r\nDirected by Leland Gaunt.\r\nEdinburgh Comedy Award Best Show Nominee as seen and heard on  BBC Radio 4, BBC Radio 1, 6 Music, Dave, ITV2, BBC, SKY Movies and BBC Three.\r\n\r\nOne of The 50 Funniest Comedians of the 21st Century  - The Telegraph\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Elf Lyons: Raven","instanceDates":"27 October-28 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"498803AQNPPDPCGHQGNSPBTGRTDQGRHMC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-27T23:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-27T22:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-28T23:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-28T22:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Comedian’s Choice Award and Sky Arts Award winner, cult clown, and ★★★★★ Fringe IT Girl brings her critically acclaimed Bird Trilogy to Soho. Swan, Chiffchaff, and Raven return, packed with clowning, chaos, watermelons and a live birth on stage performed by a lion.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Elf Lyons: The Bird Trilogy","instanceDates":"12 December-20 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"665603ASLPGJVSPSSPJGDTCLKGJPBDMLC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-12T21:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-12T21:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-20T21:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-20T21:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Internationally acclaimed clown Ella The Great brings together, for the first time, a collection of playful acts lovingly grown from the UK Drag and Cabaret scene.  \r\nIn this inventive hour of visual Comedy and Circus, we are invited into a world of possibilities by the enchanting 'Richard Melanin The Third.' inspired by silent cinema, mime and the absurd, this “king of clowning brings it every time“ (BoiBox London)\r\n“Richard Melanin III is pure joy in drag/clown form and had the audience giggling like schoolchildren“ Theatre And Other Things LDN\r\n“lights up the stage” The Scotsman\r\nElla The Great/Ella Golt is a multi disciplinary artist based in London with a background in Circus Theatre and Fine Art Sculpture.  After first venturing on the stages at the age of 7, as part of London’s premiere children’s circus, Albert & Friends. Ella has since gone on to do extensive research in clowning, and performed on some of the world’s biggest stages, such as - Macy’s Thanksgiving Day Parade New York, Adelaide Fringe, The Royal Vauxhall Tavern, Beijing International Festival ,The National Theatre, The Royal Albert Hall, and more sharing Joy Magic and Laughter!\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ella The Great WIP","instanceDates":"15 May-15 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"477803ABJSCVGPVKPHTMVQDTPLSJSQBMQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-15T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-15T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-15T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-15T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Internationally acclaimed clown Ella The Great brings together, for the first time, a collection of playful acts lovingly grown from the UK Drag and Cabaret scene.  \r\nIn this inventive hour of visual Comedy and Circus, we are invited into a world of possibilities by the enchanting 'Richard Melanin The Third.' inspired by silent cinema, mime and the absurd, this “king of clowning brings it every time“ (BoiBox London)\r\n\r\n16+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ella The Great: with Richard Melanin The Third (WIP)","instanceDates":"15 June-15 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"478803AHJKRDSTVMKMTNHSBQKVQDRRMNB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-15T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-15T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-15T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-15T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_Venue":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Comedy's best nepo baby (and there's a lot) hits the road.\r\nFrom near life-altering injuries sustained at jiu jitsu to everyday Gen-Z life, this new show will leave you in fits of laughter. Elliot is a regular at Britain's top comedy clubs despite only being in his mid-twenties and has gained huge success online. Seen on Comedy Central's Roast Battle and Comedy Central at the Comedy Store. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Elliot Steel: Love and Hate Speech","instanceDates":"13 March-17 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"517003ALMCCSGHCJKCCMBLDBPJVBQNDTM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-13T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-13T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-17T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-17T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The Edinburgh Comedy Award-nominated comedian brings her show to London for the first time!\r\nYou’ve had a lifetime of lame anecdotes from all the average-looking comedians, but the reviews are in – self-deprecation is DEAD! It’s time to hear from Australia’s First Attractive Comedian. After sold out seasons & standing ovations across Australia and Edinburgh this past year, join Elouise for this award-winning hour of comedy as she subverts the meaning of feminism, attractiveness and owning yourself in a world that tells you to hate yourself to be funny. \r\n\r\nEdinburgh Comedy Awards nomination for Best Newcomer 2025\r\nISH Edinburgh Comedy Awards longlist for Best Show 2025\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Elouise Eftos: Australia's First Attractive Comedian","instanceDates":"7 October-11 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"654603ABBCQLCQLGQJPKHVVRNVQDHRCHQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-07T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-07T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-11T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-11T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"An hour of stand-up about trying to make sense of things—family, belief, materialism, and whatever we’re all supposed to care about right now. 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Emil Wakim: My Way","instanceDates":"15 July-18 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"719603AVKPBQJNNCHNHNRHHJGTCNJGVJL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-15T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-15T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-18T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-18T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Smash hit Irish comedian, best-selling author, podcast host and viral online star Emma Doran hits the road with her brand-new stand-up show, Emmaculate.\r\nThere's no such thing as a perfect family, but she wouldn't want one anyway...\r\n \r\nThe many trials and tribulations of Emma’s blended family are laid bare, womanhood examined, and relationships put to the test in this witty, rambunctious show from one of Ireland’s most beloved stand-ups. Strap in for a night to remember, jam-packed with razor-sharp observations, riotous on-stage antics and conspiratorial gossipmongering.\r\n \r\nAs seen and heard on No Worries If Not! (RTÉ 2), The Tommy Tiernan Show (RTÉ 1), LOL: Last One Laughing (Prime Video) hosted by Graham Norton, The Late Late Show (RTÉ), Celebrity Gogglebox (Virgin Media One), Modern Love (Prime Video) alongside Kit Harington, The Deirdre O’Kane Show (SKY), Bridget and Eamon (RTÉ), Callan Kicks (RTÉ), Republic Of Telly (RTÉ) and Irelands Fittest Family (RTÉ), while her podcast credits include: You’re Grounded with daughter Ella, And Another Thing! with Muireann O’ Connell and the four-part series Mischief Makers. \r\n \r\nEmma currently co-hosts the podcast Keep It Tight alongside fellow stand-up and LOL: Last One Laughing contestant Deirdre O’Kane. \r\n \r\nEmma is also author of best-selling book, Mad, Isn’t It? (published in 2024).\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Emma Doran: Emmaculate","instanceDates":"7 November-7 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"681003AVBMCLTMQGCQJVHKDVNSTPKJQHV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-07T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-07T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-07T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-07T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"In her biggest solo show to date, comedian Emma Doran reflects on what just happened. One minute she was an 18-year-old stumbling off the Waltzers in Courtown and now she’s hurtling through her late 30s with a 19-year-old daughter and 2 other kids.\r\n“One of the hottest young stars in Irish Comedy” – Irish Independent.\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Emma Doran: Mad Isn’t It","instanceDates":"6 June-7 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"473803ABDQHQNCLDQRPDBPJLCKLSHJJST","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-06T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-06T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-07T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-07T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Emma Sidi, star of Starstruck, Ghosts and the next season of Taskmaster, brings her brand new character-comedy phenomenon to Soho Theatre, fresh off a rave-reviewed, sold-out run at Edinburgh Fringe.\r\nEmma Sidi is an acclaimed character comedian. And now she’s Sue Gray.\r\n\r\nBut who is Sue Gray?\r\n\r\nWell, she's [REDACTED].\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Emma Sidi is Sue Gray","instanceDates":"28 October-2 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"565403ASLJDNLCMQRLVQJNKHNNDVGHPPS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-28T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-28T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-02T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-02T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Double Edinburgh Comedy Award Nominee Emmanuel Sonubi returns to Soho Theatre with his brand new show.\r\nA hilarious and heartfelt story that explores all the jobs that Emmanuel has had before becoming a comedian and how those experiences helped shape his comedic voice. Recently seen on QI, Alan Davies As Yet Untitled, Apprentice 'You're Fired’ and headlining Live at the Apollo. Following up on his Edinburgh Comedy Award Best Newcomer nominated debut in 2022 with a Best Show nomination this yea, this Fringe smash-hit is not to be missed.\r\n\r\nEdinburgh Comedy Award Best Show Nominee 2023\r\nEdinburgh Comedy Award Best Newcomer Nominee 2022\r\n\r\nEmmanuel takes the audience on a hilarious and sometimes poignant journey through a variety of jobs and industries, many of which he was wildly unqualified to do. From working in IT to the doors of London's nightlife, all while building up an impressive list of musical theatre credits.\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Emmanuel Sonubi: Curriculum Vitae","instanceDates":"5 October-7 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"495603APMSDLGNBVPCSRHTKPHHHDQLPML","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-05T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-05T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-07T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-07T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Two-time Edinburgh Comedy Award nominee Emmanuel Sonubi is back on tour after sold-out performances at the Edinburgh Fringe, his European Tour, and a hit New York Soho Playhouse run ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Emmanuel Sonubi: Life After Near Death","instanceDates":"21 March-21 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"662803APPGVPTRCGMLDBPQHJCHTSRKSMV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-21T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-21T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-21T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-21T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"An infamous production of Shakespeare’s Henry V\r\nThe death of a national sweetheart.\r\nA friendship tested by a bloody act.\r\nFollowing its critically acclaimed run at the Camden People’s Theatre this laugh out loud Shakespeare deconstruction is coming to Soho Theatre.\r\nThis tell-all dark comedy peels back the skin of English cultural identity revealing the streaming battlefield that lies beneath… would you die for your country?\r\nVeterans of the Shakespeare’s Globe Ensemble. Nina Bowers and Philip Arditti take us from rehearsal room microaggressions to the battlefields of France, into the bureaucracy of applying for citizenship, weaving in their own histories with England’s as unwilling actors in a national story.\r\nWritten and performed by Nina Bowers and Philip Arditti\r\nCreative Producers The Project People\r\nOriginally commissioned and co-produced by Camden People’s Theatre\r\nProduced by María Cuervo in its premiere at Camden People’s Theatre \r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":80,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"English Kings Killing Foreigners","instanceDates":"16 September-18 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"638003AGRLDKHHDRLKNKRQLTTSSSVLTSH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-16T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-16T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-18T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-18T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"After three decades investigating the strange edges of human behaviour—from public shamings, psychopaths, to modern moral panics—Jon Ronson’s latest true story turns unexpectedly close to home.\r\nWhen his son is lured to a mysterious castle deep in the forests of New England, Jon finds himself on a darkly comic, perilous quest to uncover what was really happening inside its walls. The Castle, Jon’s first book in 11 years, is his most personal, revealing and gripping journey yet—a twisting tale of unmoored men, lost purpose and the absurd, frightening ways it can all go wrong. Does a world of disinhibition, where seemingly anything goes, lie ahead of us?\r\nIn this brand-new live show, Jon brings the book’s extraordinary stories to life on stage with astonishing footage and online clips, including jaw-dropping material that has long since vanished from the internet. You’ll also get a first look at what’s coming in the next season of Things Fell Apart, and of course the chance to put your questions directly to Jon. Funny, unsettling, and unforgettable.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Enter THE CASTLE with Jon Ronson: Mystery, Crime & Unmoored Men","instanceDates":"27 September-27 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"679803ADPGRLCNRGHKBDRCKLLBBTPVTGD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-27T14:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-27T13:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-27T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-27T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"In 2004, Eric Rushton was cast in his primary school Nativity. Despite absolutely smashing it, he immediately retired from being a child actor. Now he’s found the correct antidepressants to give showbusiness another go. \r\n\r\n WINNER Channel 4 Sean Lock Comedy Award. \r\n WINNER Leicester Mercury Comedian of the Year. \r\n\r\nDirected by Matthew Crosby\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Eric Rushton: Innkeeper","instanceDates":"26 January-27 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"667403AMHRGTPJKJRJQBMCJRCTKNHPTLS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-26T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-26T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-27T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-27T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Erika Ehler navigates the disturbing reality of what it's like to be young, hot and yet so alone; platonic relationships and the bittersweet transition of hangouts becoming reunions.\r\nThere’s plenty of stories out there about how to get through romantic break-ups but not so much about what happens when you break-up with your close friends. Erika Ehler wants to change that.\r\nAs seen on Frankie Boyle's New World Order, Comedians Giving Lectures and Comedy Central Live. Erika’s writing credits include  Never Mind The Buzzcocks (Sky), The Emily Atack Show (ITV), Late Night Mash (Dave), Netflix’s Attack of the Hollywood Cliches, Sex:Unzipped and Charlie Brooker's Death to 2020 and Death to 2021.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Erika Ehler: I Got Some Dope Ass Memories With People That I'll Never F*ck With Again","instanceDates":"30 May-31 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"604203ARJVBMCDHMVGGJMVJTBMQMRDLVR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-30T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-30T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-31T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-31T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Esther Manito is furious. Furious at the state of the world. At being considered dead at 40. At online comments. And, in her brand new stand-up show, she’s furiously funny.\r\nAnger is not a good quality in a woman (scorned or otherwise). Or so Esther has always been told. When a woman is angry, she’s labelled ‘hysterical’ or ‘hormonal’. When a man’s enraged, he’s praised for being ‘passionate’ and ‘opinionated’.\r\nIn Hell Hath No Fury, Esther is at her most passionate and opinionated. She’s tried to keep a lid on it, but a coat rack has tipped her over the edge. It has far too many coats on it and it’s definitely not a metaphor for anything else.\r\nAs seen and heard on Live at the Apollo (BBC One), The Stand Up Sketch Show\r\n(ITV), Hypothetical (Dave), The Prank Podcast Show (4OD), The News Quiz (Radio 4)\r\nand Mark Watson Talks a Bit About Life (Radio 4).\r\n\r\n★★★★ Evening Standard\r\n★★★★ Funny Women\r\n★★★★ The List\r\n★★★★ EdFest Mag\r\n‘Simply brilliant’ ★★★★ The Voice\r\n\r\n14+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Esther Manito: Hell Hath No Fury","instanceDates":"17 August-19 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"465803ALVLKGCMPSCHKHTKGLDVGQHRQNL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-17T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-17T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-19T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-19T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Feminist","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Esther’s new show ‘Slagbomb’ takes a nosedive into the awkward sandwich years of life. The phase when youthful freedom gives way to the reality of adult responsibilities. It’s a time when one finds oneself juggling everything from prostate checks to hosing faeces off the garden decking, whilst clad in questionable footwear like crocs. Growing up, Esther imagined she would fulfil all the expectations of a lady, poised and dignified, but looking around she realises that just hasn't happened. Esther's life seems to be a magnet for embarrassing moments and endless cockups. No matter how hard she tries to project sophistication, she often ends up highlighting her unrefined side. Now she wants to embrace her lack of dignity - whether it’s her less-than-graceful posture, cringeworthy encounters with shady drug dealers, or the painful realities of waxing gone wrong. At its core, Esther’s show is an exploration of the challenges and hilarities of navigating the sandwich years, and an invitation to the audience to feel good about the madness in their own lives. After all, she has a Lebanese father dealing with war, a mother dealing with cancer, two kids (who seem to have permanently lost their PE kit), a husband who just wanted some birthday nooky, and a sudden loss of hearing. It’s all part of the messy, chaotic, and often hilarious journey of a right Slagbomb. ★★★★ “Manito skilfully weaves her own personal story with a wider look at gender issues in society” Evening Standard ★★★★ “An absolute riot from start to finish” Everything Theatre ★★★★ “Effervescent…Incisivley funny’ The Skinny ★★★★ “Simply brilliant” Voice ★★★★ “Absorbing” One4Review ★★★★ Funny Women ★★★★ The List “At times it’s like Victoria Wood has taken the mic” Radio Times “A comedian with keen instincts, and punchlines often delivered with a nice turn of phrase and a vivid metaphor.” Fest Mag\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Esther Manito: Slagbomb","instanceDates":"18 September-20 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"619604ALHHBLLMVCQKHPGQBJMGBSPGHMT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-18T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-18T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-20T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-20T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Eugene Mirman is a comedian and actor who lives somewhere in Massachusetts. \r\nHe voices “Gene” on Fox’s Emmy Award winning animated series Bob’s Burgers. He appeared regularly on HBO’s Flight of the Conchords, Adult Swim’s Delocated, Archer and a bunch of other TV shows he has forgotten. He’s released several comedy albums and stand-up specials. Eugene is the co-founder of Pretty Good Friends Records, which puts out wonderful comedy albums and other fantastic things. \r\nHis love of London and Soho Theatre goes back decades, and he’s thrilled to return and work on a new hour where he hopes people leave having greatly enjoyed themselves, but probably not being any closer to understanding humanity as a whole, sorry.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Eugene Mirman: An Evening of Whimsy and Mild Grievances Work in Progress","instanceDates":"15 April-18 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"608003AJGCKQSQDRQCNGNKHKDCCPSKGMS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-15T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-15T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-18T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-18T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Created and Performed by Keith Ramsey\r\n\r\nA hypnotising mash-up of queer mythology for the post-Stonewall generation; this fever dream of ambition, fury, fire & song was born from a fascination with the 1950 Joseph L Mankiewicz movie All About Eve.  ‘Eve’ makes a Dante-esque journey into the interior lives of the great writers and artists of yesteryear and daringly plays with what it is to blaze, burn and dazzle at oblivion’s brink.  \r\n\r\nWINNER: The Stage Award for Acting Excellence 2022\r\n \r\n‘A visceral cabaret performance exploring the intense lure of the spotlight… engrossing.’ \r\n***** The Stage\r\n \r\nWINNER: The David Johnson Emerging Talent Award 2022\r\n\r\n‘He’s thrown Hollywood’s great icons into a blender with a dash of everything from Shakespeare and Dante to Marianne Faithfull, then pressed ‘pulse’. He delivers the resulting stream of consciousness with a blazing and unforgettable intensity.’ Helen Hawkins, chair of the David Johnson Emerging Talent Award\r\n \r\n‘Electric throughout’ **** Everything Theatre\r\n‘Magnetic … absorbing’ **** Culturefix\r\n\r\n‘A rising star’ Metro   \r\n\r\n16+ recommended","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Eve: All About Her","instanceDates":"24 August-26 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"433603ARTHVBBBHLGQMBLVCTPMDKPBPMD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-24T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-24T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-26T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-26T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing","attribute_Venue":""},{"description":"Improvised mayhem with Tim Meadows, Matt Walsh, Brad Morris and Joe Canale\r\nEXPATS starts with a short chat, launching the performers into a fast-moving, fully improvised first act, featuring irreverent characters and heightened spins on recognizable situations. For the second half, a local mystery guest will join them onstage, pushing the show further and breaking new ground. \r\n\r\nThough entirely unpredictable, audiences can be sure of a side-splitting, thoughtful and truly unique adventure, every night. \r\n\r\nTim Meadows has been seen on SNL, Mean Girls and Grown Ups 1 and 2. Matt Walsh has been seen in Veep, Ted and Flamin’ Hot. Brad Morris and Joe Canale have also been seen on TV and in films. \r\n\r\nAll are veterans of the American improvisational comedy scene. Tim, Joe and Brad are alumumni of the Second City in Chicago and began performing as Uncle’s Brother at Improv Olympic in Chicago 15 years ago to packed houses. Matt is also an alumuni of Second City and Improv Olympic as well as being a founding member of The Upright Citizens Brigade in New York and LA. \r\n\r\nPerforming longform improvisation is their first love, and after spending years traveling America with their shows, they have decided to let Europe in on the fun.\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"EXPATS","instanceDates":"8 January-13 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"519203ABLQDBKSRGGRRKCKJVGNVCHJJVV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-08T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-08T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-13T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-13T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Failure Project is a raw, funny, and heartfelt exploration of what it truly means to \"fail\"—and how we rebuild from it.\r\nFollowing her critically acclaimed run at the Edinburgh Festival, BAFTA nominee Yolanda Mercy returns with her bold new show, Failure Project.\r\n\r\nMeet Ade—a writer who seems to have it all. Her career is taking off, she's finally out of her mum's house, and even her situationship is (mostly) under control. But just when life seems perfect, things start to unravel.\r\n\r\nFailure Project is a raw, funny, and heartfelt exploration of what it truly means to \"fail\"—and how we rebuild from it. Ade’s journey is filled with humour, vulnerability, and unexpected twists that will strike a chord with anyone who’s ever hit a setback and found their way through.\r\n\r\nDon’t miss this relatable and inspiring new work that will leave you laughing, reflecting, and rooting for Ade every step of the way!\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Failure Project by Yolanda Mercy","instanceDates":"27 May-14 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"614803ATVLBNQCSCNTPTJKDTJPPHVMGTL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-27T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-27T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-14T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-14T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Go backstage at the theatre and see how we make all the shows. You’ll see dressing rooms, props, costumes and have a chance to go onstage, with some surprises along the way. The tours involve walking around the building but are accessible for those with mobility differences. As we will be going into some backstage spaces, capacity is tight and all attendees will need a ticket, excluding babes in arms which can be carried throughout the tour. ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":30,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Family Building Tours","instanceDates":"25 July-25 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"739604ANMLJDTVNSLSBMRBKTDBMPBTBSJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-25T11:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-25T10:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-25T14:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-25T13:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Families","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Family","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"A fun-filled 30-minute family yoga session combining movement, imagination, games and simple yoga, followed by a creative craft activity for everyone to enjoy together. Led by East of Eden teacher Hermione Armitage, it’s a joyful opportunity to move, play, connect and create as a family. The session is designed for children and adults to participate in together and as such all children must be accompanied in the sessions.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":30,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Family Yoga with East of Eden","instanceDates":"25 July-25 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"740604ADMPLKNGQGCJVCRJVVJHKGHRGCN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-25T10:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-25T09:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-25T12:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-25T11:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Families","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Dance","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Family"},{"description":"Star of the upcoming The Office (Australia), Felicity Ward returns for her first national tour in 5 years…only to make you laugh! Out loud.\r\nBirth, Quorn, fingering, and transition lenses – there's no matter too big or too small that she can't get worked up about. As seen on Wakefield, BBC’s Live At The Apollo, Mock The Week, Stand Up Sketch Show and direct from her very own Amazon Prime stand-up comedy special. As heard on The Guilty Feminist, The News Quiz and The Now Show.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":135,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Felicity Ward: I'm Exhausting!","instanceDates":"2 July-6 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"534403AHJPSCHLJPGVNJNLKBHVMNKBDJT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-02T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-02T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-06T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-06T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"What happens when a former Colgate exec’s wife leaves him?\r\nDoes he let it get to him? Does he have some sort of breakdown? No. He embarks on a walk from London to New Zealand and then takes up stand-up comedy. \r\n\r\nMartin Fishback, the star of countless viral videos, is single and he’s ready to mingle.\r\n\r\nFergus Craig is a multi-award winning writer, actor and comedian. He starred in both series of the International EMMY winning sitcom Hoff The Record and Martin Fishback, the BBC2 pilot based on the character he created. He has won a Writers' Guild Award for his live comedy work and a Chortle Award for his online comedy videos. Fergus has written two parody novels based on his character Detective Roger LeCarre. The second, Murder At Crime Manor, was shortlisted for the Bollinger Everyman Wodehouse Prize for Comic Fiction. His next book will be released in February 2026 and has been purchased in a six-figure deal by Penguin Random House US.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Fergus Craig is Martin Fishback: Live","instanceDates":"11 August-13 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"630603APGMNQQSPPDVCHBRBQHGBRSKRBP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-11T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-11T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-13T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-13T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join Figs in Wigs for Astrology Bingo - a cosmic game show for astrology lovers, bingo wingers and their sceptic friends.  \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Figs in Wigs: Astrology Bingo ","instanceDates":"10 July-10 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"732603AKHKKVDNHLLPSDPTGTBJVSDQVSD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-10T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-10T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-10T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-10T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"A live art, feminist ‘adaptation’ of Louisa May Alcott’s classic novel Little Women.\r\nFigs in Wigs are back (again) and this time they’ve got their period (dresses).\r\n\r\nWild, irreverent and cosmically comical, this production dismantles the traditional canon to make way for the doomed future of humankind.\r\n\r\nPrepare to laugh at the traditions of theatre and poke fun at people’s obsession with ‘the classics’ as the Figs use the story as their very own trojan horse, turning it on it’s head and mutating it into an unrecognisable cartoon catastrophe that talks about climate change, astrology and the infinite nature of the universe. \r\n\r\nP.S. Beth dies.\r\nCo-commissioned by HOME Manchester and Cambridge Junction through Stobbs New Ideas Fund. Supported by the artsdepot Creation Space Bursary, Battersea Arts Centre, Pleasance Theatre, Metal Southend, New Diorama Theatre and Queen Mary University of London.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Figs in Wigs: Little Wimmin","instanceDates":"2 December-3 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"722803AJMCTMCQPRJLMHQLPLQNGRLKRTP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-02T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-02T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-03T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-03T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Performance Art","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Comedy"},{"description":"Come celebrate and/or cry about The End of Succession. As we inch toward the last ever episode, husband and wife Geoff Lloyd & Sara Barron report for duty as Firecrotch & Normcore with a live version of their cult-hit Succession Love-In. Expect fun games, marital discord, and the usual reverence for the most prestigious prestige TV.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Firecrotch & Normcore: A Succession Podcast – Live","instanceDates":"24 May-24 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"475003ANBJVHGSNQNPSJTCKMSMCNVSDLV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-24T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-24T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-24T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-24T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"In Jo’s attempts to avoid her violent and sexual intrusive thoughts from ruining her life, she finds herself in a dark farce.\r\nJo has dealt with her deeply disturbing intrusive thoughts all her life - but when she starts to be confused about her feelings towards her housemate, things really start to unravel. How can a person with Pure OCD tackle their sexuality, when they're so used to dismissing their taboo sexual thoughts daily?\r\nAfter a week of self destruction and a (literal) shitshow of a shag, she finds herself trapped - where every door that opens threatens to stand between herself and the person she loves. She will do anything it takes to be a ‘good person’ and to prove these thoughts don’t control her, even if that means giving up on love itself. \r\nFlicker is a dark sex-farce exploring Pure OCD, created through consultation with OCD UK.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Flicker by Gabriella Foley","instanceDates":"18 February-19 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"587403AKPNLDTJGPPVQDJVLKTNQBQNQDC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-18T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-18T22:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-19T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-19T22:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"An evening of bold conversation, creative expression, and community hosted by the Anti-Islamophobia Working Group.\r\nThis event is an opportunity to reclaim narratives and celebrate British Muslims in the creative sector, all whilst addressing the serious issue of Islamophobia.  \r\nThe night begins with a panel discussion featuring creatives, exploring identity and the role of art in challenging Islamophobia. Confirmed speakers include the Theatre’s Co-Chair and Actor, Alessandro Babalola, Actor Mim Shaik, Actor Ainy Jaffri Rahman, Radio Presenter/Audio Artist Shemiza Rashid, Founder of Black Muslim Collective Noura A. Sheikh, Perfoming Artist Nomadic Libaax, Founder/CEO of Waw Creative Arts Nusaiba Mohammad-Timol and AIWG Founder/Director, Anisa Mahmood (Chair).\r\nFollowing the panel, enjoy a lively performance segment showcasing leading Muslim artists, followed by informal networking.\r\nCome for the insight, stay for the artistry, and leave inspired. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Flip the Script and Pass the Mic - Muslim Creatives Panel","instanceDates":"20 November-20 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"671203ANSNNDTVNVPKBLHBBJTHPCCCRNV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-20T18:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-20T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-20T18:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-20T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Studio 1","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Fuel return to Soho Theatre with this sharp satire from acclaimed writer Racheal Ofori, which asks how we can live our best authentic lives in a world of algorithms… \r\nMeet Carleen and Crystal: influencers with cultural commentary that will have you in stitches! Love them or hate them, there’s no stopping their fast-growing online following. \r\n\r\nCarleen has her reservations about their cyber personas, but she would follow Crystal anywhere...even to FLIP!, the new social media giant that has everyone hooked. For Carleen and Crystal, FLIP! is the answer to everything they’ve ever dreamed of. But at what cost?\r\n\r\nThis sharp satire from acclaimed writer Racheal Ofori asks how we can live our best authentic lives in a world of algorithms intent on proving just how disposable we all are...\r\n\r\nCo-commissioned by Fuel and Soho Theatre, as part of Soho Six. Supported by the Cockayne Foundation - Grants for the Arts and The London Community Foundation, Arts Council\r\nEngland, Fenton Arts Trust, the Noel Coward Foundation, and the Leche Trust.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"FLIP!","instanceDates":"7 November-25 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"490203ATHNQGLJVLMGMTDPKGQDGBVBCGM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-07T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-07T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-25T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-25T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Description/copy – bold text intro for website (20-25 words)\tThe time has come for critically acclaimed musical comedy duo Flo & Joan to write another bio as they make their highly anticipated return to the stage with a brand-new show.\r\n“Gosh, they are almost like a real band” (Bruce Dessau, Beyond a Joke). \r\nThe pair will try and take up as much of the stage and as little of your patience as possible as they use another \"real band's\" setlist to write their own show - ruminating on themes such as ‘what is music?’, ‘how do you be a band?’, and ‘is comedy?’ in the sharp-tongued, deadpan way they have become accustomed to. \r\nAs seen on Live at the Apollo, The Royal Variety Performance, Comic Relief's Red Nose Day Live 2023 and their own comedy special 'Alive on Stage' for Amazon Prime.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Flo & Joan: With Feeling","instanceDates":"12 December-12 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"715403AMHSCHHVGSCCDBJHRQGSLTVJLPG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-12T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-12T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-12T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-12T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A new play by multi award-winning Lin Coghlan.\r\n“Dartford. Hastings. Margate by the sea.”\r\nRobbie wants nothing more than to be a grown up, and live with his sister Cel. Cel wants to go to university and find the kind of love her mother never had. They both want to be free from the care system.\r\nFollow these siblings as they take on the complexities of growing up in care whilst navigating early adulthood.\r\n“Touching, provoking & beautifully written, Lin Coghlan has crafted a play which challenges the shocking way we treat the vulnerable in our society with empathy, humour and truth” Tanika Gupta\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Flock ","instanceDates":"8 October-2 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"562603ARCRCDLDVQRKPVMRRPNMLPDJDBT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-08T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-08T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-02T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-02T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Welcome to the FOC IT UP! Comedy Club! \r\nJoin founder Kemah Bob and her incredibly hilarious camarades in comedy for a night the Evening Standard calls “a riot of positivity and inclusivity”. The FOC IT UP! Comedy Club is an unapologetic celebration of comedians of colour that are not cis-men! \r\nSince 2018 FOC IT UP! has brought its revolutionary energy to sold out shows in London, the Edinburgh Fringe, Latitude and Southbank Festival. ‘a vibrant and inclusive space for femmes (including women, non-binary and trans people) of colour in comedy to thrive… changing the industry, one gig at a time…” -Pink News \r\nHot off recording the first season of the FOC IT UP! podcast, featuring stand-up from over 50 comedians, the Femmes of Colour Comedy Club are coming to Soho Theatre and white audience members are encouraged to check their privilege at the door! \r\nAbout Kemah Bob: Kemah (she/they) is a comedian, presenter, writer, actor, drag artist and producer. She founded the Femmes of Color Comedy Club with one intention: to create a joyful and empowering experience for her acts and her audience. She has supported Hannah Gadsby, Nish Kumar, Desiree Burch, Jess Fostekew and The Guilty Feminist on tour. Her TV work includes It’s A Sin: After Hours, Jonathan Ross’ Comedy Club (ITV), 8 out of 10 Cats Does Countdown (Channel 4), Richard Osman’s House of Games (BBC), Meet the Richardsons (Dave), Guessable (Comedy Central),Question Team (Dave), Stand Up For Live Comedy (BBC), Don’t Hate The Playaz, Karaoke Club: Drag Edition, and Stand-Up Sketch Show (all iTV2). \r\n“A vibrant and inclusive space for femmes (including women, non-binary and trans people) of colour in comedy to thrive… changing the industry, one gig at a time…” -Pink\r\n“Kemah Bob and her brilliantly diverse FOC IT UP! podcast are blowing the doors of comedy wide open” - Evening Standard\r\n “It’s an unapologetic celebration of comedians of colour” - Diva Magazine\r\n“Kemah Bob and her brilliantly diverse FOC IT UP! podcast are blowing the doors of comedy wide open” - Evening Standard\r\n\r\nPay it forward tickets – FOC IT UP would like to make the shows as accessible as possible. You can add a donation of an additional ticket for the set price of £16.\r\n\r\nTo book a ‘pay it forward’ ticket, please call the box office on 020 7478 0100. These tickets are subject to availability and on a first come, first serve basis. You will be contacted the week before the show if we have tickets available.\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"FOC IT UP Comedy Club with Kemah Bob.","instanceDates":"17 April-13 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"445003ARGPMPMCKGBKKKJLBHHGNRSCCGC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-17T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-17T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-13T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-13T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Access"},{"description":"Welcome to the FOC IT UP! Comedy Club! Join founder Kemah Bob and her incredibly hilarious camarades in comedy for a night the Evening Standard calls “a riot of positivity and inclusivity”. The FOC IT UP! Comedy Club is an unapologetic celebration of comedians of colour that are not cis-men! Since 2018 FOC IT UP! has brought its revolutionary energy to sold out shows in London, the Edinburgh Fringe, Latitude and Southbank Festival. ‘a vibrant and inclusive space for femmes (including women, non-binary and trans people) of colour in comedy to thrive… changing the industry, one gig at a time…” -Pink News Hot off recording the first season of the FOC IT UP! podcast, featuring stand-up from over 50 comedians, the Femmes of Colour Comedy Club are coming to Soho Theatre and white audience members are encouraged to check their privilege at the door! About Kemah Bob: Kemah (she/they) is a comedian, presenter, writer, actor, drag artist and producer. She founded the Femmes of Color Comedy Club with one intention: to create a joyful and empowering experience for her acts and her audience. She has supported Hannah Gadsby, Nish Kumar, Desiree Burch, Jess Fostekew and The Guilty Feminist on tour. Her TV work includes It’s A Sin: After Hours, Jonathan Ross’ Comedy Club (ITV), 8 out of 10 Cats Does Countdown (Channel 4), Richard Osman’s House of Games (BBC), Meet the Richardsons (Dave), Guessable (Comedy Central),Question Team (Dave), Stand Up For Live Comedy (BBC), Don’t Hate The Playaz, Karaoke Club: Drag Edition, and Stand-Up Sketch Show (all iTV2).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"FOC IT UP with Kemah Bob","instanceDates":"11 July-11 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"710003ASGTKRVDQJPGVNJHVTPDLGRJGGP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-11T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-11T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-11T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-11T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Comedy"},{"description":"Join founder Kemah Bob and her incredibly hilarious comrades in comedy for a night the Evening Standard calls 'a riot of positivity and inclusivity'.\r\nWelcome to the FOC IT UP! Comedy Club! \r\nJoin founder Kemah Bob and her incredibly hilarious camarades in comedy for a night the Evening Standard calls “a riot of positivity and inclusivity”. The FOC IT UP! Comedy Club is an unapologetic celebration of comedians of colour that are not cis-men! \r\nSince 2018 FOC IT UP! has brought its revolutionary energy to sold out shows in London, the Edinburgh Fringe, Latitude and Southbank Festival. ‘a vibrant and inclusive space for femmes (including women, non-binary and trans people) of colour in comedy to thrive… changing the industry, one gig at a time…” -Pink News \r\nHot off recording the first season of the FOC IT UP! podcast, featuring stand-up from over 50 comedians, the Femmes of Colour Comedy Club are coming to Soho Theatre and white audience members are encouraged to check their privilege at the door! \r\nAbout Kemah Bob: Kemah (she/they) is a comedian, presenter, writer, actor, drag artist and producer. She founded the Femmes of Color Comedy Club with one intention: to create a joyful and empowering experience for her acts and her audience. She has supported Hannah Gadsby, Nish Kumar, Desiree Burch, Jess Fostekew and The Guilty Feminist on tour. Her TV work includes It’s A Sin: After Hours, Jonathan Ross’ Comedy Club (ITV), 8 out of 10 Cats Does Countdown (Channel 4), Richard Osman’s House of Games (BBC), Meet the Richardsons (Dave), Guessable (Comedy Central),Question Team (Dave), Stand Up For Live Comedy (BBC), Don’t Hate The Playaz, Karaoke Club: Drag Edition, and Stand-Up Sketch Show (all iTV2). \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"FOC IT UP with Kemah Bob 0ct 25","instanceDates":"14 January-18 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"670803ANBPMSCTTSDNJKVQKQCCSMHGDQD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-14T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-14T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-18T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-18T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Welcome to the FOC IT UP! Comedy Club! \r\nJoin founder Kemah Bob and her incredibly hilarious camarades in comedy for a night the Evening Standard calls “a riot of positivity and inclusivity”. The FOC IT UP! Comedy Club is an unapologetic celebration of comedians of colour that are not cis-men! \r\nSince 2018 FOC IT UP! has brought its revolutionary energy to sold out shows in London, the Edinburgh Fringe, Latitude and Southbank Festival. ‘a vibrant and inclusive space for femmes (including women, non-binary and trans people) of colour in comedy to thrive… changing the industry, one gig at a time…” -Pink News \r\nHot off recording the first season of the FOC IT UP! podcast, featuring stand-up from over 50 comedians, the Femmes of Colour Comedy Club are coming to Soho Theatre and white audience members are encouraged to check their privilege at the door! \r\nAbout Kemah Bob: Kemah (she/they) is a comedian, presenter, writer, actor, drag artist and producer. She founded the Femmes of Color Comedy Club with one intention: to create a joyful and empowering experience for her acts and her audience. She has supported Hannah Gadsby, Nish Kumar, Desiree Burch, Jess Fostekew and The Guilty Feminist on tour. Her TV work includes It’s A Sin: After Hours, Jonathan Ross’ Comedy Club (ITV), 8 out of 10 Cats Does Countdown (Channel 4), Richard Osman’s House of Games (BBC), Meet the Richardsons (Dave), Guessable (Comedy Central),Question Team (Dave), Stand Up For Live Comedy (BBC), Don’t Hate The Playaz, Karaoke Club: Drag Edition, and Stand-Up Sketch Show (all iTV2). \r\n“A vibrant and inclusive space for femmes (including women, non-binary and trans people) of colour in comedy to thrive… changing the industry, one gig at a time…” -Pink\r\n“Kemah Bob and her brilliantly diverse FOC IT UP! podcast are blowing the doors of comedy wide open” - Evening Standard\r\n “It’s an unapologetic celebration of comedians of colour” - Diva Magazine\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"FOC IT UP with Kemah Bob Apr25","instanceDates":"5 April-5 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"602403AQJNLRRTBVLHMNLDNPLDLRBMTML","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-05T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-05T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-05T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-05T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Join founder Kemah Bob and her incredibly hilarious comrades in comedy for a night the Evening Standard calls 'a riot of positivity and inclusivity'.\r\nWelcome to the FOC IT UP! Comedy Club! \r\nJoin founder Kemah Bob and her incredibly hilarious camarades in comedy for a night the Evening Standard calls “a riot of positivity and inclusivity”. The FOC IT UP! Comedy Club is an unapologetic celebration of comedians of colour that are not cis-men! \r\nSince 2018 FOC IT UP! has brought its revolutionary energy to sold out shows in London, the Edinburgh Fringe, Latitude and Southbank Festival. ‘a vibrant and inclusive space for femmes (including women, non-binary and trans people) of colour in comedy to thrive… changing the industry, one gig at a time…” -Pink News \r\nHot off recording the first season of the FOC IT UP! podcast, featuring stand-up from over 50 comedians, the Femmes of Colour Comedy Club are coming to Soho Theatre and white audience members are encouraged to check their privilege at the door! \r\nAbout Kemah Bob: Kemah (she/they) is a comedian, presenter, writer, actor, drag artist and producer. She founded the Femmes of Color Comedy Club with one intention: to create a joyful and empowering experience for her acts and her audience. She has supported Hannah Gadsby, Nish Kumar, Desiree Burch, Jess Fostekew and The Guilty Feminist on tour. Her TV work includes It’s A Sin: After Hours, Jonathan Ross’ Comedy Club (ITV), 8 out of 10 Cats Does Countdown (Channel 4), Richard Osman’s House of Games (BBC), Meet the Richardsons (Dave), Guessable (Comedy Central),Question Team (Dave), Stand Up For Live Comedy (BBC), Don’t Hate The Playaz, Karaoke Club: Drag Edition, and Stand-Up Sketch Show (all iTV2). \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"FOC IT UP with Kemah Bob Nov24","instanceDates":"16 November-18 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"566803AVGHCBCGGJPKBDTKMTMHGQPHSKC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-16T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-16T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-18T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-18T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Join founder Kemah Bob and her incredibly hilarious comrades in comedy for a night the Evening Standard calls 'a riot of positivity and inclusivity'.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"FOC IT UP with Kemah Bob.","instanceDates":"28 June-28 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"627603AGGLRNPBVJTSTHPDRVHLVDKSQGM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-28T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-28T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-28T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-28T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"A fully BSL-led hip-hop gig theatre show, Follow the Signs is performed through BSL, rap, spoken English, movement, and creative captioning, to be shared and celebrated by Deaf and hearing audiences together. \r\n\r\nChris is Deaf in a hearing world. Chris is Black on a racist island.\r\nNo code. No imprint. No escape. \r\nBut this is not a tragedy. This is a story of hope. This is a story about owning your identity.\r\nOnce upon a time there was a boy from down the road\r\nHe contracted meningitis at the age of two years old\r\nHis life had been ok but now little did he know\r\nHis hearing was to leave him and was due to change his world\r\nA fully BSL-led hip-hop gig theatre show, Follow the Signs is performed through BSL, rap, spoken English, movement, and creative captioning, to be shared and celebrated by Deaf and hearing audiences together. It tells the story of acclaimed dancer and choreographer Chris Fonseca: from infanthood when he lost his hearing after contracting meningitis, through a school system unable to value his differences, into teenage years where music and dance entered his life, to meeting Raffie Julien, a mixed-race Deaf woman who’s lived experience couldn’t be more different…or is it?\r\nYou’ve heard of the 5 elements of hip hop right? Emceeing, deejaying, breakin’, graffiti and beatboxing. Well now it’s time to introduce you to the 5 elements of Raffie. I’m half black, half white. I’m oral and I sign. On top of that, I’m a woman. \r\nAll performances will be in BSL, Spoken English, Rap and English Captions.\r\n\r\nInstagram: @fusetheatre\r\n\r\nCredits\r\nCo-Writers Chris Fonseca and Harry Jardine\r\nDirector Harry Jardine\r\nChoreographer Chris Fonseca\r\nCreative Producer Sian Weeding\r\nComposer Yacoub Didi\r\nSound Designer Gareth Tucker\r\nLighting Designer Simeon Miller\r\nVideo and Caption Designer Rachel Sampley\r\nDramaturg Kirsty Housley\r\nProduction Manager Ed Borgnis\r\n\r\n16+ \r\nIncludes scenes with bullying, racism and autism.\r\n\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":65,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Follow the Signs ","instanceDates":"24 September-12 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"559603AHSQVLRVQQJPJCRGBVGDVMMSTLH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-24T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-24T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-12T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-12T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Access","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Access","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"'Enter the ‘bizarre and beautiful’ world of Fool’s Moon, an anarchic, genre-bending cabaret night where the mischievous come out and play. Expect extravagant costumes, elaborate props and multiple left feet that may alleviate, if only momentarily, your existential crisis. 'It’s hard to think of a better escape’ ★★★★ To do List\r\n\r\nHosted by ‘magnificent physical comedian’ Paulina Lenoir, the night features the UK's most exciting performers across clowning, music, dance, drag and live art.  \r\n\r\nPast acts include Lucy Hopkins, Julia Masli, Charlie Partridge, Lorna Rose Treen, Frankie Thompson, Coral Bevan, Chewy She, Mermaid Chunky, WET MESS, Sara Segovia, Lachlan Werner, Ella Evans, Ryan Lane, Gemma Soldati, Nancy Trotter Landry, Kaajel Patel, Sarah Woolfenden, Hazel Townsend, Vic Diamente, Dan Lees, Serena Flynn, Alejo de Mesa, Luke Rollason, Anna Marie Simonsen, Charlie Wood and many more.’\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":100,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Fool’s Moon","instanceDates":"19 February-1 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"512403AMPVBQLBPTLKRRCVVSGVKMJVSHN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-19T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-19T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-01T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-01T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"'Enter the ‘bizarre and beautiful’ world of Fool’s Moon, an anarchic, genre-bending cabaret night where the mischievous come out and play. Expect extravagant costumes, elaborate props and multiple left feet that may alleviate, if only momentarily, your existential crisis. 'It’s hard to think of a better escape’ ★★★★ To do List\r\n\r\nHosted by ‘magnificent physical comedian’ Paulina Lenoir, the night features the UK's most exciting performers across clowning, music, dance, drag and live art.  \r\n\r\nPast acts include Lucy Hopkins, Julia Masli, Charlie Partridge, Lorna Rose Treen, Frankie Thompson, Coral Bevan, Chewy She, Mermaid Chunky, WET MESS, Sara Segovia, Lachlan Werner, Ella Evans, Ryan Lane, Gemma Soldati, Nancy Trotter Landry, Kaajel Patel, Sarah Woolfenden, Hazel Townsend, Vic Diamente, Dan Lees, Serena Flynn, Alejo de Mesa, Luke Rollason, Anna Marie Simonsen, Charlie Wood and many more.’\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Fool’s Moon Apr23","instanceDates":"11 April-11 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"449803AGDVDLSVNNQCJJRNBPRPPNBPSRJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-11T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-11T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-11T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-11T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Description / copy\r\n\t'Enter the ‘bizarre and beautiful’ world of Fool’s Moon, an anarchic, genre-bending cabaret night where the mischievous come out and play. Expect extravagant costumes, elaborate props and multiple left feet that may alleviate, if only momentarily, your existential crisis. 'It’s hard to think of a better escape’ ★★★★ To do List\r\n\r\nHosted by ‘magnificent physical comedian’ Paulina Lenoir, the night features the UK's most exciting performers across clowning, music, dance, drag and live art.  \r\n\r\nPast acts include Lucy Hopkins, Julia Masli, Charlie Partridge, Lorna Rose Treen, Frankie Thompson, Coral Bevan, Chewy She, Mermaid Chunky, WET MESS, Sara Segovia, Lachlan Werner, Ella Evans, Ryan Lane, Gemma Soldati, Nancy Trotter Landry, Kaajel Patel, Sarah Woolfenden, Hazel Townsend, Vic Diamente, Dan Lees, Serena Flynn, Alejo de Mesa, Luke Rollason, Anna Marie Simonsen, Charlie Wood and many more.’\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Fool’s Moon Jul23","instanceDates":"19 July-19 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"470003AQSVDCSSRRRBVHQQDKLLHCHVDGC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-19T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-19T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-19T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-19T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"'Enter the ‘bizarre and beautiful’ world of Fool’s Moon, an anarchic, genre-bending cabaret night where the mischievous come out and play. Expect extravagant costumes, elaborate props and multiple left feet that may alleviate, if only momentarily, your existential crisis. 'It’s hard to think of a better escape’ ★★★★ To do List\r\n\r\nHosted by ‘magnificent physical comedian’ Paulina Lenoir, the night features the UK's most exciting performers across clowning, music, dance, drag and live art.  \r\n\r\nPast acts include Lucy Hopkins, Julia Masli, Charlie Partridge, Lorna Rose Treen, Frankie Thompson, Coral Bevan, Chewy She, Mermaid Chunky, WET MESS, Sara Segovia, Lachlan Werner, Ella Evans, Ryan Lane, Gemma Soldati, Nancy Trotter Landry, Kaajel Patel, Sarah Woolfenden, Hazel Townsend, Vic Diamente, Dan Lees, Serena Flynn, Alejo de Mesa, Luke Rollason, Anna Marie Simonsen, Charlie Wood and many more.’\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Fool’s Moon Nov23","instanceDates":"25 November-25 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"501403AVBNGKMKPVKBRCGHVHLMTPCLTLK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-25T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-25T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-25T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-25T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Max Rushden, Barry Glendenning and special guests hit the stage to unpack the World Cup, outtakes and too-hot-for-podcast tales.\r\nIn London on 9 September, a host of your favourite Football Weekly panellists will take to the stage in Soho Theatre Walthamstow. \r\n\r\nWe’ve checked the data, Walthamstow is statistically the most Football Weekly place on the planet so anything less than a sell-out is a disaster for us and our vast team of analysts. \r\n \r\nExpect to see Football Weekly regulars, surprise cameos, outtakes and behind the scenes and too-hot-for-podcast content from our time in the USA this summer.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Football Weekly Live","instanceDates":"9 September-9 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"729203AMHRPPCMKDRVKCNMCDMRLNGQPRS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-09T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-09T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-09T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-09T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Podcast","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Talk","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Podcast","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Talk","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":""},{"description":"Joe Pickett (The Onion) and Nick Prueher (Late Show With David Letterman) have over 14,000 VHS tapes in their cluttered office in Brooklyn and will take viewers on a guided tour of their latest/greatest finds in this brand new Volume 11 show for 2026. \r\nHighlights include a psychotic dollar store salesman, a video catalog of frightening porcelain dolls, two wonderfully homemade Bigfoot videos and a new age “miracle” treatment from the 80s called “Psychic Surgery.”\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Found Footage Festival Volume 11","instanceDates":"5 May-7 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"699403ACRBQCNLCCHBGPKCVSMBKSVCTGL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-05T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-05T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-07T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-07T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Step into the joyful and absurd world of Francisco de Nata - A giraffe. \r\nIn a G-string. \r\nWith a job to do.\r\nIn this non-verbal clown show featuring audience interaction, puppetry and yes, a very special Portuguese custard tart, Francisco invites you on a playful journey where nonsense, vulnerability and wonder take centre stage.\r\nTasked with painting a ceiling, his world soon unravels into beautiful chaos, but as the clock ticks and the paint dries, a tender and ridiculous story unfolds about this giraffe's love for his Avó (grandma). \r\nWill it come together before time runs out?\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Francisco de Nata","instanceDates":"29 January-31 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"688003APBLQVRPDGDGGRRNLGLSNNVBCKV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-29T22:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-29T22:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-31T22:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-31T22:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Washed-up club-comic and ‘last straight man in showbiz’ FRANK LAVENDER springs forward from the smoky concert halls of yesteryear to win over modern audiences with one promise: a laugh a minute or their money back. He’s trying his best.\r\n \r\nMore character comedy from Gareth Joyner, the brain (and legs) behind Myra DuBois.\r\n \r\nFeaturing ‘Dave’s 6th Funniest Joke at the Edinburgh Fringe 2023’, which is something to look forward to.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Frank Lavender","instanceDates":"20 May-21 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"535803AJDRLDQJBSGHLCVCVNPSKCGJPPG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-20T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-20T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-21T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-21T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Comic legend Frank Skinner brings his critically acclaimed stand-up show ‘30 Years of Dirt’ for two exclusive performances!\r\nThese shows will be filmed live for Frank’s brand-new stand-up special, set to air later this year.\r\nFollowing three sold-out West End runs and an 85-date, sold-out national tour, this marks the final chance to see 30 Years of Dirt live on stage.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Frank Skinner: 30 Years of Dirt (Live Special Recording)","instanceDates":"25 April-25 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"700603AHRVHPBGHNBMKRTQSDRMLQCGLPJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-25T17:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-25T16:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-25T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-25T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A rare opportunity to see comic legend Frank Skinner as he presents brand new material for the first time since his Showbiz tour which sold out venues around the country from 2019-2021, including a 5 week sell-out residency at The Garrick Theatre in London’s West End. \r\nIn Frank Skinner: Work in Progress, Frank will be developing original material in an intimate setting.\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Frank Skinner: Work in Progress","instanceDates":"2 May-6 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"447603APBRRTRGSPQKDBSHBLSSHPRTQGJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-02T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-02T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-06T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-06T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Work In Progress","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Frankie tells some jokes. Some of them new.\r\nSome shows will have support, possibly all of them, unless he starts writing soon. Some old bits, and reading chunks of his new book, to widespread dismay\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Frankie Boyle: Work in Progress","instanceDates":"21 October-7 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"568803ABVMJCVPVTGSTDCRKBCGJVLPBJN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-21T17:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-21T16:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-07T17:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-07T17:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Catch Melbourne’s Most Outstanding Show nominee straight off the back of their Edinburgh debut.\r\nfter a lifetime of anxiety, complex PTSD, and low self-esteem, Frankie is finally done making themselves small. So now whenever self-doubt creeps in, they ask themselves one simple question: “What would someone with a huge ass do in this situation?” \r\n\r\nA chaotic love letter to comedy, delusional optimism, resilience & becoming the ass you want to see in the world! \r\n\r\nMost Outstanding Show nominee, Melbourne International Comedy Festival 2026 \r\n\r\nBest Newcomer winner, Melbourne International Comedy Festival 2022 \r\n\r\nPLEASE NOTE: Huge Ass Mindset contains topics of sexual assault, childhood sexual assault and wobbly mental health, and may not be suitable for everyone. Audience members are welcome to step out of the show at any time and there will be support phone numbers available :) 18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Frankie McNair: Huge Ass Mindset","instanceDates":"7 September-12 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"720603AGLHDGKGPQBTSPVKPRTCNRVPSTL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-07T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-07T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-12T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-12T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Catch Melbourne’s Most Outstanding Show nominee previewing at Soho ahead of their Edinburgh debut.\r\nAfter a lifetime of anxiety, complex PTSD, and low self-esteem, Frankie is finally done making themselves small. So now whenever self-doubt creeps in, they ask themselves one simple question: “What would someone with a huge ass do in this situation?” \r\n\r\nA chaotic love letter to comedy, delusional optimism, resilience & becoming the ass you want to see in the world! \r\n\r\nMost Outstanding Show nominee, Melbourne International Comedy Festival 2026 \r\n\r\nBest Newcomer winner, Melbourne International Comedy Festival 2022 \r\n\r\nPLEASE NOTE: Huge Ass Mindset contains topics of sexual assault, childhood sexual assault and wobbly mental health, and may not be suitable for everyone. Audience members are welcome to step out of the show at any time and there will be support phone numbers available :) \r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Frankie McNair: Huge Ass Mindset (Edinburgh Preview)","instanceDates":"31 July-1 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"720403ADNKLLTDSTCDSPHBSHVPNCGMBSM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-31T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-31T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-01T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-01T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Yorkshire's Biggest Bastard is back again and doing his biggest bastard shows to date.\r\nThis time you can see Frankie perform his first two sell out, award winning shows LIVE and DEAD back-to-back in one evening. \r\nCatch the full saga as Frankie saves his working men’s club from demonic ruin, escapes hell, and have LOADS of big daft laughs. \r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":100,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Frankie Monroe: DEAD AND ALIVE!!!!","instanceDates":"26 September-26 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"702403ATKCMVSQNLJSVHGLPJNTLJNJGTQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-26T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-26T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-26T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-26T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"What burns at the end of the world? Bodies? Bridges? Calories? Liv Ello and Frankie Thompson present deeply strange, confoundingly funny dark duet of electric, eclectic, unspoken-word about the meeting of dysmorphia, dysphoria, and dystopia.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Frankie Thompson & Liv Ello: Body Show","instanceDates":"25 September-14 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"485403AVPHPGRMRGNCJKGTBGGCQDSNNLT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-25T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-25T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-14T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-14T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Performance Art","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"What burns at the end of the world? Bodies? Bridges? Calories? Liv Ello and Frankie Thompson present deeply strange, confoundingly funny dark duet of electric, eclectic, unspoken-word about the meeting of dysmorphia, dysphoria, and dystopia.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Frankie Thompson & Liv Ello: Body Show (Preview)","instanceDates":"19 July-21 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"474403ASPMDVBGNGNJCDDVQLGVGSVRJHM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-19T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-19T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-21T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-21T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Not a work in progress. \r\nNo progress will be made. \r\nThis is a work in regress. \r\nIn an experiment that is kind of like Bagpuss except horrible, Frankie Thompson is collecting horrible things. Things she’s picked out of her ear, found stuck to the bottom of her shoe, retrieved from the back of the sofa and unexpectedly found in a sandwich. She sniffs them, licks them and then puts them into a show. This is part of her ‘I just need to get this out and see what shape it lands in’ season, around the theme ‘horrible’. At least 70% of the horrible things will have been created in the two days before the show, so please do not come if you’re expecting content, plot and/or structure. Any horrible things that are exactly the flavour she’s looking for will stay, all other horrible things will be recycled responsibly. If you laugh it’s comedy, if you don’t it’s live art.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Frankie Thompson Collects Horrible Things","instanceDates":"14 June-15 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"546003ALDVHGNQSRDQSLDTPTNHJLSMRGB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-14T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-14T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-15T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-15T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Performance Art","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"everybody wants to be a cat because a cat is just a cat\r\nFollowing sell-out runs in Edinburgh and London, the smash hit clown cat cabaret returns.\r\nFrom ‘acclaimed clown’ (To Do List London) and concerted idiot Frankie Thompson comes an anarchic one-woman adaptation of Cats (the musical). But not about cats, not about musicals, not about Cats (the musical). CAttS is a lip-sync ballet through the distractions and obsessions that help us cope with an increasingly dystopian reality. Because after all, wouldn’t we rather think about cats? \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Frankie Thompson: CAttS","instanceDates":"3 June-15 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"545803AKJCGGBCVDKTTRCBLBGJCLKQQRC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-03T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-03T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-15T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-15T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"“Go for the cat-worship, stay for the side-splitting silliness, and rave about it to all your friends... Catts is like nothing you've ever seen before” ★★★★★ (ToDoList.London).\r\n\r\neverybody wants to be a cat \r\n\r\nbecause a cat\r\n\r\nis just \r\n\r\na cat \r\n\r\nFrom “acclaimed clown” (ToDoList.London) and emerging idiot Frankie Thompson, an anarchic one-woman adaptation of Cats (the musical). But not about cats, not about musicals, not about Cats the musical. CAttS is a lip-sync ballet through the distractions and obsessions that help us cope with an increasingly dystopian reality. Because after all, wouldn't we rather think about cats?\r\n16+_\r\n\r\nNew 2023 dates added due to phenomenal demand!","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Frankie Thompson: CAttS.","instanceDates":"2 May-6 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"403603ACJRGHKHCDMMDQCQTMGBRKRPLDD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-02T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-02T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-06T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-06T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Acclaimed clown Frankie Thompson has been collecting horrible things. Things she found down the back of the sofa and floating in her soup uninvited, things she found in the bins of the people in power, things she found in your mum’s daydreams and your dad’s secret past, things she found dusting your grandmother's bedside cabinet (you don’t want to know), and things your uncle uploaded on YouTube in 2008 (you really don’t want to know). Find out if something horrible you’ve done is included, and come along to the formal presentation of all horrible things found thus far. If you laugh, it’s comedy; if you don’t, it’s live art. \r\n\r\n14+ (References to cultural/political issues and mental health issues. Check webpage for current details).\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Frankie Thompson: Horrible Things ","instanceDates":"9 November-21 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"746203AMGTSKPDKNVJJPCPLLTSKJVHCBM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-09T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-09T21:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-21T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-21T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Performance Art","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"Acclaimed clown Frankie Thompson has been collecting horrible things.Things she found down the back of the sofa and floating in her soup uninvited, things she found in the bins of the people in power, things she found in your mum’s daydreams and your dad’s secret past, things she found dusting your grandmother's bedside cabinet (you don’t want to know), and things your uncle uploaded on YouTube in 2008 (you really don’t want to know).\r\nFind out if something horrible you’ve done is included, and come along to the formal presentation of all horrible things found thus far. If you laugh, it’s comedy; if you don’t, it’s live art.\r\nCatch Frankie previewing Horrible Things before she heads up to the Edinburgh Fringe.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Frankie Thompson: Horrible Things (Edinburgh Preview)","instanceDates":"20 July-22 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"716003AMBLMKKQLJLBRQSVMDKQSVDJBNS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-20T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-20T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-22T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-22T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Performance Art","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"Acclaimed clown Frankie Thompson has been collecting horrible things.\r\nThings she found down the back of the sofa and floating in her soup uninvited, things she found in the bins of the people in power, things she found in your mum’s daydreams and your dad’s secret past, things she found dusting your grandmother's bedside cabinet (you don’t want to know), and things your uncle uploaded on YouTube in 2008 (you really don’t want to know).\r\nFind out if something horrible you’ve done is included, and come along to the formal presentation of all horrible things found thus far. If you laugh, it’s comedy; if you don’t, it’s live art.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":false,"name":"Frankie Thompson: Horrible Things Oct26","instanceDates":"12 October-24 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"716203ALLBCCDKBRGVGVSTNSPSJDPKBBR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-12T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-12T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-24T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-24T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Performance Art","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"Fred Strangebone has something to show you... Unbolt the creaky door to an unsettled world of creeping, dark comedy and clownish physical humour. Master of the uncomfortable silence, Fred will attempt to amuse you with macabre material, inspired by his peculiar life in a world that rejects and abuses him. A performance by Fred Strangebone is an experience you won’t forget... no matter how hard you try.\r\nFred Strangebone is a character created by voice artist and comedy actor Ben Whitehead, best known as the voice of Wallace in recent and upcoming ‘Wallace & Gromit’ Productions from Aardman animations\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Fred Strangebone Performs Comedy","instanceDates":"20 June-20 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"617403AMVCBCGQNNSBBBPGNRMNRCMGVMR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-20T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-20T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-20T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-20T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Outrageous faux magic show by puppeteer and clown Freddie Hayes as The Magic Lady. This haphazard showbiz loon infiltrates the Magic Circle after years of toiling as a magician's glamorous assistant, stepping out of the shadows and into the spotlight to tread the boards once more.\r\nExpect puppetry, camp surprises, body popping, levitation, exorcisms and hypnotism.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Freddie Hayes: The Magic Lady","instanceDates":"21 June-21 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"615404ACTVCQSDMVMGRBKVQCKHTGCBBNM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-21T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-21T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-21T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-21T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"This could really be a sick night.\r\nA self-appointed thought leader holds court in the smoking area of a club, unpacking masculinity, fame and the algorithm while soft launching himself to strangers. The critically acclaimed debut hour from character comedian Freddie Meredith. There'll be confusion at the bar, grace on the dance floor, honesty by the bins. No filter, no followers. The wrong strategy for the right night.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Freddie Meredith: Need a Light?","instanceDates":"21 September-19 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"744603AGSLTDLKSDGTRHDSMGBBDRQHSTJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-21T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-21T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-06-19T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-06-19T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"FUCCBOIS: LIVE IN CONCERT is a comedy-boyband-extravaganza: an irreverent satire full of bangers!\r\nThe Fuccbois are the world’s biggest boyband. They’ve sold more tickets and broken more hearts than anyone, but now it’s time to say goodbye to their frosted tips forever; they’re done. \r\nFrom award-winning writer Bridie Connell, FUCCBOIS: LIVE IN CONCERT is a massive comedy-boyband-extravaganza. It’s an irreverent satire of toxic dating culture, but most importantly: the music is banging. \r\n15+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"FUCCBOIS: LIVE IN CONCERT","instanceDates":"2 September-5 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"723603ABDGLRTBLRDRRVDLBSKBTNLGRSK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-02T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-02T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-05T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-05T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"“A funny comedy show all about a silly little guy called me.\"\r\n\r\nAlternative comedian and kindly clown Mikey Bligh-Smith presents an open-house tour of his carefully constructed mind-palace. Madcap prop chaos. Tremendous jokes and wordplay. Hardcore, unfiltered, Full-Frontal Mikey Mode.  \r\n\r\nMember of anarchic sketch comedy group The Lovely Boys. Sketch Off Finalist.  \r\n\r\nAs seen on CH4 and Disney+  \r\n\r\n\"Very fun... meticulously weird\" (Guardian)  \r\n\r\n\"Unexpectedly and unexplainably brought me to tears\" (Entertainment Focus)  \r\n\r\n\"Cracking physical comedy\" (Chortle)\r\n\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Full Frontal Mikey Mode","instanceDates":"18 August-19 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"733204ARKLVJTNLNSRMKGJVQTDTCQKKQT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-18T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-18T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-19T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-19T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"After sold out Soho Theatre runs and touring around Australia, Furiozo returns to London. This solo punk-rock comedy show stars one man – Furiozo: an aggressive hooligan with a giant heart. Police chases, petty theft, drugs, and longing for the greatest thrill of all: true love. A disturbing yet absurdly funny portrait of toxic masculinity. You will love him. You will hate him. You will experience the presence of the beast. \r\nAs Furiozo would say: Live fast; Die.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Furiozo: Man Looking For Trouble","instanceDates":"30 June-4 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"632604ALNNMHQPLGBNNMRMSJJPVHVLLKN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-30T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-30T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-04T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-04T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Furiozo returns to London after a sell-out season at 2023 Edinburgh Fringe. This solo punk-rock comedy show stars one man – Furiozo: an aggressive hooligan with a giant heart. Police chases, petty theft, drugs, and longing for the greatest thrill of all: true love. A disturbing yet absurdly funny portrait of toxic masculinity. You will love him. You will hate him. You will experience the presence of the beast. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Furiozo: Man Looking For Trouble Apr24","instanceDates":"26 April-27 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"534803ASCJBPGPTCQCRCGLGRVQNTVBJJH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-26T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-26T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-27T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-27T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A punk-rock clown comedy. Meet Furiozo, an aggressive hooligan with a giant heart. Police chases, petty theft, drugs and longing for the greatest thrill of all – true love. Love him, hate him, feel the presence of the beast. Part of London Clown Festival 2024.\r\nPick of the Week Award, Adelaide 2024. Comedy of the Week Award, Perth 2024. Shortlisted for Best Show in Comedians' Choice Awards, Edinburgh 2023.\r\nThis solo punk-rock comedy show stars one man – Furiozo: an aggressive hooligan with a giant heart. Police chases, petty theft, drugs, and longing for the greatest thrill of all: true love. A disturbing yet absurdly funny portrait of toxic masculinity. You will love him. You will hate him. You will experience the presence of the beast.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Furiozo: Man Looking for Trouble.","instanceDates":"11 July-11 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"546603AJJDRJDMCQDBHGDTLPCHTNTJTGN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-11T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-11T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-11T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-11T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Puberty. So good, he did it twice.\r\nAfter an award-nominated run at the Brighton Fringe, transgender DILF clown Indy Nile is bringing his solo show to Soho Theatre.\r\nFeaturing Microsoft PowerPoint, Shania Twain, and Lynx Africa, this is set to be the gender reveal party of the century. And you're all invited.*\r\nA mash-up of drag, stand-up, and theatre, He/He/He is Indy Nile's second-coming-of-age story. And there's a lot he wants to get off his chest. Sorry.\r\n*Party gifts optional, but very welcome.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Gabriel Harris: He/He/He","instanceDates":"13 February-13 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"587603ABQGBSCDBCVHKPDQCMPTRPTRCDC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-13T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-13T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-13T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-13T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"In the wake of a relationship, a woman tries to contain the overflow of her thoughts… She ends up stuck in a ladder, making out with a komodo dragon, fighting up against house leaks, holes and jam jars- that only seem to multiply.\r\nInspired by a break-up and over 40 interviews from a social media call-out, DELUGE puts a magic realist spin on dealing with and overcoming grief. Blurring imagination with real stories by invoking a surreal, tender and humorous dreamscape.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Gabriela Flarys: DELUGE","instanceDates":"18 February-18 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"590603ARDNMKTNCSKCNQLSQCKSHLPRVNH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-18T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-18T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-18T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-18T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Theatre"},{"description":"Join GAY TIMES as we celebrate the launch of GAG!, our exciting new series that showcases the best of queer comedy and cabaret talent. With a focus on diverse performers who push boundaries and challenge conventions, GAG! is the ultimate destination for fans of comedy that is fresh, funny and fabulous.\r\nFeaturing:\r\nDaniel Foxx\r\nDan Wye \r\nLeila Navabi \r\nJodie Mitchell\r\nVictoria Olsina\r\nSu Mi\r\nDom McGovern \r\n\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"GAG! A Queer Comedy Night","instanceDates":"30 June-30 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"482003AMNQJBDNTSTHSKQVGCHLKNPPCJG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-30T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-30T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-30T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-30T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Literature! Literature! Literature! It might not rhyme with anything but it’s still very important. Following a smash-hit, sell out Edinburgh Festival last year, Garry Starr is back and he’s hell-bent on saving books from extinction by performing every Penguin Classic novel ever written. Mostly naked (but with flippers). \r\nComic wunderkind Starr takes us on a literary adventure through the world’s most iconic works of fiction. From The Little Prince to Moby Dick and everything in between, nothing is safe from being lampooned with the utmost nincompoopery.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Garry Starr: Classic Penguins","instanceDates":"14 July-26 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"611403AJQVPSBGBNKTRLSRVMRHVTQQLQM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-14T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-14T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-26T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-26T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The polar ice caps are melting! By this time next year, penguins will have nowhere to live. Having already saved pretty much everything else, Garry Starr is now taking it upon himself to single-handedly save our flightless, feathered friends from extinction by performing every Penguin Classic novel ever written. In an hour. Mostly naked (but with flippers).\r\n18+ (nudity)","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Garry Starr: Classic Penguins.","instanceDates":"16 May-18 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"537803AGBMVQRLJDLGJTJCBPRQSPJCMQM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-16T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-16T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-18T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-18T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"An overzealous idiot attempts to perform all of Greek Mythology in order to save his Hellenic homeland from economic ruin.\r\nNever before has Medusa been looser, Achilles more sillies or Uranus so heinous.\r\n\r\nWINNER Pick of the Fringe - Adelaide Fringe 2022\r\nWINNER Best Comedy - Manchester Fringe 2022\r\nWINNER Best in Fest - Gothenburg Fringe 2022\r\n\r\nHaving single handedly saved the performing arts in 2018 with his multi-award-winning debut show Garry Starr Performs Everything, comic wunderkind Garry returns with another anarchic masterclass not to be mythed.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Garry Starr: Greece Lightning","instanceDates":"15 August-19 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"485003APNKLNRBTNHKRTLGBCSVGQQLNCP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-15T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-15T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-19T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-19T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Grandiloquent is Gary Gulman’s hilarious new show about insecurity, empathy, self-acceptance and how a thoughtful boy learned to use humour, reading and writing to cope with the consequences of his parents’ blunders.\r\nLearn why a seemingly confident middle-aged man feels most comfortable in a large room where hundreds of strangers are laughing at him.\r\n\r\nFresh form a sell-out Off-Broadway run at the Lucille Lortel Theatre, one of the most respected comics in the US makes his UK debut with his critically acclaimed one-man show.\r\n\r\nDirected by Tony Award winner Moritz von Stuelpnagel\r\n\r\nGary Gulman has made five masterful TV specials including his most recent universally acclaimed stand-up specials for HBO Max, Born On 3rd Base, lending his meticulous comedic craft to the current Tale of Two Cities-esque wealth gap, and The Great Depresh, a tour de force look at mental illness, which is equal parts hilarious and inspiring. In 2019, he appeared in the international blockbuster Joker and can most recently be seen co-starring with Amy Schumer in the hit Hulu comedy series, Life & Beth. \r\nLearn why a seemingly confident middle-aged man feels most comfortable in a large room where hundreds of strangers are laughing at him.\r\n\r\nFresh form a sell-out Off-Broadway run at the Lucille Lortel Theatre, one of the most respected comics in the US makes his UK debut with his critically acclaimed one-man show.\r\n\r\nDirected by Tony Award winner Moritz von Stuelpnagel\r\n\r\nGary Gulman has made five masterful TV specials including his most recent universally acclaimed stand-up specials for HBO Max, Born On 3rd Base, lending his meticulous comedic craft to the current Tale of Two Cities-esque wealth gap, and The Great Depresh, a tour de force look at mental illness, which is equal parts hilarious and inspiring. In 2019, he appeared in the international blockbuster Joker and can most recently be seen co-starring with Amy Schumer in the hit Hulu comedy series, Life & Beth. \r\nLearn why a seemingly confident middle-aged man feels most comfortable in a large room where hundreds of strangers are laughing at him.\r\n\r\nFresh form a sell-out Off-Broadway run at the Lucille Lortel Theatre, one of the most respected comics in the US makes his UK debut with his critically acclaimed one-man show.\r\n\r\nDirected by Tony Award winner Moritz von Stuelpnagel\r\n\r\nGary Gulman has made five masterful TV specials including his most recent universally acclaimed stand-up specials for HBO Max, Born On 3rd Base, lending his meticulous comedic craft to the current Tale of Two Cities-esque wealth gap, and The Great Depresh, a tour de force look at mental illness, which is equal parts hilarious and inspiring. In 2019, he appeared in the international blockbuster Joker and can most recently be seen co-starring with Amy Schumer in the hit Hulu comedy series, Life & Beth. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":80,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Gary Gulman: Grandiloquent","instanceDates":"6 October-11 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"648803AHNGSJKPBGNJCLHLMHVCDCCHTKD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-06T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-06T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-11T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-11T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Gașca Zurli, together with Maya and Mirela Retegan, are returning to London! Join us on 7 November at Soho Theatre Walthamstow!","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"GASCA ZURLI","instanceDates":"7 November-7 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"754003AQDRCKQNCRRMPVVNHGCTLHVRDQQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-07T12:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-07T12:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-07T12:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-07T12:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Families","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"After a sold-out North American tour and the release of his debut comedy special A SENSE OF URGENCY, New York City-based standup comedian and co-host of the acclaimed StraightioLab podcast George Civeris brings his \"monster wit and broad palette\" to London!\r\nGeorge Civeris is an NYC-based comedian and writer, and the co-host of the acclaimed podcast StraightioLab. He was named one of the New Faces of Comedy by the Just for Laughs Comedy Festival and one of Vulture's \"Comedians You Should and Will Know in 2024.\" George has written for shows on Comedy Central, FOX, and the BBC, and spent two years as a senior editor at the reboot of Gawker.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"George Civeris: Is That True?","instanceDates":"23 February-24 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"687603AMTPCCDTMHKMPRCSGSCCHHMLDGB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-23T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-23T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-24T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-24T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Melbourne Comedy Festival best show winner Geraldine Hickey makes her Soho Theatre debut. \r\nJoin Gerladine as she shares stories about acknowledging & enjoying new-found privileges, like getting married & being able to buy a nice camera to take photos of birds.  \r\n\r\nGeraldine is very good at telling funny stories, it’s why she’s won comedy awards in Australia and can afford nice cameras and horses.  \r\n \r\nOkay the horses aren’t technically hers, they belong to her wife Cath & one of them is a pony. As they say, “what’s mine is yours”.  \r\n \r\nIt will be a very joyful show. \r\n \r\nAs seen on Have You Been Paying Attention?. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Geraldine Hickey: Of Course We’ve Got Horses","instanceDates":"29 August-2 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"489603ANSRGHCTTMDCJJPGKVLMHDPGPJS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-29T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-29T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-02T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-02T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"An improv comedy show… with a brilliant live band. Improvisation meets improvisation as hilarious improv comedians and virtuoso jazz musicians inspire each other in real time into leaps of comedy and creativity. Created by Max Dickins and Conor Jatter, Giant Steps features a rotating ensemble of top talent from hit improv shows like Showstoppers and Austentatious, plus the best up-and-coming music talent. Expect fresh licks and big laughs in a one-of-a-kind show that's different every night. **** The Times **** List **** Fest **** The Stage **** ‘Seamless silliness’ Reviews Hub **** ‘Great charm and talent’ The Scotsman ***** ‘An absolute must see’ Theatre Weekly ***** ‘Lethal levels of laughter’ Three Weeks ***** ‘Truly gifted improvisers’ Joke Pit: 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"GIANT STEPS","instanceDates":"3 August-5 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"734003AJDLQDJJRDSRGTRMQRBJTDGQLHP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-03T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-03T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-05T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-05T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":""},{"description":"An improv comedy show… with a brilliant live band. Improvisation meets improvisation as hilarious improv comedians and virtuoso jazz musicians inspire each other in real time into leaps of comedy and creativity. Created by Max Dickins and Conor Jatter, Giant Steps features a rotating ensemble of top talent from hit improv shows like Showstoppers and Austentatious, plus the best up-and-coming music talent. Expect fresh licks and big laughs in a one-of-a-kind show that's different every night.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"GIANT STEPS 25","instanceDates":"7 July-9 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"627403ASKVBBGLQTRPRLCQRSRQPKCBSTK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-07T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-07T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-09T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-09T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"illian Cosgriff won Most Outstanding Show at the 2023 Melbourne International Comedy Festival with this brilliant hour of hilarious original songs, killer stand-up, and a big book of things that are actually good.\r\nIn 2022, she started asking people what they like. The answers were simple and complex, hilarious and beautiful. Cloves. Fancy hotel foyers. Seeing a cow and yelling, 'Cow!' This is a show about the little things that make the big hard things manageable, and pointing at the bits of the world that make you yell, 'Wow! Isn't this great?!\"\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Gillian Cosgriff: Actually, Good","instanceDates":"7 May-18 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"518603AHJSKTHMTVKQVLCCBDBKQSMKSNS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-07T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-07T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-18T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-18T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join comedian, crash mat and winner of Drag Race UK Ginger Johnson as she swaps her stilettos for safety goggles and takes a death-defying leap from the runway to the real world. \r\nExpect big hair, big heart and big laughs as Britain’s ditziest daredevil takes on her biggest challenge yet and asks the question: just how far will she go for a round of applause?\r\n \r\nBursting with stunning looks and cunning stunts, GINGER JOHNSON BLOWS OFF! is a hilarious new show about taking risks, pushing yourself and living up to expectations. \r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ginger Johnson Blows Off at HOME, Manchester","instanceDates":"22 November-22 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"557603APQDNDPNGGBGTBPMLGJVBPRRLKD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-22T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-22T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-22T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-22T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"HOME, Manchester","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Join comedian, crash mat and winner of Drag Race UK Ginger Johnson as she swaps her stilettos for safety goggles and takes a death-defying leap from the runway to the real world.\r\nBursting with stunning looks and cunning stunts, GINGER JOHNSON BLOWS OFF! is a hilarious new show about taking risks, pushing yourself and living up to expectations. \r\n \r\nNot for the faint of fart.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ginger Johnson Blows Off!","instanceDates":"23 September-12 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"554403ALCTGCVJCJPJHVVNMRBHPBDQCSN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-23T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-23T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-12T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-12T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Join comedian, crash mat and winner of Drag Race UK Ginger Johnson as she swaps her stilettos for safety goggles 