ow about taking risks, pushing yourself and living up to expectations. \r\n \r\nNot for the faint of fart.\r\n14+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ginger Johnson Blows Off! at Crescent Theatre, Birmingham","instanceDates":"24 October-24 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"555603ALMGQSVSVSLTPDCHGVCSHKQNPPL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-24T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-24T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-24T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-24T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Crescent Theatre, Birmingham","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Join comedian, crash mat and winner of Drag Race UK Ginger Johnson as she swaps her stilettos for safety goggles and takes a death-defying leap from the runway to the real world.\r\nExpect big hair, big heart and big laughs as Britain’s ditziest daredevil takes on her biggest challenge yet and asks the question: just how far will she go for a round of applause?\r\n \r\nBursting with stunning looks and cunning stunts, GINGER JOHNSON BLOWS OFF! is a hilarious new show about taking risks, pushing yourself and living up to expectations. \r\n \r\nNot for the faint of fart.\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ginger Johnson Blows Off! at Komedia Bath","instanceDates":"17 October-17 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"554603AMDVJTLHJNLNDRBJHGKVCQJPPKG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-17T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-17T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-17T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-17T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Komedia Bath","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Join comedian, crash mat and winner of Drag Race UK Ginger Johnson as she swaps her stilettos for safety goggles and takes a death-defying leap from the runway to the real world.\r\nExpect big hair, big heart and big laughs as Britain’s ditziest daredevil takes on her biggest challenge yet and asks the question: just how far will she go for a round of applause?\r\n \r\nBursting with stunning looks and cunning stunts, GINGER JOHNSON BLOWS OFF! is a hilarious new show about taking risks, pushing yourself and living up to expectations. \r\n \r\nNot for the faint of fart.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ginger Johnson Blows Off! at The Y Theatre, Leicester","instanceDates":"27 October-27 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"554803APHQBCTNVRGQCNBVPGTQPRRMHKJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-27T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-27T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-27T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-27T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Leicester Y","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Direct from the runway of Rupaul’s Drag Race UK, join award-winning artist, writer and all round silly sausage, Ginger Johnson, for a wild night in by the festive fireside.\r\nFeaturing live renditions of camp christmas classics, as well as deep cuts from the stranger side of the holiday songbook, Ginger All the Way! promises more ham than a boxing day buffet.\r\n\r\nBest known for her barnstorming theatrics and sweet tooth for the ridiculous, Ginger’s unique blend of camp laughs and bareknuckle confessional have earned her a reputation for being a powerhouse performer with a big heart and an even bigger mouth.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ginger Johnson: Ginger All the Way!","instanceDates":"12 December-6 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"508203AVHVVRQTPPCDHJMRVLCLVLLLHPQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-12T22:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-12T22:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-06T22:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-06T22:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"You’ve seen her in the Masterchef kitchen… You’ve seen her on the Drag Race runway… Now it's time to see her in her element: outrageous, untamed and completely off the reins.\r\nFollowing the explosive success of her smash hit 2024 tour ‘Ginger Johnson Blows Off!’, the nation’s silliest sausage is back on the road with her brand new live spectacular: Show Pony!\r\n\r\nPromising high camp, low morals, and double helpings of her trademark ridiculousness, Show Pony is a barnstorming night of whip-smart comedy and top-tier talent that proves why Ginger is one of Britain’s most beloved queens.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ginger Johnson: Show Pony","instanceDates":"2 November-7 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"681803ATGVKVQRCLDTVHSSQKSSRLVKPKN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-02T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-02T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-07T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-07T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Crackling stand-up, raucous cabaret, brilliantly chaotic performance art and electrifying original music from the “The Queen of the West Midlands” & original “Bastard of Drag” Ginny Lemon. A not to be missed debut solo show from one of the UK’s most celebrated drag artists. \r\n‘What an asshole’ RuPaul \r\n‘I Love You’ Su Pollard\r\n‘Very, VERY funny’ John Waters \r\n‘Hideous’ Simon Cowell \r\n\r\nGinny Lemon is a midlands based singer-songwriter, improvisational comedienne, TV personality, character actor and spiritualist. Their work explores the intersections of their working-class identity, queerness, disability and taking the piss. Ginny’s distinct acidic wit, aesthetic and unique perspective on life have made them one of the UK’s most celebrated drag and performance artists.\r\nA breakout star of RuPaul’s Drag Race UK Season 2, they have performed to sell-out audiences across the UK and made television appearances for BBC, ITV & Channel 4, including The X Factor, Joe Lycett’s Got Your Back & Celebrity Coach Trip. Their previous work includes as creator of Ginny Lemon’s Pick ‘n’ Mix residency at the Village Inn, Birmingham, a co-creator & cast member for Fantabulosa: A Drag Show For Kids, Mobilise: A Sober Party for the LGBTQ+ Community and starred in the Birmingham 2022 Commonwealth Games Opening Ceremony flying in in a giant lemon shaped hot air balloon. \r\nThey released their second album, Tonic, supported by Arts Council, England. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ginny Lemon: Bitter","instanceDates":"16 July-20 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"560003AQRJBMRHLJDKGHBQVTKDGDDPDNN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-16T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-16T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-20T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-20T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"After a culture-shifting stint in Los Angeles, where Hollywood was changed to its very core, Iraqi drag sensation Glamrou comes back to London to share new tales of mothers, lovers and anal.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Glamrou Returns! (Work in Progress)","instanceDates":"8 July-9 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"548603AMSMRQHCVVVNNVVPLKHMVBDPDDK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-08T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-08T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-09T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-09T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Drag","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Work In Progress","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Comedy"},{"description":"A tale of two mothers. Renowned Iraqi queen Glamrou, and renowned Iraqi queen, Glamrou's mother, fight for the spotlight with their competing narratives of WHAT REALLY HAPPENED. Come get lost in this drag hall of mirrors, where one queen's truth is another queen's fiction. Featuring live music, live comedy and live delusion, Muslim drag sensation Glamrou is here to activate your Freudian wounds. With a stiletto.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Glamrou: Drag Mother","instanceDates":"20 January-25 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"585003ANRCVNDHJVRSSVLJJLNJKCQCRHP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-20T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-20T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-25T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-25T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"LGBTQ+","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Drag","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Edinburgh Comedy Award nominee Glenn Moore has written too many jokes again. Expect a fast-paced whirlwind of punchlines from one of the greatest joke-writers of his generation.\r\nAs seen on Live At The Apollo, Have I Got News For You, Mock The Week, Cats Does Countdown. As heard on The Dave Berry Breakfast Show on Absolute Radio, The News Quiz, Just A Minute, and his own Radio 4 series Glenn Moore's Almanac.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Glenn Moore: Please Sir, Glenn I Have Some Moore?","instanceDates":"8 September-13 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"629403AQHTJPGJMCLSJCLLTJNVDGHGBCJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-08T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-08T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-13T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-13T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Fresh from sell out Soho Theatre run, Gobby Girls are back! \r\nCreated from scratch by two women-led comedy production powerhouses, Gobby Girl Productions and Female Pilot Club, this is a brand new hour following a sold-out run at the Edinburgh Festival of Gobby Girls: The 11% Club.\r\nWritten and performed by a hand-picked bunch from the frontlines of TV and stand-up, this is an unmissable hour of female-led fun. These women are the future of funny. And they’ll have you laughing along as they let you into their fabulous and frustrating worlds.\r\nTheir Edinburgh show was filmed by NextUp Comedy and won Mervyn’s Pick of the Fringe.\r\nNow they’re back with an after party that’s bigger, bolder and a little bit naughtier.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Gobby Girls: The After Party","instanceDates":"1 April-4 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"700003AMBVQQQPPMSVMCSMHCQJQCGJLKR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-01T16:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-01T15:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-04T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-04T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Sketch","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Created from scratch by two women-led comedy production powerhouses, Gobby Girl Productions and Female Pilot Club, this is a brand new hour following a sold-out run at the Edinburgh Festival of Gobby Girls: The 11% Club.\r\nWritten and performed by a hand-picked bunch from the frontlines of TV and stand-up, this is an unmissable hour of female-led fun. These women are the future of funny. And they’ll have you laughing along as they let you into their fabulous and frustrating worlds.\r\nTheir Edinburgh show was filmed by NextUp Comedy and won Mervyn’s Pick of the Fringe.\r\nNow they’re back with an after party that’s bigger, bolder and a little bit naughtier.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Gobby Girls: The After Party.","instanceDates":"20 November-22 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"667803ATBLBSSKGDLGKNQMQMCBMRNCBRS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-20T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-20T22:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-22T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-22T22:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Sketch","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"This is a story of an unlikely friendship with a 50-year age gap. Oh, and death!\r\nTold by real-life siblings (Maddie on the mic, Marcus on the keys), Goodbye Dandelion follows 87-year-old Darcy’s last years on earth through the eyes of a new friend. Blending storytelling and live piano, this bold and witty new show tries to make sense of the un-make-sense-able and asks what’s stopping us from really living. From the team behind Fringe hit Pickle Jar. 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Goodbye Dandelion","instanceDates":"23 July-23 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"729603ANPVTKBTVHLDGQBRJJVMMHKQKNC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-23T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-23T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-23T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-23T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Work In Progress","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Levy Rozman aka GothamChess, the world’s most prominent chess creator, is coming back to London.\r\nFollowing a successful European tour in 2025, international creator Levy Rozman (better known as GothamChess) is returning with his biggest London show yet. The live show is aimed not only at seasoned chess connoisseurs and experts, but at all chess enthusiasts. On his tour, he shares strategic know-how in an entertaining and informative way. The audience can look forward to interviews and exciting guessing games, such as the popular “Guess the ELO” format. Fans can watch live as Levy Rozman takes on multiple players simultaneously (including celebrity guests) in blitz chess. The chess star will comment on and analyse the moves, providing deep insights into the infinitely diverse world of chess. Levy Rozman is known for his entertaining and educational chess content on YouTube, Twitch and other platforms. He holds the title of International Master and, as GothamChess, reaches more than 10 million people worldwide.\r\n\r\nAll ages","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"GothamChess: The GothamChess Europe Tour 2026","instanceDates":"10 November-10 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"711003AMPJCJVCHVPRPDPVMSSSQJSLCVP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-10T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-10T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-10T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-10T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"“Comedy genius” (The Independent) Grace Campbell hosts some of her comedy friends.\r\nJoin the chart-topping, self-obsessed, limitlessly-opinionated Grace Campbell for a wild night of comedy featuring some of the people she finds the funniest. Expect the unexpected. \r\n\r\nFull line up to be announced very soon. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":125,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Grace Campbell & The People She Finds Funny","instanceDates":"1 October-2 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"639403AGJJQNDDSDBHDCJTKMVSMMQNBJR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-01T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-01T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-02T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-02T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"One night only. Some of Grace’s funniest mates. And a festive show you won’t forget - even after three glasses of prosecco.\r\nJoin Grace for a night of sparkling stand-up, unexpected guests, and some classic seasonal oversharing, all (gift) wrapped up in what can only be described as a very funny, very fun Christmas special. \r\nThere might be a spot of carolling. There might be jollity. Grace might get a kiss under the mistletoe.\r\nExpect the unexpected - from rising comedy stars to surprise appearances - as Grace curates a line-up of the people she personally finds hilarious (and she has very good taste).\r\nIt’s your ultimate December night out: entertaining, slightly unhinged (in a joyful way), and absolutely not your average Christmas show.\r\nOne night only. Tickets are limited. Guests announced soon.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":145,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Grace Campbell & The People She Finds Funny: A Very Funny Christmas","instanceDates":"6 December-6 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"668203AGDRKGPTHDDVTPCJQRBGTPNMTSP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-06T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-06T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-06T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-06T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"Are you a lesbian or a straight guy? Are you neither & just looking to learn more about both? That’s so freaking awesome!\r\nBefore Grace Kuhlenschmidt gets on stage she heavily encourages you to introduce yourself & meet every other audience member. Feel free to walk around with a pen and paper & take notes. When the show begins, sit down. Shut up. As soon as the show is over, the rest of your life will begin. From this point on, you will know up to 149 lesbians or straight guys (maybe even gay guys or straight girls although what can we really depend on them for?). This is what you are paying for. The show is free, you are paying for the experience. Grace’s gift to you... she loves you?\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Grace Kuhlenschmidt: Lesbian and Straight Guy Night","instanceDates":"23 April-24 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"605003ARBCKPTMVPRDQGRQPBRBDNKGDCQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-23T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-23T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-24T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-24T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Founders of legendary, smash-hit improv shows 'Austentatious' and 'The Bear Pack', these two \"best friends\" (Graham) are on a mission to convince you that improv is actually pretty cool. Spoiler alert: it just might be. Come and watch these two \"colleagues\" (Steen) as they make up an entire show on the spot before your astonished eyes.  16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Graham & Steen","instanceDates":"20 May-21 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"621003ALPQGBPJKKRBGBJGGNTQHHGNBVP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-20T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-20T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-21T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-21T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"A workshop production of a fabulous new musical comedy based on the extraordinary life of artist, potter and national treasure, Grayson Perry.\r\nWhat the hell is normal?  Follow Grayson, as he struggles to make his mark in life, never quite feeling like he fits in.  From the wrong class, wearing the wrong dress and making the wrong choices, Grayson journeys from his Essex working class council estate to the dizzy heights of the Tate Modern – an irreverent odyssey via marital breakdown, career disasters and some life-coaching from a six-foot teddy bear.  \r\nWith music by Richard ‘Jerry Springer’ Thomas, book by Sara-Ella Ozbek and lyrics & life story by Sir Grayson Perry this is a show about growing up to be a man, with themes of domestic violence, therapy, art and cross-dressing – you know, all your usual musical comedy tropes. \r\nRecommended for 14+.  Some depiction of emotional & physical domestic abuse, plus frank exploration of childhood trauma and fetishised sexuality.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":140,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"GRAYSON THE MUSICAL","instanceDates":"16 July-19 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"721003ASPMDJRQPGGKKQRRSSLNLKVCBGK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-16T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-16T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-19T15:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-19T14:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"Olive and Teddy are back. And this time, it’s vertical.\r\nIt’s 1985, and past-it explorer Teddy Tyrell has blindly pledged to both find, then conquer, a mountain bigger than Everest. Even with his ever-doting assistant, Olive Bacon, by his side, surely this is one boast too far. Or is it? Is there really anything bigger than Everest? Will their crampons give them cramp? And is it actually possible for two performers to look like they’re climbing a mountain while only two feet off the ground?\r\nBAD ALTITUDE is a stupid 1980s action film adventure that pulls at the excesses of the decade and rubs them in your face. You say “rip off”, we say, “lovingly referenced”.\r\nWith sold-out runs at the Edinburgh Fringe under their thermal belts, Great British Mysteries are thrilled to be back at the Soho Theatre with this extremely tall tale.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Great British Mysteries: BAD ALTITUDE.","instanceDates":"23 August-26 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"487603AKPJTSCKNNVJGCKCSQMCNGGHHTV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-23T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-23T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-26T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-26T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Sketch","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Olive and Teddy are back. And this time, it’s vertical.\r\nIt’s 1985, and past-it explorer Teddy Tyrell has blindly pledged to both find, then conquer, a mountain bigger than Everest. Even with his ever-doting assistant, Olive Bacon, by his side, surely this is one boast too far. Or is it? Is there really anything bigger than Everest? Will their crampons give them cramp? And is it actually possible for two performers to look like they’re climbing a mountain while only two feet off the ground?\r\nBAD ALTITUDE is a stupid 1980s action film adventure that pulls at the excesses of the decade and rubs them in your face. You say “rip off”, we say, “lovingly referenced”.\r\nWith sold-out runs at the Edinburgh Fringe under their thermal belts, Great British Mysteries are thrilled to be back at the Soho Theatre with this extremely tall tale.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":65,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Great British Mysteries: MAN MOUNTAIN","instanceDates":"30 July-3 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"558403ACCTRNLRCBRCMNTRPHBTDJJSTLK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-30T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-30T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-03T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-03T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Sketch","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"\"If my son was hypothetically gay, hypothetically, where would the Greek church stand with that? The church said ‘Soulla, you know, we love the sinner.’ I said, shut up.\"\r\nNorth London’s Cypriot goddess Soulla brings her crazy, unpredictable madness to life in Soho. But don't be nervous. You're Jennifer Lopez. Greek Expectations dives into the life of a Greek influencer navigating the highs and lows of family, culture, and the mess of everyday life. Get ready for an audacious night of laughter, unapologetic craziness, some tears, and pure joy.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Greek Expectations - An Evening with Soulla Aug24","instanceDates":"9 August-14 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"558603ADJKLHMDBPGVDVPGMMDNSCKBMBP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-09T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-09T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-14T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-14T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Drag","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"North London’s Cypriot goddess Soulla brings her crazy, unpredictable madness to life in Soho. But don't be nervous. You're Jennifer Lopez. Greek Expectations dives into the life of a Greek influencer navigating the highs and lows of family, culture, and the mess of everyday life. Get ready for an audacious night of laughter, unapologetic craziness, some tears, and pure joy.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Greek Expectations: An Evening with Soulla","instanceDates":"17 June-21 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"628203AJHNCLRNPHBBHLMVHVRJMHVMPSS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-17T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-17T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-21T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-21T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Drag","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join The Taskmaster Greg Davies, as he tries out new new material ahead of his sold out national tour! \r\nGreg is heading back out on tour for the first time in 7 years with his brand-new 2025 stand-up show Full Fat Legend. \r\nStar of shows such as Taskmaster, The Inbetweeners, The Cleaner, Never Mind The Buzzcocks, Man Down and Cuckoo, this is Greg’s biggest live tour yet, so don’t miss this rare opportunity for a sneak preview of the next phase of Greg’s comedy journey!\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Greg Davies WIP","instanceDates":"6 January-8 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"589003AKJTVDGDHQRJTGVHBSQTHRQKCGB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-06T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-06T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-08T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-08T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Description / copy\r\n\tSee the Proopcast Live in Swinging London. Greg will record the podcast with the usual mix of so- called jokes, singing, poor dancing and boring preachy parts. Then meet all you kittens. Everyone wins and then we go for chips. Sexy people only.\r\nBe there and experience joy for once in your life.\r\nDownload for free at: Proopcast.com or gregproops.com\r\n“Here he is, though, in front of a live audience each\r\nweek, bravely recording some of the boldest comedy on the podcasting frontier right now.”\r\nRolling Stone Magazine\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Greg Proops is The Smartest Man In The World","instanceDates":"26 July-26 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"469803ATJLPSRGJVVPLLQNQQSKCCPJPKQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-26T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-26T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-26T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-26T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"This intimate evening of storytelling and song thrillingly investigates the most deranged and dramatic person in Greta's life – herself.\r\nAfter blissfully living life lacking self-awareness, Greta's determined to change that. Between a childhood bully, drug-filled stints at boarding school, rich boyfriends and a dying mother, Greta leaves no stone unturned. Delightfully cringey, desperate and slightly disgusting, this intimate and juicy show is like spending a late-night gossiping with your best friend. Star of Search Party, Shrill, Together Together and more. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Greta Titelman: Exquisite Lies","instanceDates":"20 May-25 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"534603APQHLVMKTVLTJRHQQRJSBNLNNVT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-20T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-20T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-25T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-25T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A bright red storm in a broken tea cup, clasped in the crooked hands of the human condition, fighting for breath at the end of the world…\r\nBut don’t panic - we’re safe down here! This is sketch comedy, remember?\r\nGrubby Little Mitts are back with their third magnum opus. Amplifying the normal to chaotic extremes, their signature surrealist style is more affronting, confronting and stunting than ever, with rapid dialogue, musical interludes and an aggressively red aesthetic decomposing the genre like never before. From familial ties to unrequited love, through “Supporting Artists” and the Eurasian Eagle Owl, not even the civil service is safe…\r\nDon’t text him back. Don’t forget the milk. And don’t look up…\r\nWINNER: Amused Moose Comedy Award for Best Sketch Show 2022\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Grubby Little Mitts: Eyes Closed, Mouths Open","instanceDates":"22 May-24 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"612003AGQKQRHJHJJSPHMLMMGPJVSQRCH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-22T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-22T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-24T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-24T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Grubby Little Mitts, or “The White Stripes of comedy…” (Reviews Hub ★★★★) presents the sequel to their award winning debut! Traverse the perils of employment, friendship and love; be dazzled with ear splitting music; try not to be sick if you see too much flesh. At once slapstick, sitcom and surreal, the normal rules of engagement do not apply in this biting hour of sketch at breakneck speed. \r\n\r\n“Uproarious idiocy…” Guardian \r\n“Daring and manic hour…” Scotsman ★★★★\r\n\r\nWinners of the Amused Moose Comedy Award 2022 for Top Debut Sketch Show. \r\nFeaturing Rosie Nicholls & Sullivan Beau Brown (NewsRevue; Les Enfants Terribles; No Rolls Barred)\r\n\r\n“A delightfully extraordinary ‘must see’ show…” One 4 Review ★★★★½  \r\n“A finale that has to be seen to be believed…” Longstaff Reviews ★★★★\r\n“A stroke of brilliance…” Lost in Theatreland ★★★★\r\n\r\nPraise for previous work: \r\n”Material that just gets better and better... ” The List ★★★★\r\n“Two talented, immensely watchable performers…” Chortle ★★★★\r\n“Chemistry to burn…” The Wee Review ★★★★★\r\n“Ones to watch…” Voice Mag\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Grubby Little Mitts: Hello, Hi","instanceDates":"9 October-11 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"498003ARRBDQRBQLCLLVJHQTLHHDMTHNG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-09T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-09T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-11T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-11T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Hosted by Guardian columnist Zoe Williams, Led By Donkeys reveal the true stories behind the activism that has shaken and stirred UK politics since 2019\r\n\r\nWith their headline-grabbing guerrilla actions, the group has campaigned on everything from Brexit, to the Covid crisis, to the wars in Ukraine and Gaza – and they’re only just getting started.\r\n\r\nLed By Donkeys was founded in early 2019 when four friends, Ben Stewart, James Sadri, Oliver Knowles and Will Rose – motivated by the chaos Britain had been pitched into – started going out at night to paste guerrilla billboards of the leading Brexiters’ historic tweets. Soon after, the group was reaching millions of people and have continued their work mixing art and activism to create some of the most memorable images of our political age.\r\n\r\nBut what keeps the group going? And has their campaigning changed anything?\r\n\r\nJoin them live in London and online, as they reveal the true stories behind the activism that has shaken and stirred UK politics since 2019. And as we face a new political landscape, this is also your opportunity to ask them your own questions on what we can expect next from them.\r\n\r\nIn-person ticket holders will have the exclusive opportunity to purchase a signed copy of 'Led By Donkeys: Adventures in Art, Activism, and Accountability' onsite at the event. \r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Guardian Live Presents: Led By Donkeys, In Conversation With Zoe Williams ","instanceDates":"30 September-30 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"631603APQSJSRNPGQDGNKJDDJQDDVSSSP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-30T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-30T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-30T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-30T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Political","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Gutter is London's underground cult comedy night, born in the filth of The Pen Theatre and crawling into the light for the first time. \r\nHosted by a vicious bouffon troupe-'a little bit nasty' (Philippe Gaulier)-they emerge from a bin to run the show, drawing the audience in and spitting them out irreversibly changed.\r\nIf comedy is truth telling, bouffon is truth telling with teeth.\r\nA world of clowning, drag and alternative cabaret, with a line-up of stand-out and emerging performers. Natalie Palamides, Julia Masli, Red Bastard, Jordan Brookes, Rosa Garland and Luke Rollason are among over 60 acts who've given their debauchery to the bin.\r\nIn just over a year, Tom Greaves' (Fudgey: Best Reviewed Shows 2024) scrappy, sell-out night has been nominated for a Chortle Award for Best Alternative and Clowning, and produced Gutter Fest-the world's first bouffon festival-a chaotic 60-act celebration including the legendary 30-act opening night Gutter Royale. \r\nNow, for the first time, Gutter leaves its lair. Debuting at the London Clown Festival and Underbelly at this year’s Edinburgh Fringe. \r\nThe bin has arrived.\r\n18+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Gutter – A Bouffon Comedy Ritual","instanceDates":"5 June-29 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"713603ANHHMMLHGCMQCVSLQDNQNJPCJGN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-05T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-05T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-29T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-29T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Guy Montgomery (Taskmaster NZ, Guy Mont-Spelling Bee, born at Wellington Women's Hospital, 1988) hasn't been to the United Kingdom since 2019 but he is coming back to show everyone how funny he has become in the intervening years. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Guy Montgomery: Over 50,000,000 Guy Fans Can't Be Wrong","instanceDates":"15 August-17 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"558203ACNBJQMDTKKRKBTJDRTRMRQNTDL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-15T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-15T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-17T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-17T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"For the first time in its history, and for ONE NIGHT ONLY, the Guy Mont-Spelling Bee will come to life in London, England - one of the most British cities in the entire world. \r\nJoin us as a line-up of four all-star spellers will take their rightful place under the bright lights of the stage and maniacal glare of Guy Montgomery, as they attempt to be recognised as better at spelling than three of their peers! All in front of an audience of people who are almost definitely more intelligent than them.\r\nThere will be LAUGHTER, there will be SURPRISES, you will have a GOOD TIME...\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Guy Montgomery’s Guy Mont-Spelling Bee","instanceDates":"2 September-2 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"707603AKBHRNLDSCKPMPMNGHDBPMLRBPH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-02T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-02T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-02T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-02T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"We bring you three more very special line-up shows hosted and curated by the phenomenal Guz Khan\r\nGuz is one of the UK’s best comedy writers and performers. As well as his BAFTA-nominated work as creator and star of the BBC’s Man Like Mobeen, he has also appeared on shows such as Taskmaster, Would I Lie To You, A League Of Their Own and twice on stand-up institution Live At The Apollo. Guz also recently starred in hit Prime Video show Bait alongside Riz Ahmed.\r\n \r\nJoin this ‘formidable entertainer’ (Evening Standard) and some of his stand-up friends for an unmissable night of comedy at Soho Theatre Walthamstow.\r\n16+\r\n \r\n\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":125,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Guz Khan & Friends","instanceDates":"27 August-29 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"707203AVQLHSJSTDPNQNSVSTLQNVQCHLK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-27T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-27T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-29T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-29T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Three very special line-up shows hosted and curated by Guz Khan.\r\nGuz is one of the UK’s best comedy writers and performers. As well as his BAFTA-nominated work as creator and star of the BBC’s Man Like Mobeen, he has also appeared on shows such as Taskmaster, Would I Lie To You, A League Of Their Own and twice on stand-up institution Live At The Apollo.\r\n \r\nJoin this ‘formidable entertainer’ (Evening Standard) and some of his stand-up friends for an unmissable night of comedy at Soho Theatre Walthamstow.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":125,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Guz Khan & Friends Sep25","instanceDates":"19 September-21 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"645203ABSRLMKCQLMSLRMDDRVHBBTMMMC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-19T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-19T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-21T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-21T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"By popular demand, Guz Khan adds more opportunities for you to see him on his kick ass comedy tour! \r\n\r\nThis loveable, funny guy is known for bringing his big-screen persona and BAFTA-nominated hilarity to the stand-up stage. \r\n“As a stand-up Khan is very much a star. Make no mistake.” (Bruce Dessau The Evening Standard)\r\nGuz is the creator and star of BBC’s Man Like Mobeen, alongside his appearances on Taskmaster (C4), The Last Leg (C4), Live at the Apollo (BBC), Would I Lie To You (BBC), QI (BBC), Four Weddings and A Funeral (Hulu), & movies Army of Thieves and The Bubble (Netflix), How To Date Billy Walsh (Amazon) and much more.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Guz Khan: WIP","instanceDates":"14 December-28 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"515003AMMQTKDDMQLTTPMNLMBBHQMRVTH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-14T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-14T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-28T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-28T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"British-Iranian standup and singer brings her debut hour to Soho.\r\nHajar J. Woodland was raised in a strict Muslim household where birthdays weren’t celebrated and singing on stage was banned... and yet somehow she ended up a professional singer performing for footballers and finance bros at luxury events and private parties.\r\n\r\nFirst Love weaves songs, standup and state-school nostalgia into a moving show that explores what it means to find love and your voice.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Hajar J Woodland: First Love","instanceDates":"11 February-11 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"587803APHHCTMMNSGKHDBLLVQSPDHMHPH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-11T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-11T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-11T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-11T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Prepare to Fail is an idea award-nominated writer/performer Haley McGee has been carrying around for over a decade but been too scared to tackle… till now. \r\nFringe First-winning, Olivier-nominated writer/performer of Age is a Feeling, Haley McGee is trying out some very new material for her new solo show. Prepare to Fail is an idea Haley has been carrying around for over a decade but been too scared to tackle... till now. \r\n‘What happens when we make meaning of our tragedies in all the wrong ways?’ That’s what Haley’s trying to figure out in this show about camping, monsters, teenage girls and the perils of preparation.\r\nIf you’d like to see a very early iteration of Haley’s newest project, as she figures it out, she would LOVE to have you there. \r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Haley McGee: Prepare to Fail (Work in Progress)","instanceDates":"18 March-23 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"530003AMBJGJCMKLKBRNLVRKCPVVJDJQN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-18T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-18T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-23T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-23T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A kinky eco-hijacking of Shakespeare’s Hamlet about meat, madness, and the power of shame. \r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"HAM","instanceDates":"29 September-31 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"734603AVBQKCVKGVLLQKPKPCGPQVLHNSR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-29T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-29T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-31T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-31T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Performance Art","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"A grief-stricken vegan seeks revenge for the death of a pig… by putting on a play.   \r\n\r\nFirst, he thinks for a long time. Second, he blames his mother. Finally, he wreaks the ultimate vengeance… by putting on a play. \r\n\r\nThe “Fringe sensation” (The Stage) Hotter Project twists this high-brow tragedy into a sordid wrestle between a vegan and a sausage-lover. As we hurtle towards the end of humankind, every one of us must decide: to eat, or not to eat? Is that the question? \r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"HAM (Jul 2026)","instanceDates":"28 July-28 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"727203AVJJDTNPRTBSBHGQMHLTMSLMRKC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-28T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-28T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-28T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-28T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Work In Progress","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Lolly Bag is a one woman show, “...a mix of delicious creations” (Kaleidoscope Arts) and Hannah has prepared this chef’s menu of character comedy, designed to delight and inspire, for her upcoming debut London season at the prestigious Soho Theatre. \r\nMelbourne born and based but cosmopolitan at heart, Hannah is coming to the UK to give you a taste of her funny little bag o’ sketch comedy sweets. \r\nTake a chance on this lucky dip - rigged so that everyone’s a winner. ‘Deserves her own TV show immediately’ ★★★★ (The Age). ‘Camilleri really has perfected... characters’ ★★★★ 1/2 (Hi Fi Way, Adelaide Fringe). ‘Magnificently assured one-woman sketch show’ ★★★★ (Chortle).\r\n\r\n12+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Hannah Camilleri: Lolly Bag","instanceDates":"29 August-2 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"489403AMDRKVQNHJLBDRHNMNTJKCQNRKM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-29T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-29T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-02T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-02T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Hannah East’s new comedy show hilariously captures the madness of parenting. With millions of views online, her sketches are brutally honest, wildly relatable, and laugh-out-loud funny.\r\nFrom pregnancy and labour to breastfeeding, postpartum struggles, and everyday parenting challenges, her sketches hit home with honesty and humour. Audiences love her for saying what mums are really thinking—but rarely say out loud.  \r\n\r\nWith her warm-hearted tone, relatable mum impressions, and fearless wit, Express Yourself is a must-watch. Expect brand-new skits, more wigs, celebrity send-ups, and laugh-out-loud moments every parent will relate to. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":100,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Hannah East: Express Yourself","instanceDates":"9 October-9 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"657203AMTDQPNCBRQMDNQLBNJNCHVMCRR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-09T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-09T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-09T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-09T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Hannah Gadsby is hosting a comedy lineup with some cool queer people. Hannah thinks they're pretty great and very funny, and we suspect you will, too.\r\nWell, actually some of them they know quite well. But some of them are new, and Hannah thinks they're pretty great and very funny, and we suspect you will, too.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":80,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Hannah Gadsby And Close Personal Acquaintances They've Never Met...Except Maybe One Or Two","instanceDates":"11 October-12 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"499203ABJCCHLJVVDQPBCBHPKSBMLNHPJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-11T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-11T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-12T21:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-12T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Named ‘voice of a generation’ (The Skinny) with ‘humour sharp enough to draw blood’ (The Guardian), Hannah Platt is ‘an undeniable rising star’ (Fest Mag) of the UK comedy scene. \r\nIn this multi-award-nominated debut, Hannah unravels her frank and acerbic world view - and after a diagnosis of body dysmorphia, how the world looks back at her.\r\nTour support for Fern Brady, Kiri Pritchard-McClean and Ashley Gavin.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Hannah Platt: Defence Mechanism","instanceDates":"20 March-22 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"593203AVNKSPRJLJBRMTRJGHLPNDHSCJB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-20T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-20T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-22T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-22T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Harriet Dyer (as seen on Last One Laughing, Live at The Apollo and Cats Does Countdown) is a very daft lady. 16+ (References to mental health issues, death and drug use. Check webpage for current content advice).\r\nThe latest in jaunty endeavours sees her finding good in the world, pianos made from teeth, trying to be more than deaf and mental and fish wearing the faces of people that have just had face transplants. ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Harriet Dyer: Easily Distra…","instanceDates":"15 October-17 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"750203ASCJPBKSVNLVLSNCBVCQNVSHCNJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-15T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-15T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-17T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-17T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Harriet Dyer (as seen on The Russell Howard Hour) is an award winning comedian, mental health advocate and an experience to behold. Here doth lie (fresh from critical acclaim of Edinburgh Fringe 2022) quite the harrowing tale, one you won’t forget in a hurry. Far funnier than it should be. “half mania, half Victoria Wood. Her sprawling stand-up is endearing and complex. Hilarious… She has quietly reinvented the confessional stand-up.” ***** Neurodiverse Review “Delightful…wonderful…a performance of understated excellence. A fabulous hour…with a sense of the joyful absurdity of life. Entirely charming.” ***** One4Review “Much of Trigger Warning is heartbreaking and sobering…her astute humour elevating it to anecdotal art that humanises the horror and is all the more affecting for it.” **** Chortle Winner of the Neurodiversity Representation Award\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Harriet Dyer: Trigger Warning","instanceDates":"11 April-11 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"432203ADJKBQPLVKCSJMRQGHLNKPNTDHB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-11T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-11T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-11T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-11T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Ridiculous things always happen to Harriet, but this year it’s out of control. She’s got to rebuild her whole life but she cannot work out which way the building blocks go.\r\nThe multi award-winning Harriet Kemsley is back with a new show about break-ups, sloths and trying to think positively while everything descends into absolute chaos.\r\n\r\nAs seen on Live at the Apollo, 8 Out of 10 Cats Does Countdown, Hypothetical and Roast Battle.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Harriet Kemsley: Everything Always Works Out For Me","instanceDates":"25 November-27 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"574403APHBHVJSMPJJLRPLLRQKRPKMBNM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-25T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-25T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-27T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-27T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A creep can be a person. It can also be a slow, almost inevitable movement towards something you definitely shouldn't want.\r\nFollowing a sold-out, critically acclaimed, and award-nominated Edinburgh Fringe run, Harriet Richardson makes her Soho debut with a darkly funny show about obsession, shame, and the fatal magnetism of the man from the TV.  16+ RESTRICTION (Audience participation, strong language, sexual content and imagery of full-frontal nudity - see webpage for current advice).","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Harriet Richardson: Creep","instanceDates":"27 November-9 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"744803AGRDJRRBHVKVPPSRBBQVJGBBLRB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-27T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-27T21:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-01-09T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-01-09T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Join us for a rare and entertaining evening with legendary satirical comedian and self-styled “stupid idiot\", Harry Enfield.\r\nFrom the meteoric rise of Loadsamoney, a Thatcherite Visionary, to the fury of Kevin the Teenager, Harry will reflect on 40 years of arsing about in comedy and bring some of his favourite characters vividly back to life on stage.  \r\nThen it’s over to your questions: your chance to ask how it all works for him, what he’s most proud of, and what he says to the many who ask, “You wouldn’t be allowed to do your stuff today, would you?”  \r\nDon’t miss an unforgettable evening with a brilliantly silly and strikingly insightful comedian.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Harry Enfield and No Chums!","instanceDates":"17 October-10 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"669803APDCJNQVSHMTKLNDLRRLBGDBKMQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-17T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-17T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-03-10T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-03-10T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Sketch","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Last chance to see! \r\nThe Badger Parade is back on for one night only! With full 20 foot Sausage Finale!\r\n \r\nHarry says:\r\n \r\n'Join me as I commit 60 Glorious Years of fun, laughter and low level disruption to tape - filmed live at Soho Theatre Walthamstow!\r\n \r\nMarvel! As I offer new insights into the hot topics of the day such as the demise of the SCART lead, The Culture Wars and shin out onto an ingoing board whilst being attacked by a heron! \r\n \r\nGuffaw with delight! As I delve into my back catalogue using my patented Wheel Of Jokes!\r\n \r\nCough Awkwardly! As Gary, (my son from my first marriage) attempts to take over the business again.\r\n \r\nWatch in Wonder! at the return of The Badger Parade with guest appearances from The Knitted Character and Abu Hamster \r\n \r\nPlus one lucky audience member will get to join me in a double act! It could be you!'\r\n \r\nGET ON BOARD THE LAUGHTER TRAIN!\r\n9+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Harry Hill: New Bits & Greatest Hits (TV Special Recording)","instanceDates":"1 February-1 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"676203ADLMGNPVTMGSPRMKSTQBQHGQPVS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-01T16:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-01T16:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-01T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-01T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Arab. Muslim. Brummy. Hasan Al-Habib was born to Iraqis that moved to Birmingham after deciding Baghdad wasn’t dangerous enough.\r\nThe Birmingham Comedy Festival Breaking Talent Award 2023 Winner’s show is about his love for both cities - despite being hated by the US Government / Leicester.\r\n\r\nAn exploration of racism, sectarianism, and a high metabolism, this is the show that Tommy Robinson, Saddam Hussein, and Joe Wicks DON’T WANT you to see. You’re not gonna listen to them, are ya, bab?!\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Hasan Al Habib Death to the West (Midlands).","instanceDates":"12 February-12 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"588003AVCPLVQHBBRRRTVRTQRMMTNJJSS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-12T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-12T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-12T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-12T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Arab. Muslim. Brummy. \r\nBut when Britain invaded Iraq, friends and teachers saw him as the enemy within.  \r\nThis story involves Big Tescos, why Saddam Hussein would have loved Drayton Manor, and - amidst a search for those pesky weapons of mass destruction - finding self-acceptance. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Hasan Al-Habib: Death to the West (Midlands)","instanceDates":"8 April-9 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"695803AJLQJQLSVBKKJQJRKQSGMGVCNHC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-08T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-08T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-09T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-09T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Arab. Muslim. Brummy. \r\nBut when Britain invaded Iraq, friends and teachers saw him as the enemy within.  \r\nThis story involves Big Tescos, why Saddam Hussein would have loved Drayton Manor, and - amidst a search for those pesky weapons of mass destruction - finding self-acceptance. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Hasan Al-Habib: Death to the West (Midlands).","instanceDates":"10 November-15 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"654803ALDVRNCPLPBDPJCRNLPNDKGRDVN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-10T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-10T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-15T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-15T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Following an extended, sold-out 2026 Edinburgh Fringe run, Brummy Iraqi comedian Hasan Al-Habib returns to Soho Theatre with his most relatable stand-up show yet for white British audiences: being a child of divorce. \r\n\r\nFrom cancer to cutting off family, and a lifelong fear of injections, the star of BBC Two’s Pilgrimage promises nothing but laughs. 16+ (References to domestic violence, check webpage for current content advice).\r\n\r\nAlso one half of the repeatedly sold-out Fringe double act 2 Muslim 2 Furious. ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Hasan Al-Habib: Stuck in the Middle (East) With You ","instanceDates":"21 October-24 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"750403ATSPLLDSHLNDCVLQKJBDPLJSLNQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-21T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-21T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-24T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-24T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"After her breakthrough stand-up routine on Australia's Got Talent went viral around the world, Chinese native and self- proclaimed 'Tiger Daughter' is making her much anticipated London debut.\r\nHe Huang has packed her bags and is ready to take you on an hilarious journey around the world. Whether she’s 'backpacking' in Thailand, eating fried bushrats in Africa or trying to not get arrested in North Korea, her adventures will have you laughing out loud.\r\nDrawn from He’s experiences as unmarried 'leftover lady' Chinese woman, living as a non-native English speaker coping with linguistic and cultural differences, family drama, and sexual liberation, this show is raw, honest and hilarious.\r\nForget your travel guidebook because if you want to survive in this world -  the only guide you need is…Tiger Daughter.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"He Huang: Tiger Daughter vs The World","instanceDates":"15 August-17 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"561403ACQSQHPJKBCDGVKRPBKSCQHCQDB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-15T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-15T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-17T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-17T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Description / copy\r\n\tKing Herod, famed for his Massacre of the Innocents, now leads a self-development pyramid scheme. Audiences transform from ancient soldiers into modern clients in an interactive, drag-clown, group therapy session. Through improvised songs, political parodies, breathing exercises and cult-like rituals, Herod asks one thing: forgive...yourself. Within the show's chaotic absurdity lurks male accountability, self-reckoning and facing trauma. Who is Herod's process really for? \r\nHealing King Herod is a recipient of Phoebe Waller-Bridge’s Keep it Fringe fund. Come to our only full-length official London preview before Herod heads to Edinburgh. \r\nCreated by Comedy Central-endorsed clown Riss Obolensky and director Eloïse Poulton. \r\nA VAULT Festival sell-out show, nominated for Show of the Week.\r\n'Funny, memorable, bold’ ★★★★.5 The Reviews Hub\r\n‘Side-splitting laughs’ ★★★★★ BroadwayBaby.com \r\n‘Raging lesbian’ ★★★★★ DIVA Magazine\r\n‘Brilliantly weird’ ★★★★ Fringe Biscuit\r\n'Weird, fun, undefinable' No Proscenium\r\n‘The weirdest and best thing I’ve ever seen’ Lost Cabaret Bristol\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Healing King Herod.","instanceDates":"17 June-17 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"476805ALVHGLGPQDKNTQQBKMLKRBTJDBK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-17T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-17T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-17T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-17T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Two Angels land in no-where, yet-somewhere, yet-everywhere.\r\nThis surreal-dadasist-clown-sound duo is waiting-for? The miraculous tension and slack and lack so full. We share the shore of our delight and plight. A quasi-ritual experience to deliver the un-deliverable. A dreamscape encounter.\r\nWaiting in the archetypal nothingness, two winged beings of majesty and misfortune play with the music of time. Linger at this threshold with us in a tribute to all who know little of much, a tribute to the in-between. Gather here and sing this song with us. A tune we know well and continuously forget. Our divine damnation dimly delights the downward dawning deafness. Come hither. Come thither.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Hear We Ahh: ANGELS","instanceDates":"3 June-3 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"714003AQLDCDLMQLGLNVDKPMQPRCJVQCM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-03T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-03T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-03T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-03T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"This one's for the young hearts, the old hearts, and the broken hearts.\r\nStory, science and a synth combine in an exhilarating performance that examines what happens in our bodies when we’re bereft. From acclaimed New Zealand company EBKM (Yes Yes Yes), Heartbreak Hotel tracks a woman’s broken heart in a wrenching and relatable journey that's studded with classic break-up songs and razor-sharp observations on the physiology of love.\r\nDevelopment credits: Development of Heartbreak Hotel was supported by Creative New Zealand, Hawkes Bay Arts Festival & The Hannah Playhouse Trust.\r\nWinner Actor of the Year (Karin McCracken) at the Wellington Theatre Awards 2024\r\nWinner Sound Design of the Year (Te Aihe Butler) at the Wellington Theatre Awards 2024\r\n12+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Heartbreak Hotel","instanceDates":"19 August-23 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"635603ANNJTQJVHBRPLLCTRVKPLNCDBCN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-19T18:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-19T17:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-23T18:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-23T17:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Fresh off a sold-out North American tour, Rob Anderson is bringing his comedy show to Europe! Taking on the role of a young scientist, Rob tries to get a better understanding of the homosexual species in different cities by pulling data from the audience. Rob also shares his own personal stories that he's kept far away from the internet. It comes highly recommended for anyone who's witnessed gay sex, or is doing serious research on the subject.\r\n\r\nRob Anderson is a comedian best known for his Gay Science series, where he answers serious LGBTQ+ questions like \"Why can't gays sit in a chair properly?\" or \"Why don't lesbians have electricity in their movies?\" He also wrote The Fergamerican National Anthem, a best-selling picture book based on Fergie's infamous National Anthem performance. He was in Book of Queer (Discovery+) and was recently named one of OUT Magazine's 100 most influential LGBTQ+ people of 2022.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":65,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Heartthrob Live with Rob Anderson","instanceDates":"15 May-20 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"435003AVHLNKSNJJBKTVGTKQKLKQSKKJH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-15T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-15T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-20T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-20T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Observational comedy about growing up as a black nerd in the 90s, coming to London to come out and embracing her inner 'Carlton'\r\nHeleana was a weirdo, according to the small town that she was raised in. A huge fan of the Fresh Prince of Bel Air in the 90s she wished she were more like Will, but was too nerdy. She finds out that despite her modest background living with her proud, fiercely independent and resourceful single mother, they both have a bit more in common with those TV characters that she might have thought possible, and that sometimes it's the crappy things in life that are the most motivating...16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Heleana Blackwell: Attack of the 5ft Woman","instanceDates":"22 February-22 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"590803AVVJVVSHJJRNSKCDHGMLGBNMDJH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-22T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-22T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-22T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-22T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Helen is back and is struggling.\r\nShe has spent the last year being forced to hang out with someone she doesn’t like and who honestly does not like her. It’s tense, it’s uncomfortable, they won’t leave. \r\nA brand new show from award-winning comedian Helen Bauer. Star of Live at the Apollo (BBC2), 8 Out Of 10 Cats (C4),  Am I Being Unreasonable (BBC One) and Extraordinary (Disney+). She also co-hosts the extremely popular and award-winning podcast Trusty Hogs. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Helen Bauer: Bless Her","instanceDates":"17 December-20 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"675203ALBMMHPNJRCKCSKBSLQHJNKSHDL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-17T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-17T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-20T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-20T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Helen is back and is struggling.\r\nShe has spent the last year being forced to hang out with someone she doesn’t like and who honestly does not like her. It’s tense, it’s uncomfortable, they won’t leave. \r\nA brand new show from award-winning comedian Helen Bauer. Star of Live at the Apollo (BBC2), 8 Out Of 10 Cats (C4),  Am I Being Unreasonable (BBC One) and Extraordinary (Disney+). She also co-hosts the extremely popular and award-winning podcast Trusty Hogs. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Helen Bauer: Bless Her.","instanceDates":"20 October-25 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"621404AQSBBRNJLNTDBMMVTGTSHQHDJBR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-20T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-20T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-25T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-25T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Star of Live at the Apollo, Late Night Mash and Edinburgh Comedy Award Best Newcomer nominee, brings a show all about the women in her life, from her mother to her best friend and that one girl who was mean in 2008. Oh, and Disney Princesses, obvs. Co-host of the smash-hit podcast Trusty Hogs and seen on BBC3, Comedy Central, Dave, ITV and more. 'Sticking out for all the right reasons’ **** (Scotsman). ‘Utterly brilliant’ **** (List).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Helen Bauer: Grand Supreme Darling Princess","instanceDates":"25 September-30 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"474803AHPJJTVHRTSGLTQBGCVPCTGSSRS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-25T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-25T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-30T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-30T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Henry queen of Squats is \"like having a scandalous gossip with a good friend... Peppered with pop culture references from rom-coms to Broadway and reality TV, a real and infectious love of performance runs through the show\" - The Reviews Hub\r\nMoss unpacks flashbacks from his days as a young ballet dancer to now planning his wedding and asks is this enough of an emotional throughline? A high camp jukebox stand-up hour.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Henry Moss: Henry Queen of Squats","instanceDates":"8 February-8 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"521204AKCHJVLHNTGTDJPGDSMLRTSSJTQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-08T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-08T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-08T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-08T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"You’ve looked behind a Wizard’s Curtain. You’ve visited a sausage factory. Do you dare to gaze inside a cartoonist’s pencil case?\r\nNew comedy show from Henry Paker, featuring live illustration. Leave your preconceptions about comedy/illustration at the door and expect to find them in an absolute state on the way out. As heard on Three Bean Salad podcast. As seen on The Last Leg and Russell Howard’s Good News. Cartoons as seen in Joe Wilkinson: My Autobiography and Kay’s Anatomy.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Henry Paker: Pencil Case","instanceDates":"29 October-30 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"709603ADQRMDMNMCQJDBNLDMTGTMHHMQD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-29T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-29T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-30T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-30T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"HEXENHAMMER is loosely based on The Hammer of Witches, the 15th century guide to witch hunting. Written by two Dominican monks, it kick-started the European witch craze and was partly responsible for the murder of tens of thousands of women over the next few hundred years.\r\nHeinrich Kramer is the Jordan B Peterson of mediaeval Bavaria, the Andrew Tate of the Catholic Church.\r\nJacob Sprenger is a weird little guy with sweaty hands.\r\nAll Heinrich wants is an orderly cosmos, a sizable following and a lucrative book deal. \r\nJacob just wants a friend. \r\nJoin them on their rabid quest to save the world, one witch trial at a time. \r\nHEXENHAMMER is a physical comedy loosely based on The Hammer of Witches, the 15th century guide to witch hunting. Written by two Dominican monks, it kick-started the European witch craze and as partly responsible for the murder of tens of thousands of women over the next few hundred years.\r\nIncorporating text taken directly from Die Hexenhammer and verbatim text found on online incel forums, HEXENHAMMER explores how men end up killing women as a way to solve their own problems, why that hasn’t changed in the past 500 years.\r\nHEXENHAMMER is directed by Complicité Associate Catherine Alexander was shortlisted for the Untapped Award 2022. Secretariat presents HEXENHAMMER ⭐⭐⭐⭐ “Like a sinister Monty Python sketch” - FringeBiscuit ⭐⭐⭐⭐”A brilliant show” - Everything Theatre “Hilarious yet extremely poignant” - The Play’s The Thing “HEXENHAMMER is a witty wild ride on the misogyny train” -Gabriel Gatehouse, creator of the BBC podcast “The Coming Storm”\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Hexenhammer by Sidsel Rostrup and Suzy Kohane","instanceDates":"7 February-7 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"521404APTHRTHBLPPVTMHHSRNJHQNQJQG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-07T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-07T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-07T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-07T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"NB – Directed by Daniel Bailey\r\nStarring Josh Radnor and Noah Galvin\r\n12+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Hit Machine by Jonathan Caren","instanceDates":"8 July-15 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"705203ACHBSTBVKQMJVHPKKGGJRKDLNNC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-08T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-08T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-15T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-15T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Hive Mind is a chaotic late night gameshow in which contestants have to crowdsource their way to victory.\r\nCome watch Kiri Pritchard-McLean and Tarot go all shiny floor and sequins as they try and crowdsource their way to a format. Expect special guest contestants every night! Previous guests include: Jack Rooke, Katy Wix, Sarah Keyworth and Chloe Petts. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Hive Mind with Kiri Pritchard-McLean and Tarot","instanceDates":"26 March-29 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"529403AKRTMMDGSCVGVPCHRSKMQBBBDBB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-26T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-26T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-29T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-29T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Plug up thy hole! A religious sect in Nebraska wears butt plugs at all times because they believe a wrathful God shall suck the unplugged up, ass-first, to burn on the face of the sun. The crazy thing is… they're right.\r\n\r\nHOLE! is an epic love story set in the apocalyptic aftermath of The Great Sucking, when the only people left on Earth are the fanatical Nebraskans - and anyone else who happened to be doing butt stuff at the time.\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":80,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"HOLE!","instanceDates":"17 July-1 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"721803AQDJSRDQQGBCPGJCGPPMVSJBSKT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-17T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-17T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-01T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-01T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Big Little Sister is a darkly funny and emotionally sharp solo play about growing up in someone else’s shadow- when that someone is your sibling with disabilities. The show cuts through the clichés of “inspirational” disability-adjacent sibling narratives. Through surrealist storytelling, monologue, and multimedia- including dialogue voiced by her brother’s communication aid. Inspired by the term “glass children,” used to describe the ‘invisible’ siblings who grow up in the background of siblings with additional needs, Big Little Sister asks: what happens when the glass finally cracks? Born from Holly’s lived experience, the show challenges the people and systems who benefit from sanitising or silencing the real stories around disability and care. It is a tribute- to growing up alongside someone profoundly different, and to the defiant joy stitched through the seams of grief, guilt, and fierce love.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Holly Gifford: Big Little Sister","instanceDates":"5 February-5 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"684403AGTMCMKRPSSRTLGGVDLHBTRJRPV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-05T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-05T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-05T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-05T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"\r\nJoin ‘riveting’ (★★★★ Chortle) comedian Holly Spillar in her muff-busting comedy on sex, pain and the brain. \r\n\r\nAfter a diagnosis of vaginismus (a condition preventing penetrative sex) Hole showcases the determination of one woman to achieve the basic, beige sex life of her dreams, with only a little red loop pedal for company. Once described as 'Tim Minchin bumping into Kate Bush at full speed' this tightly packed one-woman show is full of unexpected advice from doctors, Joe Rogan-obsessed boyfriends and a whole lot of holes.\r\n\r\nBritish Comedy Guide Best Reviewed Shows at the Edinburgh Fringe.\r\n\r\nProducers: Brightmouth Productions\r\nDramaturg: Ben Francombe\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Holly Spillar: HOLE","instanceDates":"2 April-3 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"504603AHPTGBSNCSCJSNTJPQJKPQNKRSL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-02T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-02T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-03T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-03T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"No one does sketch comedy like these two freaks.\r\nFresh from their award-winning sold-out shows, Hot Department make their London debut with an all-new full hour of high-energy, cinematic, unhinged sketch comedy.\r\n\r\nAs seen on Just For Laughs, ABC Comedy and opening for the likes of Patti Harison and Aunty Donna, this Australian sketch duo are the rising MILFs of international comedy. Bring a towel. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Hot Department","instanceDates":"29 August-31 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"564203ALDBTHHHTSHKLGVSNSHHCDBKGJB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-29T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-29T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-31T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-31T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Sketch","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Swords clash against armour in an endless war… An arrow pierces a mage’s skull and a secret is lost… One ancient spell conjures forth a dark power that should have been left to rot… These heroes don’t care about any of that shit. They’re just out here trying to get laid. HOT SINGLES IN YOUR AREA PLAY D&D is a comedy Dungeons & Dragons* show following a party of adventurers who are much more interested in the quest’s romanceable options than stopping the goblin insurrection or saving the elf king’s mum or whatever. Watch these horny heroes vie for love n’ kisses from the knights, demons, and villagers of this fantasy land. \r\nPlease note: the Dungeon Master will require help from the audience inventing these characters. 18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Hot Singles In Your Area Play D&D","instanceDates":"20 November-20 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"761203ACBTLSMDNMJJHDGDSBHSJRNHKBC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-20T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-20T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-20T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-20T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Swords clash against armour in an endless war… \r\n\r\nAn arrow pierces a mage’s skull and a secret is lost…\r\n\r\nOne ancient spell conjures forth a dark power that should have been left to rot…\r\nThese heroes don’t care about any of that shit. They’re just out here trying to get laid. \r\n\r\nHOT SINGLES IN YOUR AREA PLAY D&D is a comedy Dungeons & Dragons* show following a party of adventurers who are much more interested in the quest’s romanceable options than stopping the goblin insurrection or saving the elf king’s mum or whatever. Watch these horny heroes vie for love n’ kisses from the knights, demons, and villagers of this fantasy land. Please note: the Dungeon Master will require help from the audience inventing these characters. \r\n\r\nHoSIYAP D&D comes from the queers behind LESBIAN SPACE CRIME (“raucously funny”, London Pub Theatres), PANSEXUAL PREGNANT PIRACY (“fantastically ridiculous”, The Reviews Hub) and upcoming comedy at Soho Theatre, COUNT DYKULA. \r\n\r\n*(No knowledge of Dungeons & Dragons? No problem! And also, what was it like being popular at school?)\r\n18+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Hot Singles In Your Area Play D&D 2024","instanceDates":"25 January-25 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"584203ANRQLCNTQPCVQTSKQVHNBGQLLVB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-25T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-25T22:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-25T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-25T22:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Swords clash against armour in an endless war…\r\nAn arrow pierces a mage’s skull and a secret is lost…\r\nOne ancient spell conjures forth a dark power that should have been left to rot…\r\n\r\nThese heroes don’t care about any of that shit. They’re just out here trying to get laid.\r\n\r\nHOT SINGLES IN YOUR AREA PLAY D&D is a comedy Dungeons & Dragons* show following a party of adventurers who are much more interested in the quest’s romanceable options than stopping the goblin insurrection or saving the elf king’s mum or whatever. Watch these horny heroes vie for love n’ kisses from the knights, demons, and villagers of this fantasy land.\r\n\r\nPlease note: the Dungeon Master will require help from the audience inventing these characters.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Hot Singles In Your Area Play D&D 2025","instanceDates":"16 May-17 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"621203APNLBCMNJQBVDKMTPMJKKKKLNMD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-16T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-16T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-17T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-17T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Swords clash against armour in an endless war…\r\nAn arrow pierces a mage’s skull and a secret is lost…\r\nOne ancient spell conjures forth a dark power that should have been left to rot…\r\n\r\nThese heroes don’t care about any of that shit. They’re just out here trying to get laid.\r\n\r\nHOT SINGLES IN YOUR AREA PLAY D&D is a comedy Dungeons & Dragons* show following a party of adventurers who are much more interested in the quest’s romanceable options than stopping the goblin insurrection or saving the elf king’s mum or whatever. Watch these horny heroes vie for love n’ kisses from the knights, demons, and villagers of this fantasy land.\r\n\r\nPlease note: the Dungeon Master will require help from the audience inventing these characters.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Hot Singles In Your Area Play D&D 2025","instanceDates":"3 November-3 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"667003AJPGJCDLKVVNKLJKGQCVVRLNTBD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-03T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-03T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-03T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-03T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Swords clash against armour in an endless war…\r\nAn arrow pierces a mage’s skull and a secret is lost…\r\nOne ancient spell conjures forth a dark power that should have been left to rot…\r\n\r\nThese heroes don’t care about any of that shit. They’re just out here trying to get laid.\r\n\r\nHOT SINGLES IN YOUR AREA PLAY D&D is a comedy Dungeons & Dragons* show following a party of adventurers who are much more interested in the quest’s romanceable options than stopping the goblin insurrection or saving the elf king’s mum or whatever. Watch these horny heroes vie for love n’ kisses from the knights, demons, and villagers of this fantasy land.\r\n\r\nPlease note: the Dungeon Master will require help from the audience inventing these characters. *No knowledge of Dungeons & Dragons? No problem! And also, what was it like being popular at school? \r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Hot Singles In Your Area Play D&D Mar26","instanceDates":"23 March-6 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"699803AGHKRRDHGHKJJCCGPLRSQPKDMHK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-23T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-23T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-06T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-06T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"WELCOME ALL TO THE HOUSE OF LIFE!\r\nWould you like to feel a sense of euphoric togetherness? \r\n \r\nAre you ready to be 100% never sad again? \r\nWe have the answer. \r\n \r\nHouse of Life is a place of worship with one goal: happiness for all, at any cost. \r\nOne part sermon, one part rebirth, three parts party, this is a space to let it all out. \r\n \r\nLed by the glitter-clad RaveRend, House of Life provides a scientifically proven* sense of total togetherness and eleva-tion at a time when people feel more disconnected than ev-er. \r\n \r\nHeal through music, joy and noise, in an eight-step musical programme that was hailed as “BIGGEST FEEL-GOOD SENSA-TION\" (The Telegraph) \r\n  \r\nJoin the RaveRend on his mission to get you HAPPY. \r\n \r\nJoin the RAVEolution. \r\n10+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"HOUSE OF LIFE","instanceDates":"27 May-31 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"617803AQGJSMRHHDHTHTKPMRBLJHPGQGR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-27T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-27T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-31T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-31T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"One-part sermon, one-part purge, three-parts party. House of Life is a travelling musical cult collective hosted by the RaveRend, with one mission: to get you happy, at any cost. A space to celebrate. To elevate. To lay out your shit and wash it away. The chance to achieve absolute euphoric togetherness through the relentless powers of music and vibes. Made up of alumni of the BAFTA-winning Television Workshop, Sheep Soup are back following five-star smash hits Mrs Green and The Invention Of Acting. ***** (Metro). ***** (EdFringeReview.com). ***** (BroadwayBaby.com).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"House of Life Jun24","instanceDates":"18 June-6 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"513603AVMQDPLDHQKLGDDMQPDMHNCTLJG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-18T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-18T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-06T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-06T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Have you been naughty or nice this year…? Well we’re about to find out AREN’T we.\r\nHave you been naughty or nice this year…? Well we’re about to find out AREN’T we.\r\nGuildfordian Steve Porters (Lock Up Ur Daughters) has been on a big journey with the ladies. He’s been listenin. Learnin. Lovin. \r\nTo the committed couples… \r\nit’s never too late to spice it up. Hoiii! \r\nAnd to my Single Pringles… \r\nDON’T PANIC. STEVE’S GOT U.\r\nHis tree may be fake. But Steve’s connection to u lot won’t be. Wheyy.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"HOW TO FLIRT: The TED XXX-mas EDITION","instanceDates":"14 December-16 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"502203ANVLDHHSRHRSRVMBDVMPHSCPTJQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-14T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-14T22:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-16T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-16T22:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Drag","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Last year Steve aced feminism. The result? A girlfriend. Now he's venturing beyond second base and sayin’ yes to luv!\r\nJoin the Guildfordian iPod-DJ for a spicy seminar where you mite just find ur special someone. \r\nNote: Only appropriate for anyone who isn’t afraid of feelings.\r\n\r\n\r\nWritten and performed by Daisy Doris May\r\nDirected by Mpilo May\r\nProduced by Lucy Benson Brown with HÄUS OF DONS\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"HOW TO MATE: The SECOND TED XXX Talk","instanceDates":"23 October-26 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"573203AVNSPKBKSJSLPLBNRVVKNQJLQCS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-23T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-23T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-26T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-26T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"For nearly 20 years, Rev Derek Gritt has brought a little bit of holy into Britain's homes with his TV show At Your Service - now only available online (which is FINE!). Mega-fan Jane Plemley's last wish was to have her funeral delivered by the Reverend, so this week he's heading to the quaint village of Godsby-Upon-Treen. As usual, he'll lead the service, chat church and answer your burning questions. Except the ones about Jane. She's NOT a witch.\r\nFrom the creator of cult Fringe hit Hot Rubber.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Hudson Hughes: At Your Service","instanceDates":"19 November-21 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"753003AHRTRBLLKDVTSJDCTLMLDJQQMLL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-19T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-19T22:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-21T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-21T22:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Huge will be performing a series of songs, but not songs he’s written – these are songs passed down from his family members and ancestors (dead).\r\nFrom his Grandpa Joe finally winning a ticket to the chocolate factory to his brother Elliot finding a stray alien in the garden shed, there’s something for everyone. \r\nThe show will feature Huge’s well known and loved personalised wearable keyboard, intricate deadpan style of humour and crowd participation all in an attempt to finally honour his incredible ancestors which include Batman, Ash Ketchum, Joey, Monica, Phoebe, Rachel, Chandler and Ross.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Huge Davies: Album For My Ancestors (Dead)","instanceDates":"13 February-15 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"576403ACMMBBJBSQDDHRVBLDHCBDVLRRP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-13T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-13T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-15T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-15T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Wearable keyboard? Check! Deadpan delivery? Check! Jokes about murder? \r\n \r\nWhodunnit promises to be a thrilling ride as Huge (Roast Battle, Cats Does Countdown) takes on the classic role of determined detective using all his wits to solve the murder mystery at hand. With his quick wit, dark humour and surreal material, Huge will guide audiences through the show as they encounter a maze of clues and red herrings and try to uncover the identity of a killer.\r\n \r\nCreator, writer and star of Channel 4 sitcom The Artists, Huge, known for his deadpan delivery whilst wearing a full-sized customised keyboard strapped to himself, has quickly risen to become one of the most unique and captivating acts in the UK. His previous show The Carpark was nominated for Best Newcomer at the Edinburgh Fringe, had three sold-out runs at Soho Theatre and was featured in Time Out as the Number 1 Comedy Show to See. \r\n\r\n‘Heaving, dry wretched of laughter…Huge Davies [knocks] this wonder of stand-up narrative trickery out of the park!’\r\n★★★★1/2 ToDoList\r\n\r\n‘It’s a dark treat…had me shaking with laughter.’\r\n★★★★ Telegraph\r\n \r\n‘Huge Davies is possibly the most miserable man you'll see at this year's Fringe, and you'll have a bloody brilliant time.’\r\n★★★★ Fest\r\n\r\n‘Huge Davies is becoming a master of the craft’\r\n★★★★ List\r\n \r\n‘His comedy crackles with energy.’\r\n★★★★★ EdFringe Review\r\n \r\n‘A truly unique act, there wasn’t a dull moment.’\r\n★★★★ Entertainment Now\r\n\r\n16+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Huge Davies: Whodunnit","instanceDates":"27 February-2 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"517803ABBDSQQTNHRHPNTPSMBSLHPBHKM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-27T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-27T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-02T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-02T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"I F*CKED YOU IN MY SPACESHIP\r\nBy Louis Emmitt-Stern\r\n“If you don’t want it, I mean, it’s a bit fucking weird… isn’t it? You’re just a guy in an alien costume.”\r\nTwo couples each invite a stranger into their homes with hope of sparking new life. Instead, they find themselves threatened by invasion, alienation, and abduction…\r\nDirect from its sold-out smash-hit run at VAULT Festival 2023, where it won the Origins Award for Outstanding New Work, I F*cked You in My Spaceship is a “wickedly funny” and razor-sharp comedy-drama about sex and relationships by Tony Craze Award-winning playwright Louis Emmitt-Stern. \r\nWINNER: Origins Award for Outstanding New Work (VAULT Festival 2023)\r\n“A rising-star playwright” \r\nTime Out https://www.timeout.com/london/theatre/i-fucked-you-in-my-spaceship\r\n\r\n“Invigorating […] Commendably fresh and candid […] Impressive polish all around”\r\nLost in Theatreland ★★★★★ https://lostintheatreland.co.uk/review-i-fucked-you-in-my-space-ship-vault-festival/\r\n\r\n“Witty, realistic and incredibly funny” \r\nCentre Stage Reviews ★★★★1/2 https://cfrycentrestage.wordpress.com/2023/02/09/review-i-fcked-you-in-my-spaceship-vault-festival/\r\n\r\n“An absolute triumph […] It really is out of this world.”\r\nAll That Dazzles ★★★★ https://www.allthatdazzles.co.uk/post/review-i-f-cked-you-in-my-spaceship-vault-festival/\r\n\r\nCreatives\r\nLouis Emmitt-Stern\r\nWriter\r\nJospeh Winer\r\nDirector\r\nLaura Howard\r\nLighting Designer \r\nBella Kear\r\nSound Designer\r\nPatrice Bowler \r\nMovement Director\r\n\r\n16+ recommendation\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":65,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"I F*cked You In My Spaceship","instanceDates":"19 June-8 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"465403AKRJRQCLMTDHMRJSPPVRHPDNTDK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-19T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-19T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-08T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-08T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Storytelling","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"Fear and Loathing meets South Park in a screwball monologue that's part romance, part buddy comedy, part body horror.\r\nTwo miles north of Hell, a nameless deadbeat narrator spots Satan buying soy milk at the 7-Eleven. Satan's a washed-up has-been, who’s totally lost his edge. That is until he falls in love with our narrator and the two embark on a debauched misadventure, by turns slapstick, violent, whimsical, dreamlike and tender. 18+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"I Saw Satan at the 7-Eleven By Christopher Brett Bailey ","instanceDates":"21 April-11 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"691403APHKKVKJDJTVQLKLSSQQDQQQCRN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-21T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-21T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-11T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-11T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"\"I don’t want to hang out with people just because they have babies. Do you want to hang out with people just because they have scrotums?\" Sophie used to be a person, now she has a baby. Her husband may or may not be a liar, but her mother-in-law is definitely a c—. I, Mother is a savagely funny portrayal of the first year of motherhood, sexless nights and full fat breast milk. 16+ (check webpage for content advice).","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":80,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"I, Mother","instanceDates":"26 February-3 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"761403AHPSDNHVKTJNTLNKTRJKMKGRBTN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-26T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-26T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-04-03T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-04-03T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Iain Stirling brings his critically acclaimed comedy to Soho Theatre Walthamstow for two special recorded shows- his only live shows in London this year!\r\nHe's a BAFTA winning comedian, and the iconic voice behind Love Island UK (ITV2) & Love Island USA (Peacock). Iain Stirling's show is packed with hilarious bite, observational humour, and Scottish charm that made him a global fan favourite.\r\nAs seen and heard on Taskmaster, Murder They Wrote, Live at The Apollo. Iain is also star and writer of sitcom Buffering on ITV.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Iain Stirling (Live Special Recording)","instanceDates":"24 April-24 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"702803ATBNVQKJDPRHRCDQSJRCDMDSJCH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-24T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-24T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-24T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-24T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Edinburgh Comedy Award Best Show Nominee 2023 Ian Smith (as heard on BBC Radio 4’s The News Quiz and co-hosting the Northern News podcast) presents a show about stress, love and driving a tank with your hairdresser.\r\nThree classic and timeless themes. Fresh from a sell-out run at the Edinburgh Fringe, Ian Smith brings his critically acclaimed and multi-award nominated show to Soho Theatre.\r\n\r\nEdinburgh Comedy Award Best Show Nominee 2023\r\n(ISH) Edinburgh Comedy Award Shortlist 2023\r\nNext Up Biggest Award in Comedy Runner-up 2023\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ian Smith: Crushing","instanceDates":"29 January-31 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"509403APLNTPBBTDNVGMTSSVQQJBBDBNN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-29T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-29T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-31T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-31T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Edinburgh Comedy Award Best Show Nominee 2023 Ian Smith (as heard on BBC Radio 4’s The News Quiz and co-hosting the Northern News podcast) presents a show about stress, love and driving a tank with your hairdresser.\r\nThree classic and timeless themes. Fresh from a sell-out run at the Edinburgh Fringe, Ian Smith brings his critically acclaimed and multi-award nominated show to Soho Theatre.\r\n\r\nEdinburgh Comedy Award Best Show Nominee 2023.\r\n\r\n(ISH) Edinburgh Comedy Award Shortlist 2023\r\nNext Up Biggest Award in Comedy Runner-up 2023\r\n‘There are few shows as purely funny as this on the Fringe.’ ★★★★ Guardian\r\n‘His observations and exaggerations are masterful’ ★★★★★ Quintessential Review\r\n‘Sheer brilliance’ ★★★★1/2 Chortle\r\n‘He's one of our most consistent comedians - properly funny.’ ★★★★ Fest\r\n\r\n★★★★★ One4Review\r\n★★★★★ Fringe Monkey\r\n★★★★★ Quintessential Review\r\n★★★★★ Edinburgh Festivals\u2028\r\n★★★★ 1/2 Chortle\u2028\r\n★★★★ 1/2 RGM\r\n★★★★  Guardian\r\n★★★★ Scotsman\r\n★★★★ Fest Mag\r\n★★★★ Beyond The Joke\r\n★★★★ EdFringe Review\r\n★★★★ Phoenix Remix\r\n★★★★ The Comic’s Comic\u2028\r\n★★★★ Mumble\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ian Smith: Crushing.","instanceDates":"2 October-7 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"494603ANGNGQJJCCSHDJDTKQRKPSDMQHJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-02T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-02T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-07T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-07T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Nominated for Best Show at the Edinburgh Comedy Awards 2025.\r\nFollowing a sold-out run in the Autumn, two-time Edinburgh Comedy Award nominee Ian Smith (co-host of the Northern News podcast) returns to Soho Theatre this Spring with his critically acclaimed show about stress, love and buying a magic spell off Amazon.\r\n\r\nAs seen on Live at the Apollo, Have I Got News For You and The Stand Up Sketch Show - and heard on The News Quiz, The Unbelievable Truth, Just A Minute and his own Radio 4 series, Ian Smith is Stressed. \r\n\r\nHis last show Crushing was also shortlisted for the (ISH) Edinburgh Comedy Award, runner-up in Next Up’s “Biggest Award in Comedy” and nominated for a Chortle Award for Best Show. It was one of the Guardian’s Top 10 Comedy Shows of 2023 and featured on the British Comedy Guide’s Best Reviewed Shows of 2023.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ian Smith: Foot Spa Half Empty","instanceDates":"29 April-1 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"698803AGHVTQRBBPDVPGJQRJGLJVVRMCP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-29T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-29T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-01T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-01T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Edinburgh Comedy Award nominee Ian Smith (co-host of the Northern News podcast) heads back out on tour with a new show about stress, love and buying a magic spell off Amazon.\r\n\r\nAs seen on Live at the Apollo, Have I Got News For You and The Stand Up Sketch Show - and heard on The News Quiz, The Unbelievable Truth, Just A Minute and his own Radio 4 series, Ian Smith is Stressed. \r\n\r\nHis last show Crushing was also shortlisted for the (ISH) Edinburgh Comedy Award, runner-up in Next Up’s “Biggest Award in Comedy” and nominated for a Chortle Award for Best Show. It was one of the Guardian’s Top 10 Comedy Shows of 2023 and featured on the British Comedy Guide’s Best Reviewed Shows of 2023.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ian Smith: Foot Spa Half Empty.","instanceDates":"25 November-29 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"633803ALHGPKLCKGQDJTVNLGKDJVNNQVL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-25T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-25T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-29T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-29T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Emmy-nominated comedian and “gentleman-scholar of alt-comedy” Ikechukwu Ufomadu seeks to provide you, the Audience, with the finest Amusements he can muster.\r\nExpect a rigorously nonsensical evening of comic absurdity that defies genre while operating within the bounds of international law.\r\nIkechukwu Ufomadu is an Emmy-nominated and Drama Desk Award-winning actor, writer and comedian, named a “Comedian You Should and Will Know” by Vulture/New York Magazine and a “Comic to Look Out For” by Time Out New York. He can be seen in the Oscar-nominated Judas and the Black Messiah, Los Espookys (HBO), Three Busy Debras, Joe Pera Talks To You (Adult Swim) and has written for Ziwe (Showtime).\r\n\r\nSold-Out Run at 2023 Edinburgh Fringe\r\nBiggest Award in Stand-Up (Next Up) Nominee\r\nTelegraph: Top 5 Shows of 2023\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ikechukwu Ufomadu: Amusements","instanceDates":"26 February-2 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"528603AMQBHRBMTKSHRTSCMCPCGJGKKPN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-26T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-26T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-02T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-02T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"After a personal tragedy, a failing comedian starts listening to the wrong voices in his head. Hilarious, mind-bending storytelling theatre from Daniel Bye. \r\nAfter a personal tragedy, a floundering TV comic starts listening to the wrong voices in his head. His moral compass is getting derailed. He kind of knows it. But all these ideas for his new show are brilliant.\r\nIs it ok to go too far so long as you’re on the right side of history? How far would you go?\r\nDaniel Bye’s award-winning stand-up storytelling is at its best in this startling new show. Book now for a wild ride through the warped mirror of twenty-first century culture.\r\n12+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Imaginary Friends by Daniel Bye","instanceDates":"19 May-24 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"610603ADDGLHDJKQRJPLTTPDTNBTNDBPL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-19T18:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-19T17:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-24T18:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-24T17:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join Soho Theatre Walthamstow Associate and Olivier Award winning actor Alessandro Babalola, with acting teacher Aoife Smyth for a playful, high-energy introduction to improvisation. Fast, fun and packed with imagination, this practical workshop introduces young people to the core skills of improvisation: listening, collaboration, confidence and creativity. Participants will learn how to think on their feet, build stories together and create characters and scenes in the moment. ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Improv Skills Workshop","instanceDates":"25 July-25 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"740203AQKMMMDBSRHTVPGPJVRJTVNVCCN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-25T13:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-25T12:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-25T13:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-25T12:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Families","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":420,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Intro to Improv - Intensive","instanceDates":"18 July-18 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"741803ANQDQSRNPRMLGNJRBNLHRNKJBJQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-18T10:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-18T09:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-18T10:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-18T09:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"A sweaty show with songs asking: what does it mean to feel strong?\r\nTwo confrontation-avoidant gentle beings finally decide to live out their 1990s TV fantasies and pump iron, strap on armour, and learn how to fight.\r\nMixing interviews with children, teens, and elders, with their own personal stories and medieval gymcore beats they made up, She Goat set forth on a quest to get strong, stay strong and find out what “strong\" even means. In search of assertiveness! In search of a six-pack! Armed with flute, autoharp, and a lot of cottage cheese… This is IRON FANTASY.  \r\nWritten and performed by She Goat (Shamira Turner and Eugénie Pastor). \r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Iron Fantasy","instanceDates":"10 March-21 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"689803APDJSKBNTJDPRMMJLTPBCTJBCRD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-10T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-10T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-21T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-21T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"One of the Best Reviewed Shows of Edinburgh Fringe 2025 – British Comedy Guide.\r\nComedian Ismael Loutfi's father tried to convert the state of Florida to Islam. He did not succeed. \r\nThis hilarious solo show examines those efforts, and the impact they had on Ismael's family. Heavenly Baba is a show that needs to be seen to be believed, a hilarious and touching exploration of what it means to express oneself honestly and authentically, and how not to lose yourself in said expression. \r\nIsmael is a comedian, writer and actor, currently writing on the upcoming animated show Mating Season, from the team behind Big Mouth\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ismael Loutfi: Heavenly Baba","instanceDates":"25 March-28 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"691804ATSDBBGSTTQMNGDSNMKJMRBJPDJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-25T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-25T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-28T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-28T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Isobel and her guitar ask modern life's essential questions: Is there ever a right time to have a baby? Are you your therapist's favourite client? Are polyamorous relationships as rad as moving into your mum's house (with your boyfriend)? Witty, warm, inventive - and very funny.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Isobel Rogers: How To Be Content","instanceDates":"29 May-29 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"610003ALCHJQBKDKTQNQGRBVSCRTLCKPN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-29T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-29T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-29T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-29T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"“We’re starting in a boardroom, there’s been an incident, someone has done an ableism…”\r\n\r\nUsually disabled people just want to do the right thing. But what if they don’t?  What if they were out to make as much money as possible from the guilt of non-disabled, anxious people (like you)?\r\n\r\nHot off the back of their smash-hit VAULT Festival run, multi-award winning disability-led theatre company FlawBored present “It’s a Motherf**king Pleasure”; a smart, scathing satire on the monetisation of identity politics that spares no-one.\r\n\r\nA ‘fully’ accessible show (well.. we tried!) A “witty, hilarious and absurd” deconstruction of identity politics. \r\n\r\nWINNER: Greenwich Theatre Award in association with LET\r\nNOMINEE: VAULT Festival Show of the Week\r\nNOMINEE: Off West End Awards IDEA\r\nNOMINEE: Off West End Awards ACCESS\r\nPleasance Associate Artists\r\nTheatre Deli Resident Artists\r\nCamden People’s Theatre Seed Commission\r\n\r\n“This is the type of show where you wanna be able to say I was there, “ or “Raucously brilliant”  There ought to be clowns \r\n“The show is witty, hilarious and absurd in delightful turns.” - Disability arts online\r\n\r\n“This is one of the funniest shows I’ve seen this year, and that’s not able anxiety talking, it’s just that good.” - Lost In Theatreland\r\n\r\n★★★★★ @voicemaguk\r\n★★★★★ Lost in theatreland\r\n★★★★★ Fringe Biscuit \r\n ★★★★½ stars - @TheReviewsHub \r\n★★★★ London Fringe Review\r\n★★★★ @BroadwayWorldUK \r\n★★★★ @LiamODellUK \r\n★★★★ LondonTheatre1\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":65,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"It’s A Motherf**king Pleasure","instanceDates":"24 April-13 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"462203AMLLDVQLSCCKPKDCQDDNCHDBCTL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-24T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-24T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-13T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-13T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Access","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Access","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"Using an old board game, projection-mapping and a pinch of magic, Joe Sellman-Leava and Dylan Howells uncover how the economy wins elections, dominates our lives, and why it’s so bloody complicated!\r\nby Joe Sellman-Leava, with Dylan Howells\r\ndeveloped with and directed by Katharina Reinthaller\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"It’s The Economy, Stupid!","instanceDates":"10 March-15 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"592603AGVHJBHRBMVBBJNHSSBGLGVQLSL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-10T18:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-10T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-15T18:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-15T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Political","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"What is the best orange thing in the world? Aperol spritz? Sunsets? Claudia Winkleman? \r\nYou probably never stopped to think about what your favourite orange thing was, but you’re damn sure thinking about it now. Maybe it’s marmalade, or maybe it’s Garfield, or maybe it’s the album ‘Channel Orange’ by Frank Ocean. There’s just so many to consider. And no one on earth has considered more of them than Ivo Graham. \r\nIvo Graham has always been a fan of orange things. Baked beans. Sriracha mayo. The Tiger Who Came To Tea. But in 2025, a series of emotional days in his favourite colour prompted Ivo to commit harder than ever to the bit: colour-coordinating his life for his daughter, for his mother, for his football team, and, he desperately hopes, for your entertainment. Come and help this orange lunatic make his orange list, in a show about hats, haters, hometown heroes, and whether Hare Krishnas are better than Hobnobs.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ivo Graham: Orange Crush","instanceDates":"12 October-17 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"729403ATKLJTQHHDDDDDQCQTTLCSMDGTM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-12T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-12T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-17T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-17T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join Jack as he tries out new material!","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jack Dee: Work in Progress","instanceDates":"11 May-13 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"462003AKNNDHDHDQKBMRBSTKBMKGSCBRV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-11T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-11T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-13T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-13T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Jack Docherty is Chief Commissioner Cameron Miekelson - your Chief, our Chief, The People’s Chief! As seen on BBC Scotland’s Scot Squad and The Chief, this national hero will be bringing his wit and wisdom (and let’s be honest, his still simmering good-looks) to Soho Theatre. You may have seen The Chief’s ‘Apology sketch’ - a viral sensation, racking up more than 80 million views - well now’s your chance to see The Chief live in his critically acclaimed, sell-out show, No Apologies. The show will feature your favourite sketches from Scot Squad and lots of hilarious new jokes as The Chief dissects the state of the nation, from politics to policing, football to families, bams to biscuits. The Chief will also read excerpts from his forthcoming best-selling memoir, No Apologies, a book that tells his unique personal story of how a white, middle-class, public school educated boy from Edinburgh somehow overcame all the odds to become the Chief Commissioner of The Scottish Police Force. This is sure to be the theatrical event of this, or any other, year. Don’t miss out! (Please note - bams and radges will be denied entry)\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jack Docherty in The Chief - No Apologies","instanceDates":"1 June-6 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"688403ADBVVBPRTGHNKRDQNDKKBBDRHKR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-01T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-01T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-06T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-06T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Following rave reviews and a sell-out run at the Edinburgh Festival Fringe, BAFTA award-winning star of Scot Squad and cult classic Absolutely, returns with his critically-acclaimed show David Bowie & Me.\r\nThe comic, author, actor and writer uses his time spent with Bowie on The Jack Docherty Show in 1997 as a jumping off point to take audiences through topics from first love, hedonism, mortality and why you should always meet your heroes. From AI to culture wars, families to teenage years, David Bowie and Me - Parallel Lives is a journey of comedy and storytelling, taking fans on a trip through the inner workings of his masterful mind. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jack Docherty: David Bowie & Me – Parallel Lives","instanceDates":"7 May-11 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"532603ATQGDRDPHDVGBCJDPVHNDVQCCBN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-07T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-07T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-11T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-11T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Teacher-by-trade Jack Harris’ hit Edinburgh Fringe show comes to Soho Theatre. A guide to everything the classroom may throw at you. Difficult questions. Problem pupils. Chairs. A jam-packed hour of gags, multimedia and, of course, teacher training.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jack Harris: Teaching Teachers How To Teach","instanceDates":"2 August-3 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"489003AGLPMLLSSLBQKLPCJPQLHHCDKHV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-02T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-02T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-03T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-03T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Teacher-by-trade Jack Harris’ hit Edinburgh Fringe show comes to Soho Theatre. A guide to everything the classroom may throw at you. Difficult questions. Problem pupils. Chairs. A jam-packed hour of gags, multimedia and, of course, teacher training.\r\n\r\n‘This brilliant debut is a gem of a show… effortlessly funny’\r\n★★★★ - Scotsman\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jack Harris: Teaching Teachers How To Teach [May23]","instanceDates":"30 May-31 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"461003AQLMBHTCGMLLGQNSNGSSTQDNGMQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-30T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-30T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-31T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-31T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Soho Theatre Comedy Lab Alumni, BAFTA winner and recovering spoken-word artist Jack Rooke (Creator of Hulu / C4’s Big Boys), brings back his debut comedy-theatre hour ‘Good Grief’ for the exact 10 year anniversary of it’s first run at Soho Dean Street. \r\n\r\nFeaturing snippets from the 2015 show co-written with his nan, this retrospective will further explore grief, ambition, being a class traitor, milking having a dead dad for personal / professional gain, the innocence of writing just for oneself before the interference of \"telly wankers\", and the palpable regret of his own decline into becoming said \"telly wanker\". \r\n\r\nDirected by Gabriel Bisset-Smith (now a telly wanker) and made with support from Soho Theatre.\r\n\r\nContent Warning: this show may contain potentially triggering stories around grief, suicide and losing awards. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jack Rooke's Good Grief: a decade retrospective of capitalising on my dead dad","instanceDates":"9 December-10 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"675003ASNCQTTHJRGKHDTCHMQMBNCSRDT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-09T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-09T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-10T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-10T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Carpet-fitter turned comedian Jack Skipper delivers his debut, Edinburgh Comedy Award nominated, stand-up hour with a show about how he went from a tradesman with no qualifications to a full-time comedian (with no qualifications) – offering insights into the endeavours of a working-class father struggling to navigate his way through life. \r\n\r\nSeen on The Stand Up Sketch Show.  Tour support for Michael McIntyre and Russell Kane. Over 16 million likes on TikTok. \r\n\r\nNominated for Best Newcomer at the Edinburgh Comedy Awards 2024. \r\nWinner of Best Debut Show at Leicester Comedy Festival 2024.  \r\nNominated for Next Up’s Biggest Award In Comedy 2024.\r\nSo You Think You’re Funny 2022 runner-up. \r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jack Skipper: Skint","instanceDates":"10 January-11 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"584603APDPKDQDHVDQMPTHSDSKRNNRHDC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-10T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-10T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-11T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-11T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Carpet-fitter turned comedian Jack Skipper delivers his debut, Edinburgh Comedy Award-nominated stand-up show.\r\nJoin Jack as he tells you how he went from a tradesman with no qualifications to a full-time comedian (with no qualifications) – offering insights into the endeavours of a working-class father struggling to navigate his way through life. \r\n\r\nSeen on The Stand Up Sketch Show.  \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":100,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jack Skipper: Skint (Special Recording)","instanceDates":"1 May-1 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"690603ADVKDVTHGQBBBJTLRBHVBCCVVCV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-01T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-01T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-01T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-01T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"After an eleven week run Off-Broadway in NYC with four extensions and a New York Times Critic’s Pick, the bad boy of clown Zach Zucker comes to Soho Theatre Walthamstow for his biggest London show yet as his award-winning alter-ego Jack Tucker.\r\nNew York Times Critic’s Pick (2024)\r\nVulture’s Top Comics You Should Know (2023)\r\nChortle Comedian’s Comedian Award (2020)\r\nA well-respected journeyman and bonafide legend on the Upstate New York regional comedy scene, Jack Tucker is the ultimate comedian's comedian. Fighting to save his marriage, regain the respect of his son, and pay off countless loansharks looking to collect their debts, Tucker (Jack) will do whatever it takes to make you laugh.\r\nIf the joke doesn't land, it's not because it isn't funny - you just didn't get it. Nothing can stop him... except himself.\r\nThis show has sold out in New York, London, Los Angeles, Edinburgh, Sydney, Adelaide, Melbourne and Mumbai, achieving a total of 498 walkouts worldwide.\r\nCreated and Performed by Zach Zucker\r\nDirected by Jonny Woolley\r\nCo-Devised by Jonny Woolley and Dylan Woodley\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jack Tucker: Comedy Stand Up Hour","instanceDates":"5 September-5 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"581603AGTRSDHNCPNHVBLBDHPSCQBRBPJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-05T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-05T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-05T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-05T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"After an eight week run Off-Broadway in NYC with two extensions and a New York Times Critic’s Pick, the bad boy of clown Zach Zucker returns to Soho Theatre with his award-winning, alter-ego: Jack Tucker\r\n\r\nNew York Times Critic’s Pick (2024)\r\nVulture’s Top Comics You Should Know (2023)\r\nChortle Comedian’s Comedian Award (2020)\r\n\r\nA well-respected journeyman and bonafide legend on the Upstate New York regional comedy scene, Jack Tucker is the ultimate comedian's comedian. Fighting to save his marriage, regain the respect of his son, and pay off countless loansharks looking to collect their debts, Tucker (Jack) will do whatever it takes to make you laugh. \\\r\n\r\nIf the joke doesn't land, it's not because it isn't funny - you just didn't get it. Nothing can stop him... except himself. \r\n\r\nThis show has sold out in New York, London, Los Angeles, Edinburgh, Sydney, Adelaide, Melbourne and Mumbai, achieving a total of 498 walkouts worldwide.\r\n\r\nCreated and Performed by Zach Zucker\r\nDirected by Jonny Woolley\r\nCo-Devised by Jonny Woolley and Dylan Woodley\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":80,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jack Tucker: Comedy Stand Up Hour.","instanceDates":"15 July-23 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"541003AMGHRVGRMTGBSKLHNLRMTCCGQMC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-15T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-15T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-23T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-23T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Catch stand-up sensation Jacqueline Novak as she workshops the follow-up show to the acclaimed Get on Your Knees.\r\nJacqueline Novak received a 2024 Emmy nomination for her Netflix special Get On Your Knees, directed by Natasha Lyonne for screen and described as “one of the most intricately conceived and written specials I’ve ever watched” by The Hollywood Reporter, “it unfolds with astonishing breathlessness.”\r\nBeginning life at the Edinburgh Fringe and Off-Broadway, the one-woman stand-up show was a New York Times ‘Critic’s Pick’, extending numerous times in New York City before touring the U.S and selling out across multiple London runs. The Guardian named Get On Your Knees as one of the top three comedy shows of 2022, while the Evening Standard described it as “exuding both wit and wisdom... thoroughly deserving of its standing ovation”.\r\nJacqueline has been described as “a stone cold genius” by Anne Hathaway, and “the Muhammed Ali of comedy” by John Mulaney. Cracked Magazine declared that “Netflix Should Let Jacqueline Novak Do Anything She Wants, Forever.”\r\nFormer hosts of the popular wellness podcast Poog, Jacqueline and Kate Berlant now present new weekly episodes of Berlant & Novak. Vogue describes the experience as “an intellectual investigation of contemporary life between your two smartest and funniest friends.”\r\nThis is a unique chance to see Jacqueline work on her new hour, and be the first in line to have the opportunity to see its beginnings. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jacqueline Novak: Work in Progress","instanceDates":"11 March-22 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"606603AKMSHQTNKBRHTTDGTSQLGJLTSNT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-11T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-11T21:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-22T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-22T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Jake Lambert brings his sell-out, 5 star show, Liminal, to Soho Theatre. \r\nA show about identity, friendship, culture wars, and epilepsy, but don’t worry there’s also jokes. Plenty of jokes.\r\nA friendly encounter with a stranger at a baseball game in New York seemed perfectly innocuous at the time, but when that stranger became a friend on social media it lead Jake down a rabbit hole of far-right political opinions, and extreme views. This resulted in Jake questioning the way we judge people and what makes a person who they are. But discovering the darker side to someone’s personality whilst simultaneously finding a friend he hadn’t spoken to in over 10 years leaves Jake wanting to figure out one big question; is the internet making people more connected than ever, or pulling us apart? But as mentioned before, there’s also jokes, plenty of jokes.\r\nWith three acclaimed sell-out runs at the Edinburgh Festival Fringe, Jake is quickly establishing a name for himself. His combination of one-liners, short stories and unique observations have seen him appear on shows on The BBC, Comedy Central, Dave, ITV, and ITV2 as well on stages up and down the country supporting Michael McIntyre, Jack Dee, Romesh Ranganathan, Kerry Godliman, Tom Allen, Seann Walsh and Rob Beckett. You can see Jake on screen, on stage, and online; in just 3 months his videos have collected over 75 million views on Tiktok and Instagram. His excellent joke writing has made him a firm favourite for TV shows. Having written the opening monologues for The National Comedy Awards, The Apprentice: You’re Fired, and The Royal Variety Performance. He has also written sketches for Stand Up To Cancer, and provided jokes on shows including; The Ranganation, Bake Off Extra Slice, 8 Out Of 10 Cats, Mock The Week, The Now Show, The News Quiz, There’s Something About Movies, Complaints Welcome, and Cooking With The Stars. \r\n\r\n***** \"...pure brilliance from start to finish\" - London Theatre 1 \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jake Lambert: Liminal","instanceDates":"26 May-9 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"460203AGVBCRBTQNNQBHBSSMCTQNMLRPQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-26T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-26T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-09T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-09T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Storytelling","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Political","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Former UK number one recording artist, singer, songwriter, and performer Jake Roche presents Neporrhoids! — his critically acclaimed comedy debut, a bold new narrative show asking what comes after having the world at your feet. Working alongside Edinburgh Comedy Award winner Jordan Brookes and renowned theatre maker Laurence Cook (Drive Your Plow Over the Bones of the Dead), Neporrhoids! is a darkly comic exploration of ambition, inheritance and collapse — a story about losing certainty and confronting who you are when the applause ends. 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jake Roche: Do You Know Who I Think I Am?","instanceDates":"7 April-11 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"688603ASVRMRHKSRVPVVVKLBVTPRLGBKB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-07T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-07T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-11T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-11T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Description / copy\r\nJali: noun: a West African historian, storyteller, praise singer, poet, or musician.\r\nOliver Twist: a charismatic comedian and performer refusing to be defined by his turbulent past.\r\nIn this one-person show that is as delicately told as it is captivating, Oliver uses his exceptional storytelling abilities to reflect on his time as a refugee and to unpack what his life looks like now.\r\nAfter fleeing the Rwandan civil war at the age of four, Oliver spent his childhood in Malawi, first in a refugee camp, and later in the city where his mother and father started a small convenience store. After acceptance into the Australian government’s refugee intake, the family arrived in Ipswich in 2014 to begin a new life.\r\nUsing personal anecdotes, drama and humour as a powerful antidote to trauma JALI is a vibrant and emotional journey that patiently proves there is light at the end of the tunnel.\r\nIn a four star review, the Sydney Morning Herald declared “Twist is a star” and “this is why we came back to the theatre”, and the Sydney Arts Guide called JALI “an unmissable experience” and “a wonderful accomplishment both in terms of writing and acting”.\r\nJALI was nominated for Best Independent Production at the Sydney Theatre Awards for 2021, with Oliver Twist also nominated for Best Newcomer.\r\nSelect Press:  \r\n★★★★★ “So brightly does he paint the opportunities of the future, he leaves us with the fresh realisation that new life is always possible.” OUT in Perth : https://www.outinperth.com/oliver-twist-jali-perth-festival/jali/\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jali by Oliver Twist ","instanceDates":"21 June-24 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"468003ATNTKJMPSLMKJNNVPDTBKQVHHGV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-21T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-21T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-24T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-24T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Political","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A brand-new show, full of everything you love about James Acaster and more!\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"James Acaster","instanceDates":"30 March-31 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"678803AHQGKCDBVCJRNJHLNNVJLLMDKHK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-30T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-30T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-31T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-31T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"'One of comedy’s most original voices’ (Evening Standard) has written a new show. He’s very proud of it. That being said, you are allowed to ruin it. Fill your boots.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"James Acaster: WIP","instanceDates":"8 July-8 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"488803AMNLQJNDTNQPQDTHCQCCJLJVDQC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-08T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-08T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-08T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-08T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"James Acaster tries new ideas for an hour.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"James Acaster: Work-in-Progress","instanceDates":"28 July-2 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"630403AGVCPBNPRJNVDVPLCHKHCTJPNGM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-28T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-28T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-02T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-02T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Work In Progress","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"JAMES AUSTIN JOHNSON is a comedian originally from Nashville and a featured player on SATURDAY NIGHT LIVE. The New York Times has called him “one of SNL’s most versatile celebrity impressionists.” His spot-on impression of Trump paired with his improvisational ramblings about Weird Al, Julia Louis Dreyfus and Scooby Doo have garnered over 5 million views, with profiles on James in Vanit Fair, Slate, Mashable and VICE to name a few. As an actor, James' TV/Film credits include FUTURE MAN, BASKETS, ROBBIE, BETTER CALL SAUL, THE LAST TYCOON and the Coen Brothers’ feature HAIL, CAESAR!. As a stand up, James has performed on the Vice series FLOPHOUSE, as well as RIOT LA and JUST FOR LAUGHS as a New Face.\r\n\r\n16+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"James Austin Johnson: Live","instanceDates":"5 June-10 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"464403ADSGCRSPGLTDMLHNLQCHRQQSRQH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-05T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-05T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-10T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-10T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Domestic abuse isn’t funny, but this show is.\r\nTrailblazing comedian James Barr is going on tour around the UK with a bold, \"genre-defying\" (ArtsHub) hour of stand-up. A darkly hilarious reckoning with shame, survival and a pushy-wushy down the stairsy-wairsy.\r\nNominee for Best Show at the ISH Edinburgh Comedy Awards, NextUp’s Biggest Award in Comedy and the Queer Performers Award at the 2025 Edinburgh Fringe, Sorry I Hurt Your Son (Said My Ex To My Mum) was also named one of the best reviewed shows of Edinburgh Fringe.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"James Barr: Sorry I Hurt Your Son (Said My Ex to My Mum)","instanceDates":"13 April-14 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"695003ACJSQGLBSCSMNDBGMHGQLTMQKMH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-13T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-13T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-14T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-14T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"\"Who are you Jamie!?\"\r\n\"I'm THAT BITCH!\"\r\nJamie is not in fact, that bitch. Jamie has just been dumped for a man who goes to the gym. Jamie is a hot mess. Jamie needs to reinvent himself. And fast.\r\nAmerican spin instructor and rock-n roll powerhouse, Lily, takes him in and changes the course of his life. Jamie spends the next five years learning how to move forward on a bike that doesn't move.\r\nIt feels like the fun will never end. But what do you do when a friend breaks up with you?\r\nJAMIE FINN blends storytelling, comedy and original music as he explores the chaotic wilderness of his 20's.\r\nThis is a story of how to mourn more than one type of relationship.\r\nThis is a story about the romance of platonic Love.\r\nThis is a story of why nobody is talking about Jamie.\r\n16","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jamie Finn: Nobody’s Talking About Jamie","instanceDates":"3 June-4 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"518803AGJMLHBNCGRRPLKHVGVPTVKBHPT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-03T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-03T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-04T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-04T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Janine thought she knew her family. Then she took a DNA test and things got messy.\r\nThe highly anticipated second hour from Edinburgh Comedy Award Best Newcomer nominee Janine Harouni. The quick-witted New Yorker returns with a show that explores her Arab roots, pregnancy and what happens when your mail order DNA test does not go to plan.\r\n\r\nStar of ITV2’s Buffering. Seen and heard on The Russell Howard Hour, The John Bishop Show, Comedians Giving Lectures, Question Team, The Stand Up Sketch Show and The Now Show.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Janine Harouni: Man’oushe","instanceDates":"5 December-9 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"492403ACBNRSVVNLKQGBKLGKNJJJSDNBN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-05T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-05T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-09T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-09T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Two-time Edinburgh Comedy Award nominee and ‘unstoppably entertaining’ (***** Times) Janine Harouni hits the road with a brand-new hour of hilarious, high-octane stand-up.\r\nFresh off a world tour – including an Off-Broadway run in New York and a performance at the Netflix is a Joke Festival in LA – the New York native returns with a razor-sharp new show about marriage, parenting, and all the other wonderful milestones that slowly degrade your sleep and sanity.\r\n\r\nWith over 10 million views online, an Amazon Prime special, and rave reviews across the board, Harouni is one of the most electric comics working today.\r\n\r\nHarouni is a regular on UK TV (Live at the Apollo, The Last Leg, The Russell Howard Hour, The John Bishop Show), and has opened for comics like Michael Che and Adam Rowe. She has featured in films and TV shows like Bob’s Burgers, The Franchise, Collette, Patrick Melrose, The People We Hate At The Wedding and The Batman. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Janine Harouni: This Is What You Waited For","instanceDates":"20 October-1 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"632003AGCMBJPKQDNDJTHVQVVSPBTNTKC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-20T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-20T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-01T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-01T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Jason Manford is back with his brand-new live show.\r\nJason Manford is back with his brand-new live show, A Manford All Seasons. Jason’s been busy since his last smash-hit stand up show but fans of his Absolute Radio show will know this nationally acclaimed comedian hasn’t changed a bit. A Manford All Seasons is Jason’s latest comic offering that is set to hit the road in 2024, his iconic ‘expert observational comedy’ (The Guardian) is sure to be ‘comic gold’ (Mail on Sunday). \r\n\r\n‘Starstruck’ (ITV1), ‘Unbeatable’ (BBC One), ‘Big Night of Musicals’ (BBC One), ‘The National Lottery's New Year's Eve Big Bash’ (ITV1), ‘First & Last’ (BBC One), ‘The Masked Singer’ (ITV1), ‘What Would Your Kid Do?’ (ITV1), ‘Olivier Awards’ (ITV1), ‘Scarborough’ (BBC One), ‘8 out of 10 Cats’ (Channel 4), ‘The Nightly Show’ (ITV1), ‘Sunday Night at the Palladium’ (ITV1), ‘Live at the Apollo’ (BBC One), ‘Have I Got News For You’, (BBC One), QI (BBC Two) and ‘The Royal Variety Performance’ (ITV1) have all helped establish Jason as a nationally known comic.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jason Manford: A Manford All Seasons","instanceDates":"28 March-28 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"642603APKJCKNJMPNPLJMKCDTCMNCHJCH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-28T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-28T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-28T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-28T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"In his UK debut, Jay Jurden (Hulu, Netflix, HBO, The Tonight Show with Jimmy Fallon) presents a brand-new hour of his dumbest thoughts in the most brilliant way OR his most brilliant thoughts in the dumbest way. You decide. \"Speed kills. That sums up Jay Jurden's style. He's a motormouth whose machine-gun delivery can build up a frenzied, thrilling momentum, topping one joke with another until you might have to rewind to catch it all.\" - New York Times","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jay Jurden Takes London","instanceDates":"3 August-8 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"720803ACJPHLMPNHDDRPJHPSCNKPPHGHB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-03T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-03T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-08T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-08T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A tour-de-force celebrating the power of movement, body positivity and finding joy.\r\nScottish comedian Jay Lafferty combines comedy and pole dancing in this jam-packed hour tackling everything from ageing to internalised misogyny, celebrating the power of movement, body positivity and finding joy.\r\n\r\nBahookie is a tour-de-force celebration of what you can achieve when you're terrified of becoming irrelevant, where Jay uses her signature warm wit and sharp observations to highlight the hilarity that comes from completely overestimating your own abilities.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jay Lafferty: Bahookie","instanceDates":"31 May-1 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"527403AGLRDVCQGSLGVGSNVKNQJJVQCVS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-31T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-31T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-01T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-01T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Musical supernova Jazz Emu (The Telegraph’s 26th Funniest Comedian of the 21st Century) is back with a brand-new show, with a full live band…The Royal Variety Show. \r\nThe headline slot. \r\nAt long last, a chance for Jazz Emu to secure his long-coveted Knighthood. But it’s bad news; a series of recent tax, bribery and libel allegations are threatening to snatch the coveted prize from before his very, very, very eyes. \r\n\r\nWill Jazz and his Contractually-Less-Talented-Than-Him band, The Cosmique Perfectión, be able to put on a Heck Of A Show and secure a Royal Pardon? Or will Jazz’s next performance be in the canteen at Wormwood Scrubs? \r\n\r\nLet the Majesty commence\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jazz Emu: Knight Fever","instanceDates":"3 June-22 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"519603ADKSSJBNCCPPVMJBVNQNKTJMHSM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-03T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-03T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-22T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-22T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Musical meteor Jazz Emu was born to please you.\r\nTotal and Utter Audience Satisfaction is his middle name – finally, after a long and financially ruinous Deed Poll process. \r\nBut he's feeling uneasy. A review described his last show as 'a bit much'. What? Was his seventeenth stage-dive too tastefully executed? Not this time. This time, he's living up to his middle-namesake.\r\nFollowing multiple sell-out Soho Theatre runs, Jazz Emu is back with a brand new musical odyssey.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jazz Emu: The Pleasure is All Yours","instanceDates":"25 November-6 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"647203ACJGBPHKBCCJRNLGLTKVTRMPTKT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-25T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-25T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-06T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-06T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"\"This is a work of genius.\" ★★★★★ The Telegraph\r\nDirect from a sell-out critically-acclaimed run at the Edinburgh Fringe, global sensation Jazz Emu brings his stand-up musical spectacular You Shouldn’t Have to Soho Theatre.\r\nIn 2016, Jazz Emu played the biggest gig he'd ever landed at the Helsinki Velodrome. But during his between-song patter, he carelessly insulted one of his biggest fans. What he said doesn't bear repeating, but let's say the Scandinavian Goblin community may never look him in the eye again. Now he's back to clear his name and regain his former glory. Will he be able to surmount the insurmountable and get every single person in the world to like him? Or is it time for him to face the music?\r\n“My new favourite comedian… I didn’t stop laughing for a whole hour” ★★★★★ The Times\r\n\"Fantastically funny and ferociously funky\" ★★★★★ The List\r\n“a confident blend of surrealism and genuinely impressive musicianship\" ★★★★ The Scotsman\r\n\"…definitely not an unapologetic narcissist who expects everyone to love him.\" ★★★★ British Theatre Guide\r\n“What is going on? Where am I? Am I falling in love?” ★★★★ Broadway Baby\r\n\r\n★★★★ Chortle \r\n★★★★ Guardian\r\n★★★★ Fest Mag \r\n★★★★ The Wee Review \r\n★ Jazz Emu’s Dad\r\n\r\n16+ recommendation","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jazz Emu: You Shouldn't Have","instanceDates":"3 April-8 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"459403ATCLDDTSCLNNTQCVBJCJVMPCGBT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-03T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-03T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-08T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-08T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"The viral sensation and British Comedian of the Year alumni returns with an all-new hour of standup.\r\nFollowing on from his smash hit debut tour and comedy special ‘Smart Casual’, Jeff Innocent returns with an all-new hour of standup. At the ripe age of 71, and after decades of resistance, Jeff has finally decided to embrace his twilight years with a calm and accepting mindset. That’s the plan anyway… \r\n\"It should be made law that every British Citizen must go and see Jeff Innocent. He's that funny.\" Evening Standard \r\n\"Jeff Innocent delivers a masterclass in standup comedy every time he performs” The Times\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":100,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jeff Innocent: Leaning In","instanceDates":"22 May-22 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"753803AQNHSVBQCSHBQNKLQLPHLPRTKMQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-05-22T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-05-22T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-05-22T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-05-22T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"British Comedian of the Year Winner and social media sensation Jeff Innocent has embarked on his first ever nationwide UK tour.\r\nJeff will be bringing his unique and hilarious cultural insights on the road for the first time in a career that has spanned almost three decades and earned him a reputation as one of the greatest living comedians the country has to offer.\r\nHighly anticipated and long overdue. This will be an hour of standup comedy that you do not want to miss.  \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jeff Innocent: Smart Casual","instanceDates":"22 May-25 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"527803ALRSLVSJBJNLGBHCNVSPMJLTKBJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-22T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-22T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-25T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-25T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Jen Brister is Reactive - or so she's been told. Apparently, you don't have to respond to every little thing around you. Finding herself in a constant state of exacerbation at the state of the world and people in general, Brister has been told she needs to chill the hell out. Can Jen find her zen? It seems unlikely to be honest… \r\nJen is a critically acclaimed stand-up comedian and writer, as seen on BBC's Live at the Apollo, Frankie Boyle's New World Order, QI and Mock The Week. \r\nFollowing a sold-out show at the Eventim Apollo, Jen is bringing her hit show to the beautiful Soho Walthamstow. \r\n\"Furiously Funny\" - The Guardian \r\n\"Her energy is explosive. Her use of space and delivery, mesmerising\" - The Sunday Times\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":105,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jen Brister: Reactive","instanceDates":"11 November-11 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"707803ARKCTBQNMMNSLMQTVGGTMQKVJGC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-11T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-11T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-11T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-11T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"American comedian Jena Friedman is back in London.\r\nThis is a brand new hour she’s working out about life, death and this current political moment. 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jena Friedman: Motherf*cker – Work in Progress","instanceDates":"27 February-5 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"594003ATVKQKNSKGGKTJKHJRNRRCDVMMG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-27T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-27T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-05T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-05T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"You won't have had children yet, as Jenny is the first person to ever go through this particular ordeal, but you might be keen to learn a little something about this incredible new process called pregnancy from award-winning musical comedian and future nation's sweetheart, Jenny Bede. Jenny will navigate the entire gamut of human emotions, from despair all the way through to despair, as she jokes, sings and (at last, justifiably) Mum-dances her experience to life in this new hour. 'Lyrically genius' (Edinburgh Festivals Magazine). 16+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jenny Bede: The First Pregnant Woman in the World","instanceDates":"21 June-22 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"468603APCJDHSPJKLLGHSBQMPTTJPTMMR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-21T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-21T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-22T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-22T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Gaza. Ukraine. Syria. Sudan. Yemen. The world is facing more armed conflicts than at any point in decades, and Jeremy Bowen has reported from the centre of nearly all of them.\r\nAs the BBC's International Editor, Jeremy has spent over 40 years covering more than 90 countries and 20 wars. From El Salvador in 1989 to the frontlines today, he has interviewed world leaders, documented war crimes, been shot at, and survived to tell the stories. \r\n\r\nBut something has changed. Israel imposes restrictions on foreign journalists from entering Gaza. Russia controls the narrative in occupied Ukraine. Governments from Syria to Sudan restrict access, manipulate information, and discredit reporters who contradict official accounts. In the age of social media, competing claims flood our screens, but who is telling the truth? And how do we know? \r\n\r\nJeremy has spent his career fighting for access, verifying what others want hidden, and bearing witness when governments would rather the world look away. He will explain how the battle for truth is being waged, why press freedom is collapsing in conflict zones, and what it means when the first casualty of war is not just truth, but those trying to report it. \r\n\r\nIn the second half, audiences will have the chance to put their questions to a journalist who has made it his life's work to get as close to the truth as possible—even when that truth is dangerous, disputed, or under fire. \r\n\r\nAn essential evening for anyone who wants to understand the world as it is, not as we wish it to be. ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jeremy Bowen: Truth Under Fire","instanceDates":"21 October-21 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"753403ADNCJCHTJRNPRHGMPKPBHHQHNHQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-10-21T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-10-21T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-10-21T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-10-21T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Political","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Podcast","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":""},{"description":"A show dedicated to Mr Segway, the man who invented the Segway, performed entirely on Segways. The incomparably ridiculous Duncan Brothers play his sons to tell this inspiring story of a man who set out to change the world and how we travel within it.\r\n\r\nFrom the award-winning makers of LEGS & LOGS. Directed by Dan Lees.\r\nWINNERS: 2019 Malcolm Hardee Award for Comic Originality \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jeremy Segway: A Life Out of Balance","instanceDates":"24 May-25 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"536403AHTCVMGQSQKHLMNSKBRJRHRVCDL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-24T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-24T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-25T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-25T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join the Emmy-winning comedian for a short run of London shows…\r\nJerrod Carmichael is an Emmy-winning comedian from Winston-Salem, NC. His most recent special, Rothaniel, can be streamed on HBO. \r\n\r\nThis event will be a phone-free experience. Use of phones, smart watches and accessories, will not be permitted in the performance space.\r\n\r\nThe house will open at approximately 9pm and we ask patrons to arrive promptly so that phones, smart watches and accessories can be secured using the Yondr phone pouch system. We cannot guarantee latecomers will be admitted.   \r\n\r\nUpon arrival at the venue, all phones, smart watches and accessories will be secured in individual Yondr pouches that will be opened at the end of the event. Guests maintain possession of their devices at all times, and can access them throughout the event only in designated Phone Use Areas within the venue. All devices will be re-secured in Yondr pouches before returning to the performance space.\r\n\r\nAnyone seen using a device (phone, smart watch or accessories) during the performance will be escorted out of the venue.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jerrod Carmichael Live in London","instanceDates":"6 March-8 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"533003AMQJRTNNJSKGBDQKQVSSDBVQJLN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-06T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-06T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-08T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-08T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join the Emmy-winning comedian for a short run of work in progress shows.\r\nJerrod Carmichael is an Emmy-winning comedian from Winston-Salem, NC. His most recent special, Don’t Be Gay, can be streamed on HBO Max. Previous specials include Rothaniel, and also currently stars in HBO’s, Jerrod Carmichael Reality Show.’\r\nJerrod was recently referred to as ‘a master storyteller’, by Variety, describing 2025’s Don’t Be Gay as ‘witty, brash, guttingly honest and slightly heartbreaking’.\r\nJoin him at Soho Theatre as he works on material for his new show.\r\n\r\nThis event will be a phone-free experience. Use of phones, smart watches and accessories, will not be permitted in the performance space.\r\nUpon arrival at the venue, all phones, smart watches and accessories will be secured in individual Yondr pouches that will be opened at the end of the event. Guests maintain possession of their devices at all times, and can access them throughout the event only in designated Phone Use Areas within the venue. All devices will be re-secured in Yondr pouches before returning to the performance space.\r\nAnyone seen using a device (phone, smart watch or accessories) during the performance will be escorted out of the venue.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jerrod Carmichael: February in London","instanceDates":"26 February-28 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"693803AMLQTJBGNVTPKTRMJHQDKGKHGDC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-26T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-26T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-28T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-28T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Work In Progress","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Join the Emmy-winning comedian for a short run of London work in progress shows…\r\nJerrod Carmichael is an Emmy-winning comedian from Winston-Salem, NC. His most recent special, Rothaniel, can be streamed on HBO, was directed by Bo Burnham and received critical acclaim on its release in 2022. He currently stars in HBO’s, Jerrod Carmichael Reality Show, and was recently seen in Yorgos Lanthimos's Oscar winning film Poor Things, alongside Emma Stone, Willem Dafoe and Mark Ruffalo. Join him at Soho Theatre as he works on material for his new show.\r\n\r\n\r\nThis event will be a phone-free experience. Use of phones, smart watches and accessories, will not be permitted in the performance space.\r\n\r\nUpon arrival at the venue, all phones, smart watches and accessories will be secured in individual Yondr pouches that will be opened at the end of the event. Guests maintain possession of their devices at all times, and can access them throughout the event only in designated Phone Use Areas within the venue. All devices will be re-secured in Yondr pouches before returning to the performance space.\r\n\r\nAnyone seen using a device (phone, smart watch or accessories) during the performance will be escorted out of the venue.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jerrod Carmichael: Work in Progress","instanceDates":"25 June-28 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"553403AJGHSTLGKJDCTMDBTVGRGNJGQJT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-25T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-25T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-28T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-28T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Not all those who wander are lost. Sure... but some who wander are walking slowly because they've shattered their coccyx on the Cliffs of Moher. Jess Fuchs left home to avoid her problems and returned even more broken. This debut is less an hour of stand-up, more a much-needed debrief session with your best friend. Nominee: Next Up Biggest Award in Comedy. Support for Fortune Feimster, Gianmarco Soresi and Morgan Jay. References to mental health issues. References to mental health issues 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jess Fuchs: Feral","instanceDates":"11 March-13 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"761803AHVDKHRQCTQRQSNCNVJDGTCQNJH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-03-11T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-03-11T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-03-13T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-03-13T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Elton John’s greatest hits are reimagined by multi-award-winning Jess Robinson (Dead Ringers, The Last Leg), renowned for her pitch-perfect impressions. \r\nCelebrating Elton through the voices of iconic women: Britney, Barbra, Amy, and more. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jess Robinson: Your Song","instanceDates":"1 July-4 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"612603ATQSNPJJDKKGMJSVQNHTRKBTBCG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-01T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-01T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-04T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-04T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Mary Floppins has thrown a sh*t fit.\r\nWipe the wee from the toilet seat and pick up your dirty undies, because The Perfect Nanny is back to teach all you little boys - and girls - a thing or two about running a prim and proper household. \r\nHailed \"a rising star and quadruple threat\" (The Spy In The Stalls), Jessica Barton combines a spoonful of song, dance, clowning and deep-cleaning to present a skanky and empowering comedy debut. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jessica Barton: Dirty Work","instanceDates":"21 January-24 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"666403AMRDDSDRLPCMHKLLCHJJMLDBNQD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-21T22:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-21T22:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-24T22:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-24T22:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Mary Floppins has thrown a sh*t fit. Wipe the wee from the toilet seat and pick up your dirty undies, because The Perfect Nanny is back to teach all you little boys-and girls-a thing or two about running a prim and proper household.\r\nReturning to the UK after sold-out performances at Adelaide Fringe and Melbourne International Comedy Festival, Jessica Barton combines a spoonful of song, dance, clowning, and deep-cleaning to present a skanky and empowering London Clown Festival debut.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jessica Barton: Dirty Work.","instanceDates":"18 June-18 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"615603AHDVHGLLBTCNTMPMRLPLSJPNJPK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-18T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-18T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-18T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-18T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"One woman’s love letter to fanfiction, and all the hot nerdy freaks who read and write it. \r\nJoin Jessica Durand as she very bravely stages her very own self-insert Downton Abbey World War One fanfiction for a live audience. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jessica Durand: Over the Top","instanceDates":"4 March-4 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"684603AMGCSDKJKVMVVLJQKTRKKRJJVRG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-04T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-04T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-04T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-04T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A monster’s guide to tolerance and temperance.\r\nJess can feel herself becoming an emotional wildebeest right when her world (and the whole world, thanks) demands cool, collected ultra-detached saint-like kindness and understanding. S**t. \r\n\r\nShe goes digging around in her DNA for answers and finds so many beautiful horrors. Witness her effort to become a brand new, mythical, mystical ‘coper.’ OR NOT. She gets cancelled, she gets touched and she gets a dolphin-based epiphany all in one show. The silliest of comedy for the scariest of days from Edinburgh Best Show Award Nominee. \r\n\r\nYou’ve seen Jess on BBC’s QI, Live at the Apollo, Celebrity University Challenge and Richard Osman’s House of Games. From Travel Man on C4 and World’s Most Dangerous Roads on Dave. You know her from her two BBC R4 series of Sturdy Girl Club plus podcasts The Guilty Feminist and Hoovering. And, of course, from new mighty smash hit Gladiator’s fan-podcast Contender Ready which Jess co-hosts with Olympic weightlifting superstar, Emily Campbell. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jessica Fostekew: Iconic Breath","instanceDates":"13 October-18 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"636005AMJHMCRNKDMSDPTBHDNRVGGLKCT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-13T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-13T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-18T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-18T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A brand new stand-up show about passion, pace and purpose from the criticallyacclaimed star of BBC’s QI, Live at the Apollo and C4’s Travel Man.\r\nJess’ son’s joined a cult AND her cat’s learnt to talk – but despite all that she’s fine, actually. In fact she’s hurtling faster and hustling harder than ever for the things that she wants and needs.\r\n\r\nHer last show Wench played a sold-out Edinburgh Fringe run and UK tour and is available now as a special. Her previous show Hench was nominated for Best Show at the Edinburgh Comedy Awards and won Best Show at the Chortle Awards where Jess also won Best Act. It’s available to stream now on Amazon Prime as part of the Soho Theatre Live series. \r\n\r\nJess is a regular co-host of The Guilty Feminist podcast, host and creator of her own podcast about eating, Hoovering, and star and writer of BBC Radio 4’s Sturdy Girl Club. Jess has also appeared in the award-winning sitcom Motherland and most recently hugely-acclaimed feature film Scrapper which won the Grand Jury prize at the Sundance festival. \r\n\r\nShe’s also been on all your favourite panel shows from Celebrity Pointless to House of Games. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jessica Fostekew: Mettle","instanceDates":"8 February-10 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"516603ASHVLVHBQCRLTKGHPDPLKVLNKLJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-08T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-08T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-10T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-10T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Jessie is oversharing and overthinking as she tries to navigate her way through the chaos of heartbreak and working motherhood. Contains hope and humour and possibly a new puppet. ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jessie Cave: Work In Progress","instanceDates":"23 May-21 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"471403ABCLRQSKVNHLDQNBHHSGKCVDMHD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-23T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-23T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-21T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-21T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Work In Progress","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Jessie is oversharing and overthinking as she tries to navigate her way through the chaos of heartbreak and working motherhood. Contains hope and humour and possibly a new puppet. \r\n\r\n16+ recommended","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jessie Cave: Work in Progress.","instanceDates":"8 April-15 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"449003AQKGRMMMSBHTQMBCBHHGLBLPNRB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-08T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-08T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-15T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-15T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Jessie Nixon is putting her life on the line for this show. Or at least her livelihood/self-esteem. She's ripped out her heart, covered it in glitter and squirty cream, and offered it to you, still beating. Don't make her regret it. If you're mentally ill, a lapsed catholic, queer, occasionally distraught, too smart for your own good or have ever cried in a changing room: this is for you. As seen on BBC One and BBC Three. Tour support for Fern Brady, Helen Bauer and Lou Sanders.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jessie Nixon: Don’t Make Me Regret This","instanceDates":"13 April-14 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"678203AQLGRSLNVJVGTVHGPMDCHNDJMRV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-13T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-13T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-14T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-14T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Hot off the heels of his sell out debut hour at the Fringe, Jin Hao walks you through the seascape of his mind, filled with nightmares of being a spider, dreams of joining the yakuza and breezy memories of serving in the military with the boys.\r\nConfronting fear with mischief and imagination, he surprises with gritty softness, honest lies and pockets of joy. BBC New Comedy Awards and Chortle Student finalist. \r\n\r\n★★★★★ The Skinny, \r\n“This nonsensical tale is perfectly constructed- not a single word is wasted, nor a punchline missed\"\r\n★★★★ The Scotsman\r\n“A comic simply bursting to show you everything he’s capable of\"\r\n★★★★ Fest Mag  \r\n“A masterfully strutted fringe debut which embraces and critiques the art of stand up\"\r\n★★★★ The Arts Desk\r\n“A distinct new voice in comedy\"\r\n\r\nComedy.co.uk RECOMMENDED SHOW - “Exquisitely crafted hour…perfectly times pauses and punchlines that come out of left field”\r\n\r\n16+ (strong language)\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jin Hao Li: Swimming in a Submarine","instanceDates":"2 September-8 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"566203AJMBHDKBVGNHDKMPNSLQLQTLLGG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-02T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-02T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-08T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-08T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"By Peter Quilter \r\nDirected by Rupert Hands\r\n12+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":150,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jinkx Monsoon is Judy Garland in End of the Rainbow","instanceDates":"15 May-21 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"677603ATLLNPMTJBPMNMPLVTQSTMVNKLQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-15T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-15T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-21T14:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-21T13:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"‘I’ve dreamed of this day. My whole life.’ There’s one hour to go before the wedding, but now the wedding may not be going ahead. Following an award-winning, critically-acclaimed, sell-out Edinburgh Fringe run, Lyn Gardner recommended double act ‘Britney’ - aka Ellen Robertson (Vladimir, Mickey 17, The Pale Horse) and Charly Clive (Rooster, Pure, The Lazarus Project) - present the London debut of a new two-hander about ownership, tradition, and the all-important ‘L’ word of any relationship: leverage. 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jitters","instanceDates":"1 February-20 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"760803APMJCTNPDGVMLHCQKGKMPCMKTHR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-01T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-01T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-20T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-20T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"While everyone's settling down, Jo's busy doing all the naughty stuff she's yet to try! From day raves with Gen Zs (she's the hype-girl keeping everyone hydrated) to contemplating her first sex party (did someone say therapy cuddle puddle in the darkroom? Yes please!), she's determined to max the fun while the biological clock ticks fast. \r\nShortlisted for the BBC New Comedy Award 2023 and Funny Women Awards. \r\nSeen on Channel 4, BBC Three and Dave. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jo Griffin: Last Chance Saloon","instanceDates":"11 October-12 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"571003AJJSTVRQNDVPPDMSPQDGNTTVBNP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-11T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-11T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-12T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-12T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"John Travulva teams up with his tick-box protégé: queer, non-binary class-straddler Jodie Mitchell (Comedy Central Live). But does he need to? He's not sure, he gets plenty of praise as himself: 'John Travulva’s set is so funny it makes all the comedy in my life up to this point redundant' (TheatreBubble.com). 'The comedy turn by John Travulva... left me with actual tears of laughter' (DIVA Magazine). 'Travulva... has the audience in the palm of their hand, with excellent comic timing and real warmth' (Upper-Circle.com). ‘Standout talent’ (Stage).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jodie Mitchell: Becoming John Travulva","instanceDates":"29 January-3 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"500803AGRPDLDQJLCGPJDMVGBJJMNRRPT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-29T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-29T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-03T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-03T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"LGBTQ+","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Drag","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Yorkshire’s biggest bastard and Edinburgh Comedy Award Best Newcomer 2024 is back, after yet another sold-out run at the Edinburgh Fringe Festival!\r\nThis time he's dead… dead good! And also, dead. He's a dead man. Join the nation's favourite demonic Working Men's Club owner as he dazzles you from beyond the grave. See him now before he is well and truly gone \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Joe Kent-Walters is Frankie Monroe: DEAD!!! (Good Fun Time)","instanceDates":"17 November-29 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"651003ANCCTDHSLHVJTRLTSJRJGVSTPHP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-17T21:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-17T21:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-29T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-29T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join owner and MC of The Misty Moon (working men's club in Rotherham/portal to hell) for a slap-up feast of laughs, tricks and mucky bitter. Can Frankie save showbiz? Can he protect his club from demonic ruin?? Can you touch his special trowel??? (NO WAY!).\r\nWinner of BBC New Comedy Award 2023 and Best Show Leicester Comedy Festival 2024.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Joe Kent-Walters is Frankie Monroe: LIVE!!!","instanceDates":"12 May-14 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"614403ASGHRTPBHPDMSNJCTLCPCGGMLJC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-12T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-12T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-14T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-14T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Here he is! Yorkshire’s biggest bastard. For 6 nights only!\r\nJoin owner and MC of The Misty Moon (working men's club in Rotherham/portal to hell) for a slap-up feast of laughs, tricks and mucky bitter. Can Frankie save showbiz? Can he protect his club from demonic ruin?? Can you touch his special trowel??? (NO WAY!).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Joe Kent-Walters is Frankie Monroe: LIVE!!!.","instanceDates":"21 November-1 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"564403ARHLRDQJSNDBQSQSNTNSGVKGVKH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-21T21:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-21T21:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-01T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-01T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Joe Lycett is back and he is unleashed! He was leashed! Now the leash has been removed, so there is no leash! Don’t come if you love leashes! You will HATE this show if you want someone on a leash! ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Joe Lycett: Do You Really Lycett? Is It, Is It Wicked?","instanceDates":"18 November-19 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"734404ARTBSDVKKTMJHTLSNHHQPSDVSRP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-11-18T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-11-18T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-11-19T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-11-19T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Writer/comedian/actor Joe Mande is currently a Co-EP on the critically-acclaimed HBO Max show Hacks.\r\n\r\nHe also wrote for all four seasons of THE GOOD PLACE on NBC. Other writing credits include three seasons on PARKS AND RECREATION as well as MASTER OF NONE on Netflix, FOREVER on Amazon, and KROLL SHOW on Comedy Central. He has been the featured comedian twice on CONAN, as well as LATE NIGHT WITH SETH MEYERS and numerous Comedy Central programs. Joe’s first comedy album, \"Bitchface,\" was released by Greedhead Records and is available online. His one hour special, JOE MANDE’S AWARD-WINNING COMEDY SPECIAL can be seen on Netflix.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Joe Mande: Hero","instanceDates":"1 April-1 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"435203ANBLBTVQRPBDGPVMGNPDRBRPTKC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-01T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-01T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-01T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-01T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"A good hour of standup by New York comedian Joe Pera, best known for his Adult Swim series, 'Joe Pera Talks With You', which The LA Times referred to as ‘TV’s quietest, most artful comedy’. When the series ended last year after three seasons, Joe returned to his standup roots and has been touring round the US. This will be his first time performing in the UK since 2016. \r\n\r\nJoe has performed his subdued standup on Conan, Late Night with Seth Meyers, and Comedy Central. After his animated special 'Joe Pera Talks You To Sleep' (which many have found to work), he followed up with other projects for Adult Swim including 'Joe Pera Helps You Find the Perfect Christmas Tree' and 'Relaxing Old Footage with Joe Pera'. \r\n\r\n16+ recommendation","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Joe Pera: Spring in the Midwest and Rustbelt Tour Pt IV: SPRING IN THE UK & EUROPE","instanceDates":"17 April-29 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"434803ACQBTTCQJVHQSGPDQRKCMTJRLTP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-17T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-17T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-29T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-29T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Joe and his wife are having a baby. He's autistic so statistically it's quite likely the baby will be too.\r\nIn this new show, critically acclaimed comedian Joe Wells explores fatherhood through the lens of neurodiversity. Plus, there’s a really good joke about a parrot. As seen on: Rosie Jones’ Disability Comedy Extravaganza, BBC Two’s Ouch Storytelling Live and Channel 4’s Jokes Only a Neurodivergent Can Tell. 'Some of the most surprising and thought-provoking material coming from any comedian' (Guardian). Over 20 million online views. 'One of my favourite comics' (Frankie Boyle). ★ ★ ★ ★ ★ (NeurodiverseReview.co.uk). ★ ★ ★ ★ (Chortle.co.uk).16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Joe Wells: Daddy Autism","instanceDates":"19 July-19 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"632603ADJQPRTHNLGHDJMDDRMTGSRRCQM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-19T20:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-19T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-19T20:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-19T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Access","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Access","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Joep Beving is one of the most listened-to living pianists in the world. \r\nIn an astoundingly short amount of time, this incredibly gifted artist has found himself topping the Spotify charts, with over 300 million streams, and more than 2 million monthly listeners.\r\nJoep describes his minimalist and contemplative style as “accessible music for complex emotions”. In an overcrowded music space, he has created a unique and recognisable voice that swims between classical, pop and avant-garde – with massive appeal.\r\nAs well as his solo piano concerts, Joep can perform with acclaimed ensemble, Echo Collective, or Echo Collective and Maarten Vos (modular synth and cello). There is also an option for the addition of the renowned choir, Cappella Amsterdam.\r\nThese performances can be complimented by a simple yet utterly spellbinding light show, developed by Nick Verstand & Boris Acket.\r\nHermetism, the Dutch composer/pianist’s fourth album for Deutsche Grammophon was released globally on 8 April 2022, followed by Vision of Contentment – recorded with Maarten Vos – released on Leiter Verlag in July 2024.\r\n12+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Joep Beving","instanceDates":"8 May-8 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"678603AVDKTGSVRDPKBGJLTCDVJTTQRDT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-08T18:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-08T17:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-08T18:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-08T17:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Music","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":""},{"description":"14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"John C. Reilly is Mr Romantic","instanceDates":"17 November-19 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"637403ADPNRDVGTHHLDGGDDVJNDSRHPVB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-17T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-17T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-19T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-19T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"John Early brings ‘The Album Tour’ to Soho Theatre Walthamstow for his biggest ever London shows. \r\n\r\nJohn is an actor, comedian, writer, and producer. His HBO stand up special, “Now More Than Ever”, was released to critical acclaim in June 2023 and was nominated for a Critic’s Choice Award and Emmy Award. John was also nominated for an Emmy award for his A24 sketch special “Would it Kill You To Laugh” co-created with his frequent collaborator Kate Berlant. \r\n\r\nPreviously John starred in five seasons of the critically acclaimed Max Original series “Search Party” and co-starred in the comedy series “The Afterparty” with Tiffany Haddish. He wrote, starred, and executive produced his own episode of \"The Characters\" and the critically acclaimed web series \"555,\" also with Berlant. In the New York theatre world, he produced a revival of Wallace Shawn's \"Marie and Bruce\" and directed Jacqueline Novak's hit off-Broadway show \"Get On Your Knees.\"\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":100,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"John Early: The Album Tour","instanceDates":"28 May-29 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"581203ADBJVMCVNGTBRVPQJRGQHRGDBDB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-28T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-28T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-29T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-29T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"The Varnishing Days is the heart-stopping, glasses-dropping, hard-rocking, wig-shaking, levothyroxine-taking, knee-knocking, boot-licking, justifying, teeth rattling, digressing new show from stand-up comedian to the stars John Kearns. Go silent as I walk on! Acknowledge when something funny happens! Leave discussing dinner plans! Others will be implicated. Points will be circled and missed. Hell, it’s a man trying his best! When I visit your town dogs will start barking, as will clergy. Your microwave will go haywire. The lights in your vestibule will flicker and the Bank of England will nervously look at interest rates. On the day I write this, the pound has hit an all-time low against the dollar. Mark my words. This show will break that record again and again and again. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"John Kearns: The Varnishing Days","instanceDates":"19 June-24 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"459603ADNPMNGLQPTLJGTRSHPMQNKQPMS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-19T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-19T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-24T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-24T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Tilting at Windmills is the brand-new stand-up show from Taskmaster alumni and double Edinburgh Comedy Award Winner, John Kearns.\r\nA fragmented, digressing portrayal of a 38-year-old man’s life, alluding to books he hasn't read, touching on the modern condition. Plus VAT! More allusive and bleak as ever, it is unreal the comedian you become. And for who? Decent craic with the right crowd. A show for those who have read about but not committed to the Guinness Nitrosurge.  16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"John Kearns: Tilting at Windmills","instanceDates":"11 September-12 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"657603AGGKTNNVLJSPPGVJKRGJVKSNDKM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-11T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-11T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-12T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-12T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"\"Big Year\" is a love story about how a working-class Catholic (or \"Good Guy\" as they call themselves) who grew up during a war in Northern Ireland, tries to get over the lessons he learned to get tough and survive when he meets and falls for a stunningly beautiful, privately educated, Middle Eastern Muslim lady who needs more than the strong silent type\r\nRolling Stone magazine picked “Big Year” as one of their stand out shows of the year, calling it ‘…a furious, tender, brutal, loving and most of all hilarious hour that confounds your presumptions at every turn’, and called John ‘The next great Irish Comedian’\r\nDirected by comedy sensation Vittorio Angelone, Big Year played to sold-out crowds and critical acclaim at Edinburgh fringe 2024.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"John Meagher: Big Year","instanceDates":"15 February-15 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"588203AJGNNVBNTNGRHVLQLSLPPPGBJBP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-15T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-15T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-15T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-15T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"In a world where masculinity is dying, John Reynolds and Carmen Christopher are becoming stronger. Their brains are growing and their abs are just starting to come in. They have never cried and literally don't mess with anxiety. Their show follows two men who fit in seamlessly with the modern world. Most men only have the mental capacity to do one form of comedy, but Carmen & John, who didn't even go to school, seamlessly blend stand up, sketches, characters, and improv to prove once and for all... men can do it all.\r\nJohn Reynolds is an actor and comedian known for his performances in Search Party (HBOMAX) and Stranger Things (Netflix). He can be seen in the upcoming season of Yellowjackets on Showtime. \r\nCarmen Christopher is an actor, writer, and comedian. His stand up special, Street Special, is streaming on Peacock. He’s has recurring roles on The Bear (FX), Killing It (Peacock), and Joe Pera Talks to You (HBO Max). He’s a staff writer on the upcoming Nathan Fielder and Safdie Brothers project The Curse (Showtime).\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"John Reynolds & Carmen Christopher present - No Tengo Escuela","instanceDates":"11 July-15 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"475603ATHQQQGTQQMQVPBRCJLTQBVNRVH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-11T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-11T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-15T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-15T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Thank God you’re here. John Tothill has missed you so much. It’s actually been hell without you.\r\nA rat who orgasmed to death. The notion of Marmite. The time John deliberately got malaria. We’ve got a lot to catch up on.\r\n\r\nPour yourself six glasses of wine and settle in for an evening that, god-willing, won’t end. Maybe we could even have the tiniest cigarette??\r\n\r\nChortle's Best Newcomer nominee 2024. One of 2023’s Best-Reviewed Edinburgh Fringe Shows (British Comedy Guide). As seen on Comedy Central Live.\r\n\r\nDirected by Alex Cartlidge and Kathryn Craigmyle.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"John Tothill: Thank God This Lasts Forever","instanceDates":"14 October-1 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"567203ALPNKQCGRSJPGLQCDJJKVLJCTLR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-14T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-14T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-01T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-01T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"“one of the most brilliantly funny night’s of this year’s Fringe… potentially the best newcomer we’ve seen in recent times” ★★★★★ – To Do List\r\nJoin John Tothill, the Last Living Libertine [citation needed], for an evening of exaggeration, emancipation and dense theoretical speculation in a show that straddles cabaret and TEDTalk (also known as stand-up comedy).\r\nDon't be shy, fill full your cups with this debut hour all about pleasure, performed by a gushing bon vivant to an audience of conventionally attractive comedy-goers.\r\nFeaturing almost exclusively sleepover-style gossip, dressed up in a way that feels more important than that (but isn't).\r\nDirected by and dedicated to Adam Brace.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"John Tothill: The Last Living Libertine","instanceDates":"22 January-9 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"501203AKDKTTBRCHJVJVSBBQSLMCJSJBQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-22T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-22T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-09T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-09T22:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"In 2024, John Tothill's appendix burst onstage, just days after Trump was almost assassinated. Both men claimed that these near-death experiences changed them. Both were lying. Now join John in his own personal paradise as he attempts to monetise what body parts he has left. 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"John Tothill: This Must Be Heaven","instanceDates":"6 October-7 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"649203AVPRJBJQGTKDVSSKCBVVNKKGHHK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-06T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-06T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-07T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-07T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Once upon a time I was the best blurb writer in the business – really, I was a wonder! But as time weighed down on me and all my afternoons began to expand and contract, I started to lose my touch. At first it was just the odd phrase I couldn't manage, but soon enough I couldn't seem to come up with anything longer than a sentence or two, and certainly nothing with any great detail. Now it's all I can do to say 'come see this show,' and even that takes me half the morning.\r\n \r\nIn their 5* review of Catland, Chortle described him as ‘a truly singular mind and talent’ and having ‘qualities that are both sorcerous and plaintive.’\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Johnny White Really-Really: Catland","instanceDates":"5 April-6 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"536003ANSSKPRCVRMNCRQKSLKTCNHPBBD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-05T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-05T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-06T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-06T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jon Ronson Book Add-on","instanceDates":"27 September-27 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"680003ASDPDNCQJPTPSVRNTSSCCHBVRTK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-27T14:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-27T13:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-27T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-27T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Following a box-office busting, sell-out tour in 2024, Jon Ronson’s Psychopath Night comes to Soho Theatre Walthamstow \r\nWhat happens when a psychopath is in power? Could you learn to spot a psychopath? Are you working for a psychopath? Is there a little bit of psychopath in all us? \r\nSixteen years have passed since Jon embarked on the adventure that became his ground-breaking and best-selling work, The Psychopath Test. Now, the renowned journalist, filmmaker, and author reopens the case with exclusive anecdotes and fresh reflections, taking you on a thrilling exploration of madness and the elusive psychopathic mind.\r\nJoin Jon in 2025 for another electrifying journey into the enigmatic world of psychopaths and the perplexing concept of normalcy. In an age where society’s rationality is called into question, Jon will deliver an evening of incisive inquiry, seasoned with his trademark wit and profound insights.\r\nThis unmissable show prominently features mystery special guests whose extraordinary, twist-filled true tales are central to the story but not found in the original edition of the book. The less you know about them, the better…\r\nDon’t miss this unforgettable night of revelation, intrigue, and mind-bending insights. With a chance to ask Jon your own questions… Book your tickets now before they’re gone!\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jon Ronson’s Psychopath Night 2025","instanceDates":"5 November-5 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"604603ATPPCJRGLPTVBBVDJCNSMPLSRMV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-05T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-05T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-05T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-05T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Inspired by the Book of Jonah–and probably God–award\r\n-winning Shunt artist Simon Kane presents his hugely acclaimed, horrifyingly evergreen divine comedy about the extremist in all of us: “Jonah Non Grata”– an exciting biblical adventure in which YOU are the hero, played by HIM!\r\nFun hymns! Tiny Stunts! Is it a church for a churchless faith? Is it a loud man getting things wrong?\r\nSEE the unmapped complexities of the human soul brought to stupid life!\r\nSEE a man on a plane!\r\nSEE something in the corner!\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jonah Non Grata","instanceDates":"21 June-21 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"615803AHTVKTQMRRLMTRRGSJBJQHKNLPS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-21T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-21T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-21T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-21T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The Oxford English Dictionary describes a corpse as (1) a body or (2) spoiling a performance by laughing.\r\nJonathan Oldfield will be using both definitions in his critically acclaimed debut show of exquisitely silly character comedy. Creator and star of BBC Radio 4's award-winning Time of the Week. NextUp Biggest Award in Comedy nominee 2026. BBC New Comedy Awards finalist. Director of Lorna Rose Treen and Joe Kent-Walters. You also may have seen him in Star Wars: Andor or online in those sketches someone sent to you. Directed by John-Luke Roberts.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jonathan Oldfield: Exquisite Corpse","instanceDates":"30 November-5 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"749403AGCKLDHGSCDGTHJDDPCCTVVTTKR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-30T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-30T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-05T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-05T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Award-winning comedian Jonny Pelham is newly single, he’s moved to London and is being encouraged by the government to take speed every day.\r\nIs It Me? is a hilarious new stand-up show looking at what it means to be diagnosed as 'neurodiverse,' what constitutes normality and how to find happiness in a world that’s falling apart. As seen on Live at the Apollo, Mock the Week and Alan Davies: As Yet Untitled.16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jonny Pelham: Is It Me?","instanceDates":"11 May-12 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"682803ACQPKCMBKVJHQPLLDMGSJQNMKMJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-11T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-11T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-12T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-12T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Jonny Woo is back at Soho Theatre with his most personal show to date.\r\nSuburbia is return to his spoken word, story-telling and performance art roots - a poetic memoir charting his life from a childhood in Medway to the (sex) clubs of New York to a queer community in London. \r\nNow in his fifties, Woo is more reflective and honest about the secrets he harboured and the lessons he has learnt. His journey has been the subject of previous solo shows, but is Jonny Woo now ready to bare all? Knowing Woo, probably (wink wink). \r\nWoo’s wit is as sharp as ever and his desire to shock and surprise is evident throughout. Suburbia is everything but suburban.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jonny Woo: Suburbia","instanceDates":"14 January-25 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"579803AQHSDCBRDRPHRRCVLJDGBQGSDVK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-14T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-14T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-25T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-25T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Drag","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Jonny Woo is back at Soho Theatre with his most personal show to date.\r\nSuburbia, Jonny Woo’s critically acclaimed theatrical memoir returns to Soho Theatre after a sell-out run in 2025 and an award-winning season at The Edinburgh Fringe. \r\nA return to his performance art, cabaret and story-telling roots, Suburbia charts his life from a childhood in Medway to the 90’s rave scene of London and the (sex) clubs and drag bars of 00’s New York. \r\nHaving toured the UK and with two O ie nominations, this is Suburbia: Re-Loaded. New theatricality; greater intimacy; fresh choreography and re-vamped songs. Woo’s wit, honesty and desire to shock remain evident throughout but Suburbia: Re-Loaded hits harder, deeper and will stay with you long after the disco lights fade. \r\nBrighton Fringe Award for Excellence at Edinburgh Fringe 2025 \r\nOffie Award Nominee – Performance 2026 \r\nOffie Award Nominee – Production 2026 \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jonny Woo: Suburbia Re-Loaded","instanceDates":"13 July-25 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"727403ALNCPQCLTLBVCBTGQQHCNSTLQLP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-13T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-13T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-25T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-25T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Drag","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Earlybird tickets now on sale.\r\nBook now for the best price.\r\nLineup TBA.\r\nAfter a storming 2025 in Walthamstow, London’s major spectacle celebrating the cream of alternative performance, comedy, dance, drag, pop music and poppers. Jonny Woo’s Un-Royal Variety is back\r\n\r\nWoo curates and hosts a glorious punk pastiche of the classic ‘Royal Variety’ with a rocking in-house band, a dazzling dance troupe and a line-up of some of the best and wildest acts from Soho Theatre’s stella roster of acts alongside Woo’s own gaggle of cult collaborators.\r\n \r\nPrevious guests on the Un-Royal bill have included: Peaches, Betty Boo, Dina Martina, David McAlmont, Myra Dubois, Jayde Adams, Coco the Gogo, Ivo Dimchev, Dr Adam Perchard, Fi McClusky, Garry Star, Lisette Krol, Bolly Illusion, Camille Leon, Mr IPM, Leah Shelton, John Sizzle, A Man To Pet, Adrienne Truscott, CHRISTEENE, Mawaan Rizwan, Pete and Bambi, Lucy McCormick, Diane Chorley, La Gateau Chocolat, Robyn Herfellow, Lavinia Co-Op, Seayonce, Freida Slaves, Bourgeois & Maurice and a giant bottle of poppers.\r\n\r\n18+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":150,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jonny Woo’s Unroyal Variety","instanceDates":"26 November-28 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"687003APVHTRLCKTGHVPDNQPMDLCQMVCM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-26T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-26T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-28T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-28T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Drag","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Comedy"},{"description":"It’s back. London’s wildest spectacle of alternative performance, comedy and drag. Jonny Woo’s Un-Royal Variety. The show brilliantly un-fit for The King.\r\nIt’s been seven years since alt-drag megastar Jonny Woo unleashed this beast of a show and now it has a new home, Soho Theatre Walthamstow, a spectacular restoration of an historic music venue, where for three consecutive nights the lovely new roof will be officially raised with gasps, laughs and roars of un-adulterated joy.\r\n\r\nWoo curates and hosts this glorious punk pastiche of the classic ‘Royal Variety’ with a rocking in-house band, a dazzling dance troupe and a line-up of some of the best and wildest acts from Soho Theatre’s stella rostra of acts and Woo’s own gaggle of brilliant collaborators.\r\n\r\nPrevious guests on the ‘Un-Royal’ bill have included: Adrienne Truscott, CHRISTEENE, Mawaan Rizwan, Myra Dubois, Leah Shelton, Pete and Bambi, Jayde Adams, Lucy McCormick, Diane Chorley, La Gateau Chocolat, Lavinia Co-Op, Freida Slaves and Bourgeois & Maurice.\r\n\r\nA highlight has always been the community choir masquerading as ‘The Kate Middleton Choir’ or ‘The Theresa May Singers’. Watch this space for the 2025 Walthamstow call out and your chance to win a coveted spot in the ‘Un-Royal Box’.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":150,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jonny Woo’s Un-Royal Variety 2025","instanceDates":"13 November-15 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"598203ARGJDNHLDMHDJGJCGMSQGSCKQJT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-13T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-13T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-15T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-15T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Drag","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Comedy"},{"description":"Definitely a musical\r\nThe world is obsessed with turning everything into entertainment, finding new stories to tell in a feverish desire to ensure every moment in human history has been thrown onto the bonfire of spectacle.\r\n\r\nJordan Brookes has taken a different approach, and turned back towards one of the original moneymaker tragedies in the biz - the Titanic.\r\n\r\nConvinced there's something previously undiscovered, he's gone on an obsessive deep dive to prove there's life in the old ship yet, and by extension, him.\r\n\r\nCan he find something original to say about the most well-worn topic of all time?\r\n\r\nOr will he have to make something up?\r\n\r\nA full-blown (sort of) musical spectacular featuring a star-studded (sort of) cast from the Edinburgh Comedy Award Winner 2019\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jordan Brookes: Fontanelle","instanceDates":"13 February-1 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"576003ANJTLKKQTJCCCQVGQNNQPLJBGGS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-13T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-13T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-01T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-01T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"After a sell-out run earlier this year, the longest-reigning Edinburgh Comedy Award winner in history is back at Soho Theatre. The award-winning Elvis of comedy continues his residency at the gates of hell, with a new show inspired by an absolutely shocking incident on a train. Have you ever felt seen and unseen at the same time? Have you ever wondered what’s lurking just in the corner of your vision? Yeah me too, what is that? What IS that???\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jordan Brookes: The Part of You That’s Always Screaming","instanceDates":"5 October-10 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"742603AQRRSQLNGCSVTMTBLSGPVSPBSJG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-05T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-05T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-10T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-10T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A brand-new show from the longest-reigning Edinburgh Comedy Award winner in history.\r\nThe award-winning Elvis of comedy continues his residency at the gates of hell, with a new show inspired by an absolutely shocking incident on a train. \r\n\r\nHave you ever felt seen and unseen at the same time? Have you ever wondered what’s lurking just in the corner of your vision? Yeah me too, what is that? What IS that???\r\n\r\nAs seen on The Russell Howard Show, The Mash Report, Avoidance and Alice and Steve.\r\n\r\nTop 3 Comedy Shows of 2024 | Guardian\r\nBest Shows at Edinburgh Fringe 2024 | The i\r\nThe 50 funniest comedians of the 21st century | Telegraph\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jordan Brookes: The Part of You That’s Always Screaming.","instanceDates":"26 May-30 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"696803ABHDGRLDBKVBPGPVLTKGVGPPBPH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-26T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-26T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-30T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-30T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A new work-in-progress show from the longest reigning Edinburgh Comedy Award winner (2019-2021). Expect the usual mix of stand-up, clowning and utterly stupid ideas presented as if they mean anything. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jordan Brookes: Work in Progress","instanceDates":"23 November-25 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"508003AGQDPQBPGRMNNKHSDLHJJKDJBCH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-23T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-23T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-25T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-25T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"When Jordan stripped off live on Channel 4 (and won a BAFTA in the process), bigots around the globe went ballistic. Luckily… so were her tits.\r\nFollowing acclaimed runs in London and Edinburgh, the multi-award-winning star and creator of ITV’s Transaction hits the road with a guitar on her back, a bounty on her ballbag, and some very poorly written death threats in her DMs.\r\n\r\nWhen Jordan stripped off live on Channel 4 (and won a BAFTA in the process), bigots around the globe went ballistic. Luckily… so were her tits.\r\n\r\nIs the cost of success worth it? How do you live up to your own sky-high expectations? And most importantly, should you even be a comedian when your bum looks this good? Join Jordan as she explores all this and more in her rootinest, tootinest, shootinest hour of musical comedy yet.\r\n\r\nEdinburgh Fringe Best Show - Nominee\r\nMelbourne International Comedy Fest Best Show - Nominee\r\nChannel 4 Breakthrough Comedy Star - Winner\r\nNextUp Biggest Award In Comedy -  Winner\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":100,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jordan Gray: Is That A C*ck In Your Pocket, Or Are You Just Here To Kill Me?","instanceDates":"20 March-20 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"675803ASJGLTDSQLRMNPBBQBQLDLCLGDV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-20T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-20T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-20T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-20T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Critically acclaimed, multi-genre comedian Joseph Morpurgo brings his first new show in nine years to Soho Theatre.\r\nA decade ago, Joseph discovered something in a car boot sale. Something old, something ordinary, something mundane. But all is not as it seems. Is it ever? In Highlander 70, “the UK’s foremost alchemist of “found” comedy and irreverent, cross-media mash-up humour” (Scotsman) excavates the past and brings the audience along for the ride, with the help of some physical media, animation… and, of course, the good folks at Jim's Steak and Spaghetti House.\r\n\r\nJoseph Morpurgo is an award-winning writer and comedian. Since debuting at the Edinburgh Fringe in 2013 with his breakout hit Truthmouth, he has gone on to create the boundary-stretching, convention-flouting and hugely acclaimed comedy shows Odessa (2014), Soothing Sounds For Baby (2015) and Hammerhead (2017). He is also a founder member of improv show Austentatious – one of the UK’s biggest and best known improv shows, currently resident in London’s West End.\r\n\r\nOutside of his live work, his broadcast credits include Harry and Paul’s Story of the 2s (BBC2), Murder in Successville (BBC3), and Drunk History (Comedy Central). He was Lead Writer on the preschool series Ready Eddie Go, and has written on multiple Aardman projects, including the International Emmy Kids winner Shaun The Sheep: Adventures From Mossy Bottom. He co-created Radio 4 series The Ultimate Choice; wrote and starred in his own show, Joseph Morpurgo’s Walking Tour; and has worked with Warp Films, Baby Cow, Blink, Fudge Park, and more.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Joseph Morpurgo: Highlander 70","instanceDates":"29 September-17 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"715203ADQJHKKPTPHRMMHGKCCHJPMCVCM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-29T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-29T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-17T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-17T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Ten years after he stormed the Edinburgh Fringe, Joseph Morpurgo is set to revive his iconic, wildly acclaimed hour of excavated vinyl and throttled hyperkonzept, Soothing Sounds for Baby.\r\nJoseph has been invited onto Desert Island Discs. He has dressed up and picked his eight records. Should be exciting, right? The truth is this will be one of the most awkward experiences he's ever had.\r\n\r\nSoothing Sounds For Baby was nominated for Best Show at the Edinburgh Comedy Awards 2015, was named Best Show of 2015 by Time Out, and won three Chortle Awards. The Guardian described it as \"one of the decade’s finest fringe comedy shows”.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Joseph Morpurgo: Soothing Sounds for Baby","instanceDates":"8 December-20 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"659403ACHMKGGKKBQTHKGCMRNSSTJGVRS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-08T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-08T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-20T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-20T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Most mothers expect to help guide their child through puberty. But when your son is autistic, it's a whole different story.\r\n\r\nWelcome to Josephine's world. Expect visual aids, balloons, and a heartwarming insight into the relationship between mother and son, both determined to figure it out together.\r\n\r\nFrom Chortle's One To Watch (2023) and Leicester Mercury Comedian of the Year nominee (2023).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Josephine Lacey: Austism Mama.","instanceDates":"11 November-16 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"552403AJTLHCNNSBGTTGDVGDDLBBBBQSR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-11T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-11T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-16T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-16T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The five star smash hit show returns to Soho Theatre one final time. \r\n\r\nMost mothers expect to help guide their child through puberty. But when your son is autistic, it's a whole different story.\r\n\r\nWelcome to Josephine's world. Expect visual aids, balloons, and a heartwarming insight into the relationship between mother and son, both determined to figure it out together.\r\n\r\nFrom Chortle's One To Watch (2023) and Leicester Mercury Comedian of the Year nominee (2023).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Josephine Lacey: Autism Mama","instanceDates":"24 November-24 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"634003AQTDVMVRQHDKLVBSRMQSCPRCTNH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-24T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-24T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-24T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-24T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Most mothers expect to help guide their child through puberty. But when your son is autistic, it's a whole different story.\r\n\r\nWelcome to Josephine's world. Expect visual aids, balloons, and a heartwarming insight into the relationship between mother and son, both determined to figure it out together.\r\n\r\nFrom Chortle's One To Watch (2023) and Leicester Mercury Comedian of the Year nominee (2023).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Josephine Lacey: Autism Mama (Edinburgh preview)","instanceDates":"18 July-24 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"552203AMBCCDJHNJVTTRTNTLVSRJCJDNG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-18T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-18T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-24T21:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-24T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Welcome to the world of a mother, caring for a pubescent teenager - who happens to be autistic. \r\n\r\nSoho Theatre are delighted to welcome back Josephine Lacey’s fascinating and hilarious stand-up show about a single mum, guiding her autistic son through the first stages of puberty. Expect visual aids, balloons, and a heart-warming insight into the relationship between a mother and her son. \r\n\r\nOne to watch 2023 – Chortle\r\nLeicester Mercury Comedian of the Year 2023 - Nominee\r\n“Josephine is a comedy bombshell - watch an audience react as she explodes on stage.” – BBC\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Josephine Lacey: Autism Mama and Puberty.","instanceDates":"9 May-10 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"443603ANTJRHBSGKHJRLJCCLCHVRRBHKG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-09T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-09T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-10T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-10T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Access"},{"description":"The Last Comic Standing champ and star of America’s Got Talent comes to Soho Theatre for one night only.\r\nFollowing his ground-breaking win on Last Comic Standing, Josh Blue has risen through the ranks to become a well-established headliner all over the world - performing over 200 shows a year and continuing to spread laughter and break down stereotypes of people with disabilities along the way. His stand-up routine is in a constant state of evolution and his off-the-cuff improvisational skills guarantee that no two shows are alike.\r\n\r\nJosh placed 3rd in the 2021 season of NBC’s America’s Got Talent and followed it up with another 3rd placed finish on America’s Got Talent: All-Stars in 2023. He performed a stand-out set on The Tonight Show starring Jimmy Fallon and was honoured with a performance at the William H. Macy Gala at the prestigious Just for Laughs Comedy Festival in Montreal, Canada.\r\n\r\nJosh has represented the United States in 8 countries as a member of the US Paralympic Soccer Team. Josh and his team were thoroughly disgraced in the 2004 Paralympic Games in Athens, Greece by not scoring a single goal!\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Josh Blue: The Freak Accident Tour","instanceDates":"8 June-8 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"553603ANMPRHTKJHNJCHTPVDHLLGMNGPV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-08T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-08T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-08T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-08T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Aussie oddball Josh Glanc is back at Soho Theatre. Fresh from a completely sold-out Edinburgh Fringe run and a nomination for the Comedians Choice Award. \r\nAussie oddball Josh Glanc is back at Soho Theatre. Fresh from a completely sold-out Edinburgh Fringe run and a nomination for the Comedians Choice Award.  Don't miss it. Or do. I don't really mind. I'm just the guy he pays to write the copy. Shit. I shouldn't have written that. Damn. I shouldn't have written that either. [note: come back and delete]. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Josh Glanc: Collections 2023","instanceDates":"30 November-2 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"504203ANJRQGSTMSMKTKNKRGHVTPNRJVB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-30T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-30T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-02T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-02T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Nominated for the 2024 Edinburgh Comedy Award, the Aussie oddball doles out original songs, tender crowd-work, and a wackily inventive absurdism all his own. Listed by Rolling Stone Magazine as one of the stand-out shows from this year's Edinburgh Fringe. Don't miss it. Or do. I don't really mind. I'm just the guy who writes his copy. In fact, I'm going to write whatever I want. Lalablahabal yimmsdfi yimmo yoooo. Bing Bong Baaahh.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Josh Glanc: Family Man","instanceDates":"18 July-19 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"627203ALSLDGQPKJCDTMHBJCKLPDJRNPS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-18T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-18T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-19T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-19T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Straight off the back of his smash hit, sold out Edinburgh Fringe run, Josh Glanc returns to Soho Theatre. \r\nNominated for the 2024 Edinburgh Comedy Award, the Aussie oddball doles out original songs, tender crowd-work, and a wackily inventive absurdism all his own. Listed by Rolling Stone Magazine as one of the stand-out shows from this year's Edinburgh Fringe. Don't miss it. Or do. I don't really mind. I'm just the guy who writes his copy.  In fact, I'm going to write whatever I want. Lalablahabal yimmsdfi yimmo yoooo. Bing Bong Baaahh.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Josh Glanc: Family Man 2024","instanceDates":"30 September-5 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"569004ACHNPNSSTBDQNPSNNQJQMKLSQVK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-30T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-30T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-05T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-05T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Josh Glanc is making a brand new show. It’s not finished and he doesn’t know what it will be called, but he really wants to show you some of it.\r\nHe might read from a script. \r\nHe might improvise.\r\nWhatever happens, it’ll be very fun.\r\nNominated for the Edinburgh Comedy Award, he’s been on the Melbourne Comedy Festival Galas (ABC), Utopia (Network 10) and the Stand Up Sketch Show (UK). He was called “bonkers brilliant” by the Sydney Morning Herald and “an extraordinary talent” by The Scotsman.\r\nThere will be live accompaniment.\r\nThis new show is really exciting.\r\nHe would love you to come.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Josh Glanc: Work-in-progress show","instanceDates":"2 June-2 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"714203ADMLMJSKKNPMJMDVHGTKDJLBDRD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-02T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-02T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-02T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-02T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Josh Johnson brings The Flowers Tour to Soho Theatre Walthamstow for his first ever UK show.\r\nWith nearly 4 million followers across his social media, Josh Johnson was recently called “the funniest guy on the internet” by WIRED and is a star on the rise. He is an Emmy-nominated writer, stand-up comedian, actor, and NAACP award-winner from Louisiana by way of Chicago.\r\nJohnson is currently a correspondent on Comedy Central’s Emmy & Peabody Award-winning program The Daily Show where he was previously a writer for the past seven years. Johnson is also a former writer and performer on NBC’s The Tonight Show Starring Jimmy Fallon, where he made his late-night debut in 2017.\r\nHis most recent stand-up special, Josh Johnson: Up Here Killing Myself, premiered on Peacock earlier this year to rave reviews touting Josh as a “naturally gifted story teller”. This year alone, Josh has released over 24 hours of stand up, and the content on his YouTube channel has been viewed over 140 million times by people all over the world.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Josh Johnson: The Flowers Tour","instanceDates":"23 May-24 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"601803AHHBJQGVTMCJHQDBLTTGTLQRTSH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-23T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-23T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-24T14:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-24T13:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Josh Sharp’s ta-da! is a one-man comedy show inside of a manic 2,000 slide PowerPoint. Expect dumb but erudite jokes and sad but sweet stories alongside the Herculean feat of stupidity that is memorizing a slide every 2.1 seconds.\r\nFresh from a twice extended run off-Broadway, ta-da! is a one-man comedy show inside of a manic 2,000 slide PowerPoint. Expect dumb but erudite jokes and sad but sweet stories joined with the Herculean feat of stupidity that is memorising a slide every 2.1 seconds. \r\n\r\nAt its core, the show is an exploration of mortality and identity. Across the hour, Josh will tackle the ridiculous and the profound: getting a hand job under a bridge, trying to be a teen magician while deeply closeted and the best way to come out (a bcc email).\r\n\r\nDirected by the Tony Award-winning  director of Oh, Mary! Sam Pinkleton.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Josh Sharp: ta-da!","instanceDates":"9 February-7 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"682003AGVCNQMRHKGSLLHSJPNNCVJMTGK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-09T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-09T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-07T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-07T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Join Josh as he warms up ahead of his brand-new nationwide tour later this year.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Josh Widdicombe: Work in Progress","instanceDates":"5 March-5 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"610803ATTPBLLBRKGTQPRLGHMJTLQHQSS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-05T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-05T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-05T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-05T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Work In Progress","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Joshua Bethania is an award-winning comedian from India. His stand-up includes observations on life in London as an outsider and what he is doing to become an insider.\r\nA Work-in-progress for Joshua’s debut hour. Come see him try to find meaning forcefully in life experiences because that’s what we’re told to do especially being an Indian, an Immigrant, a Christian which makes him a minority wherever he goes. As seen on BBC, Channel 4 and Comedy Central\r\nWinner of ‘So You Think You're Funny?’, BBC New Comedy Awards Finalist, King Gong winner and NATYS Finalist. \r\n\r\nAs seen on Channel 4, OFTV and Comedy Central\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Joshua Bethania: Work in Progress","instanceDates":"9 February-9 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"521603AHQKHSLTRQMNRQVPNDHNLQQNSMR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-09T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-09T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-09T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-09T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"A new show about extinct gigantic, charismatic, megafauna from three-time Edinburgh Comedy Award nominee and very good comedian Josie Long.\r\nIn these troubled times, in this wicked world, it can feel like apocalypse is everywhere but did you know 11,000 years ago there were some really big armadillos? I’m talking about as big as a car. Really big. And they were vegetarian so don’t even worry about them. \r\n\r\nAlso my daughter has a hamster and I’m not saying distract yourself from everything, but I’m saying he’s also part of everything. \r\n\r\nJosie is back with a new show about discovery, wonder, extinction and how to walk through a landscape of monstrous disaster. There is also a good tip about silt, guaranteed.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":80,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Josie Long: Now Is The Time Of Monsters","instanceDates":"8 November-8 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"600804AKHRSMRPVLQTDGHJNRKTBVVMPCH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-08T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-08T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-08T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-08T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Political","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Twenty years ago, Hugh Jackman was offered the role of the\r\nPhantom of the Opera, a role that multi-award-winning\r\ncomedy legend/idiot Joz Norris has dreamed about his entire\r\nlife. Jackman turned it down. Now, an artist known for taking\r\nhimself way too seriously, despite his creative output\r\nconsisting of utter nonsense, will play another one playing\r\nanother one in this musical extravaganza that will reset the\r\ncourse of history. 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Joz Norris Is Hugh Jackman Is The Phantom of the  Opera (Work in Progress)","instanceDates":"28 August-29 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"735203ANKSVKSNPHGSQQMNKVVTLQLHJNR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-28T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-28T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-29T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-29T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Work In Progress","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"After his sell-out, five-star run at the Edinburgh Fringe, Comedians Choice Award Winner Joz Norris has finally completed his life's work and he's ready to unveil it to the world. But what exactly is it? How much has it cost him? And now that he's done it, what will he do next? A \"demented, meticulous, oddly moving\" (*****Distrupt) new show about ambition, closure and moving on, from the creator and star of BBC Radio 4's The Dream Factory. \"This is Norris' Mona Lisa...thoughtful purpose underpinning laughs upon ridiculous laughs.\"(***** Chortle)16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Joz Norris: You Wait. Time Passes.","instanceDates":"8 April-11 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"672203ACMSMNNJKBPKSNSNGCKKBVKLGSJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-08T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-08T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-11T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-11T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Straight off his sell-out, five-star run at the Edinburgh Fringe, Comedians Choice Award Winner Joz Norris has finally completed his life's work and he's ready to unveil it to the world. But what exactly is it? How much has it cost him? And now that he's done it, what will he do next? A \"demented, meticulous, oddly moving\" (*****Distrupt) new show about ambition, closure and moving on, from the creator and star of BBC Radio 4's The Dream Factory. \"This is Norris' Mona Lisa...thoughtful purpose underpinning laughs upon ridiculous laughs.\"(***** Chortle)\r\nBritish Comedy Guide recommended\r\nWow Awards: Best Comedy - WINNER\r\nThe Biggest Award in Comedy - NOMINEE\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Joz Norris: You Wait. Time Passes.[sep25]","instanceDates":"17 September-20 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"653803AGDKTNDHTDBDJCLGSSCCGRKKMNJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-17T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-17T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-20T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-20T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"One of the best-reviewed and most in-demand debut shows of this year's Edinburgh Fringe: an absurd homage to migration, in which a hungry Eastern European clown voyages to America for a hot dog. Choosh, by the way, means 'bullshit' - of all kinds. \r\n\r\nDramaturg: Annie Siddons\r\nSound Design: Jonny Woolley\r\n★★★★★ 'This has to be seen to be believed, delightful from beginning to end' London Theatre 1\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Julia Masli: Choosh!","instanceDates":"26 April-29 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"434203ABSCVQPVGNTMMBGGSNRBMDSBRLG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-26T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-26T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-29T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-29T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"hahahahahahahahahaha hahahahahahaha hihihi hahahahahahahaha hoho hahahhahahaha hehe hahahahahahahahahaha. 'Ha' (Guardian).\r\nFrom the legs behind the sell-out hit shows Legs, Logs, and Choosh! Winner of the Malcolm Hardee Award for Comic Originality and The Telegraph's Best Sad Clown Award. Off West End Theatre Award nominee. \r\n★★★★★ Guardian \r\n★★★★★ Chortle\r\n★★★★ Scotsman\r\n★★★★ Telegraph\r\n★★★★ Times\r\n★★★★ Skinny\r\n★★★★ List\r\n★★★★ Fest Mag\r\n★★★★ Funny Women\r\n16+ ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Julia Masli: ha ha ha ha ha ha ha","instanceDates":"30 January-11 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"493803ATMSHSBPTNBRPNRTKQSTVTJDBKM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-30T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-30T21:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-11T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-11T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Emmy®-nominated, Peabody Award and WGA-winning writer, director and comedian Julio Torres comes to Soho Theatre for strictly limited run.\r\nHot on the heels of his directorial feature Problemista (in which he stars opposite Tilda Swinton), and his six-part HBO series Fantasmas (“a beacon of hope for TV’s future” ★★★★★ – The Guardian), Julio brings his brand-new live show to Soho for its first ever UK dates.\r\n \r\nHis Peabody, GLAAD and Dorian Award-winning series Los Espookys was named one of New York Times’ Best TV Shows of 2022, and his stand-up special My Favorite Shapes was released on HBO in 2019. Named one of TIME Magazine’s TIME100 Next Artists in 2023, Julio received four Emmy® nominations for his work on Saturday Night Live, on which he has served as a writer from 2016 to 2021. He can also be seen in Search Party, The Great North, Shrill, Together Together, and The Other Two.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Julio Torres: Color Theories","instanceDates":"11 August-16 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"638803AHPVJJVSGDHHGRQVMRCRJBVLLKS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-11T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-11T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-16T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-16T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"\"Is it a bird? Is it a plane? No, it's Juno Birch, the hilariously outlandish blue alien who’d love nothing more than to speak to the manager of EarthJuno crash lands into Soho Theatre and probes the absurdity of life on this planet, in her one woman stand-up comedy show Probed.\r\n\r\nExpect jumbo hair, jarring fashion and hysterical jokes from the extra-terrestrial icon all the way from the distant planet of Manchester as she shares her struggles of life through the lens of her little pink sunglasses.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Juno Birch: Probed","instanceDates":"5 November-16 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"569603ACDVRBVTMRVNKGMPMPGCLVPSJCJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-05T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-05T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-16T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-16T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"A vicious new comedy about disinformation and dinosaurs\r\nA late-night screening of a certain Steven Spielberg classic causes carnage on a university campus. What starts as a misunderstanding about the film quickly spirals into mass redundancies and bizarre conspiracies. The fight for academic survival is on! A ridiculous satire about fake news and fossils, written by Bruntwood Prize-winning playwright Tim Foley (“A striking talent” - The Guardian).\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Jurassic by Tim Foley","instanceDates":"18 November-29 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"638403ASSKJPQNRKCCVDRGVRSTVTDBCRT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-18T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-18T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-29T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-29T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Justin Vivian Bond: Sex With Strangers","instanceDates":"11 July-12 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"625803AJDGTTBSCVRJJBBCHTMSHSLNDJR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-11T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-11T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-12T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-12T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Multi Award-winning stand-up, podcaster and author, Kai has so far toured live in 53 countries with Daniel Sloss, opening in massive theatres and arenas all over the world. Co-star of the brilliantly funny podcast 'Sloss and Humphries on the Road', Kai is also an author, producer and has created and toured eight solo shows around Australia and even to off-Broadway in New York. One of the UK’s very best stand-ups, catch Kai in his natural element - live, up close and hilarious.\r\n \r\n‘Absolutely brilliant… Pure stand-up… honest, relatable and upbeat, you can’t help but like him… Fabulous’ ★★★★ Voice Mag\r\n\r\n‘Phenomenally funny… A fantastic comic who is smart, funny, and crude all at once…  perpetually upbeat charisma, pushing and pulling us between laughter and empathy… Not to be missed… Brilliant!’ Broadway Baby \r\n\r\n‘Superb!... had folk almost falling off their chairs… collapsing with laughter.’  Fife Today\r\n\r\n‘Sunny friendliness and impossible likeability that makes his rude humour feel mischievous and thoroughly inoffensive… hilarious!' Three Weeks\r\n\r\n‘It’s always an awesome experience when a performer just nails it – this Geordie comedian gets it so right from the very beginning, it’s an amazing experience… a festival highlight’ ★★★★★ Australia Times\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kai Humphries: Mischief!","instanceDates":"26 May-27 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"440003ACTMBRDMTPTHDCDMPDDGNKBDDRC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-26T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-26T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-27T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-27T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Following his critically acclaimed debut and Soho Theatre Live Amazon comedy special, award-winning comedian Kai Samra is back with an hour about race, class, immigration, youth homelessness, India and, more importantly, 2010 indie-rock bands. \r\n\r\n'A charismatic man with a great story and the chops to tell it' (Chortle.co.uk). \r\n'It's genuinely exciting to imagine what Samra will achieve' ★★★★★ (Edinburgh Festivals Magazine). \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kai Samra: Native","instanceDates":"15 May-15 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"467603AQMVTKBTJTTMSTCJGDSJBLGBJRQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-15T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-15T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-15T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-15T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"One of India’s best comics returns to the UK…\r\nYou and Kanan are both tired of all his existential whinging - why are we here, what does it mean? Yuck. Who cares? How many specials can you try to dissect the fundamental nature of the human experience? Enough, right? Let’s party. \r\n\r\n\"WHAT IS THIS?\" is about nothing at all. So far. But what does nothing mean? What is emptiness empty of? Are thoughts thieves in an empty house? Oh shut up dude, stop it.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kanan Gill: WHAT IS THIS? - Birmingham Glee Club","instanceDates":"22 May-22 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"531003ACQGTBGMDMKHKPPMDKGKDRDCNSG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-22T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-22T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-22T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-22T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Birmingham Glee Club","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"One of India’s best comics returns to the UK…\r\nYou and Kanan are both tired of all his existential whinging - why are we here, what does it mean? Yuck. Who cares? How many specials can you try to dissect the fundamental nature of the human experience? Enough, right? Let’s party. \r\n\r\n\"WHAT IS THIS?\" is about nothing at all. So far. But what does nothing mean? What is emptiness empty of? Are thoughts thieves in an empty house? Oh shut up dude, stop it.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kanan Gill: WHAT IS THIS? - Union Chapel","instanceDates":"25 May-25 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"538203ARNTTLVQCNTLQTKSSRNSRQBDNGD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-25T15:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-25T14:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-25T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-25T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Union Chapel","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kanan Gill: WHAT IS THIS? at Queen Elizabeth Hall, Southbank Centre","instanceDates":"15 May-15 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"538403AHTPQGQLQLRJJRQLSRQBVTDTSRD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-15T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-15T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-15T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-15T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"London – Southbank Centre, Queen Elizabeth Hall","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Fresh off the release of her online comedy special ‘I Found My People’, Kaneez Surka returns with a brand new show. Originally from South Africa, with a career spanning India to New York, Kaneez brings her sharp observational humour and emotionally layered storytelling to explore the complexities of family and relationships. This is a show about connection — the ones we chase, the ones we run from, and the ones we never saw coming.\r\nKnown for her candid, intelligent comedy, Kaneez delivers warmth, wit, and truth in equal measure.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kaneez Surka Live","instanceDates":"19 August-23 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"646403ALMDMSPPGSLPTSPVPKSGPTJJQGC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-19T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-19T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-23T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-23T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"The year is 1857 and strapped to a cannon, a young Indian rebel finds themselves answering to a British officer for the crimes of Kanpur and the Indian uprising. \r\nThe year is 1857 and strapped to a cannon, a young Indian rebel finds themselves answering to a British officer for the crimes of Kanpur and the Indian uprising. Are they a hero or a villain? It doesn’t really matter, what is going to happen has already happened and whatever happens it’s going to be explosive. \r\n\"Everything is a story we tell...and yet you are the one who decides how it ends.\"\r\nColonialism and the right to resistance are satarised and deconstructed in this blistering two hander starring Niall Moorjani and Jonathan Oldfield, with live music from tabla master Sodhi. Originally commissioned for the Scottish International Storytelling Festival, with thanks to Creative Scotland and National Theatre of Scotland.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kanpur: 1857 by Niall Moorjani","instanceDates":"15 February-15 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"587003ANSLGHMBGBBTJTJBGMDMKGCPVSP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-15T16:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-15T16:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-15T16:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-15T16:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Come have the best night of your life singing karaoke and running into your ex downstairs at the Soho Theatre.\r\nHosted by comedy’s karaoke queen/alleged mezzo-soprano Olga Koch and very serious pop-duo Two Hearts, join us for a night of demented musical mayhem from only a tenner.\r\nGet up onstage to sing? Watch others do so? Some heady mix of the two? It’s up to you.\r\nExpect special guests (tba), overly ambitious song choices (tbd) and at least two lighting states (tbc). \r\n\r\nPlease note that this is a primarily standing show with very limited seating. \r\n\r\nOlga Koch, Two Hearts and Canned Laughter will be donating their split of the proceeds to The Trussell Trust.\r\n\r\nFood donations also encouraged! Donations should be non-perishable. A full list of items here.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Karaoke At The Heart Koch Café","instanceDates":"13 December-13 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"580403AVMJRMLCGCNNQMMDHPCQQDQMKJM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-13T23:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-13T23:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-13T23:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-13T23:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Come have the best night of your life singing karaoke and running into your ex downstairs at the Soho Theatre.\r\nHosted by comedy's karaoke queen/alleged mezzo-soprano Olga Koch and very serious pop-duo Two Hearts. \r\n\r\nOlga Koch, Two Hearts and Canned Laughter will be donating their split of the proceeds to The Trussell Trust.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Karaoke At The Heart Koch Café.","instanceDates":"19 July-19 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"561803ABJQKTPHQLNJCRHQGVBNKSHPPVJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-19T23:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-19T22:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-19T23:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-19T22:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"What would happen if, instead of starting clown school in Paris, you accidentally ended up following a group of Syrian refugees on their journey to seek asylum in Europe? How would your experience be different from theirs?\r\nDreamgirl is an immersive retelling of Norwegian filmmaker and clown Karen Houge’s real-life experience following refugees in her mid-20s, through storytelling, play, clown, interaction... and a bit of Lego.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":65,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Karen Houge: Dreamgirl","instanceDates":"6 July-11 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"727003AJSTMPRTDRLCPTQNTJDSSQNHQTP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-06T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-06T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-11T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-11T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"In her widely celebrated one-woman show, Kate Berlant explores the events of her life that have brought her to this moment.\r\nEmbodying many characters in this tour de force performance, she expertly morphs before our eyes and exposes a truth she has, until now, kept hidden. \r\n\r\nOriginally directed by Bo Burnham. \r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"KATE","instanceDates":"31 August-30 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"490803ACQSNHRSTMMLPVMLBHTNVKDPGMN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-31T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-31T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-30T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-30T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"In her Fringe debut, one of the rising stars of the UK stand up scene shares a raw, honest and hilarious hour of tales... with just the right amount of filth. Join the award-winning Canadian comedian as she tells her very personal story of how living in a new country, during a global pandemic, led to her making a life-threatening decision. After losing over 13 stone, Kate Barron returns to the stage a new, lighter woman, in more ways than one. \r\n \r\n★★★★★ Entertainment Now “Her delivery is that of a finely-honed instrumentalist”\r\n★★★★.5 Chortle “Raw, revealing and funny”\r\n★★★★ Fest Mag “Superb and revelatory”\r\n★★★★ The Scotsman “Dynamically funny”\r\n★★★★ Pow! Showbiz “Raw, honest and hilarious”\r\n★★★★ Voice Magazine “Hilarious and heartfelt”\r\n★★★★ The Wee Review\r\n★★★★ One4Review\r\n \r\nWINNER - Entertainment Now Edinburgh Fringe Festival Awards 2022 Best Debut\r\nWINNER - Toronto Comedy Brawl\r\nWINNER - Brantford Rising Star\r\n\r\nOfficial British Comedy Guide Edinburgh Fringe 2022 Recommendation\r\n\r\n16+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kate Barron: Losing Myself","instanceDates":"12 April-13 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"434603AJVPVQKKPJRLTNHSKGVQBNHNJNC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-12T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-12T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-13T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-13T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Following its smash-hit sell-out runs opening both Soho Theatre Walthamstow and A24’s Cherry Lane Theatre in New York, Natalie Palamides’ tour-de-force is back for a strictly limited run.\r\nKate Berlant is an Emmy nominated comedian, actress and writer. She recently concluded her fourth sold-out run of KATE, her one-woman Off-Broadway play directed by Bo Burnham, to a rapturous response – including a smash-hit run at Soho Theatre. \r\n\r\nHer comedy special Cinnamon in the Wind (directed by Bo Burnham) is now streaming on Hulu. In addition, her A24/Peacock sketch comedy special Would It Kill You to Laugh?, created with her collaborator John Early, was nominated for both a Critic’s Choice and Primetime Emmy Award. Kate’s film credits include Kristoffer Borgli’s Dream Scenario, Olivia Wilde’s Don’t Worry Darling, Quentin Tarantino’s Once Upon a Time in Hollywood, and Boots Riley’s Sorry to Bother You. She can be seen on the Amazon series A League of Their Own, starring alongside Abbi Jacobsen and Nick Offerman; her additional television credits include Search Party, The Other Two, Transparent, Fantasmas, and I Think You Should Leave with Tim Robinson, as well as her celebrated episode of Netflix’s The Characters. She was named a Just for Laughs \"New Face of Comedy\" and a Variety \"Ten to Watch.”\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":80,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kate Berlant: Live!","instanceDates":"13 February-14 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"669603APSMKDLSMLJDGDVNJCQQRCQRRNR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-13T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-13T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-14T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-14T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A work in progress from Kate Berlant.\r\nAfter the phenomenal success of her widely celebrated one-woman show, KATE, Kate Berlant makes a welcome return to Soho Theatre with a work in progress run. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kate Berlant: Live!.","instanceDates":"28 April-3 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"613203ADQRGGDQJDQNHKHCTDQKBGCQQGR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-28T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-28T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-03T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-03T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Fresh from the runway of RuPaul’s Drag Race UK, comedy crossdresser Kate Butch has written a jukebox musical based on the songs of Kate Bush (kind of like if Mamma Mia! had a nervous breakdown) but now she needs your help to get “BUSH!” to Broadway. Join the ‘great comedian’ (WhatsOnStage) as she runs up that hill, with stand-up comedy, live vocals, lip sync extravaganzas and more cloudbusting than you can shake a stick at. Buxton Fringe Best Comedy 2017 and 2019.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kate Butch: Wuthering Shites","instanceDates":"12 August-16 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"620603ACMHQCTRQJPMNBQNHRCPRRJBDPH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-12T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-12T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-16T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-16T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Drag","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"The reigning Funny Women Award winner and Chortle Best Newcomer nominee brings you her debut hour where she tries to save the world. \r\nWhere does this messiah complex come from? Is it the second coming or has she just inherited her mother's psychological disorder? If you're anxious about the state of the world (or just your own mental state), join this 'impressive, frank and relatable' (Chortle.co.uk) BBC New Comedy Awards semi-finalist as she becomes the first woman to wonder what many men have wondered before her: am I actually God?\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kate Cheka: A Messiah Comes","instanceDates":"16 January-18 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"578803ASBCPNGBPBHLGSJCVJHHVMNQQTL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-16T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-16T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-18T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-18T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"What do you do when your life explodes? 1/3 play, 1/3 stand-up, 1/3 rave.\r\nKate Dehnert's life recently blew up. We're talking: relationship; career; income; opportunities; visa; losing almost all of her possessions; what country she lived in; she almost died; and for some incredibly annoying reason she now has a way-too-overactive gag reflex. Like, she could stand in front of you and if you told her to vomit, she could. What the hell? Go out to dinner, drink some cocktails and meet Kate in the club – it's going to get raw. 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kate Dehnert: Echo","instanceDates":"14 September-19 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"726003AVCPHLQBCRVBRRNVVPMBQCVHMSK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-14T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-14T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-19T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-19T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Is being a fish in the river nicer than a woman on land? Kate Dolan presents her award-winning show 'Trout' fresh off sell-out Edinburgh Fringe and Melbourne Comedy Festival runs. 16+ (References to mental health issues, see webpage for current info).","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kate Dolan: Trout","instanceDates":"11 December-12 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"758003AHHMKBJTTBBCBSPDCTPRLVHVBLH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-11T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-11T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-12T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-12T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Sold out in New York and LA, Edinburgh Comedy Award nominated Broadway star and critically acclaimed clown Kate Owens brings her smash-hit debut to Soho.\r\nMeet Kathryn: the self-proclaimed “star\" of her family’s community cookin' show, wannabe Nigella Lawson, and down-home Southern belle with more wine in her veins than Jesus. As each absurd recipe spirals further off course, can Kathryn take the heat? \r\nWith live music, shadow puppetry, and a do or die quest to get married, join Kathryn on a mission to make her mama - and pastor - proud. A cooking show for the deranged, by the deranged. “Theatrical and unexpected... Owens deserves considerable respect and acclaim.” (4 stars Scotsman)\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kate Owens: Cooking with Kathryn","instanceDates":"5 January-10 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"670403ATNGVMVLJSGCBHQJSGMSQLQNNJL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-05T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-05T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-10T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-10T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join Katherine at this work in progress show as she warms up for her upcoming tour!","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Katherine Ryan: Work in Progress","instanceDates":"6 August-7 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"565203AVSLCCGGKLKQSMJPVNHGRDDKRRT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-06T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-06T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-07T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-07T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join award-winning comedian Kathryn Mather in this slightly dark, slightly whimsical show about working for the NHS, finding love and finding yourself against the backdrop of the pandemic.\r\n“Wickedly accomplished…  a thrilling rhythm and seamless flow… and the gags come at such a relentless rate. Mather positively revels in the macabre with a playful zeal” Rolling Stone UK \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kathryn Mather: Please Just Give Me A Chance","instanceDates":"5 February-5 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"522203AKLVLHBQQMVRDSNKCKLVNTTBNGB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-05T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-05T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-05T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-05T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Award-winning comedian Kathy Maniura brings one of the best reviewed shows of the Edinburgh Fringe 2025 to Soho Theatre.\r\nMiddle-aged and newly single, The Cycling Man has spent the salary of an NHS nurse in Decathlon and he’s on the verge of a breakdown. Get to know this absurd and deeply flawed man as he gets to know himself.\r\nGoofy drag king show from award-winning British character comedian Kathy Maniura, BBC New Comedian shortlisted, 2023 and Sketch Off winner, 2020.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kathy Maniura: The Cycling Man","instanceDates":"17 April-20 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"677803ADNTNQKSKGLDJCVGQVVHMSTBPHT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-17T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-17T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-20T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-20T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The unashamedly feel-good debut show from Latina rising star Katie Green. ¡Ay Mija! is a story about identity, family, coming of age, terrible dating choices and throwing the best party ever. She finds the funny in the differences between her Salvadoran roots and her British present, by way of a childhood growing up in California. Funny Women Finalist 2020, HBO's Women In Comedy Festival, Pleasance Comedy Reserve 2022. As seen on Comedy Central Live & ITV. Tour support for Jonathan Van Ness, Matteo Lane, Aziz Ansari, Red Richardson, Felipe Esparza and Aurie Styla. 16+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Katie Green: ¡Ay Mija!","instanceDates":"9 June-10 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"609403ARSQTQSCHCPMPHBQRQMPTLPNJKN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-09T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-09T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-10T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-10T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Fresh from the Edinburgh Fringe 2024, Farm Fatale is the smash-hit, critically-acclaimed debut solo show from an agricultural icon, likely to cause delight or distress to anyone who becomes involved with her, or her livestock. \r\n\r\nWinner: Musical Comedy Awards 2023.\r\nNomination: NextUp Biggest Award in Comedy 2024\r\nAs seen on BBC New Comedy Awards 2023. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Katie Norris: Farm Fatale","instanceDates":"11 December-14 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"578203AVCNNSTTRDSMMKQJGDPKKLJMHGK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-11T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-11T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-14T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-14T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Fresh from the Edinburgh Fringe 2024, Farm Fatale is the smash-hit, critically-acclaimed debut solo show from an agricultural icon, likely to cause delight or distress to anyone who becomes involved with her, or her livestock. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Katie Norris: Farm Fatale.","instanceDates":"23 September-28 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"566603AQJHCKSCPHGGKPHBGMDSRHJSTSV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-23T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-23T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-28T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-28T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"NOMINEE: BEST COMEDY SHOW 2025 - EDINBURGH COMEDY AWARDS\r\nCursed with the voice, face and arse of an angel, Katie Norris embarks on a personal odyssey into the untamed realms of her imagination following a sold-out run at this year's Edinburgh Fringe. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Katie Norris: Go West, Old Maid","instanceDates":"16 March-21 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"674603APVPHJVQDQVCLCGCTCVRBRJHJRD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-16T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-16T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-21T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-21T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"NOMINEE: BEST COMEDY SHOW 2025 - EDINBURGH COMEDY AWARDS\r\nCursed with the voice, face and arse of an angel, Katie Norris embarks on a personal odyssey into the untamed realms of her imagination following a sold-out run at this year's Edinburgh Fringe. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Katie Norris: Go West, Old Maid.","instanceDates":"11 September-12 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"655003ABTPDMRVQLLTBLDBDCGJVCPHVMV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-11T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-11T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-12T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-12T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Boys of the manosphere: prepare to be spooked. Women with cats: your leader has returned. Last year’s Best Show Nominee is back and ready to enter a new era. A stand-up and musical comedy show about maturing adorably from the self-appointed Godmother to the Nation.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Katie Norris: Mother Succubus","instanceDates":"14 September-19 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"743003ALCPKQGKCDSNHRMHKCJSBHPLQPV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-14T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-14T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-19T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-19T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Giraffes. VHS porn. Ketamine-infused breast milk. Acclaimed stand-up Kemah Bob (The Guardian's 10 Best Comedy Shows of 2024) returns with her much anticipated second show.\r\n\r\nLove Child is an intimate yet rowdy, personal yet electric, high-energy stand-up show from the “chest-achingly funny” (★★★★ Skinny) Kemah Bob. Join her on a hilariously unhinged tour through what it’s like to be a woman with your dad’s lips, a chaotic childhood with questionable parenting, the very real science of epigenetic baggage, and her attempts at navigating the relentless pressure to be a Good Grown Up™. ISH Edinburgh Comedy Award Best Newcomer nominee 2024. As seen on QI, Richard Osman's House of Games, Jonathan Ross' Comedy Club, Comedy Central Live, Don't Hate The Playaz and Guessable. As heard on the Off Menu podcast.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kemah Bob: Love Child","instanceDates":"1 March-6 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"730603ACCVPSJRSQTBMJQBVQHSGBBJHDG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-03-01T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-03-01T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-03-06T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-03-06T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Acclaimed comedian Kemah Bob brings their unmissable, critically acclaimed debut stand-up show to Soho Theatre after a sell-out Fringe run.\r\nAs seen on QI, Richard Osman's House of Games, Jonathan Ross' Comedy Club, Comedy Central Live, Don't Hate The Playaz, and Guessable.\r\n\r\nAs heard on the Off Menu podcast, The Guilty Feminist, James Acaster's Perfect Sounds, Springleaf, and Brett Goldstein's Films To Be Buried With.\r\n\r\nTour support for Hannah Gadsby, Nish Kumar and Desiree Burch. Host of the FOC IT UP Comedy Club and podcast.\r\n\r\nDirected by Desiree Burch.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kemah Bob: Miss Fortunate","instanceDates":"6 November-8 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"567003ACHSGNHDHTMQQRHVDKSVKNTBNQP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-06T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-06T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-08T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-08T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Catch Kevin in an intimate setting as he warms up ahead of filming his stand-up special later this year.\r\n“On his way to becoming a comedy great” - Times\r\n“Sensitive and meticulous, Kevin Bridges is one of the safest bets in UK stand-up” - Telegraph\r\n\r\nWith support from Jake Lambert\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kevin Bridges: Warm Up","instanceDates":"6 July-7 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"487803ABJLDCRPMNGTDLCJNHPVHLJTKHL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-06T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-06T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-07T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-07T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join Kevin as he warms up ahead of this upcoming tour. \r\n\r\nPlus support.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kevin Bridges: Warm Up","instanceDates":"26 May-30 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"711803ASNSQPRSPQLQTLLKLTTSDGHHPCS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-26T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-26T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-30T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-30T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Catch Kevin as he tries out new material! Plus support\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kevin Bridges: Work in Progress.","instanceDates":"17 April-19 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"542203AMBPQPPJTDTRDHKMNPQCTDSDHCD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-17T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-17T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-19T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-19T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Work In Progress","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Catch Kevin as he tries out new material! \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kevin Bridges: Work in Progress.","instanceDates":"1 June-2 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"632403ALRJPMPGQMLMKJQNJDGTMNKRGMQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-01T17:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-01T16:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-02T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-02T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join Kevin Bridges for an intimate show as he gets ready for his North American Tour. ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kevin Bridges: Work in Progress.","instanceDates":"30 July-31 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"649603AKLRPHMLLQNNCQNDPDVRPCRCTST","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-30T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-30T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-31T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-31T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A regular headliner on London’s urban comedy scene performing at the O2 and Hackney Empire, Kevin J makes his long-awaited debut at Soho Theatre.\r\n\r\nKevin J is sipping his third oat latte of the day in a boujiee East London cafe and contemplating how you can embrace your middle-class future without betraying your working-class roots. From a childhood raised on a notorious London council estate, to now doing his weekly shop in Waitrose. \r\nSharing anecdotes of being the “only white boy” in school, to navigating life on a notorious London council estate. This is the story of how our upbringing form the person we are today.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kevin J: Formative","instanceDates":"11 December-12 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"504803APCCRQJNMBDPSGRPQSSJSDHQBMV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-11T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-11T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-12T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-12T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Kiell Smith-Bynoe (star of Ghosts, Taskmaster and Stath Lets Flats)  is bringing his smash hit improv comedy show to a city near you.\r\nFeaturing: \r\nA surprise celebrity guest every night!\r\nA cast of some of the UK’s best improvisers around!\r\nStories from you, the audience, to inspire the comedy!\r\n\r\nFollowing a huge debut national tour, sold out runs across London and the Edinburgh Fringe, Kool Story Bro is coming back for another round of crazy audience stories from all over the UK.\r\n\r\nIt’s improvised comedy. But it’s Kool. \r\n\r\nPrevious special guests have included: Amelia Dimoldenberg, Lily Allen, Jamie Demitriou, Adam Buxton, Mo Gilligan, Loly Adefope and Nish Kumar.\r\n\r\nPrevious improvisers have included : Emma Sidi, Lola-Rose Maxwell, Graham Dickson, Lara Ricote, Janine Harouni, Nic Sampson, Brendan Murphy and Rob Gilbert. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kiell Smith-Bynoe & Friends: Kool Story Bro","instanceDates":"10 October-11 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"679003APLKQVJTSSMRNLCRKJBJKJRBTLQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-10T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-10T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-11T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-11T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Sketch","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The star of Taskmaster and Ghosts is joined by an all–star cast of comedians and some very special guests to turn stories from the audience into completely improvised comedy scenes. \r\nFresh from sold-out shows in Edinburgh, London and Brighton, Kool Story Bro is the unmissable improvised comedy show that spins unscripted sketches out of the audience’s weirdest and wildest anecdotes. Together with a surprise celebrity host, these “world-class improvisers” (Corr Blimey) are about to create a totally unique and utterly ridiculous show from scratch.\r\n\r\nKiell will be joined by members of Kool Story Bro’s rotating cast of improvisers,  including Starstruck favourites Lola-Rose Maxwell and Nic Sampson, Afterlife and Austentatious’s Graham Dickson, Big Boys’ Robert Gilbert, Mock The Week’s Emily Lloyd-Saini, Taskmaster’s Emma Sidi, and many more.\r\n\r\nPrevious special guests have included Lily Allen, Jamie Demetriou, Mo Gilligan, Charlotte Ritchie, Mathew Baynton, Guz Khan, and Munya Chawawa.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kiell Smith-Bynoe & Friends: Kool Story Bro Mar26","instanceDates":"19 March-21 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"675403AHKGPDCCNMNRQLSGMLJKSDHBGVH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-19T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-19T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-21T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-21T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Sketch","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The star of Taskmaster and Ghosts is joined by an all–star cast of comedians and some very special guests to turn stories from the audience into completely improvised comedy scenes. \r\nStar of Taskmaster, Ghosts and The Great British Sewing Bee, Kiell Smith-Bynoe is heading out on tour with an all–star cast of comedians and some very special guests to turn stories from the audience into completely improvised comedy scenes. \r\n\r\nFresh from sold-out shows in Edinburgh, London and Brighton, Kool Story Bro is the unmissable improvised comedy show that spins unscripted sketches out of the audience’s weirdest and wildest anecdotes. Together with a surprise celebrity host, these “world-class improvisers” (Corr Blimey) are about to create a totally unique and utterly ridiculous show from scratch.\r\n\r\nKiell will be joined by members of Kool Story Bro’s rotating cast of improvisers,  including Starstruck favourites Lola-Rose Maxwell and Nic Sampson, Afterlife and Austentatious’s Graham Dickson, Big Boys’ Robert Gilbert, Mock The Week’s Emily Lloyd-Saini, Taskmaster’s Emma Sidi, and many more.\r\n\r\nPrevious special guests have included Lily Allen, Jamie Demetriou, Mo Gilligan, Charlotte Ritchie, Mathew Baynton, Guz Khan, and Munya Chawawa.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":130,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kiell Smith-Bynoe & Friends: Kool Story Bro.","instanceDates":"22 May-4 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"596804APNBSKVTNHSVLMDJDVBNJNGSTCT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-22T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-22T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-04T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-04T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Sketch","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The return of the 5* hit show.\r\n\r\nA late night musical kids party, but for adults\r\n\r\nIt’s Story-time, kids! Now sit still and LISTEN: \r\n\r\nWhen it comes to children's entertainment, nobody does it better than Sylvester ‘Silly’ String. A charming classical virtuoso and topdog in the lucrative West London kids’ parties market, every kid within a 5 mile radius of the Kings Road wants Silly String and his Silly Songs...until Spitta comes along. SPITTA is a Grime-obsessed maverick from East London who’s shaken up the scene and quickly become the talk of the Kensington playgrounds. \r\n\r\nStarring Kiell Smith-Bynoe (star of BBC's Ghosts and Taskmaster) and Ed MacArthur ('Murder for Two'), String V SPITTA is a musical comedy about two rival children’s entertainers, from opposite sides of the tracks, who will do anything to be number one. Think Amadeus meets Flight of the Conchords, with musical numbers directed by Dizzee Rascal.\r\n\r\nThis is one party you won't want to miss.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kiell Smith-Bynoe V Ed MacArthur: String V SPITTA","instanceDates":"14 July-26 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"624803AHSDPKCPVCJDKQCCRCHRGTPJRMM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-14T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-14T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-26T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-26T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"In 2020, the world changed forever, as three time Edinburgh Comedy Award nominee Kieran Hodgson moved to Scotland. Now he's travelling around the still-just-about United Kingdom to tell you how it's working out. For him and for the Scots. \r\n\r\nYou might remember Kieran as that guy from the BBC's 'Two Doors Down' (he's Gordon), the 'Bad TV Impressions' viral videos of 'The Crown' and 'Happy Valley', and three Channel 4 specials. If you don't remember him, no worries. We all have busy lives. \r\n\r\n“A delight to watch... every line is wired for laughter” ★★★★★ The Guardian\r\n“Structure and delivery that puts most other shows to shame” ★★★★★ The Telegraph\r\n“Ravishingly entertaining, full of insight and plenty of laughs” ★★★★ The Times\r\n“Rich, thoughtful but belly-laugh stuff… a hugely accomplished storyteller” ★★★★ The Scotsman\r\n★★★★ TimeOut\r\n★★★★ The Sunday Times\r\n★★★★ Independent\r\n★★★★ Chortle\r\n★★★★ Fest\r\n★★★★ List\r\n\r\nEdinburgh Comedy Award Best Show Nominee 2015, 2016, 2018.\r\n\r\n16+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":65,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kieran Hodgson: Big In Scotland","instanceDates":"11 September-27 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"469204AQBHLLQNHBTSQTMBQRLQLBVPTRQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-11T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-11T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-27T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-27T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"The four time Edinburgh Comedy Award nominee and one of Telegraph’s 50 Funniest Comedians of the 21st Century returns to Soho due to popular demand!\r\n\r\nAmerica. What happened, man? Ever since he was a little loser kid in a little loser country (yes, England), Kieran has been putting on an American accent and dreaming a big American dream. But nowadays it’s not so simple. Didn’t America go completely bananas? Didn’t he get too old for dreaming? And when Hollywood comes calling, does Kieran actually sound American after all?\r\n\r\nJoin Kieran as he explores how a scared world feels about the USA and impersonates a bunch of old prospectors and former Presidents.\r\n\r\nAs seen on Two Doors Down, Prince Andrew The Musical and The Flash.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kieran Hodgson: Voice of America","instanceDates":"16 September-20 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"650803ANLDBNNNKSPPJJDHPGRQMRSJSLR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-16T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-16T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-20T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-20T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The four time Edinburgh comedy award nominee and star of Two Doors Down returns.\r\n  \r\nAmerica. What happened, man? Ever since he was a little loser kid in a little loser country (yes, England), Kieran Hodgson has been putting on an American accent and dreaming a big American dream. But nowadays it's not so simple. Didn't America go completely bananas? Didn't he get too old for dreaming? And when Hollywood comes calling, does Kieran actually sound American after all?\r\n\r\nJoin the one of Telegraph’s 50 funniest comedians of the 21st Century as he explores how a scared world feels about the USA and impersonates a bunch of old prospectors and former Presidents.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kieran Hodgson: Voice of America.","instanceDates":"16 June-28 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"613403ANBMTMQSHBHPHJRKJHPPVMNDCPB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-16T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-16T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-28T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-28T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kiki & Herb","instanceDates":"3 July-5 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"625603ATMJCRSPHCSKKLPJMTBNHMGBVGC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-03T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-03T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-05T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-05T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"The original soundtrack to Lullaby for Scavengers by Stephen & David Dewaele (aka Soulwax / 2manydjs) is now available on a limited edition cassette (with download code) via their DEEWEE record label. Copies can be collected at Soho Theatre, as a UK exclusive, during the run of Kim’s show. Price £11\r\n\r\n“Myself and squirrel are delighted about this album. Stephen & David Dewaele have taken their original music made for the theatre show Lullaby For Scavengers, removed all the theatrical elements. i.e the lighting, the smoke machine and the bit about sewers but adding more sound. Thus making it soooooo much better. Because let's face it..theatre is just fucken rubbish and sound amazing.” Kim Noble\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kim Noble Merch (Cassette)","instanceDates":"1 April-8 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"461403ASKMQVMBQMGPTDTCLNCKQQGTKCV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-01T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-01T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-08T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-08T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Cult comedic performance artist Kim Noble lived in a tree, down a sewer, under an insurance office desk and in an unsuspecting client's attic. Now he returns to Soho Theatre with the UK premiere of his critical acclaimed new show. \r\n\r\nHow do you fit into a world that doesn't necessarily want you? A fox and his ex lover - an angry dead squirrel - are his accomplices in search of survival strategies, friendship and knowledge of what we should pass on to the next generation Noble descends deep into the sewer and abyss of human loneliness of longing and answers the question of how to deal with rodents in your attic. \r\n\r\nFollowing the provocative hit shows ‘Kim Noble Will Die’ and ‘You’re Not Alone’ comes Part 3 of his theatrical trilogy on loneliness and connection. \r\n\r\nPraise from the European tour of Lullaby for Scavengers: \r\n\r\n‘Sublime portrayal of a deeply tragic quest for acceptance.’ \r\nTheaterkrant - Nuno Blijboom \r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kim Noble: Lullaby for Scavengers","instanceDates":"1 April-8 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"400003AKVDRVPVSLRDPKHVHPQVCGVRPPR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-01T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-01T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-08T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-08T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"In December 2022 Kiran Deol, an Indian American comedian, is hospitalised following a horrifying unprovoked attack outside of a 7-11. Yes, there are fractures and surgeries – but in front of a 7-11!? At least be original and do it in front of a Ross! But that’s not all: they caught the guy. A court case ensues and the tables are turned: Kiran is asked by the judge whether she wants her attacker to be incarcerated in prison or receive treatment for mental health issues, in what becomes an ironic and compelling twist...\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kiran Deol: Assault On Comedy","instanceDates":"11 May-16 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"708403ADMJSDRGJHRMPRHPSPBRLKRLHQL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-11T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-11T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-16T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-16T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Battling immigrant and capitalist pressure to succeed from her Desi-British-American background, Kiran Saggu wonders: must she get her ass up and work?\r\nAfter her 2024 debut run at Edinburgh Fringe Festival, Kiran Saggu presents SLACKS\r\n•  Kiran Saggu hates hard work. Battling immigrant and capitalist pressure to succeed from her Desi-British-American background, she wonders: must she get her ass up and work? Or can she be loved, adored, rich and fulfilled from the safety of a log position in her flatshare bed? This show will cover topics like: How can I live with the fact I didn't start that YouTube channel at 12 years old to make me a millionaire now? When will men I date stop telling me they want to pursue stand-up comedy? And, can I sue the Daily Mail?\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kiran Saggu: Slacks","instanceDates":"17 February-17 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"591003AHJQRPSGMPBDRTCHQTRCQJHPBBB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-17T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-17T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-17T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-17T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Josgin/Joskin/Joscin definition: a North-Walian term used in both English and Welsh to describe anyone from a rural or farming background. It is used both affectionately and in a derogatory way depending on the audience. A brand new tour from star of Live at the Apollo and QI, Kiri Pritchard-McLean. Growing up on a sheep and cattle farm in Wales with a pair of accidental farmers for parents, Kiri vowed she would never become a farmer. Fast forward 30 odd years and Kiri is back in the countryside. She’s a farm up and a parent down and has decided to fix the planet, feed the world and try and reclaim her Josgin heritage. In a digital world with increasing AI, come and see a very analogue comedian. 15+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":85,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kiri Pritchard-McLean: Josgin","instanceDates":"9 October-9 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"761603AQNVCSBKPRPLHMBQPGHJMHKGDDK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-10-09T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-10-09T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-10-09T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-10-09T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Kirsty has been keeping a huge secret - she’s a doctor. But please don’t tell anyone, she wants people to take her seriously as a comedian. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kirsty Mann: Skeletons","instanceDates":"24 June-25 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"535003ASVTJPKCKKQLSMTMRPRHDQBDBPP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-24T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-24T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-25T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-25T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"A queer, musical fantasia on pop-singer George Michael.\r\nIn ‘Kissing A Fool’, we speculatively dive into George Michael’s psyche at the lowest point in his life. After the death of his lover, Anselmo Feleppa, and losing a high-profile legal battle with Sony Music, the pop-icon feared he’d never write another song. In his despair, George awakens the Fool from deep within, a familiar clown companion whose only intelligence is play. \r\n\r\nJoin us on this musical journey into the tumultuous creative process of one of the greatest artists of a generation, and witness the transformation of grief into transcendent creativity through song. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kissing A Fool by Scarlett Stitt","instanceDates":"14 February-14 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"522005AJKGJGDCVMGRNCCVQRMGBTQHTML","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-14T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-14T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-14T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-14T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"Star of Taskmaster, Ghosts, and Stath Lets Flats, Kiell Smith-Bynoe hosts a late-night improv show featuring the best improvisers around (plus some very special guests!).\r\nExpect a different show each night, with scenes inspired by monologues from you, the audience.\r\n\r\nPrevious special guests include Jamie Demetriou, Lara Ricote and Nabil Abdulrashid. Previous improvisers have included Emma Sidi, Graham Dickson, Brendan Murphy and Emily Lloyd-Saini.\r\n\r\nAs heard on the Off Menu podcast and seen on House of Games, Dreamland, and Horrible Histories.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kool Story Bro","instanceDates":"27 October-28 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"498603ALGSJSKRBHHSTJVJMRTPRCKMNND","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-27T21:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-27T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-28T21:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-28T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Krystal's sizzling debut hour, direct from a sell-out run at the Edinburgh Fringe, finds the humour in escaping a house-fire, death, tragedy and mental illness, and how all this has – somewhat ironically – made her life funnier.\r\n\r\nAn emotional rollercoaster of a show that offers a viciously funny take on some of the defining moments in Krystal’s life. As seen on BBC’s Comedy Underground, Scot Squad, Breaking the News. Tour support for Stewart Francis and Zoe Lyons. Leicester Mercury New Comedian of the Year finalist.\r\n\r\n‘To make the content of this show so outrageously funny is an art form.’ ★★★★★ Broadway World\r\n\r\n‘An utterly beautiful show... easy, earthy style of delivery.’ ★★★★★ Beyond The Joke\r\n\r\n‘Evans is a constant professional, always in control.’ ★★★★★ Edinburgh Festivals Magazine\r\n\r\n‘Self-assured, potent, shocking.’ ★★★★ Independent\r\n\r\n‘She’s always in control of the mood, skilfully navigating between the highs of the gags and the lows of reality.’ ★★★★ Chortle\r\n\r\n‘Unapologetic hilarity... a stunning debut.’ ★★★★ Skinny\r\n\r\n‘We are grateful to be a part of it.’ ★★★★ Broadway Baby\r\n\r\n‘This is a very well crafted hour and, given the nub of the show, shockingly funny.’ ★★★★ The Arts Desk\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Krystal Evans: The Hottest Girl at Burn Camp","instanceDates":"30 November-2 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"504804AMPSCMPNPNJGKKSLPBNCRVLDNPH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-30T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-30T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-02T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-02T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"How much do you love your homeland? Do you love it enough so that, as a queer boy, you’d endure the dehumanising military service before running away? \r\nIn his debut hour, Leicester Comedy Festival Best Show nominee Kuan-wen recounts how he traded his beloved island for the rainy British isles, what it means to be Taiwanese and what it symbolises through generations of migrations.  As seen and heard on BBC Radio 4, BBC Three and Comedy Central. \r\n\r\nDirected by Dec Munro\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kuan-wen Huang: Ilha Formosa","instanceDates":"16 February-16 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"521205AHMKHCPTDCLKCKTTSSSKMJDVBGR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-16T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-16T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-16T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-16T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Kyla Cobbler is one of the fastest-rising names in comedy. The Cork-born comic first gained attention through her viral Instagram reels, before stepping on stage for her first open mic in May 2021. Just four years later, she’s built a global following, with over 450,000 Instagram followers, 100M+ video views, and a reputation as a must-see live performer.\r\nAs seen on the Tommy Tiernan Show and Ireland AM. As heard on Newstalk FM, 2FM Morning, Mike & Vittorio’s Guide to Parenting, Laura Dowling Experience, Talking Bollox, Have A Word etc. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kyla Cobbler: Gone Rogue","instanceDates":"13 October-18 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"645003AKNTTVLBGNTPVSCLPGMMPDVCRNB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-13T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-13T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-18T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-18T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"In her debut stand-up hour, Kyrah Gray works through the emotional whiplash of growing up Jamaican in the UK, a questionable dating history, and the pressure to have your life “figured out”, usually from people who very much do not. Kyrah's cracking expectations and the upbringing that shaped her, in an attempt to realign and make better decisions. Kyrahpractor is the adjustment you didn't know you needed. \r\nWinner of Best Show at the Leicester Comedy Festival 2025\r\nAs seen on Comedy Central Live, star of Comedy Central's Dating Horror Stories, host of Sky's Youtube dating series Gagging for It & Channel 4.0\r\nTour support for Judi Love, Tom Davis, Ziwe, Guz Khan & Romesh Ranganathan\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kyrah Gray: Kyrahpractor","instanceDates":"15 April-16 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"697003AQBKBQHDGVLJVTSBKLTNLLPLKNB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-15T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-15T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-16T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-16T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The horrifying debut from the award-winning poof prince of puppets RETURNS\r\nLachy is a poof, and apparently a virgin. Brew is a small, squishy witch, and she has decided to sacrifice him. To help with his self-esteem.\r\nTogether, they’ll bring your worst nightmares to life in a ceremony of paranormal tricks and treats. But when the ritual releases a sinister entity with a lust for destruction, the virginal Lachy may never be the same... \r\n\r\n\"The funniest new ventriloquist on the block\" (Telegraph) rising star, Lachlan Werner returns with his Edinburgh Fringe total sell-out horror hit. A surprising, rebellious and ridiculous hour of frights, where demonic voices come from every corner. Watch out, anyone could get puppeteered by evil\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lachlan Werner: Voices of Evil","instanceDates":"31 October-4 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"500003ARDTRCLSQKRJSCVKNTSSKCRGDMP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-31T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-31T22:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-04T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-04T22:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Twunk: head of a twink, body of a hunk. Step right this way and see him.\r\nAward-winning ventriloquist Lachlan Werner, presents a new show so strong, it's dangerous.\r\nIn Marytown, USA Jack Hammer lifts 1000kg six times daily for adoring crowds in his dad's circus. Jack was born the strongest boy in the world. And he's gay.\r\nBut is his superhuman strength everything he believes? Is it true that all other humans can only look, not touch?\r\nFollowing his award-winning debut, Voices Of Evil (Total sellout 2023/24) Lachlan Werner - \"funniest new ventriloquist on the block\" Telegraph - returns with a genre-defying, multi-5 star reviewed cult hit. Combining ventriloquism, clown, physical theatre and vocal acrobatics, Lachlan weaves a neo-vaudevillian horror fairytale packed with sea-lions, stunts and sinister secrets...\r\nCo-written and Directed by Laurie Luxe \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lachlan Werner: WonderTwunk","instanceDates":"29 October-1 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"662003ANKTJBVBRJHSCRBPNPTVNNRDRBL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-29T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-29T22:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-01T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-01T22:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The Twunk: head of a twink, body of a hunk.\r\nBehind this curtain lies a modern model of manhood.\r\nLachlan Werner (\"Hilarious. Extraordinary ventriloquist\" Guardian) invites you to roll up and step this way for a new show so strong, it's dangerous.\r\nJack Hammer is the strongest boy in the world. He can lift a ten-tonne truck and crush the strongest steel.\r\nJust don't get too close. His management says you can look, but you can't touch.\r\nFollowing his sell-out cult-hit horror debut, Voices Of Evil, Lachlan Werner welcomes you into a circus ring of stunts, sea-lions, sci-fi, secrets and minimal lip movement...\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lachlan Werner: WonderTwunk.","instanceDates":"18 June-18 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"616003ADQHRQBTGNNSHVJQKRRBRDKMDPK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-18T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-18T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-18T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-18T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"After a Sell-Out run at Edinburgh Fringe 2026, Lady Bolognese are bringing their Leicester Comedy Award-winning debut hour: CLASS WAR to Soho Theatre. “Unhinged” (British Comedy Guide), and “Twisted” (The Scotsman), Lady Bolognese are encouraging YOU, dumb-dumb, to go back to school! But beware – your old dinner ladies, Barbara and Veronica, are taking over… So, come to class. It’s going to be a riot.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lady Bolognese: Class War","instanceDates":"21 October-24 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"752603AVSLGKDSJLQDSPMKGSLCDVCHSGG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-21T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-21T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-24T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-24T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"HAVEN Coffee is excited to present the 9th instalment of their signature comedy gig Laff-Uccino during festive season 2024!\r\nHAVEN Coffee is a social enterprise that serves ethically sourced, fair-trade, organic cup of speciality coffee with a social mission of breaking false narratives around refugees and migrants through arts and culture. They do it by promoting artists from refugee background and their artwork in an effort to bring refugee communities and UK society together. \r\nLaff-Uccino is part of this social mission and started in December 2019 and this will be the 9th instalment of it. The line-up includes some very talented and Funny comedians from Refugee & Migrant Backgrounds performing for their very 1st, 2nd, or 3rd gig, refugees from our latest stand-up workshop participants, and some old horses of the stage, including Ed Night, Sam Williams, Adam Coumas on MC, and a very special Guest Headliner, TBA!\r\nAnd if you think that is enough then we have one last thing for you. There will be a Free Raffle on the afternoon with a chance to win some very good prizes!\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Laff-Uccino","instanceDates":"14 December-14 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"572803ALLBMPBGBMQQTJBLQNHSMRJGGGD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-14T15:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-14T15:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-14T15:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-14T15:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"HAVEN Coffee is excited to present the 11th instalment of their signature comedy gig this festive season.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":150,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Laff-Uccino with Rhys James","instanceDates":"11 December-11 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"664003AGGTKTJBQKTVBGCJLTTHJKSHJTV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-11T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-11T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-11T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-11T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"You know when stuff happens to you and you react in a certain way (read: cry) so then you lean in? To know thyself? A man in a museum was mean to me (classic) and I’ve gotten a lot out of it (hell yeah). My stupidest and smartest show yet (alright!). INKLING is a show about How to Salute to the Mystery of Being Alive (ok?). Might that be of intrigue?… To you? Big kisses to you and yours. Love, Lara. PS I am trying my best. 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lara Ricote: Inkling","instanceDates":"18 May-22 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"759403AQSNKLQHDCSQDJMKHDMMSKLVMMM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-05-18T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-05-18T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-05-22T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-05-22T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"You're born, you're in it, you're dead! Symbolically! Kind of! Don't think about it right now. Right now, stay present in this moment. Stay. Present. Purchase. A. Ticket. \r\n\r\nA sort of surreal, partially interactive, dark (like silly dark! not like edgelord dark...or is it) and maybe moving comedy show about what it's even like to live and what it means to care for someone if you always leave them. \r\nAll of this 2022’s Edinburgh Comedy Award Best Newcomer Winner (yeah!) and 2021 Funny Women Stage Award Winner (also!). \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lara Ricote: Little Tiny Wet Show (baptism)","instanceDates":"21 February-2 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"517403ALMKCRQBGLHJGMVNMBJVVLCVPNP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-21T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-21T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-02T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-02T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Recently married, emotionally feral.\r\nThe Gallus Glaswegian Goon returns with a riotous show about refusing to grow up.\r\nAs seen on SNL, Live at the Apollo, QI and The Royal Variety Performance.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Larry Dean: Hellbent","instanceDates":"6 November-6 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"704203APLPCSSTTDGCTQHCLVNTVLCRJQB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-06T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-06T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-06T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-06T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Three-time Edinburgh Comedy Award nominee tries some new jokes. \r\nAs seen and heard on Live at the Apollo, Mock the Week, Michael Mcintyre's Big Show and Shared Baggage. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Larry Dean: Work in Progress","instanceDates":"16 July-17 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"550003ADPBLCLDKCJHTDQBBVLJJRNDVLG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-16T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-16T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-17T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-17T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Terry's back from the dead and he's brought a chat show with him. Featuring interviews with \"real\" celebrities and accompanied by a live band.  \r\nPrevious guests include: George Lucas, Ray Parker Jr, Sir Anthony Hopkins, Liza Minelli, DB Cooper, Tim Henman, Scarlett Johansson and several different Michael Caines. Every night one lucky member of the audience will give Terry £5000. Terry Wogan is a recipient of a KBE / dead.  \r\n \r\n'A clever late-night romp' **** (Telegraph).  \r\n**** (Mervyn Stutter's Pick of the Fringe). \r\n\r\nWINNER: 2026 Brighton Fringe Komedia Award for Alternative Comedy with the Nest \r\n\r\nFor Benjamin Alborough: \r\n\r\nWINNER: 2026 Edinburgh Comedy Award Panel Prize \r\n\r\nNOMINEE: 2026 Leicester Comedy Festival Best Variety Show \r\n\r\nNOMINEE: 2025 Malcolm Hardee Award for Comic Originality\r\n\r\n16+ (check website for current content advice).","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Late Night with Terry Wogan","instanceDates":"10 October-10 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"750803ARMJBQRJVVPMJMDHJTKHCCLSPMC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-10T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-10T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-10T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-10T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Terry Wogan is back from the dead as part of his ongoing attempts to return to light entertainment no matter the cost. Featuring interviews with \"real\" celebrities and accompanied by a live band. Every night one lucky member of the audience will give Terry £5000. Recipient of a KBE and wielder of the flame of Anor.\r\nPrevious guests include George Lucas, Ray Parker Jr, Sir Anthony Hopkins, Liza Minelli, DB Cooper, Tim Henman, Scarlett Johansson and several different Michael Caines. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Late Night With Terry Wogan 24","instanceDates":"6 December-7 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"574603ATKQJBKNCGCHKRHRVPTBLRHVHMT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-06T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-06T22:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-07T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-07T22:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join multi award-winning stand up star and viral sensation Laura Lexx with her highly anticipated Australian debut: Slinky.\r\nFirmly established as one of the most sought after headliners on the UK and international comedy circuits.. this show is effortlessly heartwarming, hilarious about motherhood, and fearless with the front row.\r\nAs seen on: Mock The Week, Live at The Apollo (BBC), Hypothetical (DAVE), Pointless Celebrities (BBC), Roast Battle (Comedy Central), The Comedy Club (BBC Radio 4 Extra), The Now Show (BBC Radio 4), The News Quiz (BBC Radio 4), Mo Gilligan’s Spotlight (Audible)\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Laura Lexx: Slinky ","instanceDates":"7 May-9 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"689003AMTDLQQHPDDPVTVDCRVTJBVRGSP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-07T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-07T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-09T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-09T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"With over 1 million followers and 350 million views across social media, comedian Laura Ramoso makes her highly anticipated London debut, following an entirely sell out run at the Fringe this summer. \r\n\r\nFeaturing her most popular characters like Italian Dad, German Mom and the Three Girls Who Just Got Back From Europe, FRANCES tells a hilarious and painfully relatable story about love and loss through the best in sketch and improv comedy. \r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Laura Ramoso: FRANCES","instanceDates":"19 September-30 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"492803ADTKJNBBCHQNTCTVRTLPDKDKGPJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-19T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-19T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-30T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-30T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Standup comedy about lockdown kids, GenX men and unexpected civil wars, spoken with an annoying American accent. \r\nLaurie is a standup comedian as well as writer for the US late night show Jimmy Kimmel Live (unless Donald Trump gets his way). She also wrote on the 2025 and 2026 Oscars and was a staff writer on Conan O'Brien's show CONAN for its 11-year run. She is excited to be away from home.\r\n16+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Laurie Kilmartin: The Non-Refundable Plane Tickets Tour","instanceDates":"27 July-28 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"717804ASDNDBNBTDCLRVSSNSHKQJBPGRL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-27T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-27T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-28T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-28T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Emo teen David is a poet, a philosopher, a musical genius. And he’s here to headline Sticky Floors – the coolest under 16s band night in the Bay Area. But when his bandmate doesn't show, will he handle himself with a sense of poise and rationality? This coming-of-age character comedy with live music is a nostalgia bomb of teenage awkwardness – from angsty poetry, to failed flirtations, to the perils of wearing black layers during a heatwave. It’s a silly, sweet exploration of how teenage boys communicate when, like, words are hard. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Laurie Stevens: David's One-Man Band (F*ck You, Steven)","instanceDates":"10 February-10 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"684803ATMBLNTHQTLMBBSDQVVKKKLSKBN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-10T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-10T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-10T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-10T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"COME AND SEE THE SHOW OF YOUR LIFETIME. \r\nIt’s my (LOZDODD) show—a special show like NO other. DIFFERENT EVERYTIME. Powerful. Urgent. What even is this? Where are we going? How do we know what’s real? COME. You’ll leave changed—GUARANTEED.\r\nIn his quest to make sense of everything, Loz discovers he knows nothing. In his unravelling, he searches for meaning with what’s left: himself, a room, and the people in it.\r\nThis Can’t Be It is a semi-improvised, feverish and open-hearted exploration of how we stay open to mystery (and to each other) in times of uncertainty and collapse.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lawrence Dodd: This Can’t Be It","instanceDates":"4 June-1 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"714403APBTQDTNNLTTBDJBPKRKQMVDMPD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-04T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-04T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-01T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-01T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"With a Musical Theatre mega-memory as deep as his vocal range, Le Gateau Chocolat is your one-stop Musicals Juke Box, and he’s ready to give it all to you this Christmas.\r\nWith all the feels from Follies to Frozen, Sound of Music to – The Snowman. Gateau is ready to feed you every coco-covered Chocolat showtune in his box.\r\n\r\nExpect mountains of laughs, a stream of nostalgia, and a tug at the heartstring as Gateau crams every single musical you know and love into an hour of high kicks, high drag and high glamour.\r\n\r\nServing Do-Re-Mi with Hi-La-Ri-Tea (a drink with jam and bread).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Le Gateau Chocolat: Musicals Mayhem","instanceDates":"11 December-11 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"575403ARVDDPKKHJVHTDGNCJBHMCVTKQP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-11T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-11T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-11T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-11T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"After a sellout run at this year’s Edinburgh Fringe, Leila Navabi is bringing her debut show 'an eye-catching introduction to a comic of promise' (Guardian) to London for one week only!\r\nThe Welsh, brown, gay, Gen-Z comedian presents an audacious punk musical-comedy show about the dubious ethics of artistically exploiting marginalised identities for social gain. Leila grew up learning to utilise and monopolise her 'minority identity' for evil and mischief. Her show doesn’t rely on these identities, but her overwhelming prodigious talent, actually. Star of BBC's Vandullz and the BBC New Comedy Awards 2022, Leila has written for Bad Education (BBC) and Never Mind The Buzzcocks (Sky), and can be heard in Channel 4’s Don’t Hug Me I’m Scared. 'The actual future of comedy' (LMAOnaiseComedy.com). \r\n\r\nTEN BEST JOKES AT THE FRINGE - GUARDIAN\r\n\r\n***** FUNNY WOMEN\r\n***** THE WEE REVIEW\r\n***** THE STUDENT NEWSPAPER\r\n**** THE SKINNY\r\n**** FEST\r\n**** CHORTLE\r\n**** ONE4REVIEW\r\n**** LOST IN THEATRELAND\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Leila Navabi: Composition","instanceDates":"14 November-18 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"496603ARPRVGSBKTDJVBPCLCBCHBJVDSR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-14T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-14T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-18T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-18T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Comedy"},{"description":"A bold, joyful punk-musical one-person show about making a queer family on your own terms, written and performed by award-nominated comedian, writer and composer Leila Navabi. \r\n \r\nThe critically acclaimed show was included in The Guardian’s “10 Best Shows to Catch” at Edinburgh Fringe this summer, and was nominated for the Brighton Fringe Award for Excellence.\r\n\r\nRelay blends stand-up, electro-pop musical numbers and hand-drawn animation into a heartfelt, hilarious hour about what it takes to start a family when the odds (and the system) are stacked against you. Leila dives into the wild ride of making a baby at home with her partner, a best mate as the sperm donor, and, naturally, his boyfriend cheering from the sidelines. Navabi unpacks love, ambition, and the chaos of building a family on her own terms. Equal parts absurd and profound, Relay is proof that family is not just what you make it, but how.\r\n\r\nLeila’s debut show Composition sold out its run at the Edinburgh Fringe 2023 and transferred to London’s Soho Theatre.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Leila Navabi: Relay","instanceDates":"11 March-14 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"674803ACDJLQJJNKCTLLMGQTVMVRPMLTK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-11T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-11T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-14T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-14T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"For over five decades, Lenny Henry has been telling stories – on stage, on screen and through a host of characters etched into our collective memory.\r\nPart stand-up, part storytelling and part conversation with himself (and with you), this new live show sees Lenny return to the experiences that shaped him while also exploring the ideas, challenges and creative sparks driving him today.\r\nFrom the unforgettable days of The Lenny Henry Show and Chef! to acclaimed dramatic performances in Othello and, more recently, The Lord of the Rings: The Rings of Power, Lenny traces the roles, characters and moments that have defined his remarkable career – and shares what continues to inspire him now as he reflects on a life lived out loud.\r\nExpect big laughs, heart and a celebration of the many versions of Lenny: the actor, the impressionist, the comedian, the fundraiser and the Stand-Up Anecdotalist. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lenny Henry: Still At Large","instanceDates":"28 June-28 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"687203AMMDTQDGMGLVDNNDLKBQKVQDHVP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-28T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-28T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-28T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-28T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Your favourite dilettante sociopath is back, fresh from an acclaimed off-Broadway run, to perform his multiple award nominated show one last time.\r\n\r\n“High cheekbones” - New York Times\r\n\r\n“Life is an accumulation of losses, and their pace is accelerating” - New York Times\r\n\r\n“Taut, biting, and darkly hilarious” - New York Times\r\n\r\nNominee Most Outstanding Show Award Melbourne International Comedy Festival 2023\r\nNominee Best Newcomer 2022 Edinburgh Comedy Awards\r\n\r\n***** Time Out\r\n***** The Telegraph\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Leo Reich: Literally Who Cares?!","instanceDates":"8 September-9 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"487403ARCKMGCPLGCNDSBCMDVVQLMQMQR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-08T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-08T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-09T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-09T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Join up-and-coming US comedian Leslie Liao as she crosses the Atlantic for her first ever London shows!\r\nLeslie Liao is one of the most exciting new stars of the LA comedy scene. Having acted as tour support for Fortune Feimster, and recently being selected to be a New Face of Comedy at Montreal's prestigious Just For Laughs Comedy Festival 2023, she will next be seen on Netflix’s “Verified Standup” series, released later this year. \r\nFor the first time, she’s bringing her honest, relatable, introspective, and no-nonsense style of humour to London, with a show about the life and loves of a single Chinese-American woman living in LA.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Leslie Liao: The Nighttime Routine Tour","instanceDates":"18 March-23 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"505403ADRNJPBVMRLPBVDGMJLBNHQMQLT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-18T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-18T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-23T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-23T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"1968. Three thousand students occupy the London School of Economics, in the most significant act of protest in a generation.\r\n2024. Two friends and flatmates try to work out what radical change means today, searching through archives, photos, first-hand accounts. \r\nEverything’s connected: from the Prague Spring to MLK Jr’s murder, the Paris riots to the Nigerian Civil War, and it’s all converging here and now.\r\nLessons On Revolution is a ★★★★★ “thought-provoking” (A Youngish Perspective) piece of documentary theatre. It is a gripping and immersive journey through global and personal history which asks: in a new age of inequality and injustice, how can the voices of the past give us hope?\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lessons on Revolution by Gabriele Uboldi","instanceDates":"13 February-13 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"522803APLBSDBCHGLHPMTRBLJBVRVLLJQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-13T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-13T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-13T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-13T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"I wanna go back in time. Not too far, not Pangea. The present feels too heavy, the past feels like the moon - with less gravity, I was lighter. Meet me on the moon. Edinburgh Comedy Award Best Newcomer Li Jin Hao is bringing his latest show “Falling From A Moon” on his first ever UK tour. As seen on Mitchell & Webb Are Not Helping (Channel 4), DMs Are Open (BBC Radio 4), The Stand Up Sketch Show (ITV2), ITVX Presents: Live Comedy From The Edinburgh Fringe (ITVX) and Comedy Central Live (Comedy Central). BBC New Comedy Award and Channel 4 Sean Lock Award Finalist.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Li Jin Hao: Falling From a Moon","instanceDates":"28 October-7 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"712403AHPKNVCNNBCDGPMNJPBPBDTJTSR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-28T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-28T21:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-07T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-07T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"When Liam was 18 he moved from Dagenham to Edinburgh, and didn’t tell his parents.\r\nLiam returns to Soho Theatre with a story about leaving home, coming to terms with who your parents are and what to do when a personal trainer slides into your DM’s.\r\n\r\nLiam has over 10million TikTok/Instagram views and his 2023 Edinburgh Fringe show ‘Chronic Boom’ was a sellout success and received widespread critical acclaim, racking up sixteen 4 and 5 star reviews, making it one of the best reviewed comedy shows of 2023.  \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Liam Withnail: Big Strong Boy","instanceDates":"6 November-8 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"639203AQBNQRCVBBSBNBCMHGDHPGHCKVL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-06T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-06T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-08T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-08T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Following a critically acclaimed run at the Edinburgh Fringe, Liam Withnail takes his hit show Chronic Boom on his first UK tour. \r\nJoin the gifted comic storyteller with over 10 million TikTok and Instagram views as he battles chronic illness and hilariously reckons with his new reality during a hospital stay. \r\n\r\nThis enlightening stand-up show about how we adapt when life throws a curveball takes audiences on a rollercoaster of laughter and packs an emotional punch. \r\n\r\nWinner: Amused Moose Award for Outstanding Show 2019 and Scottish Comedy Award. Finalist of both Scottish and English Comedian of the Year. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Liam Withnail: Chronic Boom","instanceDates":"8 April-10 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"514003ACCDPQGTHQNQBGKJCCLJSHSNMRN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-08T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-08T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-10T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-10T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Baddest. Cowboy. Texas.\r\nThese are just a few words to describe the Baddest Cowboy in Texas. He roots n’ toots n’ roots from the mightiest mountains to the sauciest saloons.\r\nBut what happens when a Badder Cowboy-er Texas-er (AKA his nemesis) rides into town and steals his title?\r\nBANGTAIL is an epic tale of a man in search of his manhood. So saddle up for an hour of unbridled cowboy clown chaos as our hero journeys from the Wild West to the American office.\r\nAfter touring the US, Australia, and selling out the Edinburgh Fringe run 2024, BANGTAIL is ready to ride again.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lil Wenker: Bangtail","instanceDates":"19 June-19 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"616203AHNHVSPBNLSBNNMJGCBKDLMDRVT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-19T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-19T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-19T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-19T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Baddest. Cowboy. Texas. These are just a few words to describe the Baddest Cowboy in Texas. But something's missing. Join Bangtail on an epic search for his manhood.\r\nBaddest. Cowboy. Texas. These are just a few words to describe the Baddest Cowboy in Texas. Join Bangtail as he roots ‘n toots from the mightiest mountains to the sauciest saloons. But what happens when a Badder Cowboy-er Texas-er (AKA his nemesis) rides into town and steals his title?\r\nBANGTAIL is an epic tale of a man in search of his manhood. So saddle up for an hour of unbridled cowboy clown chaos as our hero journeys from the Wild West to the American office.\r\nBANGTAIL marks the first collaboration between award-nominated clown Lil Wenker and award-winning director Cecily Nash to create the perfectly stupid marriage of American and British clowning. The show racked up two award nominations at the Leicester Comedy Festival and sold-out at Pinch of Vaults. The show played a sold-out US tour with stops in New York City, Minneapolis, and Chicago before heading to Peckham and Brighton Fringe Festivals. \r\nCreative credits:\r\nLil Wenker performer/co-creator \r\nCecily Nash director/co-creator\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lil Wenker: BANGTAIL.","instanceDates":"7 November-9 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"571803APMLJDVMTDRVTMJPGMJJVKLQMPC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-07T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-07T22:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-09T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-09T22:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"All hail BOYKING! Eight-year-old Prince Wilfred (Willy for short) seeks power at all costs including but not limited to: death, destruction and dastardly deeds. Nowhere near in line for the throne, Prince Wilfred ruminates on a plan for total world domination while guzzling mummy's milk. Bow down - this coronation's a killer. Created by the award-winning performer / director duo Lil Wenker and Cecily Nash. 16+ (Check webpage for content advice)","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lil Wenker: BOYKING","instanceDates":"15 December-19 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"757803APKMGCPCHJNPNNLNCSBGBPKTPMJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-15T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-15T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-19T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-19T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"All hail BOYKING! \r\nEight-year-old Prince Wilfred (Willy for short) seeks power at all costs including but not limited to: death, destruction and dastardly deeds. Nowhere near in line for the throne, Prince Wilfred ruminates on a plan for total world domination while guzzling mummy's milk. \r\nBow down–this coronation's a killer. \r\nCreated by the award-winning performer / director duo Lil Wenker and Cecily Nash.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lil Wenker: BOYKING WIP","instanceDates":"5 June-5 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"714603AKSKRDHDCGDLNBNLTNPKBTBHJMP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-05T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-05T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-05T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-05T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Back with a new hour, Lily Phillips (not that one) has had a baby and she and her perineum are fuming.\r\nFollowing her critically-acclaimed run at this year’s Edinburgh Fringe, Crying transfers to Soho Theatre.\r\n \r\nLily Phillips, as seen on ITV, BBC, Comedy Central and E4 returns with her brand-new, hilarious, and unapologetically honest show, delving into the taboo truths of childbirth, IVF, early motherhood and mental health.\r\n \r\nDirected by Jordan Brookes.\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lily Phillips: Crying","instanceDates":"13 April-14 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"693203ASLHGSTHBVGHBSBTHMLMTNJPBDQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-13T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-13T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-14T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-14T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Alright bab!? Northfield's finest makes a triumphant return to Brum after a glorious Edinburgh Fringe saw her pick up a Best Newcomer Nomination (Edinburgh Comedy Awards) and winning The Biggest Prize in Comedy for her debut stand-up hour Pink Tinge.\r\nSince appearing as part of Best in Class in 2018, Lindsey has made numerous appearances across TV, radio and podcasts, including Comedy Central Live and Sarah Millican's Elephant in the Room & Fresh From The Fringe (BBC Radio 4). She has recently supported Joe Lycett on tour including support at Wembley Arena. Other accolades include 2021 Finalist at the British Comedian of the Year.\r\n★ ★ ★ ★ ★ - Theatre Weekly\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lindsey Santoro: Pink Tinge","instanceDates":"25 January-27 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"500203ADBRKNJCDGLTLQLBHJTQHDMDMDK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-25T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-25T21:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-27T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-27T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Verity Bargate award-winning production from Eoin McAndrew, directed by Emma Jordan.\r\n“I’d like you to promise me that you’re not going to try and set yourself on fire again. That way I’ll know that everything is completely fine now.”\r\nWhen Brigid gets a call from her brother Niall in the middle of the night, she knows something’s wrong. After he ends up in hospital, Niall moves in with Brigid as she helps him piece his life back together. Little Brother is a compelling exploration of a sibling relationship set in modern-day Belfast directed by Emma Jordan, award-winning Artistic Director of Prime Cut Productions.\r\nEoin McAndrew’s darkly comic and beautifully observed new play shines a light on the crisis of care in Northern Ireland, the strength of a brother-sister bond and the unpredictable journey towards recovery. Sometimes being there for the people you love is very very very difficult.\r\nAnupama Chandrasekhar: ‘Little Brother is a masterfully crafted, heart-wrenching play…a rare gem”\r\nMoira Buffini: “Little Brother has great theatricality, humour and compassion. It stayed with me long after I had finished reading.”\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Little Brother","instanceDates":"17 October-22 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"619803AJNPNNDJLBNHDPHSPTKNDDGVLNT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-17T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-17T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-22T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-22T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Little Lord Fondleroy is a saccharine nightmare in velvet and lace, whose cherubic curls and perfect manners provide foolproof cover for his constant yearnings- primarily for poetry, pleasure, head boys and complete theatrical chaos. \r\nIn this riotous hour, whirl through a formative annus eroticus at Flippitts Darstardly Boarding School for Badly Behaved Boys, where forbidden desires flourish amidst a sadistic culture of cruelty cultivated by prefects and masters alike. Here, Fondleroy discovers that masculinity and Empire are stitched together by caning, cunning and carefully repressed desire. \r\nCan he retain his innocent charm and boyish over-generosity while the forces around him attempt to stamp all that soppy, frilly, froppy feeling out of him? \r\nEnter a world of boarding-school heartbreak, homoerotic hijinks, and imperial intrigue. \r\nFusing drag, theatre and music, this hilariously subversive show rips open hidden histories to reveal the queer desires that have always been lurking beneath.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Little Lord Fondleroy: Amo, Amas, Amat & All That!","instanceDates":"14 February-14 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"685003ARKJKBQDMTCQRCJLCHMNVCQKLSS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-14T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-14T22:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-14T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-14T22:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Soho Theatre and Little Sing Song have teamed up to bring some song into our new venue for families this summer.\r\nA fun and heart-warming group for babies, toddlers and their grown ups to come together and enjoy singing some of the favourite songs…and we don’t just mean nursery rhymes.\r\n\r\nFrom Classical to Jazz, Pop to Reggae and more! Expect a bit of ukulele and a whole load of smiles.\r\n\r\n “Born from a love of children’s classics but also a longing to attend concerts with my babies, these sessions don’t just include your little one’s favourite nursery rhymes but your song requests too” Danie\r\n●\t10.30: Sing Song (it’s good for the soul after all!)\r\n●\t11.00: Chit Chat (because a daytime conversation with another adult can be pretty awesome)\r\n●\t11.15: Bye Byes (until next time…)\r\n0+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":45,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Little Sing Song: Fun singalongs for little ones and their grown ups","instanceDates":"13 May-2 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"620203AHGQQLLNJKLPMLBHNGJTDHGKNPT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-13T10:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-13T09:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-02T10:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-02T10:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Families","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Come and party with LMAOnaise!\r\nFor five years, LMAOnaise Comedy has been telling you the best comedy to see in the UK and now they’re telling you that it’s right here on the Soho Theatre stage.\r\nLine-up:\r\nKate Cheka\r\nJodie Mitchell\r\nRosalie Minnitt\r\nTemi Wilkey\r\nAlex Franklin\r\nSiblings\r\nCiara O'Connor\r\nHost: Maia Tassalini\r\n \r\nJoin us for a night of side-splitting comedy and stay for a bit of a boogie, with comedians on the DJ decks after hours. \r\nLMAOnaise Comedy is an award-winning newsletter, print mag and website recommending and reviewing comedy, but in like a fun and nice way! No mean reviews, no star ratings and no all-white, all-male line-ups. LMAOnaise champions the absolute best in alternative and up-and-coming comedians!\r\nThis show is raising funds to get LMAOnaise Comedy to the Edinburgh Fringe, so we can carry on with our mission to keep uplifting great comedy through encouraging reviews and some good old-fashioned being nice to each other.\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":80,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"LMAOnaise Comedy’s Big Birthday Fundraiser!","instanceDates":"17 April-17 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"706003AQRHPKGHJPTKRNCLTPSNPHSJVJS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-17T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-17T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-17T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-17T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join us as we celebrate the opening of the 2025 London Clown Festival with a cabaret featuring some of the festival’s acts alongside some of London’s finest performers from outside of the festival.\r\nThis is a high energy night that gives you a taste of what's to come in the festival overall.\r\nCome for a night of fun and laughter and discover more to come back for.\r\nFull line up to be announced soon.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"London Clown Festival Opening Cabaret","instanceDates":"16 June-16 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"615204AHRJLNLVHQNRHMRLVJKQGSHNHHT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-16T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-16T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-16T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-16T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Ten of the world's funniest clowns compete for the highly prestigious CLONG award. Who will be crowned the biggest idiot of all?\r\nHosted by award-winning clown duo Dan Lees and Neil Frost aka The Establishment.\r\n★★★★ ‘They are clowns of the highest order’ (A Younger Theatre)\r\n★★★★★ ‘Off-the-wall, zany, crazy, very funny’ Glam Adelaide\r\n★★★★ ‘Silliness as an art form’ The Scotsman\r\n\"These skilful clowns clearly know how to work the audience and it’s a joy to witness the effects of such assured absurdity.\" Total Theatre\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"London Clown Festival Present CLONG","instanceDates":"16 June-16 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"477204AVGJCQDHJJMDDQNBCRVQJNGCPLR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-16T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-16T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-16T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-16T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Always a fun night to tick off the London Clown Festival.\r\nJoin us as we celebrate the opening of the 2023 London Clown Festival with a cabaret featuring some of the 2023 festival’s acts alongside some of London’s finest performers from outside of the festival. This is a high energy night gives you a taste of what's to come in the festival overall. \r\nCome for a night of fun and laughter and discover more to come back for. \r\nFull line up available soon.\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"London Clown Festival: 2023 Opening Cabaret","instanceDates":"12 June-12 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"478003ADPSLPRHMVDVCVMSMLSGHKJQRLL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-12T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-12T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-12T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-12T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_Venue":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Always a fun night to kick off the London Clown Festival. Come for an evening of fun and laughter and discover more to come back for throughout the week.\r\nJoin us as we celebrate the opening of the 2024 London Clown Festival with a cabaret featuring some of the festival’s acts alongside some of London’s finest performers from outside of the festival. \r\n\r\nThis is a high energy night that gives you a taste of what's to come in the festival overall. \r\n\r\nCome for a night of fun and laughter and discover more to come back for.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"London Clown Festival: Opening Cabaret.","instanceDates":"8 July-8 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"542603ANMJKLNDRDTPBGJMDNHGMLCKJGP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-08T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-08T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-08T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-08T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Award-winning character comedian Lorna Rose Treen has made a diner.\r\nShe's inviting you in for an hour of characters, nonsense and a working grill. (Now with no working grill!)\r\n\r\nAfterwards, you'll turn to your neighbour and say, 'I'll have what she's having!'\r\nFollowing multiple sell-out Soho Theatre and Edinburgh Fringe runs, the critically-acclaimed Lorna Rose Treen is back with a brand new show.\r\n\r\nChortle’s Best Sketch Act 2024.\r\nDave's Funniest Joke of the Fringe 2023.\r\nTelegraph Top 5 Comedy Shows 2023.\r\nCreator/star of Radio 4's Time of the Week.\r\n\r\nDirected by Jonathan Oldfield.\r\n14+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lorna Rose Treen: 24 Hour Diner People","instanceDates":"8 September-13 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"650403AHLBCQHQJBJTSRPKGDDNGCBKVGR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-08T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-08T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-13T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-13T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Sketch","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Lorna Rose Treen brings her smash-hit debut show back to Soho Theatre for a limited run of four final performances.\r\nCharacter comedian Lorna Rose Treen has been pretending to be other people for fun since she could dress herself. Now she's inviting you inside her mind for an hour of characters, comedy, content, content, content, costumes and content. The greatest thing to come out of Redditch since the fishing tackle. The debut show from Chortle's Best Newcomer 2023 and Funny Women Awards' first-ever double winner (2022). 'I laughed so much I violently bit my tongue' (Independent). \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lorna Rose Treen: Skin Pigeon","instanceDates":"3 July-6 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"535203APRLJPMHCGPJPVCJTSBQJJMQKQN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-03T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-03T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-06T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-06T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Character comedian Lorna Rose Treen has been pretending to be other people for fun since she could dress herself. Now she's inviting you inside her mind for an hour of characters, comedy, content, content, content, costumes and content. The greatest thing to come out of Redditch since the fishing tackle. The debut show from Chortle's Best Newcomer 2023 and Funny Women Awards' first-ever double winner (2022). 'I laughed so much I violently bit my tongue' (Independent). \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lorna Rose Treen: Skin Pigeon.","instanceDates":"19 October-28 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"493203ACMRBBBHLPMLNSJKRNJQBQLTBHS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-19T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-19T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-28T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-28T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Sketch","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Critically acclaimed debut from viral sensation Lou Taylor. A coming-of-age tale. But less Call Me By Your Name and more 'text me on your Nokia'.\r\nWhy live in the present when you could live in the past? Join Lou as she dives back in time to her happy place: the 90s. As heard on Brett Goldstein's Films to be Buried With. As seen in The Guardian. Over 20 million views online. 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lou Taylor: Jeans and a nice top","instanceDates":"10 February-10 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"588403AJGSNHJMJBPNDHHLTLDSRGQKRVL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-10T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-10T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-10T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-10T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"An intense multi layered multimedia extravaganza. This show looks at friendship, jealousy, our relationship with technology, and our relationship with ourselves.\r\nI want you to think of the person you are most jealous of. This is a show about them. Well it's also about me. And murder and the internet. Comedian Lou Wall brings you their most ambitious comedy hour yet in Lou Wall vs The Internet. A high-octane, action-packed story about the Wild Wild West of the World Wide Web. This internet battle royale is brought to you by a Gen Z who would rather tell you their pin number than their daily screen time. \r\n\r\n'The voice of a generation' **** Chortle\r\n***** Funny Women\r\n***** Arts Hub\r\n***** Comic’s Comic\r\n***** Mervyn Stutter’s Pick of the Fringe\r\n***** Lilithia Reviews\r\n***** Impulse Gamer\r\n**** Scotsman\r\n**** The Age\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lou Wall vs The Internet","instanceDates":"18 September-23 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"494803APPTBLSQRRCMBMGQVRDQRGKJPJH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-18T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-18T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-23T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-23T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A new show by Lou Wall about lying, mental breakdowns and the internet. Featuring Wall’s signature meme-fuelled PowerPoints and musical comedy, Breaking the Fifth Wall is a forensic and frankly ludicrous deep dive into the space where performance and reality collide. Nothing and everything is as it seems. Directed by Zoë Coombs Marr. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lou Wall: Breaking the Fifth Wall","instanceDates":"10 November-22 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"636803AJTHKDLRVSDQGBTNTSBJKDHRBJL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-10T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-10T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-22T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-22T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"In 2023, Lou Wall was the first ever lesbian* to go through a breakup.\r\nIn 2024 Lou Wall will be the first EVER** comedian to write a show about heartbreak. Fuelled entirely by delusion, tequila and the girls' group chat, this is a journey from the pits of personal hell to comic stardom***. Featuring Lou's signature musical comedy, deranged Powerpoints and mentally ill hot takes, this show will make you 100% gayer (derogatory) and cure your depression or your money back.\r\n\r\n*Eat my ass.\r\n**No srlsly ... eat it.\r\n***The open-mic circuit.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lou Wall: The Bisexual’s Lament","instanceDates":"11 November-15 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"569403AQGNQSKQPSKPMVTSRJSPSCNGVCM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-11T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-11T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-15T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-15T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Edinburgh Comedy Awards Best Newcomer nominee 2023.\r\nNextUp BIGGEST Award in Comedy nominee 2023.\r\nLeicester Comedy Festival Best Debut show nominee 2022.\r\nDebut hour from Geordie rising star with a show all about class, chaos and coming out. She did ask her friends if her life had been feral enough to warrant this title they laughed and assured her it still is. Tour support for Alan Carr and Tom Allen. As seen on Comedy Central Live and Channel 4's Original Comedy shorts. As heard On BBC Radio 4’s Fred at the Stand\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Louise Young: Feral","instanceDates":"25 January-27 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"500403AGDTQJDBRPBPKCTDPCNBGSJSBGH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-25T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-25T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-27T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-27T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Follow the journey of Sanjay, as he navigates through life trying to find love as a gaysian man in British society today.\r\nWhilst working away in his bookshop, Sanjay shares stories of his journey to find love, trying to find the one. As he recounts his stories, his neurodelicious mind takes him on tangents and his childhood love of Bollywood matches his emotions of his dates. Through sipping his chai, he shares what made him gay and they journey to be his authentic self today. \r\nThis show first started its journey for the Vaults Festival 2023, before winning the Emerging Talent Award from the Neurodiverse Review Awards in Fringe 2024 after 2 wee sharings and Sanjay is excited to bring this next iteration to Soho Rising.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Love Me Like A Chai Tea Latee by Sanjay Lago","instanceDates":"10 February-11 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"591203AVCCKMJTPQSTVMKQQQPRRQJMMDH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-10T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-10T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-11T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-11T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"by Katie Sayer and William Johnston\r\nFresh from a 5-star sold-out run at VAULT Festival: Meet Ben and Cyrus, this year's winners of TV's biggest reality-cum-dating show.\r\nThey're 22, they have hundreds of thousands of followers - and now, 6 months on from the show that catapulted them to fame, they're spending most of their time promoting vegan dog food, and making sponsored content about lawnmowers. Ben wants to return to his old life – while Cyrus just wants his Instagram to reach 1 million followers. When they’re offered a million-pound influencing deal in Dubai, the world looks on to see what L*ve Isl*nd’s first LGBT sweethearts will do. \r\n\r\nStarring James Akka (Pleading Stupidity, Pleasance) and Iain Ferrier (BBC 5Live) and directed by Phoebe Gibby (Spring Awakening, Anthony Burgess Foundation).\r\n\r\nWritten by Will Johnston (Netflix’s The Diplomat, National Theatre) and Katie Sayer (BBC Radio 4’s The Skewer, BBC Television). \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Love's A Beach","instanceDates":"8 February-8 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"521803AGQMCNHCBQGBHGBHLMHHCLRNRQT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-08T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-08T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-08T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-08T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"Lucy McCormick is back with her most ambitious medium-concept catastrophic show yet.\r\nJoin Lucy as she unveils her ensemble cabaret tent spectacular… Unfortunately, she has no friends, no money, and no tent.\r\n\r\nStill, there’ll be pole dancing, variety acts, strip routines and some quick reworking of social policy.\r\n\r\nIn a despairing world, lonely Lucy creates community, connection, and conversation the only way she knows how.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lucy & Friends","instanceDates":"27 February-16 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"514603ASCQQCGSKGNNPPSBSCBLDSSJVQR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-27T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-27T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-16T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-16T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"Lucy Beaumont returns with Bad at Quiz Shows, Good with Weirdos — a surreal, chaotic stand-up show proving that normal is massively overrated.\r\nLucy Beaumont has had quite the year. She lost a contestant £79,000 on The Wheel, forgot to revise for Mastermind, and generally confirmed she's terrible at quiz shows. So, she's sticking with what she does best - this autumn, she's back on the road with a brand-new show. \r\n\r\nFollowing the success of her sell-out debut UK tour, Lucy returns with Bad at Quiz Shows, Good with Weirdos - an evening packed with chaotic brilliance, mayhem, and beautifully surreal storytelling that's made her one of the UK's most beloved comedians. \r\n\r\nExpect tales of going into hiding after Celebrity Traitors, creating cow udder couture on The Great British Sewing Bee, and navigating life as someone for whom \"normal\" has never made much of an appearance. \r\n\r\nWhether you loved her on Taskmaster, know her from her award-winning sitcom, or just appreciate someone who turns everyday disasters into comedic gold, this is the night out you need. Come for the chaos. Stay for the weirdos.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lucy Beaumont: Bad at Quiz Shows, Good with Weirdos","instanceDates":"25 October-25 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"694203AQBHGMRJGBDKRBQLPKCGJHVBSJK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-25T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-25T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-25T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-25T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Welcome to the future. Two liberated elders share the wisdom from their lives so far in the form of nourishing baked goods. Expect nothing. Biscuits included.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lucy Hopkins & Lexi Strauss","instanceDates":"6 August-8 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"730803ATTVPVMLCVQSCPBGCJNQQGQQLKB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-06T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-06T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-08T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-08T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Welcome to the future.\r\nTwo liberated elders share the wisdom from their lives so far in the form of nourishing baked goods. \r\nExpect nothing. \r\nBiscuits included.\r\n18+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lucy Hopkins & Lexi Strauss june","instanceDates":"3 June-3 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"713204ABSLDHRRNKKCTCKRTCVBCKBJCTV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-03T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-03T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-03T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-03T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Calling the sweet, the courageous, the devoted and the broken to a ceremony of twinkling in the depths: a ritual of healing, a prayer to Mother and an unquantifiably silly time in the dark. \r\n\r\nBrought humbly to you by everybody’s favourite clown-priestess, light-braider, shadow-dancer and Dark Mother Lucy Hopkins.\r\n\r\nUtterly loving, always preposterous. \r\n\r\nBehold! A shining light in the deepest depths!\r\n\r\nDon't be afraid of the dark. Mummy's here.\r\n\r\n“Hopkins is fantastic” Guardian\r\n16+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lucy Hopkins: Dark Mother","instanceDates":"1 April-10 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"460603AKBVHSVGJGCLLJTKVBVKPTLNRMQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-01T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-01T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-10T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-10T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Everything is Sacred. Magic is Reality. Shhh. Tell Evryone\r\nCalling the courageous, the devoted, the faithless and the broken to the interactive ceremony of togetherness we always hoped we’d never need. A divination and reading of the collective hidden depths, probably, if you want. Hosted by everybody’s favourite priestess/shapeshifter/person Lucy Hopkins. Everything is sacred. Magic is reality. Shhhh. Tell Evryone.“Hopkins is fantastic” The Guardian\r\n“A legend among Gaulier clowns” ★★★★ The Scotsman\r\n“Only Lucy Hopkins can Lucy Hopkins like Lucy Hopkins” ★★★★★ Fringe Review\r\n“Lucy Hopkins… will transform you” ★★★★★ EdFringeReview\r\nLucy Hopkins is an internationally touring, award-winning \r\nclown/director/teacher/lover of humans. \r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lucy Hopkins: SECRT CIRCL","instanceDates":"15 June-15 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"477603ATPQHNLQDTLVDHBRBCLLQBJLJDC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-15T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-15T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-15T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-15T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Come and spend an hour with the moon while she tries her absolute best. \r\nLucy Pearman is working out a new show and wobbling around as the moon. \r\nThere will definitely be a song, a cow and in an ideal world, an audience.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lucy Pearman (Work in Progress)","instanceDates":"6 August-8 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"562203APCCDTRGVNKKKJCCGNSTLHJMHGG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-06T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-06T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-08T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-08T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"The Moon dreams of stardom so she's popped down to perform her new show.\r\nLucy Pearman (BAFTA and Edinburgh Comedy Award nominee) returns to Soho Theatre with optimistic and interactive lunacy. Leicester Comedy Festival Best Variety Show nominee 2025. \r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lucy Pearman: Lunartic","instanceDates":"29 September-4 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"653203AMCHSKHBKRCKLPTDCLBRHMJRPPQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-29T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-29T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-04T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-04T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"60 minutes, 60 impressions, one murder.\r\nStar of the West End production of Les Miserables, Luke Kempner brings his British police drama musical to Soho Theatre. \r\nIt’s Line Of Duty meets Happy Valley meets Clarkson’s Farm, meets Match of the Day meets The Traitors. Whether you’re King Charles, Ian McKellen or Claudia Winkleman, in GRITTY POLICE DRAMA... no-one is safe.\r\n As seen (and heard) on The Last Leg (C4), The Stand-Up Sketch Show (ITV2), Spitting Image (Britbox and the West End production) Steph's Packed Lunch (Channel 4) Love Island: Aftersun (ITV2) and The Now Show (BBCR4).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Luke Kempner in Gritty Police Drama: A One Man Musical","instanceDates":"23 April-27 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"528403ACNBPKVCQGDRDQSKHKQJPLBJBMH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-23T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-23T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-27T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-27T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A father approaching his 60th birthday learns to sing and dance for the first time, in a desperate attempt to create a hit single that will make enough money for his son to finally move out.\r\nOne of these was a series regular on Channel 4's 'Joe Lycett's got your back'. The other one wasn't happy about that. \r\n\r\n\"Mark Silcox and Luke McQueen brought hilarity, with terrible singing from McQueen, ridiculous personas and wardrobe and a dry, awkward style of humour. The audience was in stitches.\" Broadwaybaby\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Luke McQueen and Mark Silcox: Songs with my Father","instanceDates":"7 December-9 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"501603AMNLNMCPTLKBVTKVMLGSBGJNDCJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-07T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-07T22:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-09T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-09T22:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Episode 1043 features Luke McQueen, a fearless innovator who blurs the line between reality and performance. This conversation is so essential, it's being repeated every night at Soho Theatre. \r\nDirected by Jordan Brookes.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Luke McQueen: Comedian's Comedian","instanceDates":"10 November-15 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"655203AMCGQGGNKHKQVVDGSJBHTJMPNPH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-10T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-10T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-15T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-15T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Fringe favourite and Disney Prince heartthrob of Extraordinary (Disney+) descends from his ivory (Fairtrade) tower to glisten your eyes with this monument to creativity, fantasy and the wishes you wish you never wished. (wish show) \r\n\r\nTake a swan-dive into this physical comedy fantasia of kings and clowns, and one absolutely hideous duck. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Luke Rollason, Luke Rollason, Let Down Your Hair ","instanceDates":"4 June-7 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"610203ALNMGVTNRMPVJPQJDRCHPKBVLTP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-04T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-04T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-07T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-07T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The star of Disney+ series Extraordinary returns to the roost with his best show yet. \r\nIt’s an absurd ode to the great indoors and the relationships we form with the objects we fill it with – the armchair singing the lost loves that left behind their bum imprints, abandoned utensils with uncertain parenthood, and the sordid spooning going on in your cutlery drawer. \r\nLike visiting IKEA on acid, this is a psychedelic domestic breakdown that will make you totally rethink your mundane little life. \r\nWelcome to the Great Indoors. \r\nREVIEWS: (I would probably lead with the Telegraph quote) \r\n\"Utterly delightful... gloriously daft\" ★★★★ Telegraph\r\n\"Makes the commonplace hilarious and mesmerising\" OR \"Hilarious and mesmerising\" ★★★★ Chortle\r\n\"A madcap potpourri of mime and existential angst\" ★★★★ The List\r\n\"the master of running visual gags\" ★★★★ Wee Review\r\n\"Squeezes sunshine into the eyeballs of everyone in the room\" ★★★★ Entertainment Focus\r\n\"Utterly, wonderfully mental\" ★★★★ Entertainment Now\r\n\"One of the best shows at the Festival, full stop\" British Comedy Guide \r\n \r\nOne of the Telegraph's Top Shows of 2022\r\nSHORTLISTED: Best Show in the Comedians Choice Awards 2022\r\n\r\nUnder cast:\r\nLuke Rollason\r\nWriter and Performer \r\n\r\nMikey Bligh-Smith\r\nCo-Performer\r\n\r\nUnder creatives:\r\nObjectively Funny\r\nProducer\r\n\r\nLuke Howarth\r\nDirector\r\n\r\nMichael Julings\r\nArtistic Director\r\n\r\nKit Sullivan\r\nAdditional Music\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Luke Rollason:  Bowerbird","instanceDates":"5 July-15 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"446403ANNKHVLTHCLNVKDNDLKMQQLKQRG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-05T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-05T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-15T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-15T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"In her hit Edinburgh debut, comedian and failed child actor Lulu Popplewell, explores the links between Love Actually, smoking crack, the Daily Mail and sunburn. Is love actually all around? Why is addiction more relatable than recovery? Which drug would Mr Bean be most likely to take? \r\nNone of these questions satisfactorily answered and more!* A daft, rude and thoughtful hour of jokes, actually. *One song.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lulu Popplewell: Actually, Actually","instanceDates":"30 May-30 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"533603ASBLCTGKNKJVSPLGPDMSKBNPPNJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-30T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-30T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-30T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-30T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"William Hanson and Jonathan Vernon-Smith bring you ‘The Luxury Podcast’ Live! 18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Luxury Live","instanceDates":"22 November-22 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"735403ANCDJLGVJLSHBPTHPMCVJRKHDGT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-22T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-22T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-22T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-22T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A topsy turvy mad-as-a-hatter tea party inspired by the upcoming production of Alice in Wonderland. Enjoy snacks and drinks all hosted by colourful characters inspired by the World of Wonderland. The tea party is designed for children and adults to participate in together and as such all participants including adults and children require a ticket. There will be a selection of vegetarian and nut-free sharing snacks alongside individually served tea-time treats, so you’ll be asked to specify any dietary requirements during the booking process. ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":45,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Mad Hatter's Tea Party","instanceDates":"25 July-25 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"740603ANVRJTPJQCDTNSCVDKBNQPLSRPB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-25T12:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-25T11:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-25T13:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-25T12:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Families","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"A dystopian goddess moves in the empty space in an attempt to run away from the stillness. Part of London Clown Festival 2024.\r\nMadame Señorita creates HERz, intrigued by the universe of myths and the concept of hero vs. lover, in a piece that explores the limits of freedom and love. This, plus lots of playing around and teasing silliness.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Madame Señorita: HERz","instanceDates":"12 July-12 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"543803AGQKSHQCLRNJGTNNQKMCBMLDMDJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-12T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-12T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-12T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-12T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Roo is a deaf Punjabi boy from Birmingham, living in a world that wasn't made for him. Through pain and laughter, Roo narrates the impact of ableism and racism throughout his childhood and adult life, leading him to confront one key question: \"Where do I belong?\" All performances will be in BSL, Spoken English and Closed Captions. Director Tyrone Huggins Dramaturge Daniel Bailey Confident and Charismatic - The Stage Barpaga is a remarkable storyteller - FestMagazine ★★★★ Powerful Physicality - The Limping Chicken ★★★★★ 14+ recommendation","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":65,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Made in (India) Britain","instanceDates":"27 June-30 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"467003ASBVQLCCGCGRVJSPKGGPRBBPHGT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-27T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-27T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-30T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-30T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Access","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"What does it take to become a legend?\r\nFresh from a sell-out run at the Edinburgh Fringe, Madeleine Brettingham explores what growing up in a world of booze-soaked bad behaviour taught her about how man becomes myth. 16+ (See webpage for content advice).\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Madeleine Brettingham: Legend ","instanceDates":"29 October-31 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"749603ANVSVGGMCTBJJLBPNGVRSBMQLTM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-29T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-29T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-31T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-31T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Globally acclaimed magician, content creator, and performer Magic Singh comes to Soho Theatre for one night only with an evening of unforgettable magic. 14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Magic Singh: Live","instanceDates":"8 December-9 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"759203ASJTMHPQPKLGKLVPSMJLHDDTHVK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-08T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-08T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-09T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-09T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"This is Temi’s show. It’s all about her. Not you. Her.\r\nTemi got veeeery good at being everybody’s sassy best friend. Growing up a black girl in a white world shunts you into playing a side character in your own life. But now she’s stepping into her Main Character Energy and it’s your privi-lege, your honour, your pre-eminent pleasure to give her all the attention she deserves. As self-aware as it is self-indulgent, this show is a high-energy cocktail of comedy, au-dience interaction and cabaret. An excuse to show Soho how radiant Temi is.\r\n12+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":65,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Main Character Energy","instanceDates":"25 February-15 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"583403ACDPBNTHRMBHVVJDTMVMRMLKJHJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-25T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-25T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-15T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-15T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"A night of People of Colour singing Karaoke, hosted by Temi Wilkey. There are few things Temi Wilkey is more passionate about than Karaoke. \r\nNothing says Main Character Energy like choosing a song you love and sharing it with others, no matter how good you are at singing. Temi is inviting performers of colour and people of colour in the audience to take up space with her onstage by singing a song. It’s not about polish and all about com-mitment, this is Karaoke after all! This will be a space for self-indulgence, POC community-building and, above all, joy. \r\nThere’s nothing like singing with a room full of people and the evening’s host will definitely be encouraging the audi-ence to sing along.\r\n12+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":45,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Main Character Energy: Karaoke Kabaret","instanceDates":"5 March-5 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"586803ASVRGBSTKSGVDTGKKRRPQDCCQBQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-05T21:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-05T21:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-05T21:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-05T21:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"Straight off the back of Taskmaster, A League Of Their Own, and Last One Laughing, Maisie Adam is back with her new show Whatsherface.\r\nJoin the “tall, chaotic one with the weird hair” * as she returns with her trademark wit, firecracker gags, and probably a few angry outbursts along the way. \r\n*A genuine description given by her best friend’s Mum at a wedding this year. \r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Maisie Adam: Whatsherface","instanceDates":"11 March-11 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"727604ALPPPHLHSCRCKCLNTMLGNPVPVVM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-03-11T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-03-11T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-03-11T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-03-11T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":180,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Makers’ Lab 2025","instanceDates":"7 June-7 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"635203AHJVHMJNMCJQSKTNJSDMGMSCPMH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-07T10:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-07T09:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-07T10:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-07T09:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow Studio 1","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Come see extracts of eight exciting, genre-bending and powerful new shows created as part of our brand-new flagship talent development programme: Makers' Lab.Over the last eight months, ten up-and-coming artists have created eight hour-long shows that play with the intersection between different artforms - comedians, theatre-makers, drag performers, puppeteers and more. This performance will showcase eight formally inventive, fun & punchy stories which will take you on a journey from Japanese myth to Apartheid South Africa, from Bollywood to Hammersmith, from comedy & cabaret to shadow puppetry.\r\n\r\nOur artists presenting work are: Alice Wordsworth & Joe Young, Diana Feng, Fatima Serghini, Genevieve Sabherwal, Kathryn Bond, Mikey Bligh-Smith, Shafeeq Shajahan & Vasilis Konstantinides, and Simi Roach. They have been guided through the Lab by lead facilitator Ben Target, with support from many guest artists and the Soho team. \r\n \r\nIf you want to check out thrilling new work by the next generation of talent's most promising artists, or if you’re interested in applying for Makers’ Lab yourself, come to the Makers' Lab showcase!\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Makers’ Lab Showcase Feb26","instanceDates":"2 February-2 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"686604APSVDPSDRGKQRKLKLDSQRNGQMCS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-02T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-02T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-02T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-02T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Work In Progress","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"Makrooh: an evening of spoken word and music performed by British Muslim artists.\r\nWith a live band leading us through the night, we’ll be taking some time to connect with community and self for some much needed respite in these turbulent times. There’ll also be an open mic for all of our budding performers in the audience who have something to express. Makrooh events are more than just entertainment — they are a safe space for learning, growth and collective joy.\r\nHeadliners to be announced soon.\r\n\r\nWe believe that art should be accessible to all. If the full ticket price poses a challenge, please contact us at info@makrooh.co.uk\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":150,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Makrooh 23","instanceDates":"16 December-16 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"512803ASLCRSCBSQRPKJJJKHLVBLQNGTC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-16T15:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-16T15:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-16T15:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-16T15:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Performance Art","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Makrooh: an evening of spoken word and music performed by British Muslim artists.\r\nWith a live band leading us through the night, we’ll be taking some time to connect with community and self for some much needed respite in these turbulent times. There’ll also be an open mic for all of our budding performers in the audience who have something to express. Makrooh events are more than just entertainment — they are a safe space for learning, growth and collective joy.\r\nHeadliners to be announced soon.\r\n \r\nWe believe that art should be accessible to all. If the full ticket price poses a challenge, please contact us at info@makrooh.co.uk\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":180,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Makrooh 24","instanceDates":"11 January-11 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"590804ABNPPBSTHVMVSBBBHQQCBJQQQRJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-11T15:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-11T15:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-11T15:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-11T15:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Performance Art","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Makrooh: an afternoon of spoken word and music performed by British Muslim artists.\r\nMakrooh is more than a stage—it’s a space where we celebrate our voices, our stories, and the communities that shape us.\r\nIn a world where Muslim artists are often overlooked, we carve out a night that centers us—our joy, our artistry, and the power of collective expression. With a live band improvising throughout the evening, four headlining Muslim artists will take us on a journey through poetry, comedy, music, and storytelling.\r\nAnd the mic? It’s open. This is for the poets, the comics, the truth-tellers, and the musicians who want to take up space and be heard. Whether you’re stepping up or cheering from the crowd, you are part of this moment.\r\nMakrooh isn’t just a showcase—it’s a celebration of the artists and communities who are doing the work. Those who create, resist, and build spaces of belonging despite the narratives that try to erase us.\r\nHeadliners announced soon.\r\nWe believe art should be accessible to all. If the full ticket price is a barrier, reach out to us at info@makrooh.co.uk—we’ve got you.\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":180,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Makrooh 25","instanceDates":"5 April-5 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"613003ACDQCSGVDCDSRMTLQNCKMJNHHND","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-05T15:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-05T14:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-05T15:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-05T14:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Performance Art","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Makrooh are back at Soho Theatre for another evening of spoken word and music performed by British Muslim artists.\r\n\r\nWith a live band leading us through the night, we’ll be taking some time to celebrate our everyday heroes and those who selflessly go above and beyond. There’s also an open mic for all of our budding performers in the audience who have someone to celebrate or something to express. Makrooh events are more than just entertainment — they are a safe space for learning, growth and collective joy.\r\n\r\nHeadliners to be announced soon.\r\n\r\nWe understand that not everyone can pay the full ticket price and we want this event to be as accessible as possible. Email Makrooh by clicking here if you cannot afford a ticket and really want to come.\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Makrooh May23","instanceDates":"6 May-6 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"469003ARGPLHMRGHJTCQSHPRBSMPNNCTQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-06T15:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-06T14:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-06T15:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-06T14:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Performance Art","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Makrooh Presents: Sudan’na Foag - A fundraising night with performance and community.\r\nSudan has been engulfed in a war since 15th April 2023, and its civilians have been paying the price. Currently, Sudanese people are facing the worst famine of the last 40 years, nearly non-existent healthcare, mass displacement, and daily armed attacks. Set against active efforts to silence Sudanese people, and prevent the world from listening, this war has become one of the most profound humanitarian crises on the planet. \r\nAs artists, directors, and organisers, we are coming together to use our talents and skills in the best ways we know how. So join us in raising our voices with Makrooh presents: Sudan’na Foag - a fundraising night of performance and community. We will be continuing conversation, deepening understanding, and gathering resources for Sudanese people. \r\nThis is how we build up and sustain our community: by working towards our intertwined liberation together. The night will include poetry, music, and an auction, with all proceeds going towards providing vital resources and services for Sudanese people within Sudan, as well as for those journeying out.\r\n\r\nHeadliners to be announced via Instagram @makroohuk\r\n\r\nWe look forward to welcoming you!\r\n\r\nPhoto credits: Karari skies via ‘X’ user @mujhaeid; crowd of protesters via AFP\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":180,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Makrooh Presents: Sudan’na Foag","instanceDates":"2 September-2 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"565603AMRHHLDCRMNRCQGPVGDLKJRRLNS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-02T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-02T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-02T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-02T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Performance Art","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Drafting Futures is a scratch night dedicated to showcasing new work by emerging British Muslim playwrights. Featuring bold and authentic stories, this event provides a platform for fresh voices to explore diverse perspectives and experiences. Each script-in-hand reading offers audiences the chance to engage with new writing in its early stages, providing valuable feedback that helps shape the future development of these works.\r\n\r\nThis is more than just a night of storytelling; it’s a unique opportunity for the industry to discover and connect with rising talent. By being part of this event, you’ll witness the first steps in the development of future voices that will shape the British theatre landscape. Whether you're a theatre enthusiast or an industry professional, Drafting Futures offers a vital space for networking and connecting emerging writers with the wider theatre industry.\r\n\r\nParticipating artists to be announced soon. To stay up to date follow us @makroohuk\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Makrooh Presents… Drafting Futures","instanceDates":"14 October-14 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"575203ACQRPGKCJNCSQLNSTPNBDCQDDGP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-14T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-14T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-14T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-14T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"It’s our birthday! \r\n\r\nJoin us at Soho Theatre as we celebrate 6 years of Makrooh! Prepare for an evening of captivating spoken word, enchanting music, and heartfelt community celebration, featuring the exceptional talent of British Muslim artists. \r\n\r\nGuided by our mesmerising live band, we'll embark on a collective journey to celebrate and give thanks to the vibrant community who’ve helped shape our six-year legacy. Step up to the open mic and share your own stories of celebration and personal expression or simply sit back, enjoy a hot cup of Mama Khalid's traditional Kashmiri Pink Chai, and soak up the abundance of joyful energy that fills the air. \r\n\r\nMakrooh events are more than entertainment; they're vibrant spaces for learning, growth, and the joy of coming together.\r\n\r\nStay tuned for headliner announcements.\r\n\r\nWe believe that art should be accessible to all. If the full ticket price poses a challenge, please contact us at info@makrooh.co.uk \r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":150,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Makrooh: 6 Years of Spoken Word, Music, and Community","instanceDates":"2 September-2 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"491803ALMNTPNCQTSJGMLVRTNSTPLNJSG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-02T15:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-02T14:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-02T15:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-02T14:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Storytelling","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Maria Bamford is revered for her deeply personal and experimental comedy about mental illness.\r\nShe’s the author of the New York Times bestselling memoir Sure, I’ll Join Your Cult and is the star of four hour-long standup specials (Local Act, Weakness is the Brand, Old Baby and Maria Bamford: the special, special, special!) and the surreal, semi-autobiographical Netflix comedy series Lady Dynamite, about a comedian who suffers a nervous breakdown. \r\n\r\nMaria was the first female comic to have two half-hour Comedy Central Presents specials and starred alongside Patton Oswalt, Zach Galifianakis and Brian Posehn in The Comedians of Comedy. She also created and starred in the cult hit web series The Maria Bamford Show, in which she plays all the characters.\r\n \r\nMaria is often recognized for her prolific voiceover work, including characters on Big Mouth and its spinoff Human Resources, HouseBroken, Teenage Euthanasia, Santa, Inc., Bob’s Burgers, Bojack Horseman, Summer Camp Island, Adventure Time, Talking Tom and Friends, Legend of Korra, Puss in Boots, CatDog and PBS’s Emmy-winning series Word Girl. \r\n \r\nMaria’s late-night appearances include The Late Show with Stephen Colbert, Late Night with Seth Meyers, CONAN, The Late Late Show with James Corden and The Tonight Show. Her interview series What’s Your Ailment? deals with the various mental struggles of celebrities and is available on the Topic streaming service. Her Audible Original You Are (A Comedy) Special is a semi-mock instructional book for both standup and life.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":100,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Maria Bamford","instanceDates":"20 February-20 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"679403ASMHPPBVDHPBRSDRRBKLLPCQDTT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-20T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-20T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-20T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-20T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"One woman's attempt to write The Great Novel of the 21st Century (about all the men she's slept with).\r\nAll The Men Are Going To Hate Me follows one woman's attempt to write The Great Novel of the 21st Century (about all the men she's slept with). Part stand-up, part erotic poetry, part interpretive dance, it is an odyssey through time and sex, exploring modern romance and self-discovery.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Maria Telnikoff: All The Men Are Going To Hate Me","instanceDates":"13 February-13 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"589203APTLHQTKSMTTLVQTSHJLNGDMHTL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-13T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-13T22:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-13T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-13T22:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Reeezy returns to London with a brand new hour where she tackles everything from bugs to breakups and everything in between: laughing, Lasik and running late.\r\nMarie Faustin is a NY-based comedian and actress well known for her storytelling skills, lightning fast crowd work and ability to turn a bad date into a good story. She's hosted TV shows, live shows and radio shows in NYC. Marie has appeared in the New York Times, GQ Magazine, Broad City, HBO's That Damn Michael Che, Pause with Sam Jay and Ziwe (Showtime). She's currently hosting a dating game show called Why Are You Single in NYC to figure out wtf is wrong with us all.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Marie Faustin: Sorry I’m Late","instanceDates":"29 April-4 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"534203ATDGGSRLLQJTVCRHVSSBQKNNPSV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-29T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-29T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-04T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-04T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join Marina Hyde, one of Britain’s most popular columnists and podcasts, for a joyous and irreverent evening exploring the biggest stories from Westminster, Silicon Valley, Hollywood and more.\r\nDescribed by Phoebe Waller-Bridge as “the most lethal, vital, screamingly funny truth-teller of our time”, Marina Hyde has become one of Britain’s most popular columnists and podcasters. A Sunday Times bestselling author and co-host of the smash hit podcast The Rest is Entertainment, she has an unrivalled talent for making sense of our stranger-than-fiction times. This September, Hyde comes to venues across the UK for a live show about the state of the world, marking the launch of her new book What A Time To Be Alive! From lambasting the Trump presidency, to the increasing popularity of Nigel Farage's Reform, from the spectacle of Jeff Bezos and Lauren Sanchez’s Venice wedding to the Beckham family feud, she is chief chronicler of our gloriously chaotic age. Join her for a joyous and irreverent evening as she uses her incisive wit to skewer the biggest stories from Westminster, Silicon Valley, Hollywood and much more. You will also have the chance to ask her your questions during the Q&A.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Marina Hyde: What a Time to Be Alive!","instanceDates":"20 September-20 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"709003ADDCTVTKMJPRGGQTPBSMDCBGLHK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-20T14:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-20T13:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-20T14:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-20T13:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Storytelling","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A show about the soul, and the final installment in Marjolein's ground-breaking trilogy of standup storytelling shows in which she expertly weaves comedy and folklore to share her own personal stories.\r\nWhere her show 'Marj' explored the mind, and 'O' the body, Lein turns to the soul: what we carry, what we shed, and who we become when the stage lights dim.\r\nMarjolein was nominated for the Sir Billy Connolly Spirit of Glasgow Award in 2025, Channel 4's Sean Lock Comedy Award in 2024, and is the co-host of BBC Radio 4 Comedy series Humanwatch. \r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Marjolein Robertson: Lein","instanceDates":"17 April-17 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"693403ALRVTVPPKDJKNBPPQKQSVVQSDKC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-17T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-17T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-17T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-17T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A show about the body.\r\nMarjolein embarks on the second instalment of her standup trilogy by looking at a health condition that, left unspoken about in the past, was almost fatal. Now, shaking off the shame and armed with knowledge, Marjolein talks through menstrual health with humour and another Shetland folktale. This time the oldest story of Shetland about the deity Sea Midder. This show is not for the faint-hearted, with 9 audience members fainting and another 18 walkouts during its run at the Fringe. However, this is not gore for gore's sake. This show has the potential to save lives. Also: JOKES.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Marjolein Robertson: O","instanceDates":"2 June-3 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"611603ANJKMQGJTHVJGRNPSJNNGRPPHHL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-02T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-02T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-03T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-03T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"WINNER Dave’s BesUK Comics’ Comic 2022 - Best Act\r\nAs Seen on Mock The Week, BT Sport and ITV, ‘Master of one-liners’ Mark Simmons brings his sell-out tour show ‘Quip Off the Mark’ to Soho Theatre for a one-night-only tour finale!\r\nMark joined Dara O’Brian and Hugh Dennis on BBC2’s Mock The Week as a semi-regular on the show and now brings you his show Quip Off The Mark which has toured over 200 venues and sold over 20,000 tickets. He’s also appeared on BT Sport’s DIY pundit and The Football’s On.\r\nMark is enjoying further success with his solo podcast, Jokes With Mark Simmons, where he invites a fellow comic, such as Gary Delaney, Sarah Milican, and Milton Jones to discuss jokes that they’ve written but simply just haven’t worked.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Mark Simmons: Quip Off the Mark","instanceDates":"16 December-16 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"572003AQMDCHVNCJLRLLDNDCPGDQHQRNT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-16T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-16T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-16T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-16T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join multi award-winning, BAFTA-nominated writer and comedian Mark Steel for his new tour ‘The Leopard in My House’.\r\nThe topic? His battle with throat cancer. A battle he is winning (thankfully) and which only his rapier wit could fashion a comedy tour show out of. Cancer has done nothing to dull Mark's acute political observations or quash his \"frankly bonkers\" energy: you will laugh, you will cry, but you'll laugh again, and again, and again. The Leopard in My House is proof that this leftie, working-class, Radio 4 favourite truly deserves his place in the UK comedy pantheon.  \r\n\"The consultant had told me he was confident I had throat cancer that had spread into the lymph glands. Joyfully, I held his hand and looked up to the heavens like a South American footballer after scoring a goal. It was one of the happiest moments of my life.\"  \r\nMark Steel is best known for his critically acclaimed BBC Radio 4 show Mark Steel’s in Town (now in its 13th series), as well as his hit podcast What The F*** Is Going On…?. He has presented the BAFTA-nominated Mark Steel Lectures for BBC Two, and is a regular on BBC One’s Have I Got News for You and BBC Radio 4’s The News Quiz. He has also written several acclaimed books, including an adaptation of his critically acclaimed stand-up show Who Do I Think I Am? for Audible.\r\n14+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":150,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Mark Steel: The Leopard in My House","instanceDates":"2 May-2 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"696403APNPHVNBVPQCNHCRTPVMJSRDCMK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-02T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-02T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-02T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-02T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A typically frantic and fun-packed new show from Mark Watson…\r\n20 years in stand-up for the 'Taskmaster' cheeky texts icon, multi-award-winner, YouTube cult figure, Radio 4 favourite and recently 'Baby Reindeer' actor: Watson returns after seasons at the Adelaide, Melbourne, Sydney and Edinburgh comedy festivals. \r\n\r\nA recent encounter with a stranger caused Mark to spend some time pondering the uncertain future facing humanity. He explores this - along with equally pressing matters like the worst word he has ever said in public, the current state of the UK sausage industry, and much more - in a typically frantic and fun-packed new show.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":100,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Mark Watson: Before It Overtakes Us","instanceDates":"17 May-17 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"595603ASHBGPLKKVJRTTRDSMSNCGQQVCK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-17T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-17T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-17T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-17T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Marny Godden has brought to life a collection of very colourful characters. In this, her debut solo show, she mixes clowning and narrative storytelling to take the audience on an uplifting, fun-packed adventure. Meet the Little Wula, a hirsute 15-year-old boy; Mick, a kipper-loving wheeler dealer; Mo Moses, Poo Detective a hoover lady; and Wilmot Brown, the finest actor in London town. \r\n“Sublimely silly, brilliantly surreal” The Times. \r\n“Godden’s style is hilarious” ThreeWeeks. \r\n“Perfectly executed comedy” Edinburgh Evening News. \r\n“Outstandingly performed” Broadway Baby\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Marny Godden: Flap Em On The Gate","instanceDates":"14 June-14 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"477403AGMJJGHJDTGKJLHMQNBTVCTNBLT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-14T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-14T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-14T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-14T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Martin Urbano performs modern stand-up comedy for the current cultural climate.  \r\n\r\n#standup #funny\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Martin Urbano: #standup #funny","instanceDates":"9 December-10 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"674403ALKRBHNDTPCBGCGJSVRBDCBPSPL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-09T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-09T22:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-10T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-10T22:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"NOMINEE: Edinburgh Comedy Awards Best Newcomer (2023) \r\nMartin Urbano spent his long, lucky career talking and saying anything he wanted, until allegations surfaced, he stepped out of the spotlight, promising to take a long time to listen. Now he's back! Martin tackles his allegations (and much more!) in this long-awaited apology comeback show. He shares his humorous musings on being cancelled, woke Twitter mobs and Uber.\r\nMartin has written for The Tonight Show with Jimmy Fallon, The Chris Gethard Show, Danny Brown's show on Viceland and National Lampoon's Radio Hour. As a standup, he has been seen on Jimmy Kimmel Live!, Comedy Central's Featured, the CW's Howie Mandel Gala, and This Joka presented by Will Smith (pre-slap). \r\nMartin was a New Face at Just For Laughs, named one of Vulture's Top Comedians You Should Know back in 2019, and has performed at Bonnaroo Music & Arts Festival, New York Comedy Festival, and the Boston Calling Music Festival.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Martin Urbano: Apology Comeback Tour","instanceDates":"15 January-20 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"499403ABPDKJNHPPLBVCPVDVDDTJLLLGS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-15T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-15T21:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-20T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-20T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Gleeson begins to buck and screech; her sparky eye glows brighter. The other falls right out of her head. Leave it, she growls, pulling you headfirst into her debut hour, Dog Ear.\r\n\r\nYou'll see magpies like you've never seen, news reporters in unexpected places and flaw-filled moments of humanity.\r\n\r\nEdinburgh Comedy Awards Best Newcomer Nominee 2026, Comedian’s Choice Best Newcomer Winner 2025, BBC New Comedy Award finalist and Channel 4 Sean Lock Award 2024\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Marty Gleeson: Dog Ear","instanceDates":"5 October-23 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"747603ASCQGBLCLKNKDKGVMMGHJJQMSDM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-05T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-05T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-01-23T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-01-23T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Mary O'Connell is conflicted: she hates capitalism but she loves to shop.\r\nA hotly anticipated debut show of observational annoyance from a blunt and disturbed perspective, straight from a sell-out run at Edinburgh Fringe. The star of Stand Up for Live Comedy (BBC Three), Funny Women runner-up 2020 and OnlyFans Content Creative Fund Winner 2023 considers money, pop culture and trying to be a good person while living in London (if that's possible).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Mary O’Connell: Money Princess","instanceDates":"27 March-30 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"527603ADNCJMMQTJPKBGVDVRDKGBCHNVT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-27T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-27T21:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-30T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-30T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"With nearly 1,000 TikTok followers (at the time of going to print), be sure to book early to catch \"the king of online\" as he surfs cyberspace and reveals the World Wide Web's silliest internet videos. \r\n\r\n★★★★★ \"I could quite happily see this show every night\" - BEYOND THE JOKE\r\n★★★★ \"a knowingly shambolic marvel\" - THE TIMES\r\n★★★★1/2 \"Gags hurtling at you faster than the most impatient doom scroll\" - CHORTLE\r\n★★★★ - THE GUARDIAN\r\n★★★★★ – INDEPENDENT\r\n\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Mat Ewins: Mr TikTok*","instanceDates":"4 December-9 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"496404AKMTBJBGGJBCDDGJNBLLSDLQLQP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-04T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-04T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-09T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-09T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Fresh from wrapping up his biggest tour yet and a second series of The Matt Forde Focus Group on BBC R4, leading political comedian and satirist Matt Forde (The Royal Variety Performance, Spitting Image, HIGNFY, British Scandal) embarks on a mission with impossible odds: find joy amid global political turmoil, the rising tide of populism, and his own ongoing health challenges – several years on from a bone cancer diagnosis. 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Matt Forde: Work in Progress","instanceDates":"21 July-25 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"726403ALCJMMHJJVHJHVSPKSPVPJBBCJD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-21T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-21T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-25T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-25T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Trump. Starmer. Male incontinence. \r\nAll the classic ingredients of comedy.\r\nMatt tries out new material ahead of Edinburgh 2025 and his next tour. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Matt Forde: Work in Progress 25","instanceDates":"23 May-24 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"629603AJQMBBGDDMBLSBNJCGPHVKPRNDM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-23T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-23T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-24T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-24T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Matt Forde (Spitting Image, HIGNFY, British Scandal, The Last Leg, The Royal Variety Performance) explores the dark comedy horror that is British politics, ahead of the next election. Plus silly voices. 'Our foremost satirical stand-up... whatever your politics, you'll find excellence here' **** (Sunday Times). 'Forde is as gratifyingly sane as comedians come... smart, funny ideas' **** (Times). “Singlehandedly fulfilling comedy’s brief of taking our political masters to task. Combining spot-on impressions with up to the minute observations” Mail On Sunday\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Matt Forde: Work in Progress. 23","instanceDates":"28 May-22 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"503403ATKMPJRVDVMDCLGCDTQBQLJCCPT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-28T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-28T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-22T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-22T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Political","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Trump. Starmer. Male incontinence. \r\nAll the classic ingredients of comedy.\r\nMatt tries out new material ahead of Edinburgh 2025 and his next tour. 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Matt Forde: Work in Progress. 25","instanceDates":"28 April-30 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"607603ANNPMJHBQSLBBTBTBPCJJPPCDGT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-28T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-28T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-30T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-30T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":false,"name":"Matt King AKA Super Hans: Meet & Greet","instanceDates":"22 September-22 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"725203ATVVSSKTCJTNNMRCDQVLHNCHHPS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-22T18:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-22T17:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-22T18:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-22T17:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Matt Rogers (Las Culturistas, The Tonight Show, Variety 10 Comics To Watch) is definitely for sure leaving comedy forever with the highly anticipated release of his holiday album, Have You Heard of Christmas?\r\nTo celebrate, Matt will perform every original song from this new seasonal classic live at London’s Soho Theatre. Accompanied by talented musical director Henry Koperski, Matt welcomes you to join him for a drink or two and confront yourself with the question...Have You Heard of Christmas? \r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Matt Rogers: Have You Heard of Christmas?","instanceDates":"13 November-18 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"503003AVBGDLQPMPDTRVSVJLBLPCMHGMV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-13T21:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-13T21:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-18T21:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-18T21:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"LGBTQ+","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"Expansive comedy storytelling about fatherhood, climate change, finance and responsibility by an expert making work at the cutting edge of environmental topics Dr Matt Winning. Host of Net Zero: A Very British Problem (BBC Radio 4). It's 'The Big Short' about the climate crisis told through an authentically personal story.\r\n\r\nDirected by Ben Target.\r\n\r\nSolastalgia: noun (sol-a-stal-gi-a) the emotional, physical or existential distress caused by environmental change to your home. A portmanteau of the words solace and nostalgia.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Matt Winning: Solastalgia","instanceDates":"22 June-24 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"723403ARDTKJNRKRDBTMCGPNBKLPMSQLT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-22T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-22T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-24T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-24T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Expansive comedy storytelling about fatherhood, climate change, finance and responsibility by an expert making work at the cutting edge of environmental topics Dr Matt Winning. Host of Net Zero: A Very British Problem (BBC Radio 4). It's 'The Big Short' about the climate crisis told through an authentically personal story.\r\n\r\nDirected by Ben Target.\r\n\r\nSolastalgia: noun (sol-a-stal-gi-a) the emotional, physical or existential distress caused by environmental change to your home. A portmanteau of the words solace and nostalgia.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Matt Winning: Solastalgia.","instanceDates":"16 February-2 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"667203ANNCGRVGJMKPBKJTGDCNCCCKPPV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-16T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-16T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-02T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-02T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Music, Horror and Chaos from the Archduke O’ Darkness, plus assorted stiffs*.\r\n*Please note, other band members may not appear.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Matthew Holness: The Garth Marenghi Upheaval (Work in Progress)","instanceDates":"6 October-6 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"656803ADKDLBHLQKBLTNTDLSMVQJGRGGL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-06T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-06T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-06T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-06T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Matthew Holness presents an hour of live music and dramatised readings from the works of pulp crime author Terry Finch. Strictly work-in-progress. 16+ (References to violence, domestic violence, addiction and mental health issues. Check webpage for updated info).","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Matthew Holness: Work in Progress","instanceDates":"16 November-16 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"748603ACJSMSPLTDLHHTVCVKJNVQLKSQS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-16T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-16T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-16T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-16T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Work In Progress","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Join Perrier Award-winning comedian and bestselling author Matthew Holness for a series of early work in progress shows! 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Matthew Holness: Work in Progress (2025)","instanceDates":"18 August-26 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"643203AKDTRDNNQJJNRJLHTPDRGMPLGBD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-18T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-18T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-26T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-26T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Musical comedian Matty Hutson is bringing his hit debut show to the Soho Theatre.\r\nA multi-instrumentalist with the voice of angel, Don’t Hold Back follows Matty as he plunges head first into the terrifying awkward truth of being alive, and his journey towards accepting himself for who he really is - a bald little idiot. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Matty Hutson: Don’t Hold Back","instanceDates":"22 April-23 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"528003ABSCSBKCDTDPLKMHGHBNQSBCMGP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-22T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-22T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-23T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-23T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The 'essential' (Telegraph) Edinburgh Comedy Award nominees return with a show about fatherhood, friendship, and the future.\r\nreators of The Wrestling, Radio 4’s Casebook of Max & Ivan and ITV2’s Deep Heat. Max & Ivan’s last show Commitment was one of the Fringe's best reviewed shows, The Guardian's 4th Best Show of the year, and was nominated for Best Comedy Show at the Chortle Awards.\r\n\r\nNominee - Best Show, Edinburgh Comedy Awards 2013\r\nNominee - Best Show, Melbourne International Comedy Festival 2013\r\nWinners - Panel Prize, Edinburgh Comedy Awards 2011\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Max & Ivan: Life, Choices","instanceDates":"15 January-20 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"499003AMCTVBTHTHCKRDKLTBJDJSDDKNB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-15T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-15T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-20T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-20T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Max Fulham brings his totally sold-out Edinburgh debut to Soho in an evening of never-before-seen nonsense.\r\nWith millions of online views of his signature brand of stand-up, Max is catapulting ventriloquism into the 21st century. Expect talking ham, malfunctioning self-service checkouts, and an inner monologue that just can't be kept inside...\r\n\r\nBest Debut Show nominee – Leicester Comedy Festival 2025.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Max Fulham: Full of Ham","instanceDates":"16 February-16 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"687403ANVPMPRSCPNPTBCNNHCGSKKDNTB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-16T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-16T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-16T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-16T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"A hilarious, heartbreaking true story about love, identity and belonging, from one half of comedy double-act Max & Ivan. Adapted from Max’s critically acclaimed memoir Making the Cut: An Unorthodox Love Story (Ebury/Penguin). “Britain’s answer to David Sedaris” – Andrew O’Hagan Praise for Max & Ivan: “A thing of startling precision, imagination and crowd-pleasing charm” ★★★★★ Times “Consistently funny and perfectly structured” ★★★★★ Fest “Big of heart, packed with laughter” ★★★★ Guardian\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Max Olesker: Making the Cut","instanceDates":"3 November-9 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"718603AHMTJMQJRBCHCCJPLVRJCDQTGTS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-03T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-03T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-01-09T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-01-09T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A hilarious, heartbreaking true story about love, identity and belonging, from one half of comedy double-act Max & Ivan. Adapted from Max’s critically acclaimed memoir Making the Cut: An Unorthodox Love Story (Ebury/Penguin), this is your chance to see Max preview the show ahead a run at the Edinburgh Fringe. “Britain’s answer to David Sedaris” – Andrew O’Hagan Praise for Max & Ivan: “A thing of startling precision, imagination and crowd-pleasing charm” ★★★★★ Times “Consistently funny and perfectly structured” ★★★★★ Fest “Big of heart, packed with laughter” ★★★★ Guardian","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Max Olesker: Making the Cut Preview","instanceDates":"29 July-30 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"718003ADSJQLRJHQLMBLPNQNHLRCPVBQS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-29T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-29T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-30T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-30T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Work In Progress","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Three wild years since her legendary hit show 'Is It A Bird?', the cockiest woman in comedy returns, with a guitar on her back and a bounty on her ballbag.\r\n\r\nAfter a BAFTA-winning strip-off live on Channel 4, bigots around the globe went ballistic. Luckily... so are her tits.\r\n\r\n'Death threats'. 'Ding-dongs'. 'Dr King'. 'Daylight savings'. Jordan Gray returns with her rootinest, tootinest, shootinest hour of musical comedy yet.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"May25 Jordan Gray: Is That A C*ck In Your Pocket, Or Are You Just Here To Kill Me?.","instanceDates":"19 May-31 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"612803ADQNRKRSNBTVHSDVKDSVNCJBKND","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-19T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-19T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-31T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-31T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Cryogenically preserved and freshly defrosted, this passionate Latina with dangerous curves is ready to make you melt.\r\nIn her debut clown spectacle, The Queen of Wails FINALLY performs her Latin-melodramatic-soap-opera slash camp musical, for you. \r\nMaya Ricote is a Mexican/Venezuelan-American telenovela actress turned clown.\r\n18+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Maya Ricote: Ay Am (June 2026)","instanceDates":"2 June-2 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"714204APHLRKVKMGTDCVCJNJBMVRQLGGC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-02T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-02T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-02T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-02T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Cryogenically preserved and freshly defrosted, this passionate Latina with dangerous curves is ready to make you melt. In her debut clown spectacle, The Queen of Wails finally performs her\r\nLatin-melodramatic-soap-opera slash camp musical, for you. Recommended by The New York Times, British Comedy Guide, The Skinny\r\nand many more. 18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Maya Ricote: Ay Am!","instanceDates":"1 October-3 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"745203AQGQCCDJCTNBBVGQJCPLSJBQNLR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-01T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-01T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-03T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-03T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Everyone at Soho Theatre Walthamstow owes a huge debt of gratitude and appreciation to the incredible grassroots campaign that started in 2003, and saved the venue from being lost as an entertainment centre. Whilst very many contributed, this was started by Bill Hodgson and the McGuffin Film Society - the XXXX\r\n\r\nWe could not be more delighted to welcome  them back, to the venue and for them to take a rightfully prominent place in the Soho Theatre Walthamstow programme.  \r\n\r\nIn the words of Bill… \r\n\r\n“The McGuffin Film Society returns to its ‘home venue’ after a 22-year absence with an eclectic two-night film festival celebrating Waltham Forest’s contributions to the world of cinema from the 1800s to the present day.”\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":300,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"McGuffin presents “Waltham Forest On Film”","instanceDates":"28 June-26 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"625003ANBPNMCPGMVNDKJJBMNPBTRQDNS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-28T18:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-28T17:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-26T18:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-26T17:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Dame Meera Syal joins us to share the hilarious and heartwarming true stories that have shaped her life and work as one of Britain’s most beloved comedy legends.\r\nGrowing up in the only Asian family in a West Midlands mining village, Meera Syal wanted to take the stage long before anyone was ready to listen.\r\nAs one of the creators of Goodness Gracious Me she changed British comedy forever. As the indomitable ‘Granny Ummi’ she terrified the guests visiting The Kumars at Number 42. She’s topped the pop charts, been a Professor at Oxford, and written a musical with Andrew Lloyd Webber. She’s a Dame, a screenwriter, and the first British Asian novelist to enter the national curriculum. Young Meera always had the stories. Now she has the stage.\r\nFrom the wisdom her mother and aunties dispensed her grandfather's attempts to arrange her marriage, her working life as an actress and writer, her journey to motherhood, and the changing attitudes towards women she has experienced over her career, Meera will share all. Funny, painful, and completely honest, this evening will stay with you long after.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Meera Syal: Vigilauntie","instanceDates":"14 October-14 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"729003ABQPDHBCJNMGRLVKBPHKNNCJPBC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-14T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-14T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-14T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-14T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Theatre"},{"description":"The unhinged hybrid concert/sketch show of your wet dreams. Fresh from a sold-out at the 2026 Edinburgh Festival Fringe where it won the The List Festival Award for Best LGBTQIA+ Show, Second City Mainstage alums Ashley Blair and Drew Reilly are Megasquirt: an experimental hyperpop comedy music project based in Brooklyn, New York. MEGASQUIRT: FULLY LOADED is a high-octane flood of gay brain rot set to a sickening beat featuring hit songs like Butt of the Bread, Gooning in the DJ Booth, Centaur Boyfriend and more. Imagine being at an underground rave that is also hilarious and maybe illegal – that's the vibe. Come thirsty. Leave fully loaded. 18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"MEGASQUIRT: FULLY LOADED","instanceDates":"2 December-12 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"759603ARDBCNGNSLHLHVVJSRDGSVTHPLR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-02T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-02T21:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-12T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-12T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Pub","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"The unhinged hybrid concert/sketch show of your wet dreams. Fresh from a sold-out at the 2026 Edinburgh Festival Fringe where it won the The List Festival Award for Best LGBTQIA+ Show, Second City Mainstage alums Ashley Blair and Drew Reilly are Megasquirt: an experimental hyperpop comedy music project based in Brooklyn, New York.  \r\n  \r\nMEGASQUIRT: FULLY LOADED is a high-octane flood of gay brain rot set to a sickening beat featuring hit songs like Butt of the Bread, Gooning in the DJ Booth, Centaur Boyfriend and more. Imagine being at an underground rave that is also hilarious and maybe illegal – that's the vibe. Come thirsty. Leave fully loaded. 18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"MEGASQUIRT: FULLY LOADED","instanceDates":"14 December-23 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"759803ADPJRNGQSLKTBMGHJBSSHNKTHNM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-14T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-14T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-23T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-23T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"International singing sensation and purr-fect post, post post-modern showgirl Meow Meow descends upon Soho Theatre in her long-awaited return to London. \r\nThe crowd-surfing queen of song dazzles with her unique brand of kamikaze cabaret that has hypnotised, inspired and terrified audiences worldwide! Music. Politics. Mayhem. Magnificence. Meow Meow navigates the uncharted territory between Weimar era wit, 1930's Shanghai show tunes, 60's French pop, and post-punk hilarity, creating a parody of glitz and high art that defies categorization.\r\n \r\nA star of the Olivier award winning show LaClique, Meow’s unique brand of kamikaze cabaret kitsch and performance art exotica has hypnotised audiences worldwide from Paris to Berlin, San Francisco to Shanghai with sell-out seasons from the Sydney Opera House to New York's David Bowie’s Highline Festival.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Meow Meow: It’s Come to This","instanceDates":"6 May-24 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"592403ADDRDBGMDJHCQPJQDKCHPGRGTVV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-06T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-06T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-24T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-24T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Theatre"},{"description":"Sell-out cult shows in the North East; acclaimed short films; their own web series – now Metroland hit Soho Theatre. The North East’s answer to Monty Python, Metroland Comedy, are taking their online madness to the stage and bringing you an all-new sketch show that promises laughter, profanity and a new understanding of the term “entertainment”. Sam Fender reckons it’s ‘f*cking brilliant!’\r\n\r\nIncluded on The Guardian and Rolling Stone’s top picks of the Edinburgh Fringe 2024.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Metroland LIVE: The Box","instanceDates":"27 March-29 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"593603ARGCJTKHBPGTRJNCRMTSCGQHVQV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-27T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-27T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-29T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-29T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Sketch","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Former MP Mhairi Black embraces her trademark dark sense of humour to reflect on her time in Westminster, providing a first-hand, ruthlessly honest look at 21st century politics.\r\nMhairi became the youngest person ever elected to the House of Commons at the age of 20 and went on to make waves both in the SNP and on the wider political scene. Following on from a sold out run at Edinburgh Festival Fringe, Politics Isn’t For Me promises a behind the scenes look from someone who spent almost a decade at the heartbeat of UK politics.16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Mhairi Black: Politics Isn't for Me","instanceDates":"10 June-14 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"599803ASJDJVGMPBSKDBJSGGRPNQBNRSM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-10T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-10T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-14T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-14T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Political","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Michael Che can be seen on his 11th season of Saturday Night Live as \"Weekend Update\" Co- Anchor alongside Colin Jost, and in his HBO series That Damn Michael Che, a comedy sketch series which he stars in, wrote and executive produced.\r\nHis first hour long comedy special, “Michael Che Matters,” was released in 2016 on Netflix. It hit #1 twice on the platform, first upon its initial release and then again in 2020. Che’s second special for Netflix “Michael Che Shame the Devil” taped at the Fox Theater in Oakland and was released in November 2021. He has been nominated for multiple Emmys for his writing on “SNL,” and in 2018, he co-hosted NBC’s live Emmy Awards telecast alongside Jost. He and Colin also hosted a number of special edition episodes of “Weekend Update” on MSNBC during the 2016 Republican and Democratic national conventions.\r\nPrior to his time on “SNL,” Michael was a correspondent on “The Daily Show with Jon Stewart” and appeared alongside Chris Rock in the 2015 feature, “Top Five.” When Che is not in front of the camera, he tours the world headlining live stand-up shows\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Michael Che: Knowledge Seed","instanceDates":"31 July-8 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"565003AKCLQBHRCMTMBNCDLHMBDSCRTPL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-31T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-31T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-08T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-08T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Michael Kunze is superstar actor Mitch Coony in this Hollywood Odyssey, where you're only ever one hit away from a Tom Hanks Sex Party. \r\n\r\nJoin Mitch as he traces the arc of his career from rags to riches and back again, taking in the cowboy spectacular, smash hit, off-Broadway show ‘My Brother the Horse’ and Oscar glory in the gritty reimagining of Snow White – ‘Ah-choo: The Sneezy Story’ – to the low moments on the backside of fame. Along the way, with the help of sketches, songs and top-notch nonsense, Mitch drops names, drops his guard, and drops the ball again and again in his quest for fame. \r\n\r\nOne of British Comedy Guide's top-reviewed Edinburgh Fringe shows of 2024.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Michael Kunze: Infinity Mirror","instanceDates":"5 April-5 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"608203AMMJQMPKLBCPLRGTMNVDVLGKPTD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-05T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-05T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-05T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-05T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Don’t miss the chance to see Michael warm-up new material in an intimate setting.\r\nSTRICTLY 14+ \r\n\r\nLikely to be swearing and adult content.\r\nDo not admit children younger than this even if accompanied with an adult.\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Michael McIntyre: New Material","instanceDates":"17 October-17 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"669203ACNBKHSCHPCNRJBRDDGQSVPKLLT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-17T17:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-17T16:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-17T17:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-17T16:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Work In Progress","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Don’t miss the chance to see Michael warm-up show in an intimate setting.\r\n\r\nSTRICTLY 14+ Likely to be swearing and adult content","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Michael McIntyre: Warm Up.","instanceDates":"25 April-25 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"626803AGHMQHBTLSRHMGRCTBPKHKSDSBV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-25T17:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-25T16:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-25T17:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-25T16:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Work In Progress","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Don’t miss the chance to see Michael warm-up show in an intimate setting.\r\nSTRICTLY 14+ Likely to be swearing and adult content","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Michael McIntyre: Warm-Up","instanceDates":"24 July-24 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"647003APCCHPGDBLTLMVQQRCDPJLGBNTK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-24T17:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-24T16:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-24T17:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-24T16:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Don’t miss the chance to see Michael warm-up new material in an intimate setting.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Michael McIntyre: Work in Progress","instanceDates":"2 March-9 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"682603AHVRVVQQNBDNRDRTTMPHMVGLDDB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-02T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-02T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-09T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-09T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Work In Progress","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Michelle is the creator/writer/star of the upcoming Netflix series SURVIVAL OF THE THICKEST, inspired by her autobiographical book of essays of the same name, published by Gallery Books. She is also the host of popular reality competition show, THE CIRCLE on Netflix.  Other film and TV credits include MARRY ME, FIRST WIVES CLUB, ALWAYS BE MY MAYBE, AWKWAFINA IS NORA FROM QUEENS, RUSSIAN DOLL, and SOMEONE GREAT. She is also the Modern Manners columnist for Real Simple and hosts the popular podcast Adulting. Michelle’s one-hour comedy special WELCOME TO BUTEAUPIA is streaming on Netflix and won the Critics Choice Award for Best Comedy Special.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Michelle Buteau: Full Heart, Tight Jeans","instanceDates":"22 August-23 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"481403AVCVJJGBSKGQHCCCSMNTNNVBJTD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-22T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-22T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-23T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-23T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"She's funny, tall, glam and finally long-legging her way across the Atlantic following her sold out US run... it's the Michelle Collins stand-up tour the world has been waiting for. \r\nMichelle Collins: The Big Natural Tour brings Michelle's one-woman show to her favorite city of London, and if you think you know what to expect, believe us, you don't. In this hilarious roller coaster, we crack the case open, via first person stories, tales of moving to Amsterdam, foreign-language fights, dates gone wrong, gowns, songs, and excitingly... slides. Funny ones.\r\n\r\nA 6'1\", luscious-haired phenomenon who swears she is not writing this herself, Michelle guides you through her insane life via shocking stories, songs, gowns, and pictures that we assure you will change your life. And her lightning fast, off-the-cuff style means that no two shows are ever the same. Michelle Collins: The Big Natural Tour is a must-see for anyone in need of solid life-changing laughter. (She did write this.)\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Michelle Collins: The Big Natural Tour","instanceDates":"25 June-29 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"541603ARPHDJDVCHVLRHVLKQVCKHMMMTH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-25T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-25T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-29T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-29T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Primetime Emmy Nominee Michelle Wolf brings a brand-new stand-up show. As seen on Netflix, HBO, Comedy Central, NBC, BBC, Channel 4 & Sky.\r\nPrimetime Emmy Nominee Michelle Wolf has established herself as one of the most influential voices in the comedy landscape. Her stand-up specials across HBO and Netflix have garnered critical acclaim and top viewing figures. \r\nWolf has headlined across the world, including her infamous appearance at the White House Correspondents Dinner. Her last sold-out Edinburgh Fringe run scored a prestigious Edinburgh Comedy Award nomination. Wolf is also known for her appearances on The Daily Show (Comedy Central) and The Break with Michelle Wolf (Netflix). \r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Michelle Wolf: Best Job in the World","instanceDates":"8 July-9 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"694403ANVNKVPBMDCQQPQPCNTTPNJNJPD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-08T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-08T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-09T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-09T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Primetime Emmy Nominee Michelle Wolf has established herself as one of the most influential voices in the comedy landscape.\r\nHer stand-up specials across HBO and Netflix have garnered critical acclaim and top viewing figures. \r\nWolf has headlined across the world, including her infamous appearance at the White House Correspondents Dinner. Her last sold-out Edinburgh Fringe run scored a prestigious Edinburgh Comedy Award nomination. Wolf is also known for her appearances on The Daily Show (Comedy Central) and The Break with Michelle Wolf (Netflix).  \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Michelle Wolf: Work in Progress","instanceDates":"28 July-2 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"631803APNPDJLBCDLDSLJGMCLDLJRQMVR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-28T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-28T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-02T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-02T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Micky is back on stage performing a run of Warm-up shows this autumn and is looking forward to performing at the brilliant Soho Theatre Walthamstow for the first time this September.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":130,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Micky Flanagan: Warm Up Show","instanceDates":"23 September-28 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"745403ASNHHNRPNLSRRPCBRBRQLLHGMPQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-23T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-23T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-28T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-28T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"New stand-up show from Mike Wozniak in which a story about a bench will be prominent. Previous experience of or strong opinions about benches not required. Let Mike worry about that.\r\nAs seen on Taskmaster, Man Down and Junior Taskmaster. As heard on Three Bean Salad podcast.14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":100,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Mike Wozniak: The Bench","instanceDates":"12 March-14 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"672003AVRRTCKKMVHGQNKRMBJDRDHJBTN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-12T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-12T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-14T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-14T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"“A funny comedy show all about a silly little guy called me.”\r\nAlternative comedian and kindly clown Mikey Bligh-Smith presentsan open-house tour of his carefully constructed mind-palace. Madcap prop chaos. Tremendous jokes and wordplay. Hardcore, unfiltered, Full-Frontal Mikey Mode.\r\nMember of anarchic sketch comedy group The Lovely Boys. Sketch Off Finalist \r\nAs seen on CH4 and Disney+\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Mikey Bligh-Smith: Full Frontal Mikey Mode","instanceDates":"1 June-1 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"713205ACHVHDCNDGQRGCJHTLTBHLJDCKK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-01T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-01T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-01T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-01T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Should you know about your dad’s seduction techniques? In 2025 Milo Edwards found a box of old letters in the back of his late Mother’s wardrobe. Catamaran is a show about his parents and the letters they wrote and the 1980s, in which Milo asks what remains of a human life, what’s torn out, what happens if that life was surprisingly horny…and whatever happened to Jim Lock’s catamaran? 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Milo Edwards: Catamaran","instanceDates":"8 February-13 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"760204ANDBNNDBLGJCQSSDLKGDSTMPQDN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-08T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-08T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-13T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-13T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join Salford-born powerhouse Molly for her Edinburgh Comedy Award nominated debut show about what it means to be a slob.\r\n\r\nTo Molly, life didn’t get any better than a good buffet and belting out Meatloaf down the pub karaoke. But when the Salford-born libertine was unexpectedly laid out by a life-threatening illness, Molly was forced to slob out whether she liked it or not…\r\n\r\nAs seen on Comedy Central Live and heard on BBC Radio 4. BBC New Comedy Awards finalist. Tour support for Joe Lycett, Sophie Duker and Rachel Fairburn. “Fierce, funny, magnetic - a true Northern star on the rise” Sophie Willan\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Molly McGuinness: Slob","instanceDates":"8 January-10 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"662403ALSQCHDGDBPRJVVJTLPVKMDRJCP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-08T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-08T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-10T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-10T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"With sex, Siri, and the familiar mundane at the top of the mind, operatic bass-baritone and comedienne Monét X Change shares her anecdotal, intrusive thoughts and opinions on life and how it continues to perplex her at every turn in her debut hour. Monét is an entertainment spitfire and the first double-crown winner in RuPaul's Drag Race herstory. Known for delivering energetic and show-stopping performances, Monét's showwomanship is a reflection of a tireless work ethic to cultivate and perfect her immaculate lip-syncing skills, comedic chops and (mostly) pitch-perfect live singing.\r\nPremium ticketholders will get premium seating and a post-show meet & greet opportunity, including the chance to take your own photo with Monet.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Monet X Change: Life Be Lifein'","instanceDates":"20 March-23 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"514403AQJLJLTVRQBTCBSPNTTCCQGLMMG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-20T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-20T21:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-23T23:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-23T23:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Drag","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Experience the ultimate showdown as a selection - A lonely moon, a dirty nun, a pensive hunter with no gun... quiet little worlds come to dazzling life at the hands of these eccentrics as they fight to suppress their wildest - and most lovable-selves. \r\nTender and ridiculous, ‘Moonkid’ is a wandering dream amidst the forlorn, the pretentious, and the divine. \r\nAmerican performer Lucy Ellis presents this ‘assured and joyous’ solo debut, a crash course in yearning, ambition, loneliness, and freedom.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Moonkid","instanceDates":"6 June-6 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"714803ALTRGMQNVKNHGRVTBHTLPRKCKRC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-06T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-06T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-06T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-06T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Mary's been sleeping with strangers across Scotland for eight months. Tonight's conquest: Mike, an American tourist who's never heard of KFC. After the best sex of her life, she tells him what she's been hiding. \r\n\r\nThen he tells her what he's been hiding. \r\n\r\nFrom award-winning David Ireland (The Fifth Step, Cyprus Avenue) comes a sharp and hilarious exploration of faith and loneliness in a Travelodge, directed by Soho Theatre’s Associate Director Max Elton (The End of Hope, Not Now).","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":45,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"MOST FAVOURED","instanceDates":"11 December-24 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"664203ABJLMRGTLLMPBQNBQTQKBDCNTVJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-11T18:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-11T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-24T18:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-24T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join nasty boys Tom Lawrinson and Sam O’Leary for an exclusive screening of four brand new comedy shorts. Special guests, mad laughs, gorgeous singing voices. 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Movie x4 with Tom Lawrinson & Sam O’Leary","instanceDates":"21 July-21 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"735003AGDJDLHBSDJDMLTSLMVSPBDHCPD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-21T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-21T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-21T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-21T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Following its award-winning Edinburgh run, Mr Creep is a dark, unhinged and sharply funny dive into the uncomfortable beige leather shoes of a man we all recognise, but wish we didn’t. \r\nMeet Martin, the creep lurking in the shadows. Familiar yet alien, ‘harmless’ but predatory, comical but unsettling – he refuses to avert his gaze or listen to what you want. His fingers are all thumbs and he eats processed meat straight out of the packet, endlessly. \r\nWith her trademark blend of dark comedy, lo-fi theatricality, and razor-edged critique, Theodora van der Beek invites us into Martin’s world—where sinister, retro nostalgia meets the cursed manifestations of our modern internet brains. Through him, she plays a game of consent with herself, unmasking the mechanics of sexual predation and society’s quiet complicity. \r\nA provocative pull down the seedy rabbit hole that is Mr Creep, daring us to stop pretending he’s not there. \r\nWinner of the Birds of Paradise Emerging Talent Award 2025. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Mr Creep","instanceDates":"7 February-7 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"685203ARDPLNLVBHBGHRMCHSNNGSLDSJK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-07T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-07T22:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-07T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-07T22:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Musical Magic Box presents - interactive storytelling with live music! Original stories, original songs. Join Lottie and Andy for an energetic hour of imaginative fun! \r\nEmbark on a storytelling adventure with Lottie and her Magic Box - and the wonderful Andy and his guitar! Help tell the story, get involved in the new songs - and who knows what you will meet along the way? A brave princess? An inquisitive  inventor? A grumpy unicorn? A volcano? Even some magic recycling bins?  \r\n\r\nEnergetic, imaginative fun for small people…and their grown-ups! \r\n18 months+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Musical Magic Box","instanceDates":"31 March-28 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"703403AHQMSBBDQVNDSKBKJLHCPCGKKRM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-31T10:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-31T09:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-28T10:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-28T09:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Families","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Performance Art","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Musical Magic Box presents - interactive storytelling with live music! Original stories, original songs. Join Lottie and Andy for an energetic hour of imaginative fun! Embark on a storytelling adventure with Lottie and her Magic Box - and the wonderful Andy and his guitar! Help tell the story, get involved in the new songs - and who knows what you will meet along the way? A brave princess? An inquisitive  inventor? A grumpy unicorn? A volcano? Even some magic recycling bins? Energetic, imaginative fun for small people…and their grown-ups! \r\n18 months+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Musical Magic Box","instanceDates":"25 July-25 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"740404ABDMDPKGSNSVHLTDTMRCVQQJSHM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-25T10:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-25T09:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-25T10:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-25T09:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Families","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Performance Art","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Theatre"},{"description":"Musical Magic Box presents - interactive storytelling with live music! Original stories, original songs. Join Lottie and Andy for an energetic hour of imaginative fun! Embark on a storytelling adventure with Lottie and her Magic Box - and the wonderful Andy and his guitar! Help tell the story, get involved in the new songs - and who knows what you will meet along the way? A brave princess? An inquisitive  inventor? A grumpy unicorn? A volcano? Even some magic recycling bins? Energetic, imaginative fun for small people…and their grown-ups! 18 months+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Musical Magic Box ","instanceDates":"29 October-19 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"757003AHMKMRLLRRDJJPMRNQJVDHPPLRQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-29T10:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-29T10:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-19T10:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-19T10:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Families","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Performance Art","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Theatre"},{"description":"Soho Theatre and local interactive storytelling company Magic Box are bringing our smallest audience members some summer sessions filled with wonder and surprise.\r\nEmbark on a storytelling adventure with Lottie and her Magic Box, accompanied by the wonderful Andy and his guitar.\r\n\r\nHelp tell the story, get involved in the new songs - and who knows what you will meet along the way? A brave princess? An inquisitive  inventor? A grumpy unicorn? A volcano? Even some magic recycling bins? \r\n\r\nMusical Magic Box presents - interactive storytelling with live music. Original stories, original songs. Join Lottie and Andy for an energetic hour of imaginative fun for small people and their grown-ups.\r\n18 months+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Musical Magic Box: for toddlers, small children and their grown-ups,","instanceDates":"20 May-6 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"620403AQSBLKSSDGLHMLPPHSSTVHDKSBB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-20T10:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-20T09:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-06T11:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-06T11:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Families","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"What would you take if you were forced to leave home with no hope of returning? How would you make a fresh start somewhere completely new? This is the true story about one woman who loses everything.\r\nRemembering the tastes and aromas of her mother’s kitchen with live cooking on stage, she recreates the dishes of her childhood and homeland, building a new life and community around food.\r\nWritten by award-winning Hannah Khalil from the story by Atoosa Sepehr, and directed by Chris White, the hit play returns after sell-out runs in 2024 at Soho Theatre and Traverse Theatre during the Edinburgh Festival Fringe.\r\nOriginally presented by Soho Theatre and Traverse Theatre.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"My English Persian Kitchen","instanceDates":"30 September-11 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"632203ATSRGBGDBLSQDSHTMNNDTCNLNDM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-30T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-30T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-11T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-11T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"What would you take if you had to leave home with no hope of returning? This life-affirming new play chronicles one-woman’s quest to build a new life around cooking and food. \r\nWhat would you take if you were forced to leave home with no hope of returning? How would you make a fresh start somewhere completely new? This is the true story about one woman who loses everything.\r\n Remembering the tastes and aromas of her mother’s kitchen with live cooking on stage, she recreates the dishes of her childhood and homeland, building a new life and community around food.\r\nWritten by award-winning Hannah Khalil from the story by Atoosa Sepehr, starring Isabella Nefar (Salome, National Theatre) this life-affirming new play chronicles one woman’s quest to start again.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"My English Persian Kitchen (Edinburgh Preview)","instanceDates":"26 July-26 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"551004ATHPBBHBMMCGBGBHBJBSQBGKPHV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-26T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-26T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-26T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-26T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"What would you take if you had to leave home with no hope of returning? This life-affirming new play chronicles one-woman’s quest to build a new life around cooking and food. \r\nRemembering the tastes and aromas of her mother’s kitchen with live cooking on stage, she recreates the dishes of her childhood and homeland, building a new life and community around food.\r\nWritten by award-winning Hannah Khalil from the story by Atoosa Sepehr, starring Isabella Nefar (Salome, National Theatre) this life-affirming new play chronicles one woman’s quest to start again.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"My English Persian Kitchen.","instanceDates":"16 September-5 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"555803ADRMMKCSNQTTGVCMRHTQJSTJVCR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-16T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-16T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-05T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-05T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Myra DuBois steps away from the songs for one evening and dedicates her attention to the dying art of conversation.\r\n‘A Problem Shared’ utilises Myra’s… ‘unique’ people skills to heal the trauma of her wounded public. Myra herself shall lead meditations, contemplations and pontifications as she selflessly takes on the woes of both her celebrity guests and her adoring audience of AdMyras","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Myra Dubois: A Problem Shared","instanceDates":"11 May-13 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"434403AHVSBMTBJJQHDSMMKLTKDBKBJHK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-11T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-11T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-13T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-13T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Drag","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"A show about trying to be a good person while staying a badman. \r\nJoin the star of Live at the Apollo for this “unapologetically funny” (Telegraph) exploration of empathy, morality and political contradiction. ★★★★ Evening Standard\r\nAs seen on Live at the Apollo, Have I Got News for You, The Big Narstie Show, 8 Out of 10 Cats Does Countdown and Unapologetic. \r\nDirected by Jet Vevers \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Nabil Abdulrashid: The Purple Pill","instanceDates":"30 October-30 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"500603AHGVDTQVSBJHHCPRVMCQPJQTTBT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-30T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-30T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-30T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-30T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Weighty poetical subject matter explored in depth by a complete idiot/the perfect person for the job/Suki Tawdry. Part of London Clown Festival 2024.\r\nNancy Trotter Landry of Giffords Circus and Fools Moon fame, tackles the depth and beauty of T.S. Eliot with her inimitable physical idiocy and outlandish facial expressionism.  \r\n\r\nPhysical recital really at it’s best. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Nancy Trotter Landry: Suki Tawdry Reads","instanceDates":"9 July-9 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"543203ARVLDRGMNVTSJPLJRMCTSHJBKBK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-09T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-09T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-09T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-09T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Following its smash-hit sell-out runs opening both Soho Theatre Walthamstow and A24’s Cherry Lane Theatre in New York, Natalie Palamides’ tour-de-force is back for a strictly limited run.\r\nNew Year’s Eve 1999. Star-crossed lovers. A quarrel at the strike of midnight.\r\n\r\nEdinburgh Comedy Award Winner Natalie Palamides (Nate, Netflix) presents an achingly tender 90s rom-drom (romantic dramedy) which asks you to look at every argument from two sides.\r\n\r\nBest Show Nominee | Edinburgh Comedy Awards 2024\r\nBest Show Winner | List Festival Awards 2024\r\n\r\nTop 10 comedy shows of 2024 | Guardian\r\nTop 10 Comedy shows of 2024 | Times\r\nTop 10 Comedy shows of 2024 | Chortle\r\nThe 10 Hottest Comedy Shows 2024 | Telegraph\r\nFunniest Shows at Edinburgh Fringe 2024 | Telegraph\r\n18+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":85,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Natalie Palamides: WEER","instanceDates":"14 January-24 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"668003AGKHVHJPSMVJLQDLHVHQQSDNPJK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-14T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-14T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-24T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-24T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Natalie Palamides (NATE, LAID) is back at Soho Theatre to workshop her new hour which may or may not end up being called WEER.\r\nCome and be a part of the process. \r\n\r\nThe show will be different every night. Sometimes it might not make sense. Sometimes it will be so perfect that it can never be recreated. Sometimes it will be so bad that you feel a lil’ bad for her. \r\n\r\nThis will be fun (subjective). \r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Natalie Palamides: WEER (WIP)","instanceDates":"16 January-20 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"517203AJJPHNPVSDLJBQPRRJGJLSMDRSC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-16T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-16T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-20T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-20T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"New Year’s Eve 1999. Star-crossed lovers. A quarrel at the strike of midnight. \r\nEdinburgh Comedy Award Winner Natalie Palamides (Nate, Netflix) presents an achingly tender 90s rom-drom (romantic dramedy) which asks you to look at every argument from two sides.\r\n18+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Natalie Palamides: WEER (Work in Progress)","instanceDates":"24 July-26 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"552003AHLJNJCNNHPGVHTBCTTNGGPPPTJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-24T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-24T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-26T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-26T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"New Year’s Eve 1999. Star-crossed lovers. A quarrel at the strike of midnight. \r\nEdinburgh Comedy Award Winner Natalie Palamides (Nate, Netflix) presents an achingly tender 90s rom-drom (romantic dramedy) which asks you to look at every argument from two sides.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Natalie Palamides: WEER.","instanceDates":"6 November-30 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"553003ATMLDQMDJRSDJQGGGKTQMQNBMMT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-06T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-06T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-30T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-30T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Following its smash-hit sell-out runs in Edinburgh and at Soho Theatre, Natalie Palamides’ tour-de-force comes to Soho Theatre Walthamstow for a strictly limited run.\r\nNew Year’s Eve 1999. Star-crossed lovers. A quarrel at the strike of midnight.\r\n\r\nEdinburgh Comedy Award Winner Natalie Palamides (Nate, Netflix) presents an achingly tender 90s rom-drom (romantic dramedy) which asks you to look at every argument from two sides.\r\n\r\nBest Show Nominee | Edinburgh Comedy Awards 2024\r\nBest Show Winner | List Festival Awards 2024\r\n\r\nTop 10 comedy shows of 2024 | Guardian\r\nTop 10 Comedy shows of 2024 | Times\r\nTop 10 Comedy shows of 2024 | Chortle\r\nThe 10 Hottest Comedy Shows 2024 | Telegraph\r\nFunniest Shows at Edinburgh Fringe 2024 | Telegraph\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":85,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Natalie Palamides: WEER.","instanceDates":"2 May-10 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"600803AJHLVGNRBQMSPGGQMMPLJLRKTGR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-02T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-02T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-10T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-10T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Kitch (me) brings his absurd, alternative-sold-out-basically-award-winning fringe-comedy show to Soho. (It's sort of about Charlatans, voices and a Rasputin book that, as it stands, I still haven't read. There’s big laughs, lulls, shouting & faffing. Oh & I’ve got a hat.\"\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Nate Kitch: Something Different!!!!!","instanceDates":"13 March-14 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"678003ATMJSPMBKBRJPNHVRNNMHKLPCLK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-13T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-13T22:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-14T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-14T22:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"India’s highest-selling spoken word poetry show comes to Soho Theatre Walthamstow. A perspective shifting experience of deep, emotional and thought-provoking storytelling.\r\nWhat if stories we grew up with were never meant for us?\r\n\r\nFrom fairy tales to Fiction, we were fed what love looks like, what should you be sad or happy about. Our \"Perspective\" is never truly ours, it's almost stereotypical in this ever-changing world.\r\n\r\nRajkumari is a spoken word poetry & storytelling show that challenges the narratives we were raised on. This show is going to make you feel grateful about almost everything that happened to you in life. It is going to make you laugh, cry (happy tears), smile, feel a lot of unfelt & unspoken. Rajkumari answers a lot of what is unanswered.\r\n\r\nThis is not just a show. It's a moment of unlearning. A space where you find your \"Nayab Nazariya\", your unique perspective. A reminder that maybe it's time we stop living someone else's story... and start writing our own.\r\n\r\nPerformed in Hindi\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":130,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Nayab Midha: Rajkumari","instanceDates":"21 November-21 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"732403AKPLTGGGMBLJPRMSSCPLQNJCGTR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-21T14:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-21T14:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-21T14:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-21T14:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A nostalgic and heartfelt comedy about living with grandparents in 1980's suburban Britain. Part of London Clown Festival 2024.\r\nInspired by vintage photos taken in front of The Door, Neil Frost brings to life long lost characters as he reanimates childhood costumes. The past unravels, and we make our final goodbyes. \r\nAward-winning silly man Neil Frost is one half of the acclaimed double act The Establishment (Eton Mess and Le Bureau de Strange) and winner of Best Comedy Adelaide Fringe Weekly Award. \r\nThe Door is performed and devised by Neil Frost, Co-Directed by Lucy Hopkins (Dark Mother and Ceremony of Golden Truth) \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Neil Frost: The Door","instanceDates":"9 July-9 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"542803ACVRRGPVHJHKMMTTPVCVGBGSCJL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-09T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-09T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-09T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-09T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Trick or Treat yourself to Soho Theatre Walthamstow's spooky showcase spectacular featuring some of the most electrifying names on the comedy circuit – think superstar headliners, established favourites and rising stars\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":125,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Neon Frights With Lou Sanders","instanceDates":"31 October-31 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"708203AGNDKTCLBBGSPVKRSSLTTLQGHHM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-31T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-31T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-31T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-31T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":240,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Neon Nights After Party with Gal Pals","instanceDates":"25 July-25 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"648403AGLMDLMGQLPCJGSTDGPHNKPGJMT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-25T22:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-25T21:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-25T22:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-25T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow's showcase spectacular featuring some of the most electrifying names on the comedy circuit – think superstar headliners, established favourites and rising stars on this regular line-up show at the iconic new venue. \r\nThis round, our headliner Tim Key (The Ballad Of Wallis Island, Edinburgh Comedy Award Winner, This Time With Alan Partridge) is joined by… \r\n\r\nSam Nicoresti (2025 Edinburgh Comedy Award Winner) \r\nHasan Al-Habib (Rolling Stone 2025 Rising Comedy Stars) \r\nAlexandra Haddow (Comedy Central Live, Franke Boyle Tour Support) \r\n\r\nWith Phil Ellis (Taskmaster, Edinburgh Comedy Award Nominee) as host and more to be announced! \r\n\r\nWaltham Forest residents, run don’t walk! Enjoy exclusive access to £15 tickets (subject to availability). \r\n \r\nHere’s the small print. Line-up is subject to change. Soho Theatre Walthamstow reserves the right to add, withdraw or substitute acts at any time and if there is a change of act (headline act or supporting) no refunds are due. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":125,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Neon Nights Christmas With Tim Key ","instanceDates":"20 December-20 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"655803AKHNJSPCRBGVJJNMLHGHTKVVJRK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-20T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-20T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-20T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-20T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"This month, we’re handing over the reins of our flagship stand-up show to one of our favourite comedy nights in the world, the incredible FOC IT UP! Comedy Club. It’s the Neon Nights you know and love with a little more spice. A proportion of the proceeds from the show will also be going to Rainbow Mind, helping to tackle mental health issues for individuals within the LGBTQIA+ community. It’s a good time for a great cause. Come through!\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Neon Nights December: The FOC IT UP! Takeover ","instanceDates":"4 December-4 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"743203ANJKKLTKTGVHMJHJHBLVMCNPCTN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-04T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-04T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-04T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-04T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow's showcase spectacular featuring some of the most electrifying names on the comedy circuit – think superstar headliners, established favourites, and rising stars. This round, our headliner Michelle De Swarte (Live at the Apollo, Would I Lie To You) is joined by…  \r\n \r\n\r\nOlga Koch (Live at the Apollo, QI) \r\n\r\nHelen Bauer (Live At The Apollo, Trusty Hogs)\r\n\r\nRob Copland (Winner: Victoria Wood award at Edinburgh Comedy Awards 2024, Best Show in the Comedian’s Choice Awards 2022) \r\n\r\nAurie Styla (Jonathan Ross’ Comedy Club, Don’t Hate The Playaz) \r\n\r\nWith more acts TBA! \r\n \r\n\r\n \r\nWaltham Forest residents, run don’t walk! Enjoy exclusive access to £15 tickets (subject to availability).  \r\n\r\nHere’s the small print. Line-up is subject to change. Soho Theatre Walthamstow reserves the right to add, withdraw or substitute acts at any time and if there is a change of act (headline act or supporting) no refunds are due. 16+ (Content Advice - strong language/swearing, check webpage for current info).","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":125,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Neon Nights November With Michelle De Swarte","instanceDates":"21 November-21 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"749003AHBDRCVKQQMMDBLRJDPDHTVTCQR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-21T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-21T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-21T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-21T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow's brand-new showcase spectacular featuring some of the most electrifying names on the comedy circuit – think superstar headliners, established favourites and rising stars.\r\nThis round, our headliner Bridget Christie (Taskmaster, Would I Lie To You) is joined by… \r\n\r\nHuge Davies (8 Out Of 10 Cats Does Countdown, Jools Holland)\r\n\r\nJosephine Lacey (★★★★ The Guardian ★★★★★ WhatsOnStage)\r\nJake Lambert (Live at the Apollo, Comedy Central Live)\r\nAnd our fantastic host, Chloe Petts (Live at the Apollo, Have I Got News For You) \r\n\r\nWith more TBA…\r\n\r\nWaltham Forest residents, run don’t walk! Enjoy exclusive access to £15 tickets (subject to availability). \r\nHere’s the small print. Line-up is subject to change. Soho Theatre Walthamstow reserves the right to add, withdraw or substitute acts at any time and if there is a change of act (headline act or supporting) no refunds are due.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":125,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Neon Nights September With Bridget Christie","instanceDates":"25 September-25 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"707403ABHPNDLSKKPBMLVPKQBSCVBVRJL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-25T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-25T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-25T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-25T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow's showcase spectacular, featuring some of the most electrifying names on the comedy circuit – think superstar headliners, established favourites, and rising stars.\r\nIf you’re staying in town this summer, we’ve got you covered. Join us for our August Neon Nights (with an extra hot line up of local favourites) as part of our Summer Slam series.\r\nThis round, our headliner Sindhu Vee (QI, Live At The Apollo) is joined by… \r\n\r\nDaniel Foxx (★★★★★ Rolling Stone, ★★★★ The List)\r\n\r\nJanine Harouni (The Russell Howard Hour, Live At The Apollo)\r\nOur fantastic host, Sikisa (Live at the Apollo, Stand Up Sketch Show) \r\n\r\nAnd more exciting acts TBA…\r\n\r\nHere’s the small print. Line-up is subject to change. Soho Theatre Walthamstow reserves the right to add, withdraw or substitute acts at any time and if there is a change of act (headline act or supporting) no refunds are due.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":125,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Neon Nights Summer Special With Fern Brady","instanceDates":"22 August-22 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"716404ABKPLLHNJGQGDTRLTCNKDRTBSJN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-22T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-22T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-22T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-22T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow's showcase spectacular featuring some of the most electrifying names on the comedy circuit – think superstar headliners, established favourites and rising stars\r\nThis round our headliner is still TBC, but we thought we’d give you the chance to book early because the rest of the line-up are (of course) incredible. They are…\r\n\r\nBella Hull (Have I Got News For You, writer for SNL UK)\r\n\r\nErika Ehler (Frankie Boyle’s New World Order, Comedy Central Live, Emmy-nominated writer on Cunk On Life)\r\n\r\nJordan Brookes (Winner: Edinburgh Comedy Award for Best Comedy Show 2019, The Russell Howard Hour)\r\nFinlay Christie (Live at the Apollo, Have I Got News For You)\r\nAnd our fantastic host, Catherine Bohart (Live At The Apollo, nominee Edinburgh Comedy Awards, ★★★★★ Guardian)\r\n\r\nWaltham Forest residents, run don’t walk! Enjoy exclusive access to £15 tickets (subject to availability). \r\nHere’s the small print. Line-up is subject to change. Soho Theatre Walthamstow reserves the right to add, withdraw or substitute acts at any time and if there is a change of act (headline act or supporting) no refunds are due.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":125,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Neon Nights With Alan Davies","instanceDates":"24 July-24 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"706403ASPSQKKLJCBQVGRQLBRPPPPKRLC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-24T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-24T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-24T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-24T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Our brand-new showcase spectacular featuring some of the most electrifying names on the comedy circuit – think superstar headliners, established favourites and rising stars on this regular line-up show at Soho Theatre Walthamstow. \r\n\r\nThis round, our headliner Bridget Christie (Taskmaster, Would I Lie To You, The Change) is joined by… \r\n\r\nSindhu Vee (QI, Live At The Apollo)\r\nJen Brister (Live At The Apollo, Frankie Boyle’s New World Order)\r\nRhys James (Live At The Apollo, Mock The Week)\r\nAmy Gledhill (Live At The Apollo, Edinburgh Comedy Award 2024 Winner)\r\n\r\nAnd Kemah Bob (QI, Richard Osman’s House Of Games) as host. \r\n\r\nWaltham Forest residents, run don’t walk! Enjoy exclusive access to £15 tickets (subject to availability).\r\n\r\nHere’s the small print. Line-up is subject to change. Soho Theatre Walthamstow reserves the right to add, withdraw or substitute acts at any time and if there is a change of act (headline act or supporting) no refunds are due.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":125,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Neon Nights with Bridget Christie","instanceDates":"26 September-26 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"608803ATBMGPBCKGVPMRNVSHCGSTSPNBQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-26T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-26T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-26T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-26T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow's showcase spectacular featuring some of the most electrifying names on t