lo, Fantasy Football, We Saw That!)\r\n\r\nMicky Overman (Stand-Up Sketch Show, Channel 4’s A Comedy Thing)\r\nKrystal Evans (Mitchell & Webb Are Not Helping, author of The Hottest Girl At Burn Camp)\r\n\r\nEric Rushton (Sean Lock Award Winner, The Stand-Up Sketch Show)\r\nAnd our fantastic host, Sarah Keyworth (Winner: Most Outstanding Show Melbourne Comedy Festival, Live At The Apollo) \r\nWaltham Forest residents, run don’t walk! Enjoy exclusive access to £15 tickets (subject to availability). \r\nHere’s the small print. Line-up is subject to change. Soho Theatre Walthamstow reserves the right to add, withdraw or substitute acts at any time and if there is a change of act (headline act or supporting) no refunds are due.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":125,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Neon Nights With Ed Gamble","instanceDates":"27 March-27 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"689403AJJQPJKKSHNPQPHDCNCMPLCDPKT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-27T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-27T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-27T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-27T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow's showcase spectacular featuring some of the most electrifying names on the comedy circuit – think superstar headliners, established favourites and rising stars on this regular line-up show at the iconic new venue. \r\nThis round, our headliner Fern Brady (Autistic Bikini Queen on Netflix, Live At The Apollo, Author Of Strong Female Character) is joined by… \r\n\r\nAlison Spittle (Wheel Of Misfortune, Winner: Best Show , Comedian’s Choice Awards 2025) \r\nFrankie Monroe (8 Out Of 10 Cats Does Countdown, Edinburgh Comedy Award Winner) \r\nLara Ricote (Live At The Apollo, Edinburgh Comedy Award Winner) \r\n\r\nWith Thanyia Moore (Live At The Apollo) as host and more to be announced! \r\n\r\nWaltham Forest residents, run don’t walk! Enjoy exclusive access to £15 tickets (subject to availability). \r\n \r\nHere’s the small print. Line-up is subject to change. Soho Theatre Walthamstow reserves the right to add, withdraw or substitute acts at any time and if there is a change of act (headline act or supporting) no refunds are due. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":125,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Neon Nights With Fern Brady","instanceDates":"30 January-30 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"656003APKVSPGLGMVDQSSNGVQCPBBDVMN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-30T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-30T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-30T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-30T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow's showcase spectacular featuring some of the most electrifying names on the comedy circuit – think superstar headliners, established favourites and rising stars on this regular line-up show at the iconic new venue.\r\nThis round, our headliner Josh Pugh (twice star of Live At The Apollo,  8 Out Of 10 Cats Does Countdown) is joined by…\r\nLorna Rose Treen (***** Independent, Observer, Telegraph, Dave’s Joke Of The Fringe Winner)\r\nChristopher Hall (The Stand-Up Sketch Show)\r\nAyoade Bamgboye (Winner: Edinburgh Comedy Award Best Newcomer 2025)\r\nWith Catherine Bohart (Live At The Apollo, Edinburgh Comedy Award nominee) as host and more TBA!\r\nWaltham Forest residents, run don’t walk! Enjoy exclusive access to £15 tickets (subject to availability).\r\n\r\nHere’s the small print. Line-up is subject to change. Soho Theatre Walthamstow reserves the right to add, withdraw or substitute acts at any time and if there is a change of act (headline act or supporting) no refunds are due.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":125,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Neon Nights With Josh Pugh","instanceDates":"21 February-21 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"679203ARKDRPQKKJGBQHHNVBRPKPNNBNB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-21T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-21T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-21T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-21T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow's showcase spectacular featuring some of the most electrifying names on the comedy circuit – think superstar headliners, established favourites and rising stars on this regular line-up show at the iconic new venue. \r\nThis round, our headliner Lucy Beaumont (Taskmaster, Celebrity Traitors, Have I Got News For You) is joined by… \r\n\r\nSophie Duker (Taskmaster, Live At The Apollo \r\nLarry Dean (Live At The Apollo, The Royal Variety Performance) \r\nToussaint Douglass (Edinburgh Comedy Award Best Newcomer Nominee 2025) \r\nLouise Young (Live At The Apollo, Edinburgh Comedy Award Best Newcomer Nominee) \r\n\r\nAnd our host, Ian Smith (two-time Edinburgh Comedy Award nominee, Live at the Apollo) \r\n\r\nWaltham Forest residents, run don’t walk! Enjoy exclusive access to £15 tickets (subject to availability). \r\n \r\nHere’s the small print. Line-up is subject to change. Soho Theatre Walthamstow reserves the right to add, withdraw or substitute acts at any time and if there is a change of act (headline act or supporting) no refunds are due. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":125,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Neon Nights with Lucy Beaumont","instanceDates":"5 December-5 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"671803ARJVCSKNGPRLBMLQPTKSHDBTHND","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-05T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-05T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-05T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-05T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow's brand-new showcase spectacular featuring some of the most electrifying names on the comedy circuit – think superstar headliners, established favourites and rising stars.\r\nThis round, our headliner Nina Conti (Live At The Apollo, Russell Howard’s Good News, Sunday Night at the Palladium) is joined by… \r\n\r\nJeff Innocent (British Comedian of the Year 2021, Best Live Club Comedian 2016, performing tours upon tours across the world, with TV and film appearances including Later With Jools Holland, Red Nose Day and Mean Machine with Vinnie Jones)\r\n\r\nKyrah Gray (Won Best Debut Show at the Leicester Comedy Festival Awards, Chortle Awards Best Newcomer in 2024, and Sean Lock Comedy Award Finalist in 2023. Has also written for BBC’s Bad Education and supported the likes of Guz Khan, Judi Love and Romesh Ranganathan)\r\nSunil Patel (Finalist in BBC New Comedy Awards and a Chortle Best Newcomer nominee. TV appearances such as Stath Lets Flats, Comedy Central Live and Jonathan Ross’ Comedy Club. Time Out declared ‘one to watch’)\r\n\r\nAnd our fantastic host, Amy Annette (Nominee for 2026 Chortle Awards – Best Compare, winner of The Industry Award at Funny Women Awards 2022. Supported the likes of Rose Matafeo, Nish Kumar and Lou Sanders.) \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":125,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Neon Nights With Nina Conti","instanceDates":"7 May-7 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"701003AMKVGBSCDRPCSSCRQQCSHHPPLDR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-07T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-07T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-07T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-07T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Our brand-new showcase spectacular featuring some of the comedy world’s most exciting names.\r\n\r\nExpect appearances from superstar headliners, established favourites and rising stars on this regular line-up show at Soho Theatre Walthamstow.\r\n\r\nExclusive access to £15 tickets for Waltham Forest residents subject to availability.\r\n\r\nHeadliner Phil Wang (star of Taskmaster, Have I Got News For You and two Netflix specials) is joined by…\r\n\r\nSindhu Vee (Live At The Apollo, QI)\r\n\r\nJen Brister (Live At The Apollo, Frankie Boyle’s New World Order)\r\n\r\nOlga Koch (Live At The Apollo, QI)\r\n\r\nJin Hao Li (Edinburgh Comedy Award Nominee)\r\n\r\nAnd our host, Catherine Bohart (Live At The Apollo, Trusty Hogs). \r\n\r\nLine-up is subject to change. Soho Theatre Walthamstow reserves the right to add, withdraw or substitute acts at any time and if there is a change of act (headline act or supporting) no refunds are due.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":125,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Neon Nights With Phil Wang","instanceDates":"27 June-27 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"580803AMGTSLHLPSTRKBSCBCDJHGQCDPR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-27T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-27T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-27T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-27T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Our brand-new showcase spectacular featuring some of the most electrifying names on the comedy circuit – think superstar headliners, established favourites and rising stars on this regular line-up show at Soho Theatre Walthamstow. \r\n\r\nThis round, our headliner Sam Campbell (Taskmaster, Would I Lie To You) is joined by… \r\n\r\nDesiree Burch (Have I Got New For You, Frankie Boyle’s New World Order)\r\nJessica Fostekew (Live at the Apollo, QI)\r\nSlim (Live at the Apollo, The Russell Howard Hour)\r\nUrooj Ashfaq (Edinburgh Comedy Awards Best Newcomer Winner)\r\n\r\nAnd Ania Magliano (Live At The Apollo, Edinburgh Comedy Award Nominee) as host. \r\n\r\nWaltham Forest residents, run don’t walk! Enjoy exclusive access to £15 tickets (subject to availability).\r\n\r\nHere’s the small print. Line-up is subject to change. Soho Theatre Walthamstow reserves the right to add, withdraw or substitute acts at any time and if there is a change of act (headline act or supporting) no refunds are due.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":125,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Neon Nights With Sam Campbell","instanceDates":"25 July-25 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"594603AMNBVTBCJBLMQNMPTBKBNJVQKRB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-25T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-25T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-25T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-25T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Our brand-new showcase spectacular featuring some of the most electrifying names on the comedy circuit – think superstar headliners, established favourites and rising stars on this regular line-up show at Soho Theatre Walthamstow. \r\n\r\nThis round, our headliner Sara Pascoe (Taskmaster, QI) is joined by… \r\n\r\nRosie Jones (Live at the Apollo, 8 Out of 10 Cats Does Countdown)\r\nJanine Harouni (The Russell Howard Hour)\r\nLarry Dean (Live at the Apollo). \r\nAnd Thanyia Moore (Live At The Apollo) as host. \r\n\r\nWaltham Forest residents, run don’t walk! Enjoy exclusive access to £15 tickets (subject to availability).\r\n\r\nHere’s the small print. Line-up is subject to change. Soho Theatre Walthamstow reserves the right to add, withdraw or substitute acts at any time and if there is a change of act (headline act or supporting) no refunds are due.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":125,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Neon Nights with Sara Pascoe","instanceDates":"30 May-30 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"580203ATHHNGGQBBHJKCVJSLVHCTHQHKK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-30T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-30T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-30T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-30T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"This round, our headliner Sarah Keyworth (Live At The Apollo, Winner: Most Outstanding Show Melbourne Comedy Festival) is joined by…\r\nHelen Bauer (Live At The Apollo, Trusty Hogs)\r\nSpencer Jones (Live At The Apollo, The Mind Of Herbert Clunkerdunk)\r\nSharon Wanjohi (Comedy Central Live, Chortle Award nominee)\r\nSean McLoughlin (Live At The Apollo, Mock The Week)\r\nAnd our host, Esther Manito (Live At The Apollo, The Stand-Up Sketch Show)\r\nWaltham Forest residents, run don’t walk! Enjoy exclusive access to £15 tickets (subject to availability).\r\n\r\nHere’s the small print. Line-up is subject to change. Soho Theatre Walthamstow reserves the right to add, withdraw or substitute acts at any time and if there is a change of act (headline act or supporting) no refunds are due.\r\n\r\nThis round, our headliner \r\n\r\nWaltham Forest residents, run don’t walk! Enjoy exclusive access to £15 tickets (subject to availability).\r\n\r\nHere’s the small print. Line-up is subject to change. Soho Theatre Walthamstow reserves the right to add, withdraw or substitute acts at any time and if there is a change of act (headline act or supporting) no refunds are due.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":125,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Neon Nights With Sarah Keyworth","instanceDates":"31 October-31 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"639603AKJKJBGBTVTTLLLGGCKJQCVDLHK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-31T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-31T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-31T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-31T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"When he was 18, Nic played the Yellow Ranger in the 14th season of Power Rangers.\r\nNow years later, this shy and humble star is inviting his passionate fans (that's you) to a never-before-attempted cast reunion. This is your chance to meet Nic in person (don't be nervous) and celebrate this beloved show you've definitely all seen. And don't worry, the other rangers are definitely coming…\r\nCo-writer of Starstruck (BBC Three), The Brokenwood Mysteries (UKTV) and Paddington in Peru. International Emmy Award winner.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Nic Sampson: Yellow Power Ranger","instanceDates":"29 April-3 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"606403AGNVDHLCQMGJCSSSTTGRCJVMKJD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-29T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-29T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-03T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-03T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Penetrating questions. \r\nPalatable performance.\r\nPiss goblins welcome. \r\n\r\n‘Ever felt like a backing dancer to your own life?’\r\n\r\nJoin drag alien dance disaster Niche Lorraine for a one power hour of a show as she interrogates the greatest conspiracy theory of them all -  just getting through the day.\r\n\r\n‘Life is tough! Normal is exhausting!’\r\n\r\nRoutines, lip syncs, physical explosions and costume confusions smash together as sad little slaylien Niche tries to understand what makes us all tick. And tock.\r\n\r\n‘Why are we here? What is that smell?’\r\n\r\nA heartfelt show in a hard hat about the alien inside all of us.\r\n\r\nYou are not alone. Cue X Files theme tune.\r\n\r\nA brand new dark clown queer cabaret show conceived and performed by Carl Harrison.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Niche Lorraine: HOMOPROBIA!","instanceDates":"6 March-8 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"600003AVMSNCPHKPCLSMVCHCCBKJBDBCN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-06T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-06T22:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-08T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-08T22:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Drag","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"After fixing all the World’s problems last year, living legend and national treasure in waiting, Nick Helm returns to the stage with a WIP that promises to be every bit as awe inspiring, good looking and humble as the last one. Content in development.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Nick Helm: Masterworks in Progress 2024","instanceDates":"21 March-22 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"533203ATLHLSNQCVJSSTDRCLPRJKKQKKD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-21T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-21T22:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-22T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-22T22:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Nick Mohammed (Taskmaster, Ted Lasso, Renegade Nell, Intelligence) returns as his beloved and critically acclaimed character Mr. Swallow for a residency of work in progress shows as he builds towards a new tour. As seen on 8 Out of 10 Cats Does Countdown and the BAFTAs. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Nick Mohammed is Mr. Swallow: Work In Progress","instanceDates":"16 September-20 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"556203AQJBGBBLVCVLVGRKQHKLTTVCPPV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-16T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-16T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-20T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-20T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The virtuoso ventriloquist, BAFTA nominee and British Comedy Award winner presents an unparalleled, unscripted new show that delves deep into who we are, hijacking faces to spark a bold, hysterical reality warp. \r\n\r\n'It's genius... gut-bustingly funny' ***** Telegraph \r\n'Richly entertaining, joyfully funny chaos' **** Guardian\r\n'Outstanding! High-level comedy craftsmanship' **** Times\r\n'Laughs will definitely ensue' New York Times\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"NINA CONTI: WHOSE FACE IS IT ANYWAY? (Work in Progress)","instanceDates":"13 May-18 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"540003ATPBQRVLMGTMSMJBBQGNKVNSVCH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-13T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-13T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-18T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-18T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Work In Progress","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join the award-winning internet-sensation ventriloquist, who recently reached 170 million views on a single stand-up clip, featuring her infamous masks.\r\nAs seen on Live at the Apollo, starring in Spinal Tap II, multiple sellout tours and hot off the success of her acclaimed feature film Sunlight—Nina headlines and hosts a one-off festive night of the acts she loves most. More acts TBC! 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Nina Conti’s Christmas Cabaret","instanceDates":"10 December-10 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"737603ANRQGJRGPNRPTKSVSNTGQSTSNJK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-10T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-10T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-10T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-10T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The UK’s first - and funniest - refugee comedy collective, plus their special guests\r\n\r\nThe UK’s first - and funniest - refugee comedy collective arrives at Soho Theatre. Witness performances by aspiring comedians of refugee and migrant backgrounds, alongside their special guest headliners and hosts. \r\n\r\nLine up TBC\r\n\r\nCounterpoints Arts runs No Direction Home: it’s a project for new comics from refugee and migrant backgrounds, featuring workshops, expert tuition and gigs around the country. It was created in partnership with Camden People’s Theatre and comedian Tom Parry, and their previous shows have taken place at the Southbank Centre featuring headliners such as Romesh Ranganathan, Nish Kumar, Joel Dommett, Lou Sanders, Suzi Ruffell and more. \r\n\r\n“The No Direction Home comedians are a very exciting, interesting and creative bunch of people to be around. And they are very funny, the material is really good” – Nish Kumar \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"No Direction Home","instanceDates":"4 March-28 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"531803APNJRQMSQPBQDJTCLDLSHMCSNVC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-04T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-04T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-28T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-28T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The UK’s first - and funniest - refugee comedy collective, plus their special guests\r\n\r\nThe UK’s first - and funniest - refugee comedy collective arrives at Soho Theatre. Witness performances by aspiring comedians of refugee and migrant backgrounds, alongside their special guest headliners and hosts. \r\n\r\nApril 3: Hosted by Jessica Fostekew, headlined by Nish Kumar\r\n\r\nMay 22: Hosted by Fatiha El-Ghorri, headlined by Bridget Christie \r\n\r\nJune 26: Hosted by Chloe Petts, headlined by Sindhu Vee\r\n\r\nCounterpoints Arts runs No Direction Home: it’s a project for new comics from refugee and migrant backgrounds, featuring workshops, expert tuition and gigs around the country. It was created in partnership with Camden People’s Theatre and comedian Tom Parry, and their previous shows have taken place at the Southbank Centre featuring headliners such as Romesh Ranganathan, Nish Kumar, Joel Dommett, Lou Sanders, Suzi Ruffell and more. \r\n\r\n“The No Direction Home comedians are a very exciting, interesting and creative bunch of people to be around. And they are very funny, the material is really good” – Nish Kumar \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"No Direction Home [Old]","instanceDates":"3 April-26 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"459003APRPPPDBHBTHBLSSHCTDGMKQKBL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-03T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-03T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-26T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-26T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Show And Tell with Counterpoints Arts present\r\n\r\nNO DIRECTION HOME\r\n\r\nThe UK’s first - and funniest - refugee comedy collective, plus their special guests\r\n\r\nThe UK’s first - and funniest - refugee comedy collective arrives at Soho Theatre. Witness performances by aspiring comedians of refugee and migrant backgrounds, alongside their special guest headliners and hosts. \r\n\r\nSept 4: Headlined by MAISIE ADAM, host is TBA! \r\n\r\nOct 9: Hosted by THANYIA MOORE, headlined by CATHERINE BOHART\r\n\r\nNov 13: Hosted by MICHAEL AKADIRI, headliner is TBA! \r\n\r\nDec 11: Headlined by SHAPARAK KHORSANDI, host is TBA! \r\n\r\nCounterpoints Arts runs No Direction Home: it’s a project for new comics from refugee and migrant backgrounds, featuring workshops, expert tuition and gigs around the country. It was created in partnership with Camden People’s Theatre and comedian Tom Parry, and their previous shows have taken place at the Southbank Centre featuring headliners such as Romesh Ranganathan, Nish Kumar, Joel Dommett, Lou Sanders, Suzi Ruffell and more. \r\n\r\n“The No Direction Home comedians are a very exciting, interesting and creative bunch of people to be around. And they are very funny, the material is really good” – Nish Kumar \r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"No Direction Home.","instanceDates":"9 October-11 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"493003AHGVKDGHSTMLHGNGQCPQMCJDDQC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-09T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-09T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-11T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-11T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Merry Fishmas!\r\nThe No Such Thing As A Fish team – Dan, James, Anna and Andy – are recording their pod live at the Soho Theatre, London on 7th and 8th December, with a show which will be fun, festive, and very very nerdy. If you listen to NSTAAF, or know someone who does, this will make the perfect present for them (or for yourself). Book now, and guarantee yourself an evening with so many facts you’ll be the talk of the Christmas dinner table!\r\n12+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"No Such Thing as a Fish: Live","instanceDates":"7 December-8 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"516803AKMPRJPDCKTTQNCVRSBMBGBCTDL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-07T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-07T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-08T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-08T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Comedy"},{"description":"TBC\r\n12+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"No Such Thing as a Fish: Live.","instanceDates":"17 July-21 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"472003ARRBPRGSQBDRKPLCLPTRNNLPBML","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-17T21:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-17T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-21T21:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-21T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"The Solution to the Middle East in one woman.\r\n\r\n\r\nKnown for her razor-sharp wit and unapologetic takes on identity, politics, and cultural divides, Noam returns to London. Noam Shuster-Eliassi spent years working in peace and conflict resolution, including with the United Nations, before trading diplomacy for stand-up comedy. Raised in the only community where Palestinians and Jews live together by choice, she has seen her satire go viral across the Arab world and has become the first Jewish performer at the Palestine Comedy Festival. Her one-woman show, \"Coexistence, My Ass!\" inspired a documentary of the same name, which was shortlisted for Best Documentary Feature at the 2026 Academy Awards. Noam performs mostly in English, with a smattering of Arabic, Hebrew, and Persian too. 16+ (References to racism, death and cultural/political issues. Check webpage for current content advice.)","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Noam Shuster-Eliassi Live in London","instanceDates":"26 September-26 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"751003ABTCMMJGBDGNPDTKSDGJGNJBGTT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-26T16:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-26T15:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-26T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-26T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Writers and comedians Stevie Martin (Breeders, Late Night Mash) and Tessa Coates (Feel Good, Starstruck) co-host their smash-hit podcast Nobody Panic live at Soho Theatre.\r\n\r\nThe ‘witty, clever, and oh-so-relatable’ (Evening Standard) podcast asks life’s biggest (and smallest) questions to help you become a functioning adult without screaming all the time. Whether it’s learning How To Prioritise, How To Be Confident or How To Cope With WhatsApp Groups – no topic is too great or too trivial, because we’re all in this together, guys. \r\n\r\nSo nobody panic.\r\n\r\n‘Brilliant, honest and relatable conversations about all things “adulting”… Expect to laugh and totally relate’ Stylist\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Nobody Panic: Live!","instanceDates":"5 June-5 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"466203ANSJHQTTPSBRSHSHLBNLKVVSLLN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-05T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-05T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-05T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-05T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Nobuyuki Tsujii (Piano) with Philharmonia Chamber Players to be announced. Beethoven: Piano Sonata No. 14 in C-Sharp Minor, 'Moonlight'\r\nFranck: Sonata for Violin and Piano in A major \r\n\r\nBrahms: Piano Quartet No.1 in G minor, Op.25 \r\n To some, he is one of the world's greatest pianists. To others, he is the musical extraordinaire who, blind from birth, has become an inspiration to many. To us, he's simply Nobu, the Philharmonia’s Featured Artist for the 2026/27 season and close friend of the orchestra. In the intimate setting of Soho Theatre Walthamstow, Nobu joins musicians from the Philharmonia to curate a charming evening of chamber music with pieces close to his musical heart. Franck's violin sonata forms the heart of this evening's music. Originally dedicated as a wedding present, this warm, expressive piece unfolds as a musical marriage between the piano and violin – both equal partners across four movements of lush lyricism, euphoric joy and intimate dialogue. If you listen carefully, you can even hear the wedding bells chime in the finale!  With further works to be announced, expect an evening of all-embracing musical beauty, melody, and virtuosity. ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Nobuyuki Tsujii & Philharmonia Chamber Players","instanceDates":"15 November-15 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"746803ABMQBJGBHJTTDMJRQJBBNLNBTSP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-15T15:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-15T15:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-15T15:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-15T15:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Music","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The critically acclaimed, sell out, unmissable late-night hit is back, bigger than ever! Join Jake Bhardwaj (digital host of SNLUK’s 5 TO LIVE; co-host of hit podcast JOE MARLER WILL SEE YOU NOW), and \"celebrity\" guests for the most chaotic, high-energy quiz show in town. Expect music, comedy, interactive bonus rounds and surprise appearances.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":80,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Not Another Quiz Night (WIP)","instanceDates":"22 July-22 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"739203AKCHTBGNTKKJLQKVDVTNNBMPRCT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-22T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-22T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-22T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-22T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"CLOUD BUSTING by Helen Blakeman (based on the novel by Malorie Blackman) and performed by Chingford BITA \r\n\r\nWhen Sam wakes up, he fully believes that today will just be another ordinary day – but that’s before Mr Mackie tells Class 8M to write a poem about someone they care about. Unexpectedly, Sam volunteers to write about Davey… Davey was Sam’s friend – not that Sam wanted anyone to know that. While the cool girls in the class thought Davey was 'well cute in a sad dog sort of way', the tough boys – Morgan and his crew – just saw Davey as different. Davey liked to dance. Davey liked to look at the clouds and see the shapes they made. Davey liked looking at the world in a different way to everybody else. But no matter how much Sam liked being with Davey, he always denied their friendship. Then one day, the bullying goes a step too far… but will Sam step in to help his friend? It’s not the ordinary day Sam thought it was going to be. \r\n\r\nRIDE OR DIE by Florence Espeut-Nickless and performed by Highams Park Company \r\n\r\nThe Kids spend the whole year arguing about whether Alton Towers is actually better than Thorpe Park. At the moment Alton Towers has got 2 votes and Thorpe Park has got 2 votes. The deciding vote goes to the youngest, Angel who hasn’t actually been to any of them yet, cause he’s in year 7 and you don’t get to go on The Theme Park Extravaganza until the end of Year 7.  But that’s literally in like 2 weeks, so it’ll be settled once and for all, very very soon!  So what could possibly go wrong?....Angel getting suspended from school, Nan going off on a surprise holiday, Dad coming round to look after them (and he's useless) and lasts one night, and The Kids borrowing Nan's car and colliding with a Waitrose delivery van.  The whole affair is literally a car crash. \r\n13+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":150,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"NT Connections Double Bill: Cloud Busting & Ride or Die","instanceDates":"24 March-24 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"696003AQTHHTNCKVQMGGSBCTLVVPNGCPK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-24T18:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-24T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-24T18:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-24T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"The smash-hit medieval comedie arrives in London after a totally sold-out run in Edinburgh. Created by Dog Complex Theatre in collaboration with Zachary Hunt from globally acclaimed ‘Police Cops’. \r\n\r\nThe Place: Bavaria. \r\nThe Year: Medieval. \r\nThe Teeth: Rotten. \r\n\r\nSister Gertrude wants to be the holiest nun: forgoing sin, fearing desire, yet secretly wondering what lies beneath Monk Bertram’s robes... So when whispers of witches start to plague the convent, Gertrude teams up with mysterious witch-hunter Yarrow and sets forth to rid the world of devilry and naughty lustful thoughts. Expect yearning, burning and concerning-ly good theatre. 16+ (Strobe / flashing lights, sexually explicit themes and partial nudity. Check website)\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Nuns!","instanceDates":"2 December-5 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"754403ABPLKNHQVJPBBJLJCRQGSDJSBLL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-02T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-02T22:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-05T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-05T22:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Sketch","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Fresh from the launch of her celebrated debut sitcom, The Pharmacy (Channel 4), Ola Labib is back with Dispersible, a brand new comedy show that proves some things don’t disperse easily. \r\n\r\nJoin one of comedy’s fastest rising stars as she unpacks her journey through childhood anger management, navigating life as a healthcare professional after her Channel 4 show, sibling feuds as a middle child of the diaspora and how Britain's TV industry re-fuelled childhood rage. Expect chaos, confessions and comedy with a side effect of madness. Laughter, after all, is the best medicine. \r\n\r\nAs seen on Worlds Most Dangerous Roads (DAVE), House of Games (BBC), Sorry I Didn’t Know (ITV) and Alan Davies: As Yet Untitled (DAVE) \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"OLA LABIB: DISPERSIBLE","instanceDates":"20 August-23 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"624203AMPPKHHCVDQNHKSMHLKLPMKQSHH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-20T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-20T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-23T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-23T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The debut hour from one of stand up’s most exciting breakout stars. Join Ola as she guides us through her Sudanese upbringing in Portsmouth, her outrageous experiences working as NHS Pharmacist and how a near death experience landed her into a comedy career. AS SEEN ON: World’s Most Dangerous Road (Dave) Richard Osman’s House of Games (BBC) BBC1XTRA Comedy Gala (BBC One) Alan Davies: As Yet Untitled (Dave) Just Jokes (Dave) Don’t Hate The Playaz (ITV2) The Black British Takeover with Mo Gilligan (C4) Comedy Central Live (Comedy Central) The Lateish Show with Mo Gilligan (C4) The Now Show (BBC Radio 4)The News Quiz (BBC Radio 4) The Festival of Funny (BBC) Pointless Celebrities (BBC One) and as a Finalist at Funny Women Awards. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"OLA LABIB: POLARISING","instanceDates":"15 August-17 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"550403AMLRTBDQMRTVLNTKQQRCJVDGDSP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-15T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-15T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-17T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-17T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join two of UK comedy’s most exciting stand-ups for this uproarious double bill…\r\nSoho Theatre favourites Olga Koch and Helen Bauer are bringing their critically-acclaimed stand-up hours ‘Prawn Cocktail’ and ‘Grand Supreme Darling Princess’ to EartH Hackney and we have limited £20 tickets for entry to BOTH SHOWS! \r\n\r\nDon’t miss your final chance to see these incredible shows live in London. \r\n\r\nPlease note that this show is taking place at Hackney EartH, not Soho Theatre. Each ticket grants you entry to both performances and seating is unallocated. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":180,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Olga Koch & Helen Bauer Double Bill at EartH Hackney","instanceDates":"2 March-2 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"533403ARJMHQNBMLTCQPNBSLVSLMJMCKB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-02T18:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-02T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-02T18:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-02T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"EartH Hackney","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"From the maker of Succession and White Lotus, Money™ brings you yet another little white b*tch you will love to hate: Olga Koch.\r\nThe star of Live At The Apollo, Mock The Week and QI finally addresses the elephant in the room. \r\nDirected by Jet Vevers\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Olga Koch Comes From Money","instanceDates":"3 December-21 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"570603AHBJCHDKKTPRVMNRDRVMSLGDDTH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-03T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-03T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-21T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-21T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Olga Koch has one good story. Only it’s not really her story. Do you wanna hear it?\r\nIn Fat Tom Cruise, see the Melbourne and Edinburgh Comedy Award-nominated star comb through recent history in an immersive and genre-defying new show. \r\n\r\nDirected by Jet Vevers.  \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Olga Koch: Fat Tom Cruise","instanceDates":"23 February-7 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"677003AGTDPHJPLBKQRKJBRVKMPJPPDCS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-23T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-23T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-07T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-07T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Olga Koch turned 30, got a master's degree, went on an adult gap year, got salmonella, lost herself, found herself and washed it all down with a delicious prawn cocktail. Think less Eat Pray Love and more Shake Scream Cry. As seen on Mock the Week, QI, Late Night Mash, Frankie Boyle's New World Order and her Amazon Prime comedy special. 'A masterpiece' ***** (BroadwayBaby.com). **** (Guardian). **** (Telegraph). ***** (Skinny). ***** (Sunday Post).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Olga Koch: Prawn Cocktail","instanceDates":"23 October-27 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"488003AGNRBJBMSBQGQRGRRHLRDMGMKNC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-23T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-23T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-27T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-27T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Nominee – Most Outstanding Show, Melbourne International Comedy Festival 2024\r\nColeman comes onstage, gets straight into it. He's on fire tonight. Something has gone terribly wrong. The audience shout at him to stop. But he's acting like this happens every night. The man's a professional and he's got jokes to tell. It's beautiful in a way, but then the room begins to stink up with smoke and the fire alarm goes off. Everyone is asked to evacuate. Coleman carries on doing the show to an empty room.\r\n\r\n“an impressive show that’s both light and dense, daft and thoughtful… a rich comic feast” ★★★★ Chortle\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Oliver Coleman: Goof","instanceDates":"28 August-31 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"563803ANSDDKLVDRRLKDQJQTTRGCRPKMJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-28T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-28T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-31T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-31T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A caveman steps on stage and tries to understand everything. The world. The audience. Himself. Every discovery is fragile, ridiculous, and stupid From award-nominated comedian and Gaulier-trained clown Ollie West, Discovery is a surreal, interactive, and deeply stupid journey through human curiosity. A live experiment in play, failure, and connection — a reminder that discovery only happens once, together.16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ollie West: Discovery (wip)","instanceDates":"5 February-5 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"686803AGGLTCCJTJJDKBLLRSJBKDJCHLK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-05T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-05T22:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-05T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-05T22:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Last year, Omar Badawy accidentally found himself in the middle of a far-right march. And somehow that still wasn't the hardeJoin the Edinburgh Comedy Award-nominated Saturday Night Live UK writer for his highly anticipated debut show, a collection of stupid little tales about the comfort and cost of avoidance, The Daily Mail and nose jobs.st part of his day.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Omar Badawy: Guided Detour","instanceDates":"7 December-12 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"748003ATDMVVTQBJGJPLHGGLKQBCTRKJB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-07T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-07T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-12T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-12T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Experience True Movie Expertise with the award-winning expert opinions of Gregg Turkington, as well as Health and Body Improvements from wellness guru Dr. Newman (Tim) Heidecker\r\nA comedic cinematic universe, a grand satire of America itself–Tim Heidecker and Gregg Turkington’s On Cinema has built a dedicated cult following as a sprawling comedic soap opera masquerading as a disastrous movie review show.\r\n\r\nThroughout the years, On Cinema has manifested itself through a universe of media. The centerpiece is On Cinema At The Cinema, where two codependent and delusional losers review movies in the style of Siskel and Ebert, but it becomes clear they have more interest in their own conflicting agendas than talking about the movies they may or may not have seen. \r\n\r\nThe full live show is a combination variety show and movie review panel, featuring the usual internal strife, grandstanding, and petty battles that are the hallmark of Heidecker and Turkington's on-screen On Cinema personas. \r\n\r\nThe latest season, Season 15, is airing currently on heinetwork.tv\r\n\r\n\r\nOn Cinema was named by SPIN as one of the “30 Great TV Shows That Defined The 2010’s”:\r\n\r\n“The On Cinema universe has transcended its humble beginnings, becoming the most ambitious avant-comedy experiment in recent memory.”  - SPIN \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":100,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"On Cinema Live!","instanceDates":"18 July-19 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"600604AQLGBTPSDNPHHBGPCKDMVKHLSJB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-18T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-18T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-19T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-19T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Sketch","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Flo & Joan's award-winning smash-hit musical returns.\r\nWatch as an icon of the musical theatre world finally turns the spotlight onto the one story he’s yet to tell: his own.\r\n\r\n#1 Show of the Year\r\nThe Guardian\r\n\r\nMost Outstanding Show Nominee 2025\r\nMelbourne International Comedy Festival\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"One Man Musical","instanceDates":"17 June-3 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"726803AKBPJJCPKSNDJKGSVDSSJVKCBLQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-17T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-17T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-03T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-03T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Award-winning musical comedy duo Flo & Joan present their own original one-man musical about a very renowned gentleman. Starring George Fouracres (Daphne, Hamlet) as \"the man\", and Flo & Joan as \"the band\". \r\nDirected by Georgie Staight (Operation Mincemeat).\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"One Man Musical by Flo & Joan","instanceDates":"29 October-30 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"571203AGQQNQGGBQVGLPTDKJRSNCRJJKD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-29T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-29T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-30T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-30T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Judi Love warms up at Soho theatre for one night only!\r\nStar of Taskmaster, Loose Women, Celebrity Googlebox and too many other brilliant shows to mention Judi Love is bringing her The One Like Judi Love tour to Soho Theatre.\r\nCome and join her intimate audience for this special warm up show before she hits the road with the second leg of her sell out UK tour! \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"One Night with Judi Love","instanceDates":"26 August-26 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"494203AMPNGLCLPTPBMNJVPLLVVKRPDGT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-26T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-26T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-26T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-26T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Work In Progress","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"ne Way Mirror is an interactive story about the art of people watching, built for extroverts, introverts and everyone in-between. Do you ever get the feeling you’re being watched? Is people watching your guilty pleasure? \r\nIf either of the above rings true, this show is for you.\r\nIs people watching your guilty pleasure? Come and join the ritual as we re-create the true story of a man living with a one way mirror in his living room.\r\n\r\n“Tonight you will make a choice. Am I watching you? Or are you watching me?” \r\n\r\nOne Way Mirror is the true story of a man living with a large one way mirror in his front room. As people walk past on the busy high street, he sees them, and they see themselves. He sees everything: people pouting, people picking noses and people phoning their mum. In his time, he's seen 3 physical fights, 4 messy snogs and 1 genuine divorce. Or has he? A new interactive story about the art of people watching. \r\n\r\nMade with support from Elevate East, Theatre Royal Stratford East and Interactive Soup. With thanks to The Pleasance and Camden People Theatre.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"One Way Mirror by Jonathan Oldfield","instanceDates":"17 February-17 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"523003AVBPQMQKPQSTRGPPBHNJBBVJHMV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-17T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-17T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-17T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-17T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"An acronym for One-of-many-many-of-One, teleports you to a day in the life of 1st generation immigrant Lula Berhane as she navigates the duality of two cultures, her Habesha (Eritrean/Ethiopian) and British identity.\r\nIt asks what happens when you’ve left everything behind for the promise of something better, and the something ‘better’ isn’t ‘better’? When you have nothing but memories and memory is fading, what do you have? \r\nInterweaving language+customs+music with wearable tech MiMu gloves, it’s a poetic reflection of an emotionally visceral experience unpacked through an Afro-Futuristic East African lens. \r\nOommoO, neither a gig theatre, musical or drama… It’s a new kind of storytelling.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"OommoO By Lula Mebrahtu","instanceDates":"16 February-17 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"523203APCQTGSVRDQMDMVVMVLCJGGGPLB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-16T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-16T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-17T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-17T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Performance Art","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Multi award-winning 'magnificent Fringe legends' (Time Out) Sh!t Theatre are back! And we're totally fine! Actually all things considered, we're OK. Feeling alright. Thriving, even? That's a bit far, but we have learnt some folk songs. We've got into folk recently and it's been really helpful. Come and sing some folk songs with us! A swift 60 minutes of classic folk followed by a trip downstairs to the bar and then a singaround. Because we need a drink, don't we? But we're doing OK. \r\n“Few companies make shows that are so consistently, outrageously fun” (Guardian)\r\n*fun not guaranteed\r\nThis show runs at 60 minutes, and is followed by a chance to continue singing* and drinking** together in the performance space. Please join us after the show for the singaround if you would like to.\r\n*singing not obligatory\r\n**drinking not obligatory\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Or What’s Left Of Us","instanceDates":"18 November-1 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"556403APMGCTGQJSVLMVLKVSLHHMTQNGP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-18T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-18T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-01T18:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-01T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Multi award-winning “magnificent Fringe legends” (Time Out) Sh!t Theatre are back! And we're totally fine! Actually all things considered, we're OK. Feeling alright. Thriving, even? That's a bit far, but we have learnt some folk songs. We've got into folk recently and it's been really helpful. Come and sing some folk songs with us! A swift 60 minutes of classic folk followed by a trip downstairs to the bar and then a singaround. Because we need a drink, don't we? But we're doing OK. \r\n“Few companies make shows that are so consistently, outrageously fun” (Guardian)\r\n*fun not guaranteed\r\nThis show runs at 60 minutes, and is followed by a chance to continue to singing* and drinking** together in the performance space. Please join us after the show for the singaround if you would like to.\r\n*singing not obligatory\r\n**drinking not obligatory\r\nFor Sh!t Theatre’s previous work:\r\n‘Theatre that is true, hilarious and horrifying’\r\n★★★★★  Independent\r\n‘An unlikely pair of state-of-the-nation playwrights’\r\n★★★★ Guardian\r\n‘Surreal, clever and hilarious’\r\n★★★★ Daily Telegraph\r\n\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":135,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Or What’s Left Of Us – Preview","instanceDates":"22 July-24 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"550203ADTRTJCHKPRPSQJVBHCTNPPNDSL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-22T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-22T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-24T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-24T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Berlin's cult brother-sister duo Otto & Astrid make anexplosive return to Soho with their award-winning new show.Fresh from sold-out seasons in New York, Los Angeles andSan Francisco, and filming their first TV pilot, Otto & Astridare back to thunder through (almost) every song they've everwritten, if they can get through them without destroying eachother.A lipstick-smeared sonic collision between The B-52s, Pixies,Kraftwerk and early Ramones. Ridiculously catchy, blisteringlyfunny and surprisingly heartfelt. Think Tenacious D'sabsurdity meets Spinal Tap's incompetence, with Oasis-levelcombustibility. Fast, loud and impossible to look away from.Taylor Swift had eras. Otto & Astrid go through stag\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Otto & Astrid: The Stages Tour","instanceDates":"24 July-25 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"736203AVGMQTKKMTDVCKSHPPJTCLMMBGR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-24T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-24T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-25T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-25T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"We are in the Speed Queen, the last launderette on the Isle of Wight!\r\nHere, Pet, an ancient washerwoman, divines the fates of her customers through their dirty laundry, and a story unfolds of an island ill-at-ease. \r\nPart folklore, part pitch-black comedy, Speed Queen is a hauntingly funny debut that blends the Isle of Wight’s untold myths and hidden histories with folk horror, original music, and razor-sharp character work in this double Comedian’s Choice award-nominated, “gorgeously evocative, otherworldly debut hour from a rising star.” (The Reviews Hub).\r\nDirected by Tanika Lay-Meachen. Costumes by Sonya Mullen. Original music composed by Tom Penn,with lyrics by Ozzy Algar.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ozzy Algar: Speed Queen","instanceDates":"13 November-15 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"658203APPKGSVQMRKKNGPNQHHGSSMBDML","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-13T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-13T22:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-15T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-15T22:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Edinburgh Comedy Award 2023 Best Newcomer nominated Paddy makes his Soho Theatre debut!\r\nHe's hungry. He's horny. He's scared. He's in the gutter but he's looking down on all of you.\r\nJoin Northern powerhouse Paddy Young for his unmissable debut stand-up tour, fresh from a sell-out, smash hit run at the Edinburgh Fringe.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"PADDY YOUNG: HUNGRY, HORNY, SCARED","instanceDates":"9 November-3 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"494403AKDNBJQKJHSTHPCSGRQNHPDLLKQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-09T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-09T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-03T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-03T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A second show has hit Paddy Young, and this time he's yearning. \r\nYou ever been so loved up you had to hit yourself over the head with a hammer to calm down?  You can't stare at your crush but my god you can close your eyes and imagine your future together. Join him for thousands of kisses, hundreds of cuddles and the TINIEST bit of shagging. \r\n\r\n2023 Edinburgh Comedy Award Best Newcomer\r\n2024 Chortle Award Best Newcomer winner\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Paddy Young: If I Told You I’d Have to Kiss You","instanceDates":"10 March-15 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"577003ATTCRLJNLLHGVHBLQJRGLDMVDCL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-10T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-10T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-15T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-15T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A second show has hit Paddy Young, and this time he's yearning.\r\nYou ever been so loved up you had to hit yourself over the head with a hammer to calm down?  You can't stare at your crush but my god you can close your eyes and imagine your future together. Join him for thousands of kisses, hundreds of cuddles and the TINIEST bit of shagging. \r\n\r\n2023 Edinburgh Comedy Award Best Newcomer\r\n2024 Chortle Award Best Newcomer winner\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Paddy Young: If I Told You I’d Have to Kiss You.","instanceDates":"18 November-20 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"576803ADDSNQHKQGGPKCBPBJRCDCJPNSG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-18T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-18T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-20T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-20T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"website (20-25 words) The award-winning stand-up and star of Saturday Night Live UK heads out on tour with a brand new show.\r\nYou’re born alone, you die alone. That’s true enough. But what happened to that part in the middle? Big Year for Pad. SNL (UK, but still a big deal), a bunch of awards (hate bringing them up), and plenty of bit-parts to boot. But what’s it all about? I’ve fallen in love more times than you’ve had hot dinners and I’ve fumbled every single one of them. If you think I’ve learnt my lesson you couldn’t be wronger. I’m telling you, some of these baddies have got me winning staring competitions with the ceiling. But I don’t even think about that shit anymore. Some of my ideas are so funny that they scare me, so GOD knows how you lot are gonna feel !! As seen on: Mitchell & Webb Are Not Helping, Everyone Else Burns, and his own stand-up special Hungry. Horny. Scared.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Paddy Young: Will Sir Be Laughing Alone?","instanceDates":"19 November-20 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"710803AGBPGRJBCBGLNMQSBJCDJGRNSGC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-19T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-19T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-20T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-20T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"From Rifco Theatre comes an immersive DJ bromance.\r\nWhoever said there are too many actors in LA has never seen the number of DJs in Southall. Nowadays, anyone with a laptop and a pair of headphones can post a video of themselves online mixing a few tracks and claim to be from the same pind as Diljit Dosanjh.\r\nPali is an old school lover of the craft. His heart is set on moulding his nephew Jay into the heir to his empire, built one dancefloor tile at a time. But Jay is only interested in the perks of the gig: free food and fitties in the crowd. Meanwhile, cases of rival DJ sabotage are on the rise…\r\nUsing only their simple DJ set up and the odd cup of chai, Pali and Jay will transport you through time, from Southall’s Biggest Deck Off 1999 to now.\r\nOur uncle and nephew DJing duo must successfully navigate their latest gig to save the company, their future aspirations, and ultimately, their relationship.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Pali and Jay's Ultimate Asian Wedding DJ Roadshow – Preview","instanceDates":"23 July-27 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"548803ACRCSCHLGKNVJQMRNGLJGRCKMPJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-23T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-23T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-27T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-27T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Work In Progress","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A caustic entertainment for the winter months.\r\nA funny, wild ongoing history play \r\nabout how our great leaders grappled first with the Pandemic and then with each \r\nother.\r\nThe Johnson-Truss-Sunak years told at a furious pace in all their horrible glory. Relive the horror! The Mess! The Murk! The lying about the lies!\r\nJingle while you mingle with Bully Raab and Super Suella\r\nIt’s one big dodgy party. Bring a suitcase\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Pandemonium","instanceDates":"1 December-13 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"492203AMPTPCKBRRPDKHNGSRCMRJMJQJL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-01T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-01T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-13T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-13T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Political","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Nathan Queeley-Dennis won the Bruntwood Prize for Playwriting 2022 for his play BULLRING TECHNO MAKEOUT JAMZ - the acclaimed production was championed by lead producer Ellie Keel, who also oversees the Women’s Prize for Playwriting.\r\n As part of the Bruntwood Prize for Playwriting’s 20th anniversary celebrations, and to celebrate the arrival of BULLRING’s national tour at Soho Theatre, a selection of national playwriting prizes are coming together to discuss the role they play in the new writing ecology and theatre industry.\r\n Join the panel as they reflect on the successes and challenges these awards present to both playwrights and organisations. Panellists will include representatives from the Alfred Fagon Award, the Bruntwood Prize for Playwriting, Papatango New Writing Prize, Soho Theatre’s Verity Bargate Award, Theatre503 International Playwriting Award & the Women’s Prize for Playwriting.\r\nThe panel discussion will be chaired by critically acclaimed theatre director Matthew Xia (TAMBO & BONES, ATC/Theatre Royal Stratford East; SKELETON CREW, Donmar Warehouse)\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Panel Event: Reflecting On Playwriting Prizes","instanceDates":"12 November-12 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"581003AHSHCTHSVGJSCSQJSDKLMCTMSNJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-12T17:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-12T17:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-12T17:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-12T17:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"A raucous queer comedy with songs, Pansexual Pregnant Piracy explores the swashbuckling true story of eighteenth-century pirate Anne Bonny. Disguised as a man, Anne soars across oceans searching for booty (treasure) and booty (ass) alongside fellow pirate/partner/captain Calico Jack. \r\nBut when hot wet babe Mary Read crawls aboard, the ship's course isn't the only thing that's no longer straight. Can they flee the shadow of the Pirate Hunter General who dreams of taking down piracy and pansexuality? And what does it mean for their queer seafaring when their bellies brew more than just rum?!\r\n\r\nOutlandish comedy collides with a ne’er-before-seen queer tale in Pansexual Pregnant Piracy, the follow-up to Airlock’s Offie-nominated Lesbian Space Crime.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Pansexual Pregnant Piracy","instanceDates":"26 March-13 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"514203AGPTVKTRHHRSMGCPDSBJBDKRTRH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-26T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-26T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-13T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-13T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"Queen of Ireland Panti Bliss makes a welcome return to Soho Theatre with her smash-hit comedy show If These Wigs Could Talk.\r\n\r\nFresh from making history on RTE’s Dancing with the Stars, If These Wigs Could Talk meets notorious drag queen Panti at 54, after a lifetime of accidental activism, far-fetched shenanigans and making a full time show of herself, now taking a moment to question what her purpose and place in this changing world is.\r\n\r\nExpect salacious stories, impassioned polemics, and some seriously funny soul searching as Panti takes us from rural Mayo to London’s glittering West End to the Irish Ambassador’s residence in Vienna, where along the way the answer to her existential question presents itself where she least expects it.\r\n\r\nFollowing a record-breaking sold-out run at the Abbey Theatre in Dublin, Panti invites you to learn from her ridiculous mistakes, laugh at her glittering failures, and share in her triumphs, in this big, beautiful and brilliant night out.\r\n\r\n‘Hilariously vivid...mesmerising.’ ***** The Sunday Times\r\n‘Glittering and glorious’ **** The Reviews Hub\r\n‘Probing and lyrical’ **** The Irish Times\r\n‘A first-rate raconteur’ The Irish Independent\r\n\r\nCast & Creatives\r\n\r\nWritten and performed by Panti Bliss\r\nDirected by Phillip McMahon\r\nProduced by Jennifer Jennings and Laura Rigney\r\n\r\n16+ recommendation","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Panti Bliss: If These Wigs Could Talk","instanceDates":"26 May-10 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"464203ACHBRDSCCBQQDJPRNLJPJDVVRVS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-26T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-26T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-10T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-10T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Drag","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"Paper Swans draws on absurdist theatre, visual symbolism and the playwright's personal experience, as a woman from a post-Soviet country coming to the UK.\r\nPaper Swans is a one act play set in a closed park at night. \r\nA security guard finds a young woman in a ballet dress sitting on a bench making paper swans. \r\nAs he tries to find out what she is doing and why, he locks them in a continuous never-ending loop of having to encounter each other again and again. However, each time they meet, there is a slight change in the situation from the one before. \r\nThis work draws on absurdist theatre, visual symbolism and the playwright's personal experience, as a woman from a post-Soviet country (Lithuania) coming to the UK.\r\n14+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Paper Swans by Vyte Garriga","instanceDates":"28 April-3 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"604003AKMMKDKQBVTHBQBGCJTGBHVLPGB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-28T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-28T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-03T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-03T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Performance Art","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Fresh from a ★★★★★ sell-out Edinburgh Fringe run, comedy trio Pat Rascal present one boy’s dream to send Yorkshire to Mars (now via central London)\r\n‘One of the best examples of its kind, revelling in its absurdity’ Chortle\r\nCritically-acclaimed trio Pat Rascal (two-thirds Yorkshire-bred, one-third jealous) bring you a “manic, tightly-paced hour” (★★★★★ EdFringeReview) exploring friendship, identity, and Hull's award-winning aquarium The Deep.\r\nTop Ten Best Reviewed Shows of Edinburgh Fringe | British Comedy Guide 2025\r\nTop Picks of the Fringe | EdFringeReview\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Pat Rascal: Space Gravy","instanceDates":"26 March-28 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"690203ABCPNNBSHGJHNSPQJCVHDJLJGHJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-26T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-26T22:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-28T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-28T22:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Sketch","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Jokeless comedian Patti Harrison (\"I Think You Should Leave\",\"The Tonight Show\") is back at Soho Theatre to host a secretive variety show with some very special friends, beautiful guests, upsetting surprises, and sexual revelations. No night will be the same! Still wondering what the show will be? Don't Ask!\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Patti Harrison presents... DON'T ASK: A Variety Show With Friends","instanceDates":"28 July-7 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"635403AMJDKQGTDRBQHLHMTVRGSQKKJMM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-28T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-28T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-07T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-07T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Do you like to laugh? Haha!\r\nComedian Patti Harrison (“I Think You Should Leave”, “Shrill”, “The Tonight Show” One of Vogue Magazine’s “20 Funniest Female Comedians of All Time” (yes, they’re ranking that now!)) is back in the UK with a new HORRIBLE comedy show that will probably give you “DIARHEOAHA of THE MIND”. She doesn’t know how to spell Diarhreoaha, but hopes you understand she simply means like when the stinky dark water come out the back of you, if that helps.\r\nAnyway, the show will be a mixed bag: 1 part stand-up, 1 part variety show, maybe some horrible guests, and probably some other crap as well. Each night is sure to be different, like a snowflake. Did you know that? Every single snowflake is different. Like this show. I feel like you’re not understanding me.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Patti Harrison: Just Ironing Some Things Out!","instanceDates":"3 August-15 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"717403ANDPTJKHGRPRGJKQVRRNQDJVMHT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-03T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-03T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-15T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-15T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Patti Harrison is back at Soho Theatre with an extended run of her phenomenal show.\r\nAs seen and heard on I Think You Should Leave with Tim Robinson, The Lost City, Made For Love, Together Together, Shrill, The Tonight Show, Bob’s Burgers, Bojack Horseman, Jimmy Kimmel Live, and more.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Patti Harrison: My Huge Tits Huge Because They Are Infected NOT FAKE","instanceDates":"24 May-20 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"537403ALQSBVPCSDJVCDDMCGGLHSKGDJS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-24T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-24T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-20T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-20T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Following 2022’s sell-out Edinburgh run, cult comedy icon Patti Harrison (I Think You Should Leave, The Lost City) returns with an hour of comedy that refuses to be categorized. Expect pure, chaotic fun.\r\n‘Wildly unexpected… the most rarefied of comic pleasures.’ \r\n**** Guardian\r\n‘Once seen, Harrison is never forgotten.’ \r\n**** Scotsman\r\n‘Unique, unpredictable and eccentric.’\r\n**** Chortle\r\n\r\n16+ recommended","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Patti Harrison: My Huge Tits Huge Because They Are Infected NOT FAKE! – Work in Progress","instanceDates":"20 July-29 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"472603AKMPQQVLPTDPRSDLHQMBKHCDMCG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-20T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-20T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-29T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-29T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Cash Cow marks Paul’s much-anticipated return to stand-up after his sell-out sketch show All Sorts.\r\nIn this new show Paul delivers his trademark mix of sharp observations, colourful characters, impressions and Glaswegian charm. \r\nSir Billy Connolly Spirit of Glasgow Award Nominee 2023 & 2025. RTS Scotland Comedy Award Nominee 2023\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Paul Black: Cash Cow","instanceDates":"7 May-9 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"671403AJJTMTBNGQBQCDLHBVCSNMBSPGQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-07T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-07T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-09T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-09T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"“SHTOOM” is a brand new show for Paul Currie, for the first time in his 10th hour long show he will not speak for 60min and still bring all the laughs. After 15 years as a professional stand-up Currie will go full fool. Imagine the anarchy & grace of Charlie Chaplin, the pathos & empathy of Buster Keaton, the charm & insanity of Lucille Ball meets the mayhem and sweat of a Parisian riot & the Muppet show all rolled into one and filtered through a single human. \r\nShtoom! is a truly unique, surrealist, dada punk-clown, non-verbal, stand-up comedy experience from this award-winning Belfast comedy artist.\r\n\r\nNominated *BEST SHOW* \r\nNEW edinburgh comedy awards. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Paul Currie: Shtoom","instanceDates":"8 February-10 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"519803AHVKRDQTMRVHTCQMNTDKHHJTVJS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-08T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-08T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-10T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-10T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The SELL OUT Edinburgh fringe show and Stewart Lee’s favourite show of Ed FRINGE ‘22 has arrived to Soho. The Chorus of Ghosts’ is a true fully immersive rollercoaster of a trip into the mind of Paul Currie, dipping into every cortex from gender, ADHD, bullying, depression, Victorian music hall, musical ironing boards .. but mostly it’s about letting go, and being brutally honest! \r\n I want this show to help smash or at least crack the stigma we all have of mental health and gender. Now strap in!! And hold onto your wobbly bits as Paul Currie will be kicking everything fully in the NON BINARIES!! \r\nTCOGLIMSKTMTTASITFS is the sister show to Paul’s SELL OUT 2021 show “TEET”\r\n\r\n“The best comedy I saw was Paul Currie, which felt like the right comedy for this moment in human history.”\r\nStewart Lee\r\n⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️\r\n\r\n“What a joy this show is. Utterly unpredictable. Gloriously Funny”\r\n⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️\r\nEntertainment Now\r\n\r\n“INCREDIBLE! A treasure trove of imaginative physical comedy.”\r\nTHE SCOTSMAN\r\n⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Paul Currie: The Chorus of Ghosts Living in My Skull...","instanceDates":"11 May-13 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"445803ABDTVHBSNJMRPMKCSJBQRQSDGQM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-11T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-11T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-13T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-13T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Professional odd-ball Paul F Taylor is heading to the Soho Theatre with a supremely silly new show. Paul has been a man that has always thrown himself to the gods of chaos. Growing up; people often accused him of having his head in the clouds. With recently being diagnosed with ADHD; it’s little wonder that he’s not had his feet on the ground. And now Paul questions his place in this world of distractions that is seemingly not built for people like him. As a new father he’s learning the hard way, having something that demands him to keep his focus, when he can’t, isn’t easy. Yet in this very serious world, Paul makes his case that we now and again, can very much do with having our Head In The Clouds by airlifting audiences into a world of whimsy.\r\nPaul has appeared on Harry Hill’s Nite Club on Channel 4 and also the award winning BBC Radio 4 sketch show Please Use Other Door. He was nominated for best new show at the Leicester Comedy Festival 2017, and won the Hackney Empire New Act of the Year Award in 2013. As an actor and writer, he has starred in many comedy short films that have won critical acclaim and awards on the festival circuit as a long time collaborator with the two time BAFTA nominated director Ben Mallaby; in films such as Milk, Battlecock! and Guilt Trip and his latest film Bleep by Ben Hyland being selected my multiple BIFA and BAFTA qualifying film festivals. Along with his wife Rebecca Shorrocks, he is one half of sketch duo Short & Curly who enjoyed mass critical success at the Edinburgh Fringe as well as being nominated for Best Character and Sketch Act in the Chortle Awards.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Paul F Taylor: Head in the Clouds","instanceDates":"4 May-4 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"533803AVCDDSGPMRCMMNJTRNTSVMVSNGN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-04T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-04T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-04T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-04T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Multi-award-winning and trail-blazing comedian, Paul Foot, is back on tour with Dissolve, his most personal, surprising and ground-breaking show ever. \r\nLife is a stress: full of rushed breakfasts, angry people, internal conflict, and Jacob Rees-Mogg. But what happens when everything you thought was important – your problems, grievances against others, your very identity – simply disappears?\r\n\r\nIn the year 2022 AD something momentous changed for Paul, and in this show he will reveal how he discovered the secret of life on the outskirts of Lancaster.* Inevitably he does get distracted by King Tutankhamun, the House of Lords, Sir Cliff Richard, officious lollipop ladies and what Jesus might have achieved if he’d been a plumber.\r\n\r\nAs seen on Would I Lie To You?, Never Mind the Buzzcocks and 8 Out of 10 Cats Does Countdown.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Paul Foot: Dissolve","instanceDates":"25 November-30 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"563003AVGLTCDBMSRTSVTJCBVQBGLGSPC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-25T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-25T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-30T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-30T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join us for a special live recording of multi-award-winning and trail-blazing comedian, Paul Foot’s critically-acclaimed show, Dissolve. His most personal, surprising and ground-breaking show ever.\r\nLife is a stress: full of rushed breakfasts, angry people, internal conflict, and Jacob Rees-Mogg. But what happens when everything you thought was important – your problems, grievances against others, your very identity – simply disappears?\r\n\r\nIn the year 2022 AD something momentous changed for Paul, and in this show he will reveal how he discovered the secret of life on the outskirts of Lancaster.* Inevitably he does get distracted by King Tutankhamun, the House of Lords, Sir Cliff Richard, officious lollipop ladies and what Jesus might have achieved if he’d been a plumber.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Paul Foot: Dissolve (Filmed Performance)","instanceDates":"7 February-7 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"529203ADDBVQCGPCJPPRGJBSVTQQCDHVB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-07T18:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-07T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-07T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-07T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Multi-award-winning and trail-blazing comedian, Paul Foot, is back on tour with Dissolve, his most personal, surprising and ground-breaking show ever. \r\nLife is a stress: full of rushed breakfasts, angry people, internal conflict, and Jacob Rees-Mogg. But what happens when everything you thought was important – your problems, grievances against others, your very identity – simply disappears?\r\n\r\nIn the year 2022 AD something momentous changed for Paul, and in this show he will reveal how he discovered the secret of life on the outskirts of Lancaster.* Inevitably he does get distracted by King Tutankhamun, the House of Lords, Sir Cliff Richard, officious lollipop ladies and what Jesus might have achieved if he’d been a plumber.\r\n\r\nAs seen on Would I Lie To You?, Never Mind the Buzzcocks and 8 Out of 10 Cats Does Countdown.\r\n\r\n(ISH) Edinburgh Comedy Awards 2023 – Best Show Co-Winner\r\n\r\nNextUp Biggest Award In Comedy 2023 – Nominee\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Paul Foot: Dissolve.","instanceDates":"12 February-24 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"495203ALNJCJDRDQRHRDHMBCQSDSQCBSQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-12T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-12T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-24T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-24T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"Pioneering alt-comedy hero and star of Cats Does Countdown Paul Foot is back on tour with a brand-new stand-up show.\r\nRemember when people were excited for the future? With visions of jetpacks, friendly robots wheeling around, and solar-powered bidets. Well, we don’t have visions like that anymore, do we? But the universe is not over. The light has not gone out. Here’s a candle in the dark. Contagious and whispering. And you can take it with you when you leave. As seen on Would I Lie To You?, Never Mind the Buzzcocks and 8 Out of 10 Cats Does Countdown. Winner: (ISH) Edinburgh Comedy Awards 2023 – Best Show Co-Winner ‘Funnier and more daring than I’ve ever seen him… [has] the audience laughing so hard they’re about to leave their bodies’ ★★★★★ Chortle\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Paul Foot: The Future","instanceDates":"23 November-5 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"725803ASMNJTMRSJSTLDBRTDVPSRQKRVM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-23T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-23T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-05T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-05T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The Taskmaster New Zealand star presents a work in progress of his brand new show. Having told over a thousand jokes and received countless rounds of applause and bouts of laughter. Not to mention the smiles he's procured. Everyone is telling Paul that this is gonna be his year and he's feeling very optimistic about how it's going to go. Just don't look at him. **** (Times). **** (List). **** (Skinny).14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Paul Williams: Don't Look At Me (WIP)","instanceDates":"17 July-19 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"641803ACCMRKHSLHGGCSLGVLQRRDNPBSJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-17T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-17T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-19T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-19T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"After a sold-out run at run in 2022, New Zealand’s fastest comedian (5km and 10km) returns to Soho Theatre for an enchanting evening In the Moonlight. The show includes music, romance and even photos. He’s been on TV, starring in the critically reviewed Taskmaster New Zealand. Good for all ages but if you’re really old, please only come if you promise to stay calm. \r\n'How much of Paul Williams’ endearing clumsiness is planned, and how much is accidental, is difficult to ascertain' - Chortle \r\n'Insanely talented'  - Rose Matafeo\r\n★★★★ The Times \r\n★★★★ The Skinny\r\n★★★★ The List\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Paul Williams: In the Moonlight","instanceDates":"5 July-7 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"479603ALQKKTTLPDDRBRQNHPKMTDBJDGG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-05T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-05T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-07T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-07T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Meet Conchita and Lola, also known as ‘CONCHOLA’, the wandering, weaving, witches of the north (London). Played by Paulina Lenoir and Patricia Langa, these witches will guide you on a mystical and whimsical journey to find their lost sense of belonging and mischievous herd of goats. Through flamenco, dance, clowning, and song, they’ll unveil their dreams, spellbinding rituals and pungent potions to tell you their captivating tale.\r\nAccompanied with live music from the magical Sarah Woolfenden and Ago Hernández.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Paulina Lenoir & Patricia Langa: CONCHOLA","instanceDates":"20 June-20 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"616403ACRDDTTLPDQHVRSGTBTRTHQHSMT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-20T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-20T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-20T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-20T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Would you like to live forever?\r\nThis is a show about LIFE, in all its stages.  \r\nTold by a poetic idiot in search of eternity – between the pages.  \r\nAcclaimed designer turned 'virtuosic clown' (FringeReview) Paulina Lenoir presents a tale of birth, life and death told through the eyes of this generation's most renowned couture poet, Puella Eterna. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Paulina Lenoir: Puella Eterna","instanceDates":"13 November-16 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"571603ATGGHVKCBNMQSPCRNTLCTSPHRJV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-13T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-13T22:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-16T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-16T22:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A debut comedy show about LIFE in all its stages. Self-renowned poet Puella Eterna brings you a tale of birth, life and death. Part of London Clown Festival 2024.\r\nWould you like to live forever?\r\nThis is a show about LIFE, in all its stages.\r\nTold by a poetic idiot in search of eternity - between the pages. \r\nAcclaimed designer and theatre-maker turned \"virtuosic clown\" (FringeReview) Paulina Lenoir presents a tale of birth, life and death told through the eyes of this generation's most renowned poet, Puella Eterna.  \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Paulina Lenoir: Puella Eterna.","instanceDates":"11 July-11 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"543205ADTKRKHDBPJTTSCRGVGRLPCPDBM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-11T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-11T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-11T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-11T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Top Ten Best Reviewed Shows of the Edinburgh Fringe 2024. \r\n\r\n6 foot 7 identical twins Patrick and Hugo McPherson return to the Soho Theatre for more riotous comedy. After a sold-out stint at the Soho in 2024, followed by their third consecutive sold-out Edinburgh Fringe, Pear is an award-winning smash-hit.\r\n\r\n‘An effortlessly funny hour’ (centre of page)\r\nThe Independent (centre of page) \r\n\r\nCome witness the tallest, most identical comedians in the world (not proven, though confidently assumed). After all, \"the McPhersons are destined for greatness\" The List.\r\n\r\n\r\n*And then, if we could, could we have ALL these quotes on the bottom with the stars (I know you have that awesome feature where you can do a review slideshow)*\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Pear","instanceDates":"15 May-9 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"600203AKBPPBJCTLPPDCLLJNHQBRGTCGN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-15T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-15T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-09T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-09T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Sketch","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"6 foot 7 identical twins Patrick and Hugo McPherson bring an hour of riotous, chaotic and hilarious comedy to the Soho Theatre. Fresh from their sold-out Edinburgh Fringe 2023 and Fringe World 2024, Pear is the unique award-winning sketch show described as “hilarious from start to finish” ★ ★ ★ ★ ★ (MervsPOTFringe) and “relentlessly packed with jokes” ★ ★ ★ ★ ★ (ThreeWeeks).\r\n\r\nCome witness the tallest, most identical comedians in London (not proven, though confidently assumed).\r\n\r\nWinner – Critics’ Choice Award, FRINGE WORLD 2023\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Pear.","instanceDates":"20 June-22 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"541203ACNVBVRCPVSJKNDCKTVNVRQVTKB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-20T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-20T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-22T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-22T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Sketch","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Natalie Palamides and Lucy Pearman are two very normal girls who will share an hour. 25 mins each probably. One normal girl, then the other one, then home time. We don’t really know what they will do yet because life can be a bit like that sometimes. Please come if you don’t mind that they don’t know what will happen exactly \r\n Edinburgh Comedy Award Best Newcomer Nominee (Lucy) & WINNER (Natalie) Natalie lets Lucy hold the trophy.  \r\nBAFTA Nominee (Lucy) and BAFTA Winner wannabe (Natalie) Lucy lets Natalie look at the certificate\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":65,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"pEARMAN theN pALAMIDES","instanceDates":"22 July-24 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"484803ANSJRTHDDPPGGTPQKJPCJSMPJBP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-22T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-22T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-24T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-24T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Work In Progress","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Pecsmas is coming to town. \r\nThe wise Pecs Drag Kings return to Soho Theatre and want to treat all you nice (and naughty) queers to a big queermas cabaret that’ll leave you sleighed with laughter.\r\n\r\nWipe away that resting Grinch face and get ready to be dazzled by queermas classics and tree-mendous dances in this stocking stuffed show. \r\n\r\nBut wait there’s myrrh. Every night Santa will bring you the perfect gift, with a special guest performer from London’s drag scene that will get your baubles tingling with delight. \r\n\r\nJoin us for a show that’s anything but a silent night. \r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Pecsmas","instanceDates":"12 December-22 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"510803ADJGHSJGGRHGVCGQJBBBDRMNTSK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-12T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-12T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-22T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-22T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Theatre"},{"description":"2025 sees Penguin Cafe bringing the music of the legendary Penguin Cafe Orchestra back to life, with UK dates featuring a collection of PCO classics, celebrating the unique sound that has captivated audiences worldwide\r\n2025 sees Penguin Cafe bringing the music of the legendary Penguin Cafe Orchestra back to life, with UK dates featuring a collection of PCO classics, celebrating the unique sound that has captivated audiences worldwide.\r\nTo coincide with this revival, six original PCO albums are being re-released on vinyl for the first time since their initial pressings, courtesy of [INTEGRAL] / Universal Music Recordings at the end of 2024 and will be available to buy at live shows.\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Penguin Cafe Performs Music From The Penguin Cafe Orchestra ","instanceDates":"1 November-1 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"623803ANSCCSHNGRSLDTRMHMQGTNPJCGP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-01T18:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-01T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-01T18:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-01T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Performance Art","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Music","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":""},{"description":"From award-winning writer Gayathiri Kamalakanthan.\r\nA Tamil teenager is preparing for their period party – a traditional ritual meant to mark womanhood. But Krish isn’t a girl. And this ‘celebration’ feels more like the opening act of a never-ending performance. As expectations mount, Krish decides to take control. With help from their best friend Brenavee and a growing chosen family, Krish flips the script to throw the degendered party of their dreams.\r\nSet in 2010, in the aftermath of genocide, Period Parrrty is an ode to Tamil survival and self-determination. This is no ordinary coming-of-age story. This is a trans Tamil party. And you're invited.\r\nPeriod Parrrty (nominated for the Tony Craze Award) is the debut play from Gayathiri Kamalakanthan. A Tamil writer and performer, they are the recipient of the Disabled Poets Prize, the Faber & Andlyn Publisher's Prize and the Royal Society of Literature: Literature Matters Award. Their novel-in-verse, Bad Queer, is forthcoming with Faber.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":85,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Period Parrrty","instanceDates":"23 October-22 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"637803ASTSCSCTRTRJSVVNTCCJDPDKSGJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-23T18:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-23T17:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-22T18:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-22T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Experience the magic of Elvis like never before with Peter Serafinowicz's groundbreaking work-in-progress show. Using deep fake technology, Serafinowicz brings the King back to life on stage, channelling his iconic voice and larger-than-life persona. With his signature brand of humour and impeccable timing, Serafinowicz creates a show that's both hilarious and heartfelt, paying tribute to one of the greatest entertainers of all time.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Peter Serafinowicz presents The Elvis 2023 Comeback Special (Work in Progress)","instanceDates":"18 May-20 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"471803AJMVSLLSTGCBBMGSCNHRJRGBDRT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-18T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-18T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-20T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-20T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Using deep fake technology, Peter Serafinowicz brings the King of the Elves back to life on stage for a Christmas variety show featuring some other famous faces. With his signature brand of humour and impeccable timing, Serafinowicz creates a show that’s both hilarious and heartfelt, paying tribute to one of the greatest entertainers of all time.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Peter Serafinowicz presents: Christmas Magic with Elvis & Friends (Work in Progress)","instanceDates":"19 August-24 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"563403AKCHDGCQCCMCTJJCPJKSQGLDTSC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-19T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-19T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-24T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-24T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Work In Progress","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Peter Smith's DIANA is a one-person musical spectacular, inspired by a certain blonde British woman named Diana, and that time she bared her soul on TV.\r\n\r\nCreated by and starring performing artist and musician Peter Smith, this tour-de-force uses music, monologues, dance and comedy to extrapolate on idol worship, bodily autonomy and self-love. \r\n\r\nThe myth of Diana gets dissected through a kaleidoscope - shining new light on words said long ago. Peter also takes a larger look at why it’s so easy for people to love, or quite often - hate people that we’ve never met. \r\n\r\nPeter Smith’s DIANA is the perfect combo of stunning performance, razor edge commentary and pop culture worship.\r\n\r\nCome witness the UK debut of this truly unique, thought provoking and highly entertaining show.\r\n\r\n‘Peter Smith is one of my favorite absurdist comedians. When I’m watching her, I feel like I’m immediately inside her world and it’s such a joyous place filled with laughter and love. Can’t get enough of this human.’\r\nReggie Watts \r\n\r\n‘Peter Smith… is a genius’\r\nHollywood Reporter\r\n\r\n‘Tragic and disorienting, and occasionally hilarious.’\r\nNY Times\r\n\r\n‘Wickedly playful’\r\nNew Yorker\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Peter Smith’s DIANA","instanceDates":"14 July-29 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"479003ABLTRBGMTSPCVJJLHTPLRVRBBCK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-14T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-14T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-29T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-29T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"Multi-award winning 'comic genius' (The Scotsman) and the new star of Taskmaster (Ch4), Phil Ellis is going on his first full national stand-up tour.\r\nFollowing his three big award wins at the 2025 Edinburgh Fringe, Phil, the very definition of funny bones, presents his brand-new show ‘Bath Mat’.\r\nJam-packed with laugh-out-loud profound silliness, superbly crafted gags and constant surprises, Phil is bringing his 'Bath Mat' to a city near you.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Phil Ellis: Bath Mat","instanceDates":"9 December-13 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"656603ASKRDGPKNNDHCJCSPCKNBDSJJVG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-09T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-09T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-13T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-13T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The 2023 Edinburgh Comedy Award Best Show Nominee and winner of the Malcom Hardee Award for Comic Originality returns with a brand-new show!\r\nAfter the huge success of his 2023 Phil Ellis's Excellent Comedy Show with numerous award wins, a massive national tour and two heart scares, he takes things back to basics with an hour of pure and unapologetic stand-up. As seen and heard on BBC Radio 4, BBC2, Comedy Central and Sky. 'Touched by comedy genius' (Scotsman). 'The density of gags is impressive' (Chortle.co.uk).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Phil Ellis: Come On and Take The Rest of Me","instanceDates":"10 April-12 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"605404AVPTVTRVTDMHBNBKSCKCVVRMSSP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-10T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-10T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-12T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-12T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Do you like comedy? Do you like shows? What are your thoughts on excellence? \r\nIf you like all three, then Edinburgh Comedy Award-winning Phil Ellis's Excellent Comedy Show is the excellent comedy show for you. An hour of hilarious stand-up and fun from the North West's most punctual working-class comedian. As seen and heard on BBC Two, Channel 4, BBC Three, Comedy Central and BBC Radio 4.\r\nEdinburgh Comedy Award Best Show Nominee 2023\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Phil Ellis’s Excellent Comedy Show","instanceDates":"9 May-11 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"517603ADVJRMSBRCPKPGJHQHNSCDLSTHT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-09T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-09T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-11T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-11T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"If you like all three, then Edinburgh Comedy Award-winning Phil Ellis's Excellent Comedy Show is the excellent comedy show for you. An hour of hilarious stand-up and fun from the North West's most punctual working-class comedian. As seen and heard on BBC Two, Channel 4, BBC Three, Comedy Central and BBC Radio 4.\r\nEdinburgh Comedy Award Best Show Nominee 2023\r\n\r\n‘Ellis as a character is both completely likeable and absolutely appalling.’  ***** Scotsman\r\n\r\n**** List\r\n**** Guardian\r\n**** Times\r\n**** Chortle\r\n\r\n16+ recommended","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Phil Ellis’s Excellent Comedy Show.","instanceDates":"7 November-11 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"495403APDKNVBPRBCNTCKHTSNQQGCCVMN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-07T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-07T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-11T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-11T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"UH NO. Phil Wang’s back with a new stand-up show, and he’s older than ever before.\r\nHe’s got a moustache now. It bristles with wisdom. His eyes shine with good humour. His shoulders groan under the weight of being the only cool millennial left. Everyone's an idiot but him. Nice is out. Right is in. The vibe shift is real. Old Wang’s riding it.\r\nYou know him from one series of Taskmaster, one episode of Would I Lie to You, and one minute of Wonka.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Phil Wang: UH OH","instanceDates":"24 September-18 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"679603AQSBNGGLCVRDJTTQGDDGKJVJHNN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-24T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-24T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-18T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-18T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Is it beginning to look a lot like Christmas? After this evening, there’ll be no doubt.\r\nLike mulled wine and mince pies, there’s something irresistibly warming about the sound of a brass music at Christmas. And tonight, you’re in safe hands – with the world-class brass players of the Philharmonia Orchestra.  \r\n \r\nBack for a second year, our dazzling musicians present a programme curated and introduced from the stage by Philharmonia trombonist Philip White. Whether you’re a fan of Christmas carols, classic No. 1 hits, or seasonally inspired orchestral music by the likes of Bach and beyond, we’re sure you’ll leave Soho Theatre Walthamstow feeling just that little bit more festive.\r\n8+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Philharmonia Brass at Christmas","instanceDates":"20 December-20 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"722003AMJNDGNHGRQCHQJLDSNSQTBJQCV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-20T14:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-20T14:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-20T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-20T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Music","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":""},{"description":"8+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Philharmonia Brass at Christmas.","instanceDates":"21 December-21 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"652803AKDKJDBRJKQTRGTHHDGHQDGPSMR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-21T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-21T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-21T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-21T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Music","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":""},{"description":"Nil Venditti conductor \r\nAnastasia Kobekina cello \r\nBeethoven Coriolan Overture \r\nShostakovich Cello Concerto No. 1 \r\nBeethoven Symphony No. 7 \r\n10+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Philharmonia Orchestra - Orchestral masterpieces: Beethoven and Shostakovich ","instanceDates":"28 September-28 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"652603AKJHHTCMBBLHBBLCGSLRDGPQKTS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-28T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-28T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-28T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-28T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Music","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":""},{"description":"Michael Collins - conductor / clarinet \r\nMozart Symphony No. 40 \r\nMozart Clarinet Concerto \r\nMozart Symphony No. 41\r\n10+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Philharmonia Orchestra: Mozart Masterpieces","instanceDates":"13 January-13 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"653003AHSRPGJDKVCTKBCGRNPNVPPKCHG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-13T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-13T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-13T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-13T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Music","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":""},{"description":"Leonhard Kreutzmann (Conductor), Alim Beisembayev (Piano). TCHAIKOVSKY Romeo & Juliet Fantasy Overture GRIEG Piano Concerto - INTERVAL - BEETHOVEN Symphony No. 5 Shakespeare’s Romeo and Juliet is one of the most heartbreakingly famous love stories to have ever been written. And who could better compose equally, achingly beautiful music to the story than Tchaikovsky? From the melancholic opening to the outpouring of passion in the climactic melody, Tchaikovsky’s rip-roaring Fantasy Overture is musical drama at its best. Followed by Grieg’s Piano Concerto. From its opening timpani roll and crashing chords to its anthemic final moments, it’s brimful of passion and remains one of the most popular pieces in the orchestral repertoire. This time, we hear it in the hands of Alim Beisembayev, winner of the prestigious Leeds International Piano Competition in 2021. Closing the concert is Beethoven’s mighty Fifth Symphony. The electrifying opening of the piece is one of the most iconic and instantly recognisable moments in orchestral music, but there’s so much more than that stop-you-in-your-tracks opening. Whether you’ve heard a dozen different recordings, or never listened to it all the way through, nothing beats experiencing it live. 8+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Philharmonia Orchestra: Tchaikovsky, Grieg & Beethoven","instanceDates":"13 October-13 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"746603AJHBNKSPGBHNLRMKMLTJHLJGLGG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-13T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-13T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-13T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-13T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Music","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":""},{"description":"Tanya Truman Productions presents:\r\n\r\nPickle by Deli Segal\r\n\r\nHere’s the shtick: Ari is caught between two worlds. Still living at home in North-West London, she has her Jewish life, dominated by overbearing parents, traditions, and expectations. Then there’s her day-to-day life - the job, the pub, the foreskins.\r\nWritten and performed by award-winning Deli Segal (Channel 4Screenwriting 2023), Pickle is a darkly comic uproarious simcha of a one-woman show about being Jewish and secular in the UK today. Expect smoked salmon, guilt and a large dose of self-deprecation.\r\nFollowing a sold-out tour at Park Theatre, Manchester Jewish Museum and Radlett Centre, Pickle comes to Soho Upstairs for a limited run this July.\r\nNOMINATED: Off West End award for BEST NEW PLAY \r\nNOMINATED:  Off West End award for BEST PEFORMANCE PIECE\r\nNOMINATED: Off West End award for SOUND DESIGN\r\n‘…always funny… a joyful celebration of what it means to be a Jewish woman' ★★★★★ The Theatre Weekly\r\n'Segal’s writing is sharp and consistently lands… a charming tale of belonging’ ★★★★ Always Time For Theatre\r\n‘Rich in feeling, humour and vitality, bringing a love for culture and life that is humbling to watch’★★★★ Everything Theatre\r\n‘…the makings of a Jewish Bridget Jones' ★★★★ The Jewish Chronicle \r\n'Very funny’ ★★★★ Reviews Hub\r\n'Hilarious, raw and honest’ Lost in Theatreland\r\nWRITER & PERFORMER | DELI SEGAL\r\nDIRECTOR | KAYLA FELDMAN\r\nPRODUCER | TANYA TRUMAN\r\nSET DESIGNER I ANDY BROCK\r\nSOUND DESIGNER I EMILY ROSE SIMONS\r\nMOVEMENT DIRECTOR & SOCIAL MEDIA CONTENT CREATOR I LAURA WOHLWEND\r\nASSISTANT DIRECTOR I JOSEPHINE FRANKEL\r\nACCESS & WELLBEING COORDINATOR I TAMARA MICNER\r\nSTAGE MANAGER I REUBEN BOJANG\r\nLIGHTING DESIGNER I LAUREL MARKS\r\nPRODUCTION ASSISTANT I ANGIE LAWRENCE\r\nARTWORK PHOTOGRAPHY | AIDAN ORANGE\r\nARTWORK DESIGN | EVANN NYACK\r\nPR | CHLOE NELKIN CONSULTING \r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":65,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Pickle","instanceDates":"10 July-12 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"467803AQGMTSTDJKMHDRGTGHCHPCHJBVT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-10T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-10T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-12T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-12T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Here’s the shtick: Ari is caught between two worlds. Still living at home in North-West London, she has her Jewish life, dominated by overbearing parents, traditions, and expectations. Then there’s her day-to-day life - the job, the pub, the foreskins.\r\nWritten and performed by award-winning Deli Segal (Channel 4Screenwriting 2023), Pickle is a darkly comic uproarious simcha of a one-woman show about being Jewish and secular in the UK today. Expect smoked salmon, guilt and a large dose of self-deprecation.\r\nFollowing a sold-out tour at Park Theatre, Manchester Jewish Museum and Radlett Centre, Pickle comes to Soho Upstairs for a limited run this July.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":65,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Pickle by Deli Segal","instanceDates":"15 April-27 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"515403ASKCLVVTDPSHPPBHJGDMGGBQLMS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-15T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-15T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-27T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-27T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Pierre Novellie returns to the Soho Theatre following a sold-out UK & Ireland tour and acclaimed Edinburgh Fringe run to perform a stand-up show about life, fairness and expectations. He simply must.\r\nCo-host of The Frank Skinner Podcast and BudPod with Phil Wang. As seen on World's Most Dangerous Roads (Dave), The Mash Report (BBC Two), Stand Up Central (Comedy Central), and as heard on The Now Show (BBC Radio 4). One of the best reviewed shows of the Edinburgh Festival Fringe 2024. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Pierre Novellie: Must We?","instanceDates":"10 March-22 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"586603AJJCLKMSHTQGGJDHSMRHMQTCVKQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-10T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-10T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-22T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-22T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Pierre Novellie returns with more observational nerd comedy, one last time before bed.\r\nFollowing the success of last year's show, You Sit There, I'll Stand Here, Pierre is back with a brand-new show, Okay, One More Then Bedtime, that touches on a wide range of topics, from his unique takes on food to a deep existential crisis. Come and see – it might be years before he wakes up!","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Pierre Novellie: Okay, One More Then Bedtime","instanceDates":"21 September-1 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"742403ALSQNKJGJVVPNNHHHTGJBJSQSBJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-21T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-21T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-01T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-01T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Pierre Novellie returns with more observational nerd comedy, one last time before bed. Following the success of last year's show, You Sit There, I'll Stand Here, Pierre is back with a brand-new show, Okay, One More Then Bedtime, that touches on a wide range of topics, from his unique takes on food to a deep existential crisis. Come and see – it might be years before he wakes up! 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":100,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Pierre Novellie: Okay, One More Then Bedtime","instanceDates":"18 February-18 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"755003ARVBLKDNBCPLRCGHCLGKJKLQLBN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-18T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-18T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-18T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-18T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Pierre Novellie is known for his award-winning comedy/observations which you might have enjoyed on The Frank Skinner Show on Absolute Radio, the hit podcast BudPod with Phil Wang, World’s Most Dangerous Roads and The Now Show on Radio 4. \r\n \r\nHe can’t stress enough that he thinks these thoughts are normal and reasonable – it’s you people that don’t make sense. He is the normal one, definitely, but that does raise an important question:\r\n \r\nWhy are you laughing?\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Pierre Novellie: Why Are You Laughing?","instanceDates":"26 March-6 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"518003AJPJPCDSLKSMTJNRGGBGMGCSQPT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-26T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-26T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-06T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-06T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"It's time for Pierre to do stand-up! It's time for you to watch! \r\nWhy not just embrace that, for God's sake? All earthly glories fade!\r\nCo-host of the Frank Skinner, Budpod and Button Boys podcasts and as seen and heard on World's Most Dangerous Roads (Dave), The Mash Report (BBC2), Stand Up Central (Comedy Central), The Now Show and The News Quiz (BBC Radio 4).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Pierre Novellie: You Sit There, I’ll Stand Here","instanceDates":"19 January-31 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"666603ALSHCRVKMBRGQKHTKGCVRVTVSJV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-19T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-19T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-31T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-31T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"South African satirist Pieter-Dirk Uys returns to Soho Theatre with his latest one-man show.\r\nSell-By Date features not only the man, author and social activist as himself, but a parade of icons – male, female and political – bringing Londoners news and memories from life in the Rainbow Nation. The South African and British general elections will also be celebrated for the ‘mock’ in democracy and the ‘con’ in Constitution.\r\n\r\nAt 78, Uys, with recent surgery adding a surprising twist, delivers laughter in chaos. Audiences are in for an unforgettable experience of wit and resilience. \r\n\r\nNelson Mandela, Desmond Tutu never had a sell-by date, nor it seem do his beloved characters, Evita Bezuidenhout and Nowell Fine, but after 60 years live on stage, Uys is not surprised when he’s asked: ‘When will you retire?’ His answer is short and sweet: ‘Not re-tyre; retread!’ \r\n\r\nThis 2024 performance brings London audiences Uys on top form: laughing at fears and embracing facts with his tongue firmly in your cheek. A sell-by date on food usually means \"use quickly\". See you there!\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Pieter-Dirk Uys: Sell By Date","instanceDates":"12 August-24 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"554203ANBPKKGDDNQKLRQTSCCPHRBDBLK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-12T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-12T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-24T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-24T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Validation is addictive, what could go wrong? Fresh from a sell-out, five-star debut at the Edinburgh Fringe, Farah Ashraf’s award-winning solo show transfers to Soho Theatre.  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nAmna is a good Muslim daughter. Mostly. At home, she’s modest, obedient, invisible. \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nOnline, she’s PersianBaby - bold, flirtatious, watched. Pink Rabbit is a fierce, coming-of-age, darkly funny solo play about faith, female desire and the intoxicating power of attention. Raw, intimate and electric, Pink Rabbit explores intergenerational and cultural conflict – and the dangerous moment when being seen finally feels better than being honest. 16+ (see webpage for current advice)","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Pink Rabbit","instanceDates":"24 November-12 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"757604ARRJQLPDLRDGPRGDTSBLJLMNCKB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-24T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-24T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-12T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-12T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Julia Grogan’s ★★★★★ smash-hit transfers from Edinburgh to Soho Theatre this Spring. \r\nThree friends grow up under an ancient tree. They’re filthy, brutal and full of hope. By turns hysterical and poign-ant, Playfight is a \"stunningly accomplished\" (★★★★★ The Observer) and searing probe of their inner lives as they hunt for love. Proper, ugly love. As their roots sink deeper, the branches stretch higher... so they decide to climb.\r\nAn Edinburgh Festival smash hit, Playfight by Julia Grogan is a \"marvellous jewel of a play\" (★★★★★ The Times) that shines a vivid light on adolescent desire in a landscape of rising sexual violence.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Playfight","instanceDates":"8 April-26 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"599404ASJHTLJNVJGRDJHRHSMPPSGBMVP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-08T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-08T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-26T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-26T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"Do you have what it takes to be a successful Latinx?\r\nHalf stand-up, half Latinx grab bag of stereotypes, this fun, politically incorrect seminar will coach the audience on how to be a good immigrant.\r\n\r\nThis one-human show merges spoken word poetry, comedy and music to explore both what the ‘Latinx’ label means in the UK and on a more personal level, the lengths we all go to to fit in.\r\n\r\nOff-Comm recipient 2022\r\nKeep It Fringe Winner 2023\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Playing Latinx by Guido Garcia Lueches","instanceDates":"10 April-13 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"513403ARSTCRKMLQNBNVKMGLNMMKCCMQV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-10T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-10T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-13T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-13T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A cocky gay clown in therapy.\r\nA clueless detective.\r\nAn X-Factor sob story.\r\nPop culture and queer drama collide against a rainbow vomit backdrop. A surreal, fast-paced and darkly funny exploration of a queer relationship gone bad. Blending clowning, drag and a subversive take on the trauma-parading solo show, plewds is about the lengths we’ll go to avoid what’s right in front of us, in a story where the villains don’t look like villains.\r\nBeing queer is the best, right?\r\nWINNER Summerhall Mary Dick Award\r\nSHORTLISTED Tony Craze Award\r\nSHORTLISTED Brighton Fringe Award for Excellence\r\nSHORTLISTED Binge Fringe Queer Performer Award\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Plewds","instanceDates":"11 February-12 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"687004APSSJDHKRPKHCJCJCJTLGVVMJGK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-11T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-11T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-12T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-12T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The multi award-winning comedy blockbuster returns! To celebrate their 10 year anniversary, globally acclaimed POLICE COPS return to Soho Theatre with the show that started it all! Reloaded and supercharged for 2026, expect adrenaline-fuelled physical comedy, 80s bangers and uncompromising facial hair. \r\n\r\nWinner: Stage Award for Acting Excellence. \r\nWinner: Best Show, Toronto Fringe. \r\nWinner: Best International Show, Cape Town Fringe. \r\nWinner: Brighton Fringe Award For Excellence. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"POLICE COPS","instanceDates":"8 June-13 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"722203AVQCDRHHTDNJRDRMKDDVTRGLPSR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-08T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-08T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-13T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-13T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Sketch","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"To celebrate their 10 year anniversary, globally acclaimed POLICE COPS return to Soho Theatre with their multi-award-winning comedy horror blockbuster!  MANCHESTER 1999: On the turn of the Millenium, a gritty, kitchen-sink drama turns into a vampire-slaying epic. Expect supercharged physical comedy, ’90s rave bangers and Manchester's finest 'sweets' to keep the party going all night long: it’s not only the stakes that are high.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"POLICE COPS BADASS BE THY NAME","instanceDates":"10 June-12 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"722403ATJVLVNRTCRDMMKRGPJMDPKGHDD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-10T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-10T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-12T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-12T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Sketch","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"To celebrate their 10 year anniversary, globally acclaimed POLICE COPS return to Soho Theatre with their multi-award-winning 'Low-Fi Sci-Fi' comedy blockbuster! With a whole galaxy of five-star reviews, expect rocket-fuelled action, ’80s bangers, and out-of-this-world physical comedy.\r\n\r\nWinner: Amused Moose Comedy Award\r\nWinner: Toronto Fringe Best Comedy\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"POLICE COPS IN SPACE","instanceDates":"9 June-13 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"722603AKCLJSRHCPKCCTPDBKCKNMPDRHJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-09T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-09T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-13T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-13T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Sketch","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Forget earned media. This is about earned applause.\r\nThe people working in public relations spend their days helping others command attention. For one night, they are stepping into the spotlight themselves. PR Has Talent is The UK's first live talent show for the public relations industry, bringing together performers from across the profession to reveal talents their colleagues may never have seen.\r\nExpect singers who usually write press releases. Dancers more accustomed to navigating stakeholder meetings. Comedians, poets, musicians, magicians and performers whose talents rarely make it beyond the office. Some will be seasoned performers. Others will be stepping onto a stage for the first time. All of them will be leaving the day job behind. Come along, support your colleagues and discover who earns the biggest applause on the night.\r\nOne night. No campaigns. No clients. Just courage.\r\nProceeds from the evening will support Soho Theatre's New Writing Programme, helping to discover and develop the next generation of writers and performers. Presented by Farzana Baduel and Graham Goodkind. 18+ (Check webpage for current content advice).","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":150,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"PR Has Talent","instanceDates":"17 November-17 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"749203ALNSNHTDSLSVVNQKCBGSDTBNNQK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-17T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-17T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-17T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-17T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Growing up in a patriarchal family, Prashasti naturally had only one dream – to become a patriarch herself.\r\nInching towards 40, but pretending to be 30, Prashasti can finally mark this dream complete.\r\nBut instead of happiness, she finds herself pondering whether the ascent was even worth the price.\r\nJoin Prashasti as she questions all her life choices and meticulously assigns blame to the women and men who shaped her into this being.\r\nFollowing her debut Edinburgh Fringe, Prashasti returns to Soho Theatre. A stand-up comic and writer from India, Prashasti can be seen on Netflix’s Ladies Up, Comedy Premium League and Amazon Prime Video’s Comicstaan. She has been touring internationally with her last show Man of the House. Her stand-up special Door Khadi Sharmaaye is available on YouTube.\r\nThis show will be performed in English.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Prashasti Singh: Divine Feminine","instanceDates":"15 December-20 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"653603AGSHRDSPBKPTRNDCNPVTKGHKQCQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-15T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-15T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-20T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-20T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Ahead of her Edinburgh Fringe debut, Prashasti previews at Soho to question all her life choices.\r\nGrowing up in a patriarchal family, Prashasti naturally had only one dream – to become a patriarch herself. Inching towards 40, but pretending to be 30, Prashasti can finally mark this dream complete. But instead of happiness, she finds herself pondering if the ascent was even worth the price. In her brand new stand-up show, Prashasti questions all her life choices and meticulously assigns blame to the women and men who shaped her into this being.\r\nPrashasti Singh is a stand-up comic and writer from India. She can be seen on Netflix’s Ladies Up, Comedy Premium League and Amazon Prime Video’s Comicstaan. She has been touring internationally with her last show Man of the House. Her stand-up special Door Khadi Sharmaaye is available on YouTube.\r\nThis show will be performed in English.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Prashasti Singh: Divine Feminine – Preview","instanceDates":"23 July-26 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"631403ACGBQHVBQKKTPKJJPNHKMVGGJGN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-23T21:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-23T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-26T21:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-26T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Prashasti makes her Soho Theatre debut with a brand new stand-up show questioning her life choices.\r\nGrowing up in a patriarchal family, Prashasti naturally had only one dream - to become a patriarch herself. Inching towards 40, but pretending to be 30, Prashasti can finally mark this dream complete. But instead of happiness, she finds herself pondering if the ascent was even worth the price? In her brand new stand-up show, Prashasti questions all her life choices and meticulously assigns blame to the women and men who shaped her into this being.\r\nPrashasti Singh is a stand-up comic and writer from India. She can be seen on Netflix’s Ladies Up, Comedy Premium League and Amazon Prime Video’s Comicstaan. She has been touring internationally with her last show Man of the House. Her stand-up special Door Khadi Sharmaaye is available on YouTube.\r\n\r\nThis show will be performed in English and Hindi.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Prashasti Singh: Divine Feminine.","instanceDates":"16 December-21 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"576603AHRPLHNCJDRPPKGLGNMBBMKQLKG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-16T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-16T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-21T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-21T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Treat yourself to a pre-ordered drink, ready for you at your table when you arrive.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\tTreat yourself to a pre-ordered drink, ready for you at your table when you arrive.\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Pre Order Drinks Downstairs","instanceDates":"17 May-11 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"315805AJPQLVSBHKRQMRVQDGMMNGPTGDJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2021-05-17T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2021-05-17T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-08-11T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-08-11T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\tTreat yourself to a pre ordered drink, to collect at our Terrace Bar on your way in to the show. \r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Pre Order Drinks Main House","instanceDates":"26 July-19 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"405803ATCTSQBTBPQTMMDPNGPDKGNTSJT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2022-07-26T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2022-07-26T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-06-19T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-06-19T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Pre Order Menu for PR Has Talent","instanceDates":"17 November-17 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"751603APJCBMJJSBBMVTPDBPTNJHPKCBN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-17T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-17T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-17T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-17T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\t<img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/sohotheatre/files/015667a3-5779-459f-aacd-0000e2d2bcad.jpg\" /><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Pre order yourself pizza, from our delicious selection below, to have it sizzling hot for you on arrival.\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/sohotheatre/files/015667a3-5779-459f-aacd-0000e2d2bcad.jpg","isOnSale":true,"name":"Pre Order: Pizza","instanceDates":"20 February-28 October","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/sohotheatre/files/015667a3-5779-459f-aacd-0000e2d2bcad-thumbnail.jpg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"681403ABJRSHVHPNQNTGTGMRKSCKDVKBC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-20T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-20T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-10-28T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-10-28T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\t<span class=\"BoldText\">Book a Pre Show Tour of Soho Theatre Walthamstow</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Discover the history of the Soho Theatre Walthamstow building from its origins as a 1930s Spanish baroque cine-variety, then a swinging 60s music venue, a much loved local cinema to a brand new home for London’s most vibrant producer of new theatre, comedy and cabaret. Start time: 5.15pm.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span> <img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/sohotheatre/files/3a9eae31-bf2f-4f75-ab66-4a5fc5c33a7d.jpg\" /> \r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/sohotheatre/files/3a9eae31-bf2f-4f75-ab66-4a5fc5c33a7d.jpg","isOnSale":true,"name":"Pre Show Tour of Soho Theatre Walthamstow","instanceDates":"28 September-13 January","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/sohotheatre/files/3a9eae31-bf2f-4f75-ab66-4a5fc5c33a7d-thumbnail.jpg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"660804AHQHPJGVPRQHQBRGKDRRBLGNVPN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-28T17:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-28T16:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-13T17:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-13T17:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Treat yourself to a pre-ordered drink, ready for you at your table when you arrive. ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Pre-Order Drinks","instanceDates":"11 December-19 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"307203ABMVSNKPCGDSDNLJLVJMBCLPHGP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2020-12-11T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2020-12-11T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2020-12-19T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2020-12-19T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Pre-order drinks: Karaoke Kabaret","instanceDates":"27 February-27 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"583803AGGGQBNHMPDRKMMJVVQRVBJGLQM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-27T21:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-27T21:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-27T21:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-27T21:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Pride Booths 24","instanceDates":"29 June-29 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"558803ACPKKRVCTCBVKCKTQGPNQJMTJHM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-29T14:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-29T13:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-29T14:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-29T13:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Description / copy\r\n\tDodge the crowds and the queueing and come base yourself at Soho Theatre Bar for the day.\r\nThis year, you can book one of our Soho Theatre Bar booths for you and five mates and base yourself with us from midday. We’ll throw in a bottle of prosecco and some of our Soho Theatre Neon lager to get your day off to a good start. You’ll also get a VIP wristband so you can come and go as you want* through the rest of the day, so no need to worry about getting in somewhere. \r\nBooths cost £150 for 6 people, include one bottle of prosecco (that’s six glasses) and six cans of Neon lager and VIP wristband entry. \r\nThere’ll be DJs, banging tunes, drinks, glitter and mirror balls and the hottest pride crowd (that’s you). We’re year-round punk and queer but Pride is really when we let our hair down and party. So be who you are, wear what you want, come with Pride and bring your dancing shoes. \r\n\r\n*It’s a very busy day so we suggest you don’t leave any valuables at your table.\r\n\r\n18+ for purchases","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":720,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Pride Party Booths at Soho Theatre Bar","instanceDates":"1 July-1 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"481003ABTMPSCVNGVNRRJJSTPCRPLLBVH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-01T12:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-01T11:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-01T12:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-01T11:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"LGBTQ+","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Drag","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Bar","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join James for an hour of pure nostalgia, stepping back in time with some joyous singalong tunes to take you back to your Primary School days. You won't have to sit cross-legged on the school hall floor, but you will be encouraged to sing along! As well as the assembly bangers, there will be other musical surprises, throwback mashups and comic reflections on growing up in the 90s. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Primary School Bangers","instanceDates":"28 April-3 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"606404ARQMLBHSPLTDJNLTJKJKGPVMGDD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-28T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-28T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-03T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-03T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Private View by Jess Edwards","instanceDates":"27 November-20 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"638603ABTGCDGDVDPHBVQSPPMQQBHBQTL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-27T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-27T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-20T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-20T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Priya Hall is obsessed with her nan to an unhealthy degree.\r\nHer debut show Grandmother’s Daughter is a joyful tribute to one old Welsh lady and the impossible standards Priya has to live up to as she prepares to become a matriarch of her own family. Packed with a level of oversharing that borders on the unhinged, this show promises a healthy dose of queer joy, storytelling and more jokes about sperm than Priya intended. As seen on BBC One, BBC Three, Comedy Central, BBC Radio 4 and more.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Priya Hall: Grandmother’s Daughter","instanceDates":"29 January-31 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"501003AKJVLGVHGNGQRLRKJHPPSJVSSLT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-29T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-29T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-31T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-31T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"LGBTQ+","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"India/South Asian heritage"},{"description":"The 7-foot sad clown with the golden voice deftly combines melancholy with the absurd to create an intoxicating comedy experience.\r\nPuddles’ one-of-a-kind “textured voice laced with melancholy” (NY Times) has been hailed as “operatic” (Boston Globe) and his show both “life-affirming” (Herald, Scotland) and “hysterically funny” (LA Weekly).\r\n\r\nPuddles Pity Party has amassed almost a million YouTube subscribers and has sold out shows all over the world, including The Kennedy Center in Washington DC, San Francisco’s Palace of Fine Arts and a residency at Caesars Palace in Las Vegas.\r\n\r\nPuddles’ cover of “All the Small Things” recorded with Postmodern Jukebox was featured in the 2022 John Lewis Christmas advert. He was a quarter finalist on Season 12 of America’s Got Talent and appeared on the 2020 season of AGT The Champions.\r\n\r\nIn 2022, he performed a duet with the iconic Eric Idle in Homeward Bound: A Grammy Salute to the Songs of Paul Simon filmed for CBS and was a surprise guest on the Season 4 finale of ABC’s The Conners. Puddles has received endorsements and accolades from musical comedy legends including Jack Black, Michael McKean, Weird Al Yankovic, Drew Carey, Nick Offerman and Paul Reubens.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Puddles Pity Party","instanceDates":"11 March-18 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"520203AGQGNMJCKVGHHMNGQKKGPSKKDTT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-11T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-11T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-18T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-18T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"by Jessica L. Hagan and Ryan Calais Cameron\r\n\r\nTurned away from a nightclub for being “too black”, four women take to the stage with their own explosive true stories: the music and the misogyny, the dancing and the drinking, the women and, of course, the (white) men. \r\n\r\nLoosely based on the DSTRKT nightspot incident of 2015, Queens of Sheba tells the hilarious, moving and uplifting stories of four passionate Black Women battling every-day misogynoir; where sexism meets racism. \r\n\r\nFollowing a sell-out runs at Soho Theatre in 2021 and 2023 and prior to its USA tour, Queens of Sheba returns one week only this December.\r\n\r\nWinner! 2020 OFF WEST END AWARDS Best Performance Piece\r\n\r\nWinner! 2018 Edinburgh Untapped Award \r\n\r\nWinner! 2018 The Stage Edinburgh Festival Award \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Queens of Sheba","instanceDates":"18 December-23 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"507203AGKMPHNLLSSLLMVRLRRHQTJRQPT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-18T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-18T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-23T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-23T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Feminist","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Rachel Galvo is an incredibly shite feminist... but it’s not her fault.\r\nShe spent 15 years locked up in an all-girls Irish catholic school run by nuns- and she’s ready to tell the truth... \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rachel Galvo: The Shite Feminist","instanceDates":"23 April-25 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"693603ANLNHQHKBVCMCCSMPTQCHJBDRJG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-23T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-23T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-25T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-25T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Rachel Galvo is an incredibly shite feminist... but it’s not her fault.\r\nShe spent 15 years locked up in an all-girls Irish catholic school run by nuns- and she’s ready to tell the truth... 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rachel Galvo: The Shite Feminist.","instanceDates":"15 January-17 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"658603AGBDTDQHPMTVCKRRLRSHCMJBCTL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-15T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-15T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-17T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-17T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Rachel Kaly got her first period the same day Saddam Hussein was hanged.\r\nShe has also been to hospital over 300 times for various psychological treatments. Are these two facts related? Probably. \r\n\r\nRachel’s brings Chortle’s #2 Best Comedy Show of 2024 to London for the first time, to perfectly explain why she is so mentally ill.\r\n\r\nSupport for Joe Pera, Conner O'Malley and Chris Fleming.\r\n\r\nAs seen on Late Night with Seth Meyers, HBO and Comedy Central.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rachel Kaly: Hospital Hour","instanceDates":"26 August-30 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"639003AGCGGSNQBNMCJQMVVNCPNPBLTGC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-26T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-26T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-30T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-30T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rahul Dua: Allow Me – Attenborough Arts Centre, Leicester","instanceDates":"4 September-4 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"646203ADLJLCJDCRTKKGQLMBHTGVNHNPK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-04T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-04T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-04T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-04T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Attenborough Arts Centre, Leicester","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rahul Dua: Allow Me – Glasgow Glee","instanceDates":"3 September-3 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"646003ANKTBCNDVKDQHTSMQDJJSLMPHQH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-03T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-03T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-03T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-03T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Glasgow Glee","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"One of India’s topmost stand-comedians, Dua carries a lot of weight on his head. \r\n\r\nThat’s because there are way too many feathers in his cap. Actor, writer, comedian, creator, host of Comicstaan Season 3 Finale, host of SharkTank Season 2. \r\n\r\nIn fact, having toured over 10 countries, sold over 45,000 tickets, worked with over a hundred brands, and with a community of over 690k on IG and over a million on YT, there are very few things that Rahul hasn’t dipped his toe into.\r\nBoasting one of the biggest stand-up tours in India, selling over 30,000 tickets and encompassing over 40 cities, join one of the finest comedians around for his biggest UK show yet. \r\nPlease note this show will be performed in Hindi.\r\n\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rahul Dua: Live","instanceDates":"6 September-6 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"581403AQSRVJKBSMKNPSQPHPHVKKGDRDC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-06T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-06T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-06T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-06T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"India/South Asian heritage"},{"description":"One of India’s topmost stand-comedians, Dua carries a lot of weight on his head. That’s because there are way too many feathers in his cap. Actor, writer, comedian, creator, host of Comicstaan Season 3 Finale, host of SharkTank Season 2. In fact, having toured over 10 countries, sold over 45,000 tickets, worked with over a hundred brands, and with a community of over 690k on IG and over a million on YT, there are very few things that Rahul hasn’t dipped his toe into. Boasting one of the biggest stand-up tours in India, selling over 30,000 tickets and encompassing over 40 cities, join one of the finest comedians around for his biggest UK show yet. Please note this show will be performed in Hindi. 14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rahul Dua: Live - Birmingham Glee Club","instanceDates":"5 September-5 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"585403AHKTNJTHRTJBBBKJSRCJKSRPQJT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-05T18:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-05T17:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-05T18:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-05T17:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up","attribute_Venue":""},{"description":"After touring his stand-up comedy show “Who Are You?” for over two years and earning a nomination for Best Show at the Melbourne International Comedy Festival 2025, Rahul is back on the road with a brand new stand-up comedy show. Performed in Hinglish, this show features fresh jokes, new stories, and the same old Rahul - observant, self-aware, and intelligently silly.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rahul Subramanian Live (New Hinglish Show)","instanceDates":"5 July-5 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"698603AHBDDSLNMSHJJVGSKQTGRPLVHRR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-05T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-05T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-05T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-05T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Mumbai-based global stand-up star Rahul Subramanian comes to Soho Theatre. \r\nAfter the success of two hit stand-up shows, including releasing India's first crowd work special Rahul Talks To People, you'd think Rahul would be pretty confident in who he is as a person. Not the case. Join him in figuring it all out in Who Are You? (Disclaimer: this show will not help anyone struggling to figure out who they are, but it will be very funny.)\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rahul Subramanian: Who Are You?","instanceDates":"23 July-27 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"548403AJSPLSKHDPNDPGVGBDVGJJCQKQS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-23T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-23T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-27T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-27T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Rising star Rajiv Karia wants to be your friend. You really should support your friends, especially when they are bringing their highly anticipated & critically acclaimed debut hour to Soho Theatre. As seen on Lazy Susan (BBC Three) and Comedy Central Live. Speaking gently and joking hard. Writer for Have I Got News For You and The Now Show. Tour Support for Olga Koch & Colin Hoult. 'Excellent new talent... simply a great joke writer' ★★★★ The Skinny 'His carefully crafted material and flawless delivery make him one to watch. ' ★★★★★ WhyNow 'Dry wit akin to Jack Dee or Romesh Ranganathan' (VoiceMag).\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rajiv Karia: Gallivant","instanceDates":"1 June-3 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"457803AKRNDQQLRGKJVPRNMJQCSSMBVSK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-01T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-01T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-03T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-03T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join Ralph Barbosa as he takes a break in his US tour to play his first ever UK dates.\r\nOne of the shyest attention hogs to ever do comedy, Ralph Barbosa’s disarming and laid-back style has made him a stand-out on stage, on TV and online, including as host of the Formula Bean YouTube channel with Luis Cisneros.\r\nSince winning the Funniest Comic in Texas competition back in 2019, Ralph has since built himself a devoted online fanbase with over 4 million followers on social media, with his stand-up clips frequently reaching millions of views on TikTok. His Comedy Central and Don’t Tell Comedy performances have collectively garnered over 14 million views on YouTube. He has also appeared on HBO and The Tonight Show and recently guest starred on the Netflix series Mo, as well as releasing his own Netflix special “Ralph Barbosa: Cowabunga” in 2019.\r\nRalph’s current comedy tour is selling out theatres across North America.\r\n18+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ralph Barbosa: The Red 40 Tour","instanceDates":"6 July-11 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"705003ASBHDCLPHCMNBPVQKHHDQPLHKHP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-06T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-06T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-11T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-11T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Part of National Theatre Connections\r\nA rag tag group of self-described ‘neeks’ gather at midnight in a local park, to hold a ‘dry rave’. Will they succeed in redefining ‘cool’? Or will the powers that be succeed in shutting down the neek revolution?\r\nRAVERS is written by Rikki Beadle-Blair MBE for National Theatre Connections 2025 and performed by students from Leyton Sixth Form College. \r\nNT Connections is running for its 30th year and we’re both proud and excited to continue supporting this amazing project in our new home Soho Theatre Walthamstow. \r\n12+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"RAVERS – Written by Rikki Beadle-Blair, performed by LSC Expressive Arts","instanceDates":"12 May-12 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"601603AMBGMCRVHMVMPTNBGQMDMDQKQHJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-12T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-12T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-12T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-12T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"1 in 6 adults in the UK will lose their hearing in their lifetime; two of those are Ray Bradshaw’s parents.\r\nThe multi award winning comedian is back on tour with a brand-new show all about growing up as a CODA; A Child of Deaf Adults. His upbringing was nothing like the Oscar winning film and he’s here to tell you why.\r\nCODA is a funny, heartwarming show all about the brilliant things that happen when you grow up in a house where sign language is the first language used; whether it’s watching his dad shut his eyes to win any argument or beating his in-laws easily when they suggested playing charades against a deaf family on Christmas Day.\r\nRay’s previous shows Deaf Com One and Doppelginger were huge successes and sold-out theatres across the world. As this show is all about growing up with deaf parents every show of CODA will have a BSL interpreter. Ray has previously supported John Bishop on his UK arena tour after John described him as ‘one of the best comedians in the country’.\r\n\r\nPlease note all performances will be BSL-interpreted.\r\n[Can we make this nice and noticeable please!]\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ray Bradshaw: CODA","instanceDates":"27 April-29 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"692403AVQTRSSHLSRPHBPSNQVBQMTVSDV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-27T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-27T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-29T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-29T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Access","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Ray O’ Leary recently pulled a man from a wrecked car and as the man lay dying, he used his last ounce of strength asking Ray - Best Show Nominee at the 2024 Melbourne International Comedy Festival, 'Taskmaster New Zealand' star - to tell his children that he loved them. \r\nRay promised the man he would. \r\nBut first, he has his new tour to think about. \r\nLaughter? I Hardly Know Her played to huge audiences at the 2025 Melbourne and Edinburgh Festivals, and this burgeoning comedy legend is excited to bring his iconic two-piece suit back to London. \r\nAnd when that’s out of the way, he can get back to passing on the message.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ray O’Leary: Laughter? I Hardly Know Her","instanceDates":"9 March-11 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"648003AGCMQLRPPDKSKCVQJSHSVJHBGBL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-09T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-09T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-11T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-11T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The deadpan Ray O’Leary (Taskmaster NZ) is a big brain in an ill-fitting suit.\r\nEvery time he does stand-up and people laugh, he gets stronger. Soon he will be the most powerful man in the universe. When the show ends, he’ll be able to lift a car above his head.\r\n \r\nFresh from a sold-out Edinburgh Fringe Festival run, the Best Show Nomination at the Melbourne International Comedy Festival and 3x nominee for Best Male Comedian by the NZ Comedy Guild. Ray is a staple on Australasian television including Have You Been Paying Attention?, Thank God You’re Here, and 7 Days.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ray O’Leary: Your Laughter Is Just Making Me Stronger","instanceDates":"4 February-8 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"574803AMBTQRBCKDBHCGTJLJJBKHQVVLL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-04T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-04T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-08T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-08T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Skins star Megan Prescott’s debut solo returns to Soho Theatre, following a sold-out run at Soho Rising Festival and an award-winning ★★★★★ run at Edinburgh Fringe Festival.\r\nMolly was a child star, now she’s considering getting into porn.\r\nWhat would you do if your acting career peaked in 2009 (well before the Me Too movement) and you hadn't booked another role in years? Exposed for working as a stripper, dumped by her agent, and shunned by the public, Molly's giving mainstream success one last shot.\r\nEnter a world of child stars, strip clubs, and casting couches - and question what it means to earn a living as a performer.\r\nMegan Prescott  – aka Katie F*cking Fitch - is an actor, writer and director who starred in the Channel 4 drama Skins. Megan was part of the Soho Writers Lab in 2020 and brought her debut solo show Really Good Exposure to Edinburgh Festival Fringe in 2024, where she was nominated for the BBC’s Popcorn Writing Award and won Theatre Weekly’s Best Fringe Debut award.\r\n18+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Really Good Exposure by Megan Prescott","instanceDates":"2 September-13 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"634403ARSMBTHPNCLNSNNGKNDLCQSBCBV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-02T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-02T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-13T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-13T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Skins star Megan Prescott’s debut solo show comes to London, fresh from an award-winning ★★★★★ run at Edinburgh Fringe Festival.\r\nMolly was a child star, now she’s considering getting into porn.\r\n\r\nWhat would you do if your acting career peaked in 2009 (well before the Me Too movement) and you hadn't booked another role in years? Exposed for working as a stripper, dumped by her agent, and shunned by the public, Molly's giving mainstream success one last shot.\r\n\r\nEnter a world of child stars, strip clubs, and casting couches - and question what it means to earn a living as a performer.\r\n\r\nMegan Prescott  – aka Katie F*cking Fitch - is an actor, writer and director who starred in the Channel 4 drama Skins. Megan was part of the Soho Writers Lab in 2020 and brought her debut solo show Really Good Exposure to Edinburgh Festival Fringe in 2024, where she was nominated for the BBC’s Popcorn Writing Award and won Theatre Weekly’s Best Fringe Debut award. 16+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Really Good Exposure by Megan Prescott.","instanceDates":"17 February-18 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"590404APJTBGSNMRNSMDRJKKVMHKVQLMB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-17T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-17T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-18T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-18T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"RRP £22 ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Reece Shearsmith Book add-on","instanceDates":"18 October-18 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"732203ADQCRPCMSDKSLPQDNBMGTJGHNHQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-18T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-18T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-18T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-18T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"“The most influential absurdist in comedy today” (New York Times) and star of The Late Late Show comes to Soho Theatre Walthamstow.\r\nReggie Watts is an internationally renowned musician/comedian/writer/actor who most recently starred as the bandleader on CBS’s The Late Late Show with James Corden. \r\nUsing his formidable voice, looping pedals, and his vast imagination, Watts blends and blurs the lines between music and comedy, wowing audiences with performances that are 100% improvised. \r\n \r\nWatts’ first Netflix special Spatial released to massive critical acclaim, with the New York Times calling it “a giddy rush of escapist nonsense” and dubbing Watts “the most influential absurdist in comedy today.” The A.V. Club described Spatial as “signature Watts, meaning it’s alternately exhilarating, silly, exhausting and transcendent,” and Exclaim! Magazine called his performance “engaging, absurd, thoughtful and, most importantly, wholly unpredictable.”\r\nReggie’s recently released special, Never Mind, was included on Vulture’s 3 New Comedy Specials You Should Definitely Watch (When You Have a Moment) and praised in the LA Times. It is now available to stream on the new Veeps streaming platform. His memoir, Great Falls, MT was recently released by Penguin’s highly curated Tiny Reparations imprint, founded by Phoebe Robinson.\r\nAs a solo performer, Watts brand of musical/comedy fusion has led to sold out headlining tours in the U.S. and Europe, including festivals such as Bonnaroo, SXSW, Bumbershoot, Just For Laughs, Pemberton and more.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Reggie Watts: Live At Soho Theatre Walthamstow","instanceDates":"1 August-2 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"613603ASQSVSRPPDVGCPQJGNQNLKPMMMR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-01T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-01T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-02T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-02T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"After spending three years in prison for shoplifting Aisha decides to transform her life and go on a self healing journey.\r\nHer plans are derailed when she meets V - a wealthy young woman who she falls deeply infatuated with. \r\nAisha soon comes to the logical conclusion that stealing material items is simply not enough -  true healing will come when she steals this rich lady’s  life! \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Reparations by Maryam Garad","instanceDates":"9 February-12 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"523403ANMCRCBRHQMJTDTGHJBRBPMPNDV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-09T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-09T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-12T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-12T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Reuben Kaye is back. Sharper, sexier, and more political than ever.\r\nReuben Kaye is back. Sharper, sexier, and more political than ever. Expect glitter, guts, and the kind of biting comedy only Kaye can deliver.  \r\n\r\nSydney Comedy Festival 2026 | Best of the Fest Winner  \r\n\r\nMelbourne Comedy Festival 2026 | Most Outstanding Show Nominee \r\n\r\nGreen Room Award 2026 & 2025 | Best Cabaret Artist | Nominee \r\n\r\nEdinburgh Comedy Awards 2024 | Best Show Nominee  \r\n\r\nAdelaide Cabaret Festival 2024 | Cabaret Icon Award ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Reuben Kaye: Hard to Swallow","instanceDates":"10 September-10 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"731403ANGGGRNGCPTBNQKSNNHTKHNVHVT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-10T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-10T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-10T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-10T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"LGBTQ+","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Reuben Kaye and his band are back with his award-nominated show Live and Intimidating!\r\nThe obscenely intelligent, rib-crackingly funny Reuben Kaye returns to Soho Theatre in an explosion of high camp and filthy humour. With musical direction by Shanon Whitelock and original compositions, this Swarovski-studded revolt is what happens when you tell your children they can be anything. \r\n\r\nWINNER Cabaret Icon Award – Adelaide Cabaret Festival 2024\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Reuben Kaye: Live & Intimidating","instanceDates":"10 September-21 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"560803ASHNHGGHSKVBSNPGDMBQJVVDKCV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-10T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-10T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-21T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-21T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"LGBTQ+","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Through madcap comedy and biting satire, this explosive tale blows the roof off what it means to be Jewish in the UK.\r\n2019. Jewish Essex. One funeral. Two twins. And an 80-year-old ex-gangster with a plan that’s absolutely meshugge.\r\nMalcolm Spivak’s had enough. He corners twins Dan and Lauren, fresh from their grandfather's funeral, with a proposition: help him kidnap Jeremy Corbyn. Yes, really. What follows is a chaotic Jewish heist comedy that blends madcap comedy and biting political satire.\r\nFollowing multiple sell-out runs (The Yard Theatre, 2025; Summerhall, Edinburgh Fringe 2024), this explosive ★★★★★ show written by Nick Cassenbaum (Fringe First winner and Popcorn Writer's Award nominee) and directed by Emma Jude Harris (The Stage's Fringe Five 2024) comes to the Soho Theatre for a six week caper through the festive season. \r\nREVENGE: After the Levoyah tears through antisemitism in the diaspora, the dangers of collective hysteria, and how far you can throw a jar of chraine from a moving vehicle.\r\nDiehard Schmiehard. We’ve got pickles.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":65,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Revenge: After The Levoyah","instanceDates":"8 December-24 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"638203AMPNBMSBTGTQGJDTSPCHDMSCBLS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-08T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-08T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-24T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-24T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Comedy"},{"description":"Through madcap comedy and biting satire, this explosive tale blows the roof off what it means to be Jewish in the UK.\r\nNick Cassenbaum’s two-hander comedy heist, directed by Emma Jude Harris, romps through 2018 Jewish Essex. Through madcap comedy and biting satire, this explosive tale blows the roof off what it means to be Jewish in the UK. \r\n\r\nTwins Dan and Lauren meet ex-gangster Malcolm Spivak at their grandfather's funeral. Malcolm, who's 'had enough', enlists the siblings in a ragtag Yiddishe plot to kidnap then-Labour leader Jeremy Corbyn. \r\n\r\nREVENGE: After the Lavoyah examines antisemitism in the diaspora, the dangers of collective hysteria, and how far a nonagenarian can throw a jar of chraine from a moving vehicle.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"REVENGE: After The Levoyah Jul24","instanceDates":"15 July-17 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"556003AMRTTDKSDMVRCCTBMDJGHQTKJQN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-15T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-15T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-17T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-17T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"Inspired by the legendary Beatles album released in 1966, REVOLVER weaves together the lives of three women across generations in a shattering story of love, obsession and violence. \r\n\r\n  \r\n\r\nIn 2026, a TV researcher has her dream job; in 1966, a teenage Beatles fan writes to John Lennon; and in New York, Valerie Solanas tries to get her script produced by Andy Warhol as his celebrity star is on the rise. \r\n\r\n  \r\n\r\nTold in Woof’s compelling, rich and wryly funny voice, REVOLVER brings to vivid life a time of revolutionary change and protest. As The Beatles tour to America for the first time, John Lennon declares the band is as popular as Jesus, and everything shifts from liberated swing to drug-induced chaos, as people’s minds expand with pacifism and radical feminism…\r\n\r\nDescriptions of sexually explicit material and violence \r\n\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"REVOLVER ","instanceDates":"24 November-5 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"746403AHHDBHPTJLBCBGHJBHPPGTGBDLQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-24T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-24T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-05T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-05T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"New Writing","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"1966. Hope. Innocence. Action. Rage. \r\n\r\nInspired by the legendary Beatles album released in 1966, REVOLVER weaves together the lives of three women across the generations in a shattering story of love, obsession and violence. In 2025, a TV researcher has her dream job; in 1966, a teenage Beatles fan writes to John Lennon; and in New York, Valerie Solanas recruits for The Society For Cutting Up Men.\r\n \r\nTold in Woof’s compelling, rich and wryly funny voice, REVOLVER brings to vivid life a time of revolutionary change and protest. As The Beatles tour to America for the first time, John Lennon declares the band is as popular as Jesus, and everything shifts from liberated swing to drug-induced chaos, as people's minds explode with pacifism and radical feminism…. \r\n14+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"REVOLVER (2025)","instanceDates":"8 August-9 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"650603AJLPVJMQKTMSKDVMSPQBBMKHHPP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-08T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-08T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-09T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-09T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Dance","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"A fast, forensic show of big ideas and gag-dense overthinking from one of the nation’s sharpest stand-ups.\r\nRhys has made a discovery that could fix everything. It’s been staring him in the face the whole time, in a mirror held behind his head. If he can ignore his own problems for long enough, he might just be able to solve yours. \r\nStar of TLC’s Mock The Week and BBC Radio 4's Rhysearch, also seen furrowing his brow on QI, Live At The Apollo and his viral U&Dave lecture, 'I Stalk Strangers Online'.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rhys James: Chop Logic","instanceDates":"13 March-13 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"703803ADPQSVBKRBHSCVRCPJQNBBQCDBV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-03-13T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-03-13T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-03-13T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-03-13T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The United Kingdom? \r\nIs that you? \r\nIt's me Rhys, from comedy. How about a nice little hour where we pretend the last couple years haven’t happened, yeah? That sounds nice doesn’t it? \r\nYeah. A nice little comedy show with your ol’ pal Rhys. \r\nLovely.\r\n\r\n\r\n“The Comedy Festival Show with the highest number of laughs per\r\nminute…Nicolson is an absolute master of the form” ★★★★★ TimeOut\r\n15+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rhys Nicholson: Rhys, Rhys, Rhys","instanceDates":"27 June-1 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"436403ABLMCVLNTGPNBGHVQMHMDSJRBTN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-27T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-27T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-01T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-01T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"In the aftermath of a global pandemic, comedian and scientist, Ria Lina sees the world differently. In this work in progress show Ria tackles the issues of coming out of a global pandemic, the new normal, divorce, dating in a new digital world, motherhood and what it really means to be a woman today.\r\n\r\nFearless, provocative, and very funny, Ria Lina is the only Filipina comedian in British stand-up and a hugely admired talent in the comedy industry. \r\n\r\nHer extensive list of credits includes Live At The Apollo, Have I Got News For You, Mock the Week, Lovestruck High, Richard Hammond’s Brain Reaction, House of Games, The Last Leg and Celebrity Mastermind.\r\n\r\n ★★★★ “I guarantee you will laugh a lot.” - THE SCOTSMAN\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ria Lina: Work in Progress","instanceDates":"8 August-10 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"479204AMGHLSPMPBMQTGDKBBCNTMPKDDK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-08T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-08T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-10T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-10T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Work In Progress","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Ever wonder how batshit crazy you have to be to run for President of the United States?\r\nRich Fulcher (The Mighty Boosh) not only explains why….but why not? With up-to-date analysis of the 2024 election and all the low-lights and hijinx of the current candidates.  Rich guarantees he won’t freeze [note: if you don’t get that joke, go see a puppet show]. Not suitable for pre-teens or diabetic wolves. Work In Progress.  \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rich Fulcher’s U.S. Election Show (Work in Progress)","instanceDates":"28 October-28 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"498403ATGMRGMJLTJGVQTMSJJJMBLKMDM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-28T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-28T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-28T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-28T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"In his intimate and highly anticipated debut hour, Rich Hardisty (C4, NETFLIX, BBC) takes us on a journey through the highs and lows of his unusual life. Expect anecdotes and observations about momentous movies, missing dads and mania, all from his warm, inquisitive, childlike perspective. Rich tries to convey what mental illness looks and feels like, celebrating the beauty and silliness of it all. He shows us the interesting, hilarious and sometimes shocking things his brain is capable of doing (whether he wants it to or not). Raw, open and honest but most importantly... FUNNY!\r\n\r\n\"A thrilling life story, brilliantly told\" - Richard Gadd\r\n\r\n\"Much more than funny... but also very funny\" - Simon Amstell\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":67,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rich Hardisty: Silly Boy","instanceDates":"9 May-10 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"446803ACLMNLMKSKTPJJPPVPRGNHMHKCT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-09T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-09T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-10T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-10T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Storytelling","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join BAFTA-winning actor, comedian, director, and writer Richard Ayoade for an evening of reflections as he shares insights from his latest book Afterthoughts, or Some Pistachios Won’t Open: Wisdom for the Unreflective.\r\nPartially recognisable for being in The IT Crowd, his acclaimed films Submarine and The Double, he has also hosted TV landfill like Travel Man and The Crystal Maze, and lent his nasal voice to The Boxtrolls, Early Man, Soul and The Bad Guys.\r\nBut you may well know him best for his role as ‘photographer’ in The Life and Death of Peter Sellers in which he delivered the iconic line: ‘Please, Mer Sellers, can I get a shot of you and your mum?’\r\nNow, in the midst of some self-inflicted financial difficulty, he turns to the stage, inviting you to explore over 500 of his colossal notions. Thoughts like...\r\n‘Where’s the box to tick if you ARE a robot’\r\n‘If, when one door shuts, another door opens, there's something wrong with your doors. They shouldn't be doing that.’\r\n‘TV detectives need a gimmick. Mine would be not caring who did it.’\r\nAfterthoughts goes beyond rumination, past pondering, probing further than ever before. Drawing from a deeply private pool of questions—a reservoir so refreshing you may never need to think again.\r\n14+ at parent/guardian discretion","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Richard Ayoade: Afterthoughts ","instanceDates":"27 June-27 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"705603AVQKCVMHDVHCQCNPGNGVPPVKVPS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-27T14:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-27T13:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-27T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-27T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rick Glassman: Me and My Puppet Rick","instanceDates":"24 August-29 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"723803ANTRHMRPGKBTJSBQCDKSDVDPVHM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-24T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-24T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-29T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-29T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join NYC-based stand-up comedian Ricky Sim for the first London debut of his critically acclaimed show, ‘Coming Out to Dead People.’ \r\nCombining stand-up and storytelling, this autobiographical solo show explores the time when Ricky was grappling with the decision to come out to his Chinese-Malaysian immigrant mother, just as she was diagnosed with terminal cancer - talk about good timing! \r\n\r\n“The comic delivers an intimate performance, so heartfelt and sincere it barely feels like a show at all, building to an emotional final scene that packs a punch.” – Steve Bennett, Chortle\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ricky Sim: Coming Out to Dead People (An Asian Queer Story)","instanceDates":"22 January-24 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"511803AVJKVMBMLBNCRKSRNLHBPHJTLQP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-22T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-22T21:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-24T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-24T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"LGBTQ+","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"From Stan Zimmerman (writer of Golden Girls and Gilmore Girls), Right Before I Go highlights the raw struggles and lives of people impacted by suicide. \r\nDrawing on real suicide notes and personal testimonies, the play gives voice to individuals from a wide range of backgrounds including public figures, veterans, young people, members of the LGBTQ+ community, and people living with mental health challenges. \r\nFeaturing a rotating cast of all-stars (to be confirmed). \r\nThis show is followed by a conversation between cast and audience.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Right Before I Go","instanceDates":"5 September-10 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"744003ASLQTVKKVMVSMRCDCVRRCVDCSQV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-05T14:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-05T13:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-10T14:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-10T13:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Riki Lindhome: Dead Inside","instanceDates":"31 March-18 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"703203ABPSGTGLHQNCGVDLKCNMCCGVHCP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-31T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-31T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-18T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-18T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"It’s 2025 and King Herod is leading a self-development pyramid scheme. You remember Herod, the biblical despot and enemy of Jesus? That’s right: he’s done the work, he’s reached inside and by God, he’s got a wellness program to show for it. Expect frivolity, shock and redemption in a process which asks the big questions: Who can we really trust? What are eggs? Why are you crying? In a post-truth world punctuated by conspiracy, division and collapse, it’s time to forgive...yourself.\r\nHealing King Herod reached critical acclaim at its Underbelly run in Edinburgh, following its preview at Soho Theatre and sell out run at VAULT Festival 2023. It was nominated Show of the Week and the recipient of Phoebe Waller Bridge’s Keep it Fringe fund. \r\nThe world has changed a lot since 2023. Join Herod in a revamped hour of transformation. Created by Comedy Central-endorsed clown Riss Obolensky and director Eloïse Poulton.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"RISS OBOLENSKY: HEALING KING HEROD","instanceDates":"28 March-29 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"612403AQPKCSQJJNPRQTHSNRHPJGSCDDS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-28T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-28T22:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-29T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-29T22:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"LGBTQ+","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Multi award-winning writer, performer and actor Rob Auton presents his debut narrative show.\r\nHaving written 11 critically acclaimed shows on specific themes, Rob is now keen on telling you a story he has written about a man he made up called CAN. \r\nAt one point in his life CAN was the world's number one motivational speaker... and then something happened. \r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rob Auton: CAN (An Hour-Long Story)","instanceDates":"19 January-30 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"649403AHGGSTQVNQBNMJSNQJJSMBQVTNT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-19T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-19T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-30T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-30T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"This show is a story about a time when Rob Auton had a job as an estate agent on the planet Jupiter. It is fiction.\r\nFollowing the success of his sell-out 2025-26 nationwide tour, multi-award-winning writer, performer, podcaster and actor Rob Auton is returning to stages across the UK in 2027 with his thirteenth hour JUPITER.\r\nOn screen Rob has appeared opposite Danny Dyer in Marching Powder, in Channel 4's hit comedy The Change, and in BBC's Starstruck, with further credits including Miracle Workers (TBS), The End of the F**ing World (Netflix/Channel 4), The Russell Howard Hour (Sky), Cold Feet (ITV) and Random Acts (Channel 4). His viral stand-up appearance on Stand-Up Central with Rob Delaney (Comedy Central) Alongside his screen work, Rob is a two-time British Podcast Awards Gold winner for The Rob Auton Daily Podcast.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rob Auton: Jupiter","instanceDates":"17 May-29 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"741403ACHCBKKLLBJJGQNKGGNVBQPLJLC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-05-17T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-05-17T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-05-29T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-05-29T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Award winning writer, comedian and actor Rob Auton brings his latest show ‘The Eyes Open and Shut Show’ to Soho Theatre. Rob has written ten hit Edinburgh Festival Fringe comedy/theatre/spoken-word shows on specific themes including the colour yellow in ‘The Yellow Show’, sleep in ‘The Sleep Show’ and hair in ‘The Hair Show’. \r\nThe Eyes Open and Shut Show is a show about eyes when they are open and eyes when they are shut. With this show Rob wanted to explore what he could do to himself and others with language when eyes are open and shut. After writing ten shows on specific themes, he wanted to think about what makes him open his eyes and what makes him shut them.\r\nTV credits include – Starstruck (BBC), Cold Feet (ITV), The End of the F*cking World (Netflix/Channel 4), Miracle Workers (TBS), The Russell Howard Hour (Sky), Stand-Up Central With Rob Delaney (Comedy Central).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rob Auton: The Eyes Open and Shut Show","instanceDates":"27 January-1 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"564603AJVQMLTQSGPDNVLGTTPVQQDCBLH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-27T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-27T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-01T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-01T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Following a critically acclaimed sell-out run at the Edinburgh Festival 2023- award winning writer, comedian and actor Rob Auton brings his latest show ‘The Rob Auton Show’ to Soho Theatre.\r\nRob has written ten hit Edinburgh Festival Fringe comedy/theatre/spoken-word shows on specific themes including the colour yellow in ‘The Yellow Show’, sleep in ‘The Sleep Show’ and hair in ‘The Hair Show’. In his most autobiographical show to date, Rob turns the pen on himself to explore the memories and feelings that create his life on a daily basis.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rob Auton: The Rob Auton Show","instanceDates":"22 January-27 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"501803AJLGPPJDDPBCVPGMVTHGDLJTKJV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-22T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-22T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-27T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-27T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join Rob as he road-tests material ahead of his brand new tour!","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rob Beckett: Work in Progress","instanceDates":"27 September-9 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"573803ABQCLBHGQGLKCLJVLQLRHHGNNDT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-27T17:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-27T16:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-09T17:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-09T16:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join Rob as he road-tests material ahead of his brand new tour!\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rob Beckett: Work in Progress.","instanceDates":"2 July-2 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"562404APSKNSJHGKGMSDDDCMRSVGTHNQV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-02T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-02T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-02T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-02T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Gimme the thrills, gimme the spills, gimme a man with a microphone in his hand and careless abandon in his heart, gimme the winner of the Edinburgh Comedy Awards Victoria Wood Prize, gimme Rob Copland trying his best despite everything.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rob Copland: Gimme (One With Everything)","instanceDates":"30 September-11 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"569203AQHKKTCBLBNLLHGNHQQNKSRPDMD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-30T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-30T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-11T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-11T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The 2024 Edinburgh Comedy Award Panel Prize winner returns. Once one has one, one wants more please and comedian Rob Copland is asking for more. Who else is more-ing for one more? More for me, more for you, more for whoever wants to poke their head around the corner with us. Directed by Ben Target. 16+ Contains strobe/flashing lights - see website for further content advice.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rob Copland: ONE (more please)","instanceDates":"18 November-19 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"757403AHVGGBTMVKQTQNTLBHJRSVCTSRC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-18T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-18T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-19T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-19T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Rob Duncan (from award-winning shows Legs, Logs and Jeremy Segway) presents an hour of professionally researched nonsense, featuring relatable topics including trains and babies. \r\nWinner: The Malcolm Hardee Award for Comic Originality, 2019.\r\n“Irresistible force” ★★★★ The Scotsman\r\n “Gloriously ridiculous” ★★★★★ ThreeWeeks \r\n“Absurdity at its finest” Chortle\r\n\r\n16+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rob Duncan: Baby Trains","instanceDates":"13 June-13 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"478203ANKGCQJSMMJSMMRKHKBHTJSRTTC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-13T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-13T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-13T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-13T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_Venue":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"In 2024, Rob Duncan was named Printer of the Year. This show is an hour of printing, celebrating his award and debuting a new category of dramatic arts - Performance Printing.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rob Duncan: Printer of the Year","instanceDates":"10 April-11 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"695203ASJLGLRBHTQTSSKBKTPHVLLNQQR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-10T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-10T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-11T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-11T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Fresh from his BBC Radio 4 series Rob Newman On Air, the award-winning comedian’s new show is a stand-up epic that goes from cave paintings to car-free cities to ask: Who are we? Where are we going? And how do spiders fly? Rob Newman tells a story of how dancing in step saved prehistoric humans and how new scientific discoveries may help us take the right steps to a life after oil. \r\n\r\n‘He is one amazing comedian’ Time Out\r\n\r\n‘Newman combines proper scientific argument with dazzling shafts of wit.’  Times\r\n\r\n‘The funniest comedian I have ever seen.’ Sunday Times\r\n\r\n‘Refreshingly intelligent and hugely entertaining!’ Guardian\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":105,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rob Newman: Live on Stage","instanceDates":"4 July-8 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"473603AVCBKHNSJMPKCPNNGDSQSLSLTNV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-04T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-04T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-08T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-08T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"One of stars of Netflix’s Verified Stand-Up makes her UK debut.\r\nRobby Hoffman is a small ex-Hasidic queer Jewish stand-up comedian, writer, and true original. She can currently be seen as the breakout of Netflix’s Verified, their new selection of next generation stand-up comedians. New York Times comedy critic Jason Zinoman compares her \"bulldozing stand-up to Larry David because of her mountain-out-of-a-molehill kvetching, but her hilarious rage over people who complain about interruptions during a conversation makes her sound like a modern lesbian Andrew Dice Clay.\"\r\n\r\nShe was named one of Vulture's Top “Comedians to Watch,” one of Comedy Central's “Up Next” comedians, and was on Conan O’Brien’s “Comics to Watch” list. She has performed numerous times at the Montreal Just for Laughs festival and has twice headlined the New York Comedy Festival.  She recorded her first one-hour stand up special I’m Nervous in Toronto, available on CraveTV, and can also be seen in this year's History of the World on Hulu.\r\n \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Robby Hoffman","instanceDates":"11 March-16 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"529003AQMLTHQGJNSMHGDRTNVVQHVTKNL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-11T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-11T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-16T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-16T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Robby Hoffman is an Emmy-winning writer, Emmy-nominated actor, and comedian whose work spans stand-up, television, and podcasting. In 2025, she was named one of Variety's \"10 Comics to Watch\" and her debut Netflix stand-up special, Robby Hoffman: WAKE UP, directed by John Mulaney, premiered globally. Upon announcement of their collaboration, Mulaney boasted, “No one has owned a stage like her since James Brown.”\r\nHoffman — hailed by The New York Times as a performer who “steals every scene she’s in” has had a landmark year. She earned an Emmy nomination for her role as Randi in HBO’s Hacks, appeared opposite Michelle Williams in Hulu’s Dying for Sex, and can currently be seen in the fifth and final season of Hacks and on the HBO series Rooster alongside Steve Carell.\r\nKnown for her sharp, unfiltered perspective and singular comedic voice, Hoffman has quickly become one of the most distinctive performers in stand-up today. 18+ (Possible adult themes/sensitive content. Check webpage for current advice).","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Robby Hoffman at Glasgow Glee Club","instanceDates":"17 February-17 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"755803AMCJNBMGNSRQBGVSLMVQCTPGTDB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-17T19:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-17T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-17T19:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-17T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Glasgow Glee Club","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Robby Hoffman is an Emmy-winning writer, Emmy-nominated actor, and comedian whose work spans stand-up, television, and podcasting. In 2025, she was named one of Variety's \"10 Comics to Watch\" and her debut Netflix stand-up special, Robby Hoffman: WAKE UP, directed by John Mulaney, premiered globally. Upon announcement of their collaboration, Mulaney boasted, “No one has owned a stage like her since James Brown.”\r\nHoffman — hailed by The New York Times as a performer who “steals every scene she’s in” has had a landmark year. She earned an Emmy nomination for her role as Randi in HBO’s Hacks, appeared opposite Michelle Williams in Hulu’s Dying for Sex, and can currently be seen in the fifth and final season of Hacks and on the HBO series Rooster alongside Steve Carell.\r\nKnown for her sharp, unfiltered perspective and singular comedic voice, Hoffman has quickly become one of the most distinctive performers in stand-up today. (18+, contains adult themes/sensitive content. Check webpage for current details).","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Robby Hoffman: Live On Tour","instanceDates":"12 February-13 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"755603ACJSCVJLNRGPVNQVBTTCLKSNLVJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-12T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-12T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-13T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-13T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_Venue":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Is it possible to usurp a rural patriarch? To defeat him in a Tekken style tournament?\r\n\r\nTo overcome trauma through multimedia comedy and 90s nostalgia? Join BBC New\r\n\r\nComedy Awards nominee Roger O’Sullivan as he finds out. A nostalgic trip through\r\n\r\n90s video games, optical illusions and tales of rural Ireland. \r\n\r\nWinner of the Comedians Choice Best Newcomer 2025 and Nominated for Best Newcomer at The Edinburgh Comedy Awards 2025\r\n\r\nFind him on the internet @rogerocomedy.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Roger O’Sullivan: Fekken","instanceDates":"30 March-1 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"695403ATBCLDMTPHMNVRJJBGNVTJQGNTQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-30T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-30T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-01T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-01T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Is it possible to usurp a rural patriarch? To defeat him in a Tekken style tournament?\r\nTo overcome trauma through multimedia comedy and 90s nostalgia? Join BBC New\r\nComedy Awards nominee Roger O’Sullivan as he finds out. A nostalgic trip through\r\n\r\n90s video games, optical illusions and tales of rural Ireland. \r\nWinner of the Comedians Choice Best Newcomer 2025 and Nominated for Best Newcomer at The Edinburgh Comedy Awards 2025\r\nFind him on the internet @rogerocomedy.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Roger O’Sullivan: Fekken.","instanceDates":"5 January-7 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"661803AGGGVKSCCLQQHGSHJRVRGGPCRPM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-05T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-05T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-07T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-07T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A founding member of AIB (All India Bakchod) and one of the trailblazers of the comedy scene in India, Rohan Joshi returns to Soho Theatre.\r\nRenowned lazy stay-at-home expert Rohan Joshi has had an existential crisis like all basic b*tches do on 1st January and decided he needs to write and tour more. He has also, unfortunately, decided to subject an audience to this mid-life crisis. Join Rohan as he embraces the joys of middle-age over the course of the show and explores his gradual transformation into the pinnacle of human evolution; the Indian uncle.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rohan Joshi: Getting There ","instanceDates":"10 August-15 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"712003AJKSQPVSQKVHPBBLSPJJHBBRDKK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-10T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-10T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-15T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-15T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A founding member of AIB (All India Bakchod) and one of the trailblazers of the comedy scene in India, Rohan Joshi makes his Soho Theatre debut.\r\nRenowned lazy stay-at-home expert Rohan had an existential crisis like all basic b*tches do on 1st January and decided he needs to write and tour more. He has also, unfortunately, been diagnosed with ADD. So join him for a solo hour long show of new material which is about life, or maybe it’s about movies, or maybe it’s about unicorns. The truth is it’s about a different thing every three minutes okay? Are you happy now? Is that what you wanted to hear? But also please come for the show.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rohan Joshi: Getting There (But Not Quite)","instanceDates":"2 August-9 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"635803AMCPKBMPHMTCRRLMMKRLLDDTKMQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-02T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-02T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-09T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-09T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"\"Born entertainer\" (Scotsman) and British/Indian Rohan Sharma is/isn't bringing his critically acclaimed debut hour to Soho Theatre following a breakout Edinburgh Fringe run.\r\nA fast-paced, gag-packed multimedia odyssey, and playful interrogation of identity, all from the perspective of a man whose brain has been corroded/nourished by modern society. 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rohan Sharma: Mad Dog","instanceDates":"2 July-3 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"726203AHRVKTVSCGRGCTQPJSSDQPKNSLQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-02T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-02T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-03T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-03T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Attention is the new oil. Hey slut! With its Edinburgh Fringe run already selling out, ROLEPLAY is bringing the heat to London this Autumn. A struggling feminist podcaster reinvents herself in pursuit of fame, only to lose herself in the performance. Darkly hilarious, gripping and surreal, ROLEPLAY is a ferocious interrogation of modern sex, the commodification of feminism and the era of the personal brand. Writer, actress and comic Hannah Reilly brings her 'fresh, female-first approach' (Elle) to London in this NSFW one-woman show developed and directed by Paige Rattray (Fangirls). ROLEPLAY also marks a major collaboration between award-winning producers Francesca Moody Productions (Fleabag, Baby Reindeer) and Global Creatures (Moulin Rouge! The Musical, Muriel's Wedding The Musical). Guardian, Time Out & Telegraph Top Pick, Edinburgh Fringe 2026\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"ROLEPLAY","instanceDates":"22 October-21 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"742003AHPTGQDSNSTSDJJLMBBRTBLHBST","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-22T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-22T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-21T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-21T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Winner 2024 Melbourne International Comedy Festival Award for Most Outstanding Show, and Nominee Best Comedy Show Edinburgh Comedy Awards 2024.\r\nKeys is back, but with something a bit different. Spend an hour with award-winning comedian Sarah Keyworth as they joke and gently meander their way through an evening of playful crowd work. Expect to chat. Expect to be surprised. Every hour is completely funny and completely different!\r\n\r\nAs seen on Live at the Apollo (BBC), Mock the Week (BBC), and 8 Out of 10 Cats Does Countdown (Channel 4).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Roll to Me: An Hour Of Crowd Work with Sarah Keyworth","instanceDates":"1 April-1 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"694603ARRDNKLQCBHJGPPKPNDPBJBTPMQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-01T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-01T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-01T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-01T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Roman Harris has developed a reputation for being a 'Nice Guy' but is he? Really? Come and find out\r\nRoman Harris has developed a reputation for being a 'Nice Guy' but is he? Really?\r\nJoin him for a journey of observational, anecdotal and introspective comedy as he explores his sense of self in a quest to discover whether he really is Mr. Nice or whether he's actually just a dick!\r\n\r\nI wasn't sure whether to include some of my accolades/comedy achievements. However, if this is a good idea then here's a few.\r\n\r\nBBC New Comedy Awards, 21 - Nominee\r\nNATYS - Runner Up, 22\r\nBritish Comedian of the Year - Semi Finalist, 24\r\nBBC New Comedy Awards - Nominee\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Roman Harris: Mr Nice","instanceDates":"14 February-14 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"589403AVBHMLLJBQTVGKNVKHDLCTSDDMG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-14T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-14T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-14T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-14T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Rory Marshall has dug deep into his extremely sad and pathetic soul to create an hour of extremely sad and pathetic characters.\r\nHe adamantly claims that they're nothing like him at all, but you can be the judge of that.\r\n\r\nStraight from a critically-acclaimed, sell-out Edinburgh Fringe run, this is the debut show from South East Dartmoor's fifth-most promising character comedian.\r\n\r\nAs seen on Starstruck, Ellie & Natasia, Channel 4 and heard on Radio 4.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rory Marshall: Pathetic Little Characters","instanceDates":"29 October-1 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"659203AQGKHRVBVDDKNDDCNGQRHGLQKKD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-29T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-29T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-01T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-01T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Actor, comedian and writer Rory Scovel lands at Soho Theatre for a strictly limited 5-night run.\r\nKnow best for his 2024 HBO stand-up special Rory Scovel: Religion, Sex, and a Few Things in Between, and his starring role in the Apple TV+ series Physical opposite Rose Byrne, Rory brings his brand-new live show to Soho for its first ever UK dates.\r\nOther appearances include Babylon directed by Damien Chazelle, I Feel Pretty opposite Amy Schumer, and Old Dads alongside Bill Burr. Rory’s stand up has been featured on Comedy Central, CONAN, and Late Night with Jimmy Fallon, and he has written on The Eric Andre Show.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rory Scovel’s “Should I Live Here” Tour","instanceDates":"8 May-10 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"607803ABLMSDSJBRJNPNBHSGBRKPKKKDD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-08T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-08T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-10T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-10T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Come into the bog; the mud’s just fine.\r\n\r\nPrimal Bog is the gorgeously gross new piece from Rosa Garland, creator of cult hit Trash Salad. Join Rosa as she plunges headfirst into the muck of sexuality, slime, and unfiltered desire that’s been hailed as “filthy and fearless” (The Telegraph) and “a masterclass in comedy” (Metro).\r\n18+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rosa Garland: Primal Bog","instanceDates":"25 February-7 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"665803ATVLDNNCNTSVVQTDVKJTTRTHJNQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-25T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-25T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-07T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-07T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Sex. Love. Lettuce. Join gorgeous clown Trash Salad in her quest for connection: a genre-bending burlesque adventure, using lip sync, strip tease and song on a mission to understand intimacy. Some call it a clown opera; a sexual odyssey; a compost-heap romance. Trash calls it a joyful queer-femme love story in the shape of a salad. Come and see the piece that’s made audiences ‘laugh, cry, and nearly piss’. \r\n\r\nBirthed by award-winning performance maker Rosa Garland. \r\n\r\nNOMINEE: Vault Festival Innovation Award 2023.\r\n\r\n‘Salad at its sexiest and most unsavoury’ ★★★★★ - FringeBiscuit\r\n‘Best comedy shows of 2022’ ★★★★ - The Telegraph\r\n‘A force of nature’ ★★★★  - The Wee Review \r\n‘A queer masterpiece’ ★★★★ - Ed Fringe Review \r\n‘A knock out… riotously funny’ ★★★★ - Binge Fringe\r\n‘Indubitably deserves its cult status’ ★★★★ - The Reviews Hub \r\n\r\nFor ‘Two Super Super Hot Men’\r\n'Hilarious' ★★★★★ - The Spy in the Stalls\r\n'A masterclass of clowning' - The Play's the Thing\r\n\r\n*****\r\nRosa Garland is a clown, burlesque artist and theatre maker. She likes things that are slimy and sexy. She trained at Ecole Philippe Gaulier. \r\nTrash Salad is a burlesque clown adventure, her solo comedy debut, which had sell-out performances at Edinburgh Fringe 2022 (Pleasance) and VAULT Festival 2023. Rosa also appears as Ron in environmental drag duo Alan and Ron, who have been found at Tate Modern Lates and Camden People’s Theatre. Their show ‘Two Super Super Hot Men’ was recommended by Lyn Gardner as a VAULT Festival highlight 2020. She also works with Poltergeist collective, creating nerdy, heartfelt stories that experiment with form across a variety of media. They were named “one of the UK’s best young theatre companies” by the Guardian, and were recipients of New Diorama & Underbelly’s Untapped Award 2019, and the Samuel French New Play Award 2018. \r\n\r\n18+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rosa Garland: Trash Salad","instanceDates":"2 June-3 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"465203ARCRGNHNRPHBRGMJGVQLBDHDVGS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-02T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-02T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-03T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-03T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Lady Clementine has until her 27th birthday to find The One. \r\nWhen her latest beau goes missing, she embarks on a hilariously unhinged quest to solve the mystery of her ill fortune. But with neither sense nor sensibility, will our romantic heroine find love in time? Set roughly \"in the past'', this is a story about sickly sisters, self-love and Sylvanian Families. Bonnets at the ready, ladies, for the debut character comedy show of the (Scorpio) season. \r\nBritish Comedy Guide Best Reviewed Shows at the Edinburgh Fringe.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rosalie Minnitt: Clementine","instanceDates":"9 May-10 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"618203ANMTHHGLBMLLTKQBQVNSLCNNSDB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-09T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-09T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-10T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-10T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Lady Clementine has until her 27th birthday to find The One. \r\nWhen her latest beau goes missing, she embarks on a hilariously unhinged quest to solve the mystery of her ill fortune. But with neither sense nor sensibility, will our romantic heroine find love in time? Set roughly \"in the past'', this is a story about sickly sisters, self-love and Sylvanian Families. Bonnets at the ready, ladies, for the debut character comedy show of the (Scorpio) season. \r\nBritish Comedy Guide Best Reviewed Shows at the Edinburgh Fringe.\r\nDirected by Tristan Robinson.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rosalie Minnitt: Clementine.","instanceDates":"15 November-9 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"499803ADDGNCPSNLBPNSDMDJKHKJBVTPR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-15T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-15T22:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-09T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-09T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Lady Clementine has until her 27th birthday to find The One.\r\nWhen her latest beau goes missing, she embarks on a hilariously unhinged quest to solve the mystery of her ill fortune. But with neither sense nor sensibility, will our romantic heroine find love in time? Set roughly \"in the past'', this is a story about sickly sisters, self-love and Sylvanian Families. Bonnets at the ready, ladies, for the debut character comedy show of the (Scorpio) season. \r\nBritish Comedy Guide Best Reviewed Shows at the Edinburgh Fringe.\r\n\r\nDirected by Tristan Robinson.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rosalie Minnitt: Clementine.","instanceDates":"11 September-14 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"567403AMTVBJRMSHSMJRQQKNDRCSSKRLN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-11T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-11T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-14T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-14T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"What happens when you’ve almost reached the top of a mountain you’ve been climbing for years and you realise that maybe you should have been concentrating your efforts on another mountain entirely?\r\nThe winner of the 2025 Sir Billy Connolly Spirit of Glasgow Award, Rosco McClelland makes his debut at Soho Theatre with one of the best-reviewed shows at Edinburgh Fringe (British Comedy Guide).\r\nTwice nominated for Best Newcomer at the Scottish Comedy Awards and winner of Best International Act at New Zealand Comedy Festival 2025, Rosco is rapidly becoming one of comedy's brightest stars.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rosco Mcclelland: How Could Hell Be Any Worse?","instanceDates":"26 June-27 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"693003ARBNBVBKHPMKVLDLMDBJJCSVBPC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-26T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-26T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-27T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-27T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Jam-packed with songs from the celebrated musician Nick Cope, and story by Victoria Saxton - this is a great, big, heart-warming adventure. \r\nRosie and Hugh the Hedgehog are best friends. They want it to be the last day of summer holidays forever. Impossible? Not if they can find the witch who lives in the middle of the forest with her pet dragon. \r\n\r\nA great, big, heart-warming adventure with Rosie, Hugh, a squirrel with a wobbly tooth, a little lizard and one very rusty robot. \r\n\r\nJam-packed with songs from the celebrated musician Nick Cope (CBeebies’ Nick Cope’s Popcast) and story by Victoria Saxton, this show is for 3-8 year-old adventurers and their families, by Fringe First Award-winning The North Wall in association with Soho Theatre.\r\n3+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":65,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rosie and Hugh’s Great Big Adventure","instanceDates":"22 August-25 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"556404AMTVJDVVMVNVSQLMKMLNQNCPPDN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-22T11:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-22T10:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-25T14:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-25T13:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Rosie Holt and her MP alter ego are performing their show ‘That’s Politainment!’ for the last time right before a (possibly new?!) Prime Minister is announced. Join her as she prepares for victory, or professional annihilation. \r\nRosie is an acclaimed comedian, actor and satirist, whose popular videos on social media have achieved more than 6.5 million views. Her book Why We Were Right by Rosie Holt MP has just been published by Ebury press, she is the host of the Aria nominated parody podcast Noncensored, and has been seen/heard on The Russell Howard Hour (Sky Max), Friday Night with Niall Patterson (Sky News) BBC Radio 4’s The News Quiz, POV, DM’s Are Open, and Ashley Blaker: 6.5 Children among other credits.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rosie Holt: THAT’S POLITAINMENT!","instanceDates":"3 July-4 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"560403AKGHBKBLLGMCRVCVNLDMLVMDJQK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-03T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-03T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-04T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-04T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Political","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"* Please note that this show will be filmed, including potential audience filming *\r\nJoin self-professed prick and star of Taskmaster Rosie Jones as she films her latest stand-up show. She's talking about the big stuff: being single, the pressures of representing huge sections of the population, and gravy. Oh, and boobs. The BAFTA-nominated powerhouse returns with her loveable blend of cheek and charm following a nomination for Most Outstanding Show at Melbourne International Comedy Festival 2023. \r\nAs seen on nearly everything, including Taskmaster, Live at the Apollo, The Jonathan Ross Show, The Royal Variety Performance, QI, 8 Out of 10 Cats, Cats Does Countdown, The Last Leg, Joe Lycett’s Got Your Back, Mock the Week, and soon to be on her very own upcoming sitcom. \r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rosie Jones: I Can’t Tell What She’s Saying (Live Recording)","instanceDates":"31 March-31 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"681603ALRPGPHSJMKQSNGNVBQBJQTVKDP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-31T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-31T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-31T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-31T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Rosie Jones is embarking on her FIRST EVER UK tour and, boy, she is EXCITED.\r\nJoin Rosie as she ponders whether she is a national treasure, a little prick, or somewhere in between! This show is guaranteed to be full of unapologetic cheekiness, nonsensical fun and unadulterated JOY from the triple threat herself.\r\nBest known for her hit travel series Trip Hazard and Mission: Accessible, and for numerous appearances on shows The Last Leg, 8 Out of 10 Cats, Cats Does Countdown, Hypothetical, Mock the Week, The Ranganation and Joe Lycett's Got Your Back to name just a few! \r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rosie Jones: Triple Threat","instanceDates":"8 April-9 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"509203ANLLKPVDRQLGLVHBNRQBPNTTLBV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-08T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-08T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-09T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-09T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Rosie Jones is embarking on her FIRST EVER UK tour and, boy, she is EXCITED. Join Rosie as she ponders whether she is a national treasure, a little prick, or somewhere in between! This show is guaranteed to be full of unapologetic cheekiness, nonsensical fun and unadulterated JOY from the triple threat herself.\r\n\r\nBest known for her hit travel series Trip Hazard and Mission: Accessible, and for numerous appearances on shows The Last Leg, 8 Out of 10 Cats, Cats Does Countdown, Hypothetical, Mock the Week, The Ranganation and Joe Lycett's Got Your Back to name just a few! \r\n\r\n\r\n‘Rosie Jones is completely brazen, downright hilarious and will leave you snorting with laughter’ ★★★★★ (Edinburgh Festivals Magazine)\r\n\r\n‘Rosie embodies pure joy. She packs in the jokes, quick wit and has the audience in the palm of her hand’ ★★★★★ (Entertainment Focus)\r\n\r\n'...elegantly crafted and mischievous to its bones' ★★★★ (Scotsman)\r\n\r\n‘Her jokes are beautifully crafted with no beat wasted and punchlines that take you by surprise’ ★★★★ (iTalkTelly)\r\n\r\n14+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rosie Jones: Triple Threat.","instanceDates":"2 October-7 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"458603APCBTCPJNVMLSBRVBGVCVMSNCKH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-02T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-02T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-07T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-07T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Access","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Access"},{"description":"Dust off your spats and settle in for a timeless love/ghost story. \r\nRosie Yadid - cabaret queen, burlesque clown and \"power packing chanteuse\" (TimeOut New York) - presents the high flying antics of a vaudeville legend who will not be forgotten. In recounting the life of his late wife, Mimi, Chayim Solonely tells of the greatest star who’s ever lived. From humble beginnings as a nickel swallowing, tap dancing orphan turned child star, to rubbing shoulders with the mob in Manhattan’s shadiest speakeasies, to the dizzying heights of Hollywood’s notorious studio sets… nobody did it quite like Mimi. But what makes a life worth remembering? What does it mean to be a STAH!? \r\nIn her debut solo hour, Rosie Yadid combines burlesque, musical theatre, storytelling and clown in this bittersweet love song to unsung divas and lyrical exploration of Jewish archetypes. Mimi is a surreal surrender to foolish love that's nostalgic, naughty, silly and striking. \r\nDirected by Lachlan Werner \r\nAccompaniment by Olly Muxworthy \r\n“Fast talking dynamo” (Evening Standard) “Electric” (Broadway World) \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rosie Yadid: Mimi","instanceDates":"12 February-12 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"685403AMMBJBCSSGLRDTCRKNTBSPSKTLM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-12T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-12T22:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-12T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-12T22:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Deep dive into the weird and wonderful world of eBay! Ruby will lead you down the rabbit hole and introduce you to some of the bizarre eBay subcultures.\r\n'Ruby brings an infectious energy and steady stream of animated stories... injected with a deluge of sharp-witted reflections' (Student). Winner of Funny Women Comedy Writing Award, 2022. 'One to watch' (Funny Women Stage Award, 2021). Finalist of Amused Moose New Act of the Year, 2019.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ruby Carr: eBae By","instanceDates":"13 February-13 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"523603ALTSDHTQGNPVPCQNBMBHLGJRKTM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-13T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-13T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-13T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-13T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"In this new show, Ruby Wax dishes the dirt from the behind-the-scenes on the shows that made her into a national icon.\r\nIt's almost easier to say whom Ruby Wax DIDN'T meet, interview and coax fascinating insights from in her huge TV shows 'Ruby Wax Meets' and 'Full Wax'. Donald Trump, OJ Simpson, Pamela Anderson, Madonna and many more. \r\nHer provocative, abrasive, incomparable style was - just about - kept in check by lifelong friend and A-list producer, Clive Tulloh. Together live on stage they review clips from the extraordinary shows, tell scandalous stories never before heard - and take the audience along for the ride.\r\nFeaturing Ruby Wax & Clive Tulloh.\r\n\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ruby Wax: Absolutely Famous","instanceDates":"6 October-7 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"708003AGQHVCCVPVPMSPKPCKVGKNGVLVT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-06T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-06T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-07T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-07T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"After four years, Ruby returns to the stage following her critically acclaimed, sell out tour, How To Be Human. See her in the rawest, darkest and funniest stage show yet, a stage adaptation of her upcoming book, set for release 11th May 2023. Renowned for her comedy, her fearless approach to tackling mental well-being, and her ability to make audiences laugh and cry in equal measure. I’m Not As Well As I Thought I Was, is set to be Ruby’s rawest, darkest, funniest and most compelling stage show yet.  \r\nIn 2022, Ruby Wax went on a search to find meaning. She booked a series of potentially life-changing journeys. In the Dominican Republic, she went swimming with humpback whales; she joined a Christian monastery; in Greece, she worked in a refugee camp; in California, she did a silent 30-day mindfulness retreat. \r\nThe search to find meaning was about to take her in a different direction, no longer journeying in the outside world but within her own mind, and this inner journey would turn out to be the most life-changing journey of all.\r\nI'm Not as Well as I Thought I Was will see Ruby pushing boundaries, and making her mark as one of the most important voices in mental health today.\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ruby Wax: I’m Not as Well as I Thought I Was","instanceDates":"20 November-25 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"471203ANQBTKSVHLGQNMJKVDCPQNSNLRM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-20T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-20T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-25T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-25T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"International award-winning comedian and loveable dreamboat Runi Talwar (Amused Moose National Finalist, 2Northdown National Finalist, Have I Got News For You, Hypothetical) works through new material for his highly-anticipated debut hour.\r\nFrom the humble beginnings of being the only Indian kid in his primary school in New Zealand, to the heady heights of moving to a studio apartment on the other side of the world one month before a global pandemic, join Runi as he explores the meaning of luck and fortune, in the hilarious and heart-warming tale of a lovely bloke who's *just a little bit* incredibly cursed.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Runi Talwar: Work In Progress","instanceDates":"15 February-15 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"523803ABJPNGHQLBVSDTVBHKGRBMBRMGP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-15T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-15T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-15T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-15T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Rupi workshops new material in this intimate residency. No polish. No production. Just you, her, a small room, and everything before the final draft. \r\nA breakout literary phenomenon and #1 New York Times bestselling author, Rupi Kaur wrote, illustrated, and self-published her first poetry collection, milk and honey (2014). Next came its artistic siblings, the sun and her flowers (2017) and home body (2020), both debuting at #1 on bestseller lists across the world. These collections have sold over 12 million copies and have been translated into over 40 languages, with milk and honey becoming one of the highest-selling poetry books of the 21st century. She was also regarded as “writer of the decade” by the New Republic and recognized on the Forbes 30 under 30 list. In 2022, Kaur released her fourth book, Healing Through Words. \r\n\r\nIn 2021, Kaur produced Rupi Kaur Live, a first-of-its-kind poetry special on Amazon Prime Video. Kaur also executive produced the film This Place, which premiered at the Toronto International Film Festival in 2022, and the 2024 Academy Award–nominated film To Kill a Tiger. \r\n\r\nKaur has graced stages across the globe and completed her third sold-out world tour in 2023. Her shows are poetic theatrical experiences interlaced with Kaur’s own touch of stand-up comedy. Kaur’s work encompasses love, loss, trauma, healing, femininity, and more. \r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rupi Kaur: Uncut","instanceDates":"18 January-30 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"731003ABLKGTJBLQGJTBKSPRDKDGJHNSH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-01-18T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-01-18T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-01-30T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-01-30T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Drawing on his new memoir The Queerest of Folk: A Life in Television, he will sit down with a very special guest host for a conversation that promises to be as honest, funny, and fearless as the man himself.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Russell T Davies: The Queerest of Folk","instanceDates":"8 October-8 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"736603AGHSQSCTVTTSNMHBJCTTCPSBDVC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-08T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-08T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-08T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-08T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Storytelling","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Talk","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":""},{"description":"Saaniya Abbas takes audiences on her most personal and side-splitting journey yet in Hellarious. \r\n With sharp insights and her signature feline mischief, Saaniya dives into the cultural taboos of divorce, the absurdity of internet fame, and her playful take on the concept of hell itself. She reminds us that life isn’t about always landing on your feet - it’s about laughing when you don’t.\r\n Tracing her evolution from a sheltered upbringing in a Muslim family to carving out her own path, Hellarious is a bold celebration of resilience, defiance, and self-discovery.\r\n\r\nAs you may have heard, her show is doing great, and she got two 4-star reviews so far. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Saaniya Abbas: Hellarious","instanceDates":"9 February-14 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"652203AGDMCCGSRPBJPMPCNLJBSPBBRTQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-09T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-09T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-14T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-14T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Part of National Theatre Connections","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sad Club, created by Luke Barnes & music by Adam Pleeth, performed by St Paul’s Way Players","instanceDates":"1 May-1 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"539403AMNTPKMPMVVGHBNBBTDMJSJBDKM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-01T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-01T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-01T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-01T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Sixty minutes of world class stand-up comedy from one of New York’s hottest up-and-coming comedians.\r\nHaving opened for the likes of Hasan Minhaj, Mark Normand and Whitney Cummings, Sahib was named one of the Vulture “Comedians Your Should and Will Know of 2025” and has amassed over 1.7 million followers across TikTok and Instagram.\r\nJoin him in London for a limited run of rare UK dates.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sahib Singh","instanceDates":"9 February-14 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"671003ADDLBDNPSLDBVPTPJSBCSKTLLGG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-09T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-09T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-14T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-14T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"An hour of unfiltered comedy, puns, improvisation, props and the most bizarre thoughts that even Sahil can't comprehend.\r\nSahil Shah is a popular Indian stand-up comedian who is currently tired… of being tired! Gen Z? Gen Y? Nope. He’s Gen Ex-Hausted.\r\n\r\nAs he turns 33, he looks back at all the true yet hilarious incidents that have led him to this place. From stories of his alcoholism (a night he can’t remember but friends can’t forget) to his therapist crying (because he broke her with his problems) and his complete hatred of children (his dog is way better any day).\r\n\r\nSahil has toured India, Dubai and Toronto with his show…  he’s now super excited to bring it to Soho Theatre. \r\n\r\n‘It is hard not to laugh at Sahil Shah’s exceptional comedy. It gets as silly as it could at times, but he argues that is who he really is.’ Indian Express\r\n\r\n‘Has people cracking up.’ Deccan Chronicle\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sahil Shah is Broken!","instanceDates":"10 June-15 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"546403AVMDBBSHMNKCGQCLJSBRDPRSDQD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-10T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-10T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-15T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-15T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The candles flicker. The rain beats down. And the creature stirs. Salty Brine ventures into the dark and disturbed as he twists Mary Shelley’s Frankenstein around The Smiths’ post-punk, indie classic The Queen is Dead. Witness a hideous monster come to life as Salty Brine makes his London debut in Bigmouth Strikes Again.\r\n\r\nThe Living Record Collection is a dazzling expedition into the heart of popular music, imagining track lists as blueprints for evenings of musical mayhem. Created and performed by cabaret artist Salty Brine, The Living Record Collection takes incredible albums and twists them in style and form until they are at once familiar and foreign, nostalgic and new.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Salty Brine: Bigmouth Strikes Again – The Smith Show","instanceDates":"31 August-16 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"483203ASNSGJRCHBCLLCHCNMQPSSQDNHM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-31T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-31T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-16T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-16T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"LGBTQ+","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Drag","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"The New York cabaret scene’s most daring and delightful diva brings another of his genre-defying cabaret shows to Soho for a limited run only.\r\nSalty Brine is back – and he’s more unusual than ever.\r\nThe ghosts of two divine deviants have returned from the grave to take care of a little unfinished business. But can they get to the bottom of all their loose ends… so to speak?\r\nInspired by George Chauncey’s revelatory history book Gay New York, Salty Brine takes you on a stroll through the glittering underbelly of 1930s Manhattan set to the timeless music of Cyndi Lauper’s pop triumph She’s So Unusual.\r\nSalty Brine is the creative force behind The Living Record Collection, a dazzling expedition into the heart of popular music that imagines tracklists as blueprints for evenings of musical mayhem, creating the perfect cabaret experience for theatre-lovers.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Salty Brine: He’s So Unusual - The Cyndi Lauper Show","instanceDates":"18 November-22 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"666203ARMMPMVDTJNDQBJPBPBSTMBMSMS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-18T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-18T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-22T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-22T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Drag","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Theatre"},{"description":"In How Strange It Is, Neutral Milk Hotel's indie-rock triumph In the Aeroplane Over the Sea and Anne Frank's stunning and candid The Diary of a Young Girl fuse with confessions from Salty's adolescent longings in a genre-defying cabaret that will take your breath away. Sparks fly, time bends, and the ghosts of our past return to us in this hilarious and devastating work from Salty's acclaimed and expansive Living Record Collection. ‘Astounding’ ★★★★★ The Stage Salty Brine is the creative force behind The Living Record Collection, a dazzling expedition into the heart of popular music that imagines tracklists as blueprints for evenings of musical mayhem, creating the perfect cabaret experience for theatre-lovers. As Time Out New York puts it, ‘the outrageously talented Salty Brine takes classic pop albums—from Joni Mitchell’s Blue to the Dirty Dancing soundtrack—and weaves their songs into funny, perceptive tapestries of storytelling. The shows are highly addictive: Once you’ve been dunked into Brine, you’ll want to dive right back in’.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/sohotheatre/files/b383770f-d266-461c-ae84-c2cff8861208.jpg","isOnSale":true,"name":"Salty Brine: How Strange It Is","instanceDates":"7 September-19 September","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/sohotheatre/files/b383770f-d266-461c-ae84-c2cff8861208-thumbnail.jpg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"717603ACPGKMPQGTNQSLSTTLKBKRMVQVD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-07T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-07T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-19T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-19T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Following a critically-acclaimed run at last year's Edinburgh Fringe, darling of the New York cabaret scene Salty Brine returns to Soho Theatre with his latest sensational show.\r\n \r\nAnnie Lennox’s transcendent solo album DIVA stands at the centre of this sparkling story about strong, defiant women and the little gay boy who loves them. Careening from Judy Garland’s definitive Carnegie Hall concert to Kate Chopin’s groundbreaking feminist novel The Awakening, Salty Brine defies the cabaret form in ways that must be witnessed to be believed. High camp and heartbreaking drama collide as Salty charts his way, track by track, through Lennox’s masterpiece. \r\n \r\nSalty Brine is the creative force behind The Living Record Collection, a dazzling expedition into the heart of popular music, imagining track lists as blueprints for evenings of musical mayhem.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Salty Brine: These Are The Contents Of My Head - The Annie Lennox Show","instanceDates":"11 April-26 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"610403ALKVNLBLRHQBPLQJMDQRSSSCMSP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-11T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-11T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-26T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-26T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Step aside Stallone! Sam Dugmore is locked and loaded as the greatest action hero of all time, unearthing his ruthless man skills to confront his worst nemesis... himself. A dead- sexy mission, filled with chaos, 80s singing, dancing and workout montages, explosions, evil Russians, suppressed raw male emotion and a dog called Fluffy. Extremely camp, extremely silly, extremely entertaining, extremely Manbo. \r\nBest Weekly Comedy Award, Adelaide Fringe 2021 and\r\n2022.\r\nBest Newcomer, Sydney Comedy Festival 2021.\r\nEdinburgh Fringe Award winner, Adelaide Fringe 2022.\r\n'A physically challenging, extremely silly hour of pure, embodied entertainment' ★★★★ The Scotsman\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sam Dugmore: MANBO","instanceDates":"13 June-13 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"478404AHSBNMNTHJBSRTCVKSLBVVTQBQL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-13T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-13T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-13T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-13T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Say hello to a horrid mind. Award-winning late-night villainy from an uncomfortable mind.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sam Eley is Basil Crumbwick: Soul Sewage","instanceDates":"8 October-30 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"745003ASKDGVRGTDJDRTNMCMGLVPRQPPM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-08T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-08T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-01-30T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-01-30T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Following two successful specials and a US tour, how does a black queer woman who never felt truly a part of her country grapple with its certain demise?\r\nThrough contemplation, analysis and harsh critique. \r\nSam Jay’s \"We The People” was nominated for Best Comedy Show at Edinburgh Fringe Festival 2025, and won the 2025 Uprise Award, which recognizes shows that dare to provoke, disrupt and reframe discussions.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sam Jay: We the People","instanceDates":"2 June-6 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"692603AKLBHLBHDCJGCCGPHPHNTNDDDKR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-02T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-02T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-06T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-06T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join Sam Lake for his first UK Tour of his critically acclaimed show, Aspiring DILF! Written & performed by Sam Lake, directed by Edinburgh Comedy Award Nominee, Lauren Pattinson.\r\nWith the rise of formerly beloved male celebs turning into “anti-woke”,” why aren’t men men anymore?” toxic commentators on low-quality news outlets and podcasts, Sam has become scared of the man he may become in the future. So to combat this fragile masculinity, he’s embarking on a mission to ensure he becomes what he believes to be the last respectable form of a man, the Daddy. Join him on his journey to Daddy-dom, as he chats about Furbies, Butlins & scandalous interactions with a rugby team.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sam Lake: Aspiring DILF","instanceDates":"11 April-13 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"505203AVRQRRCJMJHRPQHTDTBJKCQLJHJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-11T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-11T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-13T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-13T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Esméralda is a heartfelt and hilarious romp through ludicrous anecdotes from Sam’s childhood, growing up in Cornwall, solving puzzles and the difficulties caused by not speaking the same language as half of his family. Setting out to better understand his Spanish Mum and the choices she made, Sam examines the lessons he learnt from her, the advice she shared and the lasting influence of her powerful last words. Expect stories about Zumba, poor sex education and a dash of Español as Sam embraces his heritage (he’s finally trying to learn some Spanish) and dives into themes of personal destiny, family legacy and living up to other people’s expectations. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sam Lake: Esméralda","instanceDates":"13 January-15 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"579003AMKLNJLDRNSVPRRRPVPNMGMBNJL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-13T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-13T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-15T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-15T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Don’t you just love a laugh? Well get into this new stand-up hour from '...a rare gem of a comic' (Rolling Stone). Feeling like life and his career has become repetitive, Sam is asking himself “are we really doing this again?”. Has he lost sight of his goals after years of entertaining countless idiotic men in comedy clubs? Has he turned into yet another version of himself to please everyone? Sam addresses the stereotypes of effeminate gay men that both hinder and help him  in his efforts to be a funny little scamp. If you’ve ever had a lifelong passion, a dream or a goal you’ve strived for and maybe failed (or are currently failing) at, this is the show for you. 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sam Lake: You’re Joking!? Not Another One!","instanceDates":"12 January-13 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"674203ACLHBJCRTLBNSDNGPNVSRHQLQGJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-12T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-12T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-13T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-13T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Fresh from a sold-out run in May, Sam Morrison brings his hit show ’Sugar Daddy' back to Soho Theatre.\r\nHailed as “the best new show in New York right now” (The Daily Beast), comedian Sam Morrison takes the audience on an outrageous journey of love, loss, diabetes, seagull attacks, and a few extraordinary coincidences.\r\nSugar Daddy follows comedian Sam Morrison as he meets his late partner at a gay bear festival, and finds hope and humour in grief after his passing. \r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sam Morrison: Sugar Daddy","instanceDates":"24 October-28 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"489203AKNRRJHPGPTLVVQVDBTCSJTLQKK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-24T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-24T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-28T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-28T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Fresh from his off-broadway run and “Late Night with Seth Meyers”, Sam Morrison brings his hit show ’Sugar Daddy' to London’s very own Soho Theatre. Hailed as “the best new show in New York right now” (The Daily Beast), comedian Sam Morrison takes the audience on an outrageous journey of love, loss, diabetes, seagull attacks, and a few extraordinary coincidences. Sugar Daddy follows comedian Sam Morrison as he meets his late partner at a gay bear festival, and finds hope and humor in grief after his passing. “Arch sass and polished panache” New York Times “It’s brilliant!!” - Alan Cumming \"beautifully told, sharp, moving, and truly laugh-out-loud, doubled-up, head-thrown-back funny.” - The Daily Beast ★★★★★ - Broadway Baby ★★★★★ - Broadway World “Massively entertaining… How Morrison can make us laugh about crying, cry laugh and then just straight-up waterworks is an entire mystery” ★★★★ - Voice Mag\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sam Morrison: Sugar Daddy [May23]","instanceDates":"17 May-20 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"449603ABMGVMDLKSVSBNPRDTDBDVPMJLL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-17T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-17T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-20T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-20T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A glistening diamond hour of stand-up from delusional queer icon Sam Nicoresti about love, insanity, and the hunt for the perfect skirt suit.\r\nFollowing a breakout run at this year's Edinburgh Fringe Festival, Sam brings her critically acclaimed hit Baby Doomer to the Soho Theatre. \r\n \r\nFrom a sartorial emergency in a TK Maxx to the standing stones of Cornwall, through the seas of change, clothes and cats, Sam Nicoresti asks the vital question: does the perfect skirt suit even exist?\r\n \r\nBaby Doomer is the follow-up to the acclaimed Wokeflake. “One of the definitive documents of the trans experience in stand-up.” Chortle. \r\n \r\nBest Show Nominee Leicester Comedy Festival 2025\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sam Nicoresti: Baby Doomer","instanceDates":"16 March-20 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"668803ATPTSGCGRBVJRQBMSRLTHHVPPMV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-16T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-16T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-20T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-20T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Description/copy – main copy\tFollowing a breakout run at this year's Edinburgh Fringe Festival, Sam brings her critically acclaimed hit Baby Doomer to the Soho Theatre. \r\n \r\nFrom a sartorial emergency in a TK Maxx to the standing stones of Cornwall, through the seas of change, clothes and cats, Sam Nicoresti asks the vital question: does the perfect skirt suit even exist?\r\n \r\nBaby Doomer is the follow-up to the acclaimed Wokeflake. “One of the definitive documents of the trans experience in stand-up.” Chortle. \r\n \r\nBest Show Nominee Leicester Comedy Festival 2025\r\n\r\nPraise for Baby Doomer:\r\n\r\n“Sam Nicoresti is a delight, and this show is fabulous” ★★★★★ One4Review \r\n\r\n“Uproariously funny, life-affirming, angry, dumb, insightful and political all at once” ★★★★.5 Chortle \r\n\r\n“A delightfully eager entertainer, they assail you with gag after gag, landing body blows that leave you gasping” ★★★★ Three Weeks \r\n\r\n★★★★ Scotsman \r\n★★★★ Fest\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sam Nicoresti: Baby Doomer.","instanceDates":"3 September-27 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"652403AMCMTDCJSDVPCBDJRGVQTBRVMMC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-03T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-03T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-27T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-27T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Santi and Naz are bestest-best friends living in a village in pre-partition India. One Sikh, one Muslim; they have little understanding of how religion will divide them. \r\nAs partition draws closer, the girls remain oblivious to the spreading social unrest and violence. They’re too busy stealing books, swimming in the lake and spying on Rahul (the local hottie). When Naz is betrothed to a tailor from the soon-to-be capital of Pakistan the threat of separation for the young women looms on the horizon. Bound by their love for each other we learn how far they will go to avoid the inevitable. \r\nSanti & Naz explores female friendship, coming of age, and coming out set against the backdrop of a country soon to be changed forever. \r\nRecipient of the Fringe Society’s Keep It Fringe Fund and Winner of the Charlie Hartill Fund 2023\r\n12+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Santi & Naz","instanceDates":"21 January-8 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"572203AVJCLRPBQVHKGJRNMQNCBVMDBJR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-21T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-21T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-08T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-08T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"A contemporary thriller with ancient roots. When a woman tells a lie to her girlfriend, a seed is planted that starts to grow in the darkness. Now roots are cracking up through the pavement and branches are coming in at the windows, and - as she starts to see things that no one else can - she becomes the focus of some seriously unwanted attention. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"SAP by Rafaella Marcus","instanceDates":"3 April-22 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"432603AMCHPQTVBBMNNDKVTSNSDCTGQTN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-03T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-03T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-22T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-22T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Sapan turned 35, became a father and also got high in Amsterdam - all within a year, but not particularly in that order. \r\nHe is cruising through life with mental burnout, a needless sense of superiority over Gen-Z and of course, chronic lower back pain.\r\nCome watch him have a meltdown on stage - and feel better about your own life.\r\n\r\nAudiences have called this show \"hilarious\", \"so fresh and likeable\" and \"where are we going for dinner now\" according to Sapan who has been hearing these people from behind the curtains as they leave afterwards.\r\nDebuts his new stand-up show in London, get your tickets for Sapan’s hilarious new hour of stand-up before they sell out and he becomes insanely famous and inaccessible - a mild threat he's been using since 2011.\r\n\r\n‘Engaging and entertaining with mass appeal.’ \r\n**** One4Review\r\n‘Combining goofy and self-deprecating humour with sharp insights into middle class Indian life.’ \r\n**** Wee Review\r\nPerformed in English (70%) and Hindi (30%).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sapan Verma: Lower Back Pain","instanceDates":"27 May-31 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"605603ACDJGRTPCLKPDBDTBHVDTJGDPBM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-27T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-27T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-31T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-31T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"India/South Asian heritage"},{"description":"After a sold-out debut Edinburgh Fringe run, catch India's stand-up star Sapan Verma live at Soho Theatre.\r\nA veteran of shows across the globe, Sapan’s killer observations and hilarious storytelling have seen him open for Coldplay and Jay-Z at India’s Global Citizen Festival, headline the first ever Indian comedy showcase at Melbourne International Comedy Festival, and train celebrities to perform comedy on two sensational seasons of his show One Mic Stand (Amazon Prime). \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sapan Verma: Shame on Me","instanceDates":"14 March-16 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"529603ADBGSKMPSSPKCTMRGVMVMTPGMPD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-14T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-14T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-16T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-16T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Catch India's stand-up star Sapan Verma live for the first time at the Edinburgh Fringe.\r\nA veteran of shows across the globe, Sapan’s killer observations and hilarious storytelling have seen him open for Coldplay and Jay-Z at India’s Global Citizen Festival, headline the first ever Indian comedy showcase at Melbourne International Comedy Festival, and train celebrities to perform comedy on two sensational seasons of his show One Mic Stand (Amazon Prime). His Edinburgh Fringe debut is not to be missed.\r\n\r\n16+ recommended","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sapan Verma: Shame on Me – Edinburgh Preview","instanceDates":"24 July-28 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"472403ABQJGVLRSVTSNBDKTGJNBRRCJTC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-24T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-24T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-28T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-28T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Comedy"},{"description":"Catch India's stand-up star Sapan Verma live at Soho Theatre following his debut Edinburgh Fringe run.\r\nA veteran of shows across the globe, Sapan’s killer observations and hilarious storytelling have seen him open for Coldplay and Jay-Z at India’s Global Citizen Festival, headline the first ever Indian comedy showcase at Melbourne International Comedy Festival, and train celebrities to perform comedy on two sensational seasons of his show One Mic Stand (Amazon Prime). \r\n\r\n16+ recommended","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sapan Verma: Shame on Me .","instanceDates":"31 August-2 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"477003AKGNBTRSCNTDPJHMRTNTJMRJRJD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-31T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-31T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-02T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-02T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Edinburgh Comedy Award nominee, Sara Barron (Would I Lie to You?; Live at the Apollo) has a new show that's fierce, savage and other adjectives from RuPaul's Drag Race. \r\nThe clock is ticking, and the questions aren't cute anymore: is it your fault you're angry? Are you too old to blame your mum? And why is she angry? Can we get some grief pie? No one's died, but we're exhausted. Do not sashay gentle into that good night.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sara Barron: Anything For You","instanceDates":"26 March-29 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"600403ACKBRGMRQVPPJPRTHDNPKCPGNSK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-26T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-26T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-29T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-29T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join Sara Pascoe and some famous friends for an unmissable night of stand-up comedy in aid of Write Back - an East London charity that helps young people rewrite their story.  \r\nSara Pascoe, alongside some well-known comedy friends, presents a night of big laughs in the Soho Theatre Walthamstow.  \r\nHost Sara Pascoe is an award-winning author, actress and comedian seen and heard on Taskmaster, Live at the Apollo, The Great British Sewing Bee, Last One Laughing UK, QI, Mock the Week, Last Woman on Earth and many others. She is also the author of Animal, Sex Power Money and Weirdo as well as the co-host of the podcast Sara & Cariad’s Weirdos Book Club. \r\nIn 2025, Sara became the first ever patron of Write Back – an East London charity helping young people to find their voices and tell their stories. Write Back runs storytelling programmes in schools and youth centres to help teenagers develop their ideas, build their confidence and publish their stories. Our first ever comedy night in April 2026 raised enough money for two transformative storytelling programmes. So, join us for the comedy, and leave knowing you helped more young people find their voice. Line up may vary. 14+ guidance.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":140,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sara Pascoe & Friends","instanceDates":"2 May-2 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"757203ASTQQBSJHTBNPTHQMBRVMJPPHBR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-05-02T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-05-02T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-05-02T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-05-02T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"An unforgettable night of stand-up comedy with Sara Pascoe and friends in aid of Write Back – a small charity making a big difference for young people in East London.\r\nSara Pascoe presents an unmissable night of hilarious comedy complete with some well-known friends at Soho Theatre Walthamstow. \r\nHost Sara Pascoe is an award-winning author, actress and comedian seen and heard on Taskmaster, Live at the Apollo, The Great British Sewing Bee, Last One Laughing UK, QI, Mock the Week, Last Woman on Earth and many others. She is also the author of Animal, Sex Power Money and Weirdo as well as the co-host of the podcast Sara & Cariad’s Weirdos Book Club. \r\nIn 2025, Sara became the first ever patron of Write Back – an East London charity helping young people to find their voices and tell their stories. Write Back runs storytelling programmes in schools and youth centres to help teenagers develop their ideas, build their confidence and publish their stories. Come for the laughs, and leave knowing you helped a good cause. \r\nLine up may vary.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":140,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sara Pascoe & Friends Apr26","instanceDates":"20 April-20 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"695603ATMVDKSSKDBSQLPJMSTDQVCKLJH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-20T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-20T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-20T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-20T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"In her new solo show, Sara Schaefer teaches you how to unlock your potential in this fake(?) seminar about defeating your hecklers, developing your TS (thick skin) and achieving total perfect comedy success. No matter your walk of life, you can make your dreams come true simply by Going Up!\r\n\r\n\r\n“Schaefer herself has done spectacular work in almost every discipline of comedy and almost on every level, and now, with that wealth of experience and acclaim, is doing a perfectly biting satirical solo show on ‘how to become a comedian’.”\r\n- The Comedy Bureau\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSara Schaefer is a critically acclaimed stand-up comedian, writer, and artist. Her Comedy Central Stand Up Presents half hour special debuted in November 2019 and she was the co-host of MTV’s late night show Nikki & Sara Live. Her stand-up show Little White Box debuted to a sold-out run at the 2017 Edinburgh Fringe Festival. Sara published her first book, Grand, in 2020 with Simon & Schuster imprint Gallery Books. She hosts a podcast called The Schaefer Shakedown.\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sara Schaefer: Going Up","instanceDates":"29 August-30 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"472203ACKSQLLCSTMDVRTNHHNJHKRSJLM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-29T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-29T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-30T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-30T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Comedy"},{"description":"Following a sold out run at Soho Theatre, Keyworth brings their joyous new show to EartH Hackney…\r\nFollowing a sold out run at Soho Theatre, Sarah Keyworth has added a new London date for their joyous new show about family, acceptance and a pair of big (well, not super big) losses. \r\n\r\nStar of BBC Radio 4’s Are You A Boy Or A Girl, BBC’s Live At The Apollo and Mock The Week, Channel 4’s 8 Out of 10 Cats and many more.\r\n\r\nPlease note that this show is taking place at EartH Hackney, not Soho Theatre. Seating is unallocated.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sarah Keyworth: My Eyes Are Up Here @ EartH Hackney","instanceDates":"19 September-19 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"534003AQQQBHCLVTGCKBMGVGVCRLRNCJM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-19T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-19T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-19T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-19T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"EartH Hackney","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Sarah Keyworth is performing, for the last time, this award-winning, joyous show about family, acceptance and a pair of big (well, not super big) losses.\r\nWINNER: Most Outstanding Show at Melbourne International Comedy Festival 2024 \r\n\r\nNOMINEE: Edinburgh Comedy Award Best Show 2024 \r\n\r\nPlease note that this performance is being professionally filmed for a stand-up comedy special. By entering the venue, you acknowledge that your image, voice, and likeness may appear in the final production.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sarah Keyworth: My Eyes Are Up Here Live Special Recording","instanceDates":"2 December-3 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"667603APDJQJJMDNBCDJPQQTCQDJJVVRM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-02T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-02T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-03T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-03T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"To kick off an international tour, Keyworth returns to Soho Theatre with a joyous new show about family, acceptance and a pair of big (well, not super big) losses.\r\nStar of BBC Radio 4’s Are You A Boy Or A Girl, BBC’s Live At The Apollo, BBC’s Mock The Week, Channel 4’s 8 Out of 10 Cats and many more.\r\n\r\nDirected by Jet Vevers.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sarah Keyworth: My Eyes Are Up Here.","instanceDates":"26 February-9 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"519604AVVLCTNCGKKCKRSSTPHPHSQQPBM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-26T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-26T21:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-09T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-09T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Sarah Roberts is the world's youngest, smallest, most normal comedian. She's been condemned to live a thousand lives. Now she's being reborn as the person she hates most: herself. \r\nDirected by Daniel Emery and Molly Stacey\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sarah Roberts: Silkworm","instanceDates":"22 April-23 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"594203AMNQKDKBTCLNPTQVRBVHRSTSHSN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-22T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-22T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-23T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-23T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Schalk Bezuidenhout is back with a brand new show. His first and (hopefully, for the love of all things good) only show post-divorce.\r\nSchalk hasn’t checked in with you all in sometime and he wants to talk to you. Actually… he NEEDS to talk to you! Why? Because it’s cheaper than therapy. That’s why! ‘Rapid-fire gags and manic energy. Highly recommended.’ ★★★★ - The Age. 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Schalk Bezuidenhout: Hey Hey Divorcè","instanceDates":"12 April-17 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"758603AHKHVKQCTCGJVQSKVGTJMTJQDPP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-04-12T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-04-12T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-04-17T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-04-17T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Schalk Bezuidenhout is fresh from his Netflix Stand Up Special, and although it's not his first time to London, he now embarks on his debut UK Tour with love in his heart and jokes in his pocket. Many say that this brand-new show is... funny. I mean, what else can we say? It's a comedy show. You will laugh. It's as easy as that. 'Fast-rising talent’ Guardian ‘Definitely one to watch’ Evening Standard 'His joke-telling is superb... pure and simple stand-up, expertly performed' (Chortle)\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Schalk Bezuidenhout: I’ll Make Laugh to You","instanceDates":"9 May-13 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"431403AVLPNVSQHCCQKSSQJKRMTMVQTKD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-09T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-09T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-13T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-13T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Newly married, Schalk feels older, wiser and much more mature (possibly), but all he wants is to stay \"hip with the youth\". Can he do it? Can he Keep Up?\r\n\r\nAs seen on Netflix and Comedy Central and fresh from supporting Trevor Noah on his arena tour.\r\n\r\n'Fast-rising talent' (Guardian).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Schalk Bezuidenhout: Keeping Up","instanceDates":"26 October-28 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"577803ASTHMCKJGLHTKKLKTBCHJVLVBMD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-26T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-26T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-28T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-28T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"One family, one condition, one hell of a hairy baby… \r\nScott Bennett (from Live at the Apollo and The News Quiz) tells the amazing true story of how his daughter fell ill with a rare genetic condition, congenital hyperinsulinism (CHI). Never heard of it?  Neither had Scott and Jemma.\r\n\r\n‘What’s so rare and satisfying is how all the jokes go hand in hand with the seriousness of the situation. It’s a wonderfully hopeful, often hilarious show from a properly funny man’  The Times ★★★★\r\n\r\nYes, it’s a story about an ill baby, but it’s a very funny one with a happy ending, as new parents Scott and Jemma fight to get the right diagnosis for their daughter and are plunged into months of bewildering treatment, sleepless nights, celebrity encounters and bizarre side effects.\r\n\r\n'Comedy's best kept secret' Evening Standard ★★★★\r\n\r\nAs heard on the Parenting Hell podcast.\r\n\r\nForthcoming TV/Radio includes The Royal Variety Performance and a Radio 4 Special.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Scott Bennett: Blood Sugar Baby","instanceDates":"7 May-10 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"584803AMRHNGTPNTSNPJCMRRPLBSBMSRQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-07T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-07T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-10T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-10T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Melbourne International Comedy Festival 2025 Most Outstanding Show nominee, Pinder Prize winner. \r\nStranded in regional Victoria without medication for the first time in 12 years, Scout pulls out all the psychological stops to survive the worst night of their life. An exquisite, darkly funny retelling of a harrowing mental marathon through manic withdrawal; Scout imagines life in the Middle Ages, trawls the strange crevices of the internet, makes peace with their own mediocrity and (briefly) surrenders to God. Part storytelling, part stand-up, all raw and unflinchingly real.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Scout Boxall: God’s Favourite","instanceDates":"4 September-5 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"725403ALJVJRNSCBGBKQMKDPRLDRKJGTN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-04T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-04T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-05T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-05T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Inside my skin is a rattling beast and when I breathe my last it will emerge. Free me from the enemy within. This is a show about fear, power and bones.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sean Morley: Soon I Will Be Dead And My Bones Will Be Free To Wreak Havoc Upon The Earth Once More","instanceDates":"24 April-26 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"606003ATMGDGCCMGVTJNSGCDTPTHQDNSS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-24T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-24T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-26T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-26T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"After an extended sell-out run the legendary Ghost-Whisperer returns and this time it's a witch trial! It's time to figure out which witch is which? Will everyone's favourite co-medium survive? Will she literally give up the Ghost? One thing is for certain: she simply must be hung! A bewitching night of mystical debauchery, cabaret ballads and camp theatrics. Join Séayoncé and murderous accomplice Leslie-Ann for a hexceptional evening where we raise the stakes... and burn the witch. You're spell-bound to be scared stiff. Created by prominent queer comedian Dan Wye.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Séayoncé She Must Be Hung!","instanceDates":"4 June-7 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"629203ABKGDDJMDSPMHSLKQCNSRSVLVVP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-04T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-04T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-07T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-07T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"The legendary Ghost Whisperer is back! Award winning, critically acclaimed comedy cabaret sensation Séayoncé…and this time it’s a witch trial! It’s time to figure out which witch is which? Will everyone’s favourite co-medium survive? Will she literally give up the Ghost? One thing is for certain she simply must be hung! A hilarious bewitching night of mystical debauchery, cabaret ballads, and camp theatrics. Join Séayoncé (aka rising queer star Dan Wye) and her murderous accomplice Leslie-Ann (aka musical genius Robyn Herfellow)… for a hexceptional evening where we raise the stakes…and burn the witch. You’re spell-bound to be scared stiff!\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":65,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Séayoncé She Must Be Hung!.","instanceDates":"30 April-17 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"537804AMTTGKKDNCPMLRJTSNJVKVJVQDS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-30T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-30T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-17T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-17T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Drag","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"The baddest b!tch in the spirit world is back, the legendary Ghost Whisperer Séayoncé! What better way to feel alive again than with a big throbbing res-erection? Ghouls just want to have fun... it's time you did too! A desperate soul haunts Soho theatre and no, not an out of work actor at the bar... it's time for a little exorcism. Séayoncé has already seen the future and it’s going to be an occult classic! Created by Dan Wye, rising queer star on the comedy scene. ★★★★★ - Deadline “It’s a hilarious, outrageous, and fabulously queer show” ★★★★★ - Wee review “hilarious” ★★★★ - Culturefix “Razor-sharp…Wye’s creation is a wonderful one” ★★★★ - EdinburghLive “Sensational… the audience were in stitches throughout” ★★★★ - EdfestMeg “A Super fun and interactive journey through the realms of the living and the dead funny” ★★★★★ - LGBTQArtsReview \"A sharp edge of wit...I found myself hoping for it to last longer.\"\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":65,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Séayoncé: Res-Erection","instanceDates":"2 May-6 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"458203AHRVBNJBLDMHHVCBMTTKMKRSPRQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-02T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-02T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-06T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-06T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Drag","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"A Graeae production in association with Soho Theatre and Theatr Iolo. \r\n\r\nSelf-Raising\r\n\r\nWritten by Mike Kenny & Jenny Sealey\r\nPerformed by Jenny Sealey\r\nDeveloped with The Incubator at The Egg, Theatre Royal Bath\r\n\"It starts with a secret, but this one's different, this one's mine.\"\r\nGraeae’s award-winning Artistic Director Jenny Sealey has spent a lifetime championing stories by Deaf and disabled artists. Now she takes to the stage to tell her own story. Unravelling the past and facing the future, Self-Raising is a blisteringly honest, laugh-out-loud one-woman show about growing up deaf in a family with secrets. \r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Self-Raising","instanceDates":"6 February-17 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"511203AKDDNQKLNVVVQLTBDNNPTKHNBSH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-06T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-06T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-17T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-17T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Access","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"Processing Soho Theatre allocation for Sh!t Theatre Or Whats Left Of Us at Summerhall. ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sh!t Theatre Summerhall 24","instanceDates":"17 August-25 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"566003AHSJNSVKTPKCGMRSSCNPBJTNMKN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-17T16:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-17T15:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-25T16:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-25T15:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Theatre for the masses that forces culture and critique through the clown horn of queer slapstick.\r\nCreated by Silky Shoemaker, Lex Vaughn and Paul Soileau, SHABOOM! is a spectacle teetering at the edge of disaster. Sharing a mind of anarchy and absurdity, they create environments and actions of pleasure and liberation. \r\n\r\nSHABOOM! is not just an experiment with failure, but a jubilant funeral procession for the notion of success, driven by maddening determination and an impressive lack of good judgement. SHABOOM! is theatre for the masses that forces culture and critique through the clown horn of queer slapstick.\r\n\r\nSilky Shoemaker is an artist from central Pennsylvania. She makes\r\nwork that explores queer community in its many despairs and ecstasies, solitudes, strangeness, and epic iterations. Recent activity includes solo shows at Art Yard in Frenchtown, NY and LAST projects in LA, and dancing backup with post gender punk Christeene at the Barbican in London.\r\n\r\nLex Vaughn is a multi-disciplinarian artist living in Los Angeles. Her\r\nwork revolves around queer absurdity and butch visibility through\r\nperformance, installation, video, and novelty items. Lex is one half of the multi-media gross-out duo, FFTWINZ, with Beth Schindler, whose focus is creating spaces and content for like minded gaywads. Lex has also been a drummer for several bands, including Lesbians on Ecstasy, co-directed and starred in Peaches’ music video Rub, and has a terrible ventriloquist act: Graham and Diane.\r\n\r\nPaul Soileau is a performer and artist manipulating and perverting\r\nthe realms of gender, identity, and good taste. He is best known for his\r\npersonas CHRISTEENE and Rebecca Havemeyer. Paul’s work has been presented in spaces ranging from The Barbican Centre in London to The Parkside Lounge in NYC. He has collaborated with, as well as performed with, numerous acclaimed musicians including Faith No More, Peaches, Fever Ray, John Grant, Kembra Pfahler, Suicide, David Hoyle and Marc Almond. He resides with his cat, Tickles Pickles, in Brooklyn, NY.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"SHABOOM!","instanceDates":"11 June-14 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"624603AGTQJBBPTKVVVNHGGBBPBGBLQTD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-11T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-11T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-14T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-14T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Theatre"},{"description":"Step into the hypnotising world of Shafeeq Shajahan with a cabaret odyssey that peels back layers of his Muslim heritage.\r\nAn homage to the 1978 Bollywood film, 'Satyam Shivam Sundaram' is a contemporary exploration of identity and metamorphosis, celebrating the journey of reconnecting with a home left behind. In collaboration with Cypriot composer Vasilis Konstantinides, the duo fuse world music to mirror the sagas of their ancestry with iconic cinematic references. Inspired by the sultry rebellion of Bollywood actresses like Zeenat Aman, Shafeeq's queer, Muslim voice cuts through the cacophony of an increasingly alienating world. \"Satyam, Shivam, Sundaram'' is an enlightening musical journey, revealing the truths, godliness, and beauty that unite us all.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Shafeeq Shajahan: Satyam Shivam Sundaram","instanceDates":"10 February-17 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"522003APQKJPGKHLTJQLGGBQQMJRRHKRL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-10T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-10T22:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-17T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-17T22:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Hell hath no fury like a Bollywood Diva scorned! - Triple-threat SHAFEEQ SHAJAHAN and musical genius VASILIS KONSTANTINIDES are back with a raucous new cabaret.\r\nTriple-threat SHAFEEQ SHAJAHAN and musical genius VASILIS KONSTANTINIDES are back with a raucous new cabaret.\r\nIn an unapologetically queer tour-de-force, the pair blend old Bollywood glamour, Indian classical music, and a sick disco beat to tell an age-old tale of sweet, sweet redemption. Enter Shafeeq’s queer, Muslim world, depicting risqué reflections on the men who have failed him, while Vasilis dazzles on the piano with haunting melodies that reimagine his scars.\r\nHell hath no fury like a Bollywood Diva scorned!\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Shafeeq Shajahan: The Bollywood Guide To Revenge","instanceDates":"1 April-5 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"603403AJJLNPBQDNGCCVCBTPJGLVQTHVV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-01T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-01T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-05T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-05T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"India/South Asian heritage"},{"description":"Shamik is the latest voice to break out from the burgeoning comedy scene in India. He returns to Soho following his Edinburgh Fringe debut with his dry wit and laid-back rants. Namaste.\r\nNever judge a book by its cover. Not many people know this, but that sentence is an idiom and not really about books. It literally means – never judge a person by their face. Take the above face for example. You might think it belongs to a sensible man, a practical man. You’d be wrong. He’s not the responsible older sibling. He’s not good at chess. He’s not a nerd. At least, not in a useful way. \r\n\r\nHe’s a scatterbrained only child who dreams of doing nothing and relies on his stand-up career to sustain that dream. Despite Appearances is an effort to put things right and break away from shallow, face-driven stereotypes. But you should just watch it for a laugh.\r\n\r\nShamik Chakrabarti is nothing short of a comedic force of nature, a stand-up sensation, and a literary maverick who’s taking over the world of humor, one punchline at a time! With the precision of a surgeon and the audacity of a rockstar, Shamik effortlessly slices through the absurdities of everyday life, leaving his audiences in stitches. \r\n\r\nIn the Indian comedy scene, Shamik isn’t just carving a niche—he’s bulldozing his way to the top with an observational style that resonates with everyone, from wise grandmothers to rebellious teenagers. When he’s not conquering stages, Shamik transforms into a writing wizard, contributing to top-tier television shows with writing so insightful - it could double as life advice. Balancing the stage and the pen like an artistic ninja, Shamik Chakrabarti is a one-man comedy revolution, unstoppable and undeniably hilarious! \r\n\r\nMost importantly, he’s a nice guy. \r\n\r\nHe has authored many gems, but this bio is not one of them. This has been written by Chat GPT, with a little bit of coaxing. The nice guy line was all him.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Shamik Chakrabarti: Despite Appearances","instanceDates":"26 August-30 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"634603ATTJDKBVNGSVHSVJRGCBKMVVKDQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-26T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-26T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-30T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-30T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Shamik is the latest voice to break out from the burgeoning comedy scene in India. He makes his international debut in 2025 with his dry wit and laid-back rants. Namaste.\r\nNever judge a book by its cover. Not many people know this, but that sentence is an idiom and not really about books. It literally means – never judge a person by their face. Take the above face for example. You might think it belongs to a sensible man, a practical man. You’d be wrong. He’s not the responsible older sibling. He’s not good at chess. He’s not a nerd. At least, not in a useful way. \r\n\r\nHe’s a scatterbrained only child who dreams of doing nothing and relies on his stand-up career to sustain that dream. Despite Appearances is an effort to put things right and break away from shallow, face-driven stereotypes. But you should just watch it for a laugh.\r\n\r\nShamik Chakrabarti is nothing short of a comedic force of nature, a stand-up sensation, and a literary maverick who’s taking over the world of humor, one punchline at a time! With the precision of a surgeon and the audacity of a rockstar, Shamik effortlessly slices through the absurdities of everyday life, leaving his audiences in stitches. \r\n\r\nIn the Indian comedy scene, Shamik isn’t just carving a niche—he’s bulldozing his way to the top with an observational style that resonates with everyone, from wise grandmothers to rebellious teenagers. When he’s not conquering stages, Shamik transforms into a writing wizard, contributing to top-tier television shows with writing so insightful - it could double as life advice. Balancing the stage and the pen like an artistic ninja, Shamik Chakrabarti is a one-man comedy revolution, unstoppable and undeniably hilarious! \r\n\r\nMost importantly, he’s a nice guy. \r\n\r\nHe has authored many gems, but this bio is not one of them. This has been written by Chat GPT, with a little bit of coaxing. The nice guy line was all him.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Shamik Chakrabarti: Despite Appearances.","instanceDates":"25 April-3 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"605403ATPDSBBRPQSKKBHQJHQDJNRRDVP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-25T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-25T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-03T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-03T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"New Tour. New Jokes. Shamik is back with a new show packed with his trademark dry wit and laid-back rants. \r\nA rising star on the burgeoning Indian stand-up scene, Shamik makes a welcome return to Soho following his hit debut run in 2025.   \r\n\r\nAs the driving force behind the ‘unstoppable rise of Indian comedy in the UK’ (The Guardian, May 2024), over the past decade Soho Theatre has introduced over 30 Indian artists to the UK, on stages ranging from Soho Theatre and Soho Theatre Walthamstow to the Royal Albert Hall. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Shamik Chakrabarti: Live","instanceDates":"13 July-18 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"706603AGMLJPHQBCPSBBDDJRVHGLGQNDH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-13T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-13T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-18T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-18T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Armed with his signature wit, razor-sharp storytelling, and a complete inability to take himself seriously, Shane is coming to Soho Theatre for the first time with his brand new stand up show.\r\nShane Todd hosts the massively popular Tea With Me podcast and performs in some of the world’s most famous comedy clubs, selling out venues in the UK, Ireland, Australia, Canada, and the Middle East. He holds the record for a solo performer in Belfast's legendary Grand Opera House with a twenty-four-night run.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Shane Todd: Hold Me Back","instanceDates":"12 March-14 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"642403AVLLGRRKVGGGGHBBGVQTVJRMQLG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-12T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-12T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-14T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-14T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Having reassessed her life through the prism of an ADHD diagnosis in last year's funny and moving memoir, one of Britain's most beloved and most scatterbrained stand-ups lets you back into her mind (warning: it's cluttered in there).\r\nAmong other things, this show will be a love-letter to letter-writing, a trip back through her early years as a comic and woman-about-town, and a whirlwind tour of a chaotic, hilarious brain.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Shaparak Khorsandi: Scatterbrain","instanceDates":"6 May-9 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"595803ALTNNNLVQSDNLCHMSJSHHPSSHMT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-06T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-06T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-09T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-09T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Having reassessed her life through the prism of an ADHD diagnosis in last year's funny and moving memoir, one of Britain's most beloved and most scatterbrained stand-ups lets you back into her mind (warning: it's cluttered in there). Among other things, this show will be a love-letter to letter-writing, a trip back through her early years as a comic and woman-about-town, and a whirlwind tour of a chaotic, hilarious brain.  \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Shaparak Khorsandi: Scatterbrain (Work in Progress)","instanceDates":"9 September-10 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"564803ACKHRKQLSMDBMKSHQVTNQDLNPCN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-09T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-09T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-10T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-10T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":""},{"description":"A brand-new show about Expectations, Identity and other DIRTY words. Shazia says 'If you look a certain way, talk a certain way, and joke about certain things, you get used to people saying what they think of you. Bring it on. But recently I was stunned when a man called me ‘a prude’, like that’s a bad thing!How is it that in 2027 being a prude has become a disgraceful slur? Something to be ashamed of, that we should want to deny? Shouldn't it be the other way round? Being a prude should be celebrated! Glorified! Rewarded!\r\nAs a Muslim girl in Birmingham, a teacher in East End schools, and a woman in showbiz, I've met them all, from prudes to pros to perverts, and trust me, I know what’s best. I’m coming out - prude and proud!' 14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Shazia Mirza: PRUDE! ","instanceDates":"25 March-25 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"755403ACVPRSJTJBPGMDHVSMHGNDPQBQB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-03-25T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-03-25T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-03-25T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-03-25T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Sheeps are working on their first NEW show in 6 YEARS and tickets are going fast. And we wrote this before they went on sale!\r\nYou learn it young. You know it as well as you know your own name. The cow goes moo. The dog goes dog. And the Sheeps boys? Well, they go straight to the top!\r\nDon’t wanna hear anybody crying about how the show was too funny. You’ve been warned. You know the risks going in.\r\nSheeps remain Al Roberts (Stath Lets Flats), Liam Williams (Ladhood) and Jonno (Seinfeld).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sheeps: The Giggle Bunch (That’s Our Name For You) (WIP)","instanceDates":"27 June-20 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"540403AGNLDHSBTBSBMDBQVDTLGPGQJVB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-27T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-27T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-20T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-20T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Work In Progress","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"In their last show, Hair, Shelf joked about being mistaken for teenage boys. Now, it’s time to grow up. It's time to stop being teenage boys and start being teenage men.\r\nThis new show from the 'easy to fall in love with' (Scotsman) double-act features anecdotes, songs, jokes about performing for kids, the Instagram algorithm, confronting your toxicity, and more. As seen on BBC3 and ITVX. Founders of the LOL Word. 'Nuanced and fresh' **** (Guardian). **** (Skinny). **** (FunnyWomen.com). **** (BeyondTheJoke.co.uk). **** (Scotsman).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Shelf: Teenage Men","instanceDates":"24 April-27 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"526203AMHRDLTCGRVLHKGSJJMQJVQTMNK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-24T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-24T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-27T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-27T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A dramatic comedy hour about drugs, murder and family. \r\nShenoah Allen’s electrifying new show plunges headlong into his wild New Mexican roots, unleashing acid-fueled tales of drugs, murder, and family with fearless comic bite.\r\nShenoah Allen grew up in an unconventional family — the grandson of a rocket engineer for the Apollo moon landing and an Air Force Colonel, and the son of a man who lived openly gay despite the Colonel’s disapproval. Around them, other relatives battled brain damage, addiction, and jail time, while his mother anchored the family with grit and warmth, raising three boys alongside her husband and his other partner under one roof.\r\nSchool wasn’t a good fit for Shenoah, he was suspended repeatedly, dropped out, and by thirteen was experimenting with LSD, punk, and goth culture while narrowly skirting the edges of gun violence and chaos.\r\nThat chaos becomes his comedy in Bloodlust Summertime. Transforming taboo subjects into sharp, fearless humor, Allen confronts societal norms and asks audiences to question their boundaries — all while inviting us to revel in the sheer madness of it.\r\nDirected by Kim Noble\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Shenoah Allen: Bloodlust Summertime","instanceDates":"18 February-21 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"678403ALMMHNGJJRPPPNDKCLKLKBVKVHL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-18T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-18T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-21T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-21T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Buckle up for an unapologetically raw and hilariously outrageous comedy experience with Shenoah Allen's electrifying new stand-up show.\r\nIn this boundary-pushing performance, Allen fearlessly dives into his wild New Mexican roots and delivers acid-fueled tales of sex, drugs and murder. Transforming taboo subjects into comedic gold, Shenoah confronts societal norms and challenges the audience to question their own boundaries while simultaneously inviting them to revel in the sheer madness of it all.\r\n\r\n‘I was doubled over in a kind of hysterical agony. I felt as if my lungs had migrated into my throat and that my anatomy would soon be inside out.’ Washington Post\r\n\r\nAs one half of the acclaimed comedy duo Pajama Men, Shenoah has received ***** from The Times, The Guardian, Time Out, Evening Standard, Irish Independent and The Scotsman.\r\n\r\nNote: this is a WORK IN PROGRESS and will doubtless be anarchic, but Shenoah reportedly can’t wait to share it with you. \r\n\r\nWARNING: this show contains sexual and violent material that some will find offensive or triggering.  16+.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Shenoah Allen: Bloodlust Summertime (WIP)","instanceDates":"5 March-5 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"527203AKQNLMJLVPDHKHMPMGSSTMLDPVQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-05T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-05T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-05T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-05T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join the award winning double-act for some sparkle, spice and spandex this Christmas. \r\n\r\nEnter their world of outrageous stand-up and sketch as they tell the unvarnished truth about motherhood. Is co-parenting better with a man cub or a lady love? Can you keep laughing as the nappies pile up? Just how badly can a pregnancy reveal go?\r\n\r\nCreators and hosts of MOTHERFUNK (Evening Standard’s Top 50 podcasts)\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Shirley & Shirley: Geriatric Mums","instanceDates":"23 December-23 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"515803ASRLLSNSGTLKSVMSBLGTLDVCTNL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-23T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-23T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-23T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-23T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The award winning double-act are back and feeling more geriatric than ever.\r\n\r\nEnter their world of outrageous stand-up and sketch as they tell the unvarnished truth about motherhood. Is co-parenting better with a man cub or a lady love? Can you keep laughing as the nappies pile up? Just how badly can a pregnancy reveal go?\r\n\r\nKnackered, jaded and clean out of cash, Shirley and Shirley have all the answers.\r\n\r\nCreators and hosts of MOTHERFUNK (Evening Standard’s Top 50 podcasts)\r\n“The punk-rock of comedy” Phill Jupitus, The Independent\r\n ★★★★ The List\r\n★★★★ Scotsgay\r\n★★★★ The Herald\r\n★★★★ Three Weeks\r\n★★★★ Broadway Baby\r\n Featured on: Sketchorama (BBC Radio 4), BBC Comedy Online, Bad Teeth (C4), Plebs (ITV2), The Increasingly Poor Decisions of Todd Margaret (C4), PhoneShop (E4), Marley’s Ghosts (Gold), Purge of Thrones (Netflix)\r\n\r\n16+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Shirley & Shirley: Geriatric Mums.","instanceDates":"22 August-22 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"465003AQDQDGSNTBNVCHNVHPRTQNJNBPD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-22T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-22T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-22T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-22T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Sketch","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Meet Shorty - a genre-questioning anti-fabulous non-binary drag-child!\r\nShorty frays at the edges and plays at the edges.\r\nThey have SO MANY things they would love to talk to you about but also show you but also are you watching are you watching are you watching?\r\nCategories don’t make sense\r\nSchool toilets are stupid\r\nSnacks are the best\r\nEveryone has a tantrum sometimes\r\n\r\nThis solo show from artist Hester Stefan Chillingworth is a joyful, urgent and delicate look at the experience of the trans child, the power of the introvert and the beautiful time we spend with our minds when the body is made awkward or under attack.\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Shorty by Hester Stefan Chillingworth","instanceDates":"5 June-10 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"471404ALGTDPDQBTSNLLVQBSJSTNNDQRM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-05T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-05T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-10T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-10T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"Come see some of the funniest new voices in comedy make their debut at the Showcase of our Stand Up Lab for Women from Muslim Backgrounds \r\n\r\nCome one, come all to see some of the freshest and boldest new artists of the comedy scene for one night only. Quick, before they’re all famous! \r\n\r\nThese 14 new comedians have been learning the ropes of Stand Up Comedy with the brilliant Esther Manito, self-proclaimed “Essex Arab Girl Comedian”, and with guests like the incredible Fatiha El-Ghorri and Isabelle Farah.  \r\n\r\nNow, they’re ready to share their smashing comedy sets with the world. \r\n\r\nIf you like comedy, fancy a good night out, or are interested in applying to the Labs yourself, come through and see what it’s all about. \r\n\r\nPlease note this will be taking place in our beautiful Studio 1 of Soho Theatre Walthamstow. There will be alcohol-free drinks and snacks available to purchase.  \r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Showcase: Stand Up for Women from Muslim Backgrounds","instanceDates":"21 July-21 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"736003ADRQSHBJKRPVRNNPQBHLCCSSLPC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-21T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-21T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-21T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-21T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Studio 1","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":""},{"description":"4+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"SHOWSTOPPER! THE CHRISTMAS KIDS SHOW (2025)","instanceDates":"6 December-14 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"651603ANCRRSJRJTLCLPLJTSBPMHQNQRB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-06T11:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-06T11:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-14T15:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-14T15:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Families","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"They're back! After a hit run at Christmas last year, the Showstopper Kids' Show bursts back on to the Walthamstow stage for an October half-term treat with their interactive musical comedy for kids! If your children could create their very own dream musical, where would they start?\r\nFrom their imaginations onto the stage – everything is made up entirely from audience suggestions, but grown-ups please take heed: we ONLY take suggestions from kids!","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Showstopper! The Kids Show ","instanceDates":"28 October-31 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"744403ATQHJQTVMNTDHSLKJBCJCTDDCLB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-28T14:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-28T14:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-31T14:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-31T14:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Families","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Famous for her straight face and animated hands, Shreeja Chaturvedi makes her Soho Theatre debut with her new show. \r\nIn her new trial hour, Shreeja seems to be angrier than usual. She jokes a little too freely about confrontations - we can only hope these are jokes.\r\n\r\nFamous for her straight face and animated hands, Shreeja has been active in the Mumbai circuit for over 7 years. She was a top 10 contestant of Comicstaan Season 2 and stars in the Amazon Prime Video special Stand Up Shorts. Alongside numerous TV writing credits, she has become a roast regular, having worked on far too many of them including Netflix’s Roast Battle for Darlings with Vijay Varma, The Roast of Zomato, The AJIO office takeover and Amazon Prime Video’s Roast of Urfi Javed.\r\n\r\nPerformed in Hindi\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Shreeja Chaturvedi","instanceDates":"26 March-28 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"586604ACKGLRRJSKGMGBKTBTJTCPPQHSM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-26T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-26T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-28T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-28T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Can pole dancing cure your existential dread?\r\n\r\nAfter a 5-star run of the Edinburgh Fringe Festival, pole dancing comedian Siân Docksey brings her genre-smashing hour to Soho Theatre. Prepare for a “beautifully untethered” (Edinburgh Festivals Magazine) collision of stand-up and stick-dangling through climate angst, politics, absurdism and tax advice.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Siân Docksey: Pole Yourself Together!","instanceDates":"21 June-22 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"537603ALDGLBLVDGKDRHDTJBQQHTRBLTS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-21T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-21T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-22T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-22T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"After a sell out run at the Edinburgh Fringe 2025, Award-winning character comedians and IRL Sisters, Maddy and Marina Bye (Byes), are back. Finally, their research is complete and you get the first glimpse into their incredibly innovative invented invention. This is sketch comedy gone subconscious. Set your alarms and see Siblings swoop into the surreal world of your sleeping minds as they crack open your brains and backflip in. Gird your loins for a knock(ed) out hour of absurd, raucous and down right delirious comedy, you bunch of dreamers! \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Siblings: Dreamweavers","instanceDates":"24 February-28 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"662603ADMGBJPPVSJRRGVPHLJRBDGBHDC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-24T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-24T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-28T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-28T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Sketch","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Award winning standup comedian Sid Singh has spent the last seven years doing comedy in Europe and raising money for asylum seekers in America. But with the world increasingly falling apart, this year he finally got so burnt out that he moved to Barcelona and did the dumbest thing you can do: he went on a date with his stalker. You are not prepared for what happens next. And trust me: whatever you think happens, it’s much dumber. 16+ (References to sexual and/or domestic violence, racism, cultural and/or political issues, mental health issues, death)","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sid Singh: Love Bombing","instanceDates":"6 November-6 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"758403APPMPRKKVBQVQDLLMKLVQCNLGJC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-06T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-06T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-06T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-06T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Following her highly acclaimed run at the Edinburgh Fringe, three-time Leicester Comedy Award nominee Sikisa heads to Soho Theatre with her second stand-up hour.\r\nThis time it’s personal, as she asks: why is it so hard to say the right things?\r\n\r\nAs seen and heard on Live at the Apollo (BBC), Jonathan Ross' Comedy Club (ITV) and the Off-Menu podcast.\r\n\r\nTour support for Kiri Pritchard-McLean and Catherine Cohen.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sikisa: Hear Me Out","instanceDates":"4 April-6 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"509204AVLTNTMTJQKSQMCGCGPPJJKKNJK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-04T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-04T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-06T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-06T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Comedy"},{"description":"Join the hilarious diva Sikisa for Serving Justice – a bold, thought-provoking hour exploring truth, identity, and what justice looks like in love and life. She dives into her love of wrestling, the pressure to have kids, and the realities of the immigration system – with a twist. As seen on Live at the Apollo and Off Menu. Host of WrestleClub UK podcast. Top 4 of Dave’s Joke of the Fringe 2023. Tour support for Judi Love, Michael Che, Ed Gamble and Catherine Cohen. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sikisa: Serving Justice","instanceDates":"20 April-21 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"680204ALTLCHHJKKLRCVGRQTCMVLGCNCH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-20T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-20T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-21T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-21T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Laugh! Cry! Applaud!\r\nIn 2018, Simon’s father performed a play about his imminent death to cancer and, to Simon’s horror, it was quite good. Now, directed by Fringe First winner Chris Larner, bouncing between genres and intertwined with footage of his late father’s show, Simon performs an hour so impressive that he’ll never be forgotten.\r\n\r\nWinner: Amused Moose Most Entertaining Show of the Edinburgh Fringe (2023)\r\nNominee: Chortle Best Variety Act (2024)\r\n18+ (full frontal nudity)","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Simon David: Dead Dad Show","instanceDates":"26 June-28 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"539603AJGLTDSPQBJGTRMHPNHLVTHQDCT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-26T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-26T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-28T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-28T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Fresh from a sold-out, critically acclaimed run at the Edinburgh Fringe, New York sketch troupe Simple Town is coming back across the pond. \r\n\r\nSimple Town combines smart ensemble riffing with dumb slapstick in one hard-hitting hour. They’ve toured their live show across the US, sold out two runs at the MOTH Club in London, and had their work appear on Adult Swim, Comedy Central, NoBudge, Cracked and more. \r\n\r\nTheir live show has played New York Comedy Festival and Netflix is a Joke Festival, and they now bring an hour of their best sketches to Soho Theatre. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Simple Town","instanceDates":"23 March-28 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"673803AVLCGKLSKRKHVKLDGPMTBBJSMDS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-23T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-23T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-28T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-28T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Sketch","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Sindhu Vee brings her critically-acclaimed, sell-out tour show, Alphabet, to Soho as she warms up for the filming of her next stand up special.\r\nSindhu has stormed Live at the Apollo (twice) and appeared on all of the top comedy TV shows, including: QI, Mock the Week, Have I Got News For You, The Last Leg and Would I Lie To You? \r\n\r\nShe also played Mrs Phelps in the smash hit Netflix feature film Matilda, is the star of forthcoming sitcom The Pradeeps of Pittsburgh for Amazon Freevee. Her other acting credits include Starstruck and Sex Education.  \r\n \r\nDon't miss this exceptional stand-up back on stage for two very special nights.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sindhu Vee: Alphabet (Work in Progress)","instanceDates":"1 February-5 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"528803ANGTVCBBDQKJJPPRQNSMQNLRDNN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-01T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-01T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-05T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-05T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Sindhu Vee is an award-winning comedian, writer, and actor. Straight from her hugely successful US tour ‘Sindhu Vee: Live’, tonight Sindhu performs new material ready for her new show. \r\nSince swapping a career in investment banking for one in comedy, Sindhu has fast become one of the most exciting and sought-after talents in comedy, across the UK, North America and India. She stars as Mrs Ohelps in Netflix’s in Matilda: The Musical and Amazon Prome’s latest comedy series The Pardeeps of Pittsburgh. Her latest stand-up special Alphabet will be available to stream soon.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sindhu Vee: Work in Progress","instanceDates":"13 January-3 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"593403AKPVMJSNVSMMNGKGCHQCSKBHHJT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-13T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-13T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-03T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-03T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Get ready to raise your voice and lower your inhibitions at Singalong with The Section.\r\nAs if our formidable Neon Nights line-up wasn’t enough…\r\nThis is a brand-new live karaoke night powered by the sensational musicians behind the critically acclaimed comedy troupe The Horne Section. \r\n\r\nTickets admit to Singalong with The Section only. To buy tickets to Neon Nights With Ed Gamble (including entry to karaoke after): \r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":180,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Singalong with The Section","instanceDates":"27 March-7 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"704003ACMTHHMPTBNCVLNTNGKVVDBLKHQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-27T23:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-27T23:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-07T23:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-07T22:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Music","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"Come and see participants of Soho Theatre’s Sketch Lab perform their hilarious fast-paced sketch show.\r\n\r\nThe comics have been working with Fran Bushe over 10 weeks to develop this new show, all written and performed by them. Strap in for an hour of giggles, for this one-off show, made by some of London’s freshest comics.\r\n\r\nIf you’re thinking about applying to the course yourself, come and see what it’s all about.\r\n16+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sketch Lab Sharing","instanceDates":"22 July-22 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"486603ANCTMVGRRLGCNMVBQSVJVQMBSTB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-22T16:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-22T15:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-22T16:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-22T15:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Sketch","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Come and see participants of Soho Theatre’s Sketch Lab perform their hilarious fast-paced sketch show.\r\n\r\nThe comics have been working with Fran Bushe over 10 weeks to develop this new show, all written and performed by them. Strap in for an hour of giggles, for this one-off show, made by some of London’s freshest comics.\r\n\r\nIf you’re thinking about applying to the course yourself, come and see what it’s all about.\r\n\r\n16+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sketch Lab Sharing apr23","instanceDates":"1 April-1 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"463403ANQVNJLCNPGTKCDNKBGDPLGRMQS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-01T16:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-01T15:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-01T16:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-01T15:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Description:\r\n(Age restrictions - blurb  performance warnings, e.g. haze/nudity/strobe)\tCome and see participants of Soho Theatre’s Sketch Lab perform their hilarious fast-paced sketch show.\r\n\r\nThe comics have been working with Fran Bushe over 10 weeks to develop this new show, all written and performed by them. Strap in for an hour of giggles, for this one-off show, made by some of London’s freshest comics.\r\n\r\nIf you’re thinking about applying to the course yourself, come and see what it’s all about.\r\n\r\n16+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sketch Lab Showcase Dec23","instanceDates":"9 December-9 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"509803ANSCJKRKCPDGKLSCQVVNLBGSNNK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-09T12:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-09T12:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-09T12:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-09T12:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Come and see participants of Soho Theatre’s Sketch Lab perform their hilarious fast-paced sketch show.\r\n\r\nThe comics have been working with Fran Bushe over 10 weeks to develop this new show, all written and performed by them. Strap in for an hour of giggles, for this one-off show, made by some of London’s freshest comics.\r\n\r\n16+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sketch Lab Showcase Mar24","instanceDates":"23 March-23 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"532003ATKCLGKVBQLSMGBCGSCTMJNCBDJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-23T12:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-23T12:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-23T12:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-23T12:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"The cult-hit East London comedy fiesta comes to Soho Theatre for a Valentine’s Day hornfest. With hosts Dom McGovern, Estefanía Baha, Kiran Saggu and some extra hot guests.\r\nPicture this: a comedy night where everyone is gorgeous. Audience included. YOU included.\r\nCult Hit comedy night Slay24 (no relation to Cult Hit film company A24) has been delighting audiences since first hitting London’s Comedy scene in November 2023. \r\nAnd now they bring their particular brand of sardonic chaos to Soho Theatre for a one night only Valentine’s Day love fest\r\nFunny, iconic, humble comedians Kiran Saggu, Dom McGovern and Estefania Baha deliver a perfectly curated lineup that is so gorgeous it will have you thinking: Am I in New York ACTUAL City?\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Slay24","instanceDates":"14 February-14 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"591803AJBVHQJNBJMMKDSSMGMQCNKCQMN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-14T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-14T22:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-14T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-14T22:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Description / copy\r\n\tOne of the UK’s most celebrated stand-up stars hosts a mixed bill of some of his favourite comedians. Expect dynamite storytelling and big laughs from some of the best acts on the UK circuit.\r\nAs seen on Live at the Apollo (BBC Two), The Russell Howard Hour (Sky One) and Black, British & Funny (C4). Tour support for both Kevin Hart and Dave Chappelle.\r\n\r\n9x WINNER OF BEST BLACK MALE COMEDIAN | BLACK ENTERTAINMENT AWARDS\r\n7x TOTAL SELL OUT TOURS\r\n6x SMASH HIT COMEDY SPECIALS\r\n\r\nLine-up:\r\nSlim \r\nRia Lina\r\nJunior Booker\r\nCurtis Walker\r\n\r\n16+ recommednation","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":105,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Slim’s Laughter Connoisseurs Apr23","instanceDates":"15 April-15 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"461203ASMHDQMVDTBRPHGRNBGGNLLKJNP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-15T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-15T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-15T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-15T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"To celebrate Black History Month, we welcome back one of the UK’s most celebrated stand-up stars for two nights of his incredible line-up show.\r\n\r\nHosted and curated by Slim, expect dynamite storytelling and big laughs from some of the best acts on the UK circuit.\r\n\r\nAs seen on Live at the Apollo (BBC Two), The Russell Howard Hour (Sky One) and Black, British & Funny (C4). Tour support for both Kevin Hart and Dave Chappelle.\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":105,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Slim’s Laughter Connoisseurs Black History Month Specials","instanceDates":"13 October-14 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"493603AKSHLLHBMGGPKCBKKTLKSKKGVNT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-13T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-13T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-14T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-14T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"One of the UK’s most celebrated stand-up stars hosts a mixed bill of some of his favourite comedians. Expect dynamite storytelling and big laughs from some of the best acts on the UK circuit.\r\nAs seen on Live at the Apollo (BBC Two), The Russell Howard Hour (Sky One) and Black, British & Funny (C4). Tour support for both Kevin Hart and Dave Chappelle.\r\n\r\n9x WINNER OF BEST BLACK MALE COMEDIAN | BLACK ENTERTAINMENT AWARDS\r\n7x TOTAL SELL OUT TOURS\r\n6x SMASH HIT COMEDY SPECIALS\r\n\r\nLine-up released soon!\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":105,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Slim’s Laughter Connoisseurs Jul23","instanceDates":"8 July-8 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"476403AGGBMRKSJNRDMQBSBHJTQJKSMSN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-08T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-08T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-08T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-08T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Join Vidya Divakaran on a raucous night out to the club-but she has the head of a slug.\r\nA surreal, absurd and intensely silly exploration into today's club culture through a masked lens (well, a literal slug mask). In this combination of clowning/stand-up/dance, experience the highs and lows of a night out like never before, and question what’s happened to dancing for dancing’s sake?\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Slug in a Club","instanceDates":"21 June-21 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"616603ACTLPSTRBJHRJHVHTGLGHVJVVPG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-21T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-21T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-21T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-21T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Sofie won Best Newcomer at the Edinburgh Festival in 2015 and she thinks you all stopped talking about it too soon.\r\nRemember TV? Yeah, she did that too. You may know her from that, but it's more likely you know her from the internet, where she's been both funny and angry at times.  \r\nSofie is from Denmark, but learned English at the age of 4, just so she could go to the UK in 2027 and do stand-up.  \r\nAnyways, despite being chronically online from 2016-2024, she never saw it coming that the fascists would be taking over. She did so many feminist tweets to prevent it. How can this be happening?  \r\nSofie has always tried to do the right thing, but now she has to ask herself: Did she do the right thing? And what will she say, with her last remaining freedom of speech? It better be good. She better be good.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sofie Hagen: I Think Some of This Is My Fault","instanceDates":"9 November-14 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"718803ASCNRLVSTDTKPDDDPHRGGHNMLDQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-09T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-09T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-14T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-14T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Soho Player Felicity Ward: Busting A Nut","instanceDates":"31 December-31 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"454803ABQCCJMVRNVRNBDNLTKGLMDQDVC","firstInstanceDateTime":"1930-12-31T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"1930-12-31T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"1930-12-31T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"1930-12-31T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Player","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":62,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Soho Player Jen Brister: Meaningless","instanceDates":"31 December-31 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"454603AMGHVKRGKMRPMPBPRCPSSBVBKJD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2030-12-31T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2030-12-31T20:00:00Z"