ibute_Venue":"Soho Player","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Soho Player: Jordan Brookes: Got Nothing","instanceDates":"31 December-31 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"453404AVRNGLDLHQKBPBTLJBVVNBCPTBC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2030-12-31T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2030-12-31T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2030-12-31T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2030-12-31T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Player","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Come and join this writing workshop to see if our Soho Theatre Walthamstow and British Pakistan Foundation Writers’ Lab might be for you! \r\n\r\nSoho Theatre Walthamstow is partnering with the British Pakistan Foundation to launch a brand-new talent development programme for aspiring writers from Pakistani backgrounds: the Soho Theatre Walthamstow and British Pakistan Foundation Writers’ Lab. \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nThis 8-session Lab will be running November – March, and applications are open September 19th – October 19th.  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nIf you’re curious about applying, but aren’t sure if this is for you, join us on Zoom for a taster session of fun and accessible exercises and chats, and see if you like it! \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nThe taster will be run by award-winning British-Pakistani writer Ishy Din (Shakespeare and Hathaway/BBC One, Ackley Bridge/Channel 4, John Barnes Saved My Life/BBC Radio 5 Live, Whose Baby/BBC Radio 4)   \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nAll participants from Pakistani backgrounds aged 18 – 35 are welcome.  \r\n\r\nAge: 18- 35","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow and British Pakistan Foundation Writers’ Lab Taster ","instanceDates":"2 October-2 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"661603ALMPBGGDPKQTQDNCHHDTPQQBQNM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-02T17:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-02T16:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-02T17:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-02T16:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Zoom","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Theatre"},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow Sneak Peek – Comedy Show 1","instanceDates":"26 April-26 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"623203AGSMNBDCPCTBBBRPKNQRVBCTRCK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-26T15:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-26T14:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-26T15:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-26T14:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":100,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow Sneak Peek – Comedy Show 2","instanceDates":"26 April-26 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"623003ATVCPMKTKGKMMMLRNKJPBCNVJPT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-26T17:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-26T16:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-26T17:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-26T16:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow is open to open its doors, and we want you to be amongst the first to step inside.\r\n\r\nFor our first Sneak Peek event we've lined up an hour of music on stage. You'll be able to explore the new space, purchase and enjoy our food a drink and catch one of the first shows on the brand new stage.\r\n\r\nWe're testing everything from the fire alarms to bar service, so we need your help to put it all through its paces. And there'll be a chance to feedback on your experience to help us fine-tune everything for the big launch in May.\r\n\r\nAnd as a big thanks, we're giving everyone that comes through the doors a Welcome Card as a thank you - so you'll be able to get 10% off at the bar, discounts on select shows until the end of October. You just need to turn up typo grab yourself one.\r\n\r\nSpots are limited to 4 people per booking.\r\n\r\nIf you can no longer make the event, please let us know so we can invite another pal to help us test the event.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow Sneak Peek - Music","instanceDates":"24 April-24 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"622803ACNHPNDNNLQLBKSSLCKBSLNPJGK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-24T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-24T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-24T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-24T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"An opportunity to come and see our gorgeously renovated new theatre, hear about the history of the building and the campaign that saved the theatre to bring it back to the Waltham Forest community.\r\n0+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow: Building Tours","instanceDates":"9 July-14 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"642203ACQTPNTPTJVPLBLJSDLNRSKCKCB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-09T12:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-09T11:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-14T11:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-14T10:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Gay & working class Soph Galustian is a gay born-and-bred poor, Mancunian comedian who is also gay and has Armenian heritage whilst being working class. \r\nDid she mention she’s gay and working class? She doesn’t like to bring it up. \r\nShe can currently be seen in Channel 4’s Everyone Else Burns.\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Soph Galustian: Hey Mammas","instanceDates":"12 February-12 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"524003ADJRDHBMSQGDGPRKNBGCCDVTDMT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-12T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-12T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-12T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-12T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Sophie Duker is BACK! The Taskmaster champ is back on tour and dealing with her (sugar) daddy issues in a hilarious new stand-up show.\r\nBUT DADDY I LOVE HER sees Sophie take the stage with her trademark naughtiness, this time arguing that we should all choose silliness over common sense and hot wet fantasies over cold, bleak reality. In this intentionally unhinged hour, delulu is the solulu.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":65,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sophie Duker: But Daddy I Love Her","instanceDates":"7 October-19 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"558003AHHRRLHBBNJPHLVBGCRDJGCCJDV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-07T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-07T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-19T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-19T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Taskmaster Champion, Edinburgh Comedy Award Best Newcomer Nominee and retired sugar daughter Sophie Duker is back with a brand-new stand-up tour, ‘Hot Beef Injection’. \r\n\r\nIn her latest hour, Sophie dares to get both sexy and political, reflecting on hypermasculinity, heavy-handed handymen and that old-chestnut Would You Rather: 'Man or Bear?’. \r\n\r\nHot Beef Injection reckons with the primal fear driving Duker’s distrust of heterosexual he/hims, and out of a challenging comedy club encounter a new question emerges: what would she say if she spoke to men, instead of shutting them out? ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sophie Duker: Hot Beef Injection","instanceDates":"26 October-7 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"741603APBPGHLRHQQGDJLBCNVKBGJLSTS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-26T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-26T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-07T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-07T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"BAFTA-nominated and double Edinburgh Comedy Award nominee brings his brand-new show back to Soho Theatre after it’s stellar Edinburgh run. As seen on Cats Does Countdown, Mind Of Herbert Clunkerdunk, Ted Lasso, Mr Winner, Live at the Apollo. A show for people who love dogs and for people who don’t. They’ll be all new characters, stupid songs, visual comedy, stories and maybe an answer to the question: Are dogs better than humans? **** (Guardian). ***** (Times). ‘The most insanely funny moments at the festival’ (Chortle.co.uk). 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Spencer Jones: Dogs","instanceDates":"7 December-23 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"746003AGKCHMNJTRRTRDPCRLJHLRRLHMP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-07T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-07T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-23T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-23T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"They’ll be all new characters, stupid songs, visual comedy, stories and maybe an answer to the question: Are dogs better than humans? \r\n\r\nAs well as two Edinburgh Comedy Award nominations, Spencer has also been seen on Cats Does Countdown, The Mind Of Herbert Clunkerdunk, Ted Lasso, Mr Winner, Live at the Apollo, and more. \r\n\r\nPraise for Spencer’s previous work: \r\n\r\n‘One of the silliest, most consuming shows of the Fringe’ ***** (Times) \r\n\r\n‘Gleefully madcap’ **** (Guardian) \r\n\r\n'Unadulterated dumb genius' [4.5 stars] Chortle \r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Spencer Jones: DOGS (June 2026)","instanceDates":"25 June-29 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"717803ARNKGRKTSTHKCKGMBHHNBSDTGTT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-25T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-25T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-29T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-29T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Work In Progress","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Double Edinburgh Comedy Award and double BAFTA-nominated professional idiot Spencer Jones is back with his brand-new show.\r\nThere will be aggressive chickens (not real ones, he’s not that weird), Devon based looped songs (whatever that is), cheap latex masks and a fair bit of Spencer talking. It will be funny. You should buy a ticket. He’s been on the telly, a little bit, if that’s your jam. \r\n\r\nStar of Mr Winner and The Mind of Herbert Clunkerdunk and as seen in Upstart Crow and Live at the Apollo (BBC), co-creator of Deep Fake Neighbours (ITV).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Spencer Jones: Making Friends","instanceDates":"10 April-20 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"535603ALNBCVLMPRBNJNPHHTTGHJRJKCH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-10T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-10T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-20T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-20T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The double Edinburgh Comedy Award nominee returns with a brand new show about moving to a new area, people he has met and losing his mind. There will be aggressive chickens (not real ones, he’s not that weird), Devon based looped songs (whatever that is), cheap latex masks and a fair bit of Spencer talking. It will be funny. You should buy a ticket. He’s been on the telly, a little bit, if that’s your jam.  Anyway, have a nice festival and if I don’t see you, make sure you behave yourself. Nice one. Cheers.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Spencer Jones: Making Friends – Edinburgh Preview","instanceDates":"19 July-22 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"474603AHCKCHTRQTGHTGRGCBBNRPRGHJQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-19T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-19T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-22T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-22T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Spilleth Thy Tea is an hour-long interactive comedy show that’s piping hot with laughter, scandal, and a little bit of chaos. Hosted by the hilarious duo Farah Sharp and Fathiya Saleh, expect a steamy blend of stand-up comedy and juicy audience confessions. These two aren’t just spilling the tea, they’re brewing it live on stage. Think part comedy show, part cheeky chat show, with belly laughs served throughout.\r\nFarah Sharp has been named ‘One to Watch’ in the Funny Women Stage Awards and a Finalist in their Content Creator Awards, featured on BBC Radio 4, and performed all over from The Royal Albert Hall to Latitude Festival, Leeds Festival, The Comedy Store and New York's Gotham Comedy Club.\r\nFathiya Saleh, a Funny Women finalist, has been described by Chortle as “an absolute delight”. With writing credits on Bad Education (BBC) and Horrible Science (BBC).\r\nTogether, Fathiya & Farah are ready to serve the hottest tea in town. So grab your mates, bring your most outrageous tales, and get ready to sip, spill, and cackle - because this is one show where the tea is always hot and never decaf. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Spilleth Thy Tea","instanceDates":"1 April-1 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"703003AMSSTBCDVKKLNBRPLDHTQMHHLDR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-01T18:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-01T17:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-01T18:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-01T17:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Lagahoo Productions present SPLINTERED\r\nWritten and directed by Emily Aboud\r\n\r\n★★★★★ “A fantastic night of festivity and foolery” The Guardian\r\n★★★★★ “Every bit as joyful and defiant as it is moving… A truly powerful piece of theatre” A Younger Theatre\r\n★★★★ “An explosion of a show” The Stage\r\n★★★★ “Bold, unabashed, energetic, fun and full of ideas” The Evening Standard\r\n\r\nPart-play, part-cabaret, join our three MCs as they take you through a queer whirlwind of Caribbean history,sad truths and joyful lies.\r\n\r\nHow do you deal with coming out joyfully in a homophobic culture? Join us and find out!\r\n\r\nCarnival is a festival despite and in spite of oppression. We Caribbean people celebrate through hard times, and here we are, celebrating - trying to unpack what it means to be queer in a place where it is outlawed. A dazzling show based upon interviews with queer women from Trinidad & Tobago – this is SPLINTERED.\r\n\r\nExpect a form-breaking, joy-inducing cabaret with plenty wining and a f*cktonne of glitter – “come free up yuhself”\r\n\r\nImage credit: Holly Revell (Pictured: Soho Upstairs 2022 cast)\r\n\r\nTEAM:\r\n\r\nWriter & Director\t\t\t\tEmily Aboud\r\nSet & Costume Designer\t\t\tHazel Low\r\nSound Designer\t\t\t\t         Annie May Fletcher\r\nLighting Designer\t\t\t\tLaura Howard\r\nProducer\t\t\t\t\tGrace Dickson\r\nAssistant Producer to Grace Dickson\t     Rory Thomas-Howes\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Splintered","instanceDates":"18 April-29 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"434003AQQGHJNVHBVNDBBPRPDJJMCQKCL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-18T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-18T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-29T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-29T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"As seen on BBC's Live at the Apollo, American transplant Spring Day provides dark comedy for nice people.\r\n\r\nSpring joined a Christian cult at 13 years old and left 13 years later. She's never talked about it before because she didn't think you heathens would understand.\r\n\r\nWatch her recount why she joined, and how she escaped a growing fundamentalist Christian community that had become her whole world.\r\n\r\nExpect one hell of a coming-of-age story about finding faith as Spring explores the nature of cults and the role they play in our everyday lives.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Spring Day: Exvangelical","instanceDates":"7 January-8 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"585603AHQBLQLLTVHQHTDRMPKQCNSDPHB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-07T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-07T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-08T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-08T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Straight-off a critically acclaimed Edinburgh Fringe run. Popcorn Award shortlisted dark comedy SQUIDGE comes to Soho Theatre.\r\nDaisy, a reluctant teaching assistant, is assigned a young Irish traveller to help with his reading. Amid phone calls with her grieving mother, a sexy plumber and whale noises, she finds hope where she least expected it.\r\n\r\nSQUIDGE is the theatrical debut of award-winning screenwriter and actress Tiggy Bayley, a dark comedy about the flaws in our education system and finding love against all odds.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Squidge by Tiggy Bayley","instanceDates":"19 February-20 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"591403AGNQRLPMHMKJNGMHRRKVPPCGRNM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-19T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-19T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-20T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-20T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Fresh from taping their debut Netflix special, the incredible Stamptown returns to Soho Theatre Walthamstow for three more nights of mayhem.\r\nA raunchy, chaotic, totally one-of-a-kind spectacle, Stamptown features the most anarchic and wildly entertaining performance from around the world. \r\n   \r\nHosted by the bad boy of clown, Zach Zucker, this show has packed out rooms at Netflix Is A Joke, Just For Laughs, Glastonbury, SXSW, Lincoln Center, Edinburgh Fringe, Soho Theatre, Melbourne International Comedy Festival, O2 Arena and Off-Broadway in New York City. \r\n   \r\nPast acts include Neil Patrick Harris, Richard Kind, David Cross, Natalie Palamides, Richard Gadd, Mae Martin, Karen Gillan, Reggie Watts, Sarah Sherman, Jamie Demetriou, Cat Cohen, Lolly Adefope, Randy Feltface, Kemah Bob, Rachel Sennott, Sam Campbell and MORE!\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Stamptown","instanceDates":"2 November-3 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"752403AMVNCRMGTDDGCQPPGMVLQKVVJLK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-02T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-02T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-03T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-03T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"A raunchy, chaotic, full-on fever dream, Stamptown is 120 minutes of pure spectacle featuring the most anarchic and wildly entertaining performance from around the world.\r\nHosted by the bad boy of clown, Zach Zucker, this show has packed out rooms at Netflix Is A Joke. Just For Laughs, Glastonbury, SXSW, Edinburgh Fringe, Soho Theatre, Melbourne International Comedy Festival, O2 Arena and Off-Broadway in New York City.\r\n\r\nPast acts include David Cross, Aisling Bea, Neil Patrick Harris, Karen Gillan, Lolly Adefope, Reggie Watts, Bridget Christie, Jamie Demetriou, Cat Cohen, Richard Gadd, Mae Martin, Huge Davies, Kemah Bob, Sam Campbell, Rachel Sennott, Randy Feltface, Natalie Palamides and MORE!\r\n\r\nLineup subject to change.\r\n18+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":150,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Stamptown Holiday Spectacular","instanceDates":"12 December-13 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"665203AJJGPBJBHTGGGNMHLCBQQKNTRBG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-12T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-12T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-13T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-13T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Fresh from taping their debut Netflix special, the incredible Stamptown returns to Soho Theatre Walthamstow for three more nights of mayhem.\r\nA raunchy, chaotic, totally one-of-a-kind spectacle, Stamptown features the most anarchic and wildly entertaining performance from around the world.\r\n  \r\n Hosted by the bad boy of clown, Zach Zucker, this show has packed out rooms at Netflix Is A Joke, Just For Laughs, Glastonbury, SXSW, Lincoln Center, Edinburgh Fringe, Soho Theatre, Melbourne International Comedy Festival, O2 Arena and Off-Broadway in New York City.\r\n  \r\n Past acts include Neil Patrick Harris, Richard Kind, David Cross, Natalie Palamides, Richard Gadd, Mae Martin, Karen Gillan, Reggie Watts, Sarah Sherman, Jamie Demetriou, Cat Cohen, Lolly Adefope, Randy Feltface, Kemah Bob, Rachel Sennott, Sam Campbell and MORE!\r\n18+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Stamptown March","instanceDates":"3 September-5 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"705403AMBGDMPJCSMCLCPVKGJDPHNVLPC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-03T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-03T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-05T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-05T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"WINNER: Best Variety Show in London, Chortle Awards (2020) A raunchy, chaotic and full-on fringe experience, Stamptown is a late-night variety show featuring the best alternative performance on the international scene. Hosted by the bad boy of clown, Zach Zucker, this show has packed out shows at Edinburgh Fringe, Melbourne International Comedy Festival, Glastonbury and Off-Broadway in New York City. Past acts include David Cross, Aisling Bea, Joe Pera, Lolly Adefope, Neil Hamburger, Bridget Christie, Jamie Demetriou, Cat Cohen, Richard Gadd, Mae Martin, Kemah Bob, Please Don’t Destroy, Sarah Squirm, Rachel Sennott, Atsuko Okatsuka, Chris Gethard, Natalie Palamides and MORE! Lineup subject to change. STARS and QUOTES ✭✭✭✭ “One of the best curated and enjoyable experiences of the fringe” Fest Mag “The best late-night show on the festival circuit” Steve Bennett, Chortle “Raucous energy… The best live comedy cabaret” The Guardian ACCOLADES WINNER: Best Variety Show in London, Chortle Awards (2020)\r\n\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Stamptown. 23","instanceDates":"5 May-6 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"460403APHDMQBBCVLPHBBNSBLPMSVDSJB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-05T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-05T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-06T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-06T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Performance Art","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"WINNER: Best Variety Show in London, Chortle Awards (2020) \r\nA raunchy, chaotic and full-on fringe experience, Stamptown is a late-night variety show featuring the best alternative performance on the international scene. \r\nHosted by the bad boy of clown, Zach Zucker, this show has packed out shows at Edinburgh Fringe, Melbourne International Comedy Festival, Glastonbury and Off-Broadway in New York City. \r\nPast acts include David Cross, Aisling Bea, Joe Pera, Lolly Adefope, Neil Hamburger, Bridget Christie, Jamie Demetriou, Cat Cohen, Richard Gadd, Mae Martin, Kemah Bob, Please Don’t Destroy, Sarah Squirm, Rachel Sennott, Atsuko Okatsuka, Chris Gethard, Natalie Palamides and MORE!\r\n\r\nLineup subject to change. \r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Stamptown. 23","instanceDates":"17 January-27 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"507603ALRCNVJJHMVTGSQLBGNMHGMJSNB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-17T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-17T22:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-27T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-27T22:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"WINNER: Best Variety Show in London, Chortle Awards (2020)\r\n\r\nA raunchy, chaotic, full-on fever dream, Stamptown is 120 minutes of pure spectacle featuring the most anarchic and wildly entertaining performance from around the world. \r\n\r\nHosted by the bad boy of clown, Zach Zucker, this show has packed out rooms at Netflix Is A Joke. Just For Laughs, Glastonbury, SXSW, Edinburgh Fringe, Soho Theatre, Melbourne International Comedy Festival, O2 Arena and Off-Broadway in New York City.\r\n\r\nPast acts include David Cross, Aisling Bea, Neil Patrick Harris, Karen Gillan, Lolly Adefope, Reggie Watts, Bridget Christie, Jamie Demetriou, Cat Cohen, Richard Gadd, Mae Martin, Huge Davies, Kemah Bob, Sam Campbell, Rachel Sennott, Randy Feltface, Natalie Palamides and MORE!\r\n\r\nLineup subject to change.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Stamptown. 24","instanceDates":"4 September-4 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"581803ATRCBDSJRGGHQCSQQRDHLSPSGJV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-04T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-04T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-04T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-04T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"Come and see participants of Soho Theatre’s Stand-Up Lab make their stand-up comedy debut. Quick, before they’re all famous! \r\n\r\nThey’ll have spent the last 10 weeks discovering the artform for the first time and developing new skills with course leader Sikisa. \r\n16+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Stand Up Lab Sharing","instanceDates":"24 July-24 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"486803AHJMSVKDCPLDDLCMPMPCJHJDPKP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-24T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-24T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-24T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-24T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Come and see participants of Soho Theatre’s Stand-Up Lab make their stand-up comedy debut. Quick, before they’re all famous! \r\n\r\nThey’ll have spent the last 10 weeks discovering the artform for the first time and developing new skills with course leader Sikisa. \r\n\