ll famous!\r\nThey have spent the last 10 weeks discovering the artform for the first time and developing new skills with course leader Sikisa. \r\n\r\nIf you’re thinking about applying for the course itself, come and see what it’s all about.\r\n16+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Stand Up Lab Showcase Dec24","instanceDates":"9 December-9 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"583203ANLBGRHCKNBJBQPRMKCNQRCQTLR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-09T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-09T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-09T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-09T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Come and see participants of Soho Theatre’s Stand-Up Lab make their stand-up comedy debut. Quick, before they’re all famous!","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Stand Up Lab Showcase Jul24","instanceDates":"22 July-22 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"559403ASQKBJKTJKLJNQPCNLJTRRLVGBT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-22T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-22T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-22T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-22T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Come and see participants of Soho Theatre’s Stand-Up Lab make their stand-up comedy debut. Quick, before they’re all famous! \r\n\r\nThey’ll have spent the last 10 weeks discovering the artform for the first time and developing new skills with course leader Sikisa. \r\n\r\nIf you’re thinking about applying for the course itself, come and see what it’s all about.\r\n\r\n16+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Stand Up Lab Showcase Mar24","instanceDates":"25 March-25 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"532403AMDSBTLJBSGBTMHQHDVRJRBPVDJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-25T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-25T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-25T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-25T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Come and see participants of Soho Theatre’s Stand-Up Lab make their stand-up comedy debut. Quick, before they’re all famous!\r\n\r\n\r\nThe group have spent the last 10 weeks discovering the artform for the first time and developing new skills with course leader Sikisa. \r\n\r\nIf you’re thinking about applying for the course yourself, come and see what it’s all about.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Stand Up Lab Showcase Mar25","instanceDates":"31 March-31 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"616803ABHLGTMSSBPPSHRJDSMPKRHPJCC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-31T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-31T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-31T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-31T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"If you’ve ever been told you should try stand-up or been curious about dipping your toe into the world of comedy, now’s your chance.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":150,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Stand Up Taster Lab May25","instanceDates":"10 May-28 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"622605ACCKPHPVSSDMMMGDMDGPCHKHSPR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-10T10:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-10T09:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-28T10:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-28T09:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Steen Raskopoulos – one half of the critically acclaimed improv duo The Bear Pack and star of The Office (Australia) – is back at Soho Theatre with his new show.\r\nSolo sketch show packed with lovable characters, charisma and inspired spontaneity, from the internationally award-nominated star of The Office (Australia), Netflix's The Duchess and Netflix's Feel Good. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Steen Raskopoulos: Friendly Stranger","instanceDates":"6 March-8 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"599403ALTPPDDBNQRCRJHDTMQCPQKVGJH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-06T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-06T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-08T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-08T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Steph Tolev caught fire on the “BILL BURR PRESENTS: FRIENDS WHO KILL” Netflix Special, that was taped as a part of the Netflix is a Joke Festival.\r\nShe was named a COMEDIAN YOU SHOULD AND WILL KNOW by Vulture, which recognized her one of Toronto’s funniest exports. She was featured on Comedy Central’s THE RINGERS stand up series, and season two of UNPROTECTED SETS. Steph will appear in the upcoming feature DRUGSTORE JUNE, as well as OLD DADS starring Bill Burr, Bobby Cannavale, and Bokeem Woodbine. She has appeared in Comedy Central’s CORPORATE, and starred in an episode of the Sarah Silverman-produced PLEASE UNDERSTAND ME. Steph has been well-received at festivals all over the world, she can be seen performing all around LA, including The Comedy Store where she is a paid regular, and headlines clubs across the country.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Steph Tolev: The Filth Queen Tour","instanceDates":"29 May-1 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"540603ADQJTSCRHDPLQRTRLKJBSGBPRGV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-29T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-29T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-01T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-01T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"\"Fabulously Funny\" (The Guardian) star of Live at the Apollo (BBC), Would I Lie To You? (BBC) and The Madame Blanc Mysteries (Channel 5), Stephen Bailey brings his latest show TART to Soho Theatre following the huge success of his recent UK tour.\r\n\"A rising star\" (The Sun), Stephen has appeared on every light entertainment show and come second on every celebrity quiz show and in his new show will gossip about everything from his funeral plans to his unrequited love for Ben Shephard - and if he needs to pad it out, he will read you secrets direct from the girlies WhatsApp group chat. \r\nBrassy, sassy and always classy – the perfect ingredients to make a proper Tart. Tour Support for Katherine Ryan, Lucy Beaumont, Jason Manford & Micky Flanagan.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Stephen Bailey: Tart","instanceDates":"22 April-25 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"676603AHGSLSBRRJTKNMJQLGVNQSVKGHR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-22T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-22T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-25T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-25T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"A rare opportunity to see Stephen Merchant developing his new stand up act in an intimate setting.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":65,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Stephen Merchant: Work in Progress","instanceDates":"28 July-28 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"650203ANLVBSCCLHRHHLJLVBNPHNRQNPM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-28T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-28T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-28T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-28T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Work In Progress","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Stevie Martin (8 out of 10 Cats, Guessable, A Thornton's Advert) has been doing online comedy for a while (45 million views worldwide) but is now returning to live comedy with her latest show, which sold out at The Edinburgh Fringe Festival this year. It's like her online stuff but she'll be on a stage and you can't pause her to get a snack (meats?). Also you have to sit in a specific room to watch it (please don’t bring your meats to this room). “Ingenious” The Guardian ★★★★\r\n “Generous, surprising and joyous” The Times ★★★★ \r\n“Hilarious” The Scotsman ★★★★ \r\n“This is a properly funny show” The List ★★★★\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Stevie Martin: Clout","instanceDates":"22 September-27 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"623403ASSDVMGBRHHPRSDKVTBNHHBNSGL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-22T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-22T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-27T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-27T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Stevie Martin (8 out of 10 Cats, Guessable, A Thornton's Advert) has been doing online comedy \r\nfor a while (45 million views worldwide) but is now returning to live comedy with her latest show, \r\nwhich sold out at The Edinburgh Fringe Festival this year. It's like her online stuff but she'll be on a \r\nstage and you can't pause her to get a snack (meats?). Also you have to sit in a specific room to \r\nwatch it (please don’t bring your meats to this room). \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Stevie Martin: CloutOct24","instanceDates":"6 December-5 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"578003ARKTSDGSDNNDKSSJRNKCBDVNTNN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-06T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-06T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-05T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-05T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Stevie (8 out of 10 cats, Guessable, A Thorntons Advert) is creating a new show (comedy) and would like to know if it works (comedy-wise). There may or may not be a joke about an owl because that bit, at the time of writing this, is on the chopping block. Come along to see if the owl makes it through? Owls are not welcome in the theatre. To be clear this is not a show about owls even though it really does look like that doesn't it. It's just a normal show (comedy).  \r\n'Funny AF' - Time Out \r\n'In complete command of the audience... tremendous.' - Ed Fest Mag\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Stevie Martin: Work in Progress","instanceDates":"31 July-2 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"463603ARNSHSGGVCSQGPBPPLCGRGQNJJR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-31T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-31T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-02T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-02T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Work In Progress","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"So they’ve both swiped right. Now they’re facing each other. The vibe is horrific and the banter is even worse. But something is keeping them in their seats. Welcome to your hot date.\r\nSo they’ve both swiped right. Now they’re facing each other. The vibe is horrific and the banter is even worse. But something is keeping them in their seats. Welcome to your hot date.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Strategic Love Play","instanceDates":"23 May-15 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"514803APPMVMMVCPSGVNBLMKPCTRTVPJN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-23T14:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-23T13:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-15T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-15T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"So they’ve both swiped right. Now they’re facing each other. The vibe is horrific and the banter is even worse. But something is keeping them in their seats… Welcome to your hot date.\r\nStrategic Love Play\r\nBy Miriam Battye\r\nDirected by Katie Posner\r\n\r\nSo they’ve both swiped right. Now they’re meeting for the first time. Facing each other. As if that’s a normal thing to do.\r\n\r\nBut she’s being uncomfortable, and he’s a total bore. The vibe is horrific and the banter is even worse. But something is keeping them in their seats. Something is making them stay. Welcome to your hot date.\r\n\r\nWith acid wit, Miriam Battye’s new play takes a scalpel to modern romance, interrogating what we really talk about when we talk about love.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Strategic Love Play.","instanceDates":"6 September-23 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"489803AKSSVTSCSDVDHPQCPQKQVSJGDBP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-06T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-06T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-23T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-23T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The return of the 5* hit show.\r\n\r\nA late night musical kids party, but for adults\r\n\r\nIt’s Story-time, kids! Now sit still and LISTEN: \r\n\r\nWhen it comes to children's entertainment, nobody does it better than Sylvester ‘Silly’ String. A charming classical virtuoso and topdog in the lucrative West London kids’ parties market, every kid within a 5 mile radius of the Kings Road wants Silly String and his Silly Songs...until Spitta comes along. SPITTA is a Grime-obsessed maverick from East London who’s shaken up the scene and quickly become the talk of the Kensington playgrounds. \r\n\r\nStarring Kiell Smith-Bynoe (star of BBC's Ghosts and Taskmaster) and Ed MacArthur ('Murder for Two'), String V SPITTA is a musical comedy about two rival children’s entertainers, from opposite sides of the tracks, who will do anything to be number one. Think Amadeus meets Flight of the Conchords, with musical numbers directed by Dizzee Rascal.\r\n\r\nThis is one party you won't want to miss.\r\n\r\n‘So ingenious, it’s hard to believe it hasn’t been done before’\r\n5* Independent\r\n4* Guardian\r\n4* Chortle\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"String V SPITTA","instanceDates":"1 August-10 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"468403AMTSLPSRMPHHCCHSDLLJDHVVHVP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-01T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-01T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-10T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-10T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Sketch","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"WINNER: Best Show, Leicester Comedy Festival 2023\r\nStuart is terrified of the climate crisis, but no-one he knows ever mentions it, so it must be fine.\r\n\r\nHilarious, optimistic, and vaguely educational, join “expert stand-up” (Sunday Times) Stuart Goldsmith for a show about hope, horror, hypocrisy and how to feel OK.\r\n\r\nAs seen and heard on TBS' Conan, The Comedian's Comedian podcast, You're Dead to Me and Trusty Hogs. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Stuart Goldsmith: Spoilers","instanceDates":"29 November-2 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"511003AGMHLVTNHCDBJDKRVVVTGVJGRDT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-29T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-29T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-12-02T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-12-02T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Political","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Last year Stuart started telling the truth on stage and was diagnosed autistic: he got the best reviews he’s ever had, and his show was a must-see. He's back baby, fresh from a critically acclaimed run at the Edinburgh Fringe, a UK tour and ready to lean into it further... It’s funny, it’s real, it’s immaculately structured and it’s a chance to see a comedian at the top of his game. \r\nAs heard on Off Menu and seen on BBC,  Amazon Prime and 800 Pound Gorilla.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Stuart Laws Has To Be Joking","instanceDates":"2 June-3 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"608603AHJHKCNJQVJSKQJCKQQNNCPNVNK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-02T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-02T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-03T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-03T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"‘a swirl of delicious flights of fancy and outright lies… a profound and sophisticated show’ 4.5/5 Chortle\r\n\r\nAcclaimed gilet-wearing stand-up, filmmaker, goalkeeper and viral Twitter star Stuart Laws takes his latest show out on tour, and this time he’s telling the truth. In ‘Stuart Laws? Is That Guy Still Going?’, the Ruislip-based stand-up has resolved to tell the truth, the whole truth and almost nothing but the truth. After an argument with his therapist about being too closed off Stuart has resolved to come clean: sperm and all. A show about getting married, nothing lasting forever, vasectomies, childfree living and long-grief from the leftfield observationalist and intricate gag-weaver. \r\nStuart’s a mainstay on the alt-comedy scene: he’s appeared on BBC iPlayer, Prime (in his own series Grave New World), BBC Radio 4, produced James Acaster's four Netflix specials, directed Nish Kumar’s latest comedy special and his online videos are regularly going viral - you might recognise him phoning a horse, saying “Never” as Michael Caine, finding the secret cocktail bar in M&M World or offsetting sex in a hilarious takedown of carbon offsetting.\r\nThe multi-talented comic has just had a comedy special released by 800 Pound Gorilla, an American comedy label and he’s also the guy behind award-winning indie production company Turtle Canyon Comedy, the makers of web series, short films, sketches and podcasts that have been watched over 20 million times and feature the likes of Lou Sanders, Joel Dommett, Harriet Kemsley and Ed Gamble.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Stuart Laws? Is That Guy Still Going?","instanceDates":"2 April-3 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"531604ARBVLCQTRBNBNSCJGPQHLDJMRVV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-02T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-02T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-03T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-03T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Total sellout Fringe 2023. \r\n\r\nLast year Stu got dumped for another more famous comedian. This is the \"relentlessly funny hour\" (Sunday Post) on the rollercoaster year that followed. \r\nStar of BBC's BAFTA winning 'Scot Squad', co-host of the Some Laugh podcast\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Stuart McPherson: Love That For Me","instanceDates":"1 July-2 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"541403ACHJRNDTQHSQQQDGMMTCGNTJSGB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-01T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-01T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-02T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-02T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Think it’s a Stand up solo show? Think again. This immersive comedy invites you all on a surreal misadventure of absurdist sketch , untamed thrash metal guitar solos and imaginary costumed personas.\r\nExpect high energy , wild storytelling and whimsical uplifting nonsense left right and centre. A wild, offbeat and exciting exploration of Stand-up, Musical , Character and Clown comedy, this one woman show celebrates the human experience growing up as an immigrant child of South-East Asian descent , born and bred in the treacherous depths of East London. \r\nSu Mi is a British Malaysian Alternative Stand up Comedienne & Musician sharing her cultivating tales of her own cultural identity. \r\nSocial commentary on Intersectionality , Queerness , Racism and Mental health as a Woman of Colour growing up in the Western world. \r\nBreaking stereotypical barriers of what a typical ‘Asian Woman’ should be and representing a voice that does exist in audiences, especially in the alternative comedy world.\r\nSOLD out run at the Camden Fringe and SOLD OUT shows at the VAULT Festival 2023.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Su Mi: Banana Beard","instanceDates":"10 February-10 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"521405ARRSJLLTVBHDJSMGPCQDKKTLBCJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-10T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-10T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-10T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-10T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"LGBTQ+","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"THISMOTHERPHUCKER is a public nuisance. A dysfunctional anti-clown whose only mission is to destroy ego. Join them for a wild exploration down the trippiest rabbit hole you could never imagine.\r\n\r\nAward-winning stand-up and drag performance artist Su Mi presents their \"absolutely bonkers\" (Binge Fringe) award-winning debut show: an immersive surreal experience resurrecting every nostalgic moment left forgotten, healing the inner child and seeking to destroy archaic stereotypes and challenge the narrative of comedy whilst navigating a predominantly white cis space.\r\n\r\nThe BBC New Comedian of the Year nominee and finalist of the Funny Women Awards and Musical Comedy Awards presents \"a glorious reclaiming of space that throws the rules of respectability out the window.\" (The Skinny)\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Su Mi: THISMOTHERPHUCKER","instanceDates":"8 May-9 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"697203AKSKPLDNPMLNBGVBNNHGRQVDDRD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-08T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-08T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-09T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-09T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Sue can’t concentrate on anything for more than five minutes and has no personal boundaries.  Thankfully the latter provides her with a lot of material. \r\nNew WIP show from one of Britain’s best-loved comedians.\r\n\r\nCurrently hosting BBC R4’s Just a Minute, Sue has presented multiple travel shows for the BBC and Netflix. She is probably best known for that cake show. \r\n\r\nContent advice\r\nMay contain swearing, sexual references and shameful scenarios.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sue Perkins: A Piece of Work in Progress","instanceDates":"5 August-10 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"549803AHPCVGJKHDBVSPSQTMVRVJPQJDC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-05T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-05T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-10T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-10T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Work In Progress","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"You may know her as Bake-Off Sue, Taskmaster Sue, Just A Minute Sue, or the Sue that gives you travel envy - but stand-up Sue is full of surprises. In this brand-new show, she shares the unlikely happenings from a career in the spotlight. \r\nWhat’s the fallout when your pituitary gland goes haywire on live TV?  How do you convince the public you didn’t really fall onto that hoover attachment? And when intimate photos get splashed all over the internet, how do you switch the shame to dignity and joy? \r\nIn her first live show in over a decade, Sue delivers a hilarious treatise on stigma, humiliation, and misunderstanding. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sue Perkins: The Eternal Shame of Sue Perkins","instanceDates":"2 April-3 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"725003AHQLMPJGHCHLRBPTVNTVSHJCRGL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-04-02T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-04-02T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-04-03T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-04-03T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"You may know her as Bake-Off Sue, Taskmaster Sue, Just A Minute Sue, or the Sue that gives you travel envy - but stand-up Sue is full of surprises. In this brand-new show, she shares the unlikely happenings from a career in the spotlight. 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sue Perkins: The Eternal Shame of Sue Perkins.","instanceDates":"10 April-11 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"656403AVNGLQLPKVLRQRSBLPVPKKBJCGD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-10T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-10T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-11T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-11T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Sugar Sammy is one of the hottest comedians on the international circuit. The New York Times calls him \"a fearless comic with a talent for provoking both laughter and outrage\". He has performed over 2,000 shows in 32 countries and is now on tour in the UK!\r\nSugar Sammy is a charismatic provocateur whose worldly outlook allows him to hit on cultural, social and political themes with great charm and finesse. He is a king of crowd work and his audience interaction makes for a unique performance every time.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sugar Sammy in London","instanceDates":"3 December-6 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"662203ASCBVQGRGNSDMRCSNHDKPVGPGRH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-03T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-03T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-06T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-06T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Tiktok’s Breakthrough Stars of 2022 the Sugarcoated Sisters bring their smash-hit sell-out Edinburgh Fringe debut to London for the first time. \r\nThe award winning, critically acclaimed and hopelessly flawed musical comedy duo move back to their home town to discover unfinished business lurking around every corner. \r\nArmed with original songs, guitar and double bass, no musical style is off-limits as ammunition for their scathing revenge on everyone who’s ever wronged them. \r\nOne has bipolar. One has diabetes. And neither of them have had sex for two years … join them as they unleash their multi-million-hit personas at Soho Theatre for a collective cathartic release!\r\n‘An absolute must-see’ ***** Entertainment Now\r\n'Flawed, fearless and fabulously feisty. Heartwarmingly filthy, these comedy queens cavort \r\nacross musical genres, dropping punchlines and truth bombs” ***** Fringebiscuit\r\n‘An exceptional show’ ***** Theatre South East\r\n‘A delight to enjoy the fresh perspective of young women comics’ **** The Scotsman\r\n‘Their comedic timing is excellent’ **** Fest\r\n‘Like sugar, these stars are easy to get hooked on’ **** The List\r\nFeatured on: \r\nBBC 5 Live\r\nBBC Radio 4\r\nHeart Breakfast Show Scotland\r\nBBC Scotland\r\nChannel 4\r\nBBC News\r\nBBC Click \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sugarcoated Sisters: Bittersweet","instanceDates":"4 April-6 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"458403AVPBDPPGTNSQVNDHLKBKBLVVVSB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-04T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-04T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-06T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-06T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Join Suhani Shah on this journey as she reads people’s minds, deciphers their thoughts, predicts their actions and leaves you speechless.\r\n\r\nIn her brand-new show, Suhani shares with you the flip side of being a child prodigy and social media sensation, while performing unbelievable feats of mentalism.\r\n\r\nExperience this stunning performance, full of plot twists, laughter and heart-warming entertainment where you can volunteer to be part of the show or sit back and enjoy an unpredictable evening of wonders. \r\n\r\n16+ recommended","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Suhani Shah: Live","instanceDates":"11 April-15 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"449203ARGDQJJSJKRPCQBNJRPCHMTPTCT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-11T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-11T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-15T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-15T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Experience the extraordinary as Suhani Shah, the world's highest-subscribed mentalist returns.\r\nIndia's most-famous mind reader, Suhani, mesmerizes audiences worldwide with her groundbreaking magic. In her latest show, she delves into the depths of mental mysteries with unexpected twists, compelling storytelling, and interactive audience engagement.\r\n\r\nWith her charismatic persona, linguistic deception, mind-reading prowess and comedic charm, Suhani guarantees an unforgettable evening that will leave you Spellbound!\r\n12+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Suhani Shah: Spellbound 2.0","instanceDates":"7 August-10 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"549003ABGKHBQSLVPPMVSQLMQJKSCKLPC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-07T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-07T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-10T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-10T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Theatre"},{"description":"Join Sukh as she approaches 40 and figures out middle age, pretending to be a grown up and the joy of a Tupperware set.\r\nSukh keeps being told that she’s successful. She’s been on telly, had a book published and even been trolled on Twitter. So why does she still feel like a toddler who has lost their Mum in Tesco’s?\r\n\r\nSukh Ojla is a comedian, actor and writer. Her first book, ‘Sunny’, was released in 2022.\r\n\r\nAs a comedian, Sukh has performed on many TV shows including, The Big Asian Stand-Up Show (BBC Two), Comedy Guide to Life (Dave), Jonathan Ross’ Comedy Club (ITV), Comedy Central Live and features in Sky’s Dating No Filter.\r\n\r\nOther television credits include Feel Good (Channel 4), Bridgerton (Netflix), The End of the F**king World (Channel 4), GameFace (Channel 4), Hospital People (BBC1), Black Mirror (Channel 4) and EastEnders (BBC1).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sukh Ojla: The Aunty Years","instanceDates":"9 May-4 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"511603ALLVPSJSGVBPCSGVDCSJKKKJTKD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-09T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-09T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-04T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-04T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Wondering what to do when the music in Lloyd Park stops? We got you covered… come and join our After Party!\r\nAfter the Summer Picnic festival wraps up in Lloyd Park come and join us for more fun. For those coming straight from the park we have a warm up bar inThe Collab. with DJs to keep you in the mood from 7pm – 10pm.  This is just two doors down from our main venue - Soho Theatre, Walthamstow.\r\n\r\nFrom 10pm (once the audience has exited from Justin Vivian Bond’s show in the main auditorium) all ticket holders can enter the Foyer Bar in Soho Theatre, Walthamstow where the party continues until the small hours.\r\n\r\nWe have some amazing guests headlining this party: Simon Lee who is one half of the pioneering duo Faze Action, known for shaping the sound of modern Disco, House, and Balearic music over the past two decades. Their debut album made instant waves when it was released on Nuphonic Records, based at the equally iconic Blu Note Club—a key force in reshaping Shoreditch’s 90s scene, hosting legends such as Goldie, Bjork, Talvin Singh, and Andy Weatherall.\r\n\r\nAlongside his brother Robin, Simon then went on to release five acclaimed albums, countless remixes, and timeless tracks like “In the Trees” and “Disco Motion,” both underground classics that fueled the global disco revival.\r\n\r\nAs a DJ, Simon brings depth and energy to the crowd, blending Afro, Disco, house and Balearic numbers with a selector’s ear and a producer’s instinct. His sets reflect years spent crate-digging, studio crafting, and performing worldwide. Joining him as co-headliner will be Lex (Athens) who is flying in from Greece to play this gig specially for us.\r\nLex’s unique psychedelic disco sound borrows from a lively palette of house and techno, always with a nod to organic funk and soul. He has an album out on local Leytonstone label Leng Records. \r\nWarm up will be provided by local DJ heroes Dom Mandrell the co-director of the Summer Picnic festival and Groova as well as a few extra surprise guests in the mix.\r\nAll proceeds from ticket sales go towards keeping the festival free and helping it grow next year.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":240,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Summer Picnic After Party","instanceDates":"12 July-12 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"637003ASPDKVSLVNLKDQVGRHNMQDDJHML","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-12T22:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-12T21:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-12T22:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-12T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"After multiple sell-out shows across India and the world, Sumukhi comes to Soho Theatre Walthamstow for her biggest show in London.\r\nSumukhi Suresh is back with Hoemonal, a stand-up show where she clarifies she’s not calling Monal a hoe (we promise).  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nOne of India’s top comics and the creator of Pushpavalli, Sumukhi turns the chaos of adulthood into laugh-out-loud therapy, tackling everything from hormonal rollercoasters and awkward dating misadventures to the fear of dying alone (relatable, right?). It’s like your group chat having an emotional breakdown, but on stage and way funnier. Armed with sharp wit and painfully honest stories, Sumukhi doesn’t just tell jokes – she rants, overshares, and roasts her own life with zero shame.  \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nIf you’re in the mood to laugh about life’s weird, messy bits while feeling a little too seen, this is the show for you. Whether you’re here for the laughs, the chaos, or because your friend dragged you here, Sumukhi has got you covered.16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sumukhi Suresh: Hoemonal","instanceDates":"29 November-29 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"651203ARTDPTVKLRQJJVGHCHMVMRKBVQG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-29T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-29T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-29T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-29T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"A stand-up show where Sumukhi justifies the spelling of her show’s name and how she is not calling Monal a Hoe.\r\nA stand-up show where Sumukhi justifies the spelling of her show’s name and how she is not calling Monal a Hoe.\r\n\r\nSumukhi Suresh is a comedian, actor, writer, show runner and most importantly a show off. She was the Host and went to become one of the Judges on the Amazon Original Comicstaan. She created and starred in the acclaimed Amazon Prime Original Pushpavalli which won her a Filmfare (SRK has 15). Her first stand up special Don’t Tell Amma (Amazon Prime) was well received by audiences but not by her mother.\r\nShe was recently named one of the BAFTA Breakthroughs from India, getting her one step closer to working with Phoebe Waller-Bridge.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":80,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sumukhi Suresh: Hoemonal.","instanceDates":"22 August-26 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"488603ASJMBDBMPBNVBDNRQBGCGRMNLRQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-22T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-22T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-26T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-26T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"'If I had asked people what they wanted, they would have said faster horses' (Henry Ford). Mad that he went and invented the car isn't it? Imagine all the people thinking 'please Henry we just want a faster horse' and then he just turns up with an engine on a bed frame that goes 3mph. Anyway, I'm coming to Soho Theatre with some faster horses - give the people what they want I say. As seen on This Time with Alan Partridge (BBC), Stath Lets Flats (Channel 4) and Jonathan Ross' Comedy Club (ITV) and heard on BBC Radio 4's 'An Idiots Guide to Cryptocurrency'\r\n\r\n•\t4 * The Telegraph \r\n•\t4 *The Skinny\r\n•\t4 *Entertainment Now\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sunil Patel: Faster Horses","instanceDates":"25 May-27 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"444003AJJDSKVBKDGNHKRHRJTMBMQNMJP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-25T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-25T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-27T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-27T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"India/South Asian heritage"},{"description":"Told via spoken word and featuring a host of characters, this epic, playful and heartfelt play forces is a call for change in the way society shapes young Black men. \r\nTheatre Peckham presents\r\nSunny Side Up\r\nBy David Alade\r\nA Peckham Fringe Transfer\r\nDavid Alade’s captivating story transfers to Soho Theatre. Based on a true story, Sunny Side Up explores the relation-ship between a young man and his father. With sensational acting, poetic storytelling, and heartfelt moments, this poignant and passionate production is a must-see.\r\nTold via spoken word and featuring a host of characters, this epic, playful and heartfelt play forces is a call for change in the way society shapes young Black men. \r\n13+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sunny Side Up","instanceDates":"28 May-1 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"547203AHVGTKTCBMRLKSNQJVMDVQCMBPQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-28T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-28T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-01T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-01T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Following a smash hit Edinburgh Fringe run, award-winning character comedian Susan Harrison is bringing her latest collection of joyfully bizarre alter-egos to Soho. Is it ok to still be dressing up as weird characters as you get older? Susan might not be sure, but a life size Sindy doll, a panda from Chester Zoo in the 90’s and a woman who’s swallowed a small girl in a well will have plenty to say about it. Some others might turn up too.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Susan Harrison: Should I Still Be Doing This?","instanceDates":"24 April-25 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"690204AKNPCHBGMLSTSSCMTGLTPHCTTSN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-24T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-24T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-25T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-25T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Suzi Ruffell likes things snappy: her stand up, her decisions and her suits. Suzi's brand-new show is all about settling down (but not settling), becoming a mother (without becoming mumsy) and still worrying about everything - of course she is - have you seen the news?\r\n\r\nMulti-award nominated comedian Suzi Ruffell's last tour, 'Dance Like Everyone Is Watching' received critical acclaim and was recorded as an Amazon special. Suzi has also appeared on numerous shows such as Live At The Apollo, The Jonathan Ross Show, QI, The Last Leg, and Womanhood to name but a few. Suzi is also best known for her hugely popular podcasts 'Like Minded Friends' and 'Out'. \r\n\r\n“instinctively, exquisitely funny from the moment she sashays onto the stage… a crowd-pleasing show packed with punchlines.” Evening Standard\r\n\r\n“a very likable presiding spirit, combining daft physical comedy… with disarming emotional candour” The Guardian\r\n\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Suzi Ruffell: Snappy","instanceDates":"1 April-3 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"428203ATJPTHCTPTSNQDSPMQJHSQDKPCR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-01T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-01T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-03T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-03T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"The Juggle is a brand new tour from multi-award winning confessional comedian Suzi Ruffell\r\nIt’s hard to be good all the time. A good mother, a good daughter, a good partner, a good friend, a good person. To be ambitious but not ruthless; a success but not a sell-out. A gentle parent but not a pushover. To be smashing life and make it look easy. The juggle. Suzi is exhausted and she hasn't even started. This is a stand-up show and a support group!\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":85,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Suzi Ruffell: The Juggle","instanceDates":"3 October-3 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"596403AKPPLTPSGVDBPQDNPHHJSMTRNNH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-03T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-03T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-03T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-03T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Swamplesque is the award-winning, critically acclaimed, burlesque parody show from Far Far Away! This \"outrageously fun\" (Adelaide Advertiser) show offers its audience a smorgasbord of performance styles.\r\nAfter taking Australia by storm and smashing box office records at Edinburgh Fringe in 2024 & 2025, everyone's favourite ogre-inspired burlesque and drag parody returns to London! \r\nPrepare for a night filled with laughter, surprises, and a touch of the risqué. Don’t be green with envy – grab your friends and secure your tickets now for this hilariously naughty night out! \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":100,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Swamplesque","instanceDates":"1 July-11 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"696603ABHPHJPHRVTKSRPDTKKVCPNKNTR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-01T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-01T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-11T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-11T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"LGBTQ+","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Drag","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"Workshops led by Bourgeoise & Maurice, ages 18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"SYC Cabaret & Drag Lab - 2017","instanceDates":"7 October-9 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"133603APJHKSJMTSMPBVPGJNCDBRDQKCC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2017-10-07T12:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2017-10-07T11:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2017-12-09T12:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2017-12-09T12:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Workshops led by George Heyworth, ages 18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"SYC Cabaret & Drag Lab - 2018","instanceDates":"27 January-27 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"157802AJMSNCVMRGMBPDRMCRQQCKKLGJN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2018-01-27T12:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2018-01-27T12:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2018-01-27T12:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2018-01-27T12:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Workshops led by Alison Thea-Skot, ages 21+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":150,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"SYC Comedy Lab  Plus - 2017","instanceDates":"7 October-16 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"133202ALSHRQHJPRKNLJCCBMMDLQMHBTD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2017-10-07T10:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2017-10-07T09:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2017-12-16T10:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2017-12-16T10:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Workshops led by Lee Griffiths, ages 21-26","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":150,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"SYC Comedy Lab  Sketch","instanceDates":"7 October-9 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"133602AVHQQCNQBCDVCJJJRHVJQCCLRKJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2017-10-07T10:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2017-10-07T09:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2017-12-09T10:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2017-12-09T10:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Workshops led by Andrew Doyle, ages 21-26","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":150,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":