:false,"attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Playwriting workshops, ages 16-26","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"SYC Writers' Lab 2 ","instanceDates":"8 November-13 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"69801ACHMQQPHNNNRPKGGCKPVPDJPPBTJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2016-11-08T18:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2016-11-08T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2017-06-13T18:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2017-06-13T17:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_Venue":"Seminar Room","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Playwriting workshops, ages 16-26","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"SYC Writers' Lab 3","instanceDates":"15 November-20 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"70002AKMHJSPCSLSDGCPJRRQGDRCDDJPN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2016-11-15T18:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2016-11-15T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2017-06-20T18:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2017-06-20T17:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_Venue":"Seminar Room","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Playwriting workshops, ages 16-26","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"SYC Writers' Lab 4","instanceDates":"22 November-27 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"70003AHQNLMNQTDMLPRLKPQDVBHMTCNCL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2016-11-22T18:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2016-11-22T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2017-06-27T18:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2017-06-27T17:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_Venue":"Seminar Room","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Sydnee Washington is a comedian, actor, and writer. In 2022, Sydnee became an Emmy Nominee for her supporting role as Judith in BRIDESMAN. She also received a WGA Award for her writing contributions to INSIDE AMY SCHUMER. In 2021, she was chosen as a New Face by Just For Laughs for her stand-up work. She has supported comedians including Chelsea Handler, Matteo Lane and Janelle James A podcast staple, she’s been the host of “The Unofficial Expert” with Marie Faustin and Headgum’s “Hobby Hunter”. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sydnee Washington: Live","instanceDates":"13 June-15 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"551603ABCSPQMDMGKRDQRGRNCQBQBJKQG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-13T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-13T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-15T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-15T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Comedy's most shameless overachiever is back with a new show about ambition and self belief in his life as a refugee.\r\n\r\nThis tour was in no way cynically timed to profiteer off the tense mood on immigration, and any such allegation will be met with litigation from his mother.\r\n\r\nTadiwa Mahlunge is one of the fastest-rising stars in British comedy, having already appeared on Stand Up Sketch Show (ITV2), Am I The A**hole (Comedy Central), Comedians Giving Lectures (Dave) and Comedy Central Live.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tadiwa Mahlunge: Hakuna Ma Tad Tad","instanceDates":"15 April-16 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"680803AKPQHLVVNMDQKVTQHSRVBNVJSBB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-15T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-15T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-16T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-16T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Fresh from a sell-out Edinburgh Fringe run, one of the country’s top new stand-ups brings their ‘impressive debut’ (The Guardian) to Soho Theatre.\r\nAs seen on BBC One, Dave, Comedy Central. Tour support for Desiree Burch, Jessica Fostekew and Kiri Pritchard-McLean. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tadiwa Mahlunge: Inhibition Exhibiton","instanceDates":"1 February-3 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"513803AQHKHHPNCDHVGRPHCTPCRSHJLBC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-01T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-01T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-03T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-03T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Winner Directors' Choice Award (2023) & Nominee for Most Outstanding Show (2024) at Melbourne Comedy Festival\r\nJapanese comedian Takashi comes to London to be a Comedy Samurai.\r\nHe thinks stand-up comedy is similar to samurai. A samurai tries to make his body and his sword one. Takashi tries to make himself and his jokes one. He puts his life and passion into this comedy show. Please don’t miss any strokes of his jokes and souls.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Takashi Wakasugi: Comedy Samurai","instanceDates":"26 August-27 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"634203AHRCQTGKNVCMKMGBRQKKRGJDRHJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-26T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-26T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-27T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-27T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The world’s biggest Manchester United podcast (brought to you by The Athletic) is back again with a brand-new show.\r\nJoin Laurie Whitwell, Carl Anka, Andy Mitten, and Ian Irving as they deliver unparalleled insight from inside Old Trafford. \r\n\r\nExpect fresh stories - heard for the first time  - that you won’t hear on the regular podcast, plus the chance to get answers to all your questions on United.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Talk Of The Devils Podcast Live","instanceDates":"11 November-11 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"621803ACVMLQJHMMHGNVJCCSBJLVTCQPG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-11T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-11T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-11T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-11T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"When working class, Cornish comedian Tamsyn Kelly (BBC New Comedy Awards, Comedy Central Live), discovers footage of her estranged father in a Channel 4 documentary, she's forced to stop and reassess her life.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tamsyn Kelly: Crying in TK Maxx","instanceDates":"18 April-20 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"510403AJSJBSBQSKCNMKPTQQKPCPQKNPQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-18T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-18T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-04-20T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-04-20T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"After just four months of dating her new boyfriend, Tamsyn Kelly blew up her life to be with him. Leaving sunshine Penzance and Cornish coastlines, for dark and rainy Glasgow. With family and friends doubting her decision, Tamsyn struggles to fit into her new life. \r\nHas she made a mistake? Or will they walk hand in hand into the sunset? Even if it is at 2.36pm…\r\nA hilarious, demented hour of family, fresh starts and questionable decisions.\r\nExpect tales of adult friendship disasters, psychic relationship advice, and the peculiar economics of Vinted. \r\nAs seen on ITV2, Comedy Central, BBC One, BBC Three, and BBC Radio 4.\r\nWinner: Comedy Awards Panel Prize, Best in Class (2022).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tamsyn Kelly: Hot Titty Bungalow","instanceDates":"22 April-23 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"688803AKSBPVHPHGTTHVSGSNRHRLPDBKC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-22T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-22T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-23T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-23T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Fresh, fearless, and laugh-out-loud funny, rising star Tarang Hardikar brings his sharp wit to the UK for the first time.\r\nFresh from his debut at the Edinburgh Fringe, Tarang takes on life’s contradictions, cultural chaos, and his habit of questioning every minute aspect of life. Why has no one ever seen a growing coconut tree? Why is the biggest prize in sports a cup? Why didn't you keep the paneer in the fridge?\r\nFor all of these pressing questions and more, catch Tarang at Soho before everyone else claims they saw him first.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tarang Hardikar: If I’m Not Wrong","instanceDates":"1 September-5 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"716603AHRCCQDTSCVVDDBSSPJPMBGMCPD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-01T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-01T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-05T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-05T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Fresh, fearless, and laugh-out-loud funny, rising star Tarang Hardikar brings his sharp wit to the UK for the first time.\r\nAhead of his debut at the Edinburgh Fringe, Tarang takes on life’s contradictions, cultural chaos, and his habit of questioning every minute aspect of life. Why has no one ever seen a growing coconut tree? Why is the biggest prize in sports a cup? Why didn't you keep the paneer in the fridge?\r\nFor all of these pressing questions and more, catch Tarang here before everyone else claims they saw him first.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tarang Hardikar: If I’m Not Wrong (Edinburgh Preview)","instanceDates":"30 July-1 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"716403ANHDBCNQPKKDGHBVNHGLBPHVCQB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-30T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-30T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-01T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-01T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"After winning British Comedy Guide’s Next Big Thing Award, Tarot bring their sell-out show Shuffle back to London for three nights only.\r\nThe best show of 2019 according to Chortle. The sixth-best show of 2022 according to the Guardian. Come watch us continue our slow descent into mediocrity.\r\n\r\nThey (our parents, partners, children) say 'sketch is dead', but if it's dead then where's all our money going?\r\n\r\nJoyously silly and uproariously live and in-the-room, we would call it improv but we’ve got some self-respect: this is sketch in nighties. Come watch a new tour of big, daft and, above all, live comedy being conjured up in front of your very eyes.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tarot: Shuffle","instanceDates":"5 June-7 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"609603ALVMBMMKHCHLLKBMSNSJNHNDTTC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-05T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-05T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-07T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-07T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The best show of 2019 according to Chortle. The sixth-best show of 2022 according to the Guardian. Come watch us continue our slow descent into mediocrity.\r\n \r\nThey (our parents, partners, children) say 'sketch is dead', but if it's dead then where's all our money going?\r\n \r\nJoyously silly and uproariously live and in-the-room, we would call it improv but we’ve got some self-respect: this is sketch in nighties. Come watch a new tour of big, daft and, above all, live comedy being conjured up in front of your very eyes.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tarot: Shuffle.","instanceDates":"21 October-26 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"556803ABBVNPDMPMGVMMTGQLCPKRGDCJT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-21T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-21T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-26T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-26T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"After a sell out Edinburgh Fringe, “That French TikTok Lady” Tatty Macleod makes her Soho Theatre return.\r\nAlso known as “That French TikTok Lady” Tatty Macleod has gained legions of followers thanks to her hilarious and astute observations of French and British culture. Born in Zimbabwe and raised in France, Tatty has distilled this global perspective into hilarious online sketches which has garnered her over 50 million views and over 320k followers across social media.\r\n\r\nShe has performed across Europe and is a regular at some of the biggest clubs in the UK including the Comedy Store and the Glee Clubs. She is currently developing her debut hour inspired from her bilingual and bicultural upbringing which she has premiered to sold out theatres around the UK including a sold out run at Edinburgh Fringe 2022 and a sold out run at the Soho Theatre in London. She was a Funny Women awards 2022 finalist.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tatty Macleod: Fugue","instanceDates":"8 January-13 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"495803ABBVVBJPNPJPBQRLLCVPBKPVTKT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-08T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-08T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-13T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-13T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Ibsen Award Winner and Pulitzer Prize finalist Taylor Mac is back at Soho after 15 years taking on the holidays to celebrate the season in all of its dysfunction.\r\nBedazzling, moving and politically stirring, Holiday Sauce is a delightfully irreverent work exploring Christmas as calamity.\r\n\r\nThere is more to the holidays than rampant gift giving – in Taylor’s world, creativity and imagination are their own spirituality. Taylor Mac reminds us of the collective power of our chosen families, a message that rings true in spite of capitalism’s attempt to hijack the holidays. \r\n\r\nTaylor Mac is joined by longtime collaborators, designer Machine Dazzle, Music Director Matt Ray and a spectacular band to reframe the songs you love and the holidays you hate. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Taylor Mac: Holiday Sauce","instanceDates":"17 December-23 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"723003APTJRKJBKRPNCGCNDCLTRDHHKRL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-17T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-17T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-23T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-23T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Ted Hill's debut stand-up show about every single US president and how they saved his life. From Washington to Biden, Ted talks about his recovery from mental breakdown and includes a joke about each and every US president. It's just your standard coming-of-age, multimedia, mental health recovery, every single US president sort of stand-up show we're all so used to these days. Featuring silly graphs, silly drawings, silly jokes and more. Absolutely no knowledge of US presidents required for this emotional, high-energy, multimedia mischief.\r\n\r\n\"Go and see Ted Hill. He is SO funny\"\r\nSofie Hagan\r\n\"Hill's childish energy belies the slickness of his tech and his irrepressible nerd's fondness for graphs\"\r\nThe Scotsman\r\n\"few comedians harness the frenetic activity of their minds quite as comprehensively as Ted Hill\"\r\nChortle\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ted Hill: All the Presidents Man","instanceDates":"14 April-15 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"441803AKPDTQSBNVVLMKMNVCGMSRHMJQQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-14T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-14T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-15T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-15T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Crubchester United Football Club are at rock bottom: relegated to non-league. Now, purchased by a 6 year old billionaire, can the club win promotion? Join award-winning character comedian Ted Milligan for this live mockumentary following Crubchester’s fervent fans, oligarch owners and pitiful players. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ted Milligan: United","instanceDates":"4 December-6 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"670603ARGHVJPMHMCKVTVGBDCKDHBRNBV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-04T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-04T22:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-06T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-06T22:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Temi is a Lover Girl – but, somehow, always single.\r\nAfter sell-out shows across the country, she thought she'd be fighting suitors off. But, no. So, she's made another one! Will you love her as much as she loves herself?\r\nSexy, surreal and gloriously self-indulgent – Temi is back. And this one’s for the lovers.\r\nBLACK OUT Nights: Thu 5th and Thu 19th Nov\r\n“A concept birthed by Slave Play playwright Jeremy O. Harris, a BLACK OUT is the purposeful creation of an environment in which an all-Black-identifying audience can experience and discuss an event in the performing arts – free from the white gaze.”\r\nFor more information on BLACK OUT nights, visit blackoutnite.com\r\n16+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Temi Wilkey: Lover Girl","instanceDates":"2 November-21 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"719203ADRGSSRGPQRQTGGPSBCTRPVRRJP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-02T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-02T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-21T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-21T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"Temi is a Lover Girl – but, somehow, always single. \r\nAfter sell-out shows across the country, she thought she'd be fighting suitors off. But, no. So, she's made another one! Will you love her as much as she loves herself? \r\n\r\nSexy, surreal and gloriously self-indulgent – Temi is back. And this one’s for the lovers.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Temi Wilkey: Lover Girl (Edinburgh Preview)","instanceDates":"27 July-28 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"719003APHDHVBDHQKTJTGJDMMGKRKQNGT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-27T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-27T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-28T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-28T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Work In Progress","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+"},{"description":"\"Thank you for trusting us with your pleasure!\"\r\nThe Dancing Bears strip club is failing. Ten covers on a Saturday night. One booking next week. The new club down the street are packing fifty women a night with their twelve-inch synchronised dicks.\r\nWhen the boss's daughter shows up, she realises they're gonna need a bigger show.\r\nFrom the ★★★★★ Tambo & Bones powerhouse duo: writer Dave Harris and director Matthew Xia comes a steamy, boisterous and tender story about breaking free from masculinity's seductive cage.\r\n18+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tender","instanceDates":"24 April-6 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"661403ANPRKSLPLKMGLJGNLNGSLNRHCQV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-24T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-24T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-06T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-06T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Political","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Test","instanceDates":"3 September-29 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"602003ATKGDDTHPMVGTTTQBQHPJKDMSPC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-03T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-03T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-29T15:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-29T14:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Test event for Crowd Engage Training","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Test: Crowd Engage","instanceDates":"14 November-4 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"512003APNTVMVGVQHVTJHCRTJVNSDPVHT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-14T16:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-14T16:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-04T12:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-04T12:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"A show about mental strength, the female body and how awesome the NHS is in Scotland.\r\nBack in 2022, after 10 years of comedy Thanyia was finally set to do her long-awaited, anticipated debut hour at the Edinburgh Festival Fringe. Everything was going to plan. Then August happened.\r\nNominated for Best Show, Leicester Comedy Festival 2024.\r\nWinner of Vault Festival’s Comedy Breakthrough Award in 2023, Thanyia has also been seen on Mock the Week, Alma's Not Normal, Celebrity Mastermind, Richard Osman's House of Games, 8 Out of 10 Cats Does Countdown, and more.\r\n16+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Thanyia Moore: August","instanceDates":"1 September-6 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"647404ATGNVPBBKSRJNHBTKPDVRBCBQSQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-01T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-01T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-06T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-06T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A show about mental strength, the female body and how awesome the NHS is in Scotland.\r\nBack in 2022, after 10 years of comedy Thanyia was finally set to do her long-awaited, anticipated debut hour at the Edinburgh Festival Fringe. Everything was going to plan. Then August happened.\r\nNominated for Best Show, Leicester Comedy Festival 2024.\r\nWinner of Vault Festival’s Comedy Breakthrough Award in 2023, Thanyia has also been seen on Mock the Week, Alma's Not Normal, Celebrity Mastermind, Richard Osman's House of Games, 8 Out of 10 Cats Does Countdown, and more.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Thanyia Moore: August – Preview","instanceDates":"16 July-17 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"631203AQDQVKVRDCDDMSKSPLJLNQBSPCM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-16T20:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-16T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-17T20:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-17T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"After 10 years of comedy, Thanyia was finally set to do her long awaited, anticipated debut hour at Edinburgh festival fringe. Everything was going to plan, until August came. A month that was forecasted to be bright and sunny, became dark and grey, and it took every bit of strength that Thanyia had, to make it through. From running around Edinburgh, to hospital visits, all whilst being triggered by strangers who review you - Thanyia's month was not the 'norm'. A show about mental strength, the female body and how awesome the NHS is in Scotland!\r\nComedy Breakthrough Award Winner Vault Festival 2023\r\nBest Show Nominee Leicester Comedy Festival 2024\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Thanyia Moore: August.","instanceDates":"10 June-11 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"539803ARRDKHSRQGBLHVVNBGGNPGNSJBK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-10T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-10T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-11T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-11T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Two daredevil brothers attempt the impossible – slipping on 1000 banana peels. \r\nNOMINEE: Edinburgh Comedy Award 2023 Best Newcomer \r\n\r\nYou either die an artist or you live long enough to see yourself become a stuntman. In his Edinburgh Comedy Award nominated UK debut, Bill O'Neill uses every trick up his sleeve to explore the oldest one in the book. \r\n\r\nDirected by the Edinburgh Comedy Award-winning Natalie Palamides (Nate, Laid), Bill O’Neill’s hugely acclaimed and Edinburgh Comedy Award nominated show is back at Soho Theatre with a run in our Main House. This hilarious debut follows two daredevil brothers attempting the impossible — slipping on 1000 banana peels. Through a surreal exploration of loss, failure, masculinity and death-defying pratfalls, O’Neill challenges the limits of the human body and spirit – one banana peel at a time.\r\n18+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Amazing Banana Brothers By Bill O’Neill & His Brother","instanceDates":"21 June-6 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"540803ADDHMNBBNJMLNHCPHMDHVLCJLNT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-21T21:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-21T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-06T21:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-06T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Two daredevil brothers attempt the impossible – slipping on 1000 banana peels. \r\n\r\nYou either die an artist or you live long enough to see yourself become a stuntman. For his Edinburgh Fringe debut, Bill O'Neill uses every trick up his sleeve to explore the oldest one in the book. Directed by the Edinburgh Comedy Award-winning Natalie Palamides (Nate, Laid), this hilarious debut follows two daredevil brothers attempting the impossible — slipping on 1000 banana peels. Through a surreal exploration of loss, failure, masculinity and death-defying pratfalls, O’Neill challenges the limits of the human body and spirit – one banana peel at a time.\r\n\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Amazing Banana Brothers By Bill O’Neill & His Brother.","instanceDates":"7 September-13 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"490003AQSBQRSSMTCMSTVNKCNBQDBRJNJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-07T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-07T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-13T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-13T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"You either die an artist or you live long enough to see yourself become a stuntman. For his Edinburgh Fringe debut, Bill O'Neill uses every trick up his sleeve to explore the oldest one in the book. Directed by the Edinburgh Comedy Award-winning Natalie Palamides (Nate, Laid), this hilarious debut follows two daredevil brothers attempting the impossible — slipping on 1000 banana peels. Through a surreal exploration of loss, failure, masculinity and death-defying pratfalls, O’Neill challenges the limits of the human body and spirit – one banana peel at a time.\r\n‘[O'Neill] evolves the time-honored comedic bit of slipping on a banana peel to performance art (on top of repeating perfectly executed, classical physical humor).’ The Comedy Bureau, The 100 Best Things in Comedy 2022\r\n\r\n18+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Amazing Banana Brothers by Bill O’Neill and his Brother – Edinburgh Preview","instanceDates":"25 July-27 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"473003ATHJSQSMSTDPKRPTKBSRJKVLPSR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-25T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-25T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-27T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-27T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"After too long barking out orders from the sidelines, the coach puts on the jersey and slips onto the court. \r\nFOR ONE NIGHT ONLY Natalie Palamides performers the Edinburgh Comedy Award-nominated Amazing Banana Brothers with Bill O’Neill in the director’s chair.\r\n\r\nWill she out-perform him and change the course of history? Or will she meet her demise on a stage of organic landmines?\r\n\r\nYes.\r\n\r\nStarring Natalie Palamies\r\nDirected by Bill O’Neill\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Amazing Banana Brothers: By Natalie Palamides and her Brother","instanceDates":"12 January-12 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"525203ABLRQNLCNQHHHPPGMVJVTHSHLSP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-12T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-12T22:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-12T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-12T22:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Part of National Theatre Connections \r\nStudent teacher Sam arrives at Redhill Youth Custody Secure Unit hoping to enrich the troubled resident's lives there by introducing them to the subject of Philosophy. The wary class resist engaging in this alien, ancient art of thinking, at first, but start to thaw when they find themselves being challenged and empowered in ways they haven't previously experienced. Yet the hope Sam's teaching offers them is fragile, particularly for hard fronting Gee, who's on the verge of being released from the unit and is secretly terrified at this prospect. \r\n\r\nTHE ANIMALS is written by Sean Buckley for National Theatre Connections 2025 and performed by students from Leyton Sixth Form College.  \r\n\r\nNT Connections is running for its 31st year and we’re both proud and excited to continue supporting this amazing project in our new home Soho Theatre Walthamstow.  \r\n15+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"THE ANIMALS – Written by Sean Buckley, performed by LSC Expressive Arts ","instanceDates":"25 March-25 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"696203ASTVVNTTHDTTGNVGDDVSCDCPNHB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-25T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-25T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-25T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-25T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Inhale, upward dog. Exhale, downward dog. Namaste.\r\nThis is the world that yoga professor Mayuri knows well: Incense, turmeric lattes, spandex. It’s absurd, especially as the only South Asian/Indian in a practice rooted in her own heritage.  \r\n \r\nJoin Mayuri Bhandari and Kali, Goddess of Death as they take on wellness capitalism and spiritual theft.  \r\n \r\nLiberation! Not Lululemon!  \r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Anti “Yogi” by Mayuri Bhandari","instanceDates":"6 May-16 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"691803AGRPPPDGRJLNBMBCPPCDGSJMLQK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-06T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-06T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-16T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-16T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"Emanate Productions Presents\r\nThe Arc: A Trilogy of New Jewish Plays\r\nBIRTH | MARRIAGE | DEATH\r\nDirected by Kayla Feldman\r\n\r\nBIRTH\r\nby Amy Rosenthal\r\nIn the aftermath of their Golden Wedding celebrations, Michael and Lynda are surprised by an uninvited guest. Will Naomi's visit be the marzipan on the fruitcake, or is she a fruitcake; and has she arrived - once again - at the wrong time?\r\n\r\n                                                          MARRIAGE\r\nby Alexis Zegerman\r\n\"We deserve more in common than just being Jewish, don't we?\"\r\nOne date. Thousands of years of exile. A million possibilities.\r\n\r\nDEATH\r\nby Ryan Craig\r\nA humorous look at how ancient death rites can bring a family together, even after it's been torn apart by divorce, illness, narcissism and neurosis.\r\n\r\nA trilogy of brand new short plays by three of the UK’s leading Jewish playwrights.\r\nThe Arc is a world premiere of three brand new short plays by Ryan Craig, Amy Rosenthal and Alexis Zegerman, exploring Birth, Marriage and Death through a distinctly Jewish lens. The Arc shines a contemporary light on the cycle of Jewish life, and what it means to live as a Jew in 2023.\r\nEmanate Productions is a theatre company that focuses on nurturing talent in emerging and established artists of Jewish heritage - platforming urgent, exciting and passionate stories with an integral Jewish soul.\r\nFollowing on from their sold-out run of at Kiln Theatre in 2022, Emanate are back at Soho Theatre this summer putting contemporary Jewish stories once again on centre stage.\r\nSupported by Arts Council England.\r\nCasting to be announced.\r\nFrom Emanate Presents: A Night of New Jewish Writing, Kiln Theatre, August 2022\r\n“This was the evening that Jewish theatregoers never knew they were waiting for until it happened” - Jewish Chronicle 5*\r\n“What Emanate Productions did was revelatory – showcasing the depth of the talent pool in all facets of theatre and challenging the community to support our own.” - Jewish Renaissance 4*\r\n“Dan Wolff and Sam Thorpe-Spinks’ decision to run an event like Emanate is a welcome salve.” - Vashti\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Arc: A Trilogy of New Jewish Plays","instanceDates":"15 August-26 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"481203ADHKNHNPNCNGNJTCSMSMVBPJTVP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-15T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-15T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-26T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-26T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Theatre"},{"description":"What are you storing in the back rooms of your brain? Who’s lurking behind your eyes? Hold still. Let’s plug you in.\r\n \r\nDreams struggle with nightmares; fact arm-wrestles fiction; and truth gives lies a wedgie. A kaleidoscope of characters collide in this hallucinatory sketch comedy feast from award-winning The Awkward Silence. You wouldn’t dream of missing it. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Awkward Silence: Mind Milk","instanceDates":"4 April-5 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"611803AJRJTQRCJKHPJVJMNGMCLLCLVVV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-04T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-04T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-05T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-05T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Sketch","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"They say you can´t choose your family … Sometimes it´s the only choice that matters. THE BOY is a new play by Joakim Daun that tackles themes of migration, loss and the meaning of family. \r\nThe lives of a Man, a Boy and a Woman from different worlds and realities become intertwined over the one thing they have in common - loss. Can they find a sense of community again after having lost everything?\r\n\r\nOn a bus from an unnamed country, an unlikely friendship forms between a young unaccompanied boy and an older man; both escaping their past. Looking for a new life in a big city, their paths cross with that of a young woman attempting to deal with her own trauma. Over the course of a poignant, charming and witty 70 minutes, THE BOY explores identity, belonging, resilience and the boundless power of human connection.\r\n\r\nTHE BOY is a new play by Joakim Daun that tackles themes of migration, loss and the meaning of family in a unique, heartwarming and sensitive way. It was developed through a research & development process together with a group of diverse theatre makers from migrant and British minority background.\r\n\r\nInternationally recognised Fake Escape are the producers of the WhatsOnStage Award nominated UK and Off Broadway hit Saving Britney. Joakim Daun is a multilingual migrant writer and theatre maker based in London, creating thought-provoking and intercultural work from the perspective of the individual as well as the collective.\r\n\r\n13+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Boy","instanceDates":"17 October-4 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"491203AHHVKHKLVKBVDMQJGKNMBHPHLCT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-17T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-17T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-04T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-04T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Political","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Experience mischief and mayhem in this acclaimed stage adaptation of Dr Seuss’ The Cat In The Hat.\r\nFrom the moment his tall, red and white-striped hat appears, Sally and her brother know that the cat in the hat is the funniest, most mischievous cat they have ever met. With the trickiest of tricks and craziest of ideas, he turns a rainy afternoon into an amazing adventure.\r\nThe Cat in the Hat is a lively and engaging first theatre experience for children aged 3+, based on the best-selling book. \r\nMeet the Cat in the Hat after the show and continue the mayhem – for free!\r\nRunning time: Approximately 45 mins with no interval\r\n3+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":45,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Cat In The Hat  ","instanceDates":"21 August-23 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"715603ANHSLCJTVKJBMBSDBGLJTMRJDTS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-21T14:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-21T13:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-23T14:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-23T13:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Families","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Welcome. Welcome to The Ceremony. Thank you. You’re welcome. \r\n\r\nPlayfully exploring ritual and tradition in the modern world, The Ceremony is an improvised, interactive ritual – part sermon, part group therapy, part comedy show. Not a cult.\r\n\r\nCrafted afresh from audience responses, the show changes every single time it’s performed. We rummage through our collective pasts/presents/futures/other to see what kind of ceremony emerges. Or is that the ceremony? Who are we? What are we doing? Does this mean anything? What does meaning mean? Hmm. \r\n\r\nCome in. Take a seat. Contemplate your life. Contemplate my life. Join me. And let The Ceremony begin…\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Ceremony","instanceDates":"18 July-19 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"636603AJRQTSNDMJKHHHKRDRQLPPHTHNB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-18T21:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-18T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-19T21:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-19T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Experience the ultimate showdown as a selection of courageous clowns compete for the prestigious London Clown Festival Clong Award.\r\nThe clowns go head-to-head in a series of hilarious tasks and challenges, and the audience decides the winner.\r\nWho will be crowned the biggest idiot of all?\r\nPrevious competitors have included Natalie Palamides, Rob Duncan, Josh Glanc, Bill O'Neil, Lil Wenker and many more.\r\nHosted by Dan Lees and Neil Frost \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Clong Show","instanceDates":"6 June-6 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"712804AQTKVTMHPVJNLGSHTBVMCKQJCNK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-06T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-06T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-06T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-06T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Experience the ultimate comedy showdown as a selection of the world's best clowns, available on 20th June 2025, compete for the prestigious London Clown Festival Clong Award.\r\nThe clowns go head-to-head in a series of hilarious tasks and challenges, and the audience decides the winner.\r\nWho will be crowned the biggest idiot of all?\r\nSee the clowns as they attempt to complete impossible challenges in order to win the ultimate prize, The Clong!\r\nLondon Clown Festival 2024 Clong Award was won by Tom, the venue technician.\r\nPrevious winners can be found listed... somewhere, we’re almost sure of that.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Clong Show Jun25","instanceDates":"20 June-20 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"617003AVKVKQMGGTGGCHCHPQQKHSCMMRJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-20T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-20T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-20T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-20T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Six of the world's funniest clowns compete for the highly prestigious THE CLONG award. \r\nWho will be crowned the biggest idiot of all?\r\nHosted by award-winning clown duo Dan Lees and Neil Frost aka The Establishment.\r\nSee the clowns as they attempt to complete impossible challenges in order to be win the ultimate prize, The Clong!\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Clong Show.","instanceDates":"13 July-13 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"545003AKKPQRSHSCHTKLKTJDTNDMNCLKM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-13T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-13T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-13T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-13T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"What happens when the cool kids of the 90s are in the depths of middle age? Are they still hip, or is the vibe more hip replacement? Join Sleeper’s Louise Wener and special guests comprising of some of the most iconic names from 90’s pop culture in this recording of her brand new podcast. Each show will see Louise talk to her peers from the worlds of music, film, comedy, art, sport and literature as they reflect on that golden era, whilst comparing it with how they are navigating their midlife. And together we decide if they are doing their mid-life crises right! \r\n\r\n16+ recommended","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Crisis Right with Louise Wener ","instanceDates":"10 July-10 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"482203AJTKLLSTQJHVDRTTPRKHMCHNGMD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-10T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-10T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-10T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-10T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A psychedelic punk rock riff on what path you choose, which identity politics you embrace or whether it’s easier to be a butterfly dreaming of being ‘Chinese’\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Dao of Unrepresentative British Chinese Experience","instanceDates":"19 June-13 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"514604APCGVSKDBMQMNQMMNKNVPSNQSTJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-06-19T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-06-19T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-13T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-13T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Welcome to THE DARK ROOM – the world’s only live-action, text-based adventure game. It’s strange, insane and addictive – it’s a choose-your-own-adventure, so choose it! \r\nWINNER – CHORTLE Legend Of Lockdown 2020\r\nSOLD OUT – Edinburgh Fringe 2023\r\n\r\nWelcome to THE DARK ROOM – the world’s only live-action, text-based adventure game. It’s strange, insane and addictive – it’s a choose-your-own-adventure, so choose it! \r\n\r\nHow do you play? The audience is trapped in a retro videogame with a sadistic end-of-level boss. Choose your options, survive the abuse simulator that is the improv comedy overlord John Robertson, and escape to win £1000 – or, be brutally murdered by the rest of the crowd!\r\n \r\nNow, will you:\r\n\r\nFind the Light Switch \r\n18Go North? \r\nA.\tAbandon Hope?\r\n\r\nNow it’s 10th year, this high-octane interactive show is the brainchild of comedian & cult leader John Robertson. Filled with stand-up, appalling prizes and more audience chanting than you’d get at a protest – it’s a gut-busting rock n’ roll geek experience for everyone who buys a ticket.\r\n\r\nJohn has performed The Dark Room to crowds of thousands at comedy and gaming festivals around the world including Insomnia Gaming Festival, London Film & ComicCon, Sci-Fi Weekender, Edinburgh Fringe Festival, FringeWorld Perth, Leeds International Festival, Sheffield Doc/Fest, and to millions online on his Twitch Partner channel: www.twitch.tv/robbotron\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Dark Room","instanceDates":"3 May-3 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"538003APNDHCDMLRGPCPPMLVLMBJPCGHP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-03T23:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-03T22:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-03T23:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-03T22:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Description / copy\r\nWINNER – CHORTLE Legend Of Lockdown 2020\r\nSOLD OUT – Edinburgh Fringe 2019\r\n\r\nWelcome to THE DARK ROOM – the world’s only live-action, text-based adventure game. It’s strange, insane and addictive – it’s a choose-your-own-adventure, so choose it! \r\n\r\nHow do you play? The audience is trapped in a retro videogame with a sadistic end-of-level boss. Choose your options, survive the abuse simulator that is the improv comedy overlord John Robertson, and escape to win £1000 – or, be brutally murdered by the rest of the crowd!\r\n \r\nNow, will you:\r\n\r\nFind the Light Switch \r\n18Go North? \r\nA.\tAbandon Hope?\r\n\r\nNow it’s 10th year, this high-octane interactive show is the brainchild of comedian & cult leader John Robertson. Filled with stand-up, appalling prizes and more audience chanting than you’d get at a protest – it’s a gut-busting rock n’ roll geek experience for everyone who buys a ticket.\r\n\r\nJohn has performed The Dark Room to crowds of thousands at comedy and gaming festivals around the world including Insomnia Gaming Festival, London Film & ComicCon, Sci-Fi Weekender, Edinburgh Fringe Festival, FringeWorld Perth, Leeds International Festival, Sheffield Doc/Fest, and to millions online on his Twitch Partner channel: www.twitch.tv/robbotron\r\n\r\n\r\n“NOT TO BE MISSED!”\r\nGuardian\r\n“What a marvellous, maddening concept this is from the twisted mind of Robertson”\r\nChortle\r\n“Will have you crying with laughter”\r\nBroadway Baby\r\n“Watching people tackle the challenge and fail is one of the funniest sights around. Don’t miss it.” The Daily Telegraph, Sydney\r\n“One of the most innovative and original comedy shows around”\r\nManchester Evening News\r\n“Loud, raucous and brilliantly daft, this is unrelenting fun for everyone”\r\n ThreeWeeks\r\n\r\n“You have to see the Dark Room at least once in your life” \r\nThe Scottish Sun\r\n\r\n“You must see this show” \r\n British Comedy Guide\r\n\r\n“A game of passionate nostalgia” \r\n The Skinny\r\n\r\n“Something of a masterpiece” \r\n Fringe Review\r\n\r\nTwitter: @Robbotron\r\nFacebook: Johnrobertsoncomedy\r\nTikTok: @RobbotronTwitch\r\n\r\n18+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Dark Room [old]","instanceDates":"5 May-12 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"464803ALCJDQQPKQCJRHMCCQMQRDLJKMR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-05T23:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-05T22:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-12T23:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-12T23:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Storytelling","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Performance Art","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"John Binjuice lived a quiet life, until everyone in his town suddenly transformed into terrifying beasts.\r\nWith horns.\r\nBig, scary horns.\r\nNow, John is the last human left. He has, so far, resisted the horn. But how long can his humanity last?\r\nA new solo show from Jacob Aldcroft (‘He has funny legs’-Philippe Gaulier), watch as John attempts to save ALL HUMANITY through lots of shouting, running and jumping, song, dance, and more vodka than is safe.\r\nPrepare to laugh (a lot), cry (a bit), and maybe do a little wee.\r\nDirected by Natalie Simone\r\nDesign by Alice Sales\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Day I Got The Horn","instanceDates":"17 June-17 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"617203AKGJMJMRQVNKBRSHKGRPJRSRBRS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-17T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-17T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-17T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-17T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Elmer Adventure ","instanceDates":"20 December-4 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"651403ADVTCKHJJSNBVHHDSDKQQVPTKRN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-20T10:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-20T10:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-04T13:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-04T13:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Families","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Described by Jay Leno as the best joke writer in America, by Gary Delaney as the best joke writer in the world, and by \"Weird Al\" Yankovic as one of the funniest people on the planet, Emo Philips has performed over 7000 times, with full-length concert specials on HBO (from the Hasty Pudding Theatre) and Channel 4 (from the Playhouse Theatre in the West End); award-winning albums (his breakthrough being \"E=MO Squared\"); and memorable acting roles on TV shows such as \"Miami Vice\" and in movies such as \"UHF\" and \"Weird: The Al Yankovic story\" (in which Emo plays Salvador Dali opposite Conan O'Brien's Andy Warhol).\r\nEmo hopes to tour the UK again but has no clue when that might be, so if seeing him live is on your bucket list...\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Emo Philips Experience","instanceDates":"29 November-30 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"571403ANVQVQRHMDDHRLDPMDLBDKQJTGB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-29T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-29T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-30T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-30T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Side-splitting, stiff-upper-lipped hilarity from multi-award-winning comedy duo Dan Lees and Neil Frost. These charming and eccentric idiots bring the belly laughs with expert clowning and quick fired wit.\r\n\r\nBEST COMEDY ADELAIDE FRINGE WEEKLY AWARD WINNER\r\n★★★★★ ‘Off-the-wall, zany, crazy, very funny.. two comic geniuses’ Glam Adelaide\r\n\r\n16+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Establishment: Le Bureau De Strange","instanceDates":"14 June-14 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"478403AJGKMRKSLGVLPJBQRSGQJGBBLMC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-14T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-14T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-14T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-14T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Award Winning Comic, Writer & Performer Kat Bond brings you The Eye Show, a parody diagnosis show inspired by a real-life diagnosis.\r\n\r\nWhen Kat was told she had a degenerative eye condition, she realised the only sensible thing to do was to make a comedy show about it. Wink, wink.   \r\n\r\nCombining an inimitable mix of character comedy, storytelling, clown, warmth, hope and Liza Minelli, we join Kat as she embarks on staging EVERYTHING anyone's ever thought about eyes, visual impairment, accessibility and able anxiety.   \r\n\r\nOnly rule is you can’t feel sorry for her.   \r\n\r\nDon’t bring tissues. 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Eye Show (Work in Progress)","instanceDates":"19 August-20 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"733603ABSDQGHSMSJDQBVGJBHSVGRQQHS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-19T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-19T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-20T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-20T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Access","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"60 minutes, 12 notes and three idiots. Dan Lees, Tom Penn and Cammy Sinclair bring their award-winning show to London for the first time. Musical mayhem and expert clowning from the greatest band in the whole wide world... ever. Part of London Clown Festival 2024.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Flop: A Band of Idiots","instanceDates":"10 July-10 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"543204AGMQPHGVKPRDBDGHLRTVQCRSBNT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-10T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-10T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-10T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-10T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Patchworks Ensemble makes its UK debut with an exhilarating new version of their hit show presented by The National Centre for the Performing Arts, India.\r\nJoin us as we enter Mumbai's pulsating underground club scene and step into the lives of the city’s electrifying drag kings. \r\nThe Gentlemen’s Club show is headlined by Rocky (AKA Shammsher) whose act is a tribute to the legendary Shammi Kapoor and the golden era of Hindi cinema. Alongside Rocky is an ensemble of drag performers who will transport you to Mumbai’s gritty underbelly where people are free to be whoever they desire. \r\nFeaturing a dazzling mix of cabaret-style performances and Bollywood dance, this show follows a provocative narrative celebrating Indian women and their exploration of masculinity.\r\nPatchworks Ensemble makes its UK debut with an exhilarating new version of their hit show presented by The National Centre for the Performing Arts, India.\r\n\r\nAge guidance 14+ (recommendation) \r\n\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":80,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Gentlemen’s Club   ","instanceDates":"1 October-12 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"565803AVLGJJNMCVKQGRRDQLVJNPQVMJV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-01T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-01T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-10-12T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-10-12T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Drag","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"India/South Asian heritage"},{"description":"The long-running cult hit The George Lucas Talk Show makes its way to London for the very first time! Comedian Connor Ratliff (Dead Eyes, Marvellous Mrs. Maisel) appears as George Lucas, the creator of Star Wars, and interviews guests like a “normal talk show”. He is joined by sidekick Watto, played by Griffin Newman (Blank Check, The Tick), and show producer Patrick Cotnoir. The show ran for over 6 years at the UCB Theatre in New York and has been streaming on Twitch since 2020. Previous guests include Seth Meyers, Weird Al, Whoopi Goldberg, Jon Hamm, Kevin Smith, Nicole Byer, Ira Glass, Lea Thompson, Ben Schwartz, Peter Serafinowicz, Ahmed Best, Tony Hale, David K. Harbour, D’Arcy Carden, Solo writer Jon Kasdan, Rogue One writers Gary Whitta and Chris Weitz, and musicians like Aimee Mann. Connor Ratliff is an actor, improviser, and stand-up comic from New York. He is a former contributor for the Chris Gethard Show and the host of the hit podcast, Dead Eyes. His work can be seen on The Marvelous Mrs. Maisel, Search Party, Last Week Tonight with John Oliver, Late Night with Seth Meyers, and live at Raaaaaatscraaaaaps in New York City. @connorratliff Griffin Newman is an actor and podcaster from New York. He’s most known for his roles as Arthur on the Amazon Prime version of The Tick and as Orko on the Netflix adaptation of Masters of the Universe. He also hosts Blank Check, a comedic film podcast, with the Atlantic’s David Sims. @grifflightning Patrick Cotnoir is a talent booker and generally funny guy from New York. His past credits include talent booking for Marvel and The Chris Gethard Show. He currently handles guests for Raaaaaatscraaaaaps, the George Lucas Talk Show, and the Exactly Right (My Favorite Murder) podcast network. @patrickcotnoir\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The George Lucas Talk Show","instanceDates":"7 April-8 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"457603ARVGHVTMCQCPDSPPBCNCDVJBMHN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-07T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-07T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-04-08T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-04-08T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Ten years ago, The Good Immigrant was crowdfunded in three days, declared a Sunday Times bestseller, and described by Zadie Smith as 'a must-read'. The publishing industry had said no. The public said otherwise.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Good Immigrant: LIVE 10th Anniversary","instanceDates":"13 September-13 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"720203AGCQTVMJVVQMSMPJBVRVJPNHNVD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-13T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-13T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-13T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-13T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The Grindles present Fancy Rat. \r\nIn a kingdom where laughter is forbidden, one rat (and a fancy one at that) attempts to bring merriment to this grim realm before it’s too late.\r\nThis show promises songs and dances in the Music Hall style, delivered by Marny Godden and Tom Turner. This is the tale of a London Fancy Rat.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Grindles: Fancy Rat","instanceDates":"10 July-10 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"543403AGGDBMLVSRPHPGGMTHBJTMLRBSV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-10T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-10T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-10T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-10T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A mouse took a stroll through the deep dark wood...\r\nTall Stories’ much-loved magical, musical adaptation of the classic picture book by Julia Donaldson and Axel Scheffler returns by popular demand, celebrating the show’s 25th anniversary. \r\n \r\nOn a daring adventure in search of hazelnuts, Mouse meets the cunning Fox, the eccentric old Owl and the high-spirited Snake. Will the story of the scary Gruffalo save Mouse from ending up as dinner for these hungry woodland creatures? After all, there’s no such thing as a Gruffalo–is there? \r\n \r\nSongs, laughs and mischievous fun for children aged 3 and up and their grown-ups, from Tall Stories, creators of imaginative storytelling theatre, where everything is possible. \r\n3+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":55,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Gruffalo","instanceDates":"12 December-13 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"721603ANBRRGRDLPVPHMVJTBMSHPHPNRH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-12T10:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-12T10:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-13T13:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-13T13:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Families","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join your favourite Guardian writers for an evening of candid conversations, witty remarks and surprises as we look back on the year-defining stories of 2026. Description/copy – main copy\tOur lineup of writers, including Zoe Williams, Jonathan Liew and more to be announced, will take to the stage for our end-of-year event. We'll revisit the year’s biggest headlines and investigations, the sporting highs and lows and the cultural moments that took over our feeds. With archive footage, front pages and audience polls, expect the conversation to be as entertaining as it is insightful. \r\n\r\nFor fans of our much-loved A year in Westminster event, we’ve got you covered. After the interval, political editor Pippa Crerar and political sketch writer John Crace will join us to skewer the biggest stories from Westminster and beyond.\r\n\r\nWe'll finish the evening with the Guardian big quiz: a lively, interactive look back at the year. With plenty of audience participation and live voting, this is your chance to settle some of 2026's biggest debates once and for all. Is The Odyssey the best film of the year? Are social media curfew for teens pointless? And do gen z and millennials have it worse than gen x?\r\n\r\nJoin us and celebrate another remarkable year of Guardian journalism with the writers whose work you've been reading all year and with fellow Guardian readers who are just as curious and passionate as you. 16+ (Strong language, references to racism, cultural and political issues. Check webpage for up to date content advice). Running time incl. interval.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":150,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Guardian’s Year In Review 2026","instanceDates":"1 December-1 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"748803ANNQLQHSRMJMKVMBCNSTSJSPTDM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-01T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-01T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-01T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-01T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Podcast","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Talk","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Podcast","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Podcast","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Talk"},{"description":"Comedian Deborah Frances-White & comic and singer Grace Petrie host this very special episode of The Guilty Feminist - in our Road to Gilead season. TV writer, national treasure and LGBTQ+ rights advocate RUSSELL T. DAVIES (Dr Who, It’s a Sin, Queer as Folk) talks to us live on stage about dangers for the LGBTQ+ community with the rise of the far right – and how the stories we tell make a huge difference to the world we live in. Don’t miss this thought provoking, engaging, inspiring show - including music from Grace Petrie.16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Guilty Feminist","instanceDates":"6 December-6 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"672803ASQJJJMHSRJSJGNNQRRQJBMSRVN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-06T14:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-06T14:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-12-06T14:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-12-06T14:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"For ten years The Guilty Feminist has championed the best in comedy. Our guests and co-hosts are among the finest comedians in the world and many of them will be taking shows to the Edinburgh Fringe this year. We’re thrilled to give you the chance to see some exclusive previews as well as the chance to discover some of the stories behind the shows. Full line-ups to be announced, but book early as these shows will sell out.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Guilty Feminist – Edinburgh Preview Showcase","instanceDates":"7 July-14 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"727803ADHVKRSKPDVRTCMQSRKGSGNLMND","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-07T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-07T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-14T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-14T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Less of a podcast and more of a global phenomenon, The Guilty Feminist, hosted by Deborah Frances-White and featuring world class guests, is part comedy, part deep dive discussion and part activism. Examining our noble goals as 21st century feminists and our hypocrisies and insecurities that undermine those goals, The Guilty Feminist has had a spectacular 100 million downloads in seven years. This is the show that proves you don’t have to be perfect to be a force for meaningful change. Come join The Guilty Feminist live and be part of this joyful movement. 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Guilty Feminist.","instanceDates":"30 May-31 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"466803ANBBVDPQJTJSSKKDQVLTTRDCMGM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-30T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-30T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-31T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-31T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Feminist","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Less of a podcast and more of a global phenomenon, The Guilty Feminist, hosted by Deborah Frances-White and featuring world class guests, is part comedy, part deep dive discussion and part activism.\r\n\r\nExamining our noble goals as 21st century feminists and our hypocrisies and insecurities that undermine those goals, The Guilty Feminist has had a spectacular 100 million downloads in seven years. This is the show that proves you don’t have to be perfect to be a force for meaningful change. Come join The Guilty Feminist live and be part of this joyful movement.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Guilty Feminist.","instanceDates":"11 August-19 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"480803APKSHRQKTNDRHMVVQJSLRBPSHJS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-11T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-11T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-19T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-19T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Feminist","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Comedy"},{"description":"Less of a podcast and more of a global phenomenon, The Guilty Feminist, hosted by Deborah Frances-White and featuring world class guests, is part comedy, part deep dive discussion and part activism.\r\n\r\nExamining our noble goals as 21st century feminists and our hypocrisies and insecurities that undermine those goals, The Guilty Feminist has had a spectacular 100 million downloads in seven years. This is the show that proves you don’t have to be perfect to be a force for meaningful change. Come join The Guilty Feminist live and be part of this joyful movement.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Guilty Feminist.","instanceDates":"3 November-10 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"503203AVGBLMTLJQBRGPCPMSPMCHRSHGB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-03T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-03T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-11-10T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-11-10T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The hit comedy podcast returns\r\nExamining our noble goals as 21st century feminists and our hypocrisies and insecurities that undermine those goals, The Guilty Feminist has had over 100 million downloads. This is the show that proves you don’t have to be perfect to be a force for meaningful change.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Guilty Feminist.","instanceDates":"18 July-19 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"640203ATJMDRCJTCVMDBCLRCCVCNHPNVC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-18T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-18T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-19T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-19T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"We're delighted to partner with @thehennahparty to create a queer alternative to traditional henna nights. Expect live performances, music, dance, poetry, chaat, chat and, of course, henna!\r\n\r\nSee the matinee performance of Vitamin D on Saturday 14th September, and then join us in the cabaret space after the show for this free amazing afternoon.\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Hen - Nah Party","instanceDates":"14 September-14 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"570803AHLHHDHHSGDHJBHVLDSHTSNHVND","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-14T15:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-14T14:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-14T15:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-14T14:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"They have their own Channel 4 TV show, a chart-topping podcast and now they’re coming to Soho Theatre with a brand-new work in progress show; it’s the one and only Horne Section! \r\n  \r\nThey are officially \"Britain's Funniest Band\" (according to the Guardian), so following their hit BBC Radio 4 series, regular appearances on Crouchy’s Year Late Euros and The Last Leg, a chart-topping podcast and many years of sell-out shows at the Edinburgh Fringe Festival and London’s West End, don’t miss everyone’s favourite Dictionary Corner regulars on 8 out of 10 Cats Does Countdown and the first band to ever host Never Mind The Buzzcocks.  \r\n  \r\nFive outstanding musicians, one non-musical stand up, there’ll be comedy, songs, enthusiastic dancing and a lot of mucking about. A unique show from the hugely talented band and Alex Horne, the creator and co-host of the BAFTA and National Comedy Award winning Taskmaster.  \r\n  \r\n“endlessly charming, offbeat humour”  \r\n  ★★★★ The Independent  \r\n  \r\n“marvellously over-the-top\"  \r\n★★★★ Daily Mail  \r\n  \r\n“funny and delightful… this is a welcome escapist treat”    \r\n★★★★ Heat \r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Horne Section: Work in Progress","instanceDates":"9 October-14 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"480603ABMVQQGSHBGTCMJMSGSGSDCTSCS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-09T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-09T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-14T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-14T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Work In Progress","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Queer, messy and f*cking hilarious.\r\nAfter a year away, the hottest ticket in town is back. Where the riskiest and most diverse acts let loose, all backed by a live band. It's late-night done right, hosted by the unforgettable Reuben Kaye. \r\nA line up of the best in comedy, circus, cabaret and everywhere in between to be announced!\r\n18+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Kaye Hole – Hosted by Reuben Kaye","instanceDates":"19 September-19 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"732003AGKDKTCCNKGTJRSRNVTTMMBJNQP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-19T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-19T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-19T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-19T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Comedy"},{"description":"Love comedy?  Love queers?  Bored of cis-male comedians?  Don’t worry, The LOL Word is BACK! \r\n\r\nYour fave queer women, trans and non-binary comedy collective is bringing you another epically gay stand-up show!  \r\n\r\nThe LOL Word has hosted sell-out runs/ absolute ragers at The Edinburgh, Brighton and Cambridge Fringe Festivals, The Southbank Centre and VAULT Festival, and they’re back at Soho Theatre with another hilarious mixed-bill show!  Expect a heck-load of queer comedy talent, absolutely no cis-male comics and plenty of punching the patriarchy. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The LOL Word","instanceDates":"20 January-20 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"578403AJVMMTDBMBMPLGBDBRDPTNTNNSB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-20T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-20T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-20T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-20T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Love comedy?  Love queers?  Bored of cis-male comedians?  Don’t worry, The LOL Word is BACK! \r\n\r\nYour fave queer women, trans and non-binary comedy collective is bringing you another epically gay stand-up show!  \r\n\r\nThe LOL Word has hosted sell-out runs/ absolute ragers at The Edinburgh, Brighton and Cambridge Fringe Festivals, The Southbank Centre and VAULT Festival, and they’re back at Soho Theatre with another hilarious mixed-bill show!  Expect a heck-load of queer comedy talent, absolutely no cis-male comics and plenty of punching the patriarchy. \r\n\r\nThe Guardian\r\n \r\n“Hilarious, slick and smart … The LOL Word is transforming comedy”\r\n \r\n“It’s refreshing and revitalising to watch: they are energetic and exciting, oozing with passion. The LOL Word is proof that you don’t have to mock the marginalised to be funny.” \r\n\r\n\"A new generation of comics retaliating against the old template of comedy\"\r\n \r\nBroadway Baby\r\n \r\n“this show is fierce, fiery and ever so funny”\r\n    \r\n \r\nThe Peg\r\n \r\n“had us crying with laughter … if you’re a fan of affordable, inclusive, abundantly queer comedy I would urge you to go see this show.”\r\n    \r\n \r\nDIVA\r\n\r\n\"Smart, insightful, hilarious and completely relatable”\r\n \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The LOL Word.","instanceDates":"9 May-3 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"427003ATDHPQVQTQVBHGQHSQKRGHJPPCN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-09T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-09T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-03T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-03T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Love comedy?  Love queers?  Bored of cis-male comedians?  Don’t worry, The LOL Word is BACK! \r\n\r\nYour fave queer women, trans and non-binary comedy collective is bringing you another epically gay stand-up show!  \r\n\r\nThe LOL Word has hosted sell-out runs/ absolute ragers at The Edinburgh, Brighton and Cambridge Fringe Festivals, The Southbank Centre and VAULT Festival, and they’re back at Soho Theatre with another hilarious mixed-bill show!  Expect a heck-load of queer comedy talent, absolutely no cis-male comics and plenty of punching the patriarchy. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The LOL Word.","instanceDates":"15 January-12 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"518404ARBKHSMBNPJLDHHDBBDTDBSKRMD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-01-15T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-01-15T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-12T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-12T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"The Moon has disappeared. The Lunatics worship her anyway.\r\n\r\n A psychedelic prog-rock band, inspired by Classical Indian and Greek sounds, brought to you by Liver & Lung, the team behind Melur The Musical and The Bollywood Guide to Revenge. \r\n\r\nPerformed by Shafeeq Shajahan, Vasilis Konstantinides, Mike Keating and William Patrick-Owen. \r\n\r\nJoin the congregation. 18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Lunatics","instanceDates":"26 August-27 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"733803ALGMVQLNGJSQJTTLHKMHSGRLBJC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-26T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-26T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-27T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-27T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"India/South Asian heritage"},{"description":"The Mayor and his Daughter are in crisis. The soul of their beloved village is in tatters, besieged by the demonic forces of modern Britain. But there’s a light in the darkness; when they discover a sacred tome - a box set of Russell Howard’s Good News (Series 2). They make it their mission to repair their fractured community with laughter. \r\nDirected by Comedians’ Choice Award winning absurdist comedian Joz Norris and produced by award-winning sketch comedian Rosie Nicholls (Grubby Little Mitts).  \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Mayor and His Daughter: A Genuine Appreciation of Comedy","instanceDates":"28 May-30 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"709203AQJGBQNPDMGCDRDKNHPNJQGMTGV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-28T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-28T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-30T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-30T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Sketch","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"The McGuffin Film Society Returns – Again!\r\nAfter a triumphant return to its home venue following a 22-year absence, the McGuffin Film Society is back for a third installment of its ongoing celebration of Waltham Forest’s rich and often surprising contribution to cinema – past and present.\r\nWhat do Alfred Hitchcock, Chiwetel Ejiofor, William Morris, Maggie O’Neill, Charles Hawtrey, Ken Russell, Thandiwe Newton, Broncho Billy, Charlie Chaplin, Naomi Ackie, Leslie Phillips, Captain Birdseye, Peter Greenaway and the Bonzo Dog Doo-Dah Band all have in common?\r\n Simple: they’re part of Waltham Forest’s cinematic story – and just a few of the names appearing (in one form or another) on the big screen, as the McGuffin Film Society continues its affectionate tribute to the borough’s offbeat and often unsung film heritage.\r\nExpect a new hand-picked programme each time – spanning feature films, TV dramas, documentaries, shorts, silent comedies, newsreels, music videos, and cinematic curios from local and legendary movie-makers alike.\r\nSpecial thanks to Bill Hodgson and the McGuffin Film Society for their work back in 2003, helping to preserve this beloved venue as a space for film and entertainment.\r\nEach event features a completely different line-up, so whether you're joining us for the first time or coming back for more, you’re in for something new. Full details of the next evening’s programme will be announced soon.\r\n16+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":150,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The McGuffin Film Society and Soho Theatre presents Waltham Forest on Film","instanceDates":"6 September-6 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"651803ALJPHPRPLRKMBRPVVBGPHDNLQLT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-06T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-06T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-06T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-06T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Studio 1","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"This Christmas, Olivier Award-winning theatre company Little Bulb (Wolf Witch Giant Fairy, CBeebie’s Christmas Pantos) invite you to experience an audacious reimagining of E. T. A Hoffman’s classic tale as a fun-filled, madcap, magical quest… with not a tutu in sight! \r\n  \r\nWhen two squabbling siblings receive a mysterious nutcracker from their flamboyant Aunty on Christmas Eve, it sets them off on a fantastical journey into ‘The Mousey Realm’. Can they put their differences aside and stop the evil, many-headed Mouse King before he ruins Christmas? Only time will tell… \r\n  \r\nThis bold and brilliantly silly tale is brought to ingenious theatrical life with clever cardboard creations, comic characters and a chorus of cheeky musical mice. It’s crammed full of action, laugh-out-loud comedy, and a sleigh-load of festive bangers that’ll have you dancing in your seat - with just the right amount of cheese. ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Nutcracker and the Mouse King","instanceDates":"22 December-3 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"741003APPLVCPTDPVLPDTQNQGTTLLTLHC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-22T13:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-22T13:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-01-03T14:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-01-03T14:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Families","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Family","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"A rhythmic circus celebration of Palestinian life, culture, and enduring hope. \r\nStep into an unforgettable experience with The Palestinian Circus! Inspired by the traditions of Palestinian Dabkeh, a joyful folk dance, and its iconic rhythm Wahdeh w Nos, this uplifting circus show is a cultural spectacle for all ages. Through a unique physical language, we celebrate life and togetherness in an inclusive demonstration of heritage, identity, and collective freedom. \r\n The Palestinian Circus is a non-profit organisation bringing hope and connection to communities across Palestine through circus arts. Blending Dabkeh with contemporary circus, this unique artistic language becomes part of our dance, our daily life, and our resistance. \r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Palestinian Circus: Step and a Half","instanceDates":"31 July-2 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"715803ADHSVKQBTBLVKDQKKVGDGBPPHSV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-31T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-31T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-02T14:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-02T13:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Dance","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"He is Mr. Cardboard and this is his PASSION \r\n \r\nIs Mr.Cardboard your absurd imaginary friend or your all powerful savior? Is Mr.Cardboard a messiah of play or can he just make you a cardboard animal? All we know is Mr. Cardboard returns to the Land Of Cardboard to face his most trying hour yet! You're along for the ride in this \"beautifully stupid\" (Natalie Palamides) theatrical clown tour de force and solo show by Miles Calderon (Netflix, Stamptown, UCB).\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Passion of Mr Cardboard","instanceDates":"6 November-14 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"752803AHQLHGMTNGGHLKJJVNMLQQQHSGR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-06T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-06T22:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-14T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-14T22:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Part of National Theatre Connections","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Periodicals, created by Sian Owen, performed by LSC Expressive Arts","instanceDates":"2 May-2 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"539203ANBHVJCLHQBGRKQHKSVVQBRKQNL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-02T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-02T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-02T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-02T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Part of National Theatre Connections","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Periodicals, created by Sian Owen, performed by Mulberry UTC Theatre Company","instanceDates":"3 May-3 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"538603APRNBTPVKSCQBNJQPKNRRMNCRTC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-03T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-03T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-03T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-03T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Spend an evening inside the genius comedic mind of Peter Serafinowicz.\r\nShowcasing cutting edge face-swap technology - developed by Peter himself - the master impressionist delivers a show packed with his trademark absurd comedy, beloved faces and characters and, of course, uncanny impersonations. Having appeared in TV favourites (Amandaland, Parks & Recreation, I’m Alan Partridge), cult classics (Spaced, Look Around You, The Peter Serafinowicz Show) and beloved movies (Star Wars: The Phantom Menace, Shaun of the Dead, Guardians of the Galaxy), Peter has established himself as one of Britain’s most inventive and distinctive comic talents. Join a true original on his first ever solo tour: The Peter Serafinowicz Live Show!\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Peter Serafinowicz Live Show","instanceDates":"25 February-26 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"751203AMBLVJLKTVCRJGNDSRCSMNKPTSB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-25T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-25T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-26T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-26T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"AUDREY AND TOLLY ARE ON TOUR! You've heard them and now it's time to see them IN THE FLESH!  Your favourite girlies, big sisters, besties and agony aunts are hitting the road and bringing you everything you love about the podcast in real life. We're talking dilemmas, special guests, undiluted chat and so much more. \r\n \r\nIt's going to be a night of cackling, gist and joy in your home town! So bring the vibes and we will do the rest! \r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Receipts Podcast Live","instanceDates":"9 May-9 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"636403ASPGVSLDQGJGJKMVSBPHHLGCPLR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-09T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-09T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-09T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-09T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Uh oh, Soho… it’s about to get spooky.\r\nThis Halloween, the Master and his royal servant Gregor must perform The Ritual and collect fresh blood before midnight — or face eternal dust. A gothic vampire comedy where nothing ever goes to plan. Do you dare accept their invitation?\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Ritual","instanceDates":"30 October-31 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"751803ANGBNRSLGNPKCLKSQCCGTJTQNMS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-30T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-30T22:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-31T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-31T22:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Comedian, author, actor and national treasure Rosie Jones is getting her comedy pals (including Katherine Ryan, Nish Kumar and many more) together for one big stand-up extravaganza, celebrating the Rosie Jones Foundation. ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":140,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Rosie Jones Foundation Comedy Gala ","instanceDates":"4 November-4 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"663203ADQJJCGJRNGVPCMCMBSSBVTPCCJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-04T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-04T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-04T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-04T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":""},{"description":"Aris has spent her whole life running away, but even at the edge of the world her problems are there to meet her. \r\n\r\nInspired by stories of yōkai, monsters from Japanese folklore, The Runaway Effect is a modern fairytale exploring self-preservation, self-acceptance and abandonment. Brought to life with puppetry, live sound and experimental multimedia, we travel through icy landscapes filled with supernatural entities.  \r\n  \r\nWhether these creatures are helpful, mischievous, malevolent, or entirely in her head, Aris must find out what they want to find her way home.  \r\n  \r\nPraise for Diana's previous work:  \r\nTheatre Weekly: 4 stars - “Beautifully crafted storytelling”  \r\n\r\n \r\nADVENTURES IN THEATRELAND - 4 stars - “not just a performance but an essential experience”  \r\n\r\nThe Stage: “[Feng] is a vibrant, versatile, and engaging performer”  \r\n\r\n \r\nScotsman: “Well worth seeing and savouring”  \r\n  \r\n\r\nCo-creators/ Performers: Diana Feng, Yojiro  \r\n\r\nPuppet Designer/ Maker: Mikayla R. Teodoro  \r\n\r\nSpecial Thanks to: Center 151 & Bold Elephant .\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Runaway Effect (Work in Progress)","instanceDates":"24 August-25 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"733404AQJVCSCNRBVPHSKRQBCKJNQDBPK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-24T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-24T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-25T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-25T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Bebe Cave’s critically-acclaimed dark comedy of delusion, desperation and dreams.\r\n\r\nBetsy Bitterly is an aspiring actress in 1930s Hollywood, so desperate to become a star that she might just sacrifice herself along the way.\r\n\r\nThrough a series of \"screen tests\" for roles that could change her life, Betsy herself changes in ways she never expected in her never ending quest to \"make it\". But what does \"making it\" really mean? And when do you let go of the dream?\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Screen Test","instanceDates":"10 July-12 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"618403AMMPNMGBGHRTJRSCMKDLQPVQLTK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-10T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-10T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-12T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-12T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Ahead of opening Soho Theatre Walthamstow, join the Soho Theatre team and guests Amrou Al-Kadhi, Sikisa Bostwick-Barnes to dig deeper into the serious business of comedy.\r\nKey talking points will include the process of becoming a comedy producer, drag and comedy writing and directing, getting an agent, and building a drag or comedy hour. We hope the event will demystify parts of the industry that are difficult to find ways into, through a panel discussion from industry leaders followed by a Q&A.\r\nGuests are:\r\nAmrou Al-Kadhi\r\nAmrou Al-Kadhi's solo drag show, GLAMROU, has toured internationally and has had several sold out shows at the Soho Theatre. Their debut feature film as writer/director, LAYLA (Film4/BFI), opened Sundance Film Festival in 2024. Their debut book, LIFE AS A UNICORN (Harper Collins) won the Somerset Maugham award and the Polari First Book Prize, and as a screenwriter, they wrote the finale of Apple's LITTLE AMERICA (S1), and episodes for THE WATCH (BBC America) and Hollyoaks. They have numerous TV shows and films in development.\r\n\r\n\r\nSikisa Bostwick-Barnes\r\nFrom South London, Barbadian citizen Sikisa has become one of the most exciting acts in the UK, having delighted crowds with her fearless and vivacious personality and immediate warmth and likability.\r\nShe won the public’s vote in the 2017 BBC New Comedy Award competition, for which she was a finalist. Since then, Sikisa’s TV appearances include Live at the Apollo (BBC); Stand Up Sketch Show (ITV2), Jonathan Ross’ Comedy Club (ITV), The Dog Ate My Homework (CBBC), Live at Comedy Central, Pie And A Pint (Comedy Central) and Period Dramas (BBC 3). Her radio and podcast credits include Off Menu, Films to be Buried with, Wheel Of Misfortune (BBC Radio 1), The Leak and Mach Fest (BBC Radio Wales).\r\nSikisa was a part of the Soho Theatre Young Company and is a hot favourite on the UK comedy circuit, regularly performing and hosting at nights such as Comedy Store, Angel Comedy Club, The 99 Club, Frog & Bucket, Monkey Barrel, Komedia Comedy Club, Top Secret Comedy Club and The Boat Show.\r\nShe took her debut stand up hour Life of the Party to the Edinburgh Fringe in August 2022, and this year her sophomore show Hear Me Out received critical acclaim with 4 and 5 star reviews up at the Festival, and a run at Soho Theatre.\r\n\r\n\r\nJet Vevers\r\nJet is the Comedy Programmer for Soho Theatre Walthamstow, bringing the best comedy and live performance to the borough of Waltham Forest. Jet is also a live comedy director, working with the likes of Sarah Keyworth, Olga Koch and Nabil Abdulrashid. Jet directed Sarah Keyworth’s show My Eyes Are Up Here which won the Melbourne International Comedy Festival Award for Most Outstanding Show in April 2024.\r\n\r\nLee Griffiths is Soho Theatre’s Comedy Producer \r\n\r\nPlease email engagement@sohotheatre.com if you have any access needs\r\nNB: The panel event is repeated in the day.  Please only book for one event. \r\nAhead of opening Soho Theatre Walthamstow we’re meeting with hundreds of local residents and working with ambitious and committed grassroots organisations from PI84U Foodbank to Leyton Orient FC and with schools and colleges across the borough.\r\nWe’re constantly making new connections. If you belong to a community group based in Waltham Forest, we’d love to hear from you and see how we can work together. Reach out to us by emailing engagement@sohotheatre.com \r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Serious Business of Comedy & Cabaret","instanceDates":"23 May-23 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"547803AHSPDQCDGNLTDCNPLDBVTPPCJSB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-23T15:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-23T14:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-23T17:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-23T16:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Lea Bridge Library","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"After a sold out run, the Sister Fig are returning…\r\nSummer Heights High meets coming of age / sisterhood drama with a sprinkle of Mexican daytime TV.\r\n\r\n\r\nGaulier-trained, character-comedy duo Blaise Wopperer and Lara Ciulli bring you a not-so-tender tale of two codependent sisters and their cow.\r\nA bountiful menu of physicality, clowning, and chemistry, join these potty-mouthed, greasy little misfits for a night you’ll hope to forget. \r\n\r\n\r\nThe Sisters Fig, ‘almost impossible to describe and all the better for it’ (**** All Edinburgh Theatre), was an ‘earth-shatteringly funny’ (***** Binge Fringe), cult hit at the Edinburgh Fringe 2024!\r\n\r\n\r\nCome and see for your stinky selves. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Sisters Fig","instanceDates":"29 May-31 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"624003AQPHDCPGDHDPGBGPSKCRPVGSNHJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-29T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-29T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-31T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-31T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Summer Heights High meets coming of age / sisterhood drama with a sprinkle of Mexican daytime TV.\r\n\r\n\r\nGaulier-trained, character-comedy duo Blaise Wopperer and Lara Ciulli bring you a not-so-tender tale of two codependent sisters and their cow.\r\nA bountiful menu of physicality, clowning, and chemistry, join these potty-mouthed, greasy little misfits for a night you’ll hope to forget. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Sisters Fig.","instanceDates":"28 February-1 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"591603ATVNTBQCLPRLTSDPCTKPMDRSVHV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-02-28T22:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-02-28T22:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-01T22:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-01T22:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"There's only one rule – everyone is welcome at Mum’s.\r\nShesus has transcended and left this pair of offbeat twins all alone. So where do they go for Crimbo now? Back to Mum’s, the original matriarch, of course!\r\nThe Sisters invite you to join them as they crash land home. Expect there to be Karaoke (Y Viva España, anyone?), a prawn ring and Sister Mary Berry's festive bangers with all the trimmings.\r\nSo throw on your best glad-rags, tootle down to Soho and be part of the Sisterhood this yuletide – your Christmas will never be the same again.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":80,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Sisters of Shesus: Christmas at Mum’s","instanceDates":"10 December-21 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"577603AMGTNRHBRPMMQQVBBGVJSLCVJMM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-10T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-10T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-12-21T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-12-21T20:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Drag","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Comedy"},{"description":"The Sketchy Ones bring their dark, farcical, online chaos to a live audience in their stage debut. \r\nA lady’s gone missing and a 35yr old baby boy detective has been summoned to the remote village of No Wye Fye to find her. The lead suspect? An alluring woman in a rocking chair. Great. He loves rocking chairs…\r\nAbout The Sketchy Ones\r\nThe Sketchy Ones formed as a lockdown baby in 2020. Married-couple actors, Natalie Perera and Hamza Jeetooa were pregnant, anxious, but instead of burying their heads in parenting books and comparing the price of nappies, they chose to push the boundaries of the types of roles they were playing and auditioning for. Together with their filmmaking bestie, wedding ordainer, and general enabler, Tom Paul Martin, the three of them parody and clown their way through the things that need to be prodded at.\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Sketchy Ones Present: The (Token) Woman In Black","instanceDates":"21 August-22 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"476803AHJMRPBSRQBLCTHDHHCHVGLTSKG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-21T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-21T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-22T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-22T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Sketch","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Sketch","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"India/South Asian heritage"},{"description":"Cult comedy pioneers Stepdads present the world’s first ever stage adaptation of Victor Hugo’s novel.\r\n\r\nFor two nights only Stepdads are joining forces with alternative comedy’s finest for a smash hit spectacular that guarantees a 100% faithful adaptation of this colossal epic - although this show *might* also feature the Phantom of the Opera, for legal reasons. \r\n\r\nApril 21st  featuring: Julia Masli, Josh Glanc, Lara Ricote, Lorna Rose Treen, Rob Duncan, Dan Lees, Paulina Lenoir, Maya Ricote, Lil Wenker and Jonathan Oldfield.\r\nNarrated by Joz Norris as The Phantom of the Opera\r\n\r\nApril 22nd  featuring: Jordan Brookes, Mark Silcox, Siblings, Lachlan Werner, Rosalie Minnitt, Kathy Maniura, Josh Glanc and Anand Sankar. \r\nNarrated by Rob Duncan as The Starlight Express\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Stepdads Les Mis","instanceDates":"21 April-22 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"707003AGPJGQVLTCVDQHCMDDPCPTGJCJQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-21T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-21T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-22T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-22T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The world's foremost neo-Brechtian-post-punk-falsetto-squeezebox-gypsy-cabaret-three-piece band takes up residence at Soho Walthamstow for one night only with a Soho-themed show drawing on frontman Martyn Jacques's life in the neighbourhood in the '80s – gangsters and working girls, late-night boozers and drugs, friends past and present.\r\nThe world of The Tiger Lillies is dark, peculiar and varied, with moments of deep sadness, cruel black humour and immense beauty. Formed in 1989, they remain one of the most unique, provocative and genre-defying bands one could come across. Olivier award winners and Grammy nominated, the music they produce is a mixture of pre-war Berlin cabaret, anarchic opera and gypsy music, echoing the voices of Bertolt Brecht and Jacques Brel fused with the savage edge of punk.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Tiger Lillies: Soho Songs","instanceDates":"6 June-6 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"599203AMPPKKDHSTBSRMDVQGNNDJCSVQC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-06T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-06T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-06T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-06T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"On 1 November, a day celebrated in many cultures around the world as the Day of the Dead, The Tiger Lillies present a special concert dedicated to their favourite subject: death. 16+ recommended.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Tiger Lillies: Songs of the Dead ","instanceDates":"1 November-1 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"735603AHDPLQJTQHKQSJSMDHMSRTTVJBS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-01T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-01T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-11-01T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-11-01T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Cabaret","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Cabaret","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Soho Theatre and The Together Space have teamed up to bring monthly events for families with both disabled and non-disabled children across the summer.\r\nThis summer we’re hosting local company The Together Space who create  spaces for disabled and non-disabled children, young people and their families to comfortably socialise, learn, play & relax together. \r\n\r\nEnjoy a hub where families of children with SEND can feel safe, feel supported and share experiences. It is a space for neurotypical families to come and learn about disability and neurodiversity. \r\n\r\nMost importantly, it is a place where all families can come to have fun and relax together, without stigma or awkwardness.\r\n\r\nAll children’s tickets include access to all activities on offer, inflatables and sensory space.\r\n\r\nBooking Tickets:\r\nFirst step: select the number of children' s tickets, then press continue\r\nSecond step: add the number of adults accompanying that child and any siblings tickets you require.\r\n0+/12+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":150,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Together Space","instanceDates":"19 July-2 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"621603ARPCVBCMBCSPDQTRKJQNPBQNDJT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-19T14:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-19T13:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-02T10:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-02T09:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Families","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Family","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Access","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Do you love staring at screens? Are you staring at a screen right now? You should get out more. Specifically, to a show that has an enormous screen smack-bang in the middle of it.\r\nThe Umbilicals take the energy of live performance and the spectacle of cinema and smash them together into a new show performed simultaneously on stage and on the big screen. It’s like nothing you’ve ever seen, and nothing they’ve ever done, and it will blow your mind way more literally than you are expecting. The Distraction: enabling your screen addiction.\r\nThe Umbilical Brothers are an international comedy phenomenon. Their unique mix of mind-bending comedy and back-breaking physicality has taken the world’s favourite Australian comedy duo to 40 countries – from stadiums supporting Robin Williams to stadiums supporting N*Sync.\r\nNamed as two of Entertainment Weekly’s 100 Most Creative People in Entertainment, they have appeared on The Late Show with Stephen Colbert, after James Brown at Woodstock ’99, and before the Queen of England. Their global gigs have included a yearlong off-Broadway run where they received raves from The New York Times and a New York Drama Desk nomination. Awards include a Helpmann for Comedy Performance of the year, The Edinburgh Critic’s Choice Award and a couple of BAFTA’s. Younger fans and stoners know them from The Upside Down Show, which they created with Sesame Workshop and won them an Emmy and a Logie. \r\nThey haven’t just broken down the rules of theatre; they’ve invented a new theatrical multiverse. Unbelievable human performances meets special-effects wizardry. It feels so much like magic, you’ll want to burn them at the stake.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Umbilical Brothers: The Distraction","instanceDates":"16 October-16 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"713803APKGNQPQQTTNRJRMQJHBCKJMPSP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-16T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-16T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-16T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-16T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"When Amba buys a pill called TwiceLifeTM that reduces human age each time it’s taken, her husband refuses to swallow. Until newer, younger Amba’s quest for personal fulfilment sets off a chain reaction… Should they go bigger, better, higher the next time around? Or simply avoid old mistakes? And is their solution the ultimate declaration of eternal love? The Undying is a play about losing and finding yourself again … About how we make ourselves and each other… What would you do if you could do it all again?\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Undying","instanceDates":"9 February-10 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"685603ATPPMRTNSNBBGSDLJTLCKGBRKLL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-09T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-09T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-02-10T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-02-10T18:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Directed by Jaz Woodcock-Stewart \r\n16+ restriction","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":85,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"The Virgins","instanceDates":"30 January-7 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"661003AMPSNKMJKCCSNLPQGTSQDSMSCCG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-01-30T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-01-30T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-07T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-07T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"A perfect hour of improvised comedy hosted by Nic Sampson (Starstruck).\r\nThe sell-out show that people are going nuts for is back. Marvel as words suggested by you the audience become scenes of wild comedy right before your shining eyes!\r\nFeaturing different line-ups of the following cast each night:\r\nEmma Sidi (Starstruck), Kiell Smith-Bynoe (Ghosts, Stath Lets Flats), Steen Raskopolous (Feel Good, The Duchess), Lara Ricote (Edinburgh Comedy Awards Best Necomer 2023), Graham Dickson (Austentatious), Lola-Rose Maxwell (Starstruck),  Joseph Moore (Two Hearts), and more guests to be announced!\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"They Seem Nice","instanceDates":"24 June-27 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"628603ARJNQSRHQHSKTNQMVQBKJDPNRPN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-24T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-24T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-27T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-27T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"For decades, Reece Shearsmith has been collecting terrible things. The screaming skull of Glamis Castle, the Highgate vampire, sea devils, witch hunters and a talking mongoose called Gef. Some of them he found. Some of them found him. Now, for the first time, he opens the door. \r\nCo-creator of The League of Gentlemen, Psychoville and Inside No. 9, Reece is no stranger to the morbid and macabre. In this live show, he will guide audiences through the bizarre artefacts and obsessions that have quietly shaped everything he has made.\r\nEach object in Reece’s collection has a story, and each story reaches further back than the last: from a terrifying childhood encounter on a Hull council estate to haunted dressing rooms, uncanny creatures at the edges of long film shoots, and stranger things still...\r\nWorking from his illustrated memoir Things I Took from the Dark: The Museum of Me, Reece will move between storytelling and performance, before engaging in conversation with a special guest host. Audiences will also have the chance to put questions directly to the curator himself...if they dare.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":110,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Things I Took from the Dark as told by Reece Shearsmith","instanceDates":"18 October-18 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"731603ABJNKHVJHSRGQPKMGCKJRQBRPNR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-18T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-18T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-18T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-18T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Podcast","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Love. Unconditionally.\r\nA deep love is challenged by divisive political realities. Jesse, an introspective Black playwright, finds his choices chal-lenged when his boyfriend, Neil, a white Black Lives Matter activist, calls him out for his political apathy. As passions and priorities collide, this couple is forced to reckon with issues of race, class and the bravery it takes to love out loud\r\n\r\nDirected by Billy Porter\r\nWritten by Harrison David Rivers\r\n\r\nStarring Omari Douglas and Alexander Lincoln\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"This Bitter Earth","instanceDates":"18 June-26 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"617603AHNKJHGPSQDLKCVPJKDHMTSDPPK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-18T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-18T18:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-26T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-26T18:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"New Writing"},{"description":"A spiralling playwright dramatises the secrets of her broken friendship, but should she let truth get in the way of a good story?\r\nHot off their award winning, sold out run, Summerhall’s worst kept secret has snuck out of it’s Edinburgh basement and burrowed into Soho’s attic. \r\n\r\nCatch this 5*,  kaleidoscopic ‘Beautifully constructed’ (The Scotsman) cult-hit before it’s New York takeover.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"THIS IS NOT ABOUT ME.","instanceDates":"25 March-18 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"691603AVTNGRSGNSSVTGSQPNVGVTSNJKP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-25T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-25T18:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-18T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-18T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Theatre","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"New Writing","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"New Writing","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"This is a show about love, life (drawings), and being not just a son to your parents – but more like a mutual friend. Thor Stenhaug is a Norwegian comedian based in the UK. In a short period of time, he has built a big online following, headlined top comedy clubs across the country and been shortlisted for British Comedian of the Year – despite not being British (wonder what happened there). 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Thor Stenhaug: One Night Stand Baby","instanceDates":"10 March-23 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"674003AVNGNRDPKNKPQTNKGHLLHCQNLNL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-10T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-10T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-23T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-23T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"This is a show about love, life (drawings), and being not just a son to your parents – but more like a mutual friend. Thor Stenhaug is a Norwegian comedian based in the UK. In a short period of time, he has built a big online following, headlined top comedy clubs across the country and been shortlisted for British Comedian of the Year – despite not being British (wonder what happened there). \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Thor Stenhaug: One Night Stand Baby.","instanceDates":"17 September-20 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"654203ALDPVDVSLHMBQNGMGVSNTSJQPQJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-17T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-17T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-20T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-20T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Lara Ciulli and Riana White are two struggling best mates desperate to make something profound, but destined to fail as they blur the platonic with the romantic and cliff-dive, naked, into the choppy seas of modern dance and Jacob Elordi impersonations. Content Advice: nudity, references to mental health issues. 18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Those People","instanceDates":"21 December-23 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"761003ATLBHBMNDSSQSVKMPKQCGKGBCTB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-21T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-21T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-23T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-23T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Lara Ciulli and Riana White are two struggling best mates desperate to make something profound, but destined to fail as they blur the platonic with the romantic and cliff-dive, naked, into the choppy seas of modern dance and Jacob Elordi impersonations. \r\nA critically acclaimed, ‘ballettically poised and clownishly daft’ (The Scotsman) fever dream of an hour. ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Those People sep2026","instanceDates":"23 September-26 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"745603AGVRMDNJKLKMVNKQVLJGSQTCPCH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-23T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-23T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-26T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-26T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"It’s rat time of year again!!!!\r\nThe chestnuts are a-sizzlin’, the figgy pudding is asteepin’ and you don’t know if that scratching sound behind the tele is Santa conducting a chimney survey or rats in the wall cavity. \r\nJoin Ben, Henry and Mike of the Three Bean Salad Podcast for a night of rat-themed stories to honour the twelve days of Ratmas!\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":100,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Three Bean Salad presents… RATMAS LIVE 2026!","instanceDates":"5 December-5 December","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"753603AKQQQGSQHSSBRTCBGNGPLMNHPDD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-05T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-05T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-12-05T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-12-05T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Tiff tells you why she’d make a good husband. There are also jokes about her actual husband. Husband material. 100% more husband-y. From the woman you have seen on Mock the Week, People Just Do Nothing and that sloth movie. As heard on The Bugle. She has made it into the Top 20 Best Reviewed Shows at the Fringe four times. 'It’s jaw-droppingly remarkable how much ground she covers, how funny she is, how intelligent her attacks are' ***** (Sunday Herald). 'Hugely accomplished and enjoyably provocative comedian' (Times). 'Charming but hard-hitting' ***** (Mirror). 16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tiff Stevenson: Husband Material","instanceDates":"1 April-2 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"606203APTJJTQGQGDJKDLSKTCSLVLRJTD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-01T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-01T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-02T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-02T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Tiff thinks once sex is out the way it’s easier to be clear headed. An insightful and hilarious new show from ‘one of the best in the business’ The Herald. 5 time best reviewed at Edinburgh Fringe. \r\nAs seen on JFL, Mock The Week, The Bugle, House Of Games, Have A Word.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tiff Stevenson: Post-Coital","instanceDates":"10 April-11 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"699603ANVRVQJGCBTMRBQHSBPQLJNHCJJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-10T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-10T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-11T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-11T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Critically acclaimed stand up, writer and actor Tiff Stevenson (Mock the Week, People Just Do Nothing, The Office, Game Face, ABC's The Weekly) invites you to spend an hour with a woman and her self-diagnosed 'Sexy Brain'... a study in trying to see all sides of every argument and driving yourself slowly mad in the process. \r\n\r\n‘Sexy Brain’ was one of Edinburgh Festival Fringe’s Best Reviewed shows of 2022. \r\n\r\nTiff's previous 5* rated shows (Bombshell, Mad Man, Mother) have all been listed in 'British Comedy Guide' Edinburgh Fringe Top 20 best shows. \r\n\r\n‘This is Tiff Stevenson at her finest’ ★★★★★ Broadway Baby \r\n★★★★★ (Mirror), ★★★★★ (Sunday Herald), ★★★★★ (Funny Women).\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tiff Stevenson: Sexy Brain","instanceDates":"19 May-23 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"427803ASTRSKQNTMBPHTMKLVQGSTDVNJS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-19T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-19T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-05-23T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-05-23T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join the cast of the Tifo Football Podcast for one night only at Soho Theatre Walthamstow.\r\nJoe Devine, Seb Stafford-Bloor, JJ Bull & Jon Mackenzie will be recording the podcast live and in person on stage, looking ahead to the Premier League and Champions League finales, presenting a few set pieces, and taking some all-important questions from the audience.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":100,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tifo Football Podcast Live","instanceDates":"24 May-24 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"598003AMMQBBSCBHGVHSLGLLMPQPJMDDB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-24T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-24T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-24T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-24T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Tim Key returns to stamp about and drink a pot of beer and bark reflectively and tighten the screws.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tim Key: L*g**b*rr* (Work-in-Progress)","instanceDates":"12 May-17 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"627803AGDTPHQHPHCDLBPPSTQLCHDVVDT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-12T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-12T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-05-17T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-05-17T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Tim Key returns to stamp about and drink a pot of beer and bark reflectively and tighten the screws.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tim Key: L*g**b*rr* (Work-in-Progress).","instanceDates":"13 January-18 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"580603ADPGTDDNKNQLQGSRPBCDPNQGLTB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-13T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-13T21:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-18T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-18T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"TIM KEY (Alan Partridge, The Ballad of Wallis Island, Tim Key’s Late Night Poetry Programme) again pops his suit on, plods about, in a brand new show.\r\nBit gutted he’s old. Guzzling continental lager. Magnetic lol. Decent reviews for previous shows. Played a pigeon in Bong Joon Ho’s latest movie. Been on Richard Herring’s podcast. Book out: “L.A. Baby!”. Met Steffi Graf in 1998/9.\r\nThis show has poems in, and he’ll stamp and howl. Won the Perrier Award in 2009!\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":85,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tim Key: Loganberry","instanceDates":"19 October-24 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"706203AGTBRHTCRNQDQBLVKSRRMGSPQNG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-19T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-19T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-24T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-24T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Tim Key returns to Soho Theatre one final time before Edinburgh to stamp about and drink a pot of beer and bark reflectively and tighten the screws.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tim Key: Loganberry (Work-in-Progress)","instanceDates":"7 July-12 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"637603ABNGLBRRGVGMKMHDQMQBRNKJSPK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-07T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-07T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-12T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-12T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Tim Key (Alan Partridge, The Witchfinder, Tim Key’s Late Night Poetry Programme) is back with an all-new show. Ruminations about the great indoors with a bit of stamping around. Velour tracksuit, continental lagers, some “poetry”.\r\n \r\n2023 National Comedy Award nominee: Best Stand-Up Show\r\n \r\n‘The greatest stand-up response to Lockdown so far’ ★★★★★ The Times\r\n \r\nKey’s new book, Here We Go Round The Mulberry Bush, is available to buy at all good bookshops and at www.utterandpress.co.uk\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tim Key: Mulberry","instanceDates":"12 June-24 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"471003ALGLQJPKPHMHNSRPNKLPLBHGPQM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-12T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-12T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-24T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-24T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Character","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Tim Minchin, the incomparable singer-songwriter, pianist, comedian, actor, musical-theatre composer-lyricist and soft-hearted provocateur, is thrilled to be going back on tour with his ironically titled new show, Songs The World Will Never Hear. The tour marks the 20th anniversary of his explosive arrival onto the British comedy scene in 2005. \r\n\r\nGet ready for an evening packed with unforgettable songs and stories, as Minchin looks back on how a Perth cabaret pianist ended up building one of the most eclectic and extraordinary careers in entertainment. Delivered with his signature blend of razor-sharp wit, musical virtuosity, and disarming honesty, the set list will draw from three decades of unique songwriting.\r\n12+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":140,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tim Minchin: Songs the World Will Never Hear","instanceDates":"4 June-5 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"604403AQGTQBNKLKSGBPSTKSJSLLKQHJL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-04T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-04T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-05T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-05T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"The masters of long-form improv are back at Soho Theatre.\r\nMaking a welcome return after last year’s five-star sell-out run, ‘the comics TJ Jagodowski and Dave Pasquesi miraculously improvise a one-hour play at every performance. This is an impressive feat of mental athletics, but the results are also observant, complex and frequently enormously funny.’ New York Times\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"TJ & Dave","instanceDates":"27 August-31 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"552803AGKMTNQVTMSCPGDKPDKBDMBLVGR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-27T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-27T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-31T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-31T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Making a welcome return to Soho Theatre, ‘the comics TJ Jagodowski and Dave Pasquesi miraculously improvise a one-hour play at every performance. This is an impressive feat of mental athletics, but the results are also observant, complex and frequently enormously funny.’ New York Times\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"TJ & Dave.","instanceDates":"5 September-9 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"485603AHGSKKTHJPKQBGCDVLMQGSRDNKM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-05T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-05T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-09T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-09T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Tom Allen brings his hit show back to London one final time as he warms up ahead of the international leg of the Completely Tour.\r\nTom Allen has finally moved out of his parents' house, which has been great news for him, better news for department stores and even better news for his stand-up as he's eager to share his life updates, get your opinions on his vegetable patch and delve into the protocol of inviting friends with children for dinner.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tom Allen: Completely","instanceDates":"29 March-29 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"604803AVKDTVGTLPNLSGCKLPHMHJMRSGH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-29T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-29T21:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-29T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-29T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Tom Ballard is undeniably one of Australia’s comedians.\r\nIn 2024 he returns to Soho Theatre with a shiny new show bursting with electric zingers and incredible points being made with expert precision. It’ll make you laugh and cry and think and then laugh again haha. \r\n\r\nBest Show Nominee, Edinburgh Comedy Awards and Melbourne Comedy Festival. As seen on Prime Video’s Deadloch. As heard on Radio 4 and The Bugle. \r\n\r\n#10 in the British Comedy Guide’s Top 50 Shows of 2023.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tom Ballard: Good Point Well Made","instanceDates":"16 September-23 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"569003AVBVQMLJMMNLQTVJKDMTSQTHHKM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-16T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-16T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-09-23T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-09-23T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Stand Up","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"One of Australia’s hottest comedians (not physically) delivers a brand-new show about robots, the monarchy and death.\r\n\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tom Ballard: It Is I","instanceDates":"5 September-9 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"488203ARGCLHHNKBCDVBRNQJGGQLGPBMP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-05T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-05T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-09-09T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-09-09T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Tom Cashman is back in Edinburgh with a new hour of stand-up that might just include the secret to happiness. You may know Tom from Taskmaster Australia, you may know him from TikTok, you may be grappling with the idea of him for the first time now as you read this. It’s pointless to continue guessing your mental state. But if you like the mental state of laughing, you shouldn’t miss this show.14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tom Cashman: 2 Truths, 1 Lie & 17 Slight Exaggerations","instanceDates":"27 August-30 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"632803ASSVRLHMVHBKJTKGVLRTSCGHCLH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-27T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-27T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-08-30T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-08-30T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"International","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Two of Australia’s best stand-ups are in London for a rare double headline show at Soho Theatre on the eve of the Lord’s Test. Australian stand-up comedy, with added cricket flavour and a very special surprise guest.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tom Gleeson & Peter Helliar: Live in London – Ashes Edition","instanceDates":"26 June-27 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"476203AJRKMTMMPMSRGJCSTCSPHJDQBJG","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-26T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-26T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-27T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-27T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Everything is awful, but let's keep it that way. This show explores my family and childhood, my dad being a human volcano and my mum being an alien from outer space. How fun it is when things are rubbish. The shared joy with siblings of a rubbish childhood\r\nGrowing up in Spain and living in a windowless room that my dad had dug underneath the one bedroom apartment 6 of us lived in. \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tom Lawrinson: Buried Alive and Loving It","instanceDates":"4 November-9 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"573003ARTTQJCSJSCPKBBVBKBBVPBJGRN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-04T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-04T21:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-11-09T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-11-09T21:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Tom Lawrinson presents Hubba Hubba; a stand-up show with weird, wonderful and completely unexpected punchlines. \r\nIf you like big laughs, mad jokes and a positive atmosphere then this is the show for you. Come along, I can’t stress how cheeky it's gonna be. \r\n15+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tom Lawrinson: Hubba Hubba","instanceDates":"20 May-22 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"518403ARBVVNTSKJPJPKMTKBSGJVDVBDV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-20T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-20T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-05-22T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-05-22T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"In this hour I will prove two things: magic is real and also, that I have been shagged.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tom Lawrinson: Work in Progress","instanceDates":"15 April-15 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"704403AJGNNQPTBPPDTVJHSDJRGKGJMMC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-15T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-15T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-04-15T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-04-15T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Award-winning duo Dan Lees and Tom Penn present The Sonic Joy Orchestra, an explosive blend of clowning and musical joy. \r\nThese two clowns set out to summon music so divine it could make the heavens quake.\r\nNot for the faint hearted.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tom Penn and Dan Lees: The Sonic Joy Orchestra","instanceDates":"4 June-4 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"715003AVVKDGJPVCNGCBPCVBCNNTBCTGV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-04T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-04T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-06-04T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-06-04T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Arctic Monkeys' album, Whatever People Say I Am, That's What I'm Not, hit the shelves in January 2006. Tracks like 'I Bet You Look Good on the Dancefloor' and 'When the Sun Goes Down' became anthems, showcasing Alex Turner's sharp lyrics and observational storytelling.\r\n\r\nTom Rosenthal's show, Whatever People Say I Am, That's What I Am, tours the UK and Ireland in 2026. Jokes like 'Wimbledon', 'Daniel Radcliffe' and 'Some Weather We're Having' have the potential to become classics, showcasing Rosenthal's sharp nose and observational squawking.\r\n\r\nStar of Friday Night Dinner (C4) and Plebs (ITV), this is Tom’s much awaited return to stand-up following his critically-acclaimed 2019 show, Manhood.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tom Rosenthal: Whatever People Say I Am, That’s What I Am","instanceDates":"23 October-8 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"624403ADJDCKJGSRPRJDJQPDRHKRDJMRL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-10-23T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-10-23T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-08T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-08T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Kiwi comedian, Tom Sainsbury, is best known for his wildly accurate character comedy and social media sketches that make audiences laugh, then immediately question themselves.\r\nA familiar face from Taskmaster NZ and Wellington Paranormal, Tom has built a huge following playing everyone from overbearing bosses and passive-aggressive neighbours to iconic ’80s mums. Blending stand-up, storytelling and razor-sharp observations, his live show dives into the gloriously awkward side of everyday life — small-town scandals, misguided confidence and people making deeply questionable decisions.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tom Sainsbury: Lessons Not Learnt","instanceDates":"11 August-15 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"725603ADJJMMCDVGDQTSMMPNRGMRPSSSP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-11T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-11T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-15T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-15T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Following a sold-out run at the Edinburgh Fringe and a nomination for Best Newcomer at the Edinburgh Comedy Awards, Tom Towelling brings his highly acclaimed hour of alternative comedy to Soho Theatre.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tom Towelling Teaches You to Knit","instanceDates":"19 October-24 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"747803AGQDHRQBCTTCHPQQSQRLPQDQPBH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-19T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-19T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-24T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-24T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Tommy Tiernan's brand new show 'tommedian' is a fun fueled trip through the comic imagination of one of the best comedians in the world.\r\nThis is a wild, uninhibited and fiercely physical display of stand up. A madcap parade of characters, memories and ridiculous flights of fancy. Theatrical, poetical and slightly unhinged.... DON'T YOU DARE MISS IT !!!\r\nTiernan’s legendary record-breaking ticket sales extend across the world. The Star of Channel 4’s hit show Derry Girls and Live at the Apollo (BBC) and the host of his own highly critically praised improvised chat show on Ireland’s RTE 1.\r\nThis event will be a phone-free experience. Use of phones, smart watches and accessories, will not be permitted in the performance space.\r\nThe house will open at 8:40pm and we ask patrons to arrive promptly so that phones, smart watches and accessories can be secured using the Yondr phone pouch system. We cannot guarantee latecomers will be admitted.   \r\nUpon arrival at the venue, all phones, smart watches and accessories will be secured in individual Yondr pouches that will be opened at the end of the event. Guests maintain possession of their devices at all times, and can access them throughout the event only in designated Phone Use Areas within the venue. All devices will be re-secured in Yondr pouches before returning to the performance space.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tommy Tiernan: tommedian","instanceDates":"19 August-24 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"552603ACSHJKCKLQBMLKCRLDSJPPVSPSJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-19T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-19T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-24T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-24T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Written & Performed by: Ms Sharon Le Grand\r\n\r\n\"Welcome to the Dusty Tuna, the only club in London where you can get piss as a mixer!\"\r\n\r\nWhat happens when an international man of mystery meets a straightforward regional woman? Meet Jimmy Pond. He's been tasked with his deadliest mission to date – assassinating the indestructible nightlife oligarch Ms Sharon Le Grand. But will Pond succeed where all men have failed before? \r\nBe thrust into a musical, bombastic, subversive world of hedonism, anarchy and androgyny in the loudmouth Liverpudlian's debut piece of theatre, Tomorrow Is Already Dead. \r\n\r\nMs Sharon Le Grand is a London-based performance artist, originally from Maghull on the outskirts of Liverpool. Working in the worlds of live art, cabaret for the past 7 years she has made a name for herself flinging her handbag across the country. Sharon has just finished starring in Sound of The Underground by Travis Alabanza at The Royal Court. In 2021 she performed in An Ode to The Underground and Ms Sharon Le Grand, written by Travis Alabanza as part of the Royal Court’s ‘Living Newspaper’ series. In 2020 she wrote and produced her sell out show The 12 Stages of Lockdown which toured clubs and queer venues across the UK. Ms Sharon’s previous collaborators include LADA, Arts Council England, Home Live Art, SLAP Fest, Take Me Somewhere Fest and Homotopia Fest.  They have performed at venues all over London including VFD, The Glory, Shoreditch Town Hall, The Karaoke Hole and the George and Dragon. They have been featured in magazines such as Dazed & Confused, i-D and Wonderland.\r\n\r\nCreatives\r\nWritten & Performed by Ms Sharon Le Grand\r\nDirected by Sam Curtis Lindsay\r\nMusician: Nicky Harris\r\nLighting: Joshua Harriette \r\nVideo Animation and Poster Design: Josh Quinton\r\nCostume: Max Allen \r\nChoreographer: Jeanie Crystal \r\n\r\n16+ recommended\r\n\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":75,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tomorrow is Already Dead ","instanceDates":"6 June-17 June","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"459803ADSHPMTHCVNVVPNJMQLNGRVJRKJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-06T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-06T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-06-17T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-06-17T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Drag","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Cabaret"},{"description":"Formerly the Soho Theatre Young Writers’ Award, the Tony Craze Award is in honour of Soho Theatre’s former Artistic Director who passed away in 2016.  Open to the 48 writers who completed the Soho Theatre Writers’ Lab in 2023, the prize celebrates some of the exciting voices and pieces which have developed through the nine-month programme. \r\n\r\n2023 shortlisted plays\r\n\r\nFat Do as Fat Does by Lashay Green\r\nFilthy Animal by Rosie Race\r\nPRESSURE by Danny Bailey\r\nWINNER: Insane Asylum Seekers by Laith Elzubaidi\r\nWINNER: Reparations by Maryam Garad\r\nHIGHLY COMMENDED: There’s a Mouse in the Kitchen by Cal-I Jonel\r\n\r\n18+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Tony Craze Award 2023","instanceDates":"22 March-22 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"536203AGPHBVHTMVKRJCKBVPKMRPRBGSC","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-22T15:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-22T15:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-22T15:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-22T15:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Robby Hoffman and Rachel Kaly bring their popular podcast, TOO FAR, LIVE! on stage.  \r\nDescribed by the New York Times as \"an addictive listen\" and that \" truly great comedy emerges from combustible hostility, discord and a melodramatic sense of conflict\"  \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"TOO FAR, LIVE!","instanceDates":"19 March-19 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"530603ALQHGVPHHMCKBJHQRSGVCCJPTQN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-19T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-19T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-03-19T19:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-03-19T19:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Hello friend. Open your mind, take out what’s inside and wish it well on its future endeavours. You’re going to need the space for this one.\r\nI’m talking life, love, loss, finding your way and pigeons... quite a lot about pigeons actually... it's pretty pigeon-heavy to be honest. So please join me, Toussaint Douglass, for an hour of joyfully absurd, charmingly awkward stand-up.\r\nToussaint brings his debut show to Soho following a run at the Edinburgh Fringe. As seen on Richard Osman’s House of Games (BBC Two), writer for Have I Got News For You (BBC One) and James Acaster’s Springleaf podcast, and tour support for Russell Howard.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Toussaint Douglass: Accessible Pigeon Material","instanceDates":"22 September-28 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"647803ATNNGMGSPDHRQCRGQLTMKBVPTLN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-22T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-22T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-03-28T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-03-28T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Hello friend. Open your mind, take out what’s inside and wish it well on its future endeavours. You’re going to need the space for this one.\r\nI’m talking life, love, loss, finding your way and pigeons... quite a lot about pigeons actually... it's pretty pigeon-heavy to be honest. So please join me for an hour of joyfully absurd, charmingly awkward stand-up.\r\nToussaint previews his debut Edinburgh Fringe show at Soho Theatre. As seen on Richard Osman’s House of Games (BBC Two), writer for Have I Got News For You (BBC One) and James Acaster’s Springleaf podcast, and tour support for Russell Howard.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Toussaint Douglass: Accessible Pigeon Material – Preview","instanceDates":"14 July-18 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"630803ARTBJRDMNSHMHTLJMQHMRNHBJPT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-14T20:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-14T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-18T20:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-18T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Direct from their critically acclaimed Edinburgh Fringe debut comes 'Troll': an ★★★★ \"irresistibly silly” (The Guardian), two-troll clown comedy about connection, scape(goat)ing and being misunderstood.\r\nFed up with years of misrepresentation, villainization and exclusion, two trolls find themselves in a theatre, ready and desperate to tell their side of the story and the truth about those three goats. Inspired by Norwegian folklore, 'Troll' is a heartwarming mash-up of music, storytelling, audience interaction, physical theatre and clown.\r\nWinner of Oslo Fringe's funniest show 2023\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Troll by Marie Kallevik and Anna Marie Simonsen","instanceDates":"15 February-15 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"524403APBTMSJGKLSLJBNMPLDGBMLKDVP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-15T22:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-15T22:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-15T22:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-15T22:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Female Led","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Trygve Wakenshaw is coming back to Soho with his hilarious mime-clown-comedy show \r\n\r\nLight and silly, absurd and Dada, and a sort of autobiographical, introspective look at all the silly little things that can make or break a friendship.\r\nRanked in the top 5 of best reviewed comedy shows at the Edinburgh Fringe for its debut season, Silly Little Things is a hilarious, moving and physically extraordinary new show by the industry leading mime Trygve Wakenshaw.\r\n\r\n Silly Little Things is at once subversive and sublime - a masterclass of mime from the man who paved the way for so many contemporary clowns.\r\nIn this new show Trygve builds an experimental playground and lets his imagination run riot. Spinning ridiculous scenes out of the smallest funny ideas, and conjuring up slapstick magic, Silly Little Things is a space of wonder and joy. It's about friendship and magic and what more could we want really?\r\n\r\nTrygve's hilarious and fun hit physical comedies are consistently a sell-out at festivals around the world.\r\n14+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Trygve Wakenshaw: Silly Little Things","instanceDates":"1 April-5 April","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"593804ANDSNDKJSTQVGVMCVJRBSCJGTTB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-01T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-01T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-04-05T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-04-05T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"New Zealand’s cult-musical-comedy powerhouses Laura Daniel (Taskmaster NZ) and Joseph Moore make an explosive return to the Soho Theatre with their critically acclaimed new hour.\r\nFresh off hit runs in Edinburgh and Melbourne Comedy Festival, Two Hearts invite you to step into a concert-like experience and forget about the horrible world we live in with this non-stop boiler-room set of uplifting comedy hits (largely about the horrible world we live in). It is physically impossible to fall asleep during this show.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Two Hearts: Don’t Stop Throbbing","instanceDates":"27 July-1 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"682403APPQCVJDTVQSNKGNNMSLSRJJMJK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-07-27T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-07-27T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-08-01T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-08-01T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"New Zealand's hottest comedy pop-music duo Two Hearts are back - now with more \"vow\" factor.\r\nA year ago, real-life power-couple Laura Daniel (Taskmaster NZ) and Joseph Moore (Snort) tied the knot, joined bank accounts and immediately drained it all for a lavish wedding. Join them for hot new songs about love, life and maintaining a successful relationship with your co-worker.16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Two Hearts: Til Death Do Us Hearts","instanceDates":"15 January-17 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"588803ARKTBMHSGBQPMNBJRLGNPHCPKJP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-15T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-15T21:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-01-17T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-01-17T21:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Stand Up","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"New Zealand's hottest comedy pop-music duo Two Hearts are back in the UK with a brand new show – and now with more ‘vow’ factor.  \r\nIn 2022, real-life power-couple Laura Daniel (Taskmaster NZ) and Joseph Moore (Snort) tied the knot, joined their bank accounts and immediately drained it all for a lavish wedding. Now they want to renew their vows in front of you for money. \r\nJoin Two Hearts for an evening of hot new songs and greatest hits as they share what they’ve learned about love, life, and maintaining a successful relationship with your co-worker.\r\nThey have decided to spend their entire lives together, so it's only fair you decide to spend an hour with them at the Soho Theatre.\r\nWarning: contains solemnly swearing.  \r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Two Hearts: Til Death Do Us Hearts.","instanceDates":"29 August-30 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"491603ABBKLRVLRDQTBQKLBCBNPCVJHBM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-29T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-29T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-08-30T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-08-30T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"International","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Music","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Your favourite pair of co-dependent Australian dickheads are hitting London, doing what they do best – filling slots. Part of London Clown Festival 2024.\r\nFeaturing unhinged sketches, silly dancing, stupid puppets and surprisingly good singing. The inseparable, pyjama-wearing, cat-obsessed duo of Sharnema and Dave have worked themselves into a tizzy deconstructing the power of love through lo-fi indie rock (*electric ukulele alert*). With songs including I Don’t Wanna Have A Baby and Fanta of the Opera. \r\n\r\nPrepare to have your slot filled with 58 minutes of clowntastic, musical nonsense, delivered with big chaos energy. The only show that guarantees to NOT make you pregnant, or your money back. \r\n\r\nBring a fling of mort and get a free sanglcrumb. \r\n16+\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Two Little Dickheads: Slot Fillers","instanceDates":"12 July-12 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"544403AMQSLCKGVTJSMPBVLPSQQLBGTMV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-12T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-12T19:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-07-12T20:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-07-12T19:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Clowning","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Join the Two Mr Ps as they take their award-winning podcast back on the road, it's a lesson in laughter you won't want to miss!\r\nPrepare for an evening filled with laughter as they share more hilarious stories and anecdotes about the challenges teachers, parents, and school staff face while working with the most unintentionally funny comedians of all—children.\r\nDrawing from their uproarious classroom experiences, as well as the most embarrassing, cringeworthy, and downright hilarious tales from educators across the UK, the Two Mr Ps will have you laughing until your cheeks hurt. And just like in school, audience participation is encouraged! You can submit your own stories, confessions, dilemmas and embarrassing moments to be read anonymously during the show here - http://bit.ly/3CDIz4x\r\nMr P has been a primary school teacher for over 17 years and is one of the leading voices for teachers and school staff in the UK. With his unique blend of practical tips and humorous insights into classroom life, he has become one of the most followed teachers on social media.\r\nSince launching their podcast in 2018 with his younger brother Adam, Two Mr Ps in a Podcast has become the UK's number one education podcast. \r\nDon't miss this chance to see the Two Mr Ps live!\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Two Mr Ps in a Podcast: Live – Let That Be A Lesson…","instanceDates":"26 October-26 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"700403AGLNMQTQRVJBJLTMVGJJLRMRJLJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-26T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-26T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-26T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-26T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Ugly Sisters is an operatic, heretic, parasitic and hallucinatory retelling of this very moment, of sisterhood, of all feminist history. piss / CARNATION return to Soho Theatre after a blistering, sell-out run at Edinburgh Fringe.\r\n18+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Ugly Sisters","instanceDates":"25 June-12 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"626003ABGJNDNBTQHTJLLCBDCLRNCTQLB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-06-25T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-06-25T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-12T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-12T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"LGBTQ+","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Performance Art","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"LGBTQ+","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Danny Robins’ live show investigates the most spine-tingling range of Uncanny stories yet, as the award-winning BBC paranormal podcast and TV series comes to thrilling, ghostly life on stage!\r\nAre you scared of the dark?\r\nChilling, intriguing and sometimes moving, prepare to investigate a collection of real-life potentially paranormal mysteries, as Danny tries to get to the heart of why we, as humans, continue to have a fear of the dark. Is it superstition? A remnant of our days as cavepeople huddled round a campfire? Or is there really something lurking out there in the darkness?\r\nDanny will be joined by experts Dr Ciarán O’Keeffe and Evelyn Hollow to examine ghostly apparitions, UFO sightings, a haunted nursery, strange creatures on lonely country lanes, and bizarre poltergeist activity in seemingly normal houses.\r\nThis is NOT an ordinary podcast show. This is story-telling and paranormal investigation at its peak. Using a unique backdrop of sound, video projection and theatrical magic, Danny will bring these stories vividly to life with the help of Ciarán and Evelyn, plus input from you the audience, as you get the chance to ask your questions and share your own experiences.\r\nAs always, whether you are #TeamSceptic, #TeamBeliever or somewhere in between, everyone is welcome!\r\nSo... do you dare to enter the darkness?\r\n\r\nLimited free tickets available for a meet and greet with Danny at the venue from 6pm - 7pm. Grab them while you can.\r\n\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Uncanny: Fear of the Dark","instanceDates":"5 May-6 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"699003AMTLHDNGQQVDBTVKPPDTGDTBBHB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-05T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-05T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-06T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-06T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Storytelling","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Soho Theatre Walthamstow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Uncanny: Fear of the Dark (Meet & Greet)","instanceDates":"5 May-6 May","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"699203ADRDRGRPGDLGJNMLGBTSNTLCPGL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-05T18:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-05T17:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-05-06T18:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-05-06T17:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Uncle Glen’s Menagerie returns to Soho Theatre.\r\n\r\nThis is the hit show that throws performers together for the first time. In every scene, one actor has the script. The other knows nothing…\r\n\r\nThe show features a rotating cast of some of the UK and US' top performers, including award-winning (EMMY/ BAFTA/ Olivier) leading actors and comedians from TV shows such as Loki, Black Mirror, Ghosts, Rivals, Starstruck, Big Boys, Veep, Curb Your Enthusiasm, I May Destroy You, This Time with Alan Partridge, Brooklyn Nine-Nine, Parks and Recreation, and live shows such as Hamilton, Austentatious, Six the Musical, Kool Story Bro, The Bear Pack and Saturday Night Live.\r\n\r\nAs brand-new versions of scenes unfold – on the spot, never to be seen again – don’t miss a hilarious, wild and completely unique experience...\r\n\r\nVery special guests to be announced shortly!\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Uncle Glen’s Menagerie","instanceDates":"25 September-27 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"648203APDKVGSQRBBJVLVRKMDRQVCMSQV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-25T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-25T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-09-27T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-09-27T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Uncle Glen’s Menagerie returns to Soho Theatre.\r\nThis is the hit show that throws performers together for the first time. In every scene, one actor has the script. The other knows nothing.\r\nThe show has played to sold-out audiences in London and Edinburgh, and features a rotating cast of some of the UK and US' top performers, including award-winning (EMMY/ BAFTA/ Olivier) leading actors and comedians from TV favourites such as Loki, Black Mirror, Rivals, Starstruck, Big Boys, Ghosts, Veep, Curb Your Enthusiasm, I May Destroy You, This Time with Alan Partridge, Brooklyn Nine-Nine, Parks and Recreation, and hit live shows such as Hamilton, Austentatious, Six the Musical, One Woman Show and Saturday Night Live.\r\nEach performance will feature special guests and new pairings. As brand-new versions of scenes unfold – on the spot, never to be seen again – don’t miss a wild, hilarious and completely unique experience...\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Uncle Glen’s Menagerie.","instanceDates":"27 March-28 March","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"608403APMJBJJPCGTHQMSKGCMSMKQSSKN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-27T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-27T21:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-03-28T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-03-28T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Monks find magic water. Magic water makes dreams come true. Monks go crazy.\r\n\r\nStarring acclaimed clowns and monks Max Baumgarten (Opium), Dee Marcucci (Absinthe), John Norris (Mr Chonkers, Piggy Time), Bill O’Neill (The Amazing Banana Brothers), and Claire Woolner (A Retrospection). Come to Soho at night and rejoice with them.\r\n\r\nCo-created with Sam Fishman. Co-directed by Corey Podell (Mr Chonkers, Vanessa 5000) and John Norris.\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Underground Monk Show","instanceDates":"11 January-23 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"738403ABDDHSGLGJJNPKLSVPTJTVMKQBQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-01-11T21:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-01-11T21:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-01-23T21:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-01-23T21:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"Theatre","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"","attribute_AudiencePreference2":""},{"description":"Edinburgh Comedy Awards Best Newcomer Urooj Ashfaq is back, but this time she’s different.\r\nNo longer is she a good girl and a relatable comedian. Most importantly, she is not sweet. Now she’s a bona fide bad girl and edgelord who at times mentions sexy things and topics. Come and watch her to find out what’s happened…\r\nOne of India’s most exciting comics, Urooj Ashfaq returns to Soho with her new show How To Be A Baddie, the follow-up to her debut show Oh No!, which won the Edinburgh Comedy Best Newcomer Award in 2023.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Urooj Ashfaq: How To Be A Baddie","instanceDates":"3 November-15 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"643003AMHQJCJTCCTJKCTVRGPCQJCDBDK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-03T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-03T19:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-15T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-15T19:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"The Edinburgh Comedy Award Best Newcomer returns to Soho to preview her brand new show.\r\nThe award-winning Urooj Ashfaq, one of India’s most exciting comics, returns to the UK once again – but this time she is different. No longer is she a good girl and relatable comedian, and most importantly, she is not sweet. A bona fide bad girl and edgelord who at times mentions sexy things and topics. Come watch to find out what happened…16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Urooj Ashfaq: How To Be A Baddie – Preview","instanceDates":"21 July-26 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"631003ACQKJMDPJKDCNBTDSDVBCRQCGTT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-21T18:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-21T17:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-07-26T18:45:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-07-26T17:45:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"Stand Up","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Urooj Ashfaq: How To Be A Baddie (Frog & Bucket, Manchester)","instanceDates":"19 November-19 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"644003ACBCDLKRHHGHHQNSSRKCVKSDQNN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-19T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-19T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-19T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-19T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"The Frog & Bucket, Manchester","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Urooj Ashfaq: How To Be A Baddie (Hat Factory Arts Centre, Luton)","instanceDates":"20 November-20 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"645803ALNJPMMBPHSKNBJRMCTNGHVNLTS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-20T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-20T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-20T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-20T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Hat Factory Arts Centre, Luton","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Urooj Ashfaq: How To Be A Baddie (Hen & Chicken, Bristol)","instanceDates":"26 November-26 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"644403AQDRCCPLPLCLJGBDTRQRRCMRCBM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-26T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-26T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-26T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-26T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"The Hen & Chickens, Bristol","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Urooj Ashfaq: How To Be A Baddie (Loading Bay, Bradford)","instanceDates":"28 November-28 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"645603AQNCMDBQQBNDSJPRDPMDDLQTVNV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-28T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-28T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-28T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-28T19:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Loading Bay, Bradford","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Urooj Ashfaq: How To Be A Baddie (The Big Difference, Leicester)","instanceDates":"21 November-21 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"644203ADKCMVQKTKGGKMCHSHTVNSHNSNR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-21T20:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-21T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-21T20:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-21T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"The Big Difference, Leicester","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Urooj Ashfaq: How To Be A Baddie (The Glee Club, Birmingham)","instanceDates":"27 November-27 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"644603AKCGVMHKHMVCSGVSHLCLJHQMJRN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-27T18:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-27T18:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-27T18:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-27T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"The Glee Club, Birmingham","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Urooj Ashfaq: How To Be A Baddie (The Stand, Glasgow)","instanceDates":"29 November-29 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"644803APVMNNGPTRNHVDRNGLHPNPKKPRL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-29T16:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-29T16:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-29T16:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-29T16:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"The Stand, Glasgow","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Urooj Ashfaq: How To Be A Baddie (The Wardrobe, Leeds)","instanceDates":"18 November-18 November","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"643803AKDCDQHMJCRJGCRNJVGPGBJGVKN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-18T20:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-18T20:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2025-11-18T20:00:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2025-11-18T20:00:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"The Wardrobe, Leeds","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"After her Edinburgh Comedy Award winning debut last year, one of India’s most exciting comics is back.\r\nA mix of stories and observations that Urooj thinks are funny, the show title is defensive because she still hasn’t figured out if it is funny to everybody and she’s sensitive.\r\nWINNER: Edinburgh Comedy Award Best Newcomer 2023\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Urooj Ashfaq: It’s Funny To Me - Work in Progress","instanceDates":"5 August-14 August","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"549403ALBVTRCNPLLVTJLQQDGVLBTDRDP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-05T19:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-05T18:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-08-14T19:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-08-14T18:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":true,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":"Stand Up"},{"description":"Urooj is an Indian stand-up who hails from a tiny, unknown city called Mumbai. She not only has a degree in psychology but went on to be in therapy herself. What’s her show about, you ask? I think you should ask YOURSELF why you insist on knowing everything. Why don’t you just show up, be surprised, and go with the flow? Okay, I’ll tell you: it’s about her, her family, things that annoy her, and things she loves. She will obviously talk about herself since she’s already speaking in third person. Please come. I love you.\r\n16+","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Urooj Ashfaq: Oh No!","instanceDates":"30 October-3 February","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"476603AQCMDHQSHNKBNJHCVKVPVVGTLQJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-10-30T20:45:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-10-30T20:45:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2024-02-03T18:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2024-02-03T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"Yes","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Downstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"Urooj is an Indian stand-up who hails from a tiny, unknown city called Mumbai. She not only has a degree in psychology but went on to be in therapy herself. What’s her show about, you ask? I think you should ask YOURSELF why you insist on knowing everything. Why don’t you just show up, be surprised, and go with \r\nthe flow? Okay, I’ll tell you: it’s about her, her family, things that annoy her, and things she loves. She will obviously talk about herself since she’s already speaking in third person. Please come. I love you.\r\n\r\n16+ recommended","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Urooj Ashfaq: Oh No! – Edinburgh Preview","instanceDates":"25 July-29 July","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"472803ATGVNSBLKVGVQTJKMKTRLBTMMLS","firstInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-25T21:15:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-25T20:15:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2023-07-29T21:15:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2023-07-29T20:15:00Z","altText":"","attribute_AudiencePreference1":"Comedy","attribute_AudiencePreference2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_DynamicPricing":"No","attribute_PriorityBooking":false,"attribute_Venue":"Upstairs","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory1":"Comedy","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory2":"India/South Asian heritage","attribute_WebsiteFilterCategory3":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":false,"name":"Urooj Ashfaq: Oh No! At Edinburgh - The Monkey Barrel","instanceDates":"23 January-23 January","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"5